window.AKK_ZOMBIE_CAT_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_ZOMBIE_CAT_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":101,"title":"Chapter 101: 0101","paragraphs":["But every classmate was watching him, calling his name: âHuang Yuntao!â","Little Huang wasnât just the class monitor. He excelled in both character and academics, and he was also the student council president. Whenever a student representative was needed to speak, he was the one who stepped up.","Everyone knew him.","Countless eyes were fixed on him, waiting expectantly.","At that moment, Little Huang finally understood Uncle Zhou Wang completely.","He clenched his teeth.","So this was why adults gathered in silence and smoked when faced with a difficult choice. Because it was just too hard.","âHuang Yuntaoâ¦â everyone called softly.","No one dared to raise their voice, afraid of attracting the zombies.","Faintly, from the other side of the laboratory building, came another scream.","In fact, many more students were still trapped in their classrooms.","Huang Yuntao clenched his teeth again and finally made up his mind. âIf weâre going to save people, we need to find weapons first!â","Zombies werenât all that frightening, but without weapons or protective gear, humans were at a disadvantage, and the risk of infection was extremely high.","But where could they find weapons? This was a school. It was hard enough to find even a stick. Desks and chairs could at most be used for defense; they were far too poor for attacking.","Thinking of desks and chairs, Little Huang remembered seeing people in the distance at the school building fuse the metal legs of desks and chairs together to make a ladder. That seemed to be a special ability, just like his own ability to sense danger in advance.","His gaze fell on the railing along the schoolâs outer wallâ¦","Some of the seventh-graders looked so young they could have been elementary school students. When they cried, they looked even younger.","The students of Class 11, Grade 7, were crying their eyes out, yet none of them dared to make much noise, afraid of alerting the zombies in the hallway.","One boyâs eyes were swollen from crying.","He was the student who had awakened a metal-based ability. He had come up with the idea of fusing the metal legs of desks and chairs into a crude single-pole ladder, allowing everyone to climb down and escape.","Who could have known that zombies would appear? The students who had already climbed down had screamed and fled. No one knew whether they had managed to get away.","Only seven students remained in the classroom. There had already been far fewer students in many classes when the new term began. Some classes had even been merged because there werenât enough teachers.","He felt that it was all his fault. If he hadnât made that single-pole ladder and sent his classmates down to escape, perhaps those people wouldnât have died.","He couldnât forgive himself.","As tears streamed down his face, he wiped away the blood from his nose and made a chair leg twist and change shape in his hand.","His head throbbed terribly. Making the ladder had nearly caused his brain to explode, and now he was still forcing himself to use his ability. The nosebleed simply wouldnât stop.","âWu Shuchen, what are you doing?â someone asked softly.","The boy gritted his teeth. âIâm going to make a sword. Iâm going out to kill zombies.â","He had decided to die alongside the zombies. Only then could he atone for the classmates who had died.","Someone tried to stop him. âDonât keep going! Your nose is bleeding!â","Another said, âHow are you going to get out? If you open the door and the zombies come in, weâll all die!â","Those words finally crushed Wu Shuchenâs resolve. He sank into despair and gave up.","âWill someone come rescue us?â","âI donât know. Dad and Mom are both at work. They must have run into a lot of zombies too.â","âWhen we were trapped at home last time, we called the police over and over, but they never came.â","The students remembered what had happened before. The zombie outbreak had begun on Saturday, but official rescue efforts had not started until Wednesday.","The children were filled with despair.","Just then, the schoolâs broadcast suddenly crackled to life.","âStudent in Building One who can fuse metal! Student in Building One who can fuse metal! This is Huang Xuetao, the student council president!â","Everyone looked up in astonishment.","Even the zombies in the hallway raised their heads. The voice was coming simultaneously from the speakers in every classroom, echoing through the corridors. Unable to pinpoint the source, the zombies wandered around in confusion, unable to find any fresh meat.","Wu Shuchen was bewildered. âIsâ¦ is he talking about me?â","âItâs you! Itâs definitely you!â","âIt has to be you!â","âStudent in Building One who can fuse metal, listen carefully. In a moment, weâll lure the zombies beneath the building toward the gymnasium. Find a way to come down while you can. I need your special ability to help everyone make weapons!â","âStudents! Many teachers have sacrificed themselves to protect us! Weâve all seen what things are like now, so stop counting on someone else to come rescue us!â","âWe have to save ourselves!â","âStudents! Everyone in Building One, please help cover for this student. I need him very much right now!â","Countless students trapped in their classrooms tilted their heads toward the speakers above the blackboards.","âItâs Huang Xuetao!â","âIs he the student representative who spoke at the entrance ceremony?â","âYes, thatâs him! Heâs the student council president!â","He was needed. People were counting on him. He still had a chance to help everyone and make up for the mistake he had made.","Wu Shuchen wiped away his tears and stood up. âIâm going!â","âWait!â","One of his classmates called out to him and pulled a roll of wide adhesive tape from a storage cabinet.","Everyone immediately understood. The workbooks and exercise books were just the right size and thickness to be wrapped around his arms as protection.","Back when the adults had gone out to kill zombies, many of them had used the same method to protect themselves. It was the first time the children had gained a direct understanding of how tough paper could be.","Sure enough, sounds began to rise from somewhere in the distance. Everyone pressed against the windows and looked out. The zombies below were heading toward the source of the noise one after another.","The seven children in Class 11, Grade 7, worked together to lower the crude single-pole ladder out of the window again. Wu Shuchen took advantage of the opportunity and climbed down.","But when he was halfway down, the people above suddenly cried out, âThere are zombies!â","Wu Shuchen looked down. Sure enough, two original zombies had been left behind because they were slower than the second-generation zombies. The sound of the ladder hitting the ground had attracted them, and they were running back.","They were almost beneath the ladder. What should he do? What should he do?","Should he climb back up?","Suddenly, a clattering sound came from behind the zombies. The two zombies turned around together.","Wu Shuchen looked up. Students on the floor above had leaned out of their windows and were throwing pencil cases in that direction, one after another, trying to send them as far as possible.","The zombies were drawn to the constant banging of the pencil cases striking the ground. They ran wildly from side to side, chasing a sound that rang out here one moment and there the next.","The students were using their ingenuity and taking real action to cover Wu Shuchen.","His vision blurred with tears as he climbed down step by step.","A boy who was a head taller than him came running over. âSo itâs you! Come on, follow me!â","It was indeed Huang Xuetao, the student council president who often appeared onstage to speak.","Little Huang also recognized Wu Shuchenâa short, bespectacled boy with a refined appearance.","At this yearâs Arts Festival, the first-place prize had gone to a dragon welded from strips of metal.","When Wu Shuchen had gone onstage to accept the award, he had said that he had welded it himself, having learned to handle all kinds of tools from his father since he was little.","A photograph of him posing with the dragon had been displayed on the bulletin board in the school building. Little Huang saw it every time he passed by.","Little Huang led Wu Shuchen toward the nearest fence. âStay close to me. Donât be afraid. I can sense danger in advance.â","The moment he finished speaking, he suddenly grabbed Wu Shuchen and pulled him in another direction, darting through the gap between two buildings.","Wu Shuchen ran while looking back over his shoulder and saw zombies coming along the road they had just taken.","âSenior! What do you want me to do?â he asked between ragged breaths.","Little Huang asked, âCan you control metal?â","âYes! I can fuse metal together and reshape it! But Iâm very slow!â Wu Shuchen replied.","As for the fact that making anything large left him with splitting headaches and a bloody nose, he kept that to himself.","Little Huang asked, âWhat about cutting metal apart?â","âHuh?â","As they spoke, they had already reached the outer edge of the school. The very perimeter consisted of dark green iron fencing.","Little Huang grabbed one of the bars. âCan you cut them loose? Take them off one by one?â","Take them off one by oneâthat would make iron rodsâ¦!","Ready-made weapons!","Wu Shuchen understood instantly, and his eyes lit up. âIâll try!â","He gripped the fence with both hands. A few seconds later, two âiron rodsâ came free from the row of fencing as if they had simply been plucked out!","Not only had he succeeded, it was also much easier than fusing metal together and reshaping it. It didnât put any additional strain on his brain!","âTake out every other one!â Little Huang reminded him. âIf you dismantle the whole thing, itâll be easy for the zombies to get in.â","âOkay!â Wu Shuchen removed the iron rods from the fence one after another.","â¦","New Technology District, Maiduo Supermarket, warehouse.","Brother Dong and Guo Jun lay side by side on the mattresses in the secret base atop the storage shelves, their eyes vacant.","Their only phone had run out of power. They couldnât contact anyone outside, and they had no idea whether Jiang Cheng and the others would come to rescue them.","They had eaten too many snacks and needed to take a dump. But with zombies below, they didnât dare climb down.","Going on top of the shelves would be too awful to contemplate, so all they could do was hold it in.","The two men were listless, their unfocused eyes fixed on the warehouse ceiling.","Suddenly, several noises rang out in the storeroom.","Neither of them moved.","âWhat was that?â Guo Jun asked in a low voice.","âProbably the zombies knocking into things,â Brother Dong whispered back.","It sounded like something had fallen to the floorâor perhaps someone had collapsed.","As they spoke in hushed voices, a furry head suddenly appeared in their field of vision.","â¦Huh?","Guo Jun shot upright.","Brother Dong nearly jumped out of his skin and sat up as well.","Back when Brother Dong had dealt with Jiang Cheng, Mo Li had always been curled up inside Jiang Chengâs crossbody bag. Unless he opened his eyes and looked closely, there was no way to tell what was inside.","Afterward, Brother Dong had shamelessly run off.","So he wasnât familiar with this little black cat.","But Guo Jun knew him!","Guo Jun had always lived in the Youth Apartments, working odd jobs in exchange for rent.","After finishing his shift at Maiduo, he had to go door to door in the Youth Apartments, fixing this or that for the residents. While making repairs, he inevitably ended up chatting with them.","âJiang Chengâs little black catâ came up in conversation quite often.","Guo Jun had also seen the little black cat sunning himself on top of the pavilion in the mornings when he went to work.","Had Jiang Cheng come to rescue them?","Before they could even celebrate, the little black cat suddenly let out a âMeow~â that rang out with startling clarity in the cavernous warehouse.","Oh, for the love of God!","Terrified, Brother Dong and Guo Jun reached out, trying to cover the catâs mouth.","But Mo Li had no intention of letting them succeed. With a twist of his body, he vanished from atop the merchandise.","Guo Jun and Brother Dong instinctively leaned over to look down.","They couldnât see the little black cat anywhere, but they did see the bodies of zombies lying in the aisle.","Huh? How had those two zombies died?"]},{"number":102,"title":"Chapter 102: 0102","paragraphs":["No matter how they had died, those two zombies were dead. And with no other zombies wandering in, Guo Jun and Brother Dong began considering closing the warehouse door.","The two of them went down together.","They crept forward quietly. A zombie suddenly flashed into view outside, and the two hurriedly ducked out of sight.","Once it had passed, they dared to emerge again and continued forward on tiptoe. They put their hands on the door and pushed upward together.","The warehouse door was broad and massive, large enough for a forklift to pass through.","It made a lot of noise when opened or closed.","The two men tried to lift it slowly as they shut it, so it would not scrape against the ground or make too much noise at the hinges.","Just then, a thread of cold air drifted over from the shopping area.","Though it was already late August, the lingering summer heat was still fierce. Yesterday, the outdoor temperature had been 32 degrees Celsius, and the buildingâs air conditioning was running as if it were still midsummer.","The warehouse had ventilation but no air conditioning, and it was stiflingly hot.","Brother Dong suddenly shivered all over. Then an uncontrollable rush of air surged through his nostrils. âAhâchoo!â","The sneeze was crisp and thunderously loud! It even echoed through the warehouse!","Guo Jun spun around and bolted without hesitation!","To hesitate for even one second would be a betrayal of his own survival!","Brother Dong had closed his eyes to sneeze. When he opened them, a zombieâs face was right in front of him! An old woman, her face covered in wrinkles!","Brother Dong nearly lost his soul. He let out a shriek and fell flat on his backside, then scrambled up and fled for his life in blind panic.","Several zombies had rushed in. Worse yet, the first two were second-generation zombies.","That bastard Guo Jun had already vanished into who knew where. When trouble came, he was absolutely useless as a companion!","At that moment, Brother Dong had completely forgotten that he himself had been the first bastardâstealing the supplies and abandoning his coworker. His mind was filled only with: âBastard, bastard, bastard! I donât want to dieeeee!â","But when he turned his head, the zombies were right behind him, almost pressed against his back. Those grayish-green hands were about to claw at his shoulders!","One swipe would leave bloody scratches, and then he would be finished.","In that split second between life and death, what came to Brother Dongâs mind was the moment at the door just now: cold air rushing against him from the front, hot air billowing behind him, the two vastly different currents of air colliding, merging, seeping into one another, winding together.","Why he thought of that, he neither knew nor understood. But something in the part of his mind that had been pricking with pain on and off since yesterday suddenly burst open!","In that instant, he looked back and saw a zombieâs claws closing in on the tip of his nose.","Then he turned forward again. Following his will, he slashed through the air before him. The air split and churned, forming a current that pushed him from behind.","Brother Dong suddenly felt weightless, as if the floor no longer had any friction. His whole body was seized by the sensation of being propelled forward.","The airflow was pushing him.","Brother Dong shot forward with a whoosh!","Another wind-type ability user.","Guo Jun was actually hiding on the bottom shelf of a rack. In such a short amount of time, there had been no way he could have climbed any higher.","He gripped a crowbar in his hand, his knees slightly bent.","The first shelf was only as high as a personâs neck, so he had to crouch a little to fit beneath it. Naturally, his head was pressed against the underside of the shelf above.","Only the upper half of his face showed through the piled-up goods.","He watched Brother Dong flee in a desperate panic, zombies chasing behind him. Then, for no apparent reason, it was as if an engine had suddenly started up in his ass, and he shot away?","Guo Jun: â...??â","Guo Jun stared after him for two seconds, then looked backâonly to meet a pair of pitch-black eyes!","A zombie stood in front of the rack, staring at him through the stacked merchandise.","Guo Jun handled it a little better than Brother Dong. He did not scream. Mainly because he was already crouching, with his head pressed against the shelf above. When his body tensed and he instinctively tried to jump up, the upper shelf stopped him.","His natural startled reaction had been interrupted just like that.","And it was a good thing it had!","Without a second thought, Guo Jun jabbed forward with the crowbar, driving it straight into the zombieâs eye socket.","This shallow stab was not enough to kill a zombie. He would have to drive it deeper, straight into the brain, and destroy it.","But at that moment, Guo Junâs desire to survive was so strong that something seemed to spark in his mind with a pop. An electric current sprang from his palm, flashing like a snake as it crawled along the iron crowbar and entered the zombieâs eye socket, seeking out its brain on its own.","The zombie let out a howl.","Guo Jun had never heard a zombie make such a howl before. It sounded... rather painful?","But the howl clearly drew the attention of the other zombies that had lost Brother Dong while chasing him. They turned back and came this way.","Guo Jun took one look and thought, Fuck, he couldnât just stupidly stay here and wait to be surrounded by zombies. He hurriedly shoved aside the large bundles of goods in front of him, stepped over the merchandise and the zombie corpse, and crawled out.","When he opened his palm, currents of electricityâsometimes white, sometimes pale blueâdarted wildly between his hand and arm like little snakes.","And the iron crowbar could conduct electricity!","He still had no idea what was happening, but in this dangerous moment, he could feel his body brimming with a strange, marvelous energy.","Even so, Guo Jun could not take on several zombies alone. He took off running too, shouting as he ran, âFuck your ancestors, Dong Guangchao! Get out here and save meeeee!â","Brother Dong was in much the same state of mind as Guo Jun. He had not figured out what was happening yet, but he could feel the power of his ability.","Once he realized the zombies could not catch him at all, he calmed down considerably.","Hearing Guo Jun call for him at the top of his lungs, he grabbed a crowbar as well, forced open the air currents, and ran toward him.","Guo Jun felt a gust of wind whoosh past him. The zombies behind him all tumbled to the floor.","Brother Dong slowed down, turned his head, and shouted, âYou kill themâI canât control it very well yetââ","Unlike Zhou Wang, who had already had time to adapt, adjust, and even improve, Brother Dongâs speed was fast but his control over the airflow was poor. When he had tried to strike while running just now, the airflow had thrown off the crowbarâs aim. He had missed the killing blow, merely knocking the zombies down.","Guo Jun ran several steps to the nearest zombie and drove the crowbar down.","The zombie happened to shift its body, and the crowbar pierced its temple. Blue-white electricity wrapped around its head, and within seconds, its brain was fried.","The zombie died.","Another zombie got up. It looked like a second-generation one.","Having killed two zombies in a row, Guo Junâs confidence soared. He tightened his grip on the crowbar, ready to face this second-generation zombie.","The second-generation zombie sprang into the air and pounced at Guo Jun. Brother Dong swept over like a gust of wind again, smacking it out of the air with one blow of his crowbar before running off again.","Brother Dong had figured something out: it was easier to control when he kept running without stopping than when he ran, stopped, then ran again. Not only did this save the airflow the initial effort of starting up, it also maintained its strength and made it increasingly smoother to control.","So he would rather run circles around the shelves than stop.","âKill it! Kill it!â he shouted.","Guo Jun was delighted. He rushed forward and jabbed the crowbar into the zombieâs ear. Electricity crackled and sizzled as it slipped into the ear canal.","Whenever their brains were attacked, these zombies howled. Clearly, they could feel pain.","It died within seconds. This took far less effort and was much more efficient than battering them violently with a crowbar.","The last few zombies were finally dead, and Brother Dong stopped at last. He stood beside Guo Jun, both of them with their hands on their hips, staring at each other in bewilderment.","Brother Dong asked, âWhat was that?â","Guo Jun raised a hand. Blue-white light flickered constantly, winding around his palm.","âElectricity,â Guo Jun said with absolute certainty.","Then he asked, âWhat happened to you? Did you turn into the Flash?â","Brother Dong held up his crowbar and made a pushing motion with both hands. âThe wind was pushing me from behind!â","With that, the two of them went back to staring at each other.","âWhatâs going on?â","âHow should I know?â","A cacophony of noise came from outside. The two of them jumped, and Brother Dong shot off to investigate.","Guo Jun couldnât help marveling. That sure was convenient.","Outside, zombies were surging toward the checkout counters in a great wave. Before long, the sounds of fighting rang out.","It turned out to be Jiang Cheng and the others. They had fought their way in.","âSheâs here. She really came.â","Even after gaining a superpower and becoming much stronger than before, Guo Jun was still so moved that his vision blurred with tears.","The two of them had superpowers now, but they had no armor.","Seeing that there were quite a few fighters outside, all of them wearing armor, the two men stood just inside the storeroom door with their crowbars in hand, peering out through the half-open doorway.","Brother Dong had been hiding in a courtyard in the rural outskirts. There were few people and few zombies in that area, and by the time the government called on everyone to mobilize, there werenât many zombies left nearby.","This was the first time Brother Dong had ever witnessed a human battle against zombies on such a large scale.","There were teams of three or four, and some even had five members. Why were several elderly men and women mixed in?","Huh. Those old men and women were pretty capable.","Whoa, they were even working together? And coordinating quite well, too. One person lured the zombie, another defended, and a third attacked. In just a few moves, they harvested a zombieâclean and efficient!","Brother Dong considered himself a man who valued his life and was rather selfish, yet watching this, he couldnât help feeling his blood heat up.","People really were products of their environment.","Wait. What was that?","Brother Dong quickly nudged Guo Jun. âLook!â","Two U-shaped forks pinned down a zombie. A young man stepped forward, spread both hands, and aimed them at the zombieâs eyes from a distance, as if casting a spell.","Thin white currents of electricity crackled as they tried to pierce the air. But the distance was a little too great, so the man had to stretch his hands farther and farther forward until he finally found the range at which the current could pass through.","It was probably less than fifteen centimetersâcertainly no more than twenty. At that distance, the white electricity pierced the air and struck the zombie in the eye sockets. The zombie let out a howl. After screaming for a while, it finally died.","The young man beamed. âI did it!â","Brother Dong and Guo Jun stood there with their mouths hanging open.","What they had seen was completely unexpected.","First of all, Guo Jun wasnât the only person with this kind of ability. There might even be quite a few others.","Then Brother Dong nudged Guo Jun with his elbow and asked, âWhyâs he doing it like that? Why doesnât he do it the way you do?â","He used the crowbar in his hand to imitate Guo Jun, making repeated jabbing motions.","Guo Jun couldnât understand it either.","Iron conducts electricity. Why not just stab the zombie with an iron rod?","What on earth was he doing? Look at himâhis forehead was covered in a fine sheen of sweat, gleaming under the supermarket lights.","Guo Jun had no idea that Gao Yuxuan had suffered from being too well educated.","Gao Yuxuan especially loved foreign movies. He had watched countless films, and in all the foreign science-fiction movies he had seen, every superpowerâwhether it involved metal, wood, water, fire, earth, wind, thunder, electricity, or anything elseâwas used from a distance.","It made for a much more dramatic shot, with special effects turned up to the max.","As a result, Gao Yuxuanâs subconscious mind was firmly convinced that superpowers were supposed to be used from a distance.","Guo Jun watched as they brought over another zombie to try again.","He could stand it no longer and stepped outside. âHey, hey!â","Gao Yuxuan was in the middle of unleashing electricity with both hands when Master Guo suddenly appeared in front of him.","Gao Yuxuan was delighted to see him. âMaster Guo, youâre all right.â","The two of them were actually fairly familiar with each other. During the disaster, Gao Yuxuan had often volunteered to help people repair their electrical wiring.","That was why Aunt Pan had assumed he was an electrician.","âIâm fine.â Guo Jun asked, âBut why donât you do it like this?â","He raised a hand. The other end of his crowbar pressed against the zombieâs head.","After a few crackles, blue-and-white electricity rapidly coiled around the zombie. The zombie howled for only a few seconds before dropping dead.","It was several times more efficient than Gao Yuxuanâs attempt.","Gao Yuxuan: ââ¦â","Only then did Gao Yuxuan realize that science-fiction movies had led him astray.","Aunt Pan and Zhao Yi were nearby, and they had both seen Guo Jun use his electrical superpower.","Aunt Panâs booming voice rang out. âSee? I told youâthe electricianâs power is electricity!â","Gao Yuxuan: ââ¦â","Although Iâm not an electrician, Big Sis, you may have actually discovered the connection."]},{"number":103,"title":"Chapter 103: 0103","paragraphs":["That said, Gao Yuxuanâs âlong-distance energy projectionâ wasnât completely wrong. It was just that his superpower hadnât reached that level yet.","The security guard Cao Jiacaiâs fire-based superpower had been leagues ahead of Wu Jianchengâs right from the start, so Wu Jiancheng couldnât help keeping an eye on him.","After the second outbreak of the zombie virus, the property management company had ten survivors in total:","Manager Wang, Yang Xinyan, Aunt Pan, two cleaners, and five security guards, including Cao Jiacai and Little Fang.","There werenât many of them, but their rate of superpower awakening was remarkably high:","Aunt Pan had an earth-based ability.","Cao Jiacai had a fire-based ability.","Of the other security guards, one had an earth-based ability and another had a metal-based ability.","Four of the ten were superpowered.","Of course, it was inaccurate to discuss the rate of superpower awakenings by dividing people into groups such as âproperty ownersâ and âproperty management employees.â","The virus didnât care whether someone owned an apartment here or worked here.","Compared with the property owner Wu Jiancheng, the security guard Cao Jiacaiâs superpower was crushingly stronger.","Moreover, unlike Gao Yuxuan, who was mentally trapped by one particular idea, Cao Jiacai had continuously tested his powers ever since awakening them. Eventually, he discovered that flames could travel through wood.","His original weapon had been something similar to a police baton, supplied by the property management company. It was probably made of plastic, because the moment he ran fire through it, it gave off a foul smell.","Then he tried a steel pipe. It conducted electricity, but fire couldnât pass through it.","Finally, he tested a mop handle. The flames traveled from one end to the other in an instant!","He had found the right material!","His current weapon was a mop handle with the mop head removed.","As the saying went, âThe longer the weapon, the stronger the advantage.â When a zombie lunged at him with its bloody maw wide open, he thrust the long stick straight into its mouth. Not only did it serve the same blocking and distancing function as a U-shaped fork, but the flames rising from his hand instantly formed a fireball and shot down the wooden shaft into the zombieâs mouth.","The zombie howled as flames poured from its eye sockets, ears, nostrils, and mouth.","Before long, its brain had been cooked through, and it dropped dead.","Wu Jiancheng: ââ¦â","Wu Jiancheng searched all over the supermarket for a mop!","Unfortunately, an entire row of them consisted of modern plastic mops.","After circling around to the back of the shelves, he finally found some traditional mops. He used scissors and pliers to remove the mop heads.","In the end, he was left with a bare wooden stick. He tried it out, and the flames passed through with remarkable easeâsmoothly, just like electricity through a wire or water through a pipe.","Wu Jiancheng abandoned his steel pipe and used the wooden stick in combination with his fire-based superpower to kill two zombies in a row. He was feeling delighted when he turned aroundâ","Cao Jiacai had advanced again.","Cao Jiacai pointed his long wooden stick at a running zombie. Although there was still some distance between them, he sent out a fireball.","The fireball traveled along the wooden stick like a plane taxiing down a runway. The instant it left the stick, it actually accelerated!","With a bang, the fireball shot into the zombieâs mouth. After all, zombies were always running around with their mouths hanging open, making for a clear and convenient target.","Of course, Cao Jiacaiâs aim was also exceptionally good.","But this was exactly the long-distance energy projection Gao Yuxuan had exhausted himself trying to achieve.","Wu Jiancheng turned around and decided to give it a try as well. After fighting for so long, the fireballs he could produce were already larger than those from yesterday and that morning. When he tested whether he could project one through the air, the fireball did manage to leave the stickâbut the moment it broke free, it visibly shrank.","Wu Jiancheng pushed his superpower as hard as he could. A needle-like pain throbbed through his head.","He glanced over at Cao Jiacai. Why did Cao Jiacai look so relaxed?","Cao Jiacai had begun to feel that the long stick was a bit cumbersome.","He went and swapped it for a rolling pin.","The shorter stick really was more convenient. Cao Jiacai thrust it out, and a fireball flew away. He thrust it out again, and another fireball flew away.","He looked just like a wizard from a foreign movie.","Guo Jun/Gao Yuxuan: ââ¦â","The two electric-type ability users exchanged glances and began experimenting in perfect tacit understanding.","Once again, Guo Jun came out ahead of Gao Yuxuan. Instead of condensing into a ball like fire, his blue-white current crackled outward from the pointed end of the crowbar.","He could even control its shapeâstretching it into a line to reach as far as possible, or spreading it into a net like a shield.","Gao Yuxuan was far behind. The electricity he could release from the end of his steel pipe reached a much shorter distance.","Then he discovered something. âWhy is yours a different color from mine? Have you measured the voltage?â","Guo Jun said, âIf I had time to measure the voltage, Iâd rather use it to find a bathroom.â","He had been holding it in for a day and a night.","Gao Yuxuan carried a voltage tester with him, so he immediately pulled it out and took a reading.","âDamn, 110 volts!â","No wonder the color was different. Gao Yuxuan had been practicing all morning and had only reached sixty or seventy volts.","âHow long ago did your superpower awaken?â Gao Yuxuan asked unwillingly.","Guo Jun thought for a moment. âI donât know. Has it even been half an hour?â","Gao Yuxuan: ââ¦â","Gao Yuxuan was determined to find the underlying pattern!","That was precisely what he and Zhao Yi had been researching!","By this point, there werenât many zombies left inside the supermarket.","The moment Mo Li saw Jiang Cheng enter, he went over to find her. Through their telepathic link, he told her: âPeople. People.â","Jiang Cheng led the others behind Mo Li. They killed the zombies and rescued two people from an office.","Mo Li: âPeople.â","Jiang Cheng followed him again and rescued someone trapped in a restroom.","Mai Duoduo was a large supermarket with plenty of space. The group rescued more than a dozen survivors from various locations.","Several of those rescues had been guided by Mo Li.","Song Jingshuo praised him as well. âThis cat is remarkably intelligent.â","By then, only a handful of zombies remained. Everyone had deliberately left them alive so the superpowered people could practice.","Whenever Cao Jiacai fired a single fireball, he was rewarded with a round of cheers.","Zhao Yi sighed to Aunt Pan, âIndoor combat really isnât favorable for earth-based abilities.â","There was hardly any earth indoors. The floor was concrete.","Aunt Pan said, âIs that so?â","She squatted down and placed a hand on the ground.","The others used their weapons to drive a zombie toward them.","Eventually, they discovered the third-generation zombie hiding among the others. This one had developed intelligence. Surrounded and driven forward by the group, it turned around and saw Zhao Yi and Aunt Pan standing motionless nearby.","The third-generation zombie charged toward them.","Zhao Yi tightened his grip on the steel pipe, preparing to fight. He was a little nervous. During the previous disaster, he had been responsible for all sorts of miscellaneous tasks, so Jiang Cheng had kept him in the rear to handle logistics. He had very little frontline combat experience.","Suddenly, Aunt Pan let out a furious shout.","With that shout, the concrete floor instantly thrust upward into a stone-spire-like shape.","It happened to trip the third-generation zombie, which fell flat on its face and slid straight to Zhao Yiâs feet.","Zhao Yi: ââ¦â","Someone shouted, âHit it!â","Zhao Yi scrambled through a flurry of movements and finally beat the zombie to death.","Aunt Pan stood up and agreed with Zhao Yiâs earlier assessment. âYouâre right. Fighting indoors really isnât ideal for us. Weâre better off outside.â","Zhao Yi: ââ¦â","Aunt Pan said, âI was trying to make a ground spike and impale it in one go. Look at what you managed to make.â","Some rural farmers installed ground spikes or animal traps to defend against wild animals.","Zhao Yi now felt as though the entire world was against him.","He had already tried it when they first entered the supermarket. On a concrete floor, all he could do was barely raise something shaped like a plateâand even that took a tremendous amount of effort.","The inherent hardness of the recipient material would rebound onto the brain of the person using the power. If he pushed too hard, his head would ache terribly. It felt like his nose was about to start bleeding again.","Zhao Yi had already noticed that, when it came to superpowers, college students were utterly defeated by manual laborers.","And both he and Gao Yuxuan were masterâs degree holders!","S City, Guangxiu District, No. 14 Middle School.","The students hiding in the classrooms on the first floor were the first to get their hands on weapons.","The windows on the first floor could be seen from outside, so the children were clever enough to draw all the curtains. After barricading both the front and back doors, they sat along the walls beneath the windows. When night came, they simply lay there and fell asleep.","The next day, they heard all kinds of sounds outside. Shadows of zombies kept passing back and forth across the curtains, but no one dared lift them, afraid that the zombies would spot them, smash through the windows, and get inside.","There were zombies in the corridors too. The students had nowhere to run.","After Student Council President Huang Xuetaoâs broadcast, there had been no further word. The children on the first floor waited anxiously.","Then, all of a sudden, someone knocked on the glass.","âIs anyone in there?â","The children felt as though they were hearing the voice of heaven itself. They pulled open the curtains and saw several ninth-graders outside, each of them gasping for breath and carrying a bundle of iron rods.","âOpen the window! We brought you weapons!â","âWeâre going to charge into the school building in a little while! Be brave too. Weâll work together from inside and out and wipe out the zombies in the corridors!â","âDo you have any tape? Here, take some tape. Use your exercise books to make arm guards!â","Every child received an iron rod. It was heavy in their hands, and somehow, that weight filled them with confidence.","Their blood began to race.","âOkay! Weâll do it together!â","No adults remained in No. 14 Middle School. A group of children began saving themselves.","In the corridors, the students faced the head of discipline, tears streaming down their faces.","The man mockingly nicknamed âShit Fattyâ by the students had been savagely torn apart and eaten by the other zombies. His once plump, rounded body was now full of ragged hollows, with white bone and internal organs exposed in places.","Yet the exposed areas had mutated just like his skin. The flesh in the open wounds seemed to have solidified, no longer bleeding or rotting.","He had become one of the zombies.","The students wept.","âDirector Shi, weâre sorry.â","Crying and apologizing, the children raised their weapons and chargedâ¦","The battle lasted until one in the afternoon. The students of No. 14 Middle School reclaimed control of the campus.","Everyone gathered on the athletic field, feeling as though they were in a dream. They had actually killed the zombies and won the battle without any adults to help them.","They hugged one another, cried, and celebrated.","But what were they supposed to do next?","Someone was the first to suggest, âLetâs go rescue the high school!â","This was the middle school campus of No. 14 Middle School. The high school campus was just one block away.","Whenever special circumstances aroseâfor example, when one of the school buildings or cafeterias was undergoing renovationsâthe two campuses would borrow classrooms and cafeterias from each other.","Besides, sixty percent of the high school students had advanced directly from the middle school.","The suggestion immediately won everyoneâs approval.","When you were young, it was easy to get swept up in the moment. Having just won a battle, they began imagining themselves heroes.","The crowd grew excited, and everyone unanimously decided to go rescue the high school!","Little Huang, however, decided to drop out.","âIâm sorry, but my father is already gone, and my mother only has me. I have to go save her.â","âGood luck, everyone.â","The middle schoolâs self-rescue operation had been led by Senior Huang Xuetao, and the students all trusted him deeply. They were reluctant to see him leave.","Wu Shuchen went so far as to call out, âSenior, wait for me!â","The boy, who looked like an elementary school student, summoned every ounce of his strength. Even as his nose began to bleed, he used his superpower to create a set of iron shoulder armor modeled after an adultâs protective gear for Senior Huang Xuetao.","It protected his shoulders, the back of his neck, and his ears, guarding against a sudden zombie attack.","Although Senior Huang possessed the ability to sense danger, if he was going to save his mother, he couldnât simply avoid every threat. He could only charge straight into danger.","Little Huangâs eyes grew a little sore.","He was reluctant to leave his classmates too. But he also knew that he wasnât a superhero. Their strength lay in their unity and courage, not in whether he was the one leading them.","His classmates helped him put on the shoulder armor. Someone even donated a shoelace to fasten it securely.","They escorted him to the bicycle shelter.","Little Huang swung onto his bicycle and tucked the iron rod, stained with zombie blood, behind his waist. He looked back at everyone.","âGoodbye,â he said. âTake care.â","Who would have thought that, at their age, they would already be saying words like those?","Who could predict what fate had in store?","Some of the students began to cry.","âYou take care too!â","They watched Little Huang ride away. Once they had wiped away their tears, the children who had just finished crying shouted, âLetâs go! To the high school!â","With exercise books strapped around their arms and iron rods clenched in their hands, the children bravely walked out of the campus. Along the way, they killed the zombies in the streets.","They had not even made it out of the block when they encountered a group of high school students coming toward them.","Both sides were stunned.","The high school students asked, âWhat are you doing?â","The middle school students replied, âWe were coming to rescue you! What are you doing?â","âWe came to rescue you!â","The high school campus was in much better shape than the middle school.","Many high school girls were even a head and a half taller than a first-year middle school boy like Wu Shuchen. High school studentsâ bodies had already developed to nearly adult proportions. In fact, for many people, high school was the physical peak of their entire lives.","The high schoolâs self-rescue effort had begun with the baseball team.","Because there was a baseball team, there were baseball batsâand those bats became the first weapons used in their rescue operation.","Then, one superpower after another awakened. The students quickly figured out how to improve and use their abilities, putting them into battle.","Thanks to that fighting strength, several of the high schoolâs teachers had survived. They even had adults on their side.","The older students and younger students met halfway, finding one another as if they were long-lost family. They cried and laughed together.","Many of the high school girls looked at the first-year middle school students as though they were adorable little chicks.","It was enough to break their hearts.","The teachers asked, âHave you eaten? Do you have anything to eat?â","Only then did the middle school students realize that they were so hungry their stomachs hurt. The high school students didnât know whether to laugh or cry.","âCome on, letâs go to the high school.â","âOur cafeteria aunties are still here. Theyâre cooking right now!â","âCome on, weâll go eat together!â"]},{"number":104,"title":"Chapter 104: 0104","paragraphs":["No. 14 Middle School was in Guangxiu District, about an hour to an hour and twenty minutes away from the High-Tech New District by bicycle.","It was quite a distance, and biking there was tiring.","But Old Huang and his wife had always made sure Little Huang exercised in every way, not just focusing on his grades. So they never drove him to and from school, and had always made him ride his bicycle himself.","Little Huang said goodbye to his classmates and left the school. Relying on his âdanger perceptionâ ability, he avoided the Second-Generation Zombies along the way, sticking to roads with either no zombies or only Primitive Zombies.","From time to time, he heard people opening windows in nearby buildings and shouting for help. He didnât stop.","People had to save themselves, or rely on the people closest to them, or rely on the country.","Strangers simply no longer had the strength to help.","Several times, he sensed intense danger, as if he were being watched.","He didnât know that a Third-Generation Zombie had spotted him from afar.","There had been discussions about âzombies evolvingâ on the Young Residence ownersâ forum, but after the disaster ended, he had stopped following the forum. He had no understanding of Third-Generation Zombies and had no idea they even existed.","When he reached a stretch of road without zombies and sensed no danger, he spotted a public phone booth by the roadside.","He stopped, fished some coins out of his schoolbag, and used the public phone to dial his motherâs cellphone number.","No one answered.","He called her work landline.","Still, no one answered.","Then he called the landline at home.","Over the past two years, many people had gotten rid of their landlines. But because of Old Huangâs job, their family had kept theirs.","He kept praying that his mother had already saved herself, been rescued, or made it home.","But the phone rang many times without anyone answering.","At last, Little Huang hung up. He didnât even retrieve the coin that had been returned, but mounted his bicycle again and sped toward the High-Tech New District.","Under the blazing sun, the boyâs bicycle shot forward like an arrow released from a bow.","High-Tech New District, Maiduo Supermarket.","By the time the fighting ended, it was already past three oâclock.","Not only had they successfully rescued Master Guo, they had also picked up Brother Dong as an extra bonus.","Because Guo Jun later joined the Young Residence community and built up an excellent and extensive network of friends there, Brother Dongâs story became a legend in the community.","Previously, most of the ordinary residents had only been focused on grabbing supplies during their two visits and had never noticed this junior manager among Maiduoâs dozen-plus employees.","This time, they finally got to meet the legendary figure.","When Brother Dong saw Jiang Cheng and the others again, he couldnât help feeling awkward. He greeted them with an ingratiating smile.","âLong time no see. Everyoneâs doing pretty well, huh? Hahaâ¦ ah, hahaâ¦â","The laughter toward the end sounded rather forced.","Everyone was speechless.","Jiang Cheng said mildly, âItâs all right now. You can go home.â","Many people turned their faces away, afraid they would burst out laughing.","Brother Dongâs mouth twitched.","He had known from the first time he met this young girl that she was no pushover.","Fortunately, Brother Dong had a very thick skin. Pretending not to understand the hint, he stated his request directly.","âGoing home is a little dangerous. Iâd like to stay and observe the situation for a few more days before leaving. I heard from Guo Jun that heâs living in your community now and working for you. Iâm pretty good at working too.â","Afraid of being rejected again and not wanting to give Jiang Cheng a chance to interrupt, he quickly laid out his terms.","âI also have a superpower. Iâm incredibly powerful now.â","Jiang Cheng raised an eyebrow. âWhatâs your superpower?â","Brother Dong replied, âI can run really fastâwhoosh! Iâm as fast as the wind. Zombies canât catch me.â","âOh, another wind-type,â Gao Yuxuan said. Then he looked at Guo Jun.","Guo Jun nodded. âItâs true. Heâs extremely fast.â","After hearing Guo Junâs confirmation, Jiang Cheng nodded as well. Brother Dong thought she had agreed to let him stay, but then she turned around and shouted, âBrother Zhou! Brother Zhou!â","Zhou Wang had pushed a ladder over and climbed up to retrieve his ebony rolling pin from the top of the shelves.","Li Jiangbing and Zhao Yi were holding the ladder steady below him.","Li Jiangbing asked in confusion, âHow did it end up there?â","As Zhou Wang climbed, he explained what had happened.","Zhao Yi said, âThat ability of yours isnât suited for using this weapon. Your arms arenât strong enough, and they canât withstand the recoil. Youâd better switch to a knifeâthe sharper, the better. With one whoosh, a head would go flying.â","Zhou Wang thought about it, then agreed. âYouâre right.â","Li Jiangbing imagined the scene. It was straight out of a martial arts movieâso cool.","Li Jiangbing was green with envy.","That afternoonâs operation had not only rescued Guo Jun and cleared out Maiduo Supermarket, but had also allowed the superpowered individuals to test and hone their abilities.","People like Gao Yuxuan, Zhou Wang, and Wu Jiancheng had all made breakthroughs or at least significant progress that afternoon. Many had figured out more effective ways to use their powers.","It had been an extremely fruitful operation.","Only Li Jiangbing was disappointed.","Because he had a water-type superpower, he had deliberately chosen to fight in the seafood section, among the glass fish tanks.","He really could control a larger amount of water and condense larger water spheres now, but actual combat had proven that his ability was useless against zombies.","He could even condense water shields and water arrows, but water had neither offensive power nor defensive strength. The moment it collided with another solid object, it shattered.","He had also tried, like the electric- and fire-type users, to pour water into the zombiesâ brains. But he soon discovered that it had no effect.","A zombieâs brain would not âdieâ simply because it was soaked in water. Fire and electricity were different: one cooked the brain, while the other electrocuted it, both rendering the zombieâs brain completely inactive.","In short, the dayâs experiments had established that a water-type superpower was useless against zombies.","Li Jiangbing was utterly devastated.","Zhou Wang had just retrieved his rolling pin when he heard Jiang Cheng calling for him.","âBrother Zhouââ","Zhou Wang called back, âComing! Iâm over here. Hang on a second.â","He climbed down backward, thanked Zhao Yi and Li Jiangbing, and then, gripping the rolling pin, vanished with a whoosh.","Li Jiangbing: Iâm tired of saying how envious I am.","When Li Jiangbing turned his head, he saw Su Yu sitting on the floor with her back against a shelf. Her face was deathly pale, and there was still blood on it that she hadnât wiped away. She looked nauseated, as though she might throw up at any moment.","Li Jiangbing took a bottle of mineral water, unscrewed the cap, and handed it to her.","âYou all right?â","Su Yu took two sips to settle her stomach and waved a hand, indicating that she was fine.","She couldnât even speak anymore. It was obvious that she had overused her superpower.","The blood on her face was clearly from a nosebleed that she had smeared across her skin.","Li Jiangbing sighed. âTake it easy. Donât push yourself so hard.â","Su Yu took several more gulps before she could finally speak.","âItâs not easy to get an ability that can help everyone,â she said. âBesides, you served in the militia for so many days back then. You didnât come back until the militia was disbanded, did you?â","That was why she believed Li Jiangbing would understand her.","The side effects she was suffering from were merely the result of practicing her superpower too intenselyâlike feeling sick after overexerting herself.","Compared with the risks Li Jiangbing had faced when he went into dangerous areas with the militia to kill zombies, this was much safer.","Li Jiangbing could indeed understand her.","He put his hands on his hips and asked, âSo? Howâs your protective barrier?â","A faint smile appeared on Su Yuâs pale face. She looked so weak, yet so happy.","âThe radius is almost a meter now.â She was genuinely delighted. âWith everyone pressed close together, eight or nine people could squeeze inâmaybe even ten.â","âIt held at this radius for a full seven minutes.â","Compared with yesterday, when her superpower had first awakened, her current ability was worlds apart.","She had improved tremendously.","But Li Jiangbing still thought her face looked far too pale. Besides, no one else had pushed themselves to the point of getting a nosebleed. She was the only one bleeding.","Although he understood and admired her, he still cautioned her, âTake it easy. Thereâs a limit to what the human body can endure.â","That was something their fitness trainer often said to clients. A trainer had to know where to draw the line. If they ran into one who didnât, they might work a new client so hard they developed rhabdomyolysis, which could easily lead to serious trouble.","Su Yu smiled at him, then lowered her head. Li Jiangbing assumed she was too tired to talk and walked away.","Su Yu looked up at his retreating back.","Although Li Jiangbing was an extremely reliable partner in her eyes, she didnât want to tell anyone that her protective shield was somewhat different from other superpowers.","When the shield was nearing its limit and beginning to weaken, the zombiesâ attacks against it would hit her brain with tremendous force.","As far as she could tell, no one else experienced anything like that.","It was a weakness of the shield, and she didnât want anyone to know about it.","Nearby, several people had gathered and were talking.","Someone had finally awakened a superpower during the battle just now, and the others were congratulating the new superpowered individual.","After todayâs battle, everyone had realized that although superpowers were weak when first awakened, they could be trained and would gradually grow stronger.","Metal, fire, electricity, and wind had all displayed powerful offensive potential in battle. Earth was somewhat weaker, but it was clear that, in the future, it would be an ability capable of both offense and defense.","Water had been proven unsuitable for combat. Wood had not shown what it could do today.","In any case, as long as someone possessed anything other than water or wood, their chances of survival immediately increased by a great deal.","Superpowers had become something everyone wanted.","Zhou Wang came hurrying over to Jiang Cheng. âHeâs here!â","Brother Dong recognized that he was a wind-type user as well. âHey!â","âI found someone with the same type of superpower as yours,â Jiang Cheng said. âYou two can talk.â","Zhou Wang looked at Brother Dong. âYou look familiar.â","âWeâve met, weâve met,â Brother Dong said. âI remember you. Back then, when we said we werenât doing business anymore, you insisted on coming in to buy things.â","Zhou Wang suddenly remembered. âOh, you worked at Duoduo.â","âYou two chat. Iâm leaving.â Jiang Cheng turned to go, then remembered something. âOh, right. He doesnât have anywhere to live at the moment. See if you can find him an empty apartment in your residential complex.â","Every residential complex had empty apartmentsâmany belonged to families who had all died.","But after dealing with Jiang Cheng so many times, Zhou Wang knew her quite well.","This wasnât like Jiang Cheng at all.","This man was a wind-type user, and he had already proven today that wind was an extremely useful superpower.","Given Jiang Chengâs personality, why would she so casually hand such a useful superpowered person over to him instead of bringing him under her own wing?","Zhou Wang suddenly remembered a conversation he had overheard elsewhere earlier.","âIs that the âBrother Dongâ guy?â","âYeah, yeah, I think thatâs him.â","âThe guy who abandoned Master Guo and more than a dozen of his coworkers, then ran off with a load of everyoneâs supplies?â","âHahaha, yeah, thatâs him.â","âWhatâs he doing here? He actually has the nerve to come back to work?â","âI heard from Gao Yuxuan that he came back to settle his wages.â","âHoly crap, hahaha!â","âRight? Hahahahaha!â","Zhou Wang asked, âWhatâs your surname?â","Brother Dong was very polite to the person who might provide him with temporary lodging. âMy surname is Dong.â","Just as he thought!","Jiang Cheng had already turned and walked away.","Zhou Wang glanced at her back, the corner of his mouth twitching despite himself."]},{"number":105,"title":"Chapter 105: 0105","paragraphs":["Jiang Cheng walked past several aisles without seeing Song Jingshuo, but fortunately, she spotted Li Jiangbing.","She gave him a meaningful glance, and he immediately came over to follow her.","They were so perfectly in sync.","Li Jiangbing even lowered his voice when he spoke. âWhatâs up?â","âCandles, lighters, and quilts,â Jiang Cheng said.","âHuh?â","Jiang Chengâs superpower was her storage space. Since she was here, she naturally had to take something with her. There was no way sheâd come all this way and leave empty-handed.","But Li Jiangbing hadnât expected her to want these things. He asked in confusion, âShouldnât we be taking rice, grain, and meat?â","âItâs different now,â Jiang Cheng said. âThis time is different.â","In fact, some people had already begun pushing shopping carts around and loading things into them. Since they had come all this way, they might as well take something. No thief ever left empty-handed.","Jiang Cheng found the candles and lighters.","Li Jiangbing watched with his own eyes as she reached out and touched them. The items vanished instantly.","Jiang Cheng frowned.","Li Jiangbing hurriedly asked, âWhatâs wrong?â","âThe candles are surprisingly heavy,â Jiang Cheng said.","They were heavy because of their mass. Her storage space wasnât limited by an itemâs shape. The amount it could hold was determined by weight.","Simply put, it was a matter of how much it could bear.","Jiang Cheng didnât take everything. She left some behind.","Li Jiangbing had already realized that Jiang Cheng always left others some leeway. She wouldnât drive people who werenât her enemies into desperate straits.","But the cleaner who had led the strike at their residential compoundâthe one whose name was Liu somethingâbelonged to the opposing side. Jiang Cheng had left that kind of person not the slightest bit of room.","Li Jiangbing especially liked Jiang Chengâs way of doing things.","Perhaps, at the beginning, he had only realized that Jiang Cheng was quick-witted and could rapidly become the core of any group, so he had wanted to cling to her.","But later on, he had genuinely come to like her and sincerely wanted to be her partner.","Song Jingshuo must have felt the same way.","Seeing that many people had started pushing shopping carts around to gather supplies, Jiang Cheng didnât go to the bedding section. Instead, she led Li Jiangbing straight to the warehouse.","Fortunately, the warehouse shelves also had clear labels. The two of them followed the signs until they found what they were looking for.","Aside from several zombie corpses, there was no one else in the warehouse. Jiang Cheng explained to Li Jiangbing, âIâm worried that this time, we wonât be able to count on water, electricity, gas, or heating.â","Li Jiangbing froze, then hesitantly said, âThat canât be, can it? Last timeâ¦â","âI told you, this time is different from last time.â Jiang Cheng looked at him. âJiangbing, how many people were there in our residential compound last time? How many are there now? How many people were in Jixiang Jiayuan last time? How many are there now?â","âTry applying that same ratio to the government and the military.â","Li Jiangbing took a moment to process her words. Cold sweat began to bead on his forehead.","When Li Jiangbing had served in the militia, regular active-duty soldiers had been in charge of his unit. He had gotten quite familiar with them.","He had learned that even those soldiers and officers didnât know exactly how many people the military had lost at the time. The authorities had never released any figures.","One could say that the losses simply hadnât been the focus back then. But, looking at it another way, it was also possible that the losses had been so devastating that the government had decided not to disclose them because of the impact and other political considerations.","An officer he had been close to had once explained that whenever a major natural disaster occurred within the country, the military would enter a state of top-level combat readiness, to prevent foreign powers from taking advantage of the situation and invading.","It was entirely possible that the losses had been so severe that the figures were being kept secret out of fear that foreign forces would start coveting the country.","After that, the country had resumed work and production. It had only been a little over a month since then, and the nation hadnât had time to recruit and replenish its forces.","Under these circumstances, the military had suffered another devastating blow.","As for the governmentâ¦ Just look at Jixiang Jiayuan. None of the people who had gone to work had returned!","Werenât government workers also people who worked in government offices?","âLast time, the formal rescue operations didnât begin until Wednesday,â Jiang Cheng said. âBut that doesnât mean the government did nothing on Sunday, Monday, and Tuesday. In fact, it should have begun taking action on Sunday. Otherwise, how could we have continued to receive water, electricity, gas, and communications?â","âBut all of that depended on the government still existing.â","âVice Mayor Zheng, Mayor Sun, and the others survived at home over the weekend. Then they gathered together and formed a new temporary government, taking on the responsibility of leading everyone. Thatâs what made everything that followed possible.â","âHow many government officials survived this time? Can they even establish a temporary government?â","Li Jiangbingâs footsteps grew heavy.","He truly felt that he wasnât suited to think about such things. Not only did they give him a headache, they also easily made him panic.","In the end, Li Jiangbing made his choice.","âYou just need to tell me what you want me to do. Whatever you tell me to do, Iâll do.â","That would certainly make things easier!","He absolutely didnât want to be made responsible for thinking about these matters!","This time, it was Jiang Chengâs turn to sigh.","âMy storage space is too small,â she said. âActually, there are ways to deal with everything else. What worries me most is winter.â","If everything went as she expected, then it wouldnât just be the water, electricity, and gas supplies that failed. The most important thing they would need in winter was heating.","They followed the signs and found the bedding section.","The warehouse was filled with large packages. Many of them were enclosed in wooden crates. That was why Master Guo and Brother Dong had been able to obtain crowbars in the warehouse.","The crates were heavy too, and using them would waste precious space. Jiang Cheng pointed at one of them. âTake this apart.â","Li Jiangbing turned around without a word, found a crowbar, and immediately began prying the crate apart with loud cracking sounds.","They only needed to open a gap large enough for Jiang Cheng to reach her hand inside.","The quilts were packed one bundle after another. As long as Jiang Cheng touched a single bundle, she could empty the entire crate into her storage space in an instant.","It was incredibly convenient. Jiang Cheng even found time to joke with Li Jiangbing.","âWhich is heavier, a pound of cotton or a pound of iron?â","Li Jiangbing looked at her as though she were an idiot. âDo you really need to ask?â","He replied with absolute certainty, âIron, of course! Iâve never heard of cotton being heavier than iron!â","Jiang Cheng was speechless.","Fine, then.","There were all kinds of quilts: soybean-fiber quilts, wool quilts, down quilts, and so on. Some were advertised as seven-hole quilts, others as nine-hole quilts.","Jiang Cheng didnât bother distinguishing between them. She shoved every last one into her storage space.","Although the quilts took up a lot of room, they didnât weigh much. In the end, Jiang Cheng managed to store far more than she had expected. It was a pleasant surprise.","âLetâs go.â After filling her storage space to capacityâand then cramming in a little moreâJiang Cheng led Li Jiangbing out of the warehouse.","Outside, the place had become a shopping frenzy.","Ever since the previous disaster, people across the country had apparently developed a hoarding disorder. It was probably a form of post-traumatic stress disorder caused by the last zombie disaster.","So this time, there was far less urgency when it came to gathering supplies.","Everyone was mainly discussing how to divide up the fresh fruits and vegetables from Mai Duoduo. There was also fresh meat. These were the things that would rot in a few days if they werenât taken away today.","Master Guo said there was still plenty of frozen meat, fish, shrimp, and other food in the cold-storage rooms. They could deal with those later. For today, they would focus on the fresh food.","Song Jingshuo was in the plant section with Aunt Pan and two other aunties who possessed wood-type abilities.","The potted plants here were mainly succulents, money trees, cacti, kalanchoes, mint, and similar varieties.","For Song Jingshuo and the others, the truly valuable items were the potted strawberries and cherry tomatoes.","Apart from those, there were seedsâvegetable seeds.","âTake them all, take them all!â the aunties urged. âAfter all, there are only three of us with wood-type abilities.â","Aunt Pan reminded them, âYou should take all the fresh fruits and vegetables too. Take them back and see what you can do with them.â","Because many plants donât necessarily need seeds.","Song Jingshuo wore a stony expression from start to finish.","There was no changing the attributes of the superpowers Heaven had given them, but accepting his fate didnât mean he had to be happy about it.","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan came over and squeezed Song Jingshuo aside, gathering around the aunties to chat with them. âWhat kind of work did you do? Are you in good health? How did you end up with a wood-type ability? Do you have any idea why?â","The aunties had been looked down on when everyone was divided into teams. But later, everyone discovered that the uncles and aunties led by Zhou Wang werenât actually that weak.","Of course, they werenât strong either, but they hadnât held anyone back. They were simply at the level of ordinary, healthy people.","Considering their age, their physical strength could be described as exceptionally good.","When Zhao Yi and the others asked, they confirmed that the two elderly ladies, along with several other seniors who had dared to put on armor and go out to kill zombies, were all the type who did morning exercises in the park and danced in the square at night.","They were the kind of elderly people with more energy than the young.","The aunties exchanged a smile. âOf course thereâs a reason.â","âThe two of us are famous for growing flowers and vegetables.â","âThatâs right. It wouldnât be surprising at all for us to have wood-type abilities. If we didnât have wood-type abilities, then who would?â","âYou young men should come visit our homes when you have time. Youâll see how well our plants grow!â","After interviewing the aunties, Zhao Yi couldnât help glancing at Song Jingshuo several times.","His movements were so obvious that Song Jingshuo no longer had the patience for polite small talk. âIf you have something to say, say it.â","Zhao Yi asked, âDo you also like growing flowers and vegetables?â","Song Jingshuo gave him a sinister smile. âWhich strand of my hair makes me look like I do?â","Gao Yuxuan, meanwhile, interviewed Aunt Pan. âSis, youâre from an agricultural household, right? Why do you think you ended up with a earth-type ability instead of a wood-type one? We all think you should have been wood-type.â","âYou just assume that farmers are born wanting to grow crops.â Aunt Pan clearly had no patience for their stereotypical thinking. âIf we liked farming that much, why would we come to the city to work? If farming was so wonderful, why would Old Luo spend money to learn how to be an electrician?â","Farmers were simply born with farmland assigned to them, which naturally tied them to the soil. That didnât mean they were born wanting to farm.","Gao Yuxuan seemed to understand. But then he asked, âWerenât you growing vegetables behind Building Six before?â","That should have meant she liked farming, right?","Aunt Pan said, âThat? The property management company had paid someone to place an order for vegetables. I saw how much money there was to be made and thought, âWhy let outsiders profit from it when I can do it myself?â Who knew the manager wouldnât allow it? He said the residents of Building Six had complained, so they dug everything up.â","So that was how it was. Gao Yuxuan and Zhao Yi had gotten the information they wanted.","In the end, Zhou Wang decided to take Brother Dong in.","After Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan finished interviewing the others, they came over to interview the two of them as well, insisting that they have a race to test their abilities.","At the request of the two âsuperpower researchers,â the pair ran a lap around the supermarket.","Brother Dong won.","Not only was he fast, but he wasnât even breathing hard.","Zhou Wang, on the other hand, was slightly out of breath.","They looked at each other.","One asked, âWhy are you out of breath?â","The other asked, âWhy arenât you?â","Brother Dong said, âWhatâs there to pant about after running such a short distance? My everyday work is more tiring than this.â","He grinned. âYou obviously worked in an office. Look at that belly.â","As he spoke, he gave Zhou Wangâs stomach a slap.","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan watched as Zhou Wangâs protruding beer belly jiggled under the impact.","They felt they had more or less formed a basic profile of the superpowers.","At that moment, Zhou Wangâs phone rang.","It was an unfamiliar number.","But Zhou Wang still answered. His phone number had been posted on the neighborhoodâs residentsâ forum, and many people in Auspicious Garden had his number.","Whenever someone he didnât know called, it showed up as an unfamiliar number.","âHello, this is Zhou Wang.â","The caller was indeed someone from Auspicious Garden. âZhou Wang, this is Longlongâs Grandma. I mean the Longlong from Building Four, not the one from Building One.â","The introduction meant nothing to Zhou Wang.","Whether it was the Longlong from Building One or the one from Building Four, he had no impression of either of them.","But he had received far too many calls like this. All he could do was pinch the bridge of his nose to ease his headache. âPlease just tell me whatâs going on. Iâm busy here.â","Longlongâs Grandma hurriedly said, âWell, Little Huang is back.â","Zhou Wang froze. âLittle Huang? Huang Xuetao?â","Longlongâs Grandma replied, âYes. His mother calls him Little Tao. Iâve heard her.â","Zhou Wang was overcome with surprise and delight. âHeâs still alive!â","For those two months, the boy had been his constant little sidekick, calling him several times a day and coming to see him several times a day.","The more time Zhou Wang spent with him, the more he realized that the boy was a textbook example of âsomeone elseâs perfect child.â Zhou Wang had even told his own child, âYou should be like Brother Little Huang when you grow up.â","After spending so much time with a child like that, it was only natural to grow attached.","Zhou Wang had been delighted for barely a second when Longlongâs Grandma continued, âHe went home, took a kitchen knife, and left again. We asked him what he was going to do, and he said he was going to rescue his mother. Oh dear, how could we let him do that? But he wouldnât listen to us. He got on his bicycle and left. The few of us old folks discussed it and decided weâd better call you.â"]},{"number":106,"title":"Chapter 106: 0106","paragraphs":["Little Huang went home for two reasons.","First, he wanted to see whether his mother had come back.","One look would be enough to make him give up hope.","Second, he needed a weapon. He was only a middle schooler; compared with high school boys and adults, he lacked strength. A blade would serve him better than a blunt weapon like an iron bar.","He took a kitchen knife, got on his bike, and headed for the Development Zone Government offices.","Using his superpower to weave around danger all the way, he avoided every threat and finally arrived at the government building.","The Development Zone Government stood on the edge of the residential district, beside the river. Across the water lay the industrial park.","Little Huang stopped his bike and stood at the entrance. Simply standing there, he could already feel the danger inside.","But just as his junior, Wu Shuchen, had thought: so what if he could sense danger? His mother was in there. Even if it meant crossing mountains of blades and seas of fire, he had to go in.","On his shoulders were makeshift pauldrons Wu Shuchen had created for him through the sheer effort of giving himself a nosebleed. Unfinished workbooks and exercise books were strapped around his arms. A kitchen knife was clenched in his hand.","Little Huang took a deep breath and charged inside.","Huangâs mother worked in the âBureau of Science, Technology, and Industrial Promotionâ within the Development Zone Government.","Little Huang had never been here before. Everything he knew came from bits and pieces he had overheard when his parents talked in the past.","For instance: the third floor; river views outside the windows; the west side of the building. Their department had three offices, and his mother was in Office No. 2.","Armed with only that information, Little Huang stormed into the government building.","There was more than one staircase. Whenever he headed in one direction and sensed danger, he would turn around and choose another route where the feeling of danger was relatively weaker.","Little Huang did not linger to fight zombies. His first priority was not to kill them and clear the building, but to find his mother.","After biking for more than an hour, the conviction that he had to save her drove him to an astonishing burst of stamina.","He was like an ancient cavalryman charging into an enemy formationâdriving forward without pause, never stopping. He swung his knife only to remove whatever stood in his way.","When a zombie snapped at him, he raised an arm to block it. As its teeth clamped down on the workbooks, he slashed out and cut away half its face, kicked it aside, and surged forward through the opening.","As long as humans put on armor and picked up weapons, primitive zombies were basically no longer a threat to their lives.","His superpower, âDanger Sense,â was still useful in combat!","In fact, it was immensely useful.","Before a second-generation zombie even pounced, Little Huang could sense it in advance. Inside a building, that advance warning amounted to only a few secondsâbut a few seconds could save his life.","He had already gotten used to this superpower during the morningâs battle to retake the school. He had adapted to those urgent warnings that came only seconds ahead of time.","But now, inside the Development Zone Government building, Little Huang realized that his ability seemed to be working even better.","Beyond the few seconds of advance warning, his senses could also tell him which direction he needed to dodge in order to avoid an attack.","He just had to move quickly and precisely.","From a third-person perspective, it would look like this: the instant a second-generation zombie sprang toward him, the boy moved at the exact same moment.","In the next instant, the zombie would miss completely.","The boy and the zombie passed one another at nearly shoulder-brushing distance.","The zombie twisted its body to change direction, but the boy had already taken another step, narrowly avoiding yet another zombie.","Inside the government building, packed with zombies, the thin boy moved through them as if by some kind of miracle.","He hacked down the original zombies with his knife and stepped around the second-generation zombies.","If this had been a game, Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan would surely have cried out in astonishment:","âGod-tier footwork!â","Little Huang had no idea that supernatural abilities could be advanced and upgraded. His âdanger perceptionâ ability had in fact evolved to the next level.","It had evolved from âlong-range danger perceptionâ into âclose-range, short-duration micro-movement guidance.â","âClose rangeâ here meant being face-to-face with a zombie, while âshort durationâ meant the instant it took to blink.","This dreamlike, god-tier footwork appeared as effortless as a leisurely stroll, but in reality, every nerve in Little Huangâs body was taut. He did not dare blink for even an instant.","The zombies had no intelligence and could not comprehend his existence. This piece of flesh seemed to be right there, yet whenever they reached or lunged for it, they always came up empty-handed.","But not every attempt missed.","Because of the cramped hallway and the density of the zombies, there was not always a gap between one danger, another danger, and yet another danger.","He had to choose the direction where the danger was relatively lesser and take a step forward, using his iron shoulder guard or workbook to withstand a collision or bite. In the next instant, he would swing his knife and sever the zombieâs neck.","By choosing to eliminate one danger from among countless others, he forced open a path forward where none had existed.","This was micro-control of astonishing precision.","Every muscle in his body had to remain completely taut, ready to move at a momentâs notice.","The rise and fall of his hand and the steps beneath his feet had to fit together perfectly, without even a secondâs error!","Because a second-generation zombie could leap and kill in just one second.","Once, he had to choose between three second-generation zombies. He could only charge straight into one of them. At the instant it pounced, he turned his body slightly and used his shoulder guard for protection. His back slammed against the wall as the zombie bit down on his iron armor, shattering its own teeth.","His cleaver struck its neck, severing it halfway through. Its head lolled to one side, still attached to its shoulder.","Little Huang shoved it away and, without pausing, took a diagonal step forward.","With a bang, another second-generation zombie slammed into the wall where his back had rested a moment before, shattering its own nasal bone and arm.","If Little Huang had been even a fraction of a second late taking that step, the zombie would have pounced on and killed him.","It was through this combination of intense stimulation, extreme risk, and high-precision maneuvering that the hallwayâpreviously blocked by three second-generation zombies and reduced to a dead endâhad begun to reveal a way out.","Little Huang planted one foot forward, then advanced another meter.","The sustained, high-intensity use of this supernatural ability was much like Su Yuâs unbroken effort to maintain her protective shield.","They were unlike those with electrical or fire-based abilities. Each time such people released a bolt of electricity or hurled a fireball, the interval before the next attack counted as rest and recovery.","But abilities like Little Huangâs and Su Yuâs, which required continuous output, allowed no rest at all.","Pain like needles stabbed through his brain, and blood began to trickle from his nose.","Little Huang was getting a nosebleed for the first time, but Wu Shuchen had already told him that it was a side effect of overusing his superpower.","But what else could he do? He was trapped in a building crawling with zombies. He couldnât let his power falter for even a second. The moment it stopped, he would die.","By the time he reached the third floor from the first, his school uniform was soaked through with sweat.","Blood was flowing from his nose and ears.","His throat tasted sweet and metallic.","His eardrums and brain throbbed with a pain like needles stabbing into them.","That morning, he had led his younger schoolmates in a bloody battle against the zombies.","Then he had ridden a bicycle for more than an hour.","And in truth, he hadnât eaten since yesterday afternoon. He had only drunk tap water to quench his thirst.","The boyâs body was already nearing its limit, burning itself out on borrowed strength under the influence of adrenaline.","His eyes hurt, and his vision was blurred.","Little Huang could no longer make out the zombies clearly. All he could sense in his perceptive field were one human-shaped outline after another, each marked as âdangerous.â","Step. Sidestep. Slash.","Little Huang had lost all emotion, including tension, worry, and fear.","He knew he had achieved a miracle.","Since the zombie virus had broken out, had anyone ever heard of a living person making his way alone through a dense mass of zombies?","No. Never.","He was a miracle.","His father and mother would surely be proud of him.","When Little Huang finally saw the sign reading âScience and Industry Promotion Bureau Office 2,â he actually smiled.","A mouthful of blood surged up his throat, and Little Huang forced it back down.","Even so, a trace of blood seeped from the corner of his mouth.","There were four zombies inside Office 2.","Even an ordinary person wearing protective armor couldnât take on four zombies at once. But superpowers gave people a cheat code. Wasnât that exactly why Heaven had granted humanity superpowersâto fight the zombies?","Even after sensing the enormous danger within, Little Huang charged inside.","The zombies from the hallway followed him in.","In the open-plan office, Little Huang darted and shifted, evading attacks by the narrowest margins before countering in an instant.","An immense danger enveloped the entire office. The boyâs life and cells were burning away.","His eyeballs throbbed with pain, and his vision grew hazier.","One. Two. Three.","Kill them. Kill them all!","Office 2 of the Science and Industry Promotion Bureau was the end of Little Huangâs journey.","There was nowhere left to bypass the zombies by weaving around them. Here, he had to kill them, because this was the end!","Kill them. Kill them all!","The cleaverâs edge curled, and every zombie in the office became a corpse on the floor.","All Little Huang could hear was his own breathing. His lungs felt ready to burst, his heart ready to split open. He could collapse at any moment.","But the âdangerâ lingering in the office did not disappear with the deaths of the zombies.","They were not the source of that danger.","Little Huang turned around.","There was another room within the open-plan office.","The directorâs office.","Huangâs mother was the director.","The door to the directorâs office had been left ajar the entire time.","Now it opened, and Huangâs mother stood in the doorway.","She had never come out. She had only watched.","Her gaze was the âdangerâ that had enveloped the office from beginning to end.","Because she was a third-generation zombie.","A tasteful suit. An elegant pinned-up hairstyle. Eyes black from edge to edge, without a trace of white. Skin tinted blue-green.","Little Huang had found his mother, just as he had hoped.","As her son, he had no regrets, no grievances, and nothing left undone.","Little Huang smiled.","Smiling, Little Huang shed tears of blood.","His hand loosened, and the chipped cleaver clattered to the ground.","Little Huang spread his arms, closed his eyes, and raised his head, exposing his throat.","He was ready to receive his motherâs deadly embrace.","At last, the family of three could be reunited.","Huangâs mother exhaled, then sprang forward in a murderous pounce!","The next instant, Little Huang felt the tremendous force of the impact!"]},{"number":107,"title":"Chapter 107: 0107","paragraphs":["The impact came from the side!","Little Huangâs eyes flew open, but he couldnât see a thing. It had happened too fast. Everything around him had turned into horizontal streaks of speed.","Glass shattered!","A fall!","Weightlessness!","Then, miraculously, the descent slowed!","It was as if some force had risen from the ground to catch him.","Only after landing safely did Little Huang see the blue sky.","High above, at the third-floor window, Huangâs mother was crouching on the windowsill, looking down.","The next second, she jumped after him!","Little Huangâs pupils contracted.","But his body suddenly lifted into the air again.","Zhou Wang and Brother Dong, both wind-type ability users, dragged him away at full speed.","Little Huang watched helplessly as his mother leapt from the third-floor window and broke her leg when she hit the ground. She let out a hoarse roar in his direction.","âFaster, faster!â someone shouted.","A large number of zombies came rushing out of the building.","But with the two wind-type ability users going all out, not only had they used an upward current to cushion their own fall from the third floor and land safely, they were still too fast for the zombies to catch even while dragging along a half-dead person.","A minibus was parked outside the courtyard, its door open. The people inside were shouting at them.","The Development Zone government offices stood on the outskirts of the Science and Technology New Districtâs residential area, quite a distance from Maidoduo. They had to drive there.","But it had been Thursday, a regular workday, when the zombie virus broke out in the afternoon. The residential area in the Science and Technology New District was nearly deserted. It wasnât like last time, when there had been plenty of abandoned cars sitting in the streets with their keys still inside. Anyone could simply climb in and drive away.","When Zhou Wang received a call from Longlong's Grandma and learned that Little Huang had gone alone to the Development Zone government offices, he froze for a moment.","He knew perfectly well that his wife and child hadnât come back. Most likely, they were dead.","His own child was gone. Now there was another child he had to save.","He looked around, rapidly sweeping his eyes over everyone nearby.","Before anyone had time to react, he grabbed Brother Dong by the collar. âOld Dong! Come with me to save someone! Hurry! Itâs a child!â","There was no abandoned car with keys conveniently left inside.","But that didnât matter. Everyone immediately fixed their eyes on the minibus by the roadside.","Cui Haiyang picked the lock.","Gao Yuxuan started the engine.","Song Jingshuo took the wheel because he was an excellent driver.","Everyone piled into the vehicle. âHurry, hurry!â","Song Jingshuo shifted gears, slammed down on the accelerator, and sent the minibus shooting away in a reverse drift.","The vehicle would make too much noise, so they didnât stop too close to the building. They left it outside the government compound. Land in the development zone was much cheaper than in the city, and there were dozens of meters between the compoundâs main gate and the entrance to the main building.","But that distance was nothing to the two wind-type ability users.","Brother Dong was yanked out of the minibus by Zhou Wang, and the two of them charged into the building like a pair of gusts.","Damn it, what terrible luck! What did this have to do with him? He didnât even know the kid.","But people were swept along by their circumstances.","Everyone had started moving, taking part in the rescue. Even many of those who hadnât joined them had crowded outside the entrance to Maidoduo to watch them leave.","That made it impossible to back out.","A person could slip away quietly, but not when everyone was watching.","Still, Brother Dong was now one of the stronger ability users, and his mindset was no longer what it had once been. He grumbled inwardly about his bad luck, but obediently followed along.","Once they got out of the vehicle, the two of them rushed into the building like twin gusts of wind.","As for Huangâs motherâs job, Zhou Wang might have understood it even better than Little Huang did.","He and Huangâs mother were both successful, middle-aged professionals. Whenever they ran into each other and exchanged pleasantries, they didnât talk about what they had eaten that day. They talked about work, policy changes after the disaster, prospects for their industries, and things like that.","He knew that Huangâs mother was the Director of the Science and Industry Promotion Bureau in the Development Zone government.","But he didnât know where her office was or which floor it was on.","Fortunately, they found it smoothly.","They were one second away from being too late!","At the instant Huangâs mother pounced on Little Huang, the two of them also lunged forward. Using the speed granted by their wind-type abilities, they seized Little Huang before Huangâs mother could reach him.","The three of them crashed through the window and fell from the third floor together.","Jiang Cheng had said he would find Zhou Wang someone with the same type of ability and have them talk.","And, as it turned out, people with the same type of ability really could come up with something to talk about.","Before Zhou Wang received the call from Longlong's Grandma, Brother Dong had suddenly wondered aloud whether their wind-type abilities could let them fly.","The two of them had given it a try.","Flying was impossible.","Using air currents to fight gravityâwith their weight, no lessâwas pure fantasy. One of them had a beer belly, while the other was built like a solid block of muscle. They were simply too heavy to fly by relying on air currents.","But they had realized that when falling from a height, they could use an upward current to cushion the descent and slow themselves down.","Brother Dong had immediately said, âNow thatâs useful!â","They might not be able to fly, but it was perfect for escaping with their lives when cornered.","For example, jumping out of a building.","How could that not count as tempting fate?","Just over half an hour later, they really were jumping from a building.","Dragging the practically unconscious Little Huang at a run, they fled with a swarm of zombies pouring out of the building behind themâ¦","âHurry!â Gao Yuxuan roared.","Brother Dong and Zhou Wang shoved Little Huang into the minibus.","Gao Yuxuan and Cui Haiyang pulled him in from the other side with all their strength.","Then Zhou Wang squeezed into the rear compartment, while Guo Jun ran around to the front and climbed into the passenger seat.","Bangâscreechâ","One sound was the car door slamming shut.","The other was the minibus flooring the accelerator and executing a high-speed drift.","The people who hadnât fastened their seat belts were thrown around, their heads banging against the windows.","Once the vehicle steadied, they looked out through the rear window and saw that they had already left the zombies from the government building far behind.","âGood Lordâ¦â Brother Dong collapsed into the passenger seat, exhausted.","Zhou Wang was no better.","The entire charge into the building might have looked brief, but with that density of zombies, their abilities had been burning through their stamina in explosive bursts.","Brother Dong gasped for breath. When his nose began to itch, he raised a hand and wiped it, coming away with blood.","Song Jingshuo glanced at him in the rearview mirror as he drove. âCheck yourself over.â","Everything had happened too suddenly. Zhou Wangâs emotions had swept everyone along. Besides, they had just finished slaughtering a large number of zombies and were still running on adrenaline. When Zhou Wang called out, everyone acted on impulse.","Zhou Wang had an emotional bond with Little Huang and was single-mindedly determined to save him.","Brother Dong had been dragged into the whole thing in a daze, like a duck being herded into line.","But once the two of them had gone inside, the three people in the minibus had calmed down.","Song Jingshuo said, âPrepare yourselves for the possibility that we came all this way for nothing.â","If the child had even one small wound, not only would this trip have been pointlessâthey would have to deal with him themselves.","Cui Haiyang sighed. âAt least weâll have a clear conscience.â","Little Huang had always stayed by Zhou Wangâs side. And he was Old Huangâs son.","Nearly everyone on the Temporary Management Committee of the Youth Apartments knew him.","After Old Huang died, Little Huang had continued staying with Zhou Wang, and people often saw him there. Under those extraordinary circumstances, it was obvious that Zhou Wang had been deliberately looking after the widow and her orphaned child.","As a leader, he could truly be called compassionate and loyal.","So everyone really did understand his desperation at that moment. His urgency to save the child had infected them.","They had followed him. Even if the child couldnât be saved, at least they could say without shame, âWe did everything we could.â","But if they hadnât gone, they might spend the days and nights ahead wondering, If I had gone that day, maybeâ¦","After Song Jingshuoâs warning, Cui Haiyang and Gao Yuxuan immediately examined Little Huang from head to toe.","Once Little Huangâs adrenaline faded, his body gave out, and he slipped into a state of exhaustion.","But fortunately, Cui Haiyang said in amazement, âThe kid doesnât have a single injury.â","How had he managed it? He had charged into a nest of zombies all by himself, rushed straight to the third floor, and come out without a scratch.","Then they thought of something. âHe made it back alive from the school. He must have awakened a superpower.â","Gao Yuxuan said, âHis armor is pretty unusual.â","The armor issued by the government was all made by a fracture-brace factory, using the same white plastic. The kidâs shoulder guards were styled after the standard armor, but they were actually made of metal.","Cui Haiyang felt them over and said with certainty, âThis was modified by a metal-element superpowered person.â","He praised it. âQuite a skilled craftsman.â","Not only had they perfectly imitated the design, they had also left plenty of ventilation holes, just like the original. Even the edges were smooth and rounded, as if they had been polished, so they wouldnât be sharp or cut anyone.","This metal-element superpowered person had been extremely meticulous.","Gao Yuxuan said, âIf thatâs the case, could the children awaken superpowers too?â","Slumped in his seat, Zhou Wang turned his head and asked blankly, âReally? Can they?â","How he wished his child could awaken a superpower tooâenough to survive, and to bring his mother home.","But the adults knew that was only a dream. The fact that Little Huang was still alive was already a miracle.","Old Huangâs wife had already become a zombie.","âYuxuan,â Song Jingshuo said. âCall Jiang Cheng. Tell her weâre all right now. Little Huang is safe too.â","Gao Yuxuan gave an âoh,â then pulled out his phone and made the call.","Jiang Cheng checked the time. Another day had passed.","She took out her phone and glanced at her call history. Six or seven hours had passed since Li Feng had called her.","After thinking it over, Jiang Cheng tried calling him back.","A stiff electronic voice came through the phone: âThe subscriber you have dialed is outside the service area. The subscriber you have dialed is outside the service area. The subscriber you have dialedâ¦â","Was he dead?","So many people had died. Li Feng wasnât particularly important to her.","Jiang Cheng calmly ended the call.","But when her gaze swept across the area, she saw many familiar faces. She had to admit that, despite her naturally cool disposition, there were still some people who were different.","For instance, there were people who had received her warning text messages but hadnât believed them and never returned.","Jiang Cheng neither grew angry at their disbelief nor grieved their deaths.","But if Li Jiangbing or Song Jingshuo had refused to believe her, she really would have been angry.","Without realizing it, the transmigrator had formed ties with other people in this world. They shared neither blood nor sexual relations.","But thisâ¦ was actually pretty nice.","Jiang Cheng looked at Li Jiangbing, who was making a great deal of noise in the distance, and the corners of her lips curved upward."]},{"number":108,"title":"Chapter 108: 0108","paragraphs":["Song Jingshuo drove the van straight back to Jixiang West Street. By the time Gao Yuxuan called Jiang Cheng, they had already returned to the complex.","Everyone divided up the fresh vegetables, fruit, and meat they had bought from Maiduo.","With fewer people around, the supplies suddenly seemed like far too much.","Apparently, in the month since the last disaster ended, sales of refrigerators and freezers had skyrocketed.","Because the Youth Apartments had such small units, few residents had bought freezers. But while Jiang Cheng was away, many people had replaced their refrigerators with larger models.","Delivery trucks arrived every day.","Song Jingshuo had gone even further and replaced his with a side-by-side refrigerator. Those were still extremely rare. They had only just entered the market, and there were no domestic models yetâonly imported brands. For the moment, they were still luxury goods.","But they had an impressive capacity and could hold a great deal more.","They were perfect for the hoarding sickness people had developed after the disaster.","This time, though, everyone had brought back a truly enormous amount of supplies. Having already been through this once, they skipped many steps altogetherâpaying, for example, or bringing their own transportation.","It was obvious that many peopleâs refrigerators wouldnât be able to hold everything.","At the Youth Apartments, plenty of people simply opened the doors of their neighborsâ units.","There were far too many vacant apartments. Jiang Cheng lived on the third floor of Building Two. Including Aunt Pan, there were now only seven people left on her floor. Every other unit was empty.","And Building Two still had the highest population in the entire complex.","Some other buildings even had several consecutive floors with no one living in them.","When the second zombie disaster broke out, people no longer seemed to feel much of anything about refusing to pay, pushing shopping carts away, entering other peopleâs homes without permission, or taking resources that didnât belong to them.","They had simply pushed carts piled high with supplies out of the supermarket.","Even Su Yu, a girl with a strong sense of morality, didnât feel that anything was wrong.","She stared at the mountain of goods piled into Li Jiangbingâs cart and exclaimed, âYou got that much meat?â","âYou need meat to have the strength to kill zombies,â Li Jiangbing replied.","âTrue.â Su Yu asked, âHow do you usually cook meat? Braised pork?â","Li Jiangbing honestly admitted, âI canât cook.â","Su Yu let out an âah.â After thinking it over, she suggested, âWhy donât we team up for meals?â","Su Yu thought it was an excellent idea. Now that they had become quite familiar with each other, she had discovered that Li Jiangbing was a dependable manârough around the edges, but thoughtful and meticulous. Compared with the other men she didnât know well, Su Yu felt she could trust his character.","Cooking together would also be more efficient, and they could make one extra dish.","Li Jiangbing waved both hands and refused. âNo, no, itâs fine. Iâve already arranged things with Aunt Pan. Iâm joining her group and eating with them.â","Aunt Pan was cooking for the property management company employees, so all the meat he had taken wasnât just for himself.","Su Yu praised him. âYouâre really good at finding solutions. Aunt Panâs cooking always smells amazing.â","When the security guards were on duty, they would take their food containers to be filled, then eat at their posts.","Whenever anyone passed by, the delicious aroma would make their mouths water. You could tell just by the smell that the food had to be wonderful.","Another girl called out to Su Yu from behind while pushing a cart. Su Yu said, âGo on ahead.â","She stopped to wait for the girl behind her.","Li Jiangbing continued on, pushing his cart piled high with meat.","Someone sidled up to him and said, exasperated, âAre you an idiot?â","Eating with Aunt Pan and the security guards was nothing like teaming up with a young woman like Su Yu!","How could he be so dense?","Li Jiangbing said, âWhat are you talking about? Aunt Panâs cooking is amazing. It makes my mouth water.â","He hummed to himself as he pushed the cart away, ignoring them completely.","Whether he was genuinely clueless or merely pretending, no one could tell.","Jiang Cheng put the things she had taken into her home, then emptied her storage space and took out everything she had stored there from Maiduo.","The moment she did, there was no room left in the apartment.","The difference between the physical laws governing her storage space and those governing real space became immediately obvious.","In the real world, storing objects depended on their volume.","The storage space Jiang Cheng had dismissed as ânot big enoughâ had somehow managed to hold four hundred quilts. The entire Youth Apartments had only a little over four hundred residents.","Now came the problem: she couldnât leave all these things occupying her storage space forever, but her apartment was tiny.","There was no time to solve the problem just then, however, because Gao Yuxuan called her.","Jiang Cheng immediately called a young woman. âLesi, go to the east gate. Iâll be there soon too. Theyâve brought Little Huang back.â","The girlâs name was Zhang Lesi, and she was an intern at Renxin Hospital.","During the previous zombie disaster, when everyone had been trapped inside the complex, anyone who fell ill would go to her. She would perform a basic preliminary examination and advise them on what medicine to take.","After Renxin Hospital was reclaimed, she was temporarily put in charge of the pharmacy, and remained there until everything returned to normal.","But her supervising physician was gone.","Although businesses and government offices had resumed operations everywhere, many organizations were still in chaos. Numerous essential and nonessential employees had died, leaving countless positions vacant, and internal procedures were far from running smoothly.","Even now, no new supervising physician had been assigned to her.","As Zhang Lesi put it, she had enjoyed the easiest month of her medical career.","If she were given the chance to start over, she said, she would never choose to become a doctor again.","Anyone who encouraged someone to go into medicine would be struck by lightning.","It was simply too exhausting.","According to her, after society returned to normal and Renxin Hospital resumed regular operations, the hospital wasnât under particularly heavy pressure despite having lost so many medical workers.","There simply werenât that many patients.","There had been a rush in the first few days after Renxin Hospital was reclaimed, when all the people who had endured their illnesses during the disaster finally crowded in for treatment. That was when it had seemed especially busy.","But once everything truly returned to normal, the number of patients actually dropped.","âHow should I put it?â she had said. âOne way of explaining it is that the old, the weak, and the sick didnât survive.â","It was true. The first zombie disaster had killed a great many people, and some hadnât died directly because of zombies. Many of the elderly, weak, and sick had failed to survive that month and a half. They hadnât lived long enough for the supply lines to reopen, or for the food and medicine sent by the government to reach them.","Zhang Lesi had said, âWhen you think about it carefully, itâs terrifying. It was almost as if humanity had been put through a process of selection and elimination.â","The van drove directly to the spot between the two gates on Jixiang West Street.","The road was technically one-way, and they had entered against traffic. But who cared now? No one was going to stop them.","Besides Zhang Lesi, a large crowd had gathered at the entrance, most of them residents of the Youth Apartments.","Many people had received the notice that Little Huang was in critical condition and might need help, so they had all come.","This was where Li Jiangbingâs practical wisdom proved particularly useful. When he heard that Little Huang was mostly unconscious, he called for someone to bring over two wheeled office chairs from the property management office.","When the van arrived and the door opened, Zhou Wang had barely stepped out before applause erupted all around him.","Deep down, people still yearned for goodness, kindness, and all the positive things in life.","Even if they had fought over vegetables and competed for meat in the supermarket, they could still applaud one anotherâs heroic rescue.","They pushed two office chairs together, and everyone worked together to lift Little Huang down.","The boy was completely spent.","Compared with adults, a middle schooler's frame was still smallerâespecially thin and slender, with the look of someone who hadn't fully grown into himself yet.","And this child had gone alone to rescue his mother.","Someone quietly asked Gao Yuxuan, âWhat about his mother?â","Gao Yuxuan sighed. âAhââ","Everyone understood.","Their hearts ached for him even more.","Both office chairs had wheels, making them difficult to control. Cui Haiyang pulled a steel pipe from the small of his back, crouched down, and pressed it against the central axles of the two chairs. The three pieces of metal connected without any welding, joining the chairs into a single unit.","They tilted back one of the chair backs, and Li Jiangbing was able to lift Little Huang onto it by himself.","When everyone saw the bloody tear tracks on Little Huangâs face, they were stunned.","Li Jiangbing had experience. One look was enough for him to know what had happened. âHe overused his superpower.â","âCan his eyes bleed too?â everyone asked in astonishment. âIsnât it only the nose?â","âThe nose, eyes, and ears can all bleed. His mouth might too. My throat felt sweet when I was practicing last night. Now that I think about it, I was probably about to throw up blood.â","âHoly shit, wouldnât that mean bleeding from all seven orifices?â","ââ¦Seems like it.â","Jiang Cheng asked first, âDoes he have any external injuries?â","Zhou Wang hurriedly said, âNo, no. We checked him thoroughly.â","âThis kidâs incredible. He went in there alone, with the whole stairwell crawling with zombies, and somehow didnât suffer a single injury.â","âItâs just that his motherâ¦â Someone sighed.","Zhao Yi asked Gao Yuxuan, âWhat kind of superpower does he have?â","Gao Yuxuan was curious too. âI donât know. He was unconscious when we rescued him. Let Zhang Lesi take a look first.â","Zhang Lesi went over and tried to lift Little Huangâs eyelid, but the moment her hand touched him, she froze.","Everyone noticed that something was wrong and hurriedly asked, âWhat is it?â","âIs he all right?â","They all thought something had happened to Little Huang. But then Zhang Lesi raised her head, her voice trembling slightly.","âIâ¦â","She said, âI have a superpower.â","According to the superpower experts, the sign that someone had developed a superpower was a stabbing pain in the brain. If that was true, Zhang Lesi was certain she should have a superpower too.","Since yesterday, she had touched all kinds of things. She had tried metal, wood, water, fire, and earth, but nothing had awakened her superpower.","Who would have thought that the moment her palm touched the unconscious Little Huang, the blocked, stabbing area in her brain would suddenly burst open.","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan pushed their way over at the same time. âWhat is it? Whatâs your superpower?â","Zhang Lesi was about to answer when Gao Yuxuan thrust a finger toward her.","âDonât tell me, donât tell meâlet me guess! Is it healing? Is it?â","Zhang Lesi was thrilled. âThatâs right! Youâre amazing!â","She continued, âThereâs nothing seriously wrong with this child. Heâs just exhausted. Heâs still extremely weak, and he has acid reflux. Iâm guessing he hasnât eaten for a long time.â","In short, he was exhausted and starvingâhe had collapsed from weakness.","The moment her palm touched Little Huangâs face, she knew the condition of his body.","Gao Yuxuan and Zhao Yi excitedly pumped their fists in the air, then slapped each otherâs palms in celebration.","The resulting clap was incredibly loud.","Li Jiangbing understood at once. He planted his hands on his hips and said, âYou two figure it out? Once you do, come back and explain it to me! I need to know!â","Li Jiangbing desperately needed to understand how to make his own seemingly useless superpower work.","Everyone elseâs superpowers were so useful. It was driving him crazy."]},{"number":109,"title":"Chapter 109: 0109","paragraphs":["Zhang Lesi suddenly became the center of attention.","Actually, she had always been something of a focal point. While everyone was trapped and resources were scarce, they had already realized how important having a doctor was. Almost everyone treated her with courtesy, even those who barely knew her.","But now, she was even more important.","âCan you use your superpower to treat him?â Jiang Cheng asked.","âHe doesnât need treatment,â Zhang Lesi said. âHe isnât sick or injuredâheâs just exhausted and starving. He needs rest and food. We have to replenish his energy as soon as possible. He needs to eat. Who lives nearby? Get him some sugar-salt water first! Anyone from Building Three?â","Building Three was the closest to the east gate. Someone immediately ran home to prepare the sugar-salt water.","The weather was still a little hot, so everyone moved Little Huang beneath the shade of a tree and fed him two sips of plain water first.","Little Huang opened his eyes, looking somewhat dazed.","Surrounded by a circle of adults, he tried to sit up, but they stopped him.","âLie down, lie down. Donât move.â","Little Huangâs mind gradually cleared. He remembered everything that had happened, but said nothing. Half reclining, he stared at the branches overhead.","The leaves swayed constantly in the breeze. Sunlight broke into fragments and flashed over and over. Every so often, blue sky and white clouds appeared between the branches.","It all looked so beautiful. Under such beautiful sunlight, why had the world become a living hell?","What had turned the world into what it was now?","Where had the zombie virus come from?","Although his eyes were vacant, Zhang Lesi said that there was nothing seriously wrong with his physical condition.","Jiang Cheng was more concerned about the situation at the development zone government offices.","Zhou Wang and Brother Dong said, âAnyway, we didnât see any living people from the first floor to the third. We donât know about the fourth floor and above. It didnât look like anyone was alive in there.â","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan asked Zhang Lesi, âCan you treat people? Illnesses or injuries?â","Zhang Lesi looked at her palms. âI donât know. Iâve never tried before. But I can feel something inside my body. Should I call it âqiâ or âenergyâ?â","The two experts hurried to settle the matter.","âEnergy! Energy!â","They firmly believed in science.","âEnergyâ sounded scientific.","âQiâ sounded a little too much like qigong healing and snake-oil salesmen. It lacked sophistication.","Zhang Lesi could sense the energy inside her body, and she could tell that it had a certain affinity with the human body. It should be capable of affecting the body in some way. However, they had yet to conduct any experiments to prove that this was the case, so she couldnât give a definite answer.","She was a medical student, after all, and she believed in science.","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan exchanged a look, then tacitly extended their fists. Without a word, they shook them three times before stopping together.","Zhao Yi had thrown scissors. Gao Yuxuan had thrown rock.","Gao Yuxuan won.","Accepting his fate, Zhao Yi went to find Cui Haiyang.","âDo you have a knife? A small one.â","Cui Haiyang had been practicing his ability nonstop since yesterday. After bending the steel pipe yesterday, he had found it quite difficult to straighten it again, and had ended up drenched in sweat.","Today, he could already reshape these metals with ease. In his hands, they were as pliable as modeling clay.","The steel pipe he had was being used to secure the two wheeled office chairs, so he looked around.","Everyone was standing outside the east gate of the Youth Apartments, on Jixiang West Street.","The elderly residents from Jixiang Gardens had also heard about what happened and kept coming over to see Little Huang.","Cui Haiyang swept his gaze around and spotted a metal plate on a concrete utility poleâthe kind engraved with the poleâs identification number. He went over and placed his hand on it. The plate transformed into a small knife.","The blade was very thin and looked quite sharp.","Zhao Yi did not take it. He stared at it. âYouâre not going to give me tetanus, are you?â","The plate had looked a little rusty around the edges.","âYouâre awfully fussy.â Cui Haiyang snorted. As he laughed, he focused for a moment while holding the knife.","Zhao Yi felt as though his vision blurred for an instant, but the little blade didnât seem to have changed at all.","âWhat did you do?â he asked suspiciously.","Cui Haiyang must have done something. As fellow superpowered individuals, they could vaguely sense one anotherâs abilities at such close range.","Cui Haiyang looked pleased with himself. âI refined and purified it.â","Zhao Yi understood immediately. âHoly crap?â","Cui Haiyang raised the blade. âLook. Itâs perfectly clean now. You can use it without worrying. You absolutely wonât get tetanus.â","Tetanus bacteria are anaerobic. The porous surface of rust can create an environment suitable for them to survive, which is why wounds caused by rusty metal are prone to tetanus infection.","After Cui Haiyang had refined and purified it, the blade was now made of clean, pure iron.","Zhao Yi took the blade and promptly cut his own arm with it. His skin split, and bright red blood immediately came pouring out.","âQuick!â Gao Yuxuan urged Zhang Lesi.","Zhang Lesi was both excited and nervous. Medical students didnât get nervous at the sight of wounds or blood. She was nervous because the moment had come to verify her superpower.","Even Zhou Wang and Jiang Cheng stopped to watch.","Zhang Lesi brought her fingertip close to Zhao Yiâs wound. She began channeling her power when her finger was close enough to brush the fine hairs on his arm.","The sunlight was so bright that it was almost impossible to see unless one narrowed their eyes. In fact, a faint white glow was emanating from her fingertip.","When she moved her hand away, the wound had become nothing more than a pale pink scar, as though it had healed perfectly. There was no raised scar tissue, either.","A chorus of âHoly crap!â rang out from the crowd.","Zhao Yi examined the fresh scar on his arm and pressed on with his question. âThatâs healing an injury. What about treating an illness?â","Zhang Lesi put her hands on her hips. âHow are we supposed to test that?â","Several elderly people in the crowd from Jixiang Gardens immediately stepped forward, all clamoring for attention.","âMiss, miss! Iâm sick! Iâm sick!â","Just like that, it became a free medical clinic.","Zhang Lesi examined them one by one.","One had high blood pressure.","Another complained of leg pain, which turned out to be varicose veins.","A third had lower back pain and suspected a slipped disc, but it was actually a misaligned facet joint. Technically, that could not even be considered an illness. It was simply the result of aging and physical deterioration.","Zhang Lesi could diagnose all of them by touch alone. When it came to diagnosis, she was already a miracle doctor.","But after trying, she found that she couldnât treat them.","Her superpowerâs energy could only heal physical injuries.","âThat makes sense.â Zhao Yi pushed up his glasses. For some reason, his eyes had been bothering him all day.","He offered his theory. âAlthough we donât yet know where these abilities originated, as far as their application is concerned, all superpowers are external forces acting upon the world and the human body. Physical injuries are also caused by external forces acting upon the body. Thatâs why a superpower can heal an injuryâthe two forces can counterbalance each other.â","âBut conditions like these are natural changes and the effects of aging. Theyâre an inevitable part of lifeâs journey toward its end.â","âIf everything could be cured with superpowers, wouldnât that mean people could avoid illness and aging and live forever?â","âIn that case, life itself would become unbalanced.â","Those with higher education could easily understand and appreciate what he meant by balance and imbalance.","But the atmosphere at the scene became distinctly strange.","Song Jingshuo had no choice but turn his face away.","Zhao Yi looked confused.","The elderly people were so angry that their eyes nearly rolled back in their heads.","The young man wasnât even bad-looking, so how could he be so tactless?","Why did he have to talk about growing old and dying? How unlucky!","Zhao Yi was horrified.","No, no, no! That wasnât what I meant!","The person from Building Three who had run home for water finally returned.","They unscrewed a bottle of mineral water, added sugar and salt, and mixed it into a sugar-and-salt solution. They even thoughtfully gave him a packet of bread.","Little Huang drank the solution, then wolfed down the entire packet of bread. It was obvious he had been starving.","After eating and drinking, Little Huang rested for a while, and the color gradually returned to his face.","When everyone questioned him, they learned that he hadnât eaten anything since yesterday afternoon.","People bombarded him with questions about the situation in the city and at the school. They were amazed to hear that so many children had survived at the school, that some of them had awakened superpowers, and that they had even retaken the campus without any adults leading them.","Several elderly women began to cry. âTheir parents would be heartbroken if they knew.â","But that was assuming their parents were still alive.","âThey said they were going to rescue the senior high school students. I had to come back to look for my mom, so I didnât go with them.â As Little Huang spoke, his eyes dimmed.","There were three great tragedies in life: losing oneâs father in youth, oneâs husband in middle age, and oneâs child in old age.","Everyone felt a pang of sympathy.","âMy parents died in a car accident when I was in college,â Jiang Cheng said gently. âAt the time, I felt as though the world had ended and my own life was over.â","âBut it wasnât. Look at meâIâm living just fine here.â","âActually, every one of us will eventually become someone without parents.â","âAll you can do is live your own life well from here on.â","âThatâs what Mom and Dad would want to see.â","Little Huang knew Jiang Cheng very well. Of course, Jiang Cheng knew Little Huang too, but his familiarity with her was decidedly one-sided.","Among the survivors, the two people Little Huang admired most were Zhou Wang and Jiang Cheng.","Huangâs mother admired Jiang Cheng as well. She had always encouraged Little Huang to grow into someone like her.","âShe looks like the kind of person nothing can bring down,â his mother had said. âAnd she doesnât look like someone who would let others bully her.â","âLook at the two people beside her. One is so strong, and the other is so tall, yet they both listen to her.â","âPeople who can command a voice for themselves are never the ones who get bullied, no matter the circumstances.â","Little Huang had asked, âWhat about Uncle Zhou?â","His mother had replied, âOld Zhou is pretty good too. But heâs like me. People like us are adaptable, but we canât compare with your father when it comes to taking the lead. Old Zhou was forced into itâlike a duck herded onto a chopping block.â","âJiang Cheng is better. Sheâs young and sharp-edged, unlike us middle-aged people, whose edges have already been worn down. Thatâs why Mom hopes youâll learn from her.â","Little Huang looked into Jiang Chengâs eyes and nodded. âOkay.â","Zhou Wang sighed as well. âThatâs how it is. Thatâs how it is for everyone. The only difference is when it happens. Youâre still young now. When you grow up, youâll marry a woman, have a child, and build a family of your own.â","His words resonated with many of the people there.","After all, among the survivors in the youth apartment complex, many had already been unable to contact their families since yesterday.","They had simply already lived through one zombie disaster and witnessed too many deaths to openly display their grief so easily anymore. Many of them were even moved by Jiang Cheng, assuming that someone with her personality must have been tempered by life after losing her parents at an early age.","Of course, no one knew that Jiang Cheng was merely borrowing âJiang Chengâsâ life story to comfort Little Huang.","Jiang Cheng was more concerned about something else. She asked, âWhat is your superpower?â"]},{"number":110,"title":"Chapter 110: 0110","paragraphs":["Little Huang thought carefully before saying, âYesterday, I could sense danger coming from far away. As soon as I felt it approaching, I could avoid it immediatelyâfor example, by turning onto another road instead of taking that one.â","âToday, I can already rely on that sense to weave and dodge between zombies at extremely close range.â","âItâs just that when there are too many zombies, it gets exhausting. I canât relax for even a second. Second-generation zombies can pounce in the blink of an eye, and Iâve had to dodge them by the skin of my teeth more times than I can count.â","âIt takes a huge amount of stamina.â","That was why he had ended up completely drained.","The elderly men and women didnât quite understand what âweavingâ meant. But the gamers from the Youth Apartments all exclaimed, âHoly crap!â","What gamer wouldnât envy an ability like that?","The ability itself might not be evasion, but with its help, it was practically the same as maxing out oneâs dodging skill.","As for becoming so exhausted that he collapsedâkid, you charged straight into a nest of zombies! Who wouldnât be completely spent after doing that?","The fact that he had survived alone was already impressive.","It sounded like an ability with little offensive power, but tremendous survival potential.","Jiang Cheng nodded. Seeing that his complexion had improved considerably and that he was able to sit up, she asked, âDo you want to go home and rest?â","Little Huang, however, stared at the west gate of his own residential compound across the street, his heart resisting the idea.","He didnât dare go back to that empty home.","Zhou Wang understood perfectly. He didnât like going home either. It was empty, and the emptiness hurt.","If he hadnât been so busy, being alone at home would have been torture.","He sighed and was just about to tell Little Huang, âWhy donât you come stay at my place?â when Jiang Cheng said gently, âIf you donât want to go home, you can come stay with us.â","Zhou Wang: ââ¦â","Jiang Cheng continued, âThere are plenty of empty apartments on our side. Theyâre all small studio units, very suitable for a young person living alone. A lot of the people there arenât much older than youâaround the age of older brothers and sisters. We can all look after one another.â","Zhou Wang: ââ¦â","Yes, this was the Jiang Cheng he knew.","The moment she heard about someone elseâs superpower, she shamelessly tried to poach them right to their face, without the slightest hesitation.","The word âembarrassmentâ probably didnât exist in this girlâs dictionary.","By comparisonâ¦","Zhou Wang couldnât help glancing at Brother Dong.","Brother Dong: ââ¦?â","Zhou Wang looked away.","Brother Dong was now considered a powerful superhuman. And he hadnât planned on staying for long anyway; he had only wanted to spend the night there out of caution and see how things developed before returning home.","Even so, Jiang Cheng had refused to let Brother Dong stay and had immediately pushed him toward Zhou Wang instead.","Zhou Wang already knew what Brother Dong had done back then.","But he still felt that Jiang Cheng was simply too young and couldnât tolerate the slightest flaw in anyone. Water that was too clear had no fish; when employing people, one should be willing to look past their shortcomings and take their value into consideration.","What Zhou Wang didnât know was that Jiang Cheng wasnât unaware of how powerful and useful Brother Dongâs ability was.","But the instant she reunited with Brother Dong, a thought had flashed through her mindâ","Loyalty is more important than value.","That understanding came from the sealed memories buried deep within her mind, from Jiang Chengâs true self.","So even after Brother Dong had made such an obvious attempt to show goodwill, Jiang Cheng had still rejected him without hesitation.","Zhou Wang actually hoped more than anything that Jiang Cheng would invite him to stay at the Youth Apartments too.","The current makeup of Auspicious Home was truly despair-inducing.","The people who had remained behind had just told him that six young and able-bodied survivors had returned from the city between noon and late afternoon. But even with those six added, the overwhelming majority of the compoundâs residents were still elderly people.","With Zhou Wangâs superpower, he could practically survive under any circumstances.","But people couldnât easily abandon their homes. He lived here, after all.","The worst part was that everyone in the compound had naturallyâeven quite reasonably, in their mindsâassumed that he should once again become their leader, responsible for keeping everyone safe and fed.","Had they even considered how few people he had left who were capable of working or fighting?","Just thinking about it gave him a headache.","Little Huang was tempted.","Leaving a place filled with sorrow and changing oneâs surroundings to avoid painful reminders was, after all, a form of emotional self-protection.","But Little Huang knew he wouldnât leave Uncle Zhou.","He had quietly observed the situation just now and understood very clearly what Auspicious Home was like at present.","Uncle Zhou needed help.","So he politely declined the offer.","Jiang Cheng didnât take it personally.","To Jiang Cheng, trying something cost nothing, and might even bring unexpected gains. But giving up without trying and missing an opportunityâthat was a real loss.","At present, Auspicious Home had sixteen young and able-bodied people at most, plus the six who had just returned and Little Huang, for a total of twenty-three. That number included two high school students and one middle school student.","The only somewhat encouraging news was that five of the six young people who had returned were superhumans.","Two earth, one metal, one fire, and one electricity.","The proportion of superhumans was surprisingly high.","Or, to put it another way, people with superpowers had a higher chance of surviving.","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan were still pestering Zhang Lesi. âCan you restore other peopleâs mana?â","Zhang Lesi: ââ¦â","Zhang Lesi: âIâll restore your high blood pressure.â","âMana and health, my ass,â Zhang Lesi snapped. âDo you two think this is a video game? Have you lost your minds? Wake up!â","The two anime fans were scolded until they hung their heads in embarrassment.","They slunk off to chat with the several superhumans who had just returned to Auspicious Home.","Those were the only ones left. They had already interviewed every other superhuman.","Little Huang felt that he could stand now. Zhou Wang helped him up and prepared to take him home.","Little Huang was still somewhat weak, so Zhou Wang said, âStay at my place for now. How are you supposed to eat if youâre living alone?â","He manipulated the airflow around Little Huang, making it easier for him to walk.","Little Huang felt as though his body were being gently supported by something soft. He praised him, âThat superpower of yours is really convenient.â","Brother Dong followed Zhou Wang as well.","Zhou Wang asked, âWhen are you going home?â","âTomorrow,â Brother Dong replied. âIâll stay here for one night.â","âHave you gotten in touch with your family?â","âNo.â","âAhâ¦â","âNo, thatâs not what I meant.â Brother Dong realized that Zhou Wang had misunderstood. In the current situation, being unable to contact oneâs family basically meant they were dead.","He said troubledly, âI lost my phone. I canât find it.â","Zhou Wang pulled out his own phone. âUse mine.â","Brother Dong looked even more troubled. âI donât remember their phone numbers.â","ââ¦You donât remember even one?â","âNot a single one.â","There was nothing they could do about that.","Zhou Wang arranged a place for Brother Dong to stay.","There were far too many empty homes now. Several belonged to families whose doors they had broken down to eliminate the zombies inside. The locks were still open, so Brother Dong could move right in.","Zhou Wang had been exhausted after the dayâs events and didnât feel like cooking.","He found an elderly woman he knew fairly well, spoke with her, and arranged for himself and Little Huang to share meals with her from then on.","Everyone dispersed on Auspicious West Street, returning to their respective residential compounds.","Song Jingshuo noticed that Jiang Cheng seemed distracted. He walked over and fell into step beside her. âWhatâs wrong? What are you thinking about?â","Jiang Cheng said, âThere are several buildings at Little Huangâs school. From what he said, as long as there was someone in a building, there were survivors there. In the end, several hundred students survived.â","Song Jingshuo sighed. âItâs really not easy.â","But Jiang Cheng wasnât lamenting the hardships of minors. She said, âZhou Wang and Old Dong searched three floors of the Development Zone government buildingâthe fifth floor down to the third. They didnât find any survivors.â","Song Jingshuo: ââ¦Maybe theyâre on the fourth or fifth floors?â","âItâs impossible that all the survivors went to the fourth and fifth floors,â Jiang Cheng said. âEven if there are people up there, there probably arenât many.â","Song Jingshuo was no longer sure. âWhat are you getting at?â","Jiang Cheng waved it off. âNothing. Maybe Iâm just overthinking it.â","Song Jingshuoâs brow furrowed even more deeply. âCanât you tell me?â","âI donât have any evidence. It would sound like wild speculation, and saying it out loud would only make people doubt me,â Jiang Cheng said. âLetâs wait and see. Maybe I really am just overthinking it.â","The anomaly Jiang Cheng had noticed was extremely subtle. There were simply too few examples to support any solid conclusion.","Objectively speaking, her own subjective assumptions made up a very large part of it.","When this kind of âwild speculationâ turned out to be correct, people often called it âkeen insight.â But when it was wrong, it was just overthinking.","Speaking carelessly before anything was confirmed could easily cause trouble or invite ridicule. Song Jingshuo understood that very well.","He trusted Jiang Cheng.","âThen tell me once youâve sorted it out.â","âOkay. For now, letâs wait and see whether the government makes an announcement.â","Song Jingshuo was silent for a moment. Jiang Chengâs words implied the possibility that there would be no announcement.","The two of them continued walking in silence.","Li Jiangbing caught up with them. âWhat are you two doing?â","Why were they walking without saying a word? It was one thing when other people did that, but when Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo fell silent together, it was unsettling.","Jiang Cheng asked, âJiangbing, can you purify water?â","Li Jiangbing: âHuh?â","Jiang Cheng explained, âLike how the ocean turned an iron plate into pure iron.â","Li Jiangbing scratched his head. âWhat would we need that for?â","Jiang Cheng gave him a scenario. âThe water supply has been cut off, and thereâs nothing but a pool of filthy water in front of us. Can you extract pure water directly from that pool for everyone to drink?â","This time, even Li Jiangbing fell silent.","He and Song Jingshuo both stared at Jiang Chengâs face.","Song Jingshuo said, âIsnât that a little too pessimistic?â","Li Jiangbing added, âExactly. You saw what happened last timeâ¦â","But he couldnât finish. Earlier that day, Jiang Cheng had already analyzed the situation for him at Duoduo Warehouse. If her analysis was correct, then this kind of situation really might occur.","Jiang Cheng, however, smiled. âHow is that pessimistic? Iâm being optimistic.â","At times like this, her eyes seemed especially bright.","âWhen I think about the superpowers the three of us have,â she said, âI feel particularly optimistic.â","Zhao Yi and Cui Haiyang came back toward them from ahead, moving against the flow of people. âJiang Cheng!â","Zhao Yi said, âAbout our superpowers, the two of usâ¦â","But Jiang Cheng narrowed her eyes and interrupted him. âWhere are your glasses?â","Zhao Yi was nearsighted. Without his glasses, he might not even recognize a tree when he saw one.","But he wasnât wearing them now.","Zhao Yi paused. Gao Yuxuan excitedly exclaimed, âYour powers of observation are really sharp.â","He slapped Zhao Yi on the back. âGo on, tell her.â","Zhao Yi said, âI donât need glasses anymore.â"]},{"number":111,"title":"Chapter 111: 0111","paragraphs":["Jiang Cheng guessed it at once. âTheir physiques have been enhanced?â","The two young men answered in unison, âExactly!â","Zhao Yiâs eyes had started feeling uncomfortable that morning, and the discomfort had steadily worsened as the day went on. After the fierce battle at Mai Duoduo that afternoon, it had reached its peak.","He had even begun to feel dizzy.","He simply couldnât stand it anymore and had taken off his glasses. That was when he realized he could see clearly which things were trees and which were people.","They remembered what Jiang Cheng had openly told everyone: after the first outbreak of the zombie virus, her physical constitution had been affected, most notably by an increase in strength.","The two men had put their heads together and asked themselves: during the disaster caused by the first zombie outbreak, what weakness did Jiang Cheng actually have?","There was nothing wrong with her mind or her personality. She was better than most people in both respects.","Her only weakness was that she was a woman, and therefore physically weaker than a man.","Yet during the first zombie disaster, that sole weakness had never manifested. Her physical constitution had been improved.","After all, given the circumstances at the time, a leader obviously had to be exceptionally intelligent. But intelligence alone wasnât enough; they couldnât be physically frail. At the very least, they couldnât be weaker than the average man.","Monsters were eating people everywhere, and death lurked around every corner. Someone physically frail could not inspire genuine confidence in others.","In those days, people needed someone strong and courageous to stand at the front.","If Jiang Cheng had fallen below that baseline, then perhaps she could only have served as Song Jingshuoâs strategist and adviser, relying on her intelligence rather than becoming the leader herself.","Actually, âbalanceâ had already existed invisibly from that time onward.","During the first zombie disaster, who knew how many peopleâs physiques had been quietly improved without their noticingâor had noticed but chosen not to say anything?","Even Jiang Cheng had concealed the matter out of caution.","âThat completes the final link in our reasoning,â the two of them declared.","The pair had spent an entire day and night studying superpowers, and now they told Jiang Cheng, âWe can summarize everything tonight. Tomorrow, weâd like to explain it to everyone. It seems like quite a few people want to know.â","âYeah, yeah, I want to know too,â Li Jiangbing said hurriedly.","Jiang Cheng also wanted to hear what the two of them had figured out that she hadnât. âAll right. Letâs have everyone gather in the square tomorrow morning and listen.â","Zhao Yi asked, âShould we ask Zhou Wang and the others to come too?â","For now, superpowers appeared to be humanityâs most effective weapon against the zombies.","If their theory was correct, it might help more people awaken superpowers. This was not something they should keep hidden.","Jiang Cheng said, âAll right.â","That evening, the residents of the Youth Apartments heard an announcement over the buildingâs broadcast system: there would be a meeting in the small square the next morning. Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan would be speaking about superpowers.","Those two had been bouncing around all day.","Everyone was looking forward to it.","Zhou Wang received Jiang Chengâs phone call.","He knew about the two young men. All afternoon, they had been going around talking to people, asking about their superpowers, what they did, and what they liked.","Zhou Wang himself wasnât particularly interested.","It was like having excellent grades and not caring much whether you attended extra tutoring after school.","But Jiang Cheng had said, âMaybe this can help other people develop superpowers.â","Zhou Wang thought it over and decided to take part. âAll right.â","After hanging up, he felt a headache coming on. Even notifying everyone in Lucky Garden about a group activity was a major hassle now.","Most of the elderly residents didnât know how to use the internet.","Before, there had been only a tiny handful of highly educated elderly residents in the community who knew how to use the internet, and none of them had survived this time.","Worse still, not every one of the surviving elderly residents even had a cell phone. Those who did generally only knew how to make calls. They couldnât manage text messages, and many couldnât read them clearly anyway.","During the previous disaster, there had been no superpowers, and it was nearly impossible for one person to survive alone. Everyone had needed to unite and rely on the strength of the collective to stay alive.","But now, Zhou Wang could survive perfectly well on his own.","Lucky Garden had become nothing but a burden.","Zhou Wang felt exhausted. He desperately wanted to throw off this burden.","That evening, Li Jiangbing began having dinner with Aunt Pan and the others in the property-management officeâs meeting room.","Cao Jiacai was holding court at the table, chatting away merrily.","He smacked his lips while eating, and flecks of saliva flew from his mouth whenever he spoke. Fortunately, everyone was eating from their own bowls. Unlike in a family setting, there werenât several shared dishes sitting in the middle of the table.","Li Jiangbing found it rather irritating. He held one hand loosely in front of his bowl to keep it from being contaminated.","Although Li Jiangbing looked like a rough, burly man, his work regularly brought him into contact with high-income clients: rich older women, white-collar career women, elite businessmen, wealthy young ladies, and fussy gay men.","Those people were incredibly particular. They had endless demands.","Li Jiangbing had long since been trained by his clients to pay attention to the details of daily lifeâtrim his nose hair, keep his fingernails neat, shower frequently so he wouldnât smell, brush his teeth regularly, and even keep mouthwash in his gym bag in case his breath bothered a client after a meal.","When he had first entered the industry, he had thought all of that was ridiculous. But after so much time, it had become part of his lifestyle.","He was already a refined, well-groomed strongman. Watching someone else smack his lips and spray saliva as he talked was genuinely hard for him to tolerate.","Li Jiangbing decided that starting tomorrow, he would take his meal home to eat. He wouldnât come here just for the convenience of eating together.","Cao Jiacai had been going on and on about how incredible his superpower had been at Mai Duoduo that afternoon.","Of all the property-management staff, only he, Aunt Pan, and Little Fang had gone. Everyone else had missed it.","Caught up in his excitement, he pointed at Li Jiangbing. âAsk Li. Li knows, right, Li?â","Li?","Li Jiangbing raised his eyelids.","The atmosphere in the meeting room turned awkward.","Manager Wang gave an embarrassed laugh.","Yang Xinyan lowered her head.","Little Fang stole a glance at him.","Several people exchanged meaningful looks.","Aunt Pan broke the awkward silence by scolding, âDid you sneak off for another drink? Youâre starting to talk nonsense again!â","After scolding Cao Jiacai, she turned to Li Jiangbing and said, âDonât mind him. A bottle of beer and he starts spouting rubbish.â","Whether she meant his boasting about his superpower or the way he had addressed Li Jiangbing as âLi,â everyone could draw their own conclusions.","Cao Jiacai clicked his tongue.","Li Jiangbing sighed. âTheyâre zombies, after all. The pressure is enormous. Having a little alcohol now and then helps people relax.â","Cao Jiacai slapped the table. âExactly!â","Li Jiangbing looked at him. âAll we can do is hope the country cleans up this mess quickly and efficiently, just like last time. A month, maybe half a monthâsure, itâll be tough, but itâll pass quickly. Then everyone can go back to their lives and get on with whatever theyâre supposed to be doing. Iâll go back to my job, and you can all go back to yours.â","No matter what kind of job Li Jiangbing held, even if it wasnât as prestigious as Song Jingshuoâs, he was still a property owner with a deed to his apartment in the Youth Apartments.","There was no way some security guard he barely knew had the right to call him âLi.â","That was a different matter if they became familiar.","Cao Jiacai looked uncomfortable for a moment, then straightened his back. âOnce this is over, I wonât keep working here. I have a superpower now.â","The zombies could be wiped out. But surely his superpower wouldnât disappear just because the zombies did.","Even if life returned to the way it had been, he was already an incredible superpowered individual.","He slapped the table and declared, âWhen the time comes, Iâll do whatever I want. Why canât I do whatever I want?â","He had the air of a man who owned the whole world.","Li Jiangbing grinned. âWhat are you planning to do?â","He asked, âWork as a boiler operator at a heating plant? Perform fire-breathing tricks at a circus? Wait!â","He jabbed his finger repeatedly at the air. âRoast sweet potatoes! Thatâs a good one! Perfect for a fire-type ability!â","âOr roast mutton skewers! Roasted mutton skewers would be pretty good too!â","Li Jiangbingâs little mouth was sharp enough to draw blood.","Little Fang turned away, trying to hold back his laughter. Yang Xinyan didnât even dare look up, afraid she would burst out laughing.","Manager Wangâs eyes wandered as he stared fixedly at the ceiling.","Cao Jiacaiâs expression darkened. He snorted. âI can always find something else to do.â","But when he thought about it carefully, if social order were restored and life returned to the way it had been, he really couldnât think of anything he could do with a fire-type superpower.","Was he seriously going to roast sweet potatoes or mutton skewers?","The more he thought about it, the more he felt there was no point in a civilized, orderly society. All he could do was work as a security guard and spend the rest of his life wasting his talents.","When Li Jiangbing had nearly finished eating, Aunt Pan said, âYou go on back first. Donât wait for me. I still have pots to wash.â","Cao Jiacai let out an exaggerated cry. âWhat? Youâre still washing the pots? You already cookedâhow hard did you work? Youâve got superpowers now, and you killed so many zombies today. How could we possibly make you wash the pots?â","Cao Jiacaiâs gaze swept across the room and landed on Manager Wang.","Manager Wangâs face looked awful.","This was already the second time they had experienced a zombie disaster. So much had happened during the previous outbreak that, by now, there was no need to spell things out.","The identities people held in a society governed by law and order became meaningless in times of chaos.","Manager Wang had spent the entire day trying to make himself look useful. At the same time, he had worked hard to preserve the dignity that came with being a manager.","And now, that bastard Cao Jiacai was trying to strip him naked in front of everyone.","Cao Jiacai really did have that intention.","But Li Jiangbingâs earlier words had genuinely affected him. When he considered that they might eventually have to return to an orderly society, Cao Jiacai ultimately decided to let Manager Wang off the hook. He pointed at him. âYou. Youâll wash the pots today. From now on, take turns.â","He continued grumbling, âIf your cooking werenât so awful, we wouldnât have made Big Sister cook in the first place. She works hard killing zombiesâhow could we make her wash dishes too?â","âOne slap, and whooshâup comes a spike!â","âOne slap, and whooshâup comes a spike!â","âOn a concrete floor, no less!â","He even imitated how Sister Gao had slapped the ground and sent stone spikes thrusting up in the shopping mall that afternoon.","Manager Wang had been spared. He let out a long breath of relief and hurriedly played along. âExactly, exactly. Big Sister, Big Sister, once youâve finished eating, just go back. Donât worry about this place. Iâll arrange for them to take turns cleaning up later. You only need to go home.â","Li Jiangbing left with Aunt Pan.","As they passed the service center, they saw that the television mounted on the wall was still on. Everyone was waiting for a government announcement, listening to the television for any sound of one. The property management office had also left this television on while they waited.","The first zombie-virus outbreak had begun at nine or ten oâclock on Saturday night, and the government had issued an announcement by Sunday morning.","Although the announcement had not said so explicitly, the government had in fact already been mobilizing forces to secure the water, electricity, and gas supplies.","This outbreak had begun yesterday afternoon. It was already the second night, and the streetlights had come on outside the property management center. So why hadnât there been any government announcement yet?","For the first time, Li Jiangbing found himself hoping that Jiang Cheng wasnât quite so clever, that she wasnât so good at predicting things.","After walking for a while, he suddenly remembered that he was walking with Aunt Pan. He turned his head and saw her walking quietly with her lips tightly pressed together, apparently deep in thought.","âAuntie, what are you thinking about?â Li Jiangbing asked.","Aunt Pan glanced at him and made up her mind. âThereâs something I need to tell Little Jiang later.â","Old Luo had said that it was Cao Jiacai who had gone to the police station to report them and ask for Jiang Cheng to be arrested.","But Old Luo had also said that they couldnât be the ones to pass the message along. It was enough for her to know; she wasnât to tell Jiang Cheng or the others.","After all, they were residents, and the others were the property management staff. They werenât all one big group.","But now another zombie outbreak had begun.","Jiang Cheng was a girl who admired capable people. Cao Jiacai was capable now, and Aunt Pan was afraid that Jiang Cheng didnât understand the situation and would place her trust in him blindly.","Cao Jiacai was no good. He couldnât be trusted.","Aunt Pan ultimately decided to tell Jiang Cheng about it."]},{"number":112,"title":"Chapter 112: 0112","paragraphs":["The television in Jiang Chengâs home still had cracks spiderwebbing across the screen, but fortunately, it was still usable.","She had only just returned from her business trip when the zombie outbreak started up again, so she hadnât had time to replace it.","The damaged cabinet door beside the dining table, however, had already been repaired. Master Luo had fixed it later.","The television remained on, and Jiang Cheng was waiting for an official government announcement. But the channels were still showing prerecorded programs.","After cooking and eating, she tried switching channels and discovered that several local stations had lost their signal, leaving only static.","Television stations were no ordinary media outlets. In the extreme circumstances of social upheaval, they were immediately upgraded into strategic command centers.","When the power of the state mobilized, television stations were among the things that had to be protected first, along with water, electricity, gas, and communications.","Emergency orders could be issued through television to calm public panic.","During the previous zombie disaster, almost everyone would sit in front of their televisions at a fixed time each day, waiting for the latest announcement.","Some people didnât even turn off their televisions all day, terrified they might miss some sudden development.","It should be the same this time.","Some of the younger residents in the Youth Apartments were addicted to computers and the internet; some homes didnât even have televisions. They had suffered for it during the last outbreak.","It was said that after the disaster ended, many people had not only upgraded their refrigerators but also bought televisions.","This time, though, even those without televisions had nothing to worry about. There were plenty of empty apartments. They could simply pick one with a television.","Jiang Cheng lived in Room 0306 in Building Two. The room next door, 0308, was being used by Master Luo and Aunt Pan, and Aunt Pan was still living there.","But including Aunt Pan, there were now only seven people left on the entire floor. All the other rooms were empty.","In a building with a reinforced-concrete frame, some apartments were separated by load-bearing walls, but most were not. Jiang Cheng knocked on the wall between her room and Room 0304 next door and confirmed that it was not load-bearing.","That made things easy.","Her room was empty now. She had temporarily put all the quilts, candles, and other supplies into her storage space, but she couldnât occupy her storage space forever.","She needed somewhere else to put them.","She had planned to look for Aunt Pan after the older woman finished eating and returned, but unexpectedly, Aunt Pan came to find her with Li Jiangbing.","âSo it was him.â After hearing what Aunt Pan had to say, Jiang Cheng nodded.","She had already guessed that the person who reported her must have been someone from property management.","The things cleaner Liu Hongwang had done had directly opposed the interests of the homeowners. No homeowner would have defended him.","Only someone from property management would understand that if one person fell, the others might be dragged down with him.","They had waited until social order was restored and the stateâs law-enforcement agencies were functioning normally again before filing a complaint. That meant they had been too weak during the disaster to oppose the provisional committee led by Jiang Cheng.","âYou need to be careful around him. Donât let his age and scruffy beard fool youâhe knows how to fight,â Aunt Pan warned.","Jiang Cheng didnât understand.","Li Jiangbing did. He translated, âHe knows martial arts?â","âExactly,â Aunt Pan said. âHe came from a martial-arts academy and started training when he was a child. He used to work in television and film as a stunt double and met a lot of celebrities. Later, when he got older and couldnât keep doing that kind of work, he became a security guard.â","For someone from a martial-arts academy, the best career path was to test into the special police force and secure a stable government job.","Going from the film industryâs stunt world to working as a residential security guard at his age meant that Cao Jiacai had not exactly done well for himself.","Li Jiangbing sneered. âYou shouldâve seen how arrogant he was at dinner. He kept bragging nonstop.â","Actually, it could hardly be called bragging, because Cao Jiacaiâs superpower really was impressive. From the moment he awakened, it had been powerfulâstrong enough to leave Wu Jiancheng, who belonged to the same category, far behind.","Everyone now said that Security Guard Cao Jiacai was the strongest combat-type superhuman in existence.","Li Jiangbing was jealous and envious at the same time, and couldnât help sounding sour.","Jiang Cheng thanked Aunt Pan.","Her warning had come at exactly the right time. Jiang Cheng truly wasnât familiar with Cao Jiacai, but he had performed so brilliantly that, judging by her usual habits, she might really have tried to recruit him.","Jiang Cheng said, âAuntie, I happen to need your help with something.â","âTell me.â","Jiang Cheng stood up and walked over to the television. She moved aside a storage cabinet between the TV stand and the computer desk at the foot of the bed, then knocked on the wall.","âThis wall. Could you help me make a doorway? I want to take over Room 0304.â","Aunt Panâs earth-type superpower was leagues beyond Zhao Yiâs.","She went over and pressed both hands against the wall. A hole the size of a fist appeared in the surface. The bricks and mortar seemed to come alive, writhing as the opening grew larger and larger until it became a doorway a person could pass through.","On the other side was Room 0304.","The three of them walked through.","Dirty socks still lay unwashed on the sofa. Half a glass of drink remained on the coffee table, while the bag of potato chips had been sealed with a plastic clip.","The apartmentâs owner had never imagined that he might not make it back.","Li Jiangbing sighed at the sight.","Jiang Cheng walked straight across the room and knocked on the opposite wall. Goodâit wasnât load-bearing either.","âAuntie.â","Aunt Pan went over and opened another doorway in the wall. The room on the other side was 0302.","Just like that, Rooms 0306, 0304, and 0302 were connected, and the space Jiang Cheng could use expanded rapidly.","In front of Aunt Pan, she took everything out of her storage space and placed it in the rooms.","She also stored the movable furniture from Rooms 0302 and 0304 in her storage space. âWeâll put it in the underground garage for now.â","Once the furniture from 0302 and 0304 was removed, there was even more usable space.","Aunt Pan was astonished. âYou collected all these quilts and bedding? And why do you have so many candles?â","Jiang Cheng glanced at the time. âItâs already this late, and thereâs still no government announcement.â","Aunt Pan fell silent for a moment. She could think of a few possible reasons herself. âIâm afraid a lot of the officials died this time too. Things probably wonât be as good as they were during the last outbreak.â","The losses in buildings where large numbers of people worked had been devastating. She had heard that in the five-story government building in the Development Zone, at least three floors were completely deserted.","The same could probably be assumed of other government offices.","Jiang Cheng said, âIâm worried that this time they wonât even be able to guarantee water, electricity, and gas. We can survive without those things, but Iâm most worried about the heating.â","Aunt Pan sighed. âIf we were back home, we could burn firewood. But this is a city full of apartment buildings. Thereâs nowhere to make a fire. What are we supposed to do?â","âWeâll think of something when the time comes. For now, Iâm stocking up on quilts and bedding. That way, if everyone gets cold later, we wonât be caught unprepared with nothing to use.â","âYou really do think ahead,â Aunt Pan said.","Aunt Pan might not have been highly educated, but she was a better person than many.","Jiang Cheng had emptied her storage space right in front of her, and Li Jiangbing had shown no surprise at all, which meant he had known about it for some time.","Aunt Pan understood perfectly. She had finally become one of Jiang Chengâs âown people.â","And Aunt Pan was willing to be one of Jiang Chengâs own.","Some people said that Jiang Cheng was ruthless, cold-blooded, and heartless.","But after observing her for so long, Aunt Pan had already realized that Jiang Cheng was actually very good to the people around her.","That morning, Jiang Cheng had awakened her superpower, and by that afternoon, she had begun displaying its might. Ever since returning from buying supplies on Duoduo, she had noticed that many people treated her differently.","It was as if she had suddenly gone from being invisible to being seen.","She could even understand Cao Jiacaiâs arrogant swelling of pride.","But Jiang Cheng had been able to âseeâ her even before that.","Perhaps Old Luo had something to do with it. When he was alive, her Old Luo had been highly valued by Jiang Cheng.","Of course, one could also say it was because Old Luo had been capable and useful to Jiang Cheng. But Old Luo had died yesterday, and Jiang Cheng still treated her the same way. She neither ignored her nor showed her less concernâin fact, she seemed even more attentive.","In Aunt Panâs heart, anyone who could keep treating others well after they were gone, who could continue to care for widows and orphans, was a good person.","Aunt Pan was worried. âIf thatâs the case, then if the government really disappears, people like Cao Jiacai will have a field day.â","Li Jiangbingâs expression turned ugly.","Cao Jiacai knew martial arts, but Li Jiangbing wasnât necessarily any weaker than him.","But once superpowers were added to the equation, that was no longer true.","Damn it, Cao Jiacai was practically a wizard now. With nothing but a rolling pin in his hand, he could raise it and send a fireball flyingâthen raise it again and send another one.","At its largest, the fireball could be as big as a basketball. The heat radiating from it was so intense that no one dared approach.","At the dinner table that day, Cao Jiacai had even said that he controlled his attacks to burn only the zombiesâ heads because he was afraid of starting a fire.","âIf I wanted to,â he had said smugly, âI could turn their whole bodies into living flames.â","Li Jiangbing believed he really could do it. That meant, however, that there was now an enormous gap in combat strength between him and Cao Jiacai.","Aunt Panâs concern was justified.","âBig sis.â There was not a trace of worry in Jiang Chengâs eyes. âFighting has never been peopleâs first priority.â","She gave them that same smileâone that could make a person feel completely at ease.","âTo survive, peopleâs most basic needsâ¦â","âAre food and water.â","Aunt Pan thought about it for a moment, then suddenly saw the light. âThatâs right, thatâs right. Whoever they are, they still have to eat and drink their fill before they can start a fight.â","She looked at Jiang Cheng, then at Li Jiangbing, and finally thought of Song Jingshuo.","Aunt Panâs heart felt much lighter.","Sister Pan had not only helped Jiang Cheng open a passage through the wall; she had also sealed off the original entrance doors of Units 0304 and 0302 from the inside.","If anyone opened the doors to those two units from outside, all they would see were two walls.","This had been Li Jiangbingâs suggestion.","âTheyâve been thinking about moving into our building,â he had said. âZhang Lesi and the others have already made arrangements with Su Yu. Theyâre moving in tomorrow so they can be Su Yuâs neighbors.â","One of Jiang Chengâs shortcomings was that she was always standing high above everything else, in control of the overall situation and able to grasp the key points. She was always separated from the people at the grassroots by a certain distance.","As her right-hand man, Li Jiangbing perfectly made up for that weakness.","Wherever he went and whoever he met, he could hit it off with everyone. Whenever âthe peopleâ had ideas or plans, he was always the first to find out and promptly report them to Jiang Cheng.","Otherwise, how could the Iron Triangle have been formed? Each of them had their own place in the ecosystem.","Li Jiangbing and Aunt Pan each took a pack of candles and several lighters from Jiang Cheng back to their homes for emergencies.","After entering his apartment, Li Jiangbing tossed the supplies onto the shoe cabinet in the entryway and went to the bathroom to urinate first.","When he finished and was about to flush, he glanced at the yellow liquid in the toilet bowl and suddenly remembered that Jiang Cheng had asked him to purify water.","As things stood, this ability might very well prove extremely useful in the future.","Li Jiangbing tightened his grip on his waistband, gathered his energy, and shouted at the toilet, âHah!â","Then he began practicing water purification."]},{"number":113,"title":"Chapter 113: 0113","paragraphs":["The next day dawned bright and sunny again. It was also a Saturday.","On such a wonderful Saturday, people should have gone for a run and a picnic in the forest park, gone on a date, or gone shopping and watched a movie with friends.","However, the remaining more than 400 residents in the youth apartment complex had all gathered in the small square.","Compared with the situation more than two months ago, it was obvious that everyone was much more relaxed.","Zombies were just that. Once you got used to them, they weren't that scary.","Once they weren't scary, it was just a matter of whether you could defeat them and a matter of who would live and who would die.","Especially this time, the urban area was the hardest - hit area, and the pressure in the suburbs was much lighter.","The science and technology new district was already considered the near - suburbs, and Brother Dong's yard was in the far - suburbs.","People from Jixiang Jiayuan came over in a scattered way. It had always been like this. Their sense of organization was much worse than that of the youth apartment complex.","Now that there were only old men and women left, it was even more so.","But when you looked around and saw all these old people, it felt quite pitiful. The residents of the youth apartment complex found that they couldn't even get angry.","They could only offer them a share of the soup when they had meat, just to soothe their conscience.","Li Jiangbing was walking around with a bottle of water and asking people to smell it. \"It's pure water. I refined it,\" he said.","He offered it to Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan to smell. Both of them put their noses to the bottle and sniffed hard, then nodded in approval. \"There's no smell at all. It's just water.\"","Li Jiangbing corrected them. \"It's pure water.\"","To be fair, he used to only control water, and he used ordinary tap water. Jiang Cheng told him to refine pure water, which he had never thought about before.","But at the moment when he really succeeded, when the \"water\" was separated from other substances, he felt something in his mind clear up.","Li Jiangbing knew that his superpower had advanced.","Sure enough, after refining pure water several times, when he controlled ordinary tap water again, the intensity and sensitivity had improved a lot.","He could now create a water shield with a diameter of one meter in mid - air.","However, a toothbrush thrown at it could penetrate the shield.","He, a well - built fitness coach, had actually awakened a non - combat - type superpower.","It was really a pity.","Zhao Yi wanted to take a sip.","Li Jiangbing, still with a shred of conscience, quietly put the bottle away. \"I'll practice more and get purer water for you later,\" he said.","Then he turned to Song Jingshuo. \"Come on, smell it, smell it.\"","Song Jingshuo didn't take the bottle. He stared at the seemingly very clean water in the bottle for a moment, then looked up. \"What did you refine it from?\"","He was so shrewd. Li Jiangbing replied calmly, \"Just ordinary liquid.\"","The two of them looked at each other for a while.","Song Jingshuo and Li Jiangbing were completely different in terms of appearance, education, occupation, and personality. In peaceful times, they were almost impossible to become friends.","But now, they knew each other like the back of their hands.","Li Jiangbing looked upright and his eyes were bright.","Song Jingshuo pointed out the truth. \"Urine?\"","Zhao Yi/Gao Yuxuan: \"â¦â¦!!!\"","Jiang Cheng came down and saw several boys chasing after Li Jiangbing.","Even though they were muscle - bound gym guys, they didn't run. Li Jiangbing was out of breath from running, but he still argued for himself. \"It's been refined! It's pure water! Don't you understand what pure water is! You wasted your time in college!\"","Finally, he was pinned to the ground and given a good rub.","The residents had gained some experience from the previous meetings. Many of them brought their own small stools, and those who didn't have stools brought magazines and sat cross - legged on them.","An old man from Jixiang Jiayuan fanned himself and said, \"It reminds me of when I was a kid watching outdoor movies in my hometown...\"","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan pushed the property management's whiteboard to the small square and commandeered the property management's electric loudspeaker. \"Ahem, hello, everyone. Please find a place to sit. Let's start.\"","Mo Li saw Jiang Cheng coming and jumped down from the tree onto her shoulder. Jiang Cheng reached out and stroked his little head.","Zhao Yi was the main speaker. \"I guess everyone is most concerned about superpowers now. Yuxuan and I have studied for a whole day and summarized some information. Of course, since the sample size is limited, it may not be completely correct. Please judge for yourselves and feel free to add. We just hope it can be helpful to everyone.\"","First, he said, \"I heard someone say that they awakened their superpowers last night. Is there anyone else? Raise your hands so I can see.\"","Seven people in the audience raised their hands, and one of them was actually an old man from Jixiang Jiayuan.","Zhao Yi asked, \"Uncle, may I ask if you usually exercise?\"","A resident from the youth apartment complex answered quickly, \"Uncle killed zombies with us yesterday!\"","The old man said proudly, \"I can do eighty pull - ups in one breath. How many can you do?\"","Laughter rang out, accompanied by whistles and applause.","He was a typical \"park morning - exercise old man\".","\"I can't match you. Thank you, uncle,\" Zhao Yi said. \"Can the other people stand up so I can have a look?\"","The other six people stood up one after another, and two of them were property management security guards. Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan scanned them, then looked at each other and nodded.","\"Okay, please sit down.\"","\"Seeing everyone's situation, it turns out that it doesn't go beyond our speculation. I'm relieved. It means the probability that we're right has increased a little.\"","Then they got to the formal part.","Gao Yuxuan wrote on the whiteboard: What is my superpower?","Zhao Yi said, \"Actually, rather than 'What is my superpower?', what everyone should be more concerned about is 'What kind of people or which people will have superpowers?'.\"","Gao Yuxuan wrote on the whiteboard again: What kind of people can have superpowers?","This was exactly what everyone was most concerned about. Why did you have superpowers while I didn't? Why did he have superpowers while I didn't?","Exactly why? Where were the differences between us?","\"Through our observation and summary, superpowers are affected by many factors, but the basic condition for having superpowers is the same,\" Zhao Yi said.","\"That is the material basis with the body as the carrier.\"","\"We speculate that the zombie virus actually acts on everyone without discrimination. All of us have actually been infected with the zombie virus.\"","\"This virus transforms us. Some people's transformation fails. Yes, yes, you're right. Those whose transformation fails turn into zombies.\"","\"For the others who didn't turn into zombies, it can't be considered a failure. It can only be said that the degree of transformation or the success rate is different.\"","\"Those with the most successful transformation show superpowers.\"","\"Those with less successful transformation at least remain human. In fact, many people may have actually had their physiques improved, but the improvement is so slight that they haven't noticed it.\"","\"Has anyone noticed that I'm not wearing glasses today? I've been wearing glasses since junior high school, but now I don't need them. My high - degree myopia has been cured.\"","\"Is there anyone like me?\" he asked. \"If so, raise your hands.\"","Several voices in the crowd shouted, \"Yes!\", and a few people raised their hands sparsely.","Among them, there was actually an old man who said, \"I noticed yesterday that I can see clearly without wearing reading glasses.\"","This was another piece of evidence for Zhao Yi. \"See, it acts on everyone without discrimination. Regardless of gender, age.\"","\"However,\" he said, \"Among so many people, men, women, old and young, everyone has a different physique, so the effects are different.\"","\"Superpowers,\" Zhao Yi concluded. \"Only those with strong and healthy bodies can possess them.\"","Before anyone could start discussing, he added, \"Here, the 'body' can be divided into two parts: the torso and limbs make up one part, and the brain is the other.\"","Gao Yuxuan drew an outline of a human figure on the whiteboard. He used a red pen to draw a circle around the part below the neck and then circled the head separately.","Li Jiangbing was a bit confused. \"What does that mean?\"","Gao Yuxuan waved at him impatiently. \"Jiangbing, come here.\"","Still feeling guilty about that bottle of water, Li Jiangbing obediently went over to serve as their human model.","Zhao Yi said, \"Look, everyone. Jiangbing is a typical example of someone with a strong and healthy body, referring to the torso and limbs here.\"","Everyone burst into laughter.","Zhao Yi continued, \"And Jiancheng is also like that.\"","Wu Jiancheng was the building leader of Building One during the previous zombie disaster. He was a tall and sturdy man.","Zhao Yi said, \"Cao Jiacai from the property management graduated from a martial arts school.\"","Cao Jiacai looked around proudly.","Zhao Yi continued, \"That uncle just now can do 80 pull - ups. Many people in our community can't do that, right?\"","The old man comforted them, \"I was a soldier. You're different. You're all students who study a lot.\"","Zhao Yi said, \"And Aunt Pan. Yesterday, Yuxuan had an arm - wrestling match with Aunt Pan and got badly beaten.\"","Everyone laughed even louder.","Gao Yuxuan said stubbornly with his neck stuck out, \"You have no idea how strong Aunt Pan is! If you don't believe it, try it yourself!\"","The laughter grew even more intense.","Aunt Pan said, \"How can you who sit in the office all day compare with me who works physically every day?\"","Zhao Yi patted Li Jiangbing, and Li Jiangbing went back to his seat.","Zhao Yi said, \"The people I just listed prove our first point - the strength of the torso and limbs, that is, physical strength.\"","\"However,\" he changed the topic, \"besides them, there are also people like me and Yuxuan.\"","He even made self - deprecating remarks, and everyone laughed uncontrollably.","Zhao Yi usually looked like an honest homebody, but when it came to his favorite field, he could handle it with ease.","After all, he was a top student. Being a homebody didn't mean he was stupid.","This was exactly what he was going to talk about next.","\"Besides us two who don't like sports, there are also some female compatriots.\"","\"Su Yu, Zhang Lesi, and Auntie Lin, Auntie Qian.\"","Auntie Lin and Auntie Qian were the two wood - type superpower holders in Jixiang Jiayuan.","\"I've asked. Auntie Lin and Auntie Qian both like to do square dancing and travel. Although they are older, their bodies are much better than their peers. Of course, they still can't compare with young people.\"","\"As for Su Yu and Lesi, they are healthy, but definitely not strong. At best, they are at the same level as me and Yuxuan. So are the aunts.\"","\"Jiangbing could probably knock all of us down with one punch. Then why can we also have superpowers?\"","Zhao Yi began to reveal the mystery. \"Everyone knows Lesi is an intern doctor and a postgraduate. Su Yu, may I ask what your educational background is?\"","Su Yu replied, \"I have a master's degree in education.\"","\"What about Auntie Lin and Auntie Qian?\"","The answer was that one was a university professor, and the other was a senior high school teacher and a special - grade teacher.","\"One last example, Little Huang.\" Zhao Yi called Little Huang. \"Little Huang, tell us which school you're from.\"","Little Huang said, \"I'm from No. 14 Middle School. It's a key junior high school in City S. I'm in the experimental class, and my grades have always been in the top five in the grade.\" The smart kid had completely understood what Zhao Yi meant and voluntarily said everything that needed to be said.","Zhao Yi pointed at the whiteboard with a pen. \"Our conclusion is that a basic condition for obtaining superpowers is physical condition.\"","\"Among us, there are those who are very strong and those who are not that strong, but there is no one who is weak and frail.\"","\"But this physical condition doesn't just refer to the strength of the torso and limbs. It's a comprehensive evaluation of both the physical body and the brain.\"","\"If your body is strong and healthy enough, you are qualified to obtain superpowers.\"","\"If you're not that strong but you meet the standard of being healthy, then you'll get an additional score, which is the level of your brain's development.\"","\"Little Huang is the most typical example among us. He hasn't had his growth spurt yet and is thin, which is common for junior high school students. But his brain must be very good.\"","\"So, you can see. He's a junior high school student who hasn't fully developed yet, but his additional score is high enough to meet the standard.\"","\"You can be not strong, but you can't be weak.\"","\"Now, I don't think this is a virus. I think it's evolution.\"","\"You can be not strong enough, or you can be not smart enough. But you can't be both not strong and not smart.\"","\"In this evolution, the weak and the inferior won't make it. Only the strong and the smart are selected.\"","\"Perhaps this virus is a screening for humanity.\""]},{"number":114,"title":"Chapter 114: 0114","paragraphs":["Jiang Cheng immediately raised an objection. âWhat about the military? Forget brainpower for now. In terms of physical fitness alone, every soldier is unquestionably fitter than ninety-nine percent of us. And yet a considerable number of soldiers still mutated into zombies. Thatâs what happened last time, and I doubt this time will be any better. I havenât been able to get in touch with Li Feng.â","At the mention of Li Feng, Zhao Yi let out a sigh as well. He and Li Feng knew each other too. Even though they had learned to face life and death, they still hoped their family and friends could survive.","Zhao Yi explained, âFirst, letâs only discuss cases where there was no failure. For now, weâll define turning into a zombie as failure. As for why someone fails, thatâs outside the scope of our discussion.â","âThe mutation must occur at the genetic level. Everyone knows that genes are said to belong to the realm of the divine.â","âAt such a highly complex level, there are countless possible causes of failure. Anyone whoâs worked in a laboratory knows that sometimes all it takes is opening a door one extra time, or letting an incubatorâs light shine on the samples once too often, and months of work can be ruined.â","âThe more complicated the experiment, the easier it is to fail.â","âWhat weâre discussing here is this: if we define ânot turning into a zombieâ as the passing grade, then above that passing grade, thereâs another benchmark. Only when your overall score reaches that benchmark do you have a chance of obtaining a superpower.â","âPay attentionâI said a chance.â","âIn other words, passing the benchmark doesnât guarantee that youâll gain a superpower. We only inferred the existence of such a benchmark by observing the results.â","âThis can explain why people below the benchmark canât obtain superpowers.â","âBut why some people above the benchmark still donât gain superpowers is something we can never know. For now, we can only attribute it to a ârandom luck factor.ââ","âIf you pass the benchmark, you have a chance of obtaining a superpower. If you donât, your chances are zero.â","âAccording to this theory, we can say that although all soldiers are physically strong, a considerable number of them will still fail and mutate into zombies.â","âBut among the soldiers who donât fail, just like with us, only those who possess that random luck factor will obtain superpowers.â","Someone in the crowd said, âThen being strong is pointless, isnât it?â","Zhao Yi had been waiting for someone to say that. He immediately pointed at the speaker. âNo, no, youâre wrong.â","âThat brings us to the second topic we need to discuss: how physical fitness affects the strength of superpowers.â","âAlthough we donât have many observable samples, the contrast between them is striking.â","âTake fire-based abilities. Everyone can see that Cao Jiacai is stronger than Wu Jiancheng.â","âWe all know Jiancheng is no weakling. Who would dare say heâs weak? Just look at his height and build! Who would dare?â","âSo Yuxuan and I specifically interviewed Cao Jiacai, and thatâs when we learned that although he looks ordinary, he actually came from a martial arts school. Heâs been practicing horse stance since he was a child.â","âJiancheng, you tell us. If you and Cao Jiacai went head-to-head, who would win?â Zhao Yi called directly to Wu Jiancheng.","Wu Jiancheng said, âArenât you setting me up? I grew this way; I didnât train this way. Against someone whoâs actually trained, donât drag me into this.â","Cao Jiacai had now become the focus of the entire gathering.","He heard people discussing and praising him. After listening to others describe his background, some of the female residents even let out little âWow~â sounds.","It was enough to make his whole body tingle.","Cao Jiacaiâs face practically glowed.","Cao Jiacai and Wu Jiancheng made a good comparison, so Zhao Yi offered another pair. âAunt Pan and I both have earth-based abilities.â","âIt took me an entire night of practice to reach the level of strength and hardness that Aunt Pan achieved the moment she awakened her ability. She completely crushed me.â","âI spent another whole morning struggling just to make the concrete floor bulge a little, while Aunt Pan can raise stone spikes directly.â","Aunt Pan cut in, âThatâs only because I failed when I tried to make earth spikes.â","Everyone finally laughed again.","âYuxuan and Master Guoâwe jokingly call ourselves the difference between a little snake and a giant python.â","âBrother Zhou from Lucky Garden and Old Dong from BuyMore ran a lap at the same time, and Brother Zhou was a full eight seconds slower. Eight seconds!â","Brother Dong had originally planned to go home that day, but after hearing Zhou Wang say that the people from the Youth Apartments were going to discuss superpowers, he decided to stay and listen.","But after listening for a while, he started wondering: Why is Zhou the one being called âOld Zhouâ even though heâs older, while Iâm the one being called âOld Dongâ even though Iâm younger?","Tsk.","âWhen everyone is lucky enough to draw the winning ticket and become a superpowered individual, differences in physical fitness donât just affect the initial strength of their superpowers. They also affect the speed at which those abilities develop.â","âBeing physically strong is absolutely not pointless. Absolutely not.â","Zhao Yi continued, âI canât help wondering: with physiques like those of Cao Jiacai, Aunt Pan, Master Guo, and Master Dong, their abilities are already that much stronger than those of ordinary office workers like us. Just imagine how powerful the abilities awakened by soldiers in military camps must be.â","âJust how powerful could they be?â","Zhao Yi was now completely obsessed with superpowers. Every word he spoke was filled with genuine emotion, and he was exceptionally good at drawing others into his enthusiasm.","After hearing him say that, everyone couldnât help letting their imaginations run wild for a moment.","No one questioned this point anymore.","The examples were right there among them. The people he had named were sitting nearby, close enough to see just by turning their heads.","The differences were visible to the naked eye.","Those who had already obtained superpowers silently made a note to themselves: practicing their abilities wasnât enoughâthey also had to train their bodies.","You need a proper stage before you can put on a good show. That was the principle.","It was both scientific and logical.","The next topic was: âNext, letâs talk about the classification and origins of superpowers. This part is really interesting.â","Gao Yuxuan wrote on the whiteboard while Zhao Yi explained beside him. âFirst, weâll classify the basic superpowers according to the traditional Five Elements: metal, wood, water, fire, and earth. We now have all five.â","âHuh? What? Why are they the same as the Five Elements?â","âDonât get cause and effect backward, class!â Zhao Yi was so immersed in his lecture that he even called them âclassmates,â which prompted a wave of laughter.","âItâs not that superpowers are conforming to some human cultural tradition. Rather, the elements of nature were observed by our ancestors, recorded, and classified into the Five Elements.â","âThe five types of superpowers are also associated with the elements and substances of the natural world, so naturally they correspond to our âFive Elements.â Got it now?â","The person who had asked the question was Little Fang, one of the security guards. He suddenly understood. âOh, I see.â","Everyone laughed good-naturedly. Zhao Yi continued, âBesides metal, wood, water, fire, and earth, there are also special types of superpowers.â","âTake Brother Zhou and Master Dongâs wind-based abilities. In truth, wind isnât included among our Five Elements, but thatâs simply a matter of classification. Other countries have descriptions similar to our Five Elements, but theirs consist of four elements. Weâll call them the Four Elements.â","âThey are wind, fire, water, and earth.â","âWind is also an objectively existing element of nature. Itâs just that our ancestors didnât include it in their system of classification. Foreign cultures, meanwhile, didnât include wood and metal in theirs.â","âBut in essence, wind is the same as the Five Elements.â","âSo, strictly speaking, there are only four people with truly special superpowers: Jiang Cheng, Little Huang, Su Yu, and Zhang Lesi.â","âLetâs set Jiang Cheng aside for now. I canât explain her ability, so weâll have to treat her as a unique exception.â","Someone below made a wisecrack. âSet aside the highest scorer?â","The remark drew a wave of laughter.","Zhao Yi continued, âAlthough the superpowers of Little Huang, Su Yu, and Zhang Lesi manifest in completely different ways, they have something fundamental in common.â","Zhao Yi pointed to his own head. âAll three of their abilities are related to the mind, not to natural elements. So weâre going to classify all three as âmental-typeâ superpowers.â","Little Huang, Su Yu, and Zhang Lesi each thought it over. They decided the classification made sense and accepted it.","The categories of superpowers were now:","Metal, wood, water, fire, earthâand wind.","Mental-type.","Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng was thinking too.","She was beginning to suspect that her space ability wasnât actually part of the evolution caused by the zombie virus.","Perhaps she had brought it with her from the old world to this one.","In other words, she might not be a superpowered individual at all. Maybe she had simply happened to possess a personal space and gotten mixed in with the superpowered people.","Natural elements and mental abilities could both be explained through logic and science.","But space was impossible to explain.","There was no way to explain it from any angle.","Unless there was another space-type superpowered individual, proving that spatial abilities were also caused by the zombie virus.","And there was another possibilityâ","Could it be that both the space and the zombie virus had been brought into this world by her, a transmigrator from another world?","Now that would be interesting.","Jiang Cheng suddenly felt someone watching her.","She turned her head and saw that Cao Jiacai was sitting on the ground as well, his triangular eyes staring at her through the gaps between the people.","Staring straight at her.","Jiang Cheng narrowed her eyes.","She remembered now. Cao Jiacai had secretly watched her before.","But as the leader of the provisional committee, Jiang Cheng was always the focus of attention. Countless people watched her, and she had never paid attention to an insignificant nobody like Cao Jiacai.","Besides, she remembered that whenever her gaze happened to fall on him, Cao Jiacai would immediately look away, refusing to meet her eyes. Like a guilty thief.","But now, when Jiang Cheng looked over, Cao Jiacai didnât avert his gaze. Instead, he stared at her even more brazenly.","It was like a provocation. Like an invasion.","His superpower had given him courage.","Jiang Cheng didnât look away either. She met his eyes calmly.","Under the sunlight, her eyes gleamed like shattered ice.","There was no panic or flustered fear in the face of a manâs malicious, violating stareâthe kind one might expect from a young woman.","There was only sharpness and coldness.","Even the black cat perched on her shoulder looked over coldly with a pair of green eyes.","Damn it, why does she look like some kind of enchantress?","Cao Jiacai cursed inwardly.","In his mind, all those city girls whom he couldnât suppress, didnât deserve, and could never reachâgirls he normally wouldnât even deign to look at properlyâwere damnable enchantresses.","They all deserved to be subdued by exorcism.","And he was the exorcist now.","Even so, Cao Jiacai, who fancied himself a righteous exorcist, still turned his face away awkwardly under Jiang Chengâs calm gaze.","He didnât dare look back.","âNext, letâs talk about why you have this particular superpower instead of another one.â Zhao Yi grew excited. âThatâs the most interesting part.â","Gao Yuxuan said, âExactly!â"]},{"number":115,"title":"Chapter 115: 0115","paragraphs":["âWhy is it interesting? Because weâve discovered that the factors affecting a superpowerâs attribute arenât singularâtheyâre varied.â","Gao Yuxuan listed them one by one on the whiteboard:","Occupation.","Background.","Interests and hobbies.","Mental state and inner desires.","Other.","But Zhao Yi said, âFirst, we need to rule out the three outliers: Jiang Cheng, Li Jiangbing, and Song Jingshuo. Or we can just put all three of them under âOther.â Theyâre abnormal data points and will interfere with my conclusions.â","The phrase âabnormal data pointsâ made everyone laugh again.","Jiang Cheng didnât care.","Li Jiangbing: âHuh?â","Song Jingshuo: ââ¦â¦â","âBig Sister Pan said that Gao Yuxuan is an electrician, so heâs an electricity-type,â Zhao Yi said. âI deal with garbage, so Iâm earth-type.â","Everyone burst out laughing.","Even Aunt Pan laughed.","Zhao Yi admitted, âAt this point, we believe Aunt Pan hit upon the truth.â","âThe first factor affecting your superpower attribute should be your occupation.â","âIâm an environmental engineer, so Iâm earth-type.â","âYuxuan is an electrical engineer, so heâs electricity-type.â","âMaster Guo is a real electrician, so heâs electricity-type.â","âZhang Lesi is a medical student. Without a doubt, she went down the healing branch of the mental-type path.â","âCui Haiyang majored in mechanical design and manufacturing, so heâs metal-type.â","âThe second factor is your background. Your superpower may have nothing to do with the work youâre doing now, but itâs closely connected to your originsâto the things youâve been exposed to since birth.â","Aunt Pan immediately raised her hand. âIâm from the countryside, so Iâm earth-type.â","Everyone laughed again.","Aunt Pan was clearly in much better spirits than yesterday. When people had something to do and kept themselves busy, they could forget their sorrows.","Zhao Yi said, âPeople in the countryside have more opportunities to come into contact with nature than we do. Farmers are connected to the land from the moment theyâre born. So, Big Sister, I actually think either earth-type or wood-type would make sense for you.â","Aunt Pan said, âIâm no good at farming. My father always thought I was useless. Heâs a hundred times better at growing crops than I am. I was just messing around. Iâm still earth-typeâletâs not make me wood-type.â","But Zhao Yi said, âYour situation actually fits the third factor we mentioned too: interests and hobbies, as well as the fourthâyour inner desires.â","âYouâre not really all that interested in farming, are you? Youâd rather go into the city to work and make money, right?â","Aunt Pan answered frankly, âThatâs right. How much can you make farming for a whole year? If I work in the city, I get paid every month, and I can even save some money.â","Zhao Yi said, âSo growing things isnât a personal interest of yours, and your inner desires reject it as well. Thatâs why, between earth and wood, your superpower chose earth.â","âBig Sister Panâs case is the result of several factors acting together.â","âItâs a bit like being assigned to a different major during the college admissions process.â","Someone suddenly raised a hand.","It was one of the security guards at the youth apartment, a man surnamed Zhao. His superpower had awakened that morning.","There was another security guard surnamed Wang, and his power had awakened that morning as well.","Little Zhao said, âIâm a farmer too, and Iâm earth-type. But what happened with him? Heâs a farmer too, so how did he end up metal-type?â","As it turned out, Young Wang, who also came from a farming family, was metal-type.","He was a freshly awakened, unrecorded wild sample who had yet to be included in their statistics.","Zhao Yi was just about to interview Young Wang on the spot when Young Wang explained himself.","âEven though Iâm from the countryside, my great-grandfather, grandfather, and father all made iron cookware. Itâs a craft our family has passed down for several generations. Iâm the last one. Nowadays, nobody buys hand-forged iron pots anymore. Everyone buys name-brand cookware. My family couldnât make a living, so I came to the city to find work.â","It was practically a perfect explanation.","Gao Yuxuan silently gave him a thumbs-up.","Zhao Yi moved on to the next item. âInterests and hobbies.â","Little Huang suddenly raised his hand.","Zhao Yi said, âLittle Huang, you go ahead.â","Little Huang said, âMy junior, Wu Shuchen, is metal-type. He made the iron shoulder armor for me. His hobby is handicrafts. He told me that his father bought him several sets of tools, and he can even do welding.â","Another perfect sample.","Gao Yuxuan gave another thumbs-up.","Zhao Yi continued with his examples. âHere, I have to mention Auntie Lin and Auntie Qian.â","Everyone looked over.","The two aunties said, âIâm especially good at growing flowers, and sheâs especially good at growing vegetables. During the last zombie outbreak, I switched to growing vegetables too. She gave me all the seedlings.â","âBack then, everyone was stuck at home eating plain rice and dry steamed buns. We were among the few who had vegetables to eat. Vegetables were incredibly valuable in those days.â","âSigh. There were so many people growing flowers and vegetables with usâmen and women alike. None of them are still aliveâ¦â","The two aunties were wood-type. But there were other wood-types in the youth apartment too.","Many people couldnât help turning their heads to look at Song Jingshuo.","Song Jingshuo was wood-type, which was completely at odds with his personality. It had surprised quite a few people.","Apparently, it had surprised him too. His face was practically black with irritation.","âStop looking at him,â Gao Yuxuan said, laughing. âI told you, heâs an abnormal data point.â","âWe interviewed him. He has absolutely no interest in growing flowers or vegetables.â","Growing flowers would have been one thing. At least it had a certain elegance to it.","But âgrowing vegetablesâ and Song Jingshuo simply did not belong in the same sentence. The more people thought about it, the more awkward it seemed. And now that everyone knew, Song Jingshuo might actually have to grow vegetables someday.","Quite a few people were laughing so hard their shoulders were shaking.","Song Jingshuo had once prided himself on his mastery of facial expressions and emotional control. Now, his eyes were rolling so far back they looked ready to reach the heavens.","His wood-type superpower was clearly heading straight toward vegetable farming, and all his dignity was crumbling.","But Zhao Yi felt that Song Jingshuo, who had recently started letting his true personality show instead of putting on airs, was much easier on the eyes.","It was a good thing.","People shouldnât keep acting so pretentious. Sooner or later, theyâd get struck by lightning.","Zhao Yi said, âAll right. Occupation, background, and interests may look like three separate things, but theyâre actually one and the same.â","âYour work, your origins, and your hobbies cause you to spend a long time in contact with a particular element.â","âUm, Zhang Lesiâ¦ Letâs tentatively treat âpatientsâ as an element too, all right?â","âWhether you like it or not, long-term contact with a particular element creates an affinity between you and that element.â","âYour cells and genes react most strongly to that element. Their activity is highest there.â","âSo when the zombie virus acts on your body and begins sorting and classifying you, it selects the option with the highest activity.â","Everyone looked thoughtful. After considering it carefully, they all nodded.","Zhao Yi pointed to the fourth item, âMental State and Inner Desires,â and said, âLetâs skip this one for now and talk about the others first. The others are easier to explain.â","âThe most common type under âOtherâ is fire-type.â","Wu Jiancheng laughed and explained to everyone, âI work in sales. I donât have any hobbies.â","As for the other fire-type, Cao Jiacai, although he was also from a farming family, he had been sent to a martial arts school at the age of six. He lived at school year-round and trained in martial arts, so earth and wood had nothing to do with him. He didnât have any particular hobbies, either.","He said, âAll Iâm into is smoking and drinking.â","People like themâphysically strong and without any particular preferencesâended up fire-type.","Zhao Yi said, âActually, we think that every personâs body contains all five elementsâMetal, Wood, Water, Fire, and Earthâdeveloping side by side. All those careers, backgrounds, interests, and hobbies serve to activate one of the elements. When thereâs no particularly strong factor pointing toward a specific element, I believe the activation is random.â","âIf thatâs the case, then Jiangbing and Jingshuo could both be lumped into âOther.ââ","Li Jiangbing shouted, âThatâs not scientific! Thatâs not scientific! If itâs random, then why didnât I awaken the Fire element?â","Li Jiangbing firmly believed that if he were Fire-aligned too, there was no way Cao Jiacai would still be the one calling all the shots.","Damn it all.","Gao Yuxuan explained, âIf Fire could be fixed in advance, then it wouldnât be random.â","Li Jiangbing huffed angrily.","Aunt Pan, however, cut in. âNo, wait. How can Jingshuoâs be random? I already told youâhe makes money, so heâs aligned with Wood. Isnât that based on his profession?â","This was not the first time Aunt Pan had said it.","At first, everyone had ignored her and let it pass.","Now that she had repeated it, people started paying attention.","Song Jingshuo said, âAuntie, what exactly do you mean? Iâm not following.â","âArenât you in the money business? Finance, right?â","âYes, I work in finance.â","âFinance and all thatâI donât understand it,â Aunt Pan said. âBut my grandfather used to say that in this world, only two things are real and tangible: making things and growing things.â","âMy grandfather said that there was no grain in the ground to begin with. We plant seeds, and they grow into crops. Thatâs how people get food.â","âWe sell the food, and only then do we have money.â","âEverything grows and flourishes before it can generate money.â","âMy grandfather said that workers make things and farmers grow things. Everything else is empty and insubstantial.â","Everyone: Holy crap.","That grandfather had gone straight from farmer to philosopher.","The simple worldview of a farmer had smashed through all false prosperity and pointed directly at the essence of things.","Song Jingshuoâs heartâ¦ finally died.","âLastly, letâs talk about the final category. This one isâ¦ wellâ¦ somewhat vague and intangible, so weâve saved it for last.â Zhao Yi pointed to âmental state and inner desires,â carefully choosing his words.","âAs we said, this is actually shaped by a combination of factors. So your inner desires and spiritual aspirations will absolutely affect your affinity with a particular element.â","âYoung Wang, your family has a homestead and farmland too, right? Yes, see? I guessed correctly. Farmers have land, even if they have some other skill.â","âBut deep down, Young Wang, you see yourself as a craftsman who makes iron cookware, not as a farmer working the land. So in the end, you awakened the Metal element.â","Zhao Yi continued, âAnd then thereâs Zhang Lesi.â","Zhang Lesi protested, âI just want to change careers. I mean it!â","Telling people to study medicine is a crime against heaven.","Gao Yuxuan laughed. âStop struggling. You just want to save the world with your medical skills.â","Zhao Yi said, âYou may say that, but why did you choose medicine as your major in the first place? Everyone knows how many years it takes to study medicine and how hard it is. Yet you still chose it. You must have had an original aspiration. Right, Lesi?â","Zhang Lesi flushed with embarrassment and anger. âCanât I regret it?â","Everyone burst out laughing.","Zhao Yi swept his gaze over several people in the crowd and said, âAll right, that concludes our summary. Now itâs time for questions and discussion. Does anyone have anything to ask?â","When it came to the final categoryââmental state and inner desiresââZhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan had deliberately avoided the genuinely representative examples. They had used Young Wang and Zhang Lesi as borderline cases, glossing over the matter.","Because the previous night, the two of them had once again shared a room and analyzed the issue until midnight.","âOld Dong betrayed everyone, fled at the critical moment, and even made off with the supplies. Itâs only too appropriate that heâs Wind-aligned!â","The ability associated with Wind was exceptional speed.","It fit Dong Guangchao to a T.","âAs for Little Huangâ¦ sighâ¦â","âHis father died on the very first day. Sigh. A mother and son, orphaned and widowed, struggling to survive. Sigh.â","From the âorphanâ in a mother-and-orphan household to the âman of the houseâ responsible for supporting the family, the boy had been forced to grow up at incredible speed.","He moved among adults, listening, understanding, taking things in, and responding as correctly as he could.","He was constantly studying peopleâs expressions and moods, teaching himself without anyoneâs guidance. His mind was perpetually wound tight.","And so he awakened the ability to sense danger.","The influence of Dong Guangchao and Huang Xuetaoâs intense inner desires on their supernatural abilities was far too obviousâso obvious that anyone could see it at a glance.","But under this theory, one person presented a particularly delicate problem.","That was Zhou Wang, respected and relied upon throughout Auspicious Garden. Even at the Youth Apartments, he received respect and courteous treatment, with people politely addressing him as âBrother Zhou.â","He really made you think.","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan downed bottle after bottle until they had finished half a case of carbonated drinks.","They stared at each other.","âHow are we supposed to explain this tomorrow?â","If they told the truth, they would be exposing Dong Guangchao in front of everyone.","They would be ripping open Little Huangâs wound in public.","And there was no way to explain Zhou Wang.","It would be unbearably awkward.","A shut-in might be antisocial, but he wasnât stupid. He disliked dealing with people and social obligations; that didnât mean he was incapable of understanding them.","In the end, Gao Yuxuan said, âKeep it brief. Keep it brief.â","They could use Zhang Lesi as a shield and hurry past the topic.","Let everyone figure it out for themselves."]},{"number":116,"title":"Chapter 116: 0116","paragraphs":["Brother Dongâs gaze wandered.","Zhou Wang looked somewhat uneasy.","Only Little Huang seemed forlorn and thoughtful, nodding along.","Everyone had indeed âdrawn their own conclusions.â","Aside from Li Jiangbing, most people could accept the information Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan had summarized. They agreed with the majority of it.","Some had already realized that, if they followed this whole theory through, even Li Jiangbing and Song Jingshuo could find a theoretical basis for their abilities.","The only truly special person was Jiang Cheng.","Unless another space-based superpowered individual appeared, there was no way to break this âspecial status.â","As for Jiang Chengâs existence, the two men who constantly talked about science and logicâZhao Yi and Gao Yuxuanâabandoned both science and logic whenever she was involved.","âThe Chosen Maiden.â","Zhao Yi declared with absolute conviction, âI feel like Jiang Cheng is the Chosen Maiden of Youth Apartments.â","It was as if she had been born in response to the times.","âPeople like her are meant to live through troubled times, emerge from the masses, and face every challenge head-on.â Gao Yuxuan asked, âAre there any anime with that kind of theme? You know, a Chosen Maiden protagonist?â","Zhao Yi thought for a moment and said, âUsually, those are shoujo series.â","Anime had protagonists of different genders, after all. The ones the two of them usually watched featured Chosen Male protagonists saving the world. Chosen Maiden stories were generally watched by girls.","Gao Yuxuan: â...Itâs not like we canât watch one.â","They just wanted to find one into which they could cast Jiang Cheng.","âPreferably one where the heroine also has a magical pet by her side.â","The discussion and question-and-answer session began in the small plaza.","Someone asked, âAccording to all this, the military should be in better shape this time than last time, right?â","Before Zhao Yi could answer, Jiang Cheng spoke first. âNot necessarily.â","The plaza fell silent at once.","Jiang Cheng still had an incredible talent for commanding everyoneâs attention.","Everyone turned to look at her.","Jiang Cheng explained, âThe day before yesterday afternoon, only a handful of people had activated their superpowers. Everyone else awakened gradually yesterday and today.â","âBesides,â Jiang Cheng asked, âGao Yuxuan, how strong was your superpower the afternoon before last?â","Gao Yuxuan held out his hand and made a pinching gesture with his thumb and forefinger. âJust a tiny bit, about this much. All the way until that night, the current was only this big. It could kill an ant, but electrocuting a cockroach wouldâve been iffy.â","âOne or two hours,â Jiang Cheng said. âIf the military didnât undergo a large-scale awakening within one or two hours, then although their experience would mean fewer casualties than last time, there still wouldnât be as many superpowered people as you imagine.â","Jiang Cheng suddenly thought that this might also explain why there had been no survivors in the district government building.","No. She immediately discarded the idea, because every tall, densely populated building with interconnected spaces would have faced the same situation. Schools had survivors.","The sample size was simply too small.","She couldnât make a judgment based on information from just one district government building. At the very least, she needed two or threeâperhaps three or fourâsamples.","There was no need to rush, though. The zombie virus had broken out on the afternoon of August 29. After yesterday, August 30, today was already August 31. If no news arrived of a provisional government being established or a new emergency command center being formed, then her hypothesis would be confirmed.","The discussion in the plaza grew heated.","Most of it revolved around three questions: âCan I awaken a superpower?â âHow should I advance my superpower?â and âCan someone share their experience and methods for advancing?â","Almost everyone wanted a superpower.","The only exceptions were the elderly residents of Jixiang Gardens. They understood that, given their physical condition, they most likely fell below the qualifying threshold and therefore didnât hold out much hope.","Even so, they still hoped that the young people would awaken.","To witness humanityâs evolution with their own eyes before they died would make their lives worthwhile.","Zhang Lesi said, âIn theory, there should be a window period. Itâs impossible for there to be no expiration point. Everyone should still be within that window right now. No one knows how long it will remain open, or when it will close.â","âIf it closes, does that mean we wonât be able to awaken anymore?â","âProbably. Thatâs only a deduction based on basic medical knowledge, though. It may not be correct.â","âThen what should we do now to increase our chances of awakening?â","âUm...exercise?â","âAnd try to find substances you have an affinity with. Oh, rightâdonât go touching fire recklessly. Several people have already gotten burned.â","On one side, those without superpowers anxiously asked how they could awaken.","On the other, the superpowered individuals clustered together to share their experiences and insights on advancing their abilities.","Brother Dong figured the discussion had more or less reached its end.","He was already one of the stronger superpowered individuals, so there was no need for him to keep listening.","He went to find Guo Jun. âHelp me get a vehicle.â","He had his eye on the minivan they had used to rescue Little Huang the previous day. It was currently parked by the east gate of Youth Apartments.","Guo Jun had shared life-and-death hardships with him yesterday, so they could let bygones be bygones. Brother Dong had already resigned, and they had settled his wages yesterday. Once he left today, they would probably never contact each other again.","Guo Jun intended to help him one last time.","But something unexpected happened.","Guo Jun failed to start the engine. Instead, he burned out the electrical system.","Smoke immediately began pouring from the vehicleâs central console.","Guo Jun and Brother Dong: â...â","Brother Dong could hardly believe it. âArenât you the strongest electric-type superpowered person?â","That young man at Youth Apartments yesterday had managed to start the vehicle without burning out its wiring.","Guo Jun stiffened his neck and said, âThatâs because Iâm too strong!â","As he spoke, the vehicle caught fire.","Fortunately, Brother Dong had been standing outside with the door open. Guo Jun hurriedly climbed out of the vehicle.","A burning car could go up in flames within seconds. Smoke quickly billowed into the air, alerting the residents of Youth Apartments.","Everyone ran out to see what had happened.","When the security guard, Little Fang, saw that a vehicle was on fire, he was about to retrieve a fire extinguisher from the security office.","Wu Jiancheng said, âNo need!â","He was about to go over and put out the fire, but Cao Jiacai moved even faster.","Cao Jiacai walked over, stopped several steps away, and reached out with one hand. The flames on the vehicle were pulled toward him as though they had been seized by an invisible force.","A huge ball of fire spun in front of him.","A wave of heat washed over everyone.","Everyone except Wu Jiancheng retreated.","Fire-type and water-type abilities differed in one major respect.","When Li Jiangbing manipulated water, he first needed a supply of water. The amount he could control depended on how much water was available. With a lot of water, he could manipulate a massive volume; with only a little, he could control only a little.","Fire-type abilities, however, needed only a tiny flame to begin with.","Combustion required three elements: fuel, an oxidizer, and an ignition source. Although no one could explain the principle, in this world, superpowers had replaced the fuel.","As for the oxidizerâoxygenâit filled the world around them, inexhaustible and freely available.","Therefore, as long as a fire-type superpowered person had even a tiny flame, the size of the fire they could control depended solely on the strength of their superpower.","Or, put another way, it was the âmanaâ Gao Yuxuan and the others had asked Chen Lesi about when they wondered whether she could ârestore someoneâs mana.â","It was really a concept from video games: red represented the health bar, while blue represented the mana bar.","Using magic consumed mana. Once your mana was gone, you could no longer cast spells.","This concept could indeed be applied to the superpowers they were dealing with now. Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan had already tested the critical limit of exhausting their âmanaâ during practice.","A nosebleed was the warning sign.","If they forced themselves to keep going, they would stop consuming mana and start consuming their own lives.","Once blood began flowing from the ears, blood was being spat from the mouth, and the eyes throbbed painfully until bloody tears trickled out, the person would be on the verge of death.","As if he were deliberately showing off, Cao Jiacai didnât immediately extinguish the fireball in his hand. Instead, he looked around smugly and said in his less-than-standard Mandarin, âEveryone, back up.â","As everyone retreated, the fireball in his hand rapidly grew larger with a whoosh.","The distance they had retreated was nowhere near enough. A wave of heat struck their faces, making them sting, while the exposed skin on their arms and necks burned painfully. Many people cried out in alarm.","Everyone hurriedly backed away again. Someone fell, and another person stepped on their hand.","Jiang Cheng was there too, but she wasnât worried.","Although the scene was chaotic, Cao Jiacaiâs purpose was to show off and intimidate them. He wouldnât really cause an accident.","Sure enough, Cao Jiacai dispelled the fireball, turning it into two miniature flames the size of pigeon eggs. They wound around his fingertips as he idly toyed with them, much like middle-aged and elderly men rolling walnuts in their hands. Only these were far more nimble, more like the coins some young people liked to flip between their fingers.","He looked at everyone with a beaming smile. âLook at you.â","Many people cursed him in their hearts, especially the ones who had fallen and been trampled.","But they only cursed him silently.","Everyone had a sense of proportion.","Just like the last time the zombies appeared, wherever Li Jiangbing went, people addressed him as âBrother Li.â He had practically ruled the neighborhood by sheer force.","This time was no different. The only difference was that physical strength alone was no longer enough. Now, what mattered was whose superpower was stronger.","Someone couldnât help complaining.","Cao Jiacai chuckled. âI was only joking.â","As he spoke, his gaze swept over Jiang Cheng and Li Jiangbing.","Following his line of sight, Jiang Cheng saw Li Jiangbing clench his fists, the veins on his arms bulging.","Jiang Cheng walked over and gently patted him on the back.","Normally, she should have patted his shoulder, but Li Jiangbing was simply too tall and broad. So Jiang Cheng went straight for his back instead.","Li Jiangbing turned his head and relaxed when he saw that it was her.","With a smile still on his face, Cao Jiacai walked past the two of them and returned to the residential complex.","His superpower really was formidable. With a single grab, he had extinguished the flames on the van. It was only still smoking, but the smoke had choked everyone badly.","Seeing Brother Dong and Guo Jun standing beside the vehicle, Zhou Wang asked, âWhat happened?â","Brother Dong said, âI wanted to drive home.â","There werenât as many cars on the streets this time, and this one had been available with its doors unlocked.","If the Youth Apartments could make use of ownerless property, then naturally he could too.","Actually, the car he had driven home last timeâeven though its keys had still been in the ignitionâhad remained unclaimed until the zombie virus broke out again the day before yesterday.","Brother Dong had no intention of returning it. But he felt guilty and hadnât dared drive it over. He had come by suburban bus instead.","So now he had no means of transportation.","He could run very fast, but his home was in a distant suburb. It was simply too far away."]},{"number":117,"title":"Chapter 117: 0117","paragraphs":["Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan came over too.","Gao Yuxuan looked confused. âWhyâd you burn it out?â","When Guo Jun saw him, it was like seeing a savior. âYuxuan! Yuxuan!â","He hurried over, grabbed him, and asked for advice. âHow did you get the car started yesterday?â","Gao Yuxuan said, âA steady voltage of twelve volts. Actually, holding it steady for three to five seconds is probably enough.â","Guo Jun: â?â","Gao Yuxuan: ââ¦Huh?â","Guo Jun asked, âYou can control the voltage?â","Gao Yuxuan looked surprised. âYou canât?â","Gao Yuxuan was thrilled.","Though everyoneâs path to enlightenment was different, Guo Jun had awakened his superpower later yet surpassed him in strength. Since those who attained mastery could serve as teachers, Guo Jun technically counted as his senior.","Gao Yuxuan had never expected there to be something he could beat Guo Jun at.","âThe night before last,â Gao Yuxuan said, âZhao Yi and I practiced all night.â","At the time, both their superpowers had still been extremely weak. But they had practiced over and over, even creating a chart to quantify their results.","Zhao Yiâs little dirt clumps could only be measured roughlyââthree punches to smash oneâ or âfive punches to smash one.â","Gao Yuxuanâs electricity, however, could be measured.","He could obtain precise data.","Lower voltage meant weaker current, which also consumed less physical and mental energy.","As an engineering-minded man, he had something of an obsession with precision, so he practiced again and again.","In the end, he mastered the technique of releasing electricity with precise control.","Of course, that was only possible with low voltage and weak current.","By the time of the battle at Duoduo Supermarket, controlling the precision of a high-voltage electric python like Guo Junâs would be much harder.","In combat, all that mattered was power and speed.","Insufficient power was Gao Yuxuanâs weak point.","In short: he was weak.","The minivanâs electrical system had already been burned out.","A few cars were scattered along Jixiang West Street.","Brother Dong picked one that looked sturdy and hard to break down, then shouted several times, âDoes this car belong to anyone? Anyone? If nobody claims it, Iâm taking it.â","No one answered, so he treated it as abandoned property.","Cui Haiyang helped him pick the lock, while Gao Yuxuan helped start the car.","Guo Jun had actually wanted to try again, but Brother Dong stopped him. âGo home and practice. Donât use me as your test subject. Iâm in a hurry to get home.â","Truthfully, nobody liked Brother Dong. But everyone knew he was trying to get home to his parents, wife, and children.","So even though they disliked him, they still lent him a hand.","Once the car started, Brother Dong climbed in and rolled down the window. âThanks, everyone.â","Then he added, âTake care.â","He wasnât a good man, but at least his farewell was sincere in that moment.","Everyone felt a little sad and said, âTake care.â","Brother Dong also thanked Zhou Wang for taking him in the previous night, then waved at the people who had gathered to watch the commotion.","Many of them instinctively waved back.","In a world overrun by zombies, who knew whether they would ever have the chance to meet again? They might as well say goodbye.","Brother Dong turned the steering wheel and made a U-turn, occasionally glancing outside.","He saw Jiang Cheng standing at the west gate of the Youth Apartments. The big man stood with his hands on his hips, bending slightly as he listened to her.","That tall, handsome man leaned his shoulder against the gatepost, arms crossed over his chest. One of his long legs was straight, while the other was folded over, its toe touching the ground.","The two girls were discussing something nearby.","Many of the elderly residents of Jixiang Garden began to cry when they saw this stranger leaving.","The metal-element superpowered person stood in front of the minivan whose electrical system had burned out, shaping the hood.","The front of the vehicle had already been turned around. Brother Dong didnât see the finished result, but he could tell it was being shaped into something resembling a shoulder guard.","The car drove out of Jixiang West Street. The main road ahead was deserted.","The residential district of the Technology New Area looked like an empty city.","The moment he left Jixiang West Street, all the warmth and bustle of human life disappeared.","Outside lay a world filled with zombies.","Fortunately, he had a home. His parents, wife, and children were waiting for him there.","Brother Dong stomped on the accelerator and sped down the empty road.","At the entrance to the Youth Apartments on Jixiang West Street, Li Jiangbing said, âI was just thinking about whether I could put out that fireball. Then I realized I didnât have any water nearby.â","At that moment, Li Jiangbing became acutely aware of the limitation of his superpower.","A fire-element superpower only needed a tiny flame to get started.","But however much water he needed depended on how much water was available nearby. That made his ability far too limited.","After all, it was obvious that a water-element superpower wasnât meant for combat.","Jiang Cheng asked, âCan you purify wastewater now?â","Li Jiangbing replied, âNo problem anymore. I just need more practice. The more I practice, the faster Iâll get, and the more water Iâll be able to produce.â","Jiang Cheng nodded, then asked, âCan you extract water directly from the air?â","Li Jiangbing blinked. âHuh?â","Ever since the one-jin-of-iron-and-one-jin-of-cotton incident, Jiang Cheng had realized just how little culture this man possessed.","âThereâs always water in the air,â she reminded him. âOtherwise, why would we use a humidity meter to measure the humidity in a room?â","âOh.â Li Jiangbing rubbed the back of his head. âIâll give it a try.â","He focused. First, he had to sense it.","The instant he did, he realized Jiang Cheng was right. There really was water all around him, filling the world between heaven and earth.","It was inexhaustible and infinite.","If he had been able to extract water from the air just now, could he have put out Cao Jiacaiâs fireball on the spot?","Butâ¦","Li Jiangbing relaxed his shoulders and panted twice.","Jiang Cheng asked, âIs it very difficult?â","Li Jiangbing nodded and explained, âItâs much harder than extracting pure water from thatâ¦ thatâ¦ that wastewater.â","Song Jingshuo was right beside them, leaning against the gatepost with his arms crossed. At those words, the corner of his mouth twitched.","You have the nerve to tell Jiang Cheng what you extracted that pure water from?","Jiang Cheng raised her head and looked at the blue sky and white clouds. The autumn air was crisp and clear.","âThat makes sense. The air is especially dry this time of year. It would probably be much easier in summer, when itâs raining or unbearably humid.â","She told Li Jiangbing, âGo back and practice slowly.â","But Li Jiangbing said, âIâll try again.â","He focused once more and exerted himself, clenching both fists.","Jiang Cheng watched as the veins on the backs of his hands and across his forehead bulged. Before long, blood began to trickle from one of his nostrils.","Why was he getting a nosebleed so quickly?","Song Jingshuo frowned and warned him, âDonât push yourself too hard!â","But Li Jiangbing was determined. He could feel the unpleasant pressure building in his head, yet he gritted his teeth and endured it. When even his ears began to ache, he suddenly said, âI did it.â","Song Jingshuo: â?â","Song Jingshuo pushed away from the post and came closer. Only then did he finally see it clearly.","Half a foot in front of the tip of Li Jiangbingâs nose, a tiny marble-sized ball of water floated in the air.","It was so transparent that they hadnât noticed it before.","But when someone moved and changed the angle, the water ball refracted the sunlight, making it visible.","Song Jingshuo carefully considered his choice of words and offered a venomously sarcastic compliment. âAdorable.â","Li Jiangbing was furious.","If he hadnât been concerned about ruining the handsome manâs image, he would have wanted to grab Song Jingshuo by the neck and force him to say it again.","âDo you know how exhausting this is?â he huffed.","Jiang Cheng, however, followed up with another question. âHow exhausting?â","Li Jiangbing answered solemnly, âExtremely exhausting.â","He tried to explain it to Jiang Cheng using his less-than-impressive command of the language.","âControlling water thatâs already there doesnât take much effort. Itâs as natural and easy as walking.â","\"Extracting pure water from sewage is a bit tiring, but not that exhausting. It's like lifting a 15-kilogram dumbbell. It has a bit of weight, but it's no big deal for me. I'll get used to it with some practice.\"","\"However, extracting water from the air feels like trying to lift a 120-kilogram barbell. It's so heavy right from the start, with no buffer at all.\"","Li Jiangbing was still recalling that feeling just now and trying to describe it more clearly: \"The water is indeed in the air, but there are other things in the air too. Ah, right, it's just the air.\"","\"Anyway, there is a kind of... um...\" between the water and the air.","Song Jingshuo said, \"Gravitational force?\"","\"Right!\" Li Jiangbing continued, \"When I want to extract the water, I have to separate it from the air. But the gravitational force between the water and the air is just giving me a hard time. It's like a tug - of - war.\"","As he said this, he gestured with his hands as if he was pulling and tugging.","Jiang Cheng said, \"Reaction force?\"","\"!!\" Li Jiangbing slapped his palm with his fist, \"Great word!\"","In the microscopic world, there are interactive forces between particles. There is an attractive force, that is, electromagnetic force, including dispersion force and induction force, between water molecules and other gas molecules in the air.","These forces in the microscopic world are, of course, tiny and imperceptible to humans in the macroscopic world.","But for the particles in the microscopic world, they are powerful or even huge.","When Li Jiangbing tried to separate the water molecules from the gas molecules, he actually intervened in the microscopic world with his superpower as the interface.","Once he intervened, he could no longer be considered purely in the macroscopic world.","When he tried to separate the water molecules, what was projected and transmitted to him at the interface between the microscopic and macroscopic worlds was not the imperceptible electromagnetic force for humans.","It was directly like a 120 - kilogram barbell.","So heavy right from the start.","That's why Li Jiangbing had a nosebleed in just a short period of time.","\"The intensity has been increased,\" Li Jiangbing's eyes sparkled with excitement.","Song Jingshuo asked, \"What do you mean?\"","Li Jiangbing described it with the most appropriate example he could think of: \"Without considering the muscle issue and just talking about improvement through weight, which is more useful, a 15 - kilogram dumbbell or a 120 - kilogram barbell?\"","\"And! And this barbell can improve my ability much faster than the dumbbell!\"","In just two days, everyone was exploring the methods of improving and advancing their superpowers even during the battles in \"Buyduoduo\".","It has now been confirmed that a person's superpower has a certain amount, just like a person's strength, which can be exhausted.","When you start having a nosebleed, it means you are approaching exhaustion. The more blood flows from your seven orifices, the closer you are to the limit and death.","But as long as you don't die, if you stop and rest, and recover your strength, your superpower will increase.","Song Jingshuo and Jiang Cheng immediately understood.","Purifying ten batches of urine indoors might not consume as much energy as extracting a few drops of water from the air.","And the time taken is very short.","Li Jiangbing has found a shortcut to improving his water - based superpower."]},{"number":118,"title":"Chapter 118: 0118","paragraphs":["Guo Jun and Gao Yuxuan were discussing the problem of precise output.","Guo Jun was eager to master the technique.","âOnce the zombies are all dead and things return to normal,â Guo Jun said, âIâll be able to charge my own phone. Iâll generate my own electricity for all the appliances at home! Thatâll save money!â","âThen youâll need a bank of lead-acid batteries as backup power,â Gao Yuxuan said. âI heard lithium batteries have already been developed, but they can only power small appliances. In the future, though, thereâll definitely be high-capacity battery banks. Weâll have it easy then.â","With suitable energy-storage equipment, people with electrical abilities could live without ever having to pay an electricity bill.","The two of them launched into an enthusiastic discussion about how large a lead-acid battery bank would need to be to support a householdâs normal power consumption.","Nearby, Cui Haiyang was eyeing the scrapped van. It had already been burned, so there was no point in wasting it. It was all metal, after all.","Metal was a wonderful thing. It could be reused.","Cui Haiyang pressed a fingertip against the hood, and the hood began to change shape.","The metal shoulder armor Wu Shuchen had made looked pretty good, and Cui Haiyang decided to copy it.","Before long, a shoulder guard formed from the vanâs hood had taken shape. It was placed on top of the engine.","The metal had also been refined during the reshaping process, leaving behind neither dust nor impurities. It gleamed brightly, with a look that combined retro style and futuristic sci-fi.","Everyone nearby let out amazed cries of, âWow!â","Someone couldnât resist. âLet me try it! Let me try!â","He reached out and picked up the shoulder guard.","A moment later, he dropped it in a hurry. âOw, fuck! Hooâhoo!â","He had forgotten that the van had just been through a fire!","Cao Jiacai grabbed the flames away in one sweep, making the van look clean and spotless, but the metal itself had not yet cooled down.","Cui Haiyang had only touched the hood lightly with his fingertip. In reality, it had been the edge of his fingernail making contact, without his fingertip pad touching it at all. He had simply overlooked the danger and forgotten to warn everyone.","He hurried over. âAre you all right? Are you all right? Go find some running water and cool it down!â","But Zhang Lesi came sprinting over in a single bound.","Everyone wanted to improve their abilities, and improving required practice. But how was Zhang Lesi supposed to train?","Now that a ready-made practice subject had appeared, how could she let it go?","âIâll do it! Iâll do it!â","Healing was truly the kind of superpower people desperately needed.","And it really worked.","Under the faint white glow, the injured person said in delighted surprise, âIt doesnât hurt anymore! It works! It really works!â","The others gathered around in astonishment and pulled his hand over to examine it closely.","Zhou Wang looked at the groups of three or five people scattered along Jixiang West Street, chatting noisily among themselves.","He knew perfectly well that zombies were everywhere in the city, that countless people had died, and that many others were still trapped and struggling to survive. Yet somehow, he felt as if they were living in peaceful, tranquil times.","Just then, Jiang Chengâs phone rang.","In the current circumstances, whenever someoneâs phone suddenly rang, it attracted an unusual amount of attention. There was a very good chance it meant trouble.","And sure enough, it wasnât good news.","The caller ID alone made Jiang Cheng raise an eyebrow.","It was one of the leaders of Yujing Xiangyuan.","Yujing Xiangyuan had never formed a particularly united organization. It had always been divided into several groups, each governing itself.","It was only later, when they began operating alongside the Youth Apartments, that they reluctantly became a temporary force under Jiang Chengâs overall command.","Jiang Cheng had the phone numbers of several people from Yujing Xiangyuan. When she had sent out the group message, she had sent it to everyone in her contacts, including them.","Whether they had made it back, however, was unknown.","Jiang Cheng answered. âHello?â","âJiang Cheng?â","âThatâs me.â","âThis is Xia Hui from Yujing Xiangyuan.â","âI know. What is it?â","âJiang Cheng, Iâm sorry. I didnât believe your warning. Iâm trapped at my company right now.â","âYou donât need to apologize to me,â Jiang Cheng said.","Xia Hui had nothing to apologize to Jiang Cheng for. He had let himself down. Someone had warned him in advanceâa stroke of incredible luckâand he had failed to seize the opportunity.","There was no such thing as a regret pill. And there was no time now to ask Jiang Cheng how she had known in advance.","Xia Hui lowered his voice and pleaded, âMy parents are at Yujing Xiangyuan. Theyâre trapped in their apartment. There are four or five zombies in the hallway on our floor. Itâs just the two of them, and they donât have any armor. Thereâs really nothing they can doâ¦ Jiang Cheng, please. Help me.â","Jiang Cheng did not answer immediately. Instead, she asked, âWhatâs the situation like in the city?â","âNot good. Weâre trapped in an office building. There are a lot of zombies on the streetsâpacked together.â","âHas anyone awakened a superpower?â","âHuh? You already knew about that? Is it already common knowledge?â Xia Hui said. âYes. Three of us, including my coworkers, have abilities.â","Jiang Cheng asked, âMetal, wood, water, fire, earth, wind, electricity, or something else? What kind of abilities do you have?â","âBy metal, do you mean manipulating metal?â Xia Hui asked. âThe three of us can all reshape metal.â","âThree metal-type ability users? What kind of work do you do?â","Xia Hui didnât understand why Jiang Cheng was asking about such âirrelevantâ information at a time like this. But he needed her help, so he answered patiently. âWe work in mechanical design and manufacturing.â","Good. Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuanâs theory was fundamentally sound.","Of course, they had worked backward from the results, so their conclusions inevitably contained subjective assumptions and skipped over some anomalous data. But at least for now, the general direction and basic framework were correct.","Jiang Cheng asked, âCan you make it back?â","Xia Hui was silent for a moment before answering firmly, âI definitely can!â","âOur floor has already been cleared. Weâve made more than twenty sets of metal armor, as well as weapons.â","âWe contacted people on the other floors through the landline. Some of them have abilities too, and everyone is preparing to make a move together.â","âIâm definitely going to make it back alive.â","âBut my parents need help right now, Jiang Chengâ¦â His voice was filled with pleading.","A metal-type ability user was asking for assistance.","Jiang Cheng said, âWhich building and which apartment?â","Xia Hui was overjoyed.","A month earlier, he had already witnessed Jiang Chengâs command abilities and the Youth Apartmentsâ combat strength. He didnât know how many people from the Youth Apartments had survived this time, but there wasnât the slightest trace of panic in Jiang Chengâs voice. She was as calm and steady as ever, and simply hearing her put people at ease.","Xia Hui gave her his apartment number, then said with ringing conviction, âJiang Cheng, I owe you one.â","âDonât say that,â Jiang Cheng replied. âJust make it back alive.â","Xia Hui said, âI will!â","Jiang Cheng hung up and looked up. Everyone around her had gathered in a circle, waiting for her to speak.","Jiang Cheng waved her phone. âWeâve got a job.â","A crowd of people whose superpowers were brimming with nowhere to go began howling excitedly.","Zhou Wang watched it all, feeling dazed and unreal.","At the very beginning, going out to kill zombies had required immense courage and a willingness to face certain death. Every person who stepped outside had been a hero.","The moment they left their homes, the air had been filled with sorrow.","How had things turned into this?","Zhou Wang thought back for a moment. It had probably started when ordinary people got their hands on armor.","The appearance of armor had dramatically reduced the risks humans faced when fighting zombies. It had allowed humanity to shift completely from defense to offense and confront the zombies in direct combat.","The difference between humans and animals lies in the use of tools.","Armor erased the imbalance between zombiesâwho âwerenât afraid of injury, pain, or deathââand humans, who could be done in by âa single minor wound.â","Zombies had been downgraded from âterrifying monstersâ to âdamned monsters.â","Humanity was no longer afraid.","âBrother Zhou, come on. Letâs figure this out together.â Jiang Cheng nodded toward the inside of the residential compoundâs gate, inviting Zhou Wang in.","Zhou Wang: ââ¦â¦â","Zhou Wang could almost predict that Yujing Xiangyuan was probably in much the same situation as Jixiang Jiayuanâthe young people had all gone downtown to work, leaving only empty-nest elderly residents behind.","He already had one such residential compound on his hands. But there was no helping it; his own home was there too.","He really didnât want to take on another compound like this. He had absolutely no desire to manage any other residential community.","But he had no choice. He still held the position and responsibilities of leader of Jixiang Jiayuan. Since he needed something from the Youth Apartments and had to rely on them, he could only lower his head and comply.","Besides, Little Huang had already hurried through the gates of the Youth Apartments and stopped inside, turning sideways to wait for him.","In the eyes of the young people, helping a neighboring residential compound escape its predicament was perfectly normal. Especially now that everyone had armor and supernatural abilities, and there were genuinely very few zombies in the Technology New District.","The advantage was entirely on humanityâs side.","Under Little Huangâs expectant gaze, Zhou Wang could only step forward and follow him.","The meeting had started at half past nine, and it was now nearly noon. After discussing the matter, everyone decided to go after lunch.","They couldnât fight on empty stomachs.","They also needed to make some preparations.","There werenât enough sets of armor for everyone, but now they had metal-type supernatural abilities.","The Youth Apartments currently had twenty-two ability users, five of whomâincluding Cui Haiyang and Security Guard Little Wangâhad metal-type abilities.","Of the six people from Jixiang Jiayuan who had returned alive yesterday, five were ability users, including one with a metal-type ability.","Now that the six metal-type ability users had gathered together, they enthusiastically began manufacturing metal armor.","Their goal was to ensure that everyone had armor and everyone had a weapon.","As for weapons, someone even tried making a crescent-shaped blade.","They sharpened the front edge, found a mop, removed the mop head, and used metal manipulation to attach the blade directly to the mop handle. In an instant, they had a long-handled weapon.","Everyone was already highly experienced at killing zombies. After testing it in their hands, they immediately realized how suitable it was.","Li Jiangbing was the first to give it a try.","With one sweep of the crescent blade, Li Jiangbing chopped through a young tree that had been replanted in the residential compound six months earlier! A long-handled weapon allowed one to maintain a safe distance from a zombieâor a tree.","â!!â Li Jiangbing exclaimed. âThis oneâs mine!â","Everyone burst out laughing. âSure, sure. Itâs yours. Weâll keep making more.â","Then they discovered that they didnât have enough suitable wooden handles.","Making the entire weapon out of metal would add too much weight and affect its use.","In the end, Zhou Wang called the people at Jixiang Jiayuan. The homes there were all traditional family-style units, and many households had old-fashioned mops.","They searched from household to household and collected more than thirty handles.","The metal-type ability users made more than thirty crescent blades.","At present, Security Guard Little Wang had the best control among the metal-type ability users.","Most of the metal-type ability users worked in fields related to machinery. Only Security Guard Little Wang was a genuine blacksmith.","He was the only one who had truly worked with iron using the strength of his own hands, rather than relying on machines.","His precision in shaping metal was exceptionally high.","The task of sharpening the weapons was therefore left to him.","The other metal-type ability users didnât waste their energy on that. They focused their abilities on shaping the blades and increasing their hardness.","Some handled the shaping, while others strengthened the metal.","The rough, unsharpened crescent blade was handed to Young Wang. Holding it in his hands, he thinned and sharpened the crescent edge in no time.","It was then passed to the next person, who secured it to a wooden handle.","Before long, a highly practical long-handled crescent blade was complete.","The ability users naturally formed an assembly line."]},{"number":119,"title":"Chapter 119: 0119","paragraphs":["After finishing the armor, they moved on to making crescent shovels.","The advantage of an assembly line was that everyoneâs proficiency in their assigned task steadily improved.","The superpowered individuals realized that using their abilities to work wasnât merely a way of contributing labor for everyoneâs sake. At the same time, it also trained and strengthened their powers.","Young Wang even started a knife-sharpening service for everyone.","Those who used edged weapons brought them to him. Most peopleâs weapons werenât very large; many of them were simply kitchen knives.","He became faster and faster at sharpening them. In the end, all it took was a pinch of two fingersâwhooshâand an extra line of icy brightness appeared along the blade, gleaming sharply.","Jiang Cheng ate by herself at home. Lately, she had been finding cooking more and more of a hassle.","She planned to leave the dishes in the sink and wash them when she got back that afternoon.","She stood up from the dining table. The dishes on the table vanished, followed immediately by the table and chairs, then the sideboard.","She walked over to the sink, and the used dishes appeared there.","When she returned to the dining area, the vanished table, chairs, and sideboard reappeared.","She passed by the sofa and coffee table. The sofa and coffee table disappeared for an instant, then reappeared. The same happened with the bed and computer desk.","Jiang Cheng wandered casually around her home. Wherever she went, the furniture and belongings vanished for a second before reappearing.","If someone had been there, they would have thought their eyes were playing tricks on them, as though everything in the room were constantly flickering.","In reality, Jiang Cheng was practicing her superpower every moment.","With repeated practice, not only did she grow faster at storing and releasing things, but she no longer needed to touch an object directly with her hands.","This meant that there could be a distance between her and whatever she wanted to store.","The significance of this was enormous.","Although the distance was tiny for now, Jiang Cheng believed that as her superpower grew stronger, it would eventually reach a range that was both convenient and safe for her.","Jiang Cheng walked over to the bed, and it vanished.","The floor beneath it wasnât dirty, because after storing the bed in her storage space for the first time, Jiang Cheng had mopped the floor.","From that perspective, having a space-type superpower made mopping incredibly convenient.","But that was beside the point. Jiang Cheng walked through the spot where the bed had been and came to the recliner. The bed reappeared behind her.","Jiang Cheng stored the recliner, then released it again. When she looked up, she saw a little bird perched on a branch outside.","Jiang Cheng narrowed her eyes.","[Mo Li.] She called him through telepathy. [Mo Li.]","In the blink of an eye, Mo Li appeared at the window.","Through telepathy, Jiang Cheng told him, [Bird. I want it alive.]","Mo Li turned his head and disappeared.","Before long, the mysterious little black cat appeared at the window again, a bird dangling from his mouth. He placed it in Jiang Chengâs hands.","Then he curled up on the recliner, watching to see what Jiang Cheng intended to do.","Jiang Cheng held the little bird in her hands.","Her mental link connected to the storage space. It was empty now, a state of pure nothingness.","She wanted to test whether a living creature could enter the space.","She stared at the bird and focused her thoughts.","Yet the little bird merely looked at her with its beady green eyes. Nothing happened.","Jiang Cheng tried several times, but every attempt failed.","It seemed that living creatures could not be stored in the space.","[Safety protocol.]","Jiang Chengâs pupils widened slightly. She had caught the information as it drifted through her mind.","There seemed to be something else as well.","Jiang Cheng struggled to grasp it.","Mo Li lay on the recliner in the sunlight, looking up at Jiang Cheng curiously.","From his perspective, Jiang Cheng was still holding the bird and standing motionless.","He had no idea that an intense battle was taking place inside Jiang Chengâs mind. She could sense that there really was a crack in whatever had been locked away deep inside her brain. All the information was leaking through that crack.","She desperately tried to force the crack completely open, but encountered an obstacle that was almost impossible to overcome.","Something deep within her mind seemed to have wrapped itself around her, as though it wanted to devour her.","The sudden ring of the telephone interrupted the struggle in her mental world.","Jiang Chengâs shoulders abruptly relaxed, and she broke free of that spiritual realm. Her forehead was covered in sweat, and she was breathing hard.","After steadying her breathing, Jiang Cheng finally freed one hand to answer the call.","âLi Jiangbing?â","Li Jiangbingâs booming voice came through the phone. âJiang Cheng, are you coming?â","Jiang Cheng composed herself and glanced at the bird in her hand. âCome over here first.â","âHuh? Sure.â","Li Jiangbing arrived almost immediately. Since they would be fighting later, he had already put on his extra-large suit of armor.","In his hand was the new crescent shovel.","Its design was extremely anime-like.","The moment he entered, he asked, âWhat do you need me for?â","Jiang Cheng closed the door and handed him the bird. âHold this.â","âWhat theâhey, holy crap!â","Li Jiangbing hurriedly set down the crescent shovel and cupped the little bird between his two bear-sized paws.","âWhereâd this bird come from? Are you going to keep it as a pet?â","Instead, Jiang Cheng said, âTry to draw the water out of its body.â","Li Jiangbing, who had been looking down and teasing the bird, froze. He lifted his head.","Jiang Cheng continued, âI was thinking about this earlier. Since you can extract water from the air, what about extracting it from a living body?â","Li Jiangbing hesitated. âYou want me to test it on this one?â","âNo. This one is for you to keep as a pet. Test it on me instead. Drain all the blood from my body.â","Li Jiangbing: â...Youâre starting to sound like Jingshuo. Heâs been acting completely nuts these past two days. Donât let him infect you.â","Song Jingshuo had completely lost it over the obvious potential of his wood-based superpower for growing vegetables.","He had abandoned his former, leader-like air of making everyone feel warmly cared for. Instead, he had begun pulling faces and making all sorts of sarcastic remarks.","Strangely enough, this hadnât made people dislike him. On the contrary, some people who had previously only had an average relationship with him began drawing closer to him.","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan, for example, had started calling him âJingshuoâ all the time.","Li Jiangbing slowly spread his hands apart. The bird lifted its round head, its eyes as tiny as green beans.","Li Jiangbing looked a little reluctant. He sighed. âIâm sorry.â","He brought his hands together, closed his eyes, and activated his power.","A second later, he opened his eyes and let out a huge sigh of relief. He was even a little pleased.","âIt doesnât work.â","The bird was completely unharmed.","Jiang Cheng got straight to the root of the matter. âWhy not?â","Li Jiangbing explained, âExtracting water from the air is like lifting a 120-kilogram barbell. Extracting water from its body is like lifting a 500âno, a 1,000-kilogram super-heavy barbell.â","At 120 kilograms, he could still excitedly regard it as a shortcut to training, pushing himself to exhaustion each time in the hope of achieving rapid progress.","At 1,000 kilograms, perhaps he really could manage it someday, after his superpower had reached a certain level. But for now, it was something he could give up on without the slightest guilt.","Jiang Cheng asked, âIs the force of attraction between the molecules greater than the attraction between the water vapor molecules in the air?â","âItâs a little different.â Li Jiangbing gave Jiang Cheng a detailed explanation. âWith the water in the air, itâs basically a matter of me wrestling with it. My strength is still small, but when I put all my effort into it, you can see that I can still extract a tiny bit, right?â","âBut itâs not just that the molecules have a stronger attraction. I also feel like it has a layer of something around itâsomething invisible and untouchable, but still perceptible. It gathers all of thisâall this, um, liquid? Blood and whatever?âtogether, holding it tightly in one mass. It seems to be a single entity. Itâs very difficult to separate.â","âIs it some kind of safety protocol?â","âWhat kind of existence is it?â","âProtecting living organisms?â","Jiang Cheng nodded. In the past, whenever they turned on the faucet, the water would gush out.","Jiang Cheng raised her hand and waved it a few times. âCan you make the water follow my hand?â","That was relatively simple.","Li Jiangbingâs supernatural ability had improved at astonishing speed. He focused and controlled a ball of water, pressing it against Jiang Chengâs palm. âHey, I can make you a hydrating facial mask, hahaha.â","Jiang Cheng moved her hand to the side, and Li Jiangbing hurriedly made the water follow.","She waved her hand several times. Li Jiangbing stopped joking around and concentrated on controlling the water ball. It could basically catch up with her on the very next instant.","But that difference of âone instantâ still created a noticeable lag.","Jiang Cheng began waving her hand continuously without letting it pause in any one position. âChase me.â","âWhoa, no way.â Li Jiangbing tossed out a cheeky remark before continuing to make the water ball chase Jiang Chengâs hand.","With continuous movement, the water ballâs lag became obvious. It kept chasing, but could never catch up.","Jiang Cheng lowered her hand. âAll right. It still has a long way to go.â","Li Jiangbing had long since grown used to the way Jiang Cheng gave instructions without explanation. He would simply do as he was told first, then ask why afterward. âWhatâs this for?â","Jiang Cheng said, âI want you to achieve this: seal someoneâs head in a ball of water. If you canât cover the whole head, then the face will do. No matter how much they struggle, they mustnât be able to break free.â","Li Jiangbing sat down on the sofa and ran a finger over the feathers on the little birdâs head. âThat wonât work.â","He said, âI already tried. I poured water into the zombiesâ brains, but they werenât afraid. They canât drown.â","Jiang Cheng walked over, braced one hand against the wall, leaned down close to Li Jiangbing, and said softly, âBut humans can.â","Li Jiangbing jerked his head up.","The room was so quiet you could hear a pin drop.","The two of them stared into each otherâs eyes.","âYouâyouâyou!â Li Jiangbing jabbed a finger angrily through the air. âStop trying to scare me all the time!â","âPsycho!â","Li Jiangbing had realized it a long time ago: everyone was a psycho now.","He didnât know whether everyone had already been crazy before the zombie outbreak, or whether the zombies had driven them all insane.","Either way, they were all lunatics.","Song Jingshuo was a psycho. Hell, with so many people unable to get enough to eat, he still insisted on maintaining his elite persona.","Jiang Cheng was one too. She looked like such a refined, clean, beautiful girl, yet all of a sudden she would calmly say something that scared the living daylights out of you.","He was a psycho himself. When he killed zombies with the militia, he was genuinely happy. He felt happier than he ever had in peaceful times. If that wasnât insanity, then what was?","A lot of people were crazy.","You couldnât tell from how everyone joked and laughed on the little plaza during the day.","Many people would suddenly sit bolt upright in bed in the middle of the night and burst into heart-rending sobs.","So many people couldnât get in touch with their parents or families. They were probably orphans in all but fact.","How could they not go insane? Deep down, everyone had already lost their minds.","Only by gathering together could they manage to keep up the appearance of being normal human beings."]},{"number":120,"title":"Chapter 120: 0120","paragraphs":["They regrouped that afternoon. When Aunt Pan arrived, her clothes were still speckled with cooking oil.","She looked like an ordinary rural migrant worker. Usually, women her age worked as housekeepers, cleaners, cooks, or something along those lines.","Who would have guessed that she was actually a formidable earth-type superhuman?","Seeing the grease spots on Aunt Panâs clothes, Jiang Cheng turned to Li Jiangbing and asked, âIs Aunt Pan still cooking for the property management office?â","âShe is,â Li Jiangbing said. âIâve even joined her for meals.â","At noon, he had taken a basin to collect his food, then carried it home to eat. That way, he didnât have to look at Cao Jiacaiâs face while eating.","The âbasinâ was actually the inner pot from a rice cooker.","âBut Auntie doesnât wash the dishes anymore,â Li Jiangbing continued. âCao Jiacai arranged for us to take turns.â","Jiang Cheng paused. âCao Jiacai arranged that?â","âYep.â Li Jiangbing snorted.","Jiang Cheng nodded. She suddenly remembered that Manager Wang had indeed been unusually inconspicuous over the past few days.","So inconspicuous, in fact, that she could barely remember there was such a person. Whenever she needed something from the property management office, she either went to Aunt Pan, Little Fang, or Yang Xinyan.","âWe have to find a way to get Auntie out of this,â Jiang Cheng said.","A society thrown into chaos was not necessarily a society without order. New forms of order would emerge spontaneously. Manager Wang was still around, but Cao Jiacai had already become the de facto head of property management.","Yet Aunt Pan, who was just as powerful a superhuman, was still huffing and puffing away, cooking for them.","âHuh?â Li Jiangbing gave her a hesitant, rising-toned response.","Jiang Cheng looked at him questioningly.","Li Jiangbing answered honestly, âAuntieâs cooking is really delicious.â","That was why Cao Jiacai had arranged for everyone to take turns washing the dishes instead of replacing Aunt Pan.","Aunt Pan was simply too honest.","Song Jingshuo walked over. âWhat are you talking about?â","Jiang Cheng asked him, âDo you cook for yourself at home?â","âI do.â","âDonât you find cooking annoying?â","Song Jingshuoâs cooking was good, which meant he must actually enjoy it. He said, âItâs all right.â","âLately, Iâve somehow started finding cooking really bothersome. Itâs strange. I cooked for such a long time before tooâ¦â Jiang Cheng suddenly understood.","That was why she had abruptly lost her enthusiasm for cooking.","She had indeed spent two months cooking before, but during the previous disaster, all she had really done was cook rice and eat it with salted eggs, canned food, or pickles. The only actual cooking involved was making a pot of rice.","Now, conditions had improved. They had vegetables and meat, which meant they were supposed to eat proper meals.","But when you were cooking a proper meal for just one person, you spent an hour preparing it and five minutes eating it.","Back when she had been working, she had only needed to cook one meal a dayâdinnerâand even that was often bought outside.","Now, she had to prepare three meals a day.","Jiang Cheng folded her arms. ââ¦We need to find a solution to this cooking problem.â","Li Jiangbing suggested, âWhy donât you share meals with Su Yu? She really likes cooking.â","Song Jingshuoâs gaze drifted away slightly.","His relationships with people had taken a strange turn over the past few days. Somehow, he had grown close to several people he had once been rather distant from.","He had already heard all the gossip from them: Su Yu had taken the initiative to invite Li Jiangbing to share meals, only to be coldly rejected by him.","Everyone was exasperated with him!","The original plan had been to take one hundred people to Yujing Xiangyuan. After contacting Xia Huiâs parents and asking about the situation in their residential compound, they learned that there were very few zombies inside, and not many in the buildings either.","Xia Huiâs parents had simply been spectacularly unlucky.","The family next door had originally been one of the lucky onesâa family of five who had all survived the first zombie disaster.","Then Vice Mayor Zheng ordered the schools to provide remedial classes for the children. But the parents of this family felt that life was difficult enough as it was and didnât want their child to be worked so hard. They took the child out of school and planned to go traveling as a family, so the child could see more of the world.","They had left their door open and even dragged their suitcases out. While they were waiting for the elevator, the second wave of the zombie virus struck.","No one knew who had transformed first or who had been bitten later. In any case, all five members of the family had ended up becoming zombies together, blocking the door to Xia Huiâs parentsâ apartment.","Xia Hui was stranded in the city and couldnât return, so he thought of asking Jiang Cheng for help.","After all, Zhou Wang had taken just over thirty people and cleared out Jixiang Jiayuan. That showed just how light the disaster inside this residential compound really was.","The hardest-hit areas were downtown, along with commercial and industrial districts.","As a result, plenty of people wanted to go. By the end, the crowd had swelled to nearly two hundred.","Some had obtained new metal armor, which made them look especially imposing. Others gathered together to study how to use the crescent shovels.","Finally, Jiang Cheng said, âLetâs go.â","To reach Yujing Xiangyuan, they didnât need to take the long way around outside. They could simply cut through.","In short, they would leave through the east gate of their own residential compound and enter Jixiang Jiayuan through its west gate. After crossing Jixiang Jiayuan, they would leave through its east gate and arrive at Yujing Xiangyuan.","Zhou Wang brought his people to meet them inside their own compound.","Jiang Cheng looked at her group, then at the people Zhou Wang had brought. In the end, she decided, âThe uncles and aunties donât need to come. Let the young people go.â","In the end, the only elderly person in Zhou Wangâs group who went with them was Uncle Eighty.","The old man had only recently awakened his superhuman ability. After doing eighty pull-ups, he had earned the nickname âUncle Eighty.â","Technically, he was old enough for everyone to call him Grandpa, but âUncleâ made him sound younger.","Uncle Eighty was delighted to accept the name.","He was a metal-type superhuman.","Why? Because when he was young, his favorite military exercise had been practicing with bayonets.","The weapon Uncle Eighty made for himself looked somewhat like an ancient spear. He shortened it slightly for easier useâit wasnât as long as the ones seen in television dramasâbut made the spearhead much longer.","Put simply, Uncle Eighty had made himself a bayonet on a long shaft.","He followed the main group toward Yujing Xiangyuan, marching with great vigor and enthusiasm.","The fighting at Yujing Xiangyuan was not particularly intense.","Just like Jixiang Jiayuan, the compound was mostly occupied by elderly people whose children no longer lived with them.","The large group had an overwhelming advantage.","When the residents of Yujing Xiangyuan saw them arrive, some of them even came downstairs to help.","One of them was a lightning-type superhuman.","Everyone asked him, âYou have superpowers. Why didnât you come downstairs and fight the zombies yourself?â","Why had he waited until the young people from the youth apartment arrived before finally coming down?","The man replied, âNo one else came down, so I didnât either.â","If even one person had taken the lead, he might have followed. The problem was that no one had been willing to lead.","This was where Zhou Wangâs value became apparent.","Without him, Jixiang Jiayuan would probably have ended up just like Yujing Xiangyuan.","Not to mention that he had also built connections and formed an alliance with the youth apartment to secure their protection.","When human beings gathered together, having a leader or not having one often led to completely different circumstances.","The crescent shovels proved to be extremely useful.","Li Jiangbing charged forward with a crescent shovel in hand. A zombie came straight at him, and Li Jiangbing charged straight at it.","The man had not even arrived yet, but his shovel had!","Using the momentum of his sprint, he swung the shovel and sent the zombieâs head flying into the air in a single blow.","Everyone was startled.","Li Jiangbing himself was startled too. âHoly crap?â","The weapon was so effective partly because its shape was genuinely suited to killing zombies, and partly because it was simply incredibly sharp.","Young Wang had sharpened it to perfection.","Xia Huiâs parents were successfully rescued.","âThank you, thank you!â His parents kept pressing their palms together and expressing their gratitude. âXia Hui said you would come, but we never dared believe it. And now youâre really here.â","These few zombies were nowhere near enough to kill.","There were simply too many people. They even started fighting over the zombies.","Li Jiangbing had someone help restrain a zombie, then moved in to test something. He gave up after two seconds and severed its neck with a shovel.","No one else knew what he had been testing.","Jiang Cheng tried it too.","Living creatures couldnât be stored in her storage spaceâbut what about zombies?","The test proved that zombies couldnât be stored either, but a zombieâs corpse could.","Since the only way to kill a zombie was to destroy its brain, Jiang Cheng guessed that there must still be active cells in a zombieâs brain. That caused the storage space to classify it as a âlivingâ organism.","From a human perspective, though, even a living zombie was already dead beyond dead.","Zhou Wang finally learned what Jiang Chengâs superpower was.","No wonder Zhao Yi had called Jiang Cheng special that morning.","He thought Jiang Chengâs superpower was exceptionally useful. Any combat-type superpowered individual who also had a storage space like Jiang Chengâs would be an unbeatable combination.","They could survive completely on their own in this world.","However, there had been no reports of anyone possessing two superpowers.","So Jiang Cheng could only have this one: a storage space.","It was certainly an excellent superpower, butâ¦ Zhou Wang felt that Jiang Cheng, as the leader of a group, was still lacking something. No matter how useful a superpower was, if it wasnât combat-oriented, it somehow fell short.","Zhou Wang observed the superpowered people from the Young Apartment and discovered that many of them were improving at an astonishing rate.","A few of them were especially powerful: Guo Jun, Aunt Pan, and Cao Jiacai.","This was bad.","Zhou Wang didnât know whether Jiang Cheng had realized it, but the three strongest superpowered people in the Young Apartment were not property owners.","Most of the time everyone spent at Yujing Xiangyuan was devoted to searching for zombies.","They had to inspect every household in the buildings.","The underground parking garage also had to be searched.","They even had to glance into every corner of the residential compoundâs grounds.","In reality, there was very little actual fighting.","What no one expected, however, was that the people from the Young Apartment would end up arguing among themselves.","Calling them âtheir own peopleâ wasnât entirely accurate, because, as Zhou Wang had realized, some of them werenât property owners.","The argument was between Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan on one side, and Cao Jiacai on the other.","Zhao Yi had always been even-tempered.","Before that morning, everyoneâs impression of him had been: âHe does a lot of work and doesnât say much.â The meeting that morning had changed many peopleâs opinion of him.","Zhao Yi wasnât the kind of top student who was all grades and no ability. He was a top student with both excellent grades and real capability.","It was simply his personality. He rarely spoke to people he couldnât see eye to eye with. For instance, he had seldom spoken with Song Jingshuo in the past.","But he truly did have a good temper. A man as mild-mannered as him was now, unusually, losing his temper.","âDo you have any idea how flammable the insulation on the buildingâs exterior walls is?â","âWhen you joined the property management company, didnât you receive fire-safety training?â","Across from him, Cao Jiacai looked completely unconcerned.","âWhatâs there to fear? I can just grab the flames and pull them back.â","âAnd what if you make a mistake?â Zhao Yi snapped furiously. âOnce the insulation on the buildingâs exterior catches fire, the flames can reach more than a dozen floors within mere seconds!â","âYou can only control fire from close range. If a fire spreads rapidly up a high-rise like this, even if you take the elevator after it, you still wonât catch up!â","âYou can control the size of the flames. Why did you have to make them so big?â","âWeâre here to rescue people, not put on a show!â"]},{"number":121,"title":"Chapter 121: 0121","paragraphs":["That last sentence had hit him where it hurt, and Cao Jiacai suddenly slammed a fireball onto the ground. With a whoosh, he flew into a rage. âI save people and Iâm the one in the wrong?! What a load of crap! Go play by yourselves! Donât call me again!â","He stormed off, gripping his rolling pin.","Young Wang and Little Zhao exchanged helpless glances before hurrying after him. âBrother Cao! Brother Cao!â","Three superpowered people had left just like that. Two of them were very strong, and the other was currently the strongest person in the entire residential compound.","The onlookers began murmuring among themselves.","Gao Yuxuan kept trying to comfort Zhao Yi. âForget it, forget it. Thereâs no reasoning with someone like that.â","They hadnât even been equals to begin with. Cao Jiacai had only been allowed a seat at the table because of his superpower.","But as a person, he hadnât changed at allânot in his outlook, nor in his understanding of the world. His narrow-mindedness and resentment toward the wealthy were plain for all to see. Everyone had merely pretended not to notice, choosing to seek common ground while tolerating their differences.","The fundamental reason was that Cao Jiacaiâs superpower was simply too powerful. No one could do anything to him.","This time, even Jiang Cheng might be powerless. Jiang Cheng couldnât possibly expel the strongest superpowered person in the entire compound, could she?","And even if she did order him out, could she actually make him leave?","What had been the name of that cleaner from before? A few men had dragged him out of the compound despite his begging and groveling. It had been useless.","But Cao Jiacai was different. A single blaze from him sent waves of heat crashing over them from a distance. No one could even get close.","What if Jiang Cheng ordered him to leave and Cao Jiacai simply refused? Jiang Chengâs authorityâand her dignityâwould be left lying on the ground.","After that, it would be hard to say whether everyone would still listen to her.","In the past, everyoneâs combat strength had been roughly equal. Li Jiangbing, the strongest among them, stood firmly with Jiang Cheng, while Jiang Cheng relied on her intelligence to win everyoneâs obedience.","But things were different now.","After superpowers appeared, Jiang Cheng, Li Jiangbing, and Song Jingshuo had all fallen into the second tier in terms of combat ability.","At the very top of the pyramid was Cao Jiacai. No wonder he was so arrogant.","Jiang Cheng had done an excellent job leading the compound, and she was fair and impartial enough to make everyone feel secure.","Still, deep down, everyone regretted that not one of their trio possessed a powerful superpower.","If even one of Jiang Cheng, Li Jiangbing, or Song Jingshuo had been a strong superpowered fighter, that would have been enough.","This conflict was reported to Jiang Cheng by Little Fang, one of the security guards, who ran to find her.","Since they had to search the buildings, everyone had split into several teams and gone to different blocks.","By the time Jiang Cheng arrived, all she could see was Cao Jiacaiâs retreating figure in the distance. She asked, âWhat happened?â","Zhao Yi had calmed down and explained the situation to Jiang Cheng. âIt wasnât just the danger of the building catching fire. Several people were burned just now. If Lesi hadnât rushed over to treat them, it could have been much worse.â","Extensive burns were extremely serious. One wrong turn, and the victim could die from infection.","This wasnât ancient times, when medical care was primitive. This was the modern world, and even with modern medicine, extensive burns were still incredibly dangerous.","Fortunately, Zhang Lesi had gained a superpower.","Zhang Lesi confirmed it as well. âYes. They were very serious.â","When it came to her field, she never joked around. Zhang Lesi was extremely serious and firmly supported Zhao Yi.","Cao Jiacai had not cared in the slightest about other peopleâs pain or lives.","Those who had been scorched were still shaken. âThat was terrifying. Itâs the first time Iâve realized how dangerous fire really is.â","âWhen I used to watch TV dramas, whenever fire blocked the way, Iâd always think, âWhy doesnât the protagonist just run through it?ââ","âNow I know. With a fire that big, your skin starts hurting even when youâre several meters away!â","âDamn, it hurt like hell just now. Luckily Lesi showed up.â","Admiration of the strong was a common human instinct.","With Cao Jiacai so powerful, it was only natural that many people wanted to team up with him.","Even though everyone no longer feared zombies, that didnât mean there was no danger left at all. People instinctively felt that if the person leading them was strong, their own danger would be reduced.","Some people abandoned Li Jiangbing and chose to join Cao Jiacaiâs team instead.","Who the hell would have thought Cao Jiacai would turn out to be more dangerous than the zombies?","Zombie teeth couldnât bite through their protective armor. Cao Jiacaiâs flames, however, had melted and warped the plastic armor on two people. One personâs metal armor had been heated until it was scorching hot, and he had endured the pain, crying out as he forcibly stripped it off.","Cao Jiacai had even laughed.","Zhang Lesi explained, âAnd it isnât only the skin thatâs at risk. In a high-temperature fire, a person may look perfectly fine on the outside and still die without warning. Simply put, their skin is unharmed, but their internal organs have already been steamed. Thereâs no saving someone in that condition.â","What made it worse was that because there were no visible burns or scorch marks, such victims were even more likely to be overlooked.","At a fire scene, medical personnel would naturally prioritize those with visible burns or smoke inhalation. Everyone would ignore the hero who had rushed in and out of the flames to save people.","The hero himself would also think he was fine. Then, all of a sudden, he would collapseâand never get back up.","Only medical professionals understood how dangerous that was.","Seeing Jiang Cheng fall silent in thought, Zhao Yi regretted what he had done.","A shut-in was only a shut-in, not an idiot. Zhao Yi had confronted Cao Jiacai in a moment of anger, but he also understood that, for Jiang Cheng, the situation had subtly changed since the last time.","Jiang Cheng no longer had enough force to suppress Cao Jiacai.","In just a few days, Cao Jiacaiâs attitude had grown increasingly arrogant as his superpower improved. Zhao Yi understood all too well that someone like him might soon begin challenging the leaderâs authority.","Conflicts between top salespeople and their managers were common in many companies. Once the tension escalated, either the top salesperson left, or the manager did.","As long as the boss wasnât an idiot, they would usually side with the top salesperson and make the manager leave.","The confrontation between him and Cao Jiacai had just accelerated the escalation.","Once he had calmed down, Zhao Yi regretted it.","Everyone elseâs superpowers were still inferior to Cao Jiacaiâs. They shouldnât have intensified the conflictânot until everyone had time to improve and refine their abilities.","Cao Jiacai could be dealt with later.","Starting a conflict now was only putting Jiang Cheng in a difficult position.","He lowered his head and apologized. âJiang Cheng, Iâm sorryâ¦â","Jiang Cheng raised her eyes, surprised. âWhat are you apologizing for? You didnât do anything wrong. Whether itâs a building or a person, you canât just recklessly set things on fire. Fortunately, Lesi was here.â","Then she added, âAt least nothing happened today.â","And that was the end of it.","Of course it was the end of it. What else could they do?","Everyone understood that, but some people were still disappointed in Jiang Cheng.","They could certainly sympathize with her. What else could Jiang Cheng do? Roll up her sleeves and beat Cao Jiacai herself?","They could sympathize with her, but that didnât stop their disappointment from rising.","Zhou Wang watched coldly from the side.","See? This was exactly what he had been worried about.","A crack had appeared in their unity.","If the leader herself lacked sufficient ability, the foundation was unstable.","Would peopleâs hearts begin to waver? Would the group eventually fall apart?","The zombie corpses had been piled together.","In the past, even when the residents of the Youth Apartments helped their neighbors kill zombies, they wouldnât have bothered cleaning up afterward.","But now, when they looked around and saw only elderly men and women, they thought, Fine. We might as well see this through and do a good deed to the end.","Wu Jiancheng asked, âShould we burn them?â","If they needed to be burned, he could help.","Jiang Cheng didnât interfere in matters like this, leaving the decision entirely to Zhao Yi. She also waited for him to make the arrangements.","But Zhao Yi merely rubbed his chin and fell deep into thought.","This time was different from the last. The emergence of superpowers had changed many things, including the way everyone thought.","Burning large numbers of corpses had been an unavoidable measure at the time.","Human resources, material supplies, and environmental conditions had all been severely limited. They had no choice but to deal with the bodies somehow.","Back then, everyone had been trapped inside the residential complex, so in the end, they had simply burned them there.","Even after the disaster was over, people with sensitive noses still complained that the small square at Youth Apartments smelled awful.","It wasnât impossible. At the time, a large amount of corpse fluids had seeped into the ground. Even if they had later been burned dry and evaporated, residual substances might still have remained and continued to give off a smell.","Now that they had superpowers, Zhao Yi had completely overturned their previous method of disposal. He wanted to bury the bodies.","He himself had an earth-based superpower, and with Aunt Panâthe strongest earth-based superhumanâdigging holes would be no problem. It wouldnât require a great deal of manpower or labor.","The key was where to bury them.","He called over someone who worked in civil engineering, stomped his foot, and asked, âHow deep is the ground here above the roof of the underground parking garage?â","The civil engineering specialist said, âThe total thickness is at least 1.5 to 2 meters. It wonât be less than 1.5 meters. Thatâs a city regulation. Otherwise, the trees in the residential complex wonât have enough depth for their roots and wonât survive. Theyâd just be blown over in a strong wind.â","âThat thickness includes both the layer of soil above the garage and the garageâs roof slab. So if youâre only considering the soil layer, itâll be less than that.â","Someone nearby chimed in, âThen it definitely wonât be deep enough!â","The man continued, âWhen burying bodies, 1.5 meters is the minimum depth. If you donât reach that depth, go ahead and bury themâbut theyâll be dug right back up. Humans might not be able to smell anything, but stray cats and dogs can. Theyâll smell the bodies and dig through the soil to pull them out.â","âAnd if itâs less than 1.5 meters, you wonât solve the maggot problem either. After a while, youâll take a look andâgood grief! That whole patch where the bodies were buried will be crawling with long, wriggling maggots.â","The people around them nearly gagged from his description.","Zhao Yi and the civil engineering specialist: ââ¦â","Gao Yuxuan dry-heaved twice and eyed the man suspiciously. âWhat exactly is your field, bro? Forensics?â","âHeh heh.â The man gave a somewhat sinister smile. âIt has nothing to do with my profession. Iâm just a fan of detective and crime novels.â","If shut-ins could be divided into factions and categories, Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan would belong to the sunny, clean-cut type.","They usually held down decent jobs and earned fairly good incomes.","They had good living habits and kept their homes clean, tidy, and cozy. Once they became adults, the money they earned was their own, and their parents could no longer control how they spent it. They were free to spend it on their hobbies.","Their homes had bright display cabinets filled with their beloved figurines. Some of the larger ones could cost several thousand, or even tens of thousands, of yuan.","No matter. They were worth it.","The man in front of them, on the other hand, clearly belonged to the gloomy, damp type of shut-in.","He seemed like the sort who would turn off the ceiling light while reading crime novels and leave only a desk lamp on, deliberately creating a dark and eerie atmosphere.","A little frightening.","Still, as frightening as he was, he had offered useful advice at a time like this.","The civil engineering specialist said, âThat wonât work. Not only is the soil layer too shallow, you also have to consider all the utility lines buried underneath. The others might be manageable, but you absolutely canât contaminate the drinking-water pipes.â","That was a very important issue.","Jiang Cheng said, âWhat about the roadside park outside the west gate?â","The west gate he referred to was the west gate of Youth Apartments.","Jiang Cheng continued, âWe also have to consider whatâs beneath the road.â","If they peeled up the asphalt, there would be natural soil underneath. The Technology New District had no subway, and there wouldnât be an underground parking garage directly beneath the road either. It was genuine bedrock and soil beneath the surface.","In the end, they chose the roadside park outside the west gate.","That was because asphalt was even harder to deal with than concrete and would consume far too much of their superpower.","Jiang Cheng said, âPile them together. Keep them packed tightly. Iâll put them in my storage space.â","Zhao Yi: âAh!â","Jiang Cheng: â?â"]},{"number":122,"title":"Chapter 122: 0122","paragraphs":["Zhao Yi asked, âWonât that cause contamination?â","Zhao Yi didnât want Jiang Chengâs storage space used for this. His hope for the space was that it would be used to transport vital suppliesâespecially for storing and moving food when resources were scarce.","He was worried that the space might get dirty or contaminated. It wouldnât be suitable for storing food afterward.","Jiang Cheng chuckled.","She explained, âThis space isnât a room. Itâs more likeâ¦ an empty void with a maximum capacity imposed on it. As long as the limit isnât exceeded, anything can be put inside. Thereâs no such thing as dirtying the walls or floor like you would in a real space. Nothing is left behind, either.â","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan leaned in until their faces were practically pressed against hers. âAnd then? What happened next?â","They crowded Jiang Cheng so closely that she had to take half a step back. âIt isnât a three-dimensional space as we understand it.â","She explained to them that the space had no restrictions on shape.","Their eyes lit up, and the two of them immediately agreed. âSo the only limit is weight.â","âI really want to go inside and take a look,â Gao Yuxuan said excitedly. âJiang Cheng, can living people enter? Can you go in yourself?â","Jiang Cheng shattered his dream. âNo. Living creatures canât enter.â","She described what it felt like: âAll I can sense is that the objects are floating in the universe. I just canât see any stars.â","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan were filled with longing.","In the end, Jiang Cheng stored the corpses in her storage space. It was the most convenient option. They didnât need to find a vehicle or waste manpower, and there was no need to worry about sticky blood or bits of brain matter dripping and splattering all the way there.","Zhao Yi said, âFrom now on, we need to factor our abilities into the way we think and plan.â","Everyone nodded.","There were three zombies in the roadside park outside the western gate.","There were snacks and drinks left on a bench, and a novel lay on a stone stool.","They must have been people who had been enjoying a moment of leisure in the park, basking in the sunlight.","The group killed the three zombies as well.","Aunt Pan dug a large pit and asked, âIs this deep enough?â","The civil engineer caught up with them. âIâll measure it!â","It turned out he had gone home to get a tape measure.","The pit was a little over two meters deep. âThatâs enough, thatâs enough.â","He pressed the button on the tape measure, and it whipped back in with a rapid whir.","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan both hurriedly stepped back. âBe careful! That thingâs sharp. Donât cut anyone.â","âRelax,â the civil engineer said. âIâve got it under control.â","Gao Yuxuan cursed, âYouâve got nothing under control!â","The civil engineer refused to back down. âDo you know how many years Iâve been using tape measures? I know exactly what Iâm doing. With a flick of my hand, I can control which way it flies.â","Gao Yuxuan was about to argue again when Cui Haiyang came over. âLet me see!â","Everyone stopped what they were doing. Cui Haiyang was a metal-element superpowered individual.","The moment he took the tape measure, it was as if he had discovered a whole new world. His face was full of excitement. âHow did I not think of this? How did I not think of this? I have a tape measure too!â","In his hands, the tape measure shot out and automatically snapped back, moving like a snake. Its range was still limited, though.","At present, only fire-element superpowers could use a wooden stick as a track to accelerate and launch fireballs.","Next came the electric-element users. Guo Jun was the strongest among them, and his electric current could strike targets several meters away.","The earth-element users could only attack a short distance in front of themselves for now. Zhao Yi and Aunt Pan both had to wait until the zombies came close before using their abilities, which placed tremendous demands on their nerves and courage.","Metal-element users could make their weapons change shape or suddenly extend into stabbing points at the moment of attack, but that didnât count as ranged combat. It was still close-quarters fighting.","Electric-element abilities could barely be considered ranged attacks.","But the only ability that truly deserved to be called ârangedâ at present was fire.","âA chainsaw,â Zhao Yi suddenly said.","Cui Haiyang froze, then immediately beamed. âThatâs right! A chainsaw!â","At first, he had been thinking of sharpening the tape measure so that it could extend like a snake and then retract, slicing through a zombieâs neck.","But a sharpened edge was suited to chopping and stabbing. What he needed was something that could cut through.","For that, a saw was the proper tool.","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan both regretted that the hardware store at the intersection had gone out of business and been completely emptied. Otherwise, they might have been able to find a chainsaw there.","They asked, âCan you make one yourself?â","âI definitely can,â Cui Haiyang said. âBut a chainsaw will take some time. The main problem is that I donât have a blueprint or a sample to work from.â","He could create objects by controlling metal and reshaping it because he had a clear idea of what he wanted to makeâthe shape, the size, and exactly where each part needed to be adjusted.","But a chainsaw was a relatively complicated and delicate machine. Without a blueprint, it would be troublesome. He would probably need to experiment many times.","Zhao Yi said, âThen make a sawtooth edge first.â","That was simple enough. Cui Haiyang clenched the tape measure in his palm. A few seconds later, he controlled it to shoot out again. This time, its edge had transformed into a row of teeth.","The young men were all excited. âTry it! Try it!â","Together, they found a small tree.","The toothed tape measure shot out and snapped back. It sawed several centimeters into the tree.","That was already incredibly impressive.","Cui Haiyang murmured, âI still need more practice. More practice.â","His goal was to sever a zombieâs neck in a single extension and retraction. Once the neck was severed, the zombie would be finished.","Zhao Yi gestured at his own neck. âSaw through about this farâtwo-thirds of the way. Iâve observed them carefully. Once you get this far, the nerve signals are completely cut off. The rest is just skin and muscle holding it together.â","Gao Yuxuan chopped the back of Zhao Yiâs neck with one hand. âOr you can saw from behind. The spine is the real target. A zombie doesnât need its throat or windpipe. Cut through the spine and itâs done.â","âBack in the residential compound, thereâs that tree you cut through with a shovel. Thereâs still a tall section left. Go get it and practice on that.â","Three ordinary men could still come up with two brilliant ideas between themâand useful ones at that.","Cui Haiyang turned and ran off.","Aunt Pan cracked a smile and said to Jiang Cheng, âYoung people these daysâ¦â","Aunt Pan liked spending time with these young people. In this world where zombies killed and devoured people, the residential compound was nevertheless full of vibrant life. It could make a person forget their grief.","Once the pit had been dug, it had to be disinfected first.","The hardware store at the intersection had been cleared out, and there was no quicklime left. The quicklime they had taken from the store earlier had eventually been used up as well.","But chlorine-based disinfectants would work too. These were common household products. The bleaching powder, bleach, effervescent tablets, and disinfectant sold in supermarkets were generally made primarily from sodium hypochlorite or calcium hypochlorite.","During the previous disaster, Zhao Yi had directed people to empty out the stocks from Mai Duoduo in several separate batches. At the time, everything had been piled up in the clubhouse and gradually used.","When the disaster ended, quite a lot was still left. After the clubhouse owner returned, he had cursed and complained while ordering Manager Wang to deal with it and restore the former gym.","Manager Wang hadnât actually been in charge of the gym, but he loved taking advantage of situations. He had people move all the leftover disinfectant into the property-management storeroom.","Now it came in handy. They didnât need to go shopping at Mai Duoduo anymore; they could bring it over directly from the residential compoundâs property storeroom.","Using this stuff in large quantities was somewhat troublesome. Everyone had to protect their mouths and noses, or they would be badly irritated by the fumes. It was also harmful to the human body to some extent.","That was where Li Jiangbing could be put to use.","Everyone simply unscrewed the bottles of disinfectant one by one and stacked them in front of him.","Someone else opened the sprinklers supplying water to the landscaped area of the roadside park and ran a plastic hose over to draw the water there.","Li Jiangbing channeled both the disinfectant and the water into the air, mixing and diluting them before letting the solution âleakâ down into the bottom of the pit like water from a showerhead.","Gao Yuxuan immediately gave Li Jiangbing a nickname: âRain God!â","While controlling the spray with both hands, Li Jiangbing kicked at him with one leg.","Gao Yuxuan hopped aside to dodge.","Everyone shouted, âYouâre spraying crooked! Gao Yuxuan, quit messing around!â","Once the bottom of the pit had been disinfected, Jiang Cheng transferred all the zombie corpses stored in her dimensional space into it.","Then they sprayed the corpses once more.","Finally, Aunt Pan and Zhao Yi controlled the soil on both sides, filling the pit back in.","The crime-fiction enthusiast reminded them from the side, âMake sure you tamp it down properly.â","The compactness of the soil was extremely important. If it wasnât packed firmly enough, the soil would settle and form cavities, allowing the stench of decomposition to escape. Animals with keen senses of smell would detect it.","Gao Yuxuan asked, âBuddy, are you sure youâve never killed anyone and buried the body?â","The crime-fiction enthusiast looked delighted. âItâs an honor to be suspected like that.â","âWeâll deal with the trash the same way,â Jiang Cheng said. âBury it.â","Zhao Yi glanced at Jiang Cheng, then took out his phone and checked it. He murmured, âItâs already this late. Why hasnât there been an announcement yet?â","The last time they had temporarily stockpiled their trash in the clubhouse swimming pool, they had done so under the assumption that they just needed to endure for a whileâthat the government would come rescue them and return them to their former lives.","And later, the government really had come. Their lives had returned to normal.","The garbage trucks had appeared again and hauled all the trash away for disposal.","Everything had gone back to normal.","But this time, Jiang Cheng had directly abandoned the temporary method of storing their trash.","Zhao Yi was sometimes afraid of Jiang Cheng.","Because he trusted Jiang Cheng too much.","And precisely because he trusted her so much, he was terrified of the prophecies hidden in her words.","He was fascinated by superpowers, curious about the mysterious dimensional space, and constantly coming up with wild ideas about how to apply everyoneâs abilities to daily life.","But in the end, he still wanted a normal, orderly life that functioned properly.","If returning to their former lives meant handing over their superpowers in exchange, then no matter how fascinated he was or how reluctant he felt, Zhao Yi would still give them up.","Jiang Cheng didnât pressure Zhao Yi, either.","After all, there were only a few hundred people left in the residential compound, and the amount of trash they produced was far less than before. There was no need to hurry.","She could give him time to process and accept it.","Li Jiangbing looked around. âWhere did Jingshuo go?â","Jiang Cheng replied, âJixiang Jiayuan.â","âWhatâs he doing there?â","Song Jingshuo was pretending to be the Friend of the Elderly at Jixiang Jiayuan.","No, that wasnât quite right. He was humbly exchanging tips with Auntie Lin and Auntie Qian on how to use wood-type superpowers.","âI tried three plants last night,â Song Jingshuo said. âEvery one of them grew to about this height, put out seven or eight new leaves, and then stopped growing completely.â","Auntie Qian was puzzled. âThat shouldnât happen. Yesterday, I urged one plant to grow, and it produced more than twenty fruits. I ripened them until they were perfectly readyâbright red and especially delicious.â","âSo did I,â Auntie Lin added.","So what was wrong with Xiao Song?","Song Jingshuo had already resigned himself to his fate. Since he was destined to farm, he might as well do it properly.","He had been a top student who scored highly all his life, yet he had encountered a setback in this particular field. All he could do was come and ask the aunties for advice.","Both aunties enthusiastically insisted that he visit their homes.","The old men nearby merely grunted. âHmph.â"]},{"number":123,"title":"Chapter 123: 0123","paragraphs":["Auntie Qianâs place was closer, so Song Jingshuo followed the two aunties there.","The moment he arrived, he knew what the problem was.","He stared in surprise. âDo we really need a pot this big?â","The aunties finally understood. âYou didnât repot them?â","The tomato seedlings they had brought back from the Mai Duo Duo Supermarket were still in their starter pots. Each pot was no bigger than a wineglass, small enough to fit in one hand.","Naturally, there was barely any soil in them.","The two aunties immediately realized that Song Jingshuo hadnât even grasped the basics.","âYou must have thought it was our superpowers that made the plants grow,â they said, setting him straight. âThatâs not how it works.â","âOur superpowers are more like catalysts. They accelerate a plantâs growth and development, compressing a process that would normally take several months into a few minutes or a dozen minutes.â","âBut the complete growth process still depends on sunlight, air, water, and nutrients from the soil.â","âIf you donât provide those things, no matter how much you accelerate it, the plant still wonât grow. Think about it: if a child doesnât eat properly, wonât they end up underdeveloped?â","âIâm guessing you didnât even water them after you got home.â","Song Jingshuo rubbed his forehead.","He really hadnât watered them. He had honestly thought that the superpowers alone would be enough.","The two aunties burst out laughing.","They proceeded to teach him a great deal about soil and fertilizer.","Auntie Qian even tried to keep him for dinner, but Song Jingshuo politely declined.","Before he left, Auntie Qian insisted on giving him a lamp. âTake this. Itâs a grow light. The supermarket doesnât sell themâyou have to go to a gardening shop at the flower and bird market to find one.â","Of course, that was no longer possible now.","Song Jingshuo thanked Auntie Qian and accepted it.","After leaving Auntie Qianâs place, Song Jingshuo spotted Jiang Cheng at the west gate of Jixiang Jiayuan.","Jiang Cheng was talking to Zhou Wang.","It seemed they had already dealt with the body. When everyone had superpowers they could use conveniently, many things became much simpler.","âJiang Cheng!â Song Jingshuo called as he walked over.","Jiang Cheng said, âI was discussing with Brother Zhou whether it would be feasible to have the aunties here run a communal kitchen at our place.â","Song Jingshuo hesitated.","Jiang Cheng said, âItâs fine. Go ahead.â","So Zhou Wang wasnât an issue.","Song Jingshuo got straight to the point. âWhat are we offering the aunties as payment?â","Until the government stepped in and restored everything to normal, money was meaningless.","Besides, everyone currently had sufficient supplies. They had plenty of food and daily necessities. The rice they had brought back from the Mai Duo Duo Supermarket yesterday would last them half a year.","So what could they use to pay the people doing the cooking?","âThatâs what weâre discussing,â Jiang Cheng said. âThe truth isâ¦ the only thing we can offer right now is to give them the same status as the owners of Youth Apartment.â","It sounded rather vague.","People who came to work for Youth Apartment wouldnât receive any tangible compensation. Instead, they would be treated as owners of the complex.","They would receive Youth Apartmentâs protection.","They would also be entitled to share in anything obtained through Youth Apartmentâs collective actions.","Song Jingshuo thought it sounded ridiculousâlike getting something for nothing. Would anyone really agree to that?","Zhou Wang, however, was instantly tempted.","He genuinely wanted to leave Jixiang Jiayuan and join Youth Apartment. If he did, Jiang Cheng would handle all the miscellaneous affairs. Every danger and arduous task would be shared by the group.","For each individual, the burden would be light.","Together, however, they would wield tremendous strength.","What Youth Apartment took for granted was exactly what Zhou Wang longed for.","Zhou Wang agreed. âIâll discuss it with everyone.â","Jiang Cheng said, âThank you, Brother Zhou.â","She really didnât want to waste time dealing with the cooking arrangements.","That wasnât to say she didnât want good food. Of course she did. But she also wanted to eat efficiently.","Take Li Jiangbing, for example. He had smartly joined forces with the property-management staff over meals. How easy was that?","But Jiang Cheng now wanted to free Aunt Pan from cooking as well.","Zhou Wang felt a little admiration for Jiang Cheng.","She was a young woman, yet she was as deep and seasoned as many middle-aged veterans of society.","A conflict like the one with Cao Jiacai had clearly shaken her authority, but she could still discuss logistical support with him without the slightest change in expression.","Wait a momentâ¦","Could it be that she hadnât realized what had happened?","Zhou Wang hesitated, but eventually spoke up. âLittle Jiang.â","Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo had just turned to leave. They both looked back when he called out to them.","Zhou Wang warned her, âIf you find a troublemaker in the team, you need to deal with them as soon as possible. The longer a troublemaker stays, the more difficult-to-repair cracks theyâll create in the group.â","Jiang Cheng nodded calmly. âUnderstood.â","Zhou Wang believed she had taken his words to heart, but could she actually do it?","He hoped she could. He wanted Youth Apartmentâs leader to remain unchanged. Or, if a change was unavoidable, replacing her with Little Li, Xiao Song, Little Wu, or one of the others would not be unacceptable.","Even Little Zhao would do.","But that security guard absolutely would not. That would be the worst possible outcome.","A middle-aged man who had been around the block knew all too well how disastrous it could be when someone from the bottom rose to power.","âWhat happened?â Song Jingshuo asked.","While checking the buildings, he, Li Jiangbing, and Jiang Cheng had been in different towers. By the time he came downstairs, they had already begun discussing how to dispose of the body.","Jiang Cheng told him about the conflict between Cao Jiacai and Zhao Yi.","Song Jingshuo had already suspected it was Cao Jiacai. Sure enough, it was him. He furrowed his brows and remained silent until they had passed through the east gate of the complex.","They walked a little farther. When they reached the place where they were supposed to part ways, Song Jingshuo said solemnly, âJiang Cheng, we canât act against Cao Jiacai lightly.â","âI know,â Jiang Cheng replied.","Then she added, âBut if the time comes when we have no choice but to act against Cao Jiacai, I hope you can cross that line.â","That line?","Which line?","What line?","Song Jingshuo stared into Jiang Chengâs eyes, his lips pressed tightly together.","Compared with the other residential compounds, Youth Apartment had experienced no criminal incidents during the first zombie outbreak.","The worst thing that had happened there was when someone had been bitten and infected, then resisted isolation and was beaten to death during the ensuing conflict.","Youth Apartment had never killed anyone who was completely healthy and uninfected.","But Cao Jiacaiâs superpower was too formidable.","He had poor character, an obvious resentment toward the wealthy, and all the telltale signs of a petty man intoxicated by sudden power.","Song Jingshuo couldnât think of any way to prevent him from seeking revenge after being punished or expelled.","He might even report them to the police and have Jiang Cheng arrested for murder because she had expelled Liu Hongwang.","His resentment toward Jiang Cheng had clearly been building for a long time.","And he was deeply vengeful.","It was one thing to leave a man like that alone. But if they decided to act against him, then they had toâ¦","Song Jingshuo agreed. âAll right.â","He had thought agreeing to this would be difficult. Yet the moment the word left his mouth, he suddenly felt light all over.","By agreeing to Jiang Cheng, he had truly let go of all the rules of the old law-based society and embraced the new order.","As the two of them prepared to part, Song Jingshuo instinctively raised his wrist.","But it was bare. He was no longer wearing the watch that had cost more than ten thousand yuan.","After the invention of the mobile phone, watches had lost their practical purpose and been relegated to the status of accessories.","Back when zombies were running rampant, he had stubbornly insisted on wearing a designer watch that projected an air of taste and sophisticationâ¦ Song Jingshuo could no longer relate to his former self.","He pulled out his phone and checked the time.","This afternoon, a lot of people had kept checking the time, all asking the same question: âStill no announcement?â","Song Jingshuo asked, âStill no announcement?â","Jiang Cheng said, âIf there were one, someone would have opened a window and started shouting by now. Do you really think the soldiers could keep it bottled up?â","Song Jingshuo said, ââ¦True.â","But it was already this late. The sun was slanting westward.","Peopleâs hearts were sinking along with it, lower and lower.","Zhang Lesi and several other girls had gathered at Su Yuâs place to cook.","They had moved in gradually over the course of the day.","Moving wasnât difficult. All the apartments had roughly the same layout and size, and they were fully furnished.","They only needed to drag over suitcases containing the clothes they wore that season, along with their sheets, pillows, cups, towels, and other essentials. After replacing the previous ownerâs belongings, they could move right in.","There were plenty of empty apartments, so everyone took their time choosing, trying to find places that were clean, tidy, and easy on the eyes.","âCao Jiacai?â Su Yu had only just learned about it too, just like Song Jingshuo.","Su Yu was quite popular now as well.","Especially when it came to sweeping buildingsâthose tight, enclosed spaces where there was little room to dodge. Everyone liked teaming up with Su Yu.","In the hallways, they had Su Yu walk in front.","Her protective shield had already become instinctive. If she encountered a sudden zombie attack while not actively using it, the shield would automatically activate to protect her life, without requiring Su Yu to consciously control its output.","When breaking down doors, Su Yu would use the shield to cover everyone.","She never used it for very long at a time, taking a short break before activating it again. With this repeated use, the protective shield was growing rapidly stronger.","Su Yu had now figured out most of the shieldâs properties.","People could pass freely through it from the inside and leave.","But from the outside, the shield was incredibly tough. Neither humans nor zombies could get through.","Even supernatural abilities couldnât penetrate it.","It was seriously badass.","The only problem was that it was still a little weak and couldnât last very long. But given enough time, it was easy to imagine Su Yu becoming one of the strongest ability users around.","âAnd then what?â Su Yu asked.","Zhang Lesi shrugged. âThatâs it. There is no âthen.ââ","Su Yu fell silent and lowered her head to chop vegetables. Zhang Lesi took a bowl and beat some eggs.","Neither of them spoke.","Among the girls, apart from Aunt Pan and Jiang Cheng, only the two of them had supernatural abilities.","Su Yu suddenly stopped chopping.","âWe have to stand with Jiang Cheng. Jiang Cheng is our only choice.â Su Yu raised her eyes, her tone firm. âJiang Cheng is the only one whoâs truly good for us. No one else could do better than her. Someone like Cao Jiacai is absolutely unacceptable.â","She said, âDonât forget Nie Kuizhang.â","Nie Kuizhang wasnât any stronger than Li Jiangbing. Any two of the other building heads could have subdued him.","That was why Nie Kuizhang didnât dare commit any real offense. All he did was make lewd jokes or sneak a touch and take advantage of someone.","When He Tian left, she had cursed him out viciously.","The other five building heads could decide how to punish him through a meeting.","At the time, everyone had been furious.","He Tian had been so enraged that even after turning into a zombie, she had still wanted to beat Nie Kuizhang to death.","Looking back now, after everything that had happened, they realized that there had actually been an order they could rely on back then.","The presence of the other building heads and Jiang Cheng had kept Nie Kuizhang in check, so he only dared commit petty offenses and didnât dare do anything truly evil.","Cao Jiacai was completely different.","Su Yu and Zhang Lesi both understood clearly that no one in the Youth Apartment Complex could hold Cao Jiacai in check anymore.","In fact, no one could use force to punish him.","The more they thought about it, the more terrified they became.","âI know.â Zhang Lesiâs voice was equally resolute. âWe have to stand with Jiang Cheng.â","âThat man kept staring at us yesterday and today.â","âBut I watched him for a while, and the person he stared at most was actually Jiang Cheng.â","Because Zhang Lesi had been paying close attention, she had noticed that whenever Cao Jiacai stared at Jiang Cheng, he would swallow.","It had disgusted Zhang Lesi.","A filthy, unkempt, foul-smelling middle-aged security guard, openly staring at a young female resident and swallowing.","He was completely shameless.","Because he was powerful now.","Zhang Lesi asked, âSu Yu, what if even Jiang Cheng canât do anything about him?â"]},{"number":124,"title":"Chapter 124: 0124","paragraphs":["Zhang Lesi asked again, âWhat if he pushes Jiang Cheng out and becomes the big shot of our residential complex?â","It was a very realistic question.","They only had to look at how many people had scrambled to team up with Cao Jiacai during todayâs building sweep to know that.","Su Yu thought about it for a moment.","She realized that she wasnât actually as anxious as she had assumed.","After all, she already possessed an incredibly powerful superpowerâone that was completely unique. It gave her confidence.","But precisely because of that, she understood Cao Jiacaiâs arrogance and sense of invulnerability all the more.","âIn that case, given Jiang Chengâs personalityâ¦â Su Yu mused, making a guess. âShe might leave.â","âSomeone like Cao Jiacai belongs to the low-awareness crowd. Put on a security guardâs uniform and he thinks he has the authority of a police officer. Give him a chair and heâll think heâs been crowned emperor.â","âIf he became the big shot of the complex, heâd definitely throw his weight around and abuse his power. The complex would become unsafe.â","âJiang Cheng wouldnât stay in an unsafe environment. Sheâd definitely leave.â","Zhang Lesi didnât hesitate. âIf Jiang Cheng leaves, Iâll go with her.â","Su Yu made up her mind as well. âThen Iâll leave too.â","They began wondering who else would go with them.","âJiangbing definitely will. Jingshuo probably will too. Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan go without sayingâthey definitely will.â","The two girls were utterly determined to follow Jiang Cheng.","But all these decisions were based on their pessimistic predictions: that Jiang Cheng couldnât beat Cao Jiacai, that she had no way to deal with him, and that she would most likely be driven out.","They sighed.","Then they both turned toward the room and asked, âStill no announcement?â","âNothing yet,â the girls inside replied as they snacked, chatted, and sorted vegetables. âThe TVâs been on the whole time. There hasnât been anything.â","Inside Jiang Chengâs apartment, all the furniture and belongings were âflickering.â","The frequency of the flickering was growing faster and faster, and Jiang Cheng was becoming increasingly adept at using her storage space.","She sat on the sofa, gazing at everything in the apartment.","âMeow.â","A black shadow appeared at the window and slipped in through the half-open pane.","It was Mo Li.","Mo Li no longer needed to stay by Jiang Chengâs side, but whenever Jiang Cheng went out, she was sure to spot him somewhere nearby.","Jiang Chengâs building sweep had gone so quickly today because, once she reached the upper floors, she discovered that Mo Li had already taken care of all the zombies in the upper half of the building.","She knew at a glance that it was his work.","The little black cat was used to the furniture and belongings at home vanishing and reappearing. He didnât care in the slightest. He leaped straight onto Jiang Chengâs lap, stretched lazily, then lay down and began licking his paws.","âYouâre back,â Jiang Cheng said, gently scratching the catâs head.","The little black cat licked his paw, sensed that something was wrong, and raised his head to look at Jiang Cheng.","âMeow?â","Jiang Cheng replied, âIâve run into trouble.â","Mo Li: âMeow? Meowââ","Jiang Cheng nodded. âYouâre right. This is our territory.â","As a human, Jiang Cheng still had all sorts of concerns and considerations.","But how could a little catâs tiny brain hold so many thoughts?","This is our territory.","Drive him away.","Bite him.","Su Yu and Zhang Lesiâs concerns were entirely justified.","When a person grew powerful, people would naturally gather around him.","Cao Jiacai had gotten into an argument with Zhao Yi halfway through the workday, then simply quit and stormed off. Little Zhao and Young Wang followed him back.","Little Zhao was a superpowered earth-element user. Young Wang was a metal-element user. Little Zhao still couldnât match Aunt Pan for the time being, but Young Wang was already about on par with Cui Haiyang. At the rate he was improving, he would soon surpass him.","âThe three of us together? What the hell do we have to fear?â Cao Jiacai cursed.","The three of them went back and drank together.","Young Wang was still somewhat uneasy. âEveryone else is still workingâ¦â","âWhat the hell does that have to do with me?â Cao Jiacai glared. âIâm not working. Letâs see if Jiang Cheng has the guts to kick me out. Iâm not Liu Hongwang!â","Aunt Pan didnât have time to fry peanuts for him, so he drank with potato chips instead, eating one after another.","âIf Liu Hongwang had had my abilities back then, he wouldnât have been driven out and died outside.â","Young Wang and Little Zhao had always been bothered by that incident.","It had made them painfully aware that they and the apartment owners belonged to different groups. The realization had been deeply uncomfortable.","Only Little Fang had foolishly thought that Jiang Cheng was in the right.","Later, when Cao Jiacai said he was going to report Jiang Cheng to the police and have her arrested, the two of them hadnât gone with him, but they had supported him.","When Cao Jiacai returned disappointed, they had even chipped in to buy him drinks and cursed the state of the world together.","Why were other people college graduates and white-collar workers while they were only security guards?","They blamed heaven, blamed earth, and blamed everyone else.","After the drinks ran out, Little Zhao and Young Wang left. Cao Jiacai remained alone in the apartment. Through the window, he watched the apartment owners return one after another.","He also saw Jiang Cheng and the others walking straight across the complex toward the west gate.","As they walked, they naturally let Jiang Cheng take the very center and lead the group.","Everyone gathered around her.","Cao Jiacai had seen scenes like that back when he was still part of the complexâs security staff, but this was the first time he had looked down on one from above.","From this vantage point, the formation was even clearer.","The person in the middle was the leader. Only the leader would be surrounded by everyone, placed at the center, and allowed to walk at the front.","Cao Jiacaiâs heart began to burn.","He wanted to stand in that position too.","Cao Jiacai thought he was the only one who had such ambitions. He never imagined that some of the apartment owners actually wanted him to become the big shot.","After dinner, when he returned to his apartment and was getting ready for bed, someone knocked on his door.","Cao Jiacai had originally had a roommate, because that was Jiang Chengâs rule: two people to a room.","Later, when the zombie crisis was over and everything returned to normal, the temporary committee was dissolved, and Jiang Cheng left town on a business trip, disappearing from sight. But there were so many empty apartments in the complex that Cao Jiacai had driven his roommate into the unit next door and claimed one apartment for himself.","When he opened the door, he found two male apartment owners he recognized. They greeted him.","âBrother Cao.â","The owners used to call him Old Cao. Over the past two days, many of them had started calling him Guard Cao. Calling him Guard Cao was probably the greatest respect these bastards were willing to show him.","To hell with that.","Look at thisâsomeone was calling him Brother Cao.","âYou areâ¦ what was your surname again?â Cao Jiacai asked. âI remember you. Youâre from Building Four, right?â","The man smiled. âThatâs right. Iâm from Building Four. My name is Wang Haotian.â","âBrother Cao,â he said. âCan we come in and talk?â","Why had two apartment owners lowered themselves enough to come looking for him?","Suspicious, Cao Jiacai let them in.","The three of them sat on the sofa and the bed, talking.","Wang Haotian began with some small talk. âBrother Cao, this apartment is pretty comfortable, isnât it?â","âYeah.â","Wang Haotian asked, âYou live here alone? I remember there were supposed to be two people.â","Cao Jiacai grew wary. âWhat are you getting at?â","Wang Haotian said, âBrother Cao, there are so many empty apartments. Do you know why they still arranged for two of you to share one?â","Cao Jiacai frowned.","Wang Haotian revealed the answer himself. âItâs because they were afraid youâd get too comfortable and forget your place. They forced you to live together in a cramped room, refusing to let you use an empty apartment even when there were plenty available. It was a reminder to remember that you were beneath the apartment owners, that you worked for them. Guess whose idea that was?â","Cao Jiacai exploded with rage. âJiang Cheng! It was her, wasnât it? Wasnât it?â","Wang Haotian gave him a thumbs-up. âBrother Cao, youâre sharp. You guessed it right away.â","Cao Jiacai launched into a string of curses.","Every now and then, Wang Haotian and the other man chimed in. âExactly. You can say that again. Right. Damn straight. Thatâs fucked-up.â","Once Cao Jiacai had vented enough, he stopped and asked, âWhat exactly did you two come here for? Donât beat around the bush. Just say it.â","Wang Haotian and the other man exchanged a glance.","Wang Haotian sat up straight, his face full of righteous indignation. âBrother Cao, this is such a huge residential compound, and itâs not like weâre short on people! So tell me, why should Jiang Cheng be the one leading us just because sheâs a woman?â","Those words struck straight at Cao Jiacaiâs heart.","Back when the interim committee had first been established, he had complained, âThose people actually let a woman boss them around.â","At the time, it had looked as though that Song guy was going to compete for power, but somehow he had ended up becoming Jiang Chengâs lackey.","Jiang Chengâa womanâwas ordering around a whole bunch of grown men.","This time, Jiang Cheng had sent out a mass text warning everyone. More than four hundred people from the youth apartments had returned, and most of them had survived.","You could say it had been a screening process.","The people who had come back and survived were, for the most part, those who trusted Jiang Cheng.","But nothing was ever absolute.","Among those four hundred-plus people were Wang Haotian and the other man. They had not returned because they trusted Jiang Cheng.","First and foremost, they were afraid of dying. They were afraid of the possibility that something might happen. Second, they had simply followed the crowd. In several group chats, many people had said they were going back. Once the numbers grew, they had panicked and followed along.","Finally, they had put their jobs on hold to return, which gave them the moral high ground. If it turned out that everything had been a false alarm, they would have been entitled to criticize Jiang Cheng.","Who would have thought it would really happen?","The zombies had come again.","Wang Haotian had finally found someone who shared his views!","âItâs only because weâre all on the same side that we can talk like this,â Wang Haotian said. âThereâs no way to discuss it with those people.â","Wang Haotian had been snapped at by Peng Ze and mocked by Song Jingshuo. In front of Li Jiangbing, one of Jiang Chengâs trusted inner-circle men, he had not even dared to bring up such a subject.","After searching for so long, he had finally found three people who shared his foul-minded outlook. This time, two of them had died, leaving only him and this other man alive.","Now there was someone cursing Jiang Cheng in such vile, filthy language, and Wang Haotian was loving every second of it.","He kept chiming in, adding a few curses about how spineless everyone else was.","After Cao Jiacai finished venting, he looked the two men up and down. âYou two have a grudge against Jiang Cheng?â","âWhether we do or not, we canât let a woman ride on our heads and shit on us!â Wang Haotian said.","That sentiment struck Cao Jiacai right in the heart. âExactly!â","Some crime and mystery novels deliberately describe criminalsâ motives in an insidious, convoluted way.","But in real life, one personâs resentment toward another can be exceedingly simple: sheâs a woman.","Some menâs most basic logic really is that simple and straightforward. They donât take even one unnecessary turn.","Novelists lavishly embellish them with all kinds of explanationsâtheir backgrounds, their families of origin, childhood trauma, the hardships of adulthood, and how one thing after another twisted their minds and drove them to commit crimesâ¦ It practically romanticizes them.","Reality is often much simpler: sheâs a woman.","âIf it were a man, I wouldnât say a thing,â Wang Haotian said. âBut sheâs a woman. Who does she think she is?â","Cao Jiacai slapped his thigh. âExactly.â","Wang Haotian fixed his eyes on Cao Jiacai. âBrother Cao, every one of them is a coward.â","There had been a Nie Kuizhang before. Wang Haotian had tried to egg him on when the matter involving He Tian came up.","But Nie Kuizhang was no fool. He knew how to read the situation. Besides, at the time, overthrowing and replacing Jiang Cheng would have cost too much, while the benefits were not especially appealing.","The country had also established an interim government, giving people hope that society would eventually return to the rule of law.","So Nie Kuizhang had ignored him.","But things were different now.","Wang Haotian pulled out his phone and showed it to Cao Jiacai. âLook at the time. What has the government done? Nothing.â","âI heard them say that Jiang Cheng analyzed the situation too. This time, the government might be completely finished.â","âIf thatâs the case, then we absolutely canât let a woman ride on our heads and shit on us. Itâs not as though sheâs the strongest person here.â","âLi Jiangbing used to be formidable, but what is he now?â","âCome to think of it, youâre the strongest person here now, Brother Cao.â","âThe two of us discussed it. We canât keep putting up with this.â","âA man like youâwhy should you be taking orders from anyone else?â"]},{"number":125,"title":"Chapter 125: 0125","paragraphs":["It was August 31, only two and a half days since the zombie virus had erupted on the afternoon of August 29.","Yet so many things had already changed.","The second outbreak of the zombie virus had not only granted people supernatural abilities and given the zombies intelligenceâit had also brought changes to the little black cat, Mo Li.","His ability to express himself had grown more sophisticated.","For example, in the past, whatever he wanted to convey would be translated into Jiang Chengâs mind as: âUs, territory.â","Now he could clearly express: âThis is our territory.â","Perhaps his brain capacity had increased, or perhaps the telepathic connection had become smoother.","Jiang Cheng didnât care which.","Everything that happened to Mo Li was good news.","She also knew that Mo Li couldnât keep hiding how extraordinary he was forever. But during the first disaster, his changes had been far too unique. If they were exposed, the government might take him away for research.","Now, however, everyone was unique. Some could create fire or control water; others could summon lightning or stir up wind.","That was wonderful.","Jiang Cheng gently scratched the little catâs fluffy head. âWe should find a chance to introduce you to everyone properly.â","Once Mo Liâs existence was made official, many things would become more convenient.","Right, Mo Li?","The little cat bumped his head against her palm.","âMeow~â","When Jiang Cheng woke up on September 1, she found a text message waiting for her. During the night after she went to sleep and earlier that morning, two more residents had returned to the neighborhood.","Both had come back from downtown.","Neither of them possessed a supernatural ability. They had simply been lucky enough to have someone awaken an ability at their workplace. After finally escaping the building, they had fled all the way back while evading zombies, found vehicles to use, and made it home alive.","The leaders of their apartment buildings had sent Jiang Cheng messages to report:","âMedical examinations completed.â","Around noon, Zhou Wang called Jiang Cheng.","âWe found a few people. How about going over to talk to them?â","Jiang Cheng agreed. âSure. See you in a bit.â","She notified several building leaders, then went downstairs.","She had spent the entire previous night practicing her supernatural ability in the apartment, doing her best to expand her storage space, and had gone to bed rather late. She hadnât done her morning exercises today.","Now that she was downstairs, she discovered that the entire area was packed with people working out.","Some were running. Others were doing push-ups.","The whole place was buzzing with activity.","Jiang Cheng: ââ¦â","Since people had awakened supernatural abilities one after another over the past two days, no one knew when this window of opportunity would close.","The experts on supernatural abilities had confidently analyzed that the only requirement was having the necessary physical foundation. As a result, even those who had not yet awakened an ability had come out to train.","They had never been this motivated before.","Those who had already awakened abilities had found various corners to practice in. Some had even devoted themselves to serving the neighborhood. At everyoneâs request, Aunt Pan and Cui Haiyang had made several pieces of exercise equipment for the community.","Pull-up bars, parallel bars, dumbbells, barbells, and the like.","Cui Haiyang handled the metal parts, while Aunt Pan took care of the weights. Working together, they had made everything sturdy and secure.","Yesterday, Song Jingshuo had taken the fill light Auntie Qian gave him back home, only to discover that he didnât have any flowerpots. He couldnât be bothered to go downstairs again to get soil.","So this morning, he simply brought several seedlings downstairs, planted them in the greenbelt, and watered them a little.","Then he began accelerating their growth.","The seedlings began to grow like footage played back from a nature documentary: leaves emerged and unfurled, flowers bloomed, withered, and fell, fruit appeared, and then ripened.","A crowd gathered around to watch.","âWow~ Wow~â","Song Jingshuo accelerated the fruit until it was fully ripe. Each plant bore more than a dozen bright red fruits.","When they were completely mature, he noticed the people around him staring at them with shining eyes. The corners of Song Jingshuoâs mouth twitched.","âGo ahead and eat.â","Everyone surged forward to grab some.","There was no dust or pesticide on them, so there was no need to wash them. They could simply be picked and eaten.","âThis is great! We donât have to worry about running out of vegetables anymore.â","âEating nothing but rice and canned food nearly killed me last time!â","âSame here! Just hearing the word âcanned foodâ makes me feel sick.â","âDonât say thatâughâ¦â","Song Jingshuo took the opportunity to announce, âIf anyone has seeds, vegetable or fruit seedlings, or fresh produce at home, bring some to me.â","âI already have seven kinds of vegetables.â He listed the seven varieties he had cultivated. âYou donât need to look for those. Iâve already started growing them. If you have anything I donât, bring it to me as soon as possible. Donât wait until itâs completely dried out or deadâthat wonât work. The fresher it is, the better.â","The fresher something was, the easier it was for him to make it take root.","At home, he had placed each variety in a bowl of water to keep it fresh while he slowly figured out how to cultivate them on a larger scale.","Aunt Pan came over to inspect the seedlings he had accelerated to maturity and clicked her tongue in admiration.","âNot bad!â","Then she crouched down and raked her fingers through the soil. After concentrating for a moment, she said, âThis soil needs fertilizer.â","She drew a circle in the air with one hand.","âAll the nutrients in this patch are gone. Theyâve been completely drained.â","Song Jingshuo crouched down for a closer look.","It was a patch of grass, and there was no visible difference or change in the soil beneath it.","âI canât see anything,â he said.","âI can tell the moment I touch it,â Aunt Pan explained. âMy hand feels it, and my brain just knows.â","Song Jingshuo nodded. âOkay.â","Just as the aunties had said, he could only accelerate growth. Plants still needed nutrients to grow.","This world still had to obey the law of conservation of matter and energy.","So large-scale cultivation would require a great deal of land, as well as a massive amount of fertilizer.","The word âfertilizerâ filled Song Jingshuo with helplessness. He crouched beside the grass, his head drooping almost to the ground.","âWhatâs wrong?â Aunt Pan asked.","After understanding what was troubling Song Jingshuo, Aunt Pan burst into cackling laughter.","By the fountain, Li Jiangbing had several people lined up with their dogs.","The dog owners all knew one another, and some of the dogs that had lost their owners had found new homes in the neighborhood.","Li Jiangbing extracted pure water from the fountain pool. Extracting clean, pure water from water that was already in liquid formâeven if it was unpurifiedâhad become extremely easy for him.","The water he extracted formed a sphere around each dog, and then began washing them with a steady splashing sound.","Some of the dogs didnât want to cooperate and ran around. The water spheres chased after them relentlessly.","Once the owners had worked up a lather, the clean water spheres came back and rinsed the dogs thoroughly. The whole process was effortless.","Afterward, the dogs shook themselves wildly, spraying water everywhere. Li Jiangbing extracted the water from their fur once more. When the owners ran a hand over the dogs, it felt as though they had just come out of a dryer.","âWow, this is so useful!â","Li Jiangbing genuinely felt that if this zombie disaster ended like the previous one, he could quit his job at the gym and open a pet-washing shop.","Extracting pure water from any liquid, or collecting water from the surface of a solid object, was very easy for him.","Extracting water from other forms was difficult. Air, for instance, was especially exhausting. Li Jiangbing had practiced all night in his apartment the day before, until his eardrums throbbed painfully. He stopped only when even his eyeballs began to hurt.","He had already tried extracting water from living organisms at Jiang Chengâs apartment. It was practically impossible and could be abandoned as an option.","Yesterday, at Yujing Xiangyuan, he separately tried it on living zombies and dead ones.","Later, they told Jiang Cheng, âTheyâre all pretty difficult. But there is a tiny bit of difference.â","âThe live zombies and the little birds are about equally difficult, but theyâre not the same.â","The little birds seemed to be protected by an invisible membrane; their flesh, blood, bones, and skin formed a single whole.","The live zombies, on the other hand, were like dry steamed buns that had been left out for many days.","âThe dead ones are a little different too.â","The dead zombies were like shaking one of those dry buns and discovering that there was some filling inside.","Still, none of them were easy to sink oneâs teeth into.","Whether alive or dead, living creatures seemed to be protected by some kind of safety protocol, Jiang Cheng thought.","When Zhou Wang led his people to the Youth Apartment, this was the scene they encountered.","Everywhere was brimming with vigorous life. Young bodies were full of vitality.","That was why Song Jingshuo couldnât understand how anyone from Jixiang Jiayuan could be willing to accept such an insubstantial, ridiculous âpaymentâ offered by Jiang Cheng.","Song Jingshuo was young, strong, and bursting with energy. He feared nothing. Not to mention that he had so many reliable companions and trusted comrades-in-arms.","The elderly were different.","Their children were trapped downtown or had already been confirmed dead.","They were frail, sickly, and left without anyone to rely on. A young man as strong and vigorous as Song Jingshuo could never truly understand that kind of panic and fear.","To them, Jiang Chengâs vague promise of being âtreated as a resident of the Youth Apartmentâ was genuinely appealing.","Zhou Wang brought several people with him, while a few other elderly residents came simply to watch the excitement.","The courtyard of the Youth Apartment was overflowing with life, exactly the sort of thing the elderly envied most.","The building heads gradually gathered. Aunt Pan came too, and everyone sat beneath the pavilion and talked.","Jiang Cheng explained her idea of setting up a communal kitchen to several of the building heads, and received unanimous support.","Quite a few of the elderly residents wanted to cook for the Youth Apartment. Two of them were full-time homemakers.","âItâs just the two of us left,â they said. âThe others all went to the schools. None of them came back.â","âOne of us never had children. The otherâs child was in college and died during the incident in June.â","During the first zombie disaster, the population of the neighborhood had already been drastically reduced, and very few children remained.","When the zombie virus came this time, the mothers who woke up and remembered that their children were at school rushed out recklessly, determined to reach them.","Some died in the stairwells, some downstairs, and some on the roads.","There were kindergartens, primary schools, and middle schools. At present, the Science and Technology New District had no high schools; the nearest ones were inside the Fifth Ring Road.","Not every family could send their children to a prestigious school downtown like Little Huangâs family. Most children still attended nearby schools from kindergarten through middle school.","No one knew how many had managed to reach their childrenâs schools successfully. In any case, none of them had returned.","Zhou Wang said, âOne person from our side came back last night, and two more returned this morning.â","Jiang Cheng said, âItâs the same for us. Two came back.â","Those who managed to return were not only lucky, but strong as well.","Zhou Wang said, âWho knows how many people are trapped downtown.â","It was already September 1âthe fourth day.","Words of power truly did possess strength.","While Zhou Wang was bringing people over to be interviewed by Jiang Cheng, his phone rang.","âBig Brother Zhou! Is that you, Big Brother Zhou?â A womanâs voice came from the phone, hoarse and strained.","âIâm from Building One. My husbandâs surname is WangâWang Changhe. Do you remember him?â","âHe used to serve on the homeownersâ committee with you. You fought zombies together.â","âBig Brother Zhou, my child and I are trapped at the school. Can you come save us?â","Say something, and it would come to pass."]},{"number":126,"title":"Chapter 126: 0126","paragraphs":["Jiang Cheng hired five people first.","One older man, two middle-aged women, and, in the end, she took on the two married women as well.","The older man had a chefâs certificate. Of the candidates, the two middle-aged women looked the most capable and clean. Jiang Cheng kept both of the other two because they were the youngest. The one without children looked under forty, while the one whose child had died looked only a little over forty. Among all the candidates, they were the strongest and most physically capable.","If everyone was elderly, Jiang Cheng was afraid they wouldnât be able to keep up physically, so she kept the two younger women.","She had just decided to tell Zhou Wang when she turned around and saw him hurrying over with his phone.","âJiang Cheng!â","âWhat is it?â","âSomeone at Gaoxin Middle School is calling for help!â","âWhat do we do?â","Some of the building captains had been sitting, some leaning against things, some playing with fireballs, and others with water spheres in their hands.","At the news, they all gathered around.","âAnother job?â","Another one.","Everyoneâs eyes lit up.","Interesting. Humanity was no longer satisfied with cowering behind the fences and barely surviving.","Yesterday, everyone had waited all night but never received an official announcement. There was no news that an emergency provisional government had been established.","Strangely, no one had been dejected, pessimistic, or dispirited that morning.","In fact, the last time, although the government had done everything it could, humanityâs eventual victory over the zombies had also relied on the strength of the people.","Humans now had confidence in themselves. They no longer feared zombies and had gained plenty of combat experience. They could no longer tolerate zombies invading their living space.","This time, they didnât need to wait for the government to issue a call to action.","Nor did Jiang Cheng need to give another impassioned speech about reason and righteousness.","All six building captains were ability users.","They were even more enthusiastic than ordinary people about killing zombies. In the process, they could test the combat methods they had devised for their abilities, and then use battle itself to stimulate and improve those abilities.","Jiang Cheng asked, âWhat exactly is the situation?â","Zhou Wang said, âItâs someone from our neighborhood. Her husband used to be part of our provisional residentsâ committee. His surname is Wang. Do you remember Wang Changhe?â","Jiang Cheng said, âThe tall one whose left shoulder was higher than his right?â","âThatâs him!â Zhou Wang said. âThe day before yesterday, our neighborhood organized a zombie-clearing operation. His family had protective armor, and his wife came out wearing it. But halfway through, she ran off. She said she was going to find her childâtheir kid is at Gaoxin Middle School. She never came back after that.â","In reality, they had killed enough zombies to clear a path to the underground garage and retrieve a car. The mother had driven off to rescue her daughter.","âI thought she was gone,â Zhou Wang said. âI didnât expect her to still be alive.â","âShe called from a landline.â","âShe said there are still over a hundred children at the school.â","Wang Changheâs wife had lost her phone, and there was no way she could have memorized the phone number.","She and several parents, along with a group of children, had fought their way through the school. Today, they finally escaped from the teaching building into the science building, where all the teachersâ offices were located.","They found a computer that could connect to the internet and logged on to the neighborhoodâs residentsâ forum.","Little Huang had been a little too diligent. He was practically obsessive about computers.","After the first zombie crisis ended, he had cleaned up the forum and removed all the pinned posts. As a result, the post containing the Jixiang Jiayuan provisional residentsâ committeeâs contact list had sunk far down the page.","The girl had searched through page after page and finally found it.","Wang Changheâs wife then used the office landline to call Zhou Wang for help.","Zhou Wang really didnât want to take on any more responsibility, but the word âchildrenâ was like a spell on him. He couldnât escape it.","So he still went to find Jiang Cheng.","Since everyone was eager to kill zombies and rescue people, Jiang Cheng was naturally delighted.","She hadnât crossed into this world just to go to work every day and put up with her bossâs nauseating advances.","She had come to this world to face challengesâor trials.","The first time the concept of the âSafety Protocolâ drifted into her mind, Jiang Cheng realized that her crossing into this world probably hadnât been an accident.","Someoneâor some organizationâhad to be manipulating the whole thing from behind the scenes.","But what was their purpose?","After thinking it over again and again, Jiang Cheng could come up with only one possibility: certain television variety shows, where contestants fought with everything they had to clear each stage and win.","Could she be a âcontestantâ placed into this world?","Gaoxin Middle School was about a ten- to fifteen-minute drive from their neighborhood, or roughly half an hour on foot.","The distance was neither especially near nor especially farâabout the same as the development-zone government offices.","âHow are we going to get there?â Jiang Cheng rested her hand against her chin.","They wouldnât just have to go there. They would have to come back, too.","And it wouldnât be only their group. There were many people at the school.","After thinking for a moment, she said, âWe still need to get some vehicles.â","The Youth Apartments were experts at getting vehicles.","Everyone immediately sprang into action.","Zhou Wang also called each person in his neighborhood who was capable of fighting.","In less than ten minutes, everyone had arrived wearing protective armor. Even Uncle Eighty came along in the metal armor he had made himself.","The long bayonet he had crafted had already been modified into a crescent-shaped shovel.","They had discovered during yesterdayâs real battle at Yujing Xiangyuan that a bayonet wasnât practical. A living human would lose the ability to moveâor lose their lifeâafter being stabbed through.","But zombies were different.","Zombies had to be killed by smashing or severing their heads. A bayonet was awkward for chopping.","In the end, Uncle Eighty had copied the crescent-shaped shovel the Youth Apartments had recently made and modified his own weapon accordingly. It worked much better.","Now he planted the crescent shovel on the ground and shouted in a voice like a thunderclap, âWhen are we leaving?â","The old man was impressive.","His appearance sparked several ideas in Jiang Chengâs mind.","These days, whenever she thought about anything, she had to approach it from the perspective of supernatural abilities and take their effects into account.","For instance, suppose something required a person to jump from the twentieth floor to accomplish it. In the past, they could have abandoned the idea immediately. There was no point even thinking about it, because no one could jump from the twentieth floor and survive.","But now, under these conditions, someone would simply say, âHave Zhou Wang jump.â","And the impossible would become possible.","With abilities to enhance them, people could let their imaginations run wild and think as boldly as they pleased.","Their supernatural abilities would make it happen.","Jiang Cheng explained the general outline of her idea to the metal-element ability users and asked, âIs it feasible?â","Cui Haiyang immediately nodded. âIt is! It absolutely is!â","The other metal-element users chimed in as well. âWe can do it! Thatâs a great idea. Why didnât I think of it?â","Jiang Cheng said, âIf itâs possibleâ¦â","Everyone waited for her to continue, but she merely smiled and changed the subject.","âAll right. Letâs see how things are going with Jingshuo.â","Song Jingshuo had gone to gather vehicles from the neighborhood.","There werenât many private cars left in their neighborhood, but there were still enough. Jixiang Jiayuan also provided several vehicles.","They collected fifteen suitable cars. Each could carry four or five people, making room for a total of sixty or seventy passengers.","While the vehicles were being prepared, people were also gathering.","In the middle of the bustling preparations, Jiang Cheng suddenly noticed several people watching from a distance with their arms folded. They didnât seem to have any intention of coming over.","The person in the middle was Cao Jiacai, with two young security guards beside him.","Someone else appeared to be standing behind the bushes, but Jiang Cheng couldnât see clearly.","A thought stirred in Jiang Chengâs mind.","She glanced around and, sure enough, spotted Little Fang, the security guard.","Little Fang was only nineteen, but he was brave enough. On the very first day, when the zombie virus had just broken out, he had dared to leave the security booth alone to rescue people.","It was also obvious that he had complete faith in Jiang Cheng. He always joined the groupâs operations and was often within Jiang Chengâs line of sight, so they had quickly grown familiar with each other.","âLittle Fang.â Jiang Cheng called to him.","The young man came running over. âWhat is it?â","âI need you to do me a favor.â","She leaned close and whispered something to Little Fang.","A few people from Cao Jiacaiâs group watched everyone bustling about in full swing. The sight irritated him.","âWhat are they running around for?â Cao Jiacai said. âThe compound has plenty of food and water. Why go out there and stir up trouble? If they were going out to find supplies, fine. But why go rescue people? Whatâs it got to do with us?â","âRescuing people is still the right thing to do, isnât it?â Young Wang said.","Young Wang had taken part in the group labor the previous day, working with the other metal-type superpowered people to make metal armor and crescent-shaped shovels.","He had actually enjoyed himself.","It had felt as though he had gone back to his childhood, when he used to hammer iron pots with his father and grandfather.","Now, watching everyone working hard in the distance, he felt a little tempted to join them.","Cao Jiacai glared at him. âYouâve got a servantâs bones. Youâre actually volunteering to work? Weâre not lowly laborers anymore! We have superpowers now! Get your head straight!â","Young Wang hesitated. âBut they have powers too. And theyâre college students.â","Cao Jiacai cursed. âTheyâve all read so many books theyâve read their brains stupid.â","He had seen it with his own eyes.","Those college-educated people would buy breakfast from a street stall, then thank the vendor after paying.","They were giving the vendor money, yet after handing it over, they actually thanked him?","Wasnât that idiotic?","Just then, Little Fang came running over.","Here was another little foolâsomeone who refused to stick with his own kind and insisted on following the property owners around.","Cao Jiacai no longer considered Little Fang one of âhis own.â He watched him approach with narrowed eyes and asked, âWhat do you want?â","âMiss Jiang asked me to find out whether youâre going on the operation later.â","Cao Jiacai sneered. âIâll go if I feel like it, and I wonât if I donât.â","Little Fang scratched his head. âSoâ¦ are you going or not?â","He couldnât understand plain speech. Cao Jiacai grew annoyed. âIâm not going!â","Little Fang glanced around furtively and leaned closer. âMiss Jiang said itâs fine if you donât go, but donât make a big deal about it.â","He continued, âMiss Jiang said that if you make a scene, it wonât look good. Itâll make her seem unable to control you, and everyone else will be unhappy too. If you donât go, other people might hear about it and refuse to go as well. Then Miss Jiang wonât be able to assign anyone to do anything.â","Those words pleased Cao Jiacai immensely.","âSheâs not stupid after all,â Cao Jiacai said. âLooks like everyone knows exactly whatâs going on.â","Who was stronger? Who deserved to be the leader?","Cao Jiacaiâs heart began to itch with excitement. He lifted his foot and was about to head over.","A hand reached out from behind the bushes and stopped him. âWhere do you think youâre going?â","Cao Jiacai began, âWerenât we going to find a bigââ","The other man cut him off, gave him a meaningful look, and shook his head.","Cao Jiacai glanced at Little Fang and said, âIâm not going. You tell her that. Donât think she can order me around.â","Little Fang looked at the man hiding behind the bushes, then ran back to find Jiang Cheng.","After Little Fang had left, Cao Jiacai finally asked the other man, âWerenât we going to find a big opportunity to drag her down? Iâd say this is the perfect time.â","Everyone over there was working themselves into a frenzy. This was exactly when he should go over, slam his hand on the table, and turn against her.","âHeyâJiang Cheng! Youâre a woman! Youâre not even that capable! You have no right to be our leader! Starting today, Iâm the leader!â","Yes, that was exactly how Cao Jiacai imagined it happening.","âDonât rush,â the other man said.","He continued, âTheyâre going to get a large vehicle. Thatâll be useful later, and we need one too. Let them get it first. Once they bring it back, weâll step forward and overthrow Jiang Cheng. Then you can become the leader!â","Cao Jiacai sighed admiringly. âYou college students really do have better brains!â","Little Fang ran back and told Jiang Cheng, âHe said he isnât going.â","âDid you tell him everything?â Jiang Cheng asked.","âI did.â Little Fang lowered his voice. âHe actually wanted to come over. He looked like he was marching over to make trouble. But someone nearby stopped him.â","âWho?â","âSomeone from Building Four. He used to follow Brother Song around all the time. What was his nameâ¦ Wang something Tian?â","Jiang Cheng narrowed her eyes and looked over. The man behind the bushes revealed half his body. Sure enough, he was someone familiar from Building Four.","Wang Haotian.","Why had he stopped Cao Jiacai? Jiang Cheng had been trying to lure the snake out of its hole.","It was only a matter of time before Cao Jiacai challenged her authority and tried to seize leadership of the group.","His thoughts were written all over his face. He made no effort to hide them.","But he still hadnât done anything. If he didnât throw the first punch, how could Jiang Cheng justifiably defend herself?","Jiang Cheng had never been the kind of person who waited for others to make the first move, passively allowing events to unfold.","She had wanted to give him a little push and speed things up, but she hadnât expected Wang Haotian to interfere.","âForget it.â Jiang Cheng reached back and stroked the little black cat resting on her shoulder.","Heâs not taking the bait. Then make your appearance at the school."]},{"number":127,"title":"Chapter 127: 0127","paragraphs":["When it came to vehicles, it still had to be the 535s.","To be honest, everyone had grown particularly attached to the four 535 buses and two forklifts from last time. The 535s were enormous. When all four drove into the residential complex, they practically filled the entire little plaza. Later, when people from the central bus terminal came to drive them away, everyone actually felt a little lost when the plaza suddenly opened up again.","When the two forklifts were driven back to Mai Duoduo, everyone had gathered around to see them off as well.","The 535s were too big to drive around casually, but who could resist trying out a forklift? Almost everyone had given it a go. By now, they were all little forklift experts.","But Mai Duoduoâs forklifts had already been driven back to themâtwo of them, in fact.","Once the 535s returned, it felt as though they had gone back to the atmosphere of two months ago.","Only, many of the neighbors from back then would never be coming back.","This time, Cui Haiyang led the team.","Li Jiangbing felt a little disappointed.","âYouâve led a team before, and so have I,â Jiang Cheng consoled him. âThey should get to do some work too.â","Li Jiangbing squatted there and watched the convoy leave. All the metal-element ability users had gone. Gao Yuxuan and Guo Jun had gone too, as had Aunt Panâeven Zhou Wang had gone.","Simply put, all the powerful ability users had been dispatched.","And he was the only one left behind.","There was work to do at the residential complex as well.","With Aunt Pan gone, there was no one left to cook for Property Management. The uncles, aunties, and older sisters had stepped up to take a trial shift.","But Jiang Cheng had recruited them for more than just cooking for Property Management, so the little kitchen there would definitely be inadequate in the future. They needed a proper large kitchen.","As it happened, there was one ready-made.","There was a cafÃ© inside the clubhouse. Before that, however, the owner had actually run a small restaurant there.","The portions were tiny despite the oversized plates, and the restaurant relied entirely on pretentious presentation to charge exorbitant prices, treating the residents like fat sheep to be fleeced. The residents quickly grew disgusted with it, and the restaurant soon went under.","That was why it had been converted into a cafÃ©.","But the owner had spent quite a bit of money renovating the kitchen, and he couldnât bear to tear it out. He had always hoped that he might find some fool willing to rent it as a restaurant one day, allowing him to collect the rent.","No one ever rented it, so it remained a cafÃ©.","The kitchen, however, was still there.","Jiang Cheng and the others reopened the door the clubhouse owner had locked and tore down the rental advertisement and phone number.","When they went inside, all the kitchen equipment was still there, merely covered in a layer of dust.","After checking, they found that it ran on natural gas rather than cooking oil. That was excellent news. If it had needed oil, it would have been troublesome; there was nowhere to get any now.","They turned on the faucet. Since it had not been used for so long, the water that came out at first was slightly discolored, but it soon ran clear.","Li Jiangbing resigned himself to his fate. Several enormous water balls floated in front of him, following as he moved. They spun as they went and washed the entire kitchen.","By the end, the water balls had turned murky, while the kitchen was spotless.","âHow convenient,â Jiang Cheng praised him.","Then she added, âYou should know that every girl dreams of having this ability.â","That was true. The girls had said as much themselves.","Especially the ones with long hair: âIt would make washing your hair so easy!â","Li Jiangbing had just gained one more possible direction for his future career.","Cui Haiyangâs team was very efficient at getting the buses. They returned an hour later.","The 535 bus terminal was only three stops away from the youth apartment complex. The roads were completely emptyânot a single car, person, or zombie in sight.","There were fewer buses parked at the terminal than last time, because the suburban express buses operated on a tidal schedule.","In the morning, large numbers of buses departed from the technology district for downtown, carrying people to work.","In the afternoon, empty buses were sent back downtown. Starting in the evening, large numbers of buses departed from downtown again, bringing the exhausted working people back home.","This time, however, no buses had returned on August 29.","A packed bus could hold around 150 to 200 people. To be safe, they drove four buses back.","The terminal had its own repair shop and warehouse, which contained a large quantity of supplies, mostly metal materials.","The metal-element ability users were like mice let loose in a granary. Everything they saw, they wanted to carry away.","Unlike earth-element ability users, who had an inexhaustible supply of material beneath their feet, or fire-element ability users, who used their own supernatural power as fuel, metal-element ability users needed metal.","Water-element abilities required water, while metal-element abilities required metal.","Every supernatural ability had its own advantages, as well as its own limitations.","This time, because the outside environment was relatively calm and there were very few zombies on the streets, the youth apartment complex and Jixiang Jiayuan did not block off Jixiang West Street as they had last time.","The four large buses drove straight onto West Street and stopped outside the east gate. They called Jiang Cheng.","âWeâre here.â","Zhou Wang, Aunt Pan, Guo Jun, Gao Yuxuan, Cui Haiyang, and several metal-element ability users waited inside the buses for everyone to come out through the east gate and board.","They chatted about how many people might have survived at the school, occasionally turning their heads to look outside.","The residential complexâs east gate was right outside the bus windows. Beyond the gate was a broad walkway. You had to walk quite a distance before you could see the inner courtyards, gardens, and little plaza.","âTheyâre coming,â someone said.","Everyone looked over. Sure enough, a large group was making its way toward them from inside the complex.","But Aunt Pan let out a surprised âHuh?â","âWhatâs Cao Jiacai doing over there?â","Several security guards stood at the east gate with their backs to the outside.","They were all wearing security uniforms.","Gates and security guards went together like a matched set. No one found it strange to see guards standing at the entrance, so they had not paid them any attention at first.","It was Aunt Pan who recognized her familiar coworkers from behind.","Once she pointed it out, everyone took a closer look. Sure enough, the man standing in the middle of the group of guards was Cao Jiacai.","Was he standing there to wait for Jiang Cheng and the others so they could board the buses together?","Why were two residents standing with him as well?","Of course not. He was standing there to play roadblock.","Cao Jiacai wanted to usurp power, and he wanted to do it with great fanfare. Wang Haotian had given him the idea: only by seizing power in front of a large crowd could he establish his authority, making people fear him and submit to him.","Cao Jiacai thought it made perfect sense.","He had to ascend the throne in a blaze of glory, under the gaze of the entire crowd.","Watching Jiang Cheng and the others approach, Cao Jiacai took a deep breath, preparing to face the grandest moment of his life.","He led his people forward to meet them and shouted, âHalt!â","Everyone actually stopped.","The little black cat leaped down from a nearby tree and landed on Jiang Chengâs shoulder. Jiang Cheng gently patted its head to reassure it.","Li Jiangbing stepped forward. âWhat are you doing?â","Cao Jiacai shot back, âWhat are you doing?â","The utterly pointless exchange left everyone speechless.","Jiang Cheng took a step forward and called out clearly, âMaster Cao, there are survivors at Gaoxin High School. Weâre going to rescue them. Are you coming?â","Oh? She had called him Master Cao.","When had Jiang Cheng ever treated him with anything but indifference? And now she was speaking to him so gently, politely, and courteously.","Cao Jiacai knew that he was no longer the down-and-out, invisible middle-aged security guard he had once been.","The attention he was receiving from her only made him swell with pride.","âIâm not going!â he shouted sternly. âAnd youâre not allowed to go either!â","Everyone was stunned.","Li Jiangbing raised his voice too. âWhat are you talking about? Weâre on our way to rescue people!â","âRescue them? You idiots, listening to some little girl!â Cao Jiacai began acting like everyoneâs father, pointing and lecturing them. âWhat do outsiders have to do with us?â","âWeâre not lacking food or clothes. We can guard Mai Duoduo, move all the supplies back here later, and live a safe, comfortable life!â","âItâs all because of this Jiang Cheng that youâve been led around by the nose, running off to save this person and that person every day.â","Cao Jiacai stuck out his belly. âJiang Cheng, let me make this clear: from today onward, you donât call the shots anymore!â","âStarting today, everyone listens to me!â","âFrom now on, Iâm the boss of this complex!â","He pointed at Young Zhao, Young Song, Young Wu, Young Zhang, and Young Suâthe people with superpowers. âAnd the rest of you, get over here. From now on, you answer to me. Stop following Jiang Cheng around like idiots. What does a woman know, anyway?â","Cao Jiacai was convinced that, with a speech as powerful as his, everyone would come rushing over the moment he raised his arm and called out to them.","In some rural areas, a village bullyâs word was law. No one dared disobey.","But he had forgotten that this was a cityâand not just any small city. This was S City, a massive metropolis of more than twenty million people.","People here had entirely different ideas. Their values were completely different too.","He thought, Why bother saving unrelated people? He assumed that if everyone no longer had to listen to Jiang Cheng, fight, or make sacrifices, and could simply lie around the complex eating and drinking, everyone would be thrilled.","Instead, not a single resident voluntarily came over to his side.","Everyone looked at him strangely. Some were stunned, some bewildered, some speechless, some disdainful. A few even looked at him with pity.","That last expression was especially unbearable.","Why wasnât this going the way he had imagined?","âAre you all deaf?â Cao Jiacai shouted, starting to lose his temper from embarrassment.","Wang Haotian quietly reminded him, âThe fire.â","Cao Jiacai suddenly realized. Rightâhe had to show off his strength.","Wu Jiancheng had been determined to master the ability to keep a flame burning in his hand without end. Cao Jiacai, however, had managed it naturally the day before.","He didnât even need to carry several lighters in his pockets as backups, the way Wu Jiancheng did. A tiny flame was always dancing playfully around his fingertips.","Cao Jiacai raised his hand. With a whoosh, a massive fireball appeared in front of him.","The bodies of fire-type superpowered individuals had already been altered by their abilities, so they no longer felt heat or pain from burning.","Other people werenât so lucky. The moment the huge fireball appeared, it failed to intimidate the people across from him and instead scalded his own allies first.","Young Wang and Little Zhao, the two superpowered security guards, had been standing behind Cao Jiacai on either side, looking like his personal guards. Wang Haotian, his scheming adviser, had also moved closer to Cao Jiacai so they could speak privately.","The wave of heat rolled over them. All three let out yelps and jumped backward.","Behind them stood one of Wang Haotianâs companions, two ordinary cleaners, and one ordinary security guardâall people Cao Jiacai had won over.","Other than Manager Wang, Yang Xinyan, Aunt Pan, and Security guard Fang, everyone else in the property-management staff had sided with Cao Jiacai.","The security guards and cleaners no longer wanted to work. Cao Jiacai had promised that anyone who followed him would enjoy good food and drink from then on. These people, who were not particularly educated, believed him.","Security guard Fang, however, had been too close to Jiang Cheng and the others, acting as their lackey and follower. Cao Jiacai had directly excluded him from his âinner circle.â","Over the past two days, Cao Jiacai had made several lewd jokes at Yang Xinyanâs expense. The young woman had told Manager Wang, but he could do nothing except advise her to avoid Cao Jiacai.","Yang Xinyan could never support Cao Jiacai.","As for Manager Wang, he understood all too well that by following Jiang Cheng and the others, he could at least preserve his dignity as a human being. If Cao Jiacai took power, a petty man from the bottom who had suddenly risen would first trample on the people who had once stood above him.","Yes, that meant Manager Wangâthe property manager.","Cao Jiacai had intended to intimidate everyone, only to scald his own people instead. The scene was simply too ridiculous. Asking everyone not to laugh would have been unreasonable.","Li Jiangbing: âPfftâpfftâughââ","Li Jiangbing really did try to hold it in, but he just couldnât.","The crowd behind Jiang Cheng also erupted in laughter.","Even outside the east gate, Cui Haiyang and the others stood up inside their vehicle to look through the windows. The atmosphere had seemed tense, and they had been preparing to get out.","Then this happened.","âHoly crap.â Gao Yuxuan had always been easy to amuse. He was bent over the large car window, laughing so hard he could barely stand.","Aunt Pan couldnât bear to watch. âSighâ¦â","The ridiculous scene put everyone at ease.","Cao Jiacai, humiliated and furious, shouted, âWhat are you laughing at?â","Jiang Cheng walked forward a few steps and called out clearly, âMaster Cao, if you have a problem with me, we can discuss it when we get back. Right now, letâs go save those people first. The school is full of underage children. Theyâve sent out a distress signal. We canât simply ignore them.â","Some people in the crowd actually felt that Jiang Cheng had walked too far ahead. But many were still laughing, and it would have been awkward for them to speak up.","Cao Jiacai had raised his arm and shouted his rallying cry, yet no one had rushed over in excitement to pledge allegiance to him. He was furious.","âIâm telling you all, following Jiang Cheng gets you nothingâand you still have to work!â he said. âFollow me, and none of you will have to work anymore. You can lie around every day, eating and drinking!â","But who would collect the trash? Who would sweep the grounds? Who would kill the zombies? Did he think the world could run itself? Someone had to do the work.","When all was said and done, he was just Liu Hongwang with a superpower.","Many of the residents couldnât help rolling their eyes.","Still receiving no response, Cao Jiacai grew increasingly agitated.","He glared viciously at Jiang Cheng. It was all her fault. Who knew what kind of spell she had cast over the others? They listened to her no matter what.","Whenever she told them to work, they obediently went and did it. What a witch.","Jiang Cheng was exceptionally beautiful.","At first, Cao Jiacai had thought that as long as she obediently stepped aside, he would keep her around for his own use later.","But now he knew he had to teach the people on the other side a lesson.","They thought he didnât dare, did they?","These city folk, these college students, were used to obeying the law. They assumed that just because they themselves wouldnât dare do something, he wouldnât dare either.","How naÃ ̄ve.","He had to kill one as a warning to the rest.","He had to behead someone.","Jiang Cheng could not be allowed to live.","It didnât matter. There were still several pretty women in the complex. Su Yu and Zhang Lesi were both attractiveâmore than enough for him.","A real man couldnât let himself be distracted by beauty.","Cao Jiacaiâs sinister gaze swept over the people behind Jiang Cheng.","Li Jiangbing was closest to her, followed by Song Jingshuo. Neither of them was particularly useful.","Wu Jiancheng.","Wu Jiancheng was fire-type, so he had to be wary of him.","Why hadnât they made a move yet? How annoying. Was she still outside their range?","Jiang Cheng took another step forward. âGet out of the way. Youâre in the way.â","Hurry up. Make your move. Iâve already come this far.","From inside the vehicle, Zhou Wang peered through the gates and also felt that Jiang Cheng had advanced too far.","Li Jiangbing felt the same.","Only Song Jingshuo stared at Jiang Chengâs back.","He had remained silent because he and Jiang Cheng had already discussed Cao Jiacai in advance. Jiang Cheng was absolutely not defenseless against Cao Jiacai, nor was she naÃ ̄ve.","As she moved closer, one step at a time, the words âlure the enemyâ flashed through Song Jingshuoâs mind.","She had said, That line.","Yes. Song Jingshuo understood now. Jiang Cheng was provoking Cao Jiacai into crossing that line first.","The overall moral standards at the Young Adult Apartments were very high. No one could kill another human being who was neither infected nor a criminal without cause.","But Cao Jiacai was too powerful. Expelling him would be useless and might even invite retaliation.","Song Jingshuo understood exactly what Jiang Cheng intended to do.","She needed Cao Jiacai to be the one who crossed the moral line first. That way, she could claim âself-defenseâ with a clear conscience.","Only then would everyone accept it, and the overall moral standards of the Youth Apartments could be preserved without corrupting the atmosphere.","With zombies swarming the entire world, once someone set a bad example, things could quickly spiral downward. This had already been proven by many residential compounds during the first zombie disaster.","But everything Jiang Cheng was doing depended on one premise: that she had the strength to overpower Cao Jiacai.","Jiang Cheng never did anything she wasnât sure she could pull off.","Song Jingshuoâs only remaining question was thisâwhat exactly was Jiang Chengâs trump card?","Li Jiangbing felt that Jiang Cheng had gone too far ahead. Uneasy, he caught up with her in a couple of strides. âAre you done yet? We still need to hurryââ","Now!","Cao Jiacai let out a furious roar.","A huge fireball shot toward them!","Its target wasnât Jiang Cheng. It was Li Jiangbing!","The fireball streaked past Jiang Cheng and engulfed Li Jiangbing from head to toe. He became a man on fire!","Shouts and screams erupted all around them.","Jiang Cheng shouted, âWu Jiancheng!â","Wu Jiancheng and Zhang Lesi simultaneously broke into a sprint.","Wu Jiancheng ran faster than he ever had in his life!","Li Jiangbing was his best buddy. If he let Li Jiangbing die here, he would never be able to forgive himself.","Wu Jiancheng stretched out his hand, his palm already feeling the scorching heat.","Put it out!","Put it the hell out!!!","But then he heard another wave of terrified cries from behind him.","Countless people screamed at the top of their lungs, âJiang Cheng!â","A fireball even larger than the one that had struck Li Jiangbing shot toward Jiang Cheng.","The attack on Li Jiangbing had been meant to lure Wu Jiancheng away.","A fire-type ability could both start fires and put them outâbut Wu Jiancheng couldnât be in two places at once.","Song Jingshuoâs pupils contracted sharply. Before his mind could even process what was happening, his body was already charging forward.","Zhao Yi charged ahead.","Su Yu charged ahead.","Many others rushed forward before their minds had even caught up.","Jiang Cheng!","In their field of vision, the crimson fireball came straight at her. Its blazing light turned Jiang Chengâs slender back into a black silhouette.","There was still a little black cat perched on the girlâs shoulder. Everyone had long since grown accustomed to seeing Jiang Cheng like this.","There was no doubt about itâthe little black cat would die alongside Jiang Cheng.","But ever since June 15, Jiang Cheng had been constantly defying expectations.","This time was no exception.","In Zhao Yiâs pupils, the silhouettes of the girl and the cat suddenly separated.","The little black cat leaped into the air.","Why was that black shadow expanding so rapidly?","It was growing huge!","The enormous black shadow charged straight at the fireball.","The gigantic body collided with the fireball.","The fireball shattered into pieces and went out in midair.","Cao Jiacai didnât even have time to react.","The enormous black shadow had suddenly smashed through the fireball and was now lunging straight at him.","All Cao Jiacai saw were stark-white fangs.","What was that thing?","How could it be so huge?","This wasnât scientific.","The flames on Li Jiangbingâs body went out. Zhang Lesi knelt on the ground, casting a healing spell over his burns while staring blankly ahead with her mouth hanging open.","Li Jiangbing lay on the ground, his head tilted backward. With the world upside down before his eyes, he too stared blankly with his mouth open.","A great many people were standing there with their mouths open.","Because that was the normal human reaction to shock.","Song Jingshuoâs question finally had an answer.","A giant beast.","Black fur.","Green eyes.","Cao Jiacai was clenched between its jaws like a tiny fish.","Sharp, snow-white teeth had pierced straight through his body.","Bright-red human blood dripped onto the ground.","His body, doomed but not yet completely dead, twitched spasmodically.","Jiang Cheng walked forward.","The girl looked so small and delicate before the giant beast.","âItâs more comfortable transforming outdoors, isnât it?â Jiang Cheng said with a smile.","The house had been too small. When Mo Li expanded to his maximum size indoors, he had to press against the ceiling. It was uncomfortable for him.","âGo on, spit him out. Donât keep biting him,â Jiang Cheng said.","The black giant obediently turned its head and spat Cao Jiacai onto the groundâright at Wang Haotianâs feet.","Wang Haotian sat on the ground, his whole body trembling. He had wet himself.","Everyone watched as Jiang Cheng raised her hand.","The giant beast leaped into the air.","Its enormous body rapidly shrank, finally transforming back into the little black cat everyone knew so well.","Every person had come up with a name of their own for the little black cat.","Black Civet, Little Black, Blackie, Two-Black, Coal, Coalballâpeople often called him whatever they pleased. They used their own names, and no one cared whether the little black cat recognized any of them.","Gao Yuxuan was especially fond of provoking him, and the little black cat had even scratched him on the butt once.","No one had ever imagined that the little black cat who so often lounged on Jiang Chengâs shoulder was actually a monstrous beast like this.","Jiang Cheng turned around and gently scratched the little black cat on the head.","âLetâs go. Weâre heading to Gaoxin Middle School,â she said.","Zhao Yi only wished Gao Yuxuan were in the car right now.","He was trembling with happiness."]},{"number":128,"title":"Chapter 128: 0128","paragraphs":["Autumn in S City was relatively dry. After a few showers in late August, the autumn rains had more or less come to an end.","For the past few days, the sky had been clear and cloudless, the autumn sunshine bright and beautiful.","The little black cat, perched on Jiang Chengâs shoulder, even yawned.","Everyone knew how much it loved basking in the sun. Every day, it searched around the residential complex for a spot where it could sunbathe and sleep.","But who could have imagined that it could transform into a gigantic creature as large as a house?","At that size, the most immediate impression it gave people was no longer âanimal.â","It was enough to trigger a full-blown fear of gigantic things.","The passageway inside the east gate fell utterly silent.","Li Jiangbing rolled over and came back to life.","In theory, although Wu Jiancheng had extinguished the flames on his body within seconds, and Zhang Lesi had used her lightning-fast healing ability to mend his burns and internal injuries, those few seconds of scorching heat, agony, and terror at the brink of death would have been enough to scar him for life.","But before that trauma had time to carve itself into his heart, the little black cat had transformed!","The process was interrupted completely.","Li Jiangbing had already skipped past the fact that he had just been burned. He scrambled to his feet and, amid the silence in which one could hear a pin drop, walked over and pointed at Mo Li.","âWas that him just now?â","His finger nearly poked Mo Li between the eyes. Mo Li opened his mouth to bite, and Li Jiangbing snatched his hand back like lightning.","They had been playing together for so long that they were quite familiar with each other.","Jiang Cheng said, âIt was him.â","Li Jiangbing planted his hands on his hips and glared at Mo Li. After a long moment, he finally spoke.","âWell, Iâll be damned. I thought he was vicious when I saw him scratch Gao Yuxuanâs ass. Turns out he was holding back!â","His mind automatically supplied an image of Mo Li biting down on Gao Yuxuan with a loud âchomp.â","Li Jiangbingâs booming voice broke through the frozen atmosphere, and the tension suddenly melted away.","A whole crowd came rushing over.","âHow did Blackie transform?â","âThatâs amazing!â","âYou scared the life out of me just now! Thank goodness for Mo Li!â","âOur Coalball is the best!â","Only Zhao Yi didnât dare approach. He kept his distance and watched from afar with reverence.","Looking at the girl and the cat bathed in golden sunlight, he felt that he had no regrets left in this life.","Song Jingshuo always played the annoying person who interrupted moments like this.","âWhat are we going to do with these people?â","The scene fell silent again.","This incident was much more serious than what Liu Hongwang had done. Liu Hongwang had merely wanted to go on strike and demand that things be distributed according to whoever made the most noise.","This time, it was the Cao family who had actually wanted to kill Jiang Cheng.","Cao Jiacai had attempted murder, and now, right before everyoneâs eyesâ¦ he was about to die.","As everyone looked at the dying man on the ground, Zhang Lesi quietly took a step backward. She didnât want anyone to call on her.","The healing ability Heaven had bestowed upon her was not meant to save someone like him.","Fortunately, everyone seemed to have collectively forgotten that there was someone at the scene who might be able to save Cao Jiacaiâs life.","No one thought he deserved to go on living.","When Cao Jiacai shouted that âeveryone could just lie around and eat and drink without working,â anyone with an education immediately understood what level of awareness he possessed.","This wasnât the first time everyone had gone through a zombie disaster.","During the previous outbreak, each person had volunteered at least four or five times.","It took an enormous number of people working hard simply to keep one residential complex functioning properly!","Take Zhao Yi, for example. He had a masterâs degree in environmental engineering, yet every day he had to deal with the smell of garbage until the stench clung to his entire body.","If everyone followed Cao Jiacaiâs idea of doing no work while lying around and eating and drinking, then during the last disaster they should have all been lying in garbage heaps, eating flies.","It was absurd.","And someone like that still wanted to seize power and become a leader. Noâin truth, what he really wanted to become was a ruler, an emperor of his own little kingdom.","And what about the others?","Everyone turned to look at the remaining conspirators.","Oh, I see. They wanted to earn credit by helping the future ruler rise to power, did they?","Jiang Cheng turned around.","The others instinctively took a step back.","Of them all, the most regrettable was Young Wang, the metal-type ability user. Everyone had worked with him yesterday, and things had gone quite pleasantly.","His ability was powerful, too.","Jiang Cheng asked, âWhat did he promise you?â","Young Wang and Little Zhao both stared at the tiles and said nothing.","One of the cleaners hurriedly tried to curry favor by selling out his accomplices.","âHe promised them a lot. He said heâd let the two of them manage the people and take charge of things from now on. He said the young lady would let them choose first.â","His words once again froze the air.","The hairs on the back of Zhang Lesiâs neck stood on end.","She raised her eyes to look for Su Yu, and Su Yu was looking for her as well.","The two girls met each otherâs gaze. In one anotherâs eyes, they saw anger, disgust, and lingering fear.","Li Jiangbing had nearly died.","If not for Jiang Chengâs little black cat transforming, who could have stopped Cao Jiacai?","A lot of people cursed.","âFuck.â","âHe was even planning to build himself a harem.â","âDamn, Iâve never even dared to fantasize that big.â","The womenâs expressions changed completely. They were shaking with rage.","Cao Jiacai tried to call for help, but blood gushed from his mouth the moment he opened it.","No one pitied him as they watched him bleed, convulseâ","Little Fang, the security guard, shouted angrily, âWang Jinchuan, Zhao Hai, I canât believe youâre that kind of people!â","Young Wang held his neck stiffly. âThat was just something he said on his own! I never agreed to it! I never had any such thoughts! I was only angry about the way theyââ","He had grievances and dissatisfaction he wanted to vent.","He hadnât wanted to join Cao Jiacai in building a harem. Ever since what happened with Liu Hongwang, he had strongly felt the inequality and unequal status between himself and the residents.","That inequality had always infuriated him.","He had so many emotions he wanted to express.","But Jiang Cheng drew two fingers through the air, cutting off his outpouring.","She had no interest in hearing about his wounded pride, inferiority complex, dysfunctional family, childhood trauma, difficult adulthood, personal journey, or anything else of the sort.","Every extra word was a waste of her time.","âYou, you, you, youâand you.â","Jiang Cheng pointed to them one by one.","There were three security guards and two cleaners in all.","Jiang Cheng announced, âYouâre fired.â","That was allâshe was only firing them.","The men, especially the three without supernatural abilities, felt their shoulders sag with relief. They looked as though they had just escaped death and were too drained to remain standing.","No one dared plead with Jiang Cheng on their behalf.","The residents involved in Liu Hongwangâs incident had gradually forgotten about it, but the property-management workers who had witnessed it in person could never forget.","Only now did they finally understand what the phrase âthank you for sparing my lifeâ meant when it appeared so often in television dramas.","Jiang Cheng pointed out several people who had not participated in the rescue operation.","âYou keep an eye on them and make sure they pack their things and leave.â","Everyone nodded.","âGot it. Leave it to us.â","Cao Jiacai continued to spew blood and convulse, and finally died.","No one paid him any attention. Once the cleaner testified that âhe said the young lady would let them choose first,â Jiang Chengâs moral standing rose to an untouchable height.","If the government had still existed, then of course the people who had committed wrongdoing should have been handed over to the authorities.","But the government still hadnât appeared.","Under these extraordinary circumstances, with neither a government nor any coercive institution in existence, it was entirely justified for ordinary people to carry out their own simple sense of justice.","Even so, everyoneâs eyes couldnât help drifting toward another direction.","There were still two people left. Everyone had seen that two residents had been in league with Cao Jiacai.","Some were curious about what they had been thinking and why they had chosen to stand with him.","Wang Haotianâs thoughts were actually very simple. He wasnât the sort of person suited to leadership, so he needed to follow the right leader if he wanted to drink more of the broth.","Unfortunately, the leadership of the Youth Apartments was firmly held by a woman named Jiang Cheng.","What effect would one woman have on a group of men?","You canât smoke during meetings.","You canât use filthy language involving genitalia.","And you certainly canât make lewd jokes.","But that wasnât even the worst part.","The worst part was that someone like Nie Kuizhang, who had done so much for the residential compound, had actually been punished just for making a lewd joke at a woman and touching her onceâjust taking a little advantage of her.","There was no justice!","How many zombies had Nie Kuizhang killed, compared with the few that woman had taken down?","In the deepest layer of many menâs thinking was the assumption that âonce my contributions are great enough, women should be part of the reward.â","Wang Haotian felt that if the provisional committee had been an all-male organization, this wouldnât have been an issue at all.","Everyone would even have treated it as an unspoken rule.","In Wang Haotianâs eyes, Nie Kuizhangâs punishment was like a whip lashing all men collectively.","Although Li Jiangbing and Song Jingshuo had stepped forward to deliver the punishment, Wang Haotian knew that the hand holding the whip actually belonged to Jiang Cheng.","If the provisional committee had not had Jiang Cheng, the matter with He Tian would have been brushed off with a few curses and laughs.","From the very beginning, Wang Haotian had wanted Jiang Cheng removed.","He had even tried to stir up gender conflict in front of Song Jingshuo, hoping to provoke him into fighting for power.","Unfortunately, Song Jingshuo had refused to take the bait and had instead mocked him.","Wang Haotian and his accomplice were terrified now.","The property-management staff had been expelled, but what about the two of them? Would they be dealt with differently?","Could it beâ¦ that they intended to kill them?","Did Jiang Cheng consider their betrayal, as property owners, more unforgivable than the crimes of those property-management employees?","Wang Haotian trembled with fear.","But he had no idea that his way of thinking was worlds apart from Jiang Chengâs.","Jiang Cheng acted as though she hadnât even noticed the two of them. âLetâs go.â","She took the lead and started toward the east gate.","Everyone glanced at the person sprawled on the ground, unable to get up. Pinching their noses, they went around him and followed Jiang Cheng.","Outside the east gate, only the first vehicle was facing directly toward it. The people inside that vehicle had witnessed everything that happened at the gateâfrom beginning to end.","Their faces were practically pressed against the windows!","They just wanted a better look.","What had happened? Why was the little black catâ¦?!","As soon as Zhao Yi got into the vehicle, he called out to Gao Yuxuan. âYuxuan!â","He leaned over and brought his face close.","Without a word, Gao Yuxuan swung his hand and slapped him hard across the face!","The crack of it rang out, startling everyone.","âOwâ¦â Zhao Yi covered his cheek, blissful. âIâm not dreaming.â","Everyone else: ââ¦â","Jiang Cheng laughed.","Back in the residential compound, those who had stayed behind whispered, âIs Jiang Cheng really going to keep those two?â","âWhat else can she do?â someone replied. âTheyâre property owners too.â","Jiang Cheng hadnât even driven those property-management employees away. She had fired them.","But how could she fire property owners?","They had bought their homes here and therefore had the right to live here. No one could drive them out.","Someone muttered, âActuallyâ¦â","Everyone understood what he was about to say.","There still hadnât been a single piece of information on television. The government had made no move at all.","Perhaps this really was the end.","But the people at Youth Apartments were neither despairing nor depressed. In fact, they were in remarkably high spirits.","Because they had something supporting them spiritually.","The government might be gone. Law-enforcement agencies might be gone. But in Youth Apartments, what was considered right under a law-based society remained right, and what ought to be done still ought to be done.","For example, anyone who had paid money to buy a home had the right to live there. No one could drive them away.","Jiang Cheng was preserving the entire framework of society.","That was what made her different from Cao Jiacai.","Cao Jiacai didnât understand how society functioned at all. He wanted to ascend the throne, become a local emperor, have absolute authority, open a vast harem, and indulge in wine, women, and luxury.","Song Jingshuo was thinking about this in the vehicle as well.","He glanced at Jiang Cheng sitting beside him. The wind blowing in through the window stirred the hair above her forehead, and in the shifting strands was a tranquil beauty.","Jiang Cheng had never wanted to become a local emperor.","She certainly had the power to drive out the property owners who held legal title to their homes.","But if she did that, she would no longer be a leader. She would become a wielder of hegemony, a dictator.","Hegemony and dictatorship were certainly satisfying in the short term.","But where there was light, there was shadow; where there was good, there was evil. Everything had two sides. There was never any absolute good.","The ultimate outcome of hegemony and dictatorship was not merely a minority profiting while the majority suffered.","Its final form was one person profiting while everyone else suffered.","Under hegemony and dictatorship, the legal framework and moral order would be reduced to ashes. In the end, one person would win, and everyone else would lose.","That was not what Jiang Cheng wanted at all.","Everything Jiang Cheng had been doing was aimed at achieving the best possible outcome under the conditions already in place, using every available person and resource.","It might not be perfect, but within the existing circumstances, it was the best that could be achieved.","What kind of thinking was this? What kind of person was Jiang Cheng?","In the breeze flowing through the vehicle window, Song Jingshuo found his answerâ","A manager.","Yes, that was it.","Jiang Cheng was a quintessential managerâa successful one.","That was why a professional wage earner like Song Jingshuo could not help but gather around her."]},{"number":129,"title":"Chapter 129: 0129","paragraphs":["Back when there had been plenty of vacant rooms, Jiang Cheng had insisted on putting Duoduo, Guo Jun, and the others together with two of the property-management staff in each room.","Song Jingshuo had joked that she was a born capitalist.","Looking back now, hadnât that been the behavior of a true operator?","A good operator would rather destroy defective products than let employees take them home as benefits.","It sounded cold, heartless, and wasteful.","But it effectively maintained quality control and prevented the defective-product rate from suddenly soaring.","What Wang Haotian wanted when he said he wanted to âfollow the right leaderâ was exactly the state Song Jingshuo was in now.","Because she had followed the right leader, everything was comfortable and went smoothly. There was no need to overthink anythingâjust follow her and get the job done.","That was the ideal state for a wage earner.","Song Jingshuo glanced at Jiang Cheng, then at Mo Li, who was snoring away on Jiang Chengâs lap. âHe fell asleep that fast?â","âYep.â Jiang Cheng stroked Mo Liâs jet-black fur.","Maximizing the energy expenditure had been quite substantial.","In fact, from a practical standpoint, there had been no need to maximize the attack. A single blow at ordinary strength would have been enough to kill Cao Jiacai. But Jiang Cheng had been determined to give Mo Li a proper debut today.","Since it was a debut, it had to be impressive.","Nothing left a stronger impression than going all out.","Everyone seemed to have accepted it quite well.","Gao Yuxuan kept shifting around as though something were poking him beneath his backside. He simply couldnât sit still, twisting this way and that.","As soon as Song Jingshuo finished speaking, he seized the opportunity to cut in. âJiang Cheng, how was Mo Li able to transform?â","The people in the bus all fell silent. Gao Yuxuan had asked the question everyone wanted answered.","Jiang Cheng said, âI donât know either, but my guess is that it has something to do with the zombie virus. Look at usâwe all have supernatural abilities. Maybe this is just a small animalâs supernatural ability.â","âAnyway, itâs a good thing for us right now.â","Yes. As long as it was a good thing, that was enough.","Song Jingshuo could actually imagine that Mo Li must have been able to transform for some time already. Jiang Cheng had clearly been waiting for the right opportunity to make Mo Liâs existence publicly acceptable.","Todayâs opportunity had been perfect. Cao Jiacai had practically delivered himself to them as a stepping stone.","The more vile Cao Jiacai behaved, the more righteous Mo Liâs appearance seemed.","No one would worry that Mo Li might be a monster, or that he might hurt them as well.","Suddenly, someone at the front let out a cry.","Everyone looked outside the bus and was struck speechless.","Their destination was Gaoxin Middle School, but they had to pass Gaoxin Elementary School on the way there.","The street outside was filled with zombies.","In the four days since the second outbreak, the only time Song Jingshuo, Zhou Wang, and the others had seen so many zombies had been at the district government offices.","There had been very few zombies in the residential areasâso few that Jixiang West Street had not even needed to be sealed off. The two residential compounds could come and go as they pleased.","So all the zombies from the residential areas had gathered here.","But everyone had already seen plenty of zombies. They had seen swarms of them, even crowds packed together as densely as ants. The sheer number of zombies lining a street would not have shocked them.","What left them speechless was that this was the first time they had seen so many female zombies.","At a glance, almost all of them were women.","There were a few male zombies, of course, but so few that they were practically negligible.","Someone muttered, âTheyâre all the mothersâ¦â","Yes. Looking down the street outside the elementary school, all they could see were zombie mothers.","Tears began streaming down Su Yuâs face.","Li Jiangbing quickly reached into his pocket and pulled out a packet of tissues for her.","While everyone was still stunned, Jiang Cheng shouted, âCui Haiyang! Give it a try!â","Cui Haiyang came back to himself. âOh! Right!â","Cui Haiyang stood up, and several other metal-type ability users rose with him.","They each grabbed one of the support poles inside the bus, or simply pressed their hands against the walls.","These 535 buses had already been modified by the metal-type ability users on the way back.","During the previous disaster, Cui Haiyang and the others had welded crude iron bars over the windows. The bus station had since removed those bars, and the windows shattered by the second-generation zombies had been replaced as well.","This time, they did not need to weld anything. They had found materials at the bus station, pressed them against the windows, and activated their abilities. In no time, they had equipped the buses with strong, tightly spaced metal grilles, ensuring the passengersâ safety.","Now, as they passed in front of the elementary school, the zombie mothers on the street leaped up and slammed against the buses. They could only strike the metal grilles; they could not break the glass behind them.","The ability users began exerting their powers.","Guillotine blades began to âgrowâ from the metal bus bodies.","From the outside, it looked as though the buses had suddenly begun spitting out metal âtonguesâ all over themselves.","They shot out in an instant, then vanished just as quickly.","They emerged at shoulder height. The moment they extended, they severed a zombieâs neck, sending its head rolling away.","The next instant, they retracted, leaving the bus body smooth and seamless once more.","Heads rolled all along the street outside the elementary school.","This was Jiang Chengâs suggestion to the metal-type ability users.","With their supernatural powers backing them up, they only needed to let their imaginations run wild. Whether they could actually do it was something the ability users could experiment with themselves.","When Cui Haiyang and the others heard the idea, they had immediately thought it was feasible.","They had turned a public bus into a moving blade-covered vehicle.","âHoly shit!â Zhao Yi exclaimed.","Gao Yuxuan burst out laughing.","As an electric-type ability user, Gao Yuxuan had gone along with them to work on the buses. He had already seen the metal users testing them on the way back.","At that moment, it became possible to distinguish the third-generation zombies from the huge mass of second-generation ones.","The second-generation zombies continued charging blindly at the buses, trying to smash through the windows.","The ones that retreated instead were the third-generation zombies.","Third-generation zombies knew that they had to stay alive. They were like people who knew to run home when it started raining.","Everyone had grown accustomed to seeing one or two third-generation zombies mixed into a swarm.","But Zhao Yi suddenly said quietly to Gao Yuxuan, âDo you think they could evolve even further?â","Could human zombies evolve into enormous creatures like Mo Li?","Mo Liâs transformation had to be connected to the zombie virus. If a tiny cat could evolve into something like that, why couldnât human zombies do the same?","Gao Yuxuan said firmly, âEven if they can, thereâll definitely be some kind of balance. Weâll be able to evolve too.â","Balance?","Zhao Yi thought about it. In fact, Mo Liâs appearance today had already upset the balance.","Before Mo Li transformed into a giant beast, the existence of third-generation zombies and the emergence of human ability users had already created a balance.","Mo Liâs appearance was not balanceâit was a disruption of balance.","And besides, balanceâ¦","That thing called balance had always existed faintly in the background.","So who, exactly, was maintaining it?","That question touched on the root of how the zombie virus had originated.","By now, almost no one asked anymore. Everyone knew there was no answer.","Although their destination was the middle school, they could not simply ignore the elementary school after seeing what had happened.","Besides, there were far too many zombies in the street. They had to clear them out.","The public buses drove back and forth along Xueqian Street several times. Soon, the road was covered with headless corpses and rolling heads.","Then they stopped.","Su Yu raised a protective barrier and got off the bus with Cui Haiyang. Together, they opened the elementary schoolâs large iron gate.","Zhou Wang entered first at flying speed to scout the area. When he returned, he let out a long sigh. âSighâ¦â","No one needed him to explain. If the mothers outside had become zombies, then the elementary school must be full of zombified students.","Everyoneâs mood grew heavy.","âLet Mo Li go first.â Jiang Cheng patted Mo Li awake. âWake up.â","Mo Li was bleary-eyed. He stretched out his front paws and gave a long, luxurious stretch across Jiang Chengâs lap.","Now that Mo Li could transform whenever it wanted, without having to hide from humans, it was very happy too. âMeow~â","Jiang Cheng said, âGo on.â","He opened the car door specifically for Mo Li and let it out.","The bus followed it into the school.","Sure enough, there were many child zombies only half a personâs height.","It was a heartbreaking sight.","But Mo Li felt no such pity.","Once humans mutated into zombies, their scent changed completely. To Mo Li, they had become an entirely different species.","Everyone crowded toward the front of the bus, especially Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan. They were practically plastered against the windshield.","So they got to watch Mo Li transform once again.","âHuh? It can control its size too?â","âDamn, thatâs so responsive!â","This time, Mo Li didnât grow to its maximum size. It transformed into a leopard roughly the size of an ordinary one.","Against elementary-school-aged zombies, it didnât even need to leap. While running, it could bite their necks clean through.","Its speed was like lightning. Only Zhou Wang could match it.","535","The bus was too large. All four vehicles couldnât drive in, so they brought in only one. That way, it would have enough room to turn around.","But the elementary-school zombies were simply too short.","Some of the lower-grade students were practically little bean sprouts.","The metal-element superpowered user had to press his face against the window to spot them clearly, then release guillotine-like blades at the exact height needed to sever their heads.","After clearing out the zombies around the school in batches, everyone finally got out of the vehicles.","Someone sighed, âThis makes things so much easier.â","At least they didnât have to fight the zombies hand-to-hand right from the start.","Gao Yuxuan raised a megaphone. âAre there any survivors? Are there any survivors?â","A window above opened, and a child shouted, âHelp! Help!â","There really were survivors.","Little Huang said, âIâll go take a look.â","He went straight into the school building.","Everyone followed him inside. They watched as Little Huang maneuvered through the zombies in the corridor. The little zombies all tried to pounce on him, but they simply couldnât lock onto him.","His footwork was god-tier. He moved through the horde as if no one else were there.","Everyone who had ever played video games was insanely jealous.","Su Yu had specifically taken an electronic watch from the supermarket so she could time her protective barrier and record how long it could last.","During battles that werenât especially intense, they tried not to push their superpowers to the point of total exhaustion.","After several days of experimenting, everyone had worked out quite a few patterns.","With normal use and repeated practice, they could quickly improve their control, such as their precision and accuracy.","Gao Yuxuan could release exactly the voltage he wantedâseveral volts if he wanted several volts. That was something he had trained himself to do.","The advantage was that it placed no additional burden on the brain, and a short rest was enough for a rapid recovery.","The disadvantage was that it had little effect on raising the upper limit of their abilities.","The other method of training was to push themselves to exhaustionâto the point where their noses and ears bled, or even their eyeballs began to ache and bleed.","The downside was that this was training with their lives on the line. It inflicted enormous pain on both the brain and the body, and recovery took a long time.","Even after sleeping through the entire night, Li Jiangbing still felt terrible the next day.","The advantage, however, was that this was the best way to raise the upper limit of their superpowers.","Su Yu had now gotten used to walking at the front and serving as a human shield.","Her protective barrier couldnât remain active for long periods, but even if she was ambushed, her body would instinctively raise the barrier on its own.","Walking in front was the safest position for her.","Su Yu was no longer afraid of zombies.","But when the little bean sprouts came shrieking and lunging at her, she still suffered.","These were elementary-school children who used to have to jump up and cling to the cafeteria serving window, their feet dangling and kicking helplessly in midair.","With tears streaming down her face, Su Yu tightened her grip on her weapon, gritted her teeth, and struck."]},{"number":130,"title":"Chapter 130: 0130","paragraphs":["Many problems only reveal themselves in practice.","Take the armor everyone uses now. Even the metal armor modeled after it by metal-type superpowered individuals was designed during the first zombie disaster.","It was a product of necessity.","Under the circumstances at the time, the priorities were speed and quantity.","The armor completely changed the course of humanityâs battles against the zombies. It greatly reduced human casualties in combat, as well as the rate at which second-generation zombies appeared.","The first zombie disaster broke out over a weekend. Except for the universities, all the schoolsâfrom kindergartens and elementary schools to middle schoolsâwere empty. The children were all at home.","The armor had mainly been designed to deal with adult zombies.","It primarily protected the shoulders and neck, arms, thighs, and calvesâthe bodyâs key vulnerable areas.","But now that they were facing the little ones at the High-Tech School, the flaws had become obvious.","For zombies that height, raising their arms or leaping up put them at exactly the right height to attack the wide-open area around the waist and abdomen.","After all, during the first zombie disaster, there had never been a situation where large numbers of elementary-school-aged zombie children gathered together. The occasional child zombie had been scattered, so no one had frequently attacked that part of the body.","The corridor was also too narrow to move around in. Most ordinary people were forced to retreat, while the superpowered individuals took the lead.","Guo Jun, Gao Yuxuan, and Wu Jiancheng were all ranged attackers. They could throw fireballs or discharge electricity from a distance.","Guo Jun only grew fiercer as the battle went on. After nearly being attacked in the stomach several times by the little zombie children, he lost his temper. The electricity he released suddenly thickened, and with a deafening boom, one of the little zombiesâ heads exploded.","Gao Yuxuan: âHoly crap!â","Everyone began to realize that ranged superpowered individuals were actually not very suitable for fighting in groups.","Although Wu Jiancheng threw his fireballs toward distant targets, the people beside him still found the waves of heat uncomfortable.","Fire-type superpowers were best suited to fighting alone.","When a group of little zombies rushed over, Aunt Panâs eyes filled with pity. She slapped the ground, and several ridges rose from the concrete floor of the corridor.","The little zombie children tripped over themâor were even sent flyingâand came rolling right up to the group.","Everyone charged forward, bringing down one shovel after another and chopping off their heads.","It was a nightmare.","This was the most horrifying battle they had faced since they began killing zombies.","It ranked alongside the baby zombies at Renxin Hospitalâthe ones that had leaped up and flailed aroundâas one of their worst nightmares.","Li Jiangbing sighed as he shoveled away the bodies.","When facing adult zombies, he had to raise the shovel to chest height and use it like a bayonet.","Against the little ones, he simply let his arm hang down and held the crescent-shaped shovel horizontally. Childrenâs necks were much thinner than adultsâ, so cutting through them required very little effort.","With his arm hanging at his side, Li Jiangbing swung the shovel again and again. Each strike took a little head.","Mo Li leaped into the second-floor corridor from outside the building.","He let out a sharp breath and shot forward.","He raced across the floor, kicked off the walls, and even paused for an instant on the ceiling, transforming into a black shadow. He streaked from one end of the corridor to the other, leaving behind nothing but bodies with their throats bitten through.","Zhou Wang, Little Huang, and Mo Li were all well suited to fighting alone.","Su Yu could act as everyoneâs shield.","In short, the group and the superpowered individuals gradually learned to work together and found a suitable way to fight.","At last, the zombies throughout the school were more or less cleared out.","The remaining corners and hidden spots were left to Mo Li, Zhou Wang, and Little Huang. One relied on speed, while the other two relied on their senses. They were the perfect cleanup team.","But only a dozen or so children had been rescued.","In that enormous school, only a dozen or so elementary school students had survived.","Every one of them was desperately hungry. The first thing they asked was, âUncle, do you have anything to eat?â","âAuntie, do you have any food?â","For the past few days, they had survived by rummaging through schoolbags and storage cabinets for snacks their classmates had brought to school in violation of the rules.","They all smelled terrible.","Their faces should have been young and innocent, yet exhaustion was written all over them.","Nervously, they asked, âDo you know where my mom and dad are?â","No one could answer.","Everyone knew that the heads of the childrenâs mothers might well be rolling around on Preschool Street.","The group consisted mostly of young, unmarried men and women who had no idea how to comfort children.","All they could say was, âI donât know.â","The children asked, âCan you take me home?â","Everyone found themselves at a loss again.","Little Huang returned after finishing his sweep. He walked over and said, âThere are students at the middle school next door waiting for us to rescue them. Thatâs urgent, so we have to deal with it first.â","âGet in the vehicles with us.â","âCome over here and line up. Boys in one line, girls in the other.â","The children seemed to find a pillar of support all at once. They quickly formed two lines in front of Little Huang.","They even adjusted their own positions automatically. Whenever the person in front completely blocked their view with the back of their head, they knew they were shorter and moved forward in line.","Within seconds, the two lines had been arranged neatly from shortest to tallest.","Everyone breathed a huge sigh of relief, though their hearts ached at the same time.","When Mo Li appeared in his leopard form, none of the children showed the slightest fear.","âHeâs so amazing!â","âOne bite and a zombie is gone!â","âIs he a leopard?â","Jiang Cheng answered, âNo. Heâs my cat.â","She held out her hand. Mo Li shrank down, then leaped along her arm and perched on her shoulder.","The children were stunned.","âWowww!â","Jiang Cheng explained to them, âBecause of the zombie virus, many people developed superpowersâwater, fire, electricity, earth, and so on. That auntie can make the floor bulge up. She has an earth-type superpower.â","âMy little cat developed a superpower too. He can grow bigger and become incredibly powerful, helping us kill zombies and rescue people.â","The children all began speaking at once.","âI know! I know!â","âTeacher Zhang can shoot fire! He locked us in the classroom and burned the zombies!â","âMingzhi Meng is in sixth grade. She can turn things into water, although she can only make a little. She left us some water to drink, then went out to find food for us, but she never came back.â","âDid you see her?â","Their voices were childish, their words innocent.","Su Yu felt as though she could hardly breathe.","âAll right, no more talking,â Little Huang said. âGet ready to board the vehicles.â","The children obediently followed.","The vehicles continued toward the middle school.","Two streets and a stadium lay between the two schools. Schools and companies in the development zone held their events at this central stadium.","Fortunately, there had been no event there on the twenty-ninth. There were a few scattered zombies, but they ignored them for now and headed straight to the middle school.","The High-Tech Middle School currently had only a junior division. A senior division had originally been under construction, and at the beginning of the year, they had announced that it would be ready to accept students in September.","Then the zombie disaster happened. Afterward, there were too few students, and they could not gather enough teachers.","The construction of the senior division was therefore suspended.","After testing the method in actual combat, they had more or less developed a new way of fighting.","First, they sent Mo Li and the vehicles into the school to clear out the large groups of zombies in batches.","The blade vehicles were truly astonishingly efficient.","The junior-high students were already close to adult height.","The metal-type superpowered individuals were much more comfortable this time. They no longer had to press their faces against the windows and peer downward, searching for the height of little zombie childrenâs necks.","The âtonguesââor perhaps more accurately, the âguillotine bladesââthat extended from the vehicles varied in length. The difference in strength between the metal-type superpowered individuals could be seen at a glance.","Overall, however, the metal-type superpowered individuals were improving extremely quickly.","This was mainly because they had been using their superpowers nonstop over the past few days. Making armor, crafting weapons, and producing all sorts of other things depended on them. Although their individual strengths varied, their overall progress was rapid.","Another reason was that Li Jiangbingâs superpower had actually improved at an astonishing rate.","That was because every night, he trained until his eardrums hurt, his vision blurred, and his eyeballs ached.","During the day, however, he used his powers for chores like cleaning and bathing the puppies, so no one else noticed how much he had improved.","But whenever Jiang Cheng saw him chasing a puppy with a water ballâor even several water balls chasing several dogs at onceâshe would smile knowingly.","Li Jiangbing was truly someone who listened to advice.","He might not have been especially clever himself, but as long as he followed the right friends and leaders, his willingness to take advice became one of his greatest strengths.","Mo Li had grown even larger. He had not reached his maximum size, which would have been truly astonishing, but he was already much bigger than he had been in elementary school.","His back rose as high as a personâs shoulders, and adults had to tilt their heads back to look at him.","Everyone quickly understood the significance of that height: one bite, and a skull was crushed.","He charged through the zombies without a care.","After watching for a while, everyone realized that the zombies could not even break through his fur.","When there were too many of them, a few zombies would occasionally grab hold of his fur. Mo Li would instantly puff up, sending the zombies flying.","Su Yu suddenly thought that if this continued, even the faces would be smashed to pieces, and the families would not be able to identify the bodies.","Then she felt foolish for thinking that.","The family members might not even still be alive. With so many deaths, there was no proper process for identifying bodies anyway. They were handled in batchesâlast time they had been burned, and this time they were being buried.","Su Yu sighed.","Zhou Wang returned. âWe found them.â","When everyone entered the school, they had already seen several zombie corpses. The traces of battle recorded the middle school studentsâ resistance and attempts to save themselves.","The surviving students had fought while retreating, eventually falling back into the cafeteria and barricading the doors.","A few parents were among them, and two cafeteria workers had survived as well.","The adults cooked food for the children.","After holding out until today, everyone felt they could no longer simply wait for death. But without armor, charging outside was far too dangerous.","Only four parents had come wearing armor to search for their children. One of them was Wang Changheâs wife.","âWe have to call for help,â she said.","Everyone was pessimistic. âWho can we call for help?â","Some of the parents had brought their phones, but the emergency number was useless. They had also tried calling the temporary emergency command centerâs hotline from the previous zombie disaster, but the number was no longer in service.","Wang Changheâs wife, however, refused to give up. Her name was Xiao Dan, and her daughter was Wang Yunya.","As the saying went, people from the same family shared certain traits. Families tended to have things in common.","Wang Changhe was a courageous man, and Xiao Dan was no different. Otherwise, she would never have come alone to rescue her daughter.","Wang Yunya had awakened a fire-based superpower. She had been repeatedly training herself in the cafeteria over the past two days. If the number of zombies was not too great, she could at least hold her own.","Several other people in the cafeteria had awakened superpowers as well.","âI want to try contacting our neighborhoodâs interim committee,â Xiao Dan said.","During the first zombie disaster, the people of Jixiang Jiayuan had organized themselves almost as effectively as those in Youth Apartments.","If no one at Jixiang Jiayuan could be reached, Xiao Dan was considering trying to contact Youth Apartments for help.","She and her husband had fought zombies alongside the people from Youth Apartments before, so they knew very well how strong they were.","She did not have a phone and did not know Zhou Wangâs number. But she knew that during the disaster, both Jixiang Jiayuan and Youth Apartments had posted the contact lists of their interim committee members on the residentsâ forums.","A few people wearing armor organized themselves and decided to make a run for the laboratory building. Only the laboratory building had computers that could connect to the internet.","Wang Yunya was one of the stronger superpowered individuals among them, so she definitely had to go. Ordinary people would be in even greater danger.","The mother and daughter argued back and forth over who should wear the armor.","In the end, another parent gave up his suit of armor. It was better to have someone with a superpower wear it; their chances of survival were higher than those of an ordinary person.","Thus, Xiao Dan and another parent led several superpowered students out of the cafeteria. After enduring numerous dangers, they successfully reached the laboratory building, found a computer with internet access, looked up Zhou Wangâs phone number, and called him for help.","They waited in an office. Every so often, zombies would pound on the door outside, making everyone tremble with fear.","Finally, after noon had passed, the sound of a car horn rang out across the campus. The noise attracted the zombies, and they rushed toward it.","Everyone looked out through the glass windows.","The car seemed to be alive. âBladesâ kept growing from its body, slicing through the zombiesâ heads.","There was also a monster as large as an elephant, biting through one zombie after another.","Everyone stared in stunned disbelief.","After observing for a long while, Wang Yunya said uncertainly, âThat looks like a cat.â","Everyone pressed up against the glass to get a better look. In the end, they confirmed it.","âYes, itâs a cat!â"]},{"number":131,"title":"Chapter 131: 0131","paragraphs":["When the people from the laboratory building left the cafeteria, the cafeteria auntie had stuffed two steamed buns into each of their hands.","At noon, each of them had eaten one bun and saved the other as a backup.","Now that rescue had arrived, they all had armor on and supernatural abilities at their disposal. They wolfed down the buns they had saved, then picked up their weapons: cleavers, rolling pins, and crowbars.","âLetâs go!â","During the previous disaster, Xiao Dan and her husband had fought zombies alongside the people from Youth Apartment. They had some experience with coordinated combat, so they had even worked out a battle plan: once the door opened, the first two people would use chairs to shove back any zombies trying to charge inside. Then everyone else would fight their way out.","Who could have guessed that when the plan was put into action and the door opened, just as the zombies were about to rush in, they would suddenly vanish right before everyoneâs eyes?","The group stood there, completely dumbfounded.","A few seconds later, a black cat as large as a leopard sauntered inside.","âA cat!â Wang Yunya couldnât help exclaiming softly.","âWhat a huge cat!â","âNo matter how big it is, itâs still not as big as the one just now.â","âWhy are there so many cats?â","âDid the entire cat squad mutate?â","Mo Li could adjust its body size to suit the situation. When facing a horde of zombies outdoors, a larger body provided greater impact force. But inside a building, such a huge body would be difficult to maneuver, so it had shrunk to the size of a leopard, making it more agile and adaptable.","Of course, the people in the office had no idea that the cat in front of them was the very same enormous black cat they had seen outside through the window, the one as big as an elephant.","They still thought these were several different cats.","Suddenly, their vision blurred. A gust of wind swept across their faces, and someone appeared beside the cat.","Xiao Dan cried out in delight, âBrother Zhou!â","It was Zhou Wang, the uncle who moved like the wind.","Wang Yunya was equally excited. âUncle Zhou!â","Zhou Wang said, âEveryone all right? Come on. If youâre fine, then follow me.â","He turned his head. âLizi, Lizi, lead the way!â","Unable to hold back her curiosity, Wang Yunya asked, âUncle Zhou, why are there so many powerful cats? There was an enormous one outside just now.â","She had never seen a cat that big in her life. It had been as huge as an elephant!","It looked like something straight out of a science-fiction movie.","âItâs just this one. Thereâs only one,â Zhou Wang said. âIt can grow bigger or smaller.â","Zhou Wang was filled with emotion.","Jiang Cheng was truly deep and unfathomable. Who knew what other trump cards she had hidden?","No wonder she hadnât panicked in the slightest when he warned her to beware of Cao Jiacai.","In fact, people like Zhou Wang and Song Jingshuo could both guess that Mo Li had not suddenly evolved today.","It might not even have evolved during this latest outbreak of the virus.","It was simply that Jiang Cheng had chosen today to reveal it.","She had kept this card hidden all along, only turning it over at the very end.","Zhou Wang said, âYouâve all seen it before. Itâs Jiang Chengâs cat from Youth Apartment.â","Xiao Dan and Wang Yunya looked incredulous. âThat one?â","Everyone in the neighborhoods nearby knew of Jiang Cheng from Youth Apartment.","The image of the little black cat that often perched on her shoulder was already deeply etched in peopleâs minds.","Who would have thought that little black cat could be so extraordinary?","Zhou Wang said, âIf I can become a human speedster, then itâs not that strange for a cat to grow bigger.â","Indeed, after the second outbreak of the zombie virus, many humans had gained supernatural abilities. As a result, people found it surprisingly easy to accept Mo Liâs mutation.","At this point, everyone was simply hoping that no animals would turn into zombies.","Wang Yunya herself possessed a fire-based ability, and there were several other ability users in the office as well, so accepting this was even easier for them.","Together, they headed outside.","The corridor was littered with zombie corpses. The zombies had vanished from sight just moments ago because Mo Li had pounced on them and bitten them to death.","Zhou Wang gave them a quick lesson as they walked. âThere are many different kinds of supernatural abilities. They can be classified by the five elementsâmetal, wood, water, fire, and earthâas well as special abilities. Iâm wind-based. I control air currents.â","âThat vehicle just now? It was operated from inside by several metal-type ability users. The idea came from Jiang Cheng, and itâs incredibly practical.â","âRight? You all saw it yourselves.â","Xiao Dan asked, âBrother Zhou, has the government sent any news?â","Zhou Wang sighed. âIâm afraid we canât count on the government this time.â","Xiao Danâs heart sank. After hesitating for a moment, she asked, âDid anyone from the residential compound come back later?â","She had left the compound and gone to the school to look for her daughter.","When she reached Preschool Street and saw that it was filled with mother zombies, she knew she couldnât force her way through. A small car was too easy for the second-generation zombies to pounce onto and cling to, making it extremely dangerous.","They had learned all this from the previous disaster.","Fortunately, she had reacted quickly. She immediately put the car into reverse, ignoring traffic laws, scrapes, and collisions, then turned around and fled.","She shook off the zombies on Preschool Street with her speed, then took a detour behind the stadium and circled around to the middle school.","She knew roughly what the situation in the compound was like. Before she left, Zhou Wang had been leading a dozen or so young, able-bodied men. Everyone else was elderly.","She herself could technically be counted among the young and able-bodied.","But she couldnât bring herself to abandon her daughter.","Some people had said, âGo.â","They understood her desperate desire to save her child.","Others had said, âDonât go.â","They believed going would only mean throwing her life away, and that abandoning the child in the compound would be safer.","But she had come anyway, ignoring everything else.","She couldnât get in touch with the childâs father. He had most likely died somewhere in the city. She had thought that if she was going to die, she might as well die together with her daughter.","Now it seemed that no one had to die after all.","But what about the future?","Zhou Wang counted on his fingers. âAs of this morning, six had come back, then seven, eight, nineâ¦ Hmm, nine in total.â","That few?","Xiao Danâs heart sank further and further.","Zhou Wang said, âThere are more people next doorâthe Youth Apartment. Over four hundred of them.â","Then he sighed again. âLook downstairs. Two hundred people have come to rescue you.â","Zhou Wang was always sighing. He really did have an astonishing number of things to sigh about.","Everyone stopped and looked outside through the corridor windows.","Several large buses had driven in. Countless people poured from them like a rising tide.","Some wore white plastic armor, while others wore silver metal armor. They looked like a futuristic combat teamâespecially impressive.","Everyone carried a weapon.","Many of the weapons looked the same, resembling the ancient weapons seen in television dramas. What were they called? Crescent-bladed shovels?","They looked extremely useful.","Xiao Danâs sinking heart finally steadied, and hope rose within her.","When the cafeteria doors opened again, many of the students burst into tears.","âWhere are Wang Yunya, Zhang Minghe, and Xu En?â","âIâm here! Iâm here!â Wang Yunya called from behind the adults as she entered. âWeâre all alive!â","The students cheered and rushed over to hug the group. They cried and laughed at the same time, pushing aside the adults who had come to rescue them.","The cafeteria auntie wiped away her tears as well.","Jiang Cheng walked inside and looked around. âA cafeteriaâ¦â","Song Jingshuo said, âPerfect.â","Li Jiangbing asked, ââ¦What are you talking about?â","Song Jingshuo replied, âAbout not leaving empty-handed.â","Jiang Cheng remained expressionless as she stepped on Song Jingshuoâs foot and walked away.","Song Jingshuo maintained his elegance and composure.","Jiang Cheng went straight to the wall, where a row of wheeled food carts stood. Each cart had four shelves, and each shelf held forty or fifty stainless-steel trays.","One by one, the carts vanished from in front of Jiang Cheng.","Song Jingshuo said to Li Jiangbing, âSee? Not leaving empty-handed.â","Li Jiangbing: ââ¦â","Li Jiangbing said, âHonestly, you were better beforeâ¦â","Back then, he had worn a dress shirt and tie, a luxury watch on his wrist, and an expression of kind benevolenceâfalse sincerity and all.","Li Jiangbing felt a pang of nostalgia.","But they could never go back. Never again.","âTake whatever you can.â","The Youth Apartments were going to start serving communal meals.","These stainless-steel trays could be taken back and used either as tableware for everyone or as raw materials for Metal-type superpowered individuals.","âTake the chopsticks too.â","âAnd the soup buckets.â","âThat huge iron pot looks great.â","âAnd that one-meter-twenty spatula.â","âTake it all, take it all!â","The survivors were stunned. âWhat is this?â","Zhou Wang said, âA Spatial-type superpower.â","The middle school students exclaimed, âThatâs so cool!â","Jiang Cheng kept taking things until the space inside her was so âfullâ that her head began to ache. Only then did she stop.","She looked over the students. There were a few parents among them, along with two middle-aged women.","Li Jiangbing put his hands on his hips. âNot a single teacher?â","The students lowered their heads dejectedly. âThe teachers told us to run to the cafeteria because there was food there, enough to last for many days. They stayed behind to cover our escape. Later, we closed the doors, but all we could hear was the zombies pounding on themâ¦â","During the first zombie outbreak, some people had literally starved to death.","There were no such deaths in the Youth Apartments or Auspicious Garden, but that didnât mean the same was true everywhere else.","Not every residential complex had been as lucky as those two and obtained supplies from the very beginning.","For many survivors, the memory of the first zombie outbreak wasnât âfear.â","It was âhunger.â","When everyone woke up and discovered that the zombie virus had returned, the teachers quickly made their decision.","âThe cafeteria has tall walls, sturdy doors, and food!â","The teachers chose the cafeteria as a shelter for the children.","They had made the right choice.","There were more than ninety middle school students in the cafeteria.","Everyone who attended High-Tech New District Middle School lived in the Technology New District.","What should they do next?","Jiang Cheng asked the students what they wanted.","âI want to go home.â","âMe too. Could you give me a knife? Weâre short on weapons.â","âSame here. Fighting with chairs is awful. We can only defend ourselves, not attack.â","When facing zombies, humans without weapons or armor would be at a severe disadvantage unless they had an overwhelming numerical advantage.","But with weaponsâand armorâthe situation was completely different.","The vast majority of the middle school students wanted to go home.","Even though they had already called and could no longer reach their parents, they still wanted to go home.","Their determination was unwavering.","A school had more than a thousand students, and Jiang Cheng didnât take all the stainless-steel trays. She left some behind because she still needed room to store other things.","Cui Haiyang, Uncle Eighty, and the other Metal-type superpowered individuals made armor and weapons out of the stainless-steel trays right there on the spot.","The students responded with repeated cries of âWow!â","Wu Jiancheng gave several Fire-type superpowered students an impromptu lesson on using a rolling pin as a track to accelerate fireballs, allowing them to attack from a distance.","Gao Yuxuan taught the only Lightning-type superpowered student one-on-one, explaining the difference between precision training and intensity training, as well as techniques for controlling lightning snakes and lightning nets.","Aunt Pan told the two Earth-type superpowered students, âYou canât have any distractions in your mind. You have to focus on it completely. Tell it what you want it to become. The fewer distractions you have, the more obediently it will follow your commands.â","In the end, everyone received armor and a weapon of their own.","The weapon of choice was the crescent shovel.","More and more people were discovering how useful crescent shovels were. Many had abandoned their original weapons, whatever they might have been, and switched to crescent shovels instead.","The adults said, âCome on. Weâll take you home.â"]},{"number":132,"title":"Chapter 132: 0132","paragraphs":["Getting from Gaoxin Middle School to the residential district didnât require retracing their steps. They only had to keep going and turn at the next corner.","But just as they continued forward and turned, someone called out, âJiang Cheng!â","There were more people on the return trip, so Jiang Cheng wasnât sitting in her seat. She stood at the front of the bus, looking over the passengers. When she heard someone call her, she turned toward the direction they were pointing and paused.","âKindergarten,â everyone murmured despite themselves.","Thatâs right. The Science and Technology New District had several private kindergartens, but only one public one: Gaoxin Kindergarten. Gaoxin Elementary School, Gaoxin Middle School, and the Gaoxin Central Sports Stadium were all clustered in this area.","Since they were already here, they might as well go.","The convoy stopped in front of the kindergarten. They first cleared out the zombies at the entrance, then prepared to get out and enter the building.","Everyone stood up, but Su Yu suddenly said, âIâ¦ Iâ¦â","Everyone turned to look at her.","A look of retreat appeared on Su Yuâs face.","Everyone knew that Su Yu was by no means timid, weak, lazy, or craftyâthe sort of person who refused to contribute and only wanted to enjoy the fruits of othersâ labor.","From the very first day of the zombie outbreak, Su Yu had participated in every operation. Even before she had any armor, she had bravely fought zombies with nothing but a frying pan. She was a reliable companion.","But now, she wanted to back down.","Su Yu said, âCan I stay hereâ¦?â","âItâs fine, itâs fine.â Li Jiangbing waved a large hand. âYou stay on the bus and look after the children.â","They needed someone to remain on the bus anyway. Besides, the buses were packed with little kids.","Su Yu nodded.","Everyone filed off the bus. Mo Li transformed into a leopard and darted into the kindergarten first.","No one thought Su Yu was wrong for staying behind.","As time passed and everyone became more familiar with one another, they gradually came to understand each otherâs true nature.","The true nature of Song Jingshuo, a refined and polished corporate elite, was that he had a vicious tongue.","Li Jiangbing looked frightening, as if he belonged to some criminal gang, but by now everyone knew that he actually had an exceptionally good temper. Whenever he strolled around the residential complex, the dogs all loved running up to him and wagging their tails.","Before this, everyone had assumed that Su Yu was a girl much like Jiang Cheng:","Brave, calm, and strong.","Now they knew that although Su Yu was capable of being brave, calm, and strong, she and Jiang Cheng were completely different kinds of people.","Jiang Chengâs heart was hardâso hard that no one knew just how hard it could be.","Su Yu was the exact opposite. The more they got to know her, the more they realized that, so long as she held to her principles and did nothing wrong, her heart was genuinely soft.","Someone had once asked Su Yu whether she was religious.","Su Yu had said no.","Why did people insist on tying inner gentleness to religion, as if that somehow gave religion all the credit?","Some people were simply born that way.","Li Jiangbing got off the bus and let out a sigh.","He knew that Su Yu had reached the limit of what she could bear today.","She had already faced the little children at the elementary school.","She couldnât face whatever might be waiting inside the kindergarten as well.","Zhao Yi had said that a personâs superpower was influenced by many factors, one of which was their innermost desires.","Brother Dong and Little Huang were typical examples. Although Zhao Yi hadnât used the two of them as examples in public, he and the others had privately told Li Jiangbing about it.","Li Jiangbing still couldnât understand why he had ended up with a water-based ability, but he could understand perfectly well why Su Yu possessed a protective barrier.","Some people wanted to run away.","Some were so frightened and anxious that they couldnât sleep at night.","Some wished they had the ability to protect others.","Su Yu stayed on the bus with the children.","One little girl asked, âAuntie, will the little brothers and sisters in the kindergarten turn into zombies?â","âI donât know either,â Su Yu said.","The little girl was tiny, yet she sighed like an adult and said, âI hope they donât.â","Su Yu pulled the little girl onto her lap and held her close.","Then a little boy shouted, âZombie!â","Su Yu looked outside.","Several zombies were approaching in the distance.","There had been many zombies on Preschool Street and outside the kindergarten. Over the past few days, they had gradually spread outward.","The group had just dealt with the ones in the street, but the zombies farther away had heard the commotion and were now coming over.","âItâs okay. Weâre safe inside the bus.â Su Yu gently patted the little girl in her arms.","She had barely finished speaking when a zombieâs face appeared at the window, climbing up the metal bars. The sight made the children scream in fear.","It was clearly a third-generation zombie.","Unlike second-generation zombies, third-generation zombies didnât charge recklessly into things or smash their heads against glass. Look at this oneâit knew how to grip the metal bars and climb. Its pitch-black eyes stared at Su Yu and the little girl inside, as if they were delicious meat.","The girl was terrified and trembled in Su Yuâs arms.","âDonât be afraid. Donât be afraid,â Su Yu said softly.","The children all saw white light spreading across Su Yuâs body.","The protective barrier unfolded, knocking the zombie away from the bus.","Go away.","Stay away from the children.","Su Yu held the little girl tightly and stared at the zombies outside.","Go away.","The child in her arms was so small. She was tinyâhardly bigger than a kitten or puppy.","Go away!","Deep down, Su Yu felt that she was far too weak.","She truly wanted a stronger ability, one that could protect more peopleâespecially children.","She lowered her head and kissed the little girlâs crown.","It was greasy and smelly, but that didnât matter. Once they got back, Auntie would give her a nice bath.","Donât be afraid. Auntieâs here.","White light radiated from Su Yu once again.","The people in the bus behind them saw a zombie climbing onto the bus ahead. They had just gotten off and were preparing to deal with it when they saw the protective barrier surrounding the bus suddenly flare with white light and expand in an instant.","The third-generation zombie that had just been knocked away had only just gotten back up when it was pushed away again.","This time, the expanding barrier forced it against the kindergartenâs outer fence, pinning it there.","The zombie struggled and let out a furious howl.","The people behind them stared in shock.","âHoly crap?â","âWas that Su Yu?â","That white protective barrier could only belong to Su Yu.","The kindergarten was cleared out very quickly.","When Jiang Cheng and the others came back outside, they were astonished to see the white barrier surrounding the large bus.","The people who had stayed behind got off and killed the scattered zombies that wandered over. They were smoking and chatting beside the bus.","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan went over and asked, âHow long has Su Yuâs barrier been up?â","âIt started as soon as you went inside.â","âWas it this big from the beginning?â","âIt covered the bus at first, then suddenly expanded like it had exploded.â","âHoly crap. A burst breakthrough?â","The protective barrier retracted. Clearly, Su Yu had seen them return.","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan immediately started toward Su Yu, eager to interview her, but Li Jiangbing grabbed one with each hand and hauled them back.","âCan you two read the situation? At least consider how sheâs feeling.â","The two men had been excited in the moment. Now that they had come back to their senses, they could only smile sheepishly.","âSorry, sorry.â","The driver opened the doors, and everyone got back onto the bus.","Su Yu looked toward Li Jiangbing.","Li Jiangbing looked away and only said to the driver, âLetâs go, letâs go. Iâm starving.â","Thank goodness they hadnât made Su Yu go inside.","Mo Li came back too. After transforming into a small cat, she chose one childâs lap and curled up there.","The child was overwhelmed with delight and carefully stroked her fur.","If they asked Zhou Wang to search a building, he might be fast, but he could still overlook survivors hiding somewhere.","Mo Li, however, couldnât. She could sense both living beings and zombies.","Su Yu looked once more at the kindergarten outside. From Li Jiangbingâs deliberate change of subject, she understood.","There wasnât a single survivor.","Li Jiangbing secretly glanced at Su Yu.","He knew she was sad.","That was simply the kind of person she was.","The way Su Yu held the little girl stirred an indescribable feeling in Li Jiangbing.","He wanted to look a little longer, but he didnât dare.","The various residential developments in the new district were all fairly close to one another.","The public elementary and middle schools followed the principle of enrolling students at the school nearest to where they lived.","The convoy dropped the middle school students off at their own residential communities. The boys and girls, dressed in gleaming armor and carrying their newly acquired weapons, said goodbye to their benefactors.","âGoodbye!â","Little Huang watched them.","They were all around the same age.","Little Huang understood better than anyone that even if the house was empty and his parents were gone, he still had to go back and take a look.","He understood that better than anyone.","The thirty-odd middle school students returning with the convoy were all from Auspicious Garden and Imperial View Garden.","After getting out of the vehicles, some were reunited with their grandparents and clung to each other, sobbing. Others couldnât find their relatives.","Not every mother who rushed out had been as quick to reactâor as luckyâas Xiao Dan.","Several had gone out and never returned.","Besides the middle school students returning home, the convoy also brought back a dozen little children and two cafeteria aunties.","One was Auntie Ma, and the other was Auntie Jiang.","Neither of them had anywhere to go, so Jiang Cheng asked them to come back with the group.","Everyone had eaten a little before setting out to stave off their hunger and planned to have a proper meal after returning.","Jiang Cheng had called the residential community along the way to report the number of extra people they were bringing back.","By the time they returned, the few people who had been recruited had already prepared the first meal.","Jiang Cheng brought out the cafeteria trays and chopsticks. Everyone was ravenous. There werenât enough chairs in the coffee shop, so each person carried a metal tray and squatted on the ground to eat.","The chairs were left for the little children.","Auntie Ma and Auntie Jiang took a look around the kitchen. When they came out, they went to find Jiang Cheng.","âWe can do this job too.â","They had both worked in a middle school cafeteria and were more professional.","Jiang Cheng agreed. âWeâll give you a room to share.â","The first communal meal was a great success. Everyone gave it positive feedback.","It looked like the arrangement could be expanded. The largest group in the community consisted of single young people who didnât want to cook. People who genuinely enjoyed cooking, like Su Yu and Song Jingshuo, were in the minority.","Most people didnât want to spend an hour cooking, five minutes eating, and another half hour washing dishes and scrubbing pots.","It simply wasnât worth it.","Among the little children, seven were girls and five were boys. They ranged in age from six to eight.","Every child could recite their parentsâ phone numbers.","But no one could get through.","The only father they managed to reach said, âI might not make it back alive. Please, Iâm begging you to take care of her.â","He wanted to speak with his daughter.","No one knew what he said to her. All they heard was the little girl repeatedly answering, âMm-hmm,â âOh,â and âOkay.â","She was very well-behaved.","After hanging up, the little girl said, âDaddy told me to listen and behave.â","The little girl was no longer afraid.","The residential community gave off a sense of safety. Everyone was living as they had before, as if there were no zombies.","And there were so many adults around.","Children instinctively trusted the adults who had rescued them, like fledglings trusting their parents.","But to the people in the Youth Apartments, more than a dozen children were a burden that had suddenly landed in their laps.","Li Jiangbing scratched his head. âWell, this is quite a mess. What are we supposed to do?â","There was only one option: keep them.","After discussing it, everyone chose three apartments on the same floor as Su Yu, all adjacent to hers.","One of the apartments already had a girl living in it, so she was moved to another one.","Aunt Pan knocked through the walls between the three apartments. Only the entrance to the middle apartment was left; the entrances to the other two were sealed.","This was where Jiang Chengâs storage space proved especially convenient. The beds and other furniture were moved out of the middle apartment, and two sets of sofas were brought in to create a shared activity room.","The two side apartments were filled with beds, lined up one after another. The girls would live in one, and the boys in the other.","The girls were put in charge of caring for the children, rather than the men.","This wasnât based on the stereotypical idea that women should do certain things and men others. It was Su Yu who had proposed the arrangement.","She said, âThe children are too young. They canât tell right from wrong, and they have no ability to resist. It wouldnât be safe to leave them with men.â","The girls all agreed, and so did Jiang Cheng.","The Youth Apartments gained fourteen residents today:","Two cafeteria aunties.","Twelve little children.","It lost eight residents:","Cao Jiacai, deceased.","Three security guards and two cleaners had been fired and left.","Wang Haotian and his companions had left of their own accord. No one stopped them.","The current population was 417.","Among them were twenty-six people with supernatural abilities.","It was September 1, the fourth day since the second outbreak of the zombie virus.","The government had still given no sign of life on television.","Information online was scarce and scattered.","The Youth Apartments now faced a shortage of vegetables.","The greens brought back from Buy More had lasted three days. There werenât many left, and they were no longer fresh.","Now that communal meals had begun, everyone had been reporting the problem.","Jiang Cheng found the only wood-element ability user in the entire community.","âYou can put everything else aside for now.â","âFocus on growing vegetables.â","âWeâre all counting on you.â","Li Jiangbing was afraid heâd get smacked if he laughed in Jiang Chengâs face, so he ran off laughing.","A group of people in the community gathered around to watch Mo Li basking in the sun.","One child asked, âCan we pet him?â","Another child said, âSure. He fell asleep on my lap in the car. Go ahead and pet him. He doesnât bite.â","âRight. Weâre not zombies, after all.â"]},{"number":133,"title":"Chapter 133: 0133","paragraphs":["Any project needed a feasibility study and proper evaluation before it could be launched. It wasnât something they could just decide to do on a whim.","Song Jingshuo had already picked out a patch of lawn in the courtyard. He had also asked Aunt Pan to assess the fertility of the soil.","She said it would do.","Since Aunt Pan and Zhao Yizhong had both taken part in the rescue operation that afternoon, Song Jingshuo grabbed a soil-type ability user who had been assigned to stay behind in the complex and had him turn over the ground.","The soil rolled and churned, pushing the grass up by the roots.","Manager Wang was nothing if not diligent. He arrived carrying the property management officeâs enormous rake and hauled away all the grass, leaving nothing but soil behind.","Song Jingshuo moved over all the seedlings he had been growing in water. With the sun still above the horizon, he planted a small vegetable plot.","It was small only by comparisonâit was actually quite large. To activate his ability over all the seedlings at once, Song Jingshuo had to stand in the middle of the plot and slowly spread his arms.","Like God bestowing a blessing.","âGod of Agriculture,â Gao Yuxuan said.","Li Jiangbing saw Song Jingshuoâs cheeks clench and warp with irritation. He lowered his voice and said, âShut up. Heâs going to throw his shoe at you in a minute.â","Gao Yuxuan knew Song Jingshuo would never do something so undignified, and so he continued provoking him without fear.","âAt least heâs serving the people,â Li Jiangbing said. âGive it a rest.â","Fine. Gao Yuxuan grinned and toned it down a little.","Song Jingshuo couldnât be bothered with these idiots. He focused his mind and calmed his breathing.","It was an incredible feeling. He could sense the vitality of the plants. It was also wonderful to urge them to grow with his own hands.","Song Jingshuo didnât know what using supernatural abilities felt like for other people, but he rather liked the sensation that came with using his own.","It gave him the feeling of leaving the city behind and returning to nature.","In the past, the only way he could find that feeling was by taking annual leave, driving his big off-road vehicle, and traveling all the way to the mountains, grasslands, or forests.","Li Jiangbing and Gao Yuxuan squatted beside the vegetable plot and watched with their own eyes as the hydroponic seedlings took root and grew, like a time-lapse sequence in a documentary.","In less than ten minutes, the small vegetable plot had turned into a lush sea of green.","âThat big?â Gao Yuxuan exclaimed in shock.","Song Jingshuo gave him a cool glance. âWith this many people eating, we either increase the number of plants or increase the yield of each individual plant.â","Increasing the number of plants would require expanding the growing area. If the area exceeded the range of his ability, he would have to work in separate sections and batches.","In reality, though, when he stimulated the plants, he could sense the limit of how much they could grow. Relying on the plants alone, it would be difficult to break through that limit.","But when he tried using his ability to support them, they really did break past it.","Many people came over to watch. When they saw how huge the vegetables had grown, they all let out amazed exclamations.","âWow!â","The cafeteria aunties arrived pulling a flatbed cart from the property management office.","âTime to harvest! Come on, time to harvest!â","Everyone pitched in, and before long, the entire vegetable plot had been picked clean.","This time, Song Jingshuo had planted three different kinds of vegetables, which meant they could have three dishes for dinner.","In the future, the cafeteria head chef would decide on a weekly menu, and Song Jingshuo would grow the vegetables according to the menu each day. That way, everyone could eat the freshest produce every day.","This outbreak of the zombie virus had left the complex with far fewer survivors than the previous one, and the government still hadnât sent any word.","Yet everyone actually felt more secure than before.","This time, they didnât have to sit around anxiously waiting for the country to send supplies, worrying that the supplies might never reach them.","This time, they could find ways to provide their own food and water.","So what was there left to fear?","The scene looked almost like an old-fashioned farm from decades ago, with everyone working together in high spirits.","They transported the vegetables to the clubhouse.","The complex officially began taking names for those who wanted to sign up for communal meals.","It solved one of everyoneâs biggest problems, and many people lined up to register.","For the time being, no one needed to contribute grain. The food they were using had been transported over by Mai Duoduoâs forklift.","Jiang Cheng also opened the blast-proof door to the basement and moved out all the supplies they had previously received from the government.","If grain was stored for too long, it would become old grain. They might as well take it out and eat it first.","Jiang Cheng had always been the leader of the complex, so everyone naturally felt that it was perfectly normal for her to handle this matter.","Only Song Jingshuo, whose eye missed nothing, asked her when they were alone, âWhen did you get the key?â","Jiang Cheng smiled faintly. âThe first day.â","Song Jingshuo knew it.","That woman was always one step ahead. On the very first day, when everyone had only just woken up and many people hadnât even awakened their abilities yet, she had already thought to get hold of the key to the basementâs blast-proof door. In other words, she had secured the grain stored down there.","Well, fine. With a leader like that, at least he could take things easy.","The little ones had already taken baths.","The elderly women from Auspicious Home knew one another well. They went to the homes of families with children and rummaged around, finding lots of clothes and bringing them over.","The little ones changed into clean clothes.","Then they went with the young women to the clubhouse for dinner.","With all the cooking utensils Jiang Cheng had brought back from the Gaoxin Middle School cafeteria, the head chef and the aunties were as powerful as tigers with wings.","The cafeteria aunties clearly had plenty of experience controlling portions. Only a small amount of food was left after dinner, which was a perfectly normal remainder.","There were now seven people working in the cafeteria. The uncle was the head chef, Auntie Ma and Auntie Jiang handled portion control, and everyone else assisted.","The two of them were supposedly especially good at making foods from dough, too.","That evening, after the head chef and the others had âclocked offâ and returned to Auspicious Home, the two aunties living in the youth apartment began preparing dough again.","âWeâre having youtiao tomorrow morning,â they announced.","They also made a request to the handsome man who grew their vegetables. âIf you can grow them, plant some beans, too. We can sprout them into bean sprouts and make soy milk.â","Mai Duoduo naturally had beans in stock. But there was no need to buy any. Someone immediately contributed an entire bag from their own home.","âI make soy milk every day. I have plenty of bags of beans at home.â","Song Jingshuo silently accepted the beans and took them home to soak. Once they had been soaked, he could stimulate their growth with far less expenditure of his ability.","The simple announcement that they would be having youtiao the next morning gave many people in the youth apartment sweet dreams that night. In their dreams, they had everything they could wish for.","On the morning of September 2, they woke up and rubbed their eyes, only to remember that there was another zombie outbreak going on. Reality wasnât nearly as wonderful as their dreams.","Butâ¦ it wasnât so bad, was it? They had reliable neighbors, and everyone was doing their part.","It wasnât so bad.","No one slept in that morning. There was already a long line at the clubhouse early in the morning to collect youtiao.","Even the little ones were waiting in line.","Someone near the front laughed and said, âTheyâre lining up too? Just let them go to the front.â","Su Yu waved her hand. âThey need to learn. Children donât suddenly understand rules on their own. They have to be taught.â","The best way to learn was to participate in the rules firsthand.","Zhou Wang brought Little Huang over to mooch breakfast.","The two of them were powerful ability users, and they had also taken part in every group operation organized by the youth apartment, contributing a great deal.","They had killed far more zombies than ordinary people.","So no one felt that they shouldnât be allowed to eat a free breakfast simply because they werenât residents of the youth apartment.","Jiang Cheng even said, âWhy donât you two join us from now on?â","âNo need. We already have people we share meals with,â Zhou Wang replied. âWe only came to mooch a meal because we heard there was going to be a meeting later.â","The youth apartment was holding another general meeting today.","Jiang Cheng had already called Zhou Wang the night before to notify him about the meeting.","Zhou Wang: ââ¦â¦â","It gave him the distinct feeling of a suzerain state summoning its vassal.","So Zhou Wang brought Little Huang along first thing in the morning.","Jiang Cheng asked about the food situation for the people in Auspicious Garden.","Zhou Wang said, âNobodyâs short on food. Everyone went and bought another round of supplies on Pinduoduo.â","There were now eighty or ninety elderly people living in Auspicious Garden. Apart from them, there were about thirty other residents who could all be considered young.","Among them, more than ten were middle school studentsâthe ones they had rescued from Gaoxin Middle School yesterday.","âThey were all crying their eyes out,â Zhou Wang sighed. âThen we held a meeting too and paired off the middle schoolers who no longer had parents with different families. They can look after each other.â","The people of Auspicious Garden formed household partnerships.","The elderly had spent their whole lives cooking and were more comfortable preparing meals in their own homes. Some of the old folks who were especially good at cooking volunteered to team up with younger people. The arrangement was that if any physically demanding work came up, the younger person had to help.","Everyone got what they needed.","The fried dough sticks were delicious.","Seriously delicious.","They heard that Song Jingshuo was already preparing to plant soybeans, and many people were asking when they would finally be able to drink some soy milk.","Song Jingshuo said, âWhere would we even get a soy milk maker?â","He was planning to grow soybeans because they were rich in protein. Song Jingshuo was already considering replacing meat with plant protein if meat became scarce in the future.","He hadnât been thinking about soy milk. A small household soy milk maker would never be able to handle enough for this many people.","But just as he finished speaking, Auntie Ma said, âWe have one! We found it yesterday!â","The owner of the clubhouse had previously run a restaurant and hadnât been willing to throw away any of the equipment. It had all been stored in the back kitchen. There really was a professional commercial machine sitting in the storage room.","Li Jiangbing hadnât seen it when he was clearing out and cleaning the kitchen. But after the cooks and aunties took over, they found it.","That was why the aunties had told Song Jingshuo to plant soybeans.","All right. Song Jingshuo agreed. âWeâll give it a try today.â","They held the general meeting in the morning.","Following their usual custom, everyone sat in a group on the ground.","The people from Auspicious Garden gradually arrived as well. Some residents from Yujing Xiang Garden even came over.","Gao Yuxuan showed up with his hair standing on end like an explosion. His face was black, and his fingernails were black too.","He looked as though heâd been struck by lightning.","Song Jingshuo was stunned. âWhat happened?â","Gao Yuxuan had an electrical superpower, after all.","Zhao Yi said, âYou actually tried it?â","Gao Yuxuan: âYeah.â","Zhao Yi flew into a rage. âYou tried it without calling me? You didnât let me observe it?â","Gao Yuxuan: âYeah.â","Zhao Yi grew even angrier. âSpeak like a normal person.â","Gao Yuxuan had no choice but to open his mouth and say, âI was worried youâd be in danger, so I only called Brother Guo.â","As he uttered that short sentence, sparks of electricity crackled from his mouth."]},{"number":134,"title":"Chapter 134: 0134","paragraphs":["Yesterday, Su Yuâs protective barrier suddenly underwent an explosive breakthrough.","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan spent a long time afterward trying to figure it out.","Su Yuâs ability had been classified as a form of mental power, and it was clearly heavily influenced by her inner desiresâin fact, one could say extremely so.","The tiny zombies at Gaoxin Elementary School had dealt a tremendous blow to peopleâs minds.","Li Jiangbing had sighed every time he shoveled away one of those little heads.","Su Yu had obviously been under immense mental pressure. So much so that she hadnât gone to the kindergarten afterward.","Then they remembered that she was majoring in education.","She was someone who ought to devote herself to teaching, not to slaughtering zombie elementary schoolers.","Actually, Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan had wondered whether the girl had been on the verge of a mental breakdown at the time. But after getting into the vehicle, they had secretly observed her and decided that she didnât seem like it.","All the way there, Su Yu had held a little girl in her arms. Her features looked both gentle and resolute.","If she really had broken down, then she had already completed the reconstruction of her inner self.","By the looks of it, both her superpower and her mind were incredibly strong.","Her thoughts had taken form, becoming a protective barrier.","This opened up a whole new line of thought for Zhao Yi and the others.","If a mental-power user could achieve a breakthrough in their superpower by shattering and reconstructing their mind, then what about other superpower users?","They thought about it for a long time, but it was difficult.","Zhao Yi said, âI canât exactly eat dirt, can I?â","Nor could he bury himself in dirt.","Still, Zhao Yi couldnât eat dirtâbut Gao Yuxuan could touch an electrical contact.","And not just an ordinary one, either. The 220 volts in peopleâs homes didnât amount to much for him. He still hadnât reached that level yet, but Guo Jun already had.","Gao Yuxuan felt that he needed to give himself a sufficiently powerful shock.","He decided to touch a high-voltage line.","But he didnât dare tell Zhao Yi. Zhao Yi had said that if he was ever going to touch an electrical contact, he absolutely had to call him.","Zhao Yi definitely wanted to observe from close range.","But Gao Yuxuan was afraid something might go wrong.","High voltage was no joke.","As an electrical superpower user, he was confident that high voltage couldnât kill him.","But Zhao Yi was another matter.","So he didnât dare tell Zhao Yi.","Instead, he secretly called Guo Jun.","Guo Jun thought it sounded interesting. After all, Gao Yuxuan would be the one touching the electrical contact, not him. There was no harm in giving it a try.","The two men sneaked out in the dead of night.","âGood thing you didnât come,â Gao Yuxuan said. âThe high-voltage arc was strong enough to break through the air. If youâd been there, youâd have died for sure.â","âOnly Brother Jun could take it.â","Zhao Yi: â...Brother Jun?â","Gao Yuxuan: âBrother Jun saved my sorry ass.â","Naturally, they had prepared some equipment, such as insulated poles.","But neither of them had expected the arc to be that powerful.","Gao Yuxuan had gotten stuck to it. His entire body had crackled and flashed, and he felt as if he were about to be burned to a crisp.","The arc had broken through the air. Only Guo Jun could withstand it. If Zhao Yi had been there, he would have died on the spot.","Guo Jun used an insulated pole to knock Gao Yuxuanâs hand loose, saving his life.","Gao Yuxuan was still shaken. âTen kilovolts is still too high for me. I overestimated myself a little.â","For an ordinary person, ten kilovolts would have turned them into charcoal in an instant. Fortunately, he was an electrical superpower user. All he had suffered was singed hair and blackened fingernails.","Zhao Yi said, âLetâs interview you about the experience.â","âPure terror. Nothing but terror,â Gao Yuxuan said. âSo no matter what youâre doing, you need a teammate covering your flank. You never know when they might have to save your sorry ass.â","Zhao Yi said, âI want to know what it feels like to have high-voltage current pass through your body.â","âWell...â Gao Yuxuan pondered. âHow should I put it? I was dazed and seemed to see my great-grandfather and great-grandmother. Or maybe I experienced a kind of freedom, soaring through the sky...â","Song Jingshuo said blandly, âIn heaven, you mean.â","Gao Yuxuan: â...Thatâs not entirely wrong, I suppose.â","He continued, âBut the moment the power was cut, it all went downhill. Damn, you have no idea how hot and stuffy that little room in the substation was. We couldnât move, so we just lay there...â","âHold on.â Song Jingshuo was always good at noticing details that other people overlooked. âThe substation?â","Gao Yuxuan: â...Yeah!â","Song Jingshuo said, âOur residential compoundâs substation?â","Gao Yuxuan, his hair standing up in an afro, said, âYeah!â","Zhao Yi didnât believe him. âI turned on the TV when I got up this morning to see whether there had been any announcements. The electricity at home was working fine.â","âThatâs why I went to touch the electrical contact in the middle of the night,â Gao Yuxuan said. âIâm not an idiot. If weâd cut the power during the day, it would have caused everyone a lot of trouble.â","The power outage in the middle of the night had gone unnoticed.","After the two electrical superpower users had lain on the ground and panted until they recovered, they began repairing the damage.","Their main goal was to avoid affecting anyone else.","âThe substation had a complete stock of spare parts, and everything was organized logically and clearly,â Gao Yuxuan said admiringly. âMaster Luoâs work ethic is truly meticulous.â","Master Luoâs only disadvantage was his lack of education. If he had gone to college, he absolutely would have become an outstanding engineer.","Gao Yuxuan continued, âWe replaced the high-voltage disconnect switch. Then I saw that there were still enough spare parts. I figured that ten kilovolts was too much for me, but it might not be too much for Brother Jun. So I suggested that he give it a try too.â","Gao Yuxuan smacked his lips in regret. âBrother Jun was too cautious. He refused to try.â","Zhao Yi and Song Jingshuo: â...â","Anyone who saw Gao Yuxuanâs current state wouldnât want to try it again either.","Guo Jun was currently the strongest electrical superpower user in the two residential compounds.","He had also broken through at Gaoxin Elementary School the previous day and could now directly blast a zombieâs head apart.","As long as he wasnât surrounded by zombies on all sides, he could basically fight a number of them alone while wearing armor and emerge unscathed.","He had no particularly urgent desire or ambition to become stronger.","In fact, Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan werenât pursuing âstrengthâ either.","Their real pleasure didnât come from becoming stronger. It came from studying superpowers themselves.","There was endless fun to be found in it.","As Gao Yuxuan talked, electricity crackled continuously in his mouth.","When he became excited and started speaking too quickly, two tiny streams of electricity even shot out of his ears.","At least he was still alive, and he didnât seem to be suffering any serious problems.","Zhao Yi focused on the results of the experiment. âHow do you feel? Did it work?â","The moment the subject came up, Gao Yuxuan became smug.","He raised his index finger. A small ball of electricity hovered above its tip, fine currents constantly flickering across its surface.","Zhao Yi and Song Jingshuo immediately noticed the difference.","âBlue?â","The core of the little electric ball was white, but its outer layer seemed to be wrapped in a blue membrane. The tiny currents that flickered continuously were blue as well.","Guo Junâs electricity had been blue from the very beginning. Gao Yuxuanâs current, however, had always been white.","Now the blue in Gao Yuxuanâs electricity was unmistakable.","Zhao Yi was both delighted and amazed. âIt really worked.â","âActually, if Brother Jun had taken a little longer to pull me off,â Gao Yuxuan said, âI think I could have gotten even stronger.â","For once in his life, he had experienced what it felt like to be a battery being charged.","That much powerful energy had surged into his body, racing through his blood vessels.","The source of his superpower deep within his brainâor, more precisely, his superpowerâs energy poolâhad been forcibly expanded. The pathways through which energy traveled in his body had been forcibly widened as well.","The electrical current he could unleash was now far stronger than before.","Gao Yuxuan himself felt that he should now be on par with Guo Jun: a single electrical strike ought to be enough to blast open a zombieâs skull.","Song Jingshuo said coldly, âWhy couldnât it just kill you outright?â","Gao Yuxuan was brimming with confidence. âIâm not going to die. I believe in fate. Heaven gave me an electricity-based superpower, so thereâs no way I can die from an electric shock.â","Gao Yuxuan would never admit that, at the time, he had genuinely thought he was a goner.","That blow from Guo Jun, knocking his hand away from the live electrical panel, had truly saved his life.","Zhang Lesi came over, surprised. âThatâs a pretty cool new look. Why are you still carrying an electric current?â","Gao Yuxuan spoke with such animation that, once he got worked up, he couldnât stop the tiny sparks from occasionally flickering across his body.","It did look cool.","Zhang Lesi suddenly reached out and poked him with her fingertip.","Zhao Yi cried out and reached for her hand!","He managed to grab it, but Zhang Lesiâs fingertip had already touched Gao Yuxuanâs shoulder.","Song Jingshuo then watched the two of them jerk together as if they were touching a live electrical panel.","No, not âas if.â They were touching a live electrical panel.","Gao Yuxuan quickly took a step back and pulled Zhang Lesiâs hand away.","âSorry, sorry. Iâm still having a little trouble containing the leakage.â","Zhao Yi hurriedly let go as well.","The current shot through his finger. It felt like an electric drill boring into it. The jolt was brief, but it still hurt.","Zhang Lesi shook her hand and grimaced. âCan you control it or not? If you canât keep it contained, sit farther away from us later, okay?â","Gao Yuxuan apologized profusely.","Zhang Lesi quickly found Su Yu, who was sitting on the ground but kept craning her neck to look into the distance.","Far away, the little ones were playing.","Someone had found them a ball, and a group of children were kicking it around.","Zhang Lesi tossed a magazine onto the ground, sat down beside Su Yu, and glanced over as well. âIs everything all right?â","Su Yu said, âJiang Cheng said heâs fine, and that Mo Li would keep an eye on him.â","Mo Li was practically a celebrity now. Whenever he strutted around the neighborhood with his tail held high, patrolling his territory, everyone made way for him.","When Jiang Cheng told him to spit out what he had swallowed from Cao Jiacai, he turned around and spat it out.","When Jiang Cheng raised a hand, he would shrink down and leap onto Jiang Chengâs shoulder.","Clearly, he had developed intelligenceâor at least something very close to it.","Zhang Lesi said, âIf Jiang Cheng says itâs fine, then itâs fine.â","Su Yu felt the same way. âI know. I just canât stop myself from looking.â","The children were too young and needed supervision. The female residents had decided that one person would sleep in the childrenâs dormitory with them every night, just in case something happened.","They took turns.","Su Yu had been the first one on duty the night before.","In the middle of the night, she discovered that several of the children were secretly crying.","âWeâve already posted notices on the neighborhood forums where they live, asking people to help locate them,â Su Yu said.","The children came from several different neighborhoods.","Their parents couldnât be reached, so Su Yu had posted missing-person notices on each neighborhoodâs forum. She included the childrenâs names, their parentsâ names, and their phone numbers.","If their parents were still alive but had merely lost their phones in the chaos, perhaps they would see the posts and find their way here.","Su Yu sighed. âThereâs so little information online this timeâ¦â","The internet had always been a tool used by only a portion of the population.","During the previous zombie outbreak, many people had been at home. This time, however, countless people were stranded outside and unable to return. To get online, they first had to find a computer with internet access.","The amount of available information had dropped drastically.","Most of it consisted of pleas for help:","âMy name is xxx. Iâm trapped in xxx Tower. Please, can someone come rescue us?â","Things like that.","The subject put a damper on their moods, and it wasnât something they could solve anyway.","The two of them decided to change the subject.","Zhang Lesi said, âDonât you think Zhao Yi is kind of handsome?â","Su Yu: ââ¦â","Su Yu turned to look at her.","Zhang Lesi asked, âYou donât?â","Su Yu thought about it. âHeâsâ¦ all right, I guess?â","âNo,â Su Yu said. âWeâve known him for so long. What made you suddenly decide heâs handsome?â","Ever since the first zombie disaster, Zhao Yi had been a well-known figure in the neighborhood. He was also widely recognized as one of its heroes, having made an indelible contribution to keeping the neighborhoodâs environment in order.","Zhang Lesi grinned. âI used to think he was just the quiet type who worked his head off. Thatâs not my type. But after hearing him talk about his superpower the other day, I realized he was actually pretty articulate. And heâs funny, tooânot the bookish nerd Iâd assumed he was.â","Su Yu said, âThereâs no way he could be a bookworm if he hangs around with Gao Yuxuan.â","Zhang Lesi asked, âYou donât think heâs handsome?â","Su Yu said, âHeâs all right.â","Zhang Lesi pressed her. âThen who do you think is handsome?â","Su Yu paused."]},{"number":135,"title":"Chapter 135: 0135","paragraphs":["The moment she saw that, she knew there was someone Su Yu thought was âhandsome.â","âWho is it? Who?â Zhang Lesi asked.","Su Yu avoided her gaze. âNobody. They all look the same, more or less.â","As if anyone would believe that.","Zhang Lesi thought for a moment, then her expression changed. âIt couldnât be Old Song, could it?â","âDonât even think about it.â Zhang Lesi tried her best to dissuade her. âMy cousin works in finance, and he warned me a long time ago: never date men from finance, advertising, or civil engineering. Each industry has its own special brand of awful.â","Su Yu immediately denied it. âDonât be ridiculous. I just think theyâre all more or less the same.â","Even if they could be friends, everyone still had a different personality.","Zhang Lesi was bold and outspoken. If she liked someone, she dared to pursue him.","Su Yu, on the other hand, clearly came from a more conservative family. She was the kind of girl who had to wait for the guy to pursue her.","Grinning mischievously, Zhang Lesi decided not to press her any further.","Meanwhile, Gao Yuxuan genuinely didnât dare sit too close to everyone else. He still couldnât fully control the energy in his body, and electricity leaked out every now and then.","Naturally, Zhao Yi stayed with him.","Gao Yuxuan was a little worried about Zhao Yi. âWhy is your face so red? You werenât shocked in the heart just now, were you?â","âItâs the autumn heat,â Zhao Yi said.","Gao Yuxuan looked up at the sky. âIs it? It doesnât seem that hot yet. Itâll be hot at noon.â","He was still concerned. âHow about we go find Zhang Lesi and have her take a look at you? Electric shocks count as external injuries. She can treat those.â","Zhao Yi waved him off. âI told you, itâs hot. Iâm hot.â","Why was his face getting even redder?","Huh?","Something wasnât right.","Gao Yuxuan stared at Zhao Yi.","Zhao Yi turned his head away.","The children were playing with a ball.","âMo Li, Mo Li!â","They called Mo Liâs name as they kicked the ball toward him.","Mo Li looked as though he was lazily lying on the ground, basking in the sunlight, but whenever the ball flew over, he would smack it back with his tail.","The children burst into laughter.","Suddenly, they all fell silent.","Over where the adults had gathered, the auntie had picked up a megaphone and begun to speak.","All the children knew her. She was Mo Liâs owner.","âAll right, everyoneâs more or less here.â Jiang Cheng raised the megaphone. âLetâs begin.â","Manager Wang had found her a red plastic stool from the property management office. Sitting on it, she was slightly higher than everyone seated on the ground.","The small plaza fell silent.","Jiang Cheng began to speak.","âThis time, things are much better than they were last time. Much better in every respect. I wonât go on about that.â","âThereâs only one topic for todayâs meeting: What do we do from here?â","âToday isâ¦â Jiang Cheng said. âSeptember 2. This wave of the virus has been spreading for five days now.â","âI came downstairs a little late because I couldnât give up. I watched the television for a while.â","âBut unfortunately, there was nothing. Nothing.â","A great many sighs rose at once.","The provisional government that had gritted its teeth, refused to give up, and led everyone to victory over the zombies last time had not appeared this time.","Not even a word.","âCompared with last time, when did the government start responding?â","âI remember very clearly. It was Sunday morning, after we had just cleared the zombies out of the courtyard. It was around ten, not yet eleven.â","âTwelveâno, thirteen hours.â","âLast time, when the zombie virus broke out, the government responded in just thirteen hours, despite having no experience dealing with it at all. It issued its first announcement to the public.â","âAlthough that announcement contained nothing of substance, at least it showed that the government had organized people to seize control of the television station.â","âToday is already the fifth day, and the television is still showing nothing but prerecorded programs. I heard that if no one manually stops them, those programs will just keep playing on a loop?â","âIn other words, by the fifth day, the government hasnât even managed to take the television station.â","âOr perhaps no one has organized people to seize it in the first place.â","Jiang Cheng paused and scanned the crowd.","The mood grew despondent. No one spoke.","Jiang Cheng raised the megaphone again.","âAll right, I wonât waste time on that. Iâll get straight to the conclusionââ","âIâ¦â","âI believe that, in reality, we no longer have a government.â","âRaise your hand if you agree with me.â","Every hand went up.","Even the new members of the Youth Apartments, Auntie Ma and Auntie Jiang, raised their hands.","The only ones who didnât were some of the elderly residents who had come from Auspicious Home Garden.","Uncle Eighty was among them.","Tears filled his eyes. âHow can there be no government? How can there be no governmentâ¦â","He kept murmuring, his lips trembling.","It was obvious that the fact that there was no government had dealt him a devastating blow.","The elderly had spent their entire lives following the government. They had watched the country flourish and prosper, only for such an excellent government to suddenly disappear.","Who could accept that?","âThis time is different. We have superpowers, and we can grow our own food.â","âOnce we find all kinds of seeds, we can grow whatever we want and eat whatever we grow.â","âLetâs think about where we can get some chickens, ducks, and geese to raise. Even pigs, cattle, and sheep. If we raise them ourselves, weâll have meat to eat.â","âThese things used to be difficult for us, but now that we have superpowers, a lot of them have become easier, havenât they?â","âSo are we just going to live like this?â","Jiang Cheng asked, âIs this really what we want?â","âStay shut inside the residential compounds, plant crops, raise chickens, and become self-sufficient? Is this how weâre going to live from now on?â","It didnât sound so bad.","But a deep sense of uncertainty still hung over everyone.","Jiang Cheng was just about to speak when someone in the crowd suddenly shouted, âJiang Cheng, lead us into the city!â","Jiang Cheng looked over. It was someone she didnât know very well.","Not being familiar with him meant he wasnât one of the core members, nor someone close to the center of things. He was just an ordinary homeowner.","Usually, people like that werenât particularly strong. The powerful ones naturally gravitated toward the center, and the center was happy to gather them in.","Yet this ordinary homeowner, whose name Jiang Cheng couldnât recall and whose face she barely recognized, had shouted out:","âWe canât stay trapped here!â","His cry shattered the uncertainty weighing on everyoneâs hearts.","Life was still long. How could they allow themselves to be trapped here?","Was their entire world going to consist of just a few residential compounds?","How could that be?","No!","âThatâs right! Jiang Cheng, lead us out!â","âLetâs take the Technology New District first, then enter the city!â","âThis world belongs to us, not those fucking zombies!â","Everyone was sitting on the ground, so they all looked short, but their fists rose high into the air, one after another.","âFight our way out!â","âFight our way out!â","The shouts rang out in a wave.","âJiang Cheng, you take command. Weâll all listen to you!â","âWe believe in you!â","Jiang Cheng lowered the megaphone and looked at the people before her.","Beneath the autumn sunlight, every face was clear.","She hadnât even said anything yet. She hadnât presented them with any options.","And they had already chosen the path she wanted them to take.","She hadnât incited or manipulated them. They had acted of their own accord, voluntarily.","They had made their own choice.","Every pair of eyes was bright, each one seeing the way forward.","As Jiang Cheng found herself watched by all those eyes, an indescribable sense of satisfaction welled up inside her.","She lifted the megaphone.","The crowd fell silent.","âIâd prepared a whole speech designed to stir your emotionsâ¦â Jiang Cheng said.","Everyone burst into laughter.","âWell, I donât need it now,â Jiang Cheng continued. âWhat I want is the same as what all of you want.â","\"We are human beings. How can we be confined to a space as small as just a few residential communities?\"","\"We must take back the living space that belongs to humanity.\"","\"Here, I have some bad news to share with you all, and it has been confirmed,\" Jiang Cheng said seriously.","Everyone focused their attention.","Jiang Cheng shared the information. \"There are no survivors in the Development Zone Government.\"","\"Mo Li went to confirm it,\" he added.","Someone below asked, \"Not a single one?\"","\"None,\" Jiang Cheng said firmly. \"Mo Li is different from us. He doesn't search with his eyes. His searching ability might be an enhanced natural skill of cats, or perhaps it's a kind of spiritual superpower. I'm not sure which, but I know it's very accurate.\"","Everyone couldn't help but turn their heads to look.","Because the adults were having a meeting, the children who had lost their parents became sensitive and quiet. They stopped playing football and making noise.","They gathered around Mo Li, gently stroking him and pretending to lull him to sleep.","Mo Li cooperated well.","Or maybe he was really asleep.","It was hard to believe that this well - behaved little kitten was the same huge beast as the one as large as a house yesterday.","You might not believe how capable a little kitten could be, but you would definitely believe the power of that huge beast.","That was a beast that could bite through a human body with its teeth.","\"So,\" Jiang Cheng said, \"it's confirmed that there is no government in the Science and Technology New District now.\"","\"How could this happen?\" many people murmured, whispering to each other. \"How could this happen?\"","Even the primary school had survivors. How could there be no survivors in such a large Development Zone Government building?","At the same time, a thought flashed through the minds of Zhao Yi, Gao Yuxuan, and Song Jingshuo -","This is unreasonable.","This is unscientific.","Even from a probabilistic point of view.","\"So, I declare -\"","Jiang Cheng's voice rang out in the square.","\"I declare -\"","\"The Provisional Government of the Science and Technology New District is hereby established!\"","The children all looked up.","Because it suddenly became extremely quiet on the adults' side.","Immediately afterwards, the adults erupted into huge cheers!","\"Yes, we are the government!\"","\"The government is gone, so we'll rebuild it!\"","\"It doesn't matter if it's gone. There's nothing to be afraid of. As long as there are still people alive, we have everything!\"","Uncle Eighty, a veteran, had tears in his eyes.","\"I was behind in my thinking,\" he said. \"I was stupid.\"","\"As long as the people are still here, what's there to fear?\"","\"After all, the government originally came from the masses!\"","On September 2nd, the fifth day after the second outbreak of the zombie virus.","The Provisional Government of the Science and Technology New District was announced to be established in the Youth Apartment.","There were more than six hundred people gathered at the scene.","At the scene, the Zombie Clearance Combat Team of the Science and Technology New District, abbreviated as the Science and Technology New District Team, was established.","The newly - established Science and Technology New District Team would no longer recruit volunteers on a fluid basis as before.","From today on, it would have a formal and fixed establishment.","With forty - five superpowered individuals from the Youth Apartment, Jixiang Jiayuan, and Yujing Xiangyuan as the core, the total number of members was two hundred.","Two hundred people was already a large number.","There was no need for the team to be overly large and bloated.","Now, people had integrated superpowers into their thinking patterns. For example, at Jiang Cheng's suggestion, having gold - type superpowered individuals control the \"knife - carts\" had been proven effective through tests and had become a trump card in outdoor battles.","Just yesterday, a new combat mode had taken shape: first, eliminate large groups of outdoor zombies in batches, and then conduct point - to - point clearances of buildings.","Under this mode, there were knife - carts outdoors, and many buildings couldn't accommodate a large number of people at the same time.","So, after discussion, it was decided that a team of 200 people was the most suitable for capturing buildings such as schools and hospitals.","The core members of the Provisional Government were transformed from the Interim Committee members of the Youth Apartment, including Jiang Cheng and all six building managers.","It also included Zhou Wang, Huang Xuetao, and Xiao Dan from Jixiang Jiayuan.","And two superpowered individuals from Yujing Xiangyuan.","These were the founding leadership of the Provisional Government."]},{"number":136,"title":"Chapter 136: 0136","paragraphs":["In practical terms, establishing the provisional government changed very little. It was still the same group of people dividing up the work and cooperating to maintain everyoneâs lives as they were.","But spiritually, it gave many people who had felt hollow and lost something to hold on to.","Breaking out of the technology district and reclaiming humanityâs living space had now become everyoneâs shared conviction.","But every journey had to be taken one step at a time, and every meal had to be eaten one bite at a time.","After the general assembly ended, they held a smaller meeting inside the clubhouse. Besides the core members, many key figures were there as well.","Zhao Yi, Gao Yuxuan, and even Little Huang were among them.","For some inexplicable reason, Zhao Yi, Gao Yuxuan, and Song Jingshuo had grown close.","Song Jingshuo understood what they wanted. He was the first to speak.","Things had progressed to the point where they could no longer consider certain matters solely on the basis of personal relationships. Some things had to be made clear.","âJiang Cheng,â Song Jingshuo asked, âare you one hundred percent certain that there are no survivors in the development-zone government?â","Everyone turned their eyes to Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng faced them calmly. âYes. One hundred percent. Mo Li wouldnât miss a single survivor. He was the one who found the survivors at Renxin Hospital. I have absolute faith in Mo Liâs abilities.â","Song Jingshuo voiced what everyone was thinking. âThat doesnât make sense.â","âItâs not only unreasonableâitâs unscientific,â Jiang Cheng added. âThatâs what I think too.â","Everyone pressed their lips together.","Jiang Cheng folded her arms and paced back and forth several times, as though weighing her options.","At last, she stopped.","âI actually didnât want to bring this up so soon. I mentioned it to Jingshuo beforeâI had a theory, but without evidence, it didnât seem appropriate to say anything too early.â","Song Jingshuo remembered. âYes, you did. Can you tell us now?â","Jiang Cheng nodded and swept her gaze across the room.","âI suspect that our government was deliberately wiped out.â","âI suspect that the zombie virus didnât emerge naturally. It was a terrorist attack with a specific target.â","They were gathered in the clubhouse lobby. The air fell completely silent; one could have heard a pin drop.","Jiang Cheng continued, âAt first, it was only a suspicion. But think about it. As long as even one or two senior government officials were still alive, they would have their own channels and means of contacting other high-ranking officials, reaching out to various departments, and calling for military assistance. Even if only a small part of the military remained, gathering them together would still make them stronger than ordinary civilians.â","âEven if only one senior official had survived, their status alone would have been enough. If they were willing to step forward, there would certainly be many people who, regardless of the danger, would rush out to join them and form a force. Weâve experienced this ourselves. Before we had armor, didnât we still charge out of the residential compound?â","âEven if they couldnât completely seize the television station, they could have found a way to contact any surviving employees inside and at least broadcast an announcement telling the civilians that someone was still alive. Even a single person remaining in the government would have been enough to preserve hope in the hearts of the people. Wouldnât it?â","âBut there was no one.â","âToday is already September 2! Itâs the fifth day!â","âLast night, I had Mo Li go to the development-zone government building.â","âRight now, this is the only definite sample I have. Itâs an isolated sample, so it canât serve as conclusive proof. But it has certainly strengthened my suspicion.â","âIt would be simple to disprove me. We go into the city and verify for ourselves whether anyone in the government is still alive.â","âAs long as a single mid- or high-ranking official is still alive, my theory can be overturned.â","âIf thatâs the case, it would be wonderful news.â","Everyoneâs expression was grim.","Middle-aged men liked to discuss national affairs and political trends.","People in finance couldnât separate economics from politics.","To some extent, everyone possessed a degree of political awareness.","Even Zhao Yi, a hardcore otaku, rubbed his face vigorously. âJiang Cheng, do you realize what youâre saying?â","âI do.â","Jiang Cheng said, âIâm saying that I believe the zombie virus was part of a terrorist operation launched by an outside forceâa mass slaughter of civilians and a targeted elimination of high-ranking officials.â","âOr perhaps itâs all just me imagining things.â","Everyone simply ignored the last sentence.","Zhao Yi said, âIf youâre right, then what weâre facing isâ¦â","A war on the scale of national annihilation.","Zhao Yi understood Jiang Chengâs description all too well.","He was an anime fan. Domestic animation had been gradually catching up, but veterans like him and Gao Yuxuan mainly watched works from a certain small country to the east.","Because that country was small, its manga and anime were constantly featuring ânation-destroyingâ events.","But in real life, Zhao Yi lived in a great nationâa thousand-year-old country with a booming economy and rapid development.","Now someone was telling him that the country might be destroyed. To Zhao Yi, it sounded far too much like anime.","And because it sounded too much like anime, it lacked any sense of reality.","But then againâ¦","Zhao Yi recalled the image of the enormous black cat standing beside the girl.","It had already been like something out of an anime for a long time, hadnât it?","Perhaps fate had existed all along.","He stared at Jiang Cheng.","The Chosen Protagonist.","With the Chosen Protagonist unveiling the truth, everything suddenly seemed more logical.","Jiang Cheng hadnât exactly lied. There was no lie in her theory.","But she had concealed the fact that she was a time traveler.","And what she called an âoutside forceâ was not the âforeign powerâ everyone else assumed it to be.","A foreign country might possess the ability to release some kind of virus.","But both times the virus had broken out, the sky had turned a stormy purple. Jiang Cheng had always believed that couldnât be a coincidence.","Based on her understanding of this world, no country currently possessed the technological power to manipulate the atmosphere and outer space on such a massive scale.","But if there were a force capable of sending a soul into a completely unfamiliar world while sealing away her memoriesâ","And if that force had also brought along the familiar âstorage spaceââ","Then Jiang Cheng believed that somewhere, some power must exist.","It was the mastermind behind her transmigration and amnesia, and the true culprit responsible for the mass deaths of ordinary people.","Jiang Cheng looked around at everyone. Then she pulled something from her trouser pocket and unfolded it.","Then she unfolded it again.","And again.","It turned out to be a map folded several times over.","Jiang Cheng spread the map across the small round table at the reception desk.","âLetâs set that aside for now. We need to keep our feet on the ground.â","It was a map of S City. Ring roads circled the city one after another, while the technology district lay beyond the Fifth Ring Road.","Within the First Ring Road was the old city, which contained a large number of protected historical buildings.","Within the Second Ring Road was the older urban district.","The Third and Fourth Ring Roads encompassed the cityâs main urban areas.","Outside the Fifth Ring Road lay clusters of factories relocated from the city, as well as residential communities that had been moved outward.","Jiang Cheng pressed her finger against the area within the Second Ring Road. âThe municipal government is here.â","Then she dragged her finger a long way across the map, all the way to the Fifth Ring Road. âWeâre here.â","She drew another circle. âThis is the entire technology district. Weâll put that matter aside for now. Even if Iâm right, all we can do at the moment is focus on whatâs directly in front of us. Letâs start by examining the technology district.â","The technology district was further divided into a residential area and an industrial park.","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuanâs companies were both located in the industrial park.","The industrial park was separated by a river called the Bailiang River. The development-zone government building stood beside the river.","Little Huangâs mother had an office overlooking the river.","The residential area was further divided into eastern and western districts.","The Youth Apartments were in the eastern district, which had been developed first. The western district was developed later, and many of its properties were still awaiting construction. Several projects had been left half-finished when the zombie disaster brought work to a halt.","Apparently, even before that, a shortage of workers had prevented several of the presale developments from resuming construction for an entire month.","The buyers had not made a fuss, because many of them were gone too.","Some properties had technically been handed over, but their occupancy rates were still low.","Farther west lay the land designated for the planned third phase of development. For now, it was nothing but wasteland, being held in reserve.","The population of the New Technology District was currently concentrated in this area.","Jiang Cheng spread her hand over the entire New Technology District. âNow that weâve established ourselves as the government of the New Technology District, the first thing we need to do is reclaim the districtâs entire livable area.â","âStep one is the residential areas, including every community where people are living.â","âThat includes the development-zone government offices, the private school, the two private kindergartens, Renxin Hospital, and Tianfu Shopping Center.â","âAm I leaving anything out?â","When people gathered together as a collective, once they had a common goal and a concrete plan of action, the power they could unleash was astonishing.","Take Cui Haiyang and Uncle Eighty, for example. Jiang Chengâs order was simple: everyone gets armor, and everyone gets a weapon.","âEveryoneâ meant every single person, including the elderly and children who had stayed behind.","That way, even if the teams at the front suffered casualties, the elderly and children could still protect themselvesâand even step in as replacements if necessary.","Jiang Cheng asked, âCan you do it?â","Uncle Eighty thumped his chest and promised, âWe can!â","Cui Haiyang had also developed a sense of destinyâor perhaps a sense of mission. He looked practically ready to swear a military oath. âWeâll complete the mission without fail.â","Materials were especially easy to find for a metal-element superpowered user. Cui Haiyang and the others requisitioned all the barriers along the streets and roads outside the residential communities, then used them to make armor and weapons inside the community. They worked feverishly.","Gao Yuxuan and Guo Jun had two suits of solid-metal armor specially made.","The armor had to cover their entire bodies, including their eyes and hands.","âLike medieval knights?â Cui Haiyang asked.","âMore or less,â Gao Yuxuan replied. âIt has to be sturdy. Make sure the zombies canât punch through it and tear us open.â","âWhat are you two planning to do?â Cui Haiyang asked. âExplain it clearly so I can adjust the design for you.â","It turned out that Zhao Yi holding Zhang Lesiâs hand and sticking them both onto Gao Yuxuan while he convulsed had given Gao Yuxuan an idea earlier that day.","He said to Guo Jun, âThe two of us donât actually need to insist on killing them with a single blow.â","A one-hit kill demanded a great deal of precision and output strength. Killing the zombies one by one consumed their superpowers quickly and was exhausting.","The principle behind using electricity to kill zombies was the same as using fire or physical force.","They already knew that zombies were half-dead corpsesâwalking dead. But their brains still possessed some activity.","Electricity, fire, and physical attacks all worked by completely destroying the brain or eliminating that remaining activity.","Gao Yuxuanâs thought was this: âIf their remaining activity can be destroyed by an electric shock, that means they should react to electricity the way a living creature does.â","âElectricity isnât like fire. If you touch a live wire, you might not die immediately. You might start dancing instead.â","âThe amount of electricity needed to make a zombie dance is far less than whatâs needed to kill one.â","âAnd they should conduct electricity just like human beings, right?â","âSo the two of us want to walk into a horde of zombies and see what happens.â","âSo you understand, Old Cuiâdonât cut corners. If you cut corners, Iâll die. Got it?â","âMake it sturdy. Reinforce it! Yes, reinforce it again! Reinforce it several more times!â"]},{"number":137,"title":"Chapter 137: 0137","paragraphs":["Song Jingshuo was not part of the teamâs official combat roster. He had been assigned to the logistics group.","Song Jingshuo had no objections.","The situation now was completely different from two months ago. Logistics was just as important as ever.","As long as the order supported by the majority remained in place, force was not the only way to gain power. Being in the logistics group would not marginalize him or cause him to lose authority.","After the meeting, he left the clubhouse and saw Manager Wang diligently fertilizing the soil.","Manager Wang had lost contact with his family, and he himself had no superpowers.","Cao Jiacai had died only yesterday, and several others had left. At present, the property management staff consisted of only him, Yang Xinyan, Aunt Pan, and Little Fang.","Seeing how short-staffed they were, Aunt Pan had taken the initiative to help clean that morning. Manager Wang had been so alarmed that he quickly snatched the broom away from her.","âYou go take care of your own work. Go on, go on. Thereâs a meeting later, isnât there?â","He absolutely refused to hand the broom back to Aunt Pan. Left with no choice, Aunt Pan could only use her superpower to help.","Wherever she went, the dust on the ground swirled after her, looking like tiny tornadoes clinging to the pavement. She made a circuit of the residential complex, gathering all the dust together, then compacted and hardened it until it became granules instead of loose powder. Finally, she moved it all into the flower beds.","The complex looked much cleaner.","Fortunately, the residents themselves were fairly civilized and did not litter everywhere.","With so few people left, Yang Xinyan now had to do physical labor as well.","Manager Wang worked even harder. The weeds he had raked out while planting vegetables the day before had dried, and today he was burning them into plant ash. He was a city dweller and did not actually know much about this sort of thing. Aunt Pan told him what to do, and he simply followed her instructions.","He was quite good at assisting Song Jingshuo.","Aunt Pan came over and touched the patch of soil where he had scattered the plant ash. The earth immediately churned, as if it were stirring itself.","Once it was evenly mixed, Aunt Pan instructed Song Jingshuo, âThis is for planting beans. Beans love plant ash. When we plant beans, we always mix the seeds with plant ash. It also helps keep away insects.â","Then she added, âBut you canât use plant ash together with human or animal manure. Plant ash will neutralize manure fertilizer. Once theyâre mixed, the manure wonât work properly.â","Song Jingshuo was stunned. âPeople in the countryside still use manure? Donât they use chemical fertilizer now?â","Aunt Pan said, âThe grain grown for city people is fertilized with chemicals. But for the plots we keep for ourselves, we country folk still prefer manure. Chicken manure and pig manure both work well. The crops and vegetables taste better, too.â","Song Jingshuo fell silent.","He planted the beans he had soaked.","Aunt Pan liked watching him grow vegetables. Although she claimed she was no expert farmer, she was actually quite attached to the soil and the crops.","Song Jingshuo grew soybeans the size of grapes, which left Aunt Pan delighted.","She reminded him to save some seeds each time, then touched the patch of soil again. âOh, thatâs impressive. This plot is worn out now. Use another one and let this patch rest.â","Song Jingshuo asked Manager Wang, âAre we out of plant ash?â","âYep,â Manager Wang replied.","Song Jingshuo was just about to move to another patch when Manager Wang said, âBut the property office has chemical fertilizer.â","Song Jingshuo fell silent again.","The complex had large areas of landscaping that needed to be maintained, so they kept chemical fertilizer in the storage room.","Song Jingshuo pinched the bridge of his nose. âIf we have chemical fertilizer, why are we still using plant ash?â","Manager Wang looked aggrieved. âAuntie told me to.â","Aunt Pan nodded. âI did. We donât like using chemical fertilizer. Besides, Old Ma and Old Jiang told me yesterday that they wanted to make soy milk. Beans grown with plant ash are better for that.â","Fine, then.","Manager Wang called Little Fang, one of the security guards, and went to haul over the chemical fertilizer.","Taking advantage of the interruption, Aunt Pan gave Song Jingshuo a crash course in soil fertility. She explained crop rotation, fallowing, and how to apply fertilizer, as well as which crops preferred which kinds of fertilizer.","Song Jingshuo listened patiently. He had now completely accepted his superpower. And since he had taken responsibility for this work, he intended to do it properly.","As he listened, he suddenly looked up and saw a man standing there with a foam box in his arms. He had no idea how long the man had been there. Clearly, he had been listening to Aunt Pan and waiting for a chance to join the conversation.","The manâs face was familiar, but not familiar enough for Song Jingshuo to recall his name.","Song Jingshuo asked, âCan I help you?â","The man hurried over. âIâm looking for Aunt Pan. No, I mean, Iâm looking for both of you.â","He thrust the foam box toward Aunt Pan. âAuntie, you can tell whether the soil is fertile enough just by touching it, right? What about this?â","Aunt Pan did as he asked, placing her hand on the box. She gave a little cry. âNot quite. Itâs too strong. Itâll burn the roots.â","âExactly. Youâre right,â the man said. Instead of being upset, he was delighted by the accuracy of her judgment. âThere wasnât enough time for it to finish decomposing, so itâll definitely burn the roots. And my conditions arenât good enough for high-temperature composting. I can only use the deep-burial method and let it break down anaerobically.â","He then turned to Song Jingshuo. âBut I figured that the vegetables you grow arenât ordinary vegetables. You must have some degree of control over the plantsâ growth process. Could you prevent them from suffering root burn when using fertilizer that hasnât fully decomposed?â","Song Jingshuo asked, âWhat do you do, exactly? Agricultural research?â","âYeah, agricultural research.â The man threw his head back and sighed. âIâm a new-generation agricultural scientist who has devoted himself to agricultural research, yet I donât have an earth-type or wood-type superpower. Whereâs the justice in that?â","Aunt Pan had been born a farmer, and it made perfect sense that she had awakened an earth-type superpower. He could understand thatâand even wholeheartedly approve.","But Song Jingshuo, a finance guy who drove an SUV, wore a watch, and used hair gel, had actually awakened a wood-type power.","Good heavens, would you please open your eyes and look?","The new-generation agricultural scientist is right here!","Look at the real agricultural researcherâs dark complexion, then look at the person you chose. At a glance, he was obviously the sort of man who did face masks at home.","Song Jingshuo was quite perceptive. He could vaguely sense that the man had some resentment toward him.","His radar for this sort of thing was especially sensitive.","He sized the man up and analyzed him. âDidnât you hear what they said? Physical fitness is the first requirement for awakening a superpower. Your body-fat percentage is too high. You probably donât exercise much. You should really start lifting weights.â","He even folded his arms across his chest and displayed his muscles.","That left the man speechless. The agricultural researcher pushed the foam box toward Song Jingshuo. âJust give it a try.â","What Song Jingshuo had brought upstairs the day before wasnât limited to beans.","The greens he had planted had already produced seeds, and he had saved some. He had soaked them at home as well. Even if soaked seeds had not yet sprouted, they required less of his superpower to coax them into growing.","Aunt Pan added, âTry some bok choy.â","Perfect.","Song Jingshuo dropped a few vegetable seeds into the foam box. Just as he had done the day before, he stimulated them with his power. Soon, roots and shoots appeared, followed by rapid growth.","But Song Jingshuo suddenly frowned. âHmm?â","The agricultural researcher asked, âThe roots are starting to burn, right?â","He explained, âRoot burn happens when the fertilizer concentration is too high. It causes water inside the plantâs roots to flow back into the soil, leaving the plant dehydrated and eventually killing it.â","Aunt Pan suddenly understood. âSo thatâs what it means. I knew it would burn the roots, but I never knew exactly why. So thatâs how it works.â","Song Jingshuo said, âSo thatâs how it works.â","He understood the tugging force that came from the soil.","The tiny seedling seemed to be screaming.","Song Jingshuo focused his mind. His superpower reached deep into the roots and began wrestling with the force pulling from the earth.","He won easily. The little seedlings quieted down and grew into plump, sturdy heads of bok choy.","Song Jingshuoâs eyes lit up. âThis soil of yours is excellent!â","As long as they overcame that pulling force and protected the roots, the plantsâ growth afterward was remarkably easy.","It was like a child who didnât need their parents to chase them around with a spoon. They could eat big mouthfuls all on their own, filling their bellies and growing up big and strong.","Just then, Manager Wang and Little Fang returned, pulling a flatbed cart loaded with several bags of fertilizer.","âWeâre here,â they said. âThis is everything.â","Song Jingshuo asked, âThatâs all? There isnât any more?â","He didnât know much about fertilizer, but it didnât look like very much. He turned to Aunt Pan. âBig Sis, thisâ¦â","âItâs nowhere near enough,â the agricultural researcher said excitedly. âThat was only enough for one meal yesterday. You have to plan for several hundred people eating three meals a day in the future. Besides, the fertilizer youâre using to accelerate the plantsâ growth canât be compared with ordinary crops in terms of absorption cycles or quantity.â","âIâm telling you, itâs not enough.â","Manager Wang thought to himself, Isnât running short of fertilizer bad news? Why are you so happy?","He quickly offered an explanation. âThis is what we had left over from before. Thereâs no need to fertilize in autumn and winter, so we were going to buy more next year. Thatâs why thereâs only this much left.â","In fact, Song Jingshuo was the only person present who didnât know Manager Wang was lying.","The landscaping around the residential complex was supposed to be fertilized once in September. This helped store nutrients safely for the winter and encouraged new growth the following year.","Aunt Pan and Little Fang knew this because they were always dragged out to do the work when the time came. The agricultural researcher knew because he was a professional.","Only Song Jingshuo, the wood-element superpowered person, was completely unaware of it.","The real situation was that after the first disaster ended, Manager Wang returned to work and discovered that a great many residents had died.","Although he had ended up with a large number of vacant apartments under his control, he soon found that he couldnât make use of them at all, let alone collect any rent.","It was a serious problem.","It meant that property-management fees would plummet in the second half of the year.","Manager Wangâs guess was right. The fees were indeed collected with dismal results.","So he began cutting the budget. The landscaping and maintenance expenses were reduced, and no fertilizer was purchased for autumn and winter.","Aunt Pan and Little Fang both knew this.","But Manager Wang was an old acquaintance and their former supervisor, so neither of them said anything.","The agricultural researcher understood as well. But since yesterday, he had been observing Song Jingshuo planting vegetables and had seen Manager Wang clumsily doing his best to help.","The middle-aged man couldnât go home, wasnât a resident, and didnât have any superpowers. His situation was rather pitiful. There was no need to expose him.","Song Jingshuo didnât know Manager Wang had been fobbing him off, but he did understand why the agricultural researcher was so excited.","He asked, âWhat should I call you?â","âZeng Qiang.â","âZeng Qiang,â Song Jingshuo said. âHow do you make this fertilizer? What does it require, and how much can you supply?â","âUnlimited quantities on a large scale,â Zeng Qiang replied. âBut letâs discuss this somewhere else.â","Aunt Pan, Manager Wang, and Little Fang watched as Zeng Qiang picked up the foam box and turned away. Song Jingshuo followed him, and the two of them went to talk beneath a tree in the distance.","Little Fang clicked his tongue. âWhat are they talking about? Why do they have to avoid us?â","Manager Wang folded both hands over his belly. âTsk, I could figure it out with my toes.â","âHuh?â","âHeâs definitely asking for better treatment,â Manager Wang said. âWeâll have so many people to feed from now on. Xiao Songâs ability is incredibly important, but it has to be used together with fertilizer. So the fertilizer is important too. And since itâs important, he naturally wants better treatment.â","Aunt Pan didnât think that was right. âWhat treatment do we have now? Tell me.â","Manager Wang couldnât come up with an answer.","âExactly,â Aunt Pan said. âThere isnât any. Everyoneâs the same.â","Those with strong abilities went out to fight zombies, while those without them helped out around the residential complex.","At the meeting that morning, they had said that the property-management staff had been reduced so drastically that they wouldnât even let her cook anymore. They said her superpower ought to be used for something else. From now on, cleaning and other chores would still have to be assigned on a rotating basis.","What special treatment was there? Everyone had to do some work.","They all ate together, and everyone got the same food.","There was no difference in treatment at all.","It wasnât as though they could be like Cao Jiacai, a toad dreaming of winning over a whole group of city girls.","Xiao Song couldnât possibly be handed the girls as a reward.","If he really had that kind of idea, Little Zhang and Little Su would beat him to death.","Note: The information about fertilizer was sourced from the internet."]},{"number":138,"title":"Chapter 138: 0138","paragraphs":["Manager Wang was merely speculating, judging others by his own standards.","Zeng Qiang had taken Song Jingshuo aside to talk about fertilizerâreally, that was all.","The three people with Manager Wang watched from a distance. First, Zeng Qiang said something, and then Song Jingshuoâs face turned utterly shocked.","Aunt Pan: âHuh?â","Although Song Jingshuo had been in a somewhat foul mood lately and had become rather sharp-tongued, he was, on the whole, the sort of person who kept his emotions firmly under control.","He was always composed and proper, and rarely ever lost his poise.","Aunt Pan began to wonder. âSurely he didnât really ask for a girl?â","Under the shade of a tree, Song Jingshuo said, âYouâ¦ How could youâ¦â","Zeng Qiang had already anticipated his reaction.","It was a perfectly normal response.","He said, âThe amount of fertilizer weâll need in the future is going to be enormous. If my observations are correct, your superpower only accelerates the plantsâ development, but the nutrients they need for that development donât decrease at all. In fact, they may consume even more nutrients than plants growing normally.â","âIf you canât accept this plan, then youâll have to accept the other one,â he said.","Song Jingshuo had no idea how many nutrients normal plants consumed, but the plants he accelerated certainly absorbed them at an astonishing rate.","After a plot of land had been accelerated through one growth cycle, Aunt Pan only had to touch the soil to tell that all its fertility had been depleted.","Zeng Qiang was right.","Song Jingshuo calmed himself and said, âWhatâs the other plan? Let me hear it.â","In truth, he had already decided that no matter what, he was choosing the other plan.","Zeng Qiang said, âWeâll have to start collecting feces. I mean everyoneâs feces. Then weâll make manure for you to use.â","Song Jingshuoâs spirit shattered.","Actually, if he hadnât been a wood-type superhuman, if he hadnât been the person specifically responsible for growing vegetables, collecting human feces and turning it into manure wouldnât have been that big a deal.","It wasnât as though they were asking him to eat shit.","But unfortunately, he was precisely the person in charge of growing the vegetables.","What difference was that from making him eat shit?","Song Jingshuo said, âIsnât there anyââ","Zeng Qiang anticipated the question and cut him off with the answer: âNo.â","His tone was firm and final.","âYou have only two choices,â he said. âSomething disgusting, or something even more disgusting.â","There was more than a hint of malicious amusement in his voice.","People liked to say that men remained boys until the day they died, or that making friends was incredibly simple for men.","Few people ever mentioned that men actually competed fiercely with one another.","Someone like Song Jingshuoâwho made plenty of money and was handsome to bootâwas a natural enemy to other men.","Zeng Qiang was delighted to watch his control over his expression finally fail.","Song Jingshuo stood there with his hands on his hips for a long while. In the end, he said, âCome on. Letâs go tell Jiang Cheng.â","If they were using human feces, there was probably no need to report it. Song Jingshuo could make that decision himself.","Zeng Qiang had already guessed which option Song Jingshuo had chosen.","Song Jingshuo led Zeng Qiang to Jiang Cheng. There were people nearby, so Song Jingshuo leaned close and quietly explained the situation in Jiang Chengâs ear.","Jiang Cheng also showed a look of surprise.","After a momentâs thought, she asked, âWhat if it transmits a virus?â","Zeng Qiang said, âIâve observed them. While zombies are alive, their bodies have indeed undergone mutations. But after death, they rot just like human bodies. Weâve all seen stray cats, dogs, flies, and crows eat zombie flesh. Yet so far, there havenât been any zombie cats, zombie dogs, zombie flies, or zombie birds.â","âYour cat has even bitten zombies to death. Its mouth came into direct contact with zombie bodily fluids, and it didnât mutate either.â","âEarlier, when we burned zombie corpses, if there had been a virus, it would have spread through aerosols long ago. But that didnât happen.â","âSo, I believe zombie corpses can safely be used as animal-based organic fertilizer.â","Thatâs right. The soil inside the foam boxes Zeng Qiang was carrying contained chunks of zombie corpses he had secretly brought home in July.","He had several boxes like that at home.","He had only wanted to try it out. Then the zombie crisis ended.","The corpses hadnât decomposed enough yet, but leaving them there hadnât caused any problems. Unexpectedly, the zombie trouble had begun again, and the Finance Guy had started growing vegetables.","It was almost as though fate had arranged it all.","Jiang Cheng said nothing. She only looked at him.","Everyone knew that Jiang Cheng was hard-hearted. If she hadnât been that kind of person, she couldnât have led everyone through their previous journey.","But a person had to experience that hard-heartedness directed at themselves before they could truly understand what Jiang Cheng was like.","After holding Jiang Chengâs gaze for several seconds, Zeng Qiang suddenly understood.","He nodded. âThe property office still has a few bags of chemical fertilizer. Theyâll be enough for Jingshuo for a few days. During that time, Iâll have him help me grow some vegetables. Iâll be the first to eat them.â","Song Jingshuo shot him a glance.","A live human experiment.","But Jiang Cheng hadnât forced Zeng Qiang into it. He had volunteered.","If he wanted everyone else to eat it, he had to be willing to go first himself.","That was only reasonable.","Song Jingshuo and Zeng Qiang left Jiang Cheng together.","Song Jingshuo didnât say a word.","Zeng Qiang consoled him. âItâs all the same, really.â","He said, âEverything in this world eventually returns to dust. Tombstones and graves are merely ways for the living to entrust their feelings and memories. Underground, everything is the same. Sooner or later, it all returns to nature, gets absorbed by plants, and is then eaten by living creatures before being excreted as human or animal feces.â","âThere are plenty of animal-based organic fertilizers on the market too.â","âUsing animals, humans, or zombies is fundamentally no different.â","âItâs all the same. You eat it, and in the end, it becomes feces.â","Zeng Qiang sighed with boundless emotion.","âBesides, you canât taste the difference at all.â","The corners of Song Jingshuoâs mouth twitched.","Ever since the zombie crisis, a great many people had become philosophers.","Li Jiangbing had been right. They were all freaking lunatics.","Zeng Qiang carried his foam boxes away.","Song Jingshuo returned to growing vegetables.","Aunt Pan, Manager Wang, and the others had already replenished the fertilizer in the plot. When they saw him return, she said, âCome on.â","The moment Song Jingshuo began, he sensed the difference.","âChemical fertilizer?â he asked.","Aunt Pan said, âYes. What else would it be?â","Song Jingshuo said nothing more and focused on activating his superpower.","It was differentâfar too different.","Plants fed chemical fertilizer were like people eating compressed biscuits.","They had to eat it, but it was an unpleasant experience.","And unlike the feeling from earlier, when Song Jingshuo had protected the roots of those few seedlings and then watched them shoot up at an astonishing rate, the plants here showed no such vigor at all.","That was when Song Jingshuo realized he could never go back.","Zombie fertilizer was still the best.","At noon, everyone enjoyed a decent lunch and admired the soybeans, which had grown as large as grapes.","âTomorrow, weâll be drinking soy milk,â everyone said happily.","After eating their fill, the people from Yujingxiang Garden and Jixiangjiayuan also arrived. The Tech New District Zombie-Clearing Squad boarded their vehicles and set out on their first mission.","Todayâs targets were two private kindergartens and one private school. One of the kindergartens and the private school were on the same street. The other private kindergarten was elsewhere.","But since they had decided to reclaim the entire Tech New District, everyone agreed that they should clear out the kindergartens and school first. Only then would they feel at ease.","The bladed vehicles went in first, with Mo Li following behind, slaughtering their way through.","The special thing today was Guo Jun and Gao Yuxuan. Their armor was different from everyone elseâs, protecting them from head to toe.","The process of making those two suits of armor revealed the differences between metal-type superhumans.","Everyoneâs superpowers were the same, that much was true.","But several of them had studied or worked in fields related to machinery, with Cui Haiyang being the most representative example.","When he made this kind of full-body armor for Gao Yuxuan, he already knew how to connect and reinforce the joints, as well as how to design the armor so it could be opened, closed, and locked securely.","Uncle Eighty, however, couldnât do that.","If you asked Uncle Eighty to reproduce a copy of the original armor, he could manage it. With a sample right in front of him, all he had to do was imitate it.","He could make the crescent shovels, too. Their shape and structure werenât difficult.","Some knives and even scissors were no problem either. Take scissors, for example: Uncle Eighty understood how they were constructed, so he could reproduce them.","But armor this complicatedâarmor that had to open, close, and lock securely so it wouldnât suddenly spring open during a fightâwas beyond him.","He simply had no concept of how it worked.","If you didnât even know what you were trying to make, how could you possibly make it?","In the end, both sets of armor turned out well, and both Gao Yuxuan and Guo Jun were satisfied.","Everyone else, however, was thoroughly fed up with Gao Yuxuan. He kept leaking electricity, and since the metal armor conducted it, he was always shocking people whenever they were in the vehicles.","Gao Yuxuan felt deeply wronged and curled up by himself in a corner.","The kindergarten and the private school were located on the same street.","Everyone chose to go to the private school first, because they all knew that visiting the kindergarten afterward would leave them in an extremely gloomy mood.","The Blade Vehicle and Mo Li went on a killing spree in the school courtyard. Like everyone else, Gao Yuxuan and Guo Jun stayed in the vehicles outside to watch.","They let the Blade Vehicle and Mo Li kill for a while before the two men in iron armor got out.","The main reason was that their armor was relatively heavy, making them less agile. If the zombies in the courtyard were too densely packed, they might fail the test and end up trapped inside.","Then they would have to trouble Mo Li to rescue them.","So they waited until the Blade Vehicle and Mo Li had thinned the horde out before going in.","Everyone pressed against the car windows to watch the spectacle. The other few electric-type ability users were especially interested.","Although the two men were wearing full-body metal armor, it was covered in countless ventilation holes. Their human scent still drifted out to the zombies.","The zombies roared and lunged at them.","Gao Yuxuan had always fought from a distance. He had never stood there like a pillar and simply refused to fight back as he did today.","He closed his eyes, chose to trust Cui Haiyang, and began discharging electricity throughout his body.","The test was a success.","The zombies that pounced on him stuck to his armor and began shaking like sieves. Without outside help, they couldnât break free.","The zombies behind them leaped forward and became stuck to the zombies in front.","Before long, Gao Yuxuan was surrounded by layer upon layer of zombies and couldnât move at all.","He carefully controlled the current, keeping it at the most cost-effective level.","In other words, he output the minimum amount of electricity sufficient to hold the zombies in place and prevent them from escaping.","With that tiny amount of power, he could stick so many zombies to himself.","It was practically a control skill straight out of a video game!","Li Jiangbing shouted, âItâs our turn!â","The car doors opened. Li Jiangbing led a group of people charging out and into the school. They raised their crescent shovels and began hacking at the necks of the zombies wrapped around Gao Yuxuan.","Some of their shovels had wooden handles. The handles of the all-metal ones had already been wrapped in insulating tape.","One swing, one head.","Their efficiency was impressive.","Guo Jun, meanwhile, was conducting a different kind of test.","He also used electricity to stick a large number of zombies together. Once there were enough of them, he released a powerful surge of electricity in an instant.","Gao Yuxuan was testing control. Guo Jun wanted to test control combined with area-of-effect attacks.","Of course, this had all been Gao Yuxuanâs idea.","But Guo Junâs test couldnât be considered a success.","The total amount of electricity needed to stick a large number of zombies together and kill them was indeed slightly less than what it took to kill them one by one.","When killing them individually, Guo Jun attacked from a distance, sending out a long serpent of electricity that lost power along the way.","An area attack could indeed reduce some of that loss, but the savings werenât especially significant. They were certainly nowhere near as impressive as Gao Yuxuanâs.","At the same time, releasing enough electricity in a single instant to kill so many zombies nearly drained Guo Jun completely.","Fortunately, Li Jiangbingâs group was nearby and rushed over to help.","Gao Yuxuan was such a menace!","Note: The information about composting came from the internet."]},{"number":139,"title":"Chapter 139: 0139","paragraphs":["The team went out to fight while Song Jingshuo stayed home to farm.","Aunt Pan had taught him that different vegetables needed different kinds of fertilizer. He had tried them all and was gradually getting the hang of it.","At everyoneâs fervent urging for fruit, he started growing strawberries today.","He set aside a permanent plot for them, added fertilizer, and began forcing them to grow.","With the mindset of âfewer plants, bigger yields,â Song Jingshuo forced the strawberries to grow as large as pears.","That ought to be enough for everyone to eat their fill.","Su Yu didnât join todayâs operation either.","The team was divided into groups. Whenever they went out, they had to leave people behind to guard the residential complex, with at least several superpowered individuals staying there in case of emergencies.","Two fire-element superpowered people were among those left behind. Everyone discussed practicing with one another.","Su Yu stood in the little plaza and spread out her protective barrier, expanding it into a huge dome about twenty meters in diameter.","Inside the barrier, the little ones exclaimed, âWhoa!â","The fire-element users launched fireballs at the barrier one after another.","Su Yu could feel the impact of the attacks against the barrier. But while her superpower was abundant and the barrier was operating at full capacity, it canceled out the impacts on its own, so none of the force rebounded onto her.","The two fire-element users used the barrier to practice their aim, hitting whatever they pointed at.","The fireballs smashed into the barrier and scattered like fireworks.","The little ones chased after the fireballs inside the barrier.","Manager Wang took one look, then turned around and somehow came back with two bamboo poles. He tied strips of cloth to the ends and handed them to the children.","âTargets.â","The little ones split into two groups and followed the bamboo poles as they ran around.","At random spots, they poked the ends of the poles through the barrier.","The fireballs came flying over.","Everyone cried, âWhoa!â","The fireballs turned into targets chasing the bamboo poles. Wherever the poles poked out, the fireballs struck.","Pretty good.","When the children grew tired from running, Song Jingshuo called out, âCome eat strawberries!â","Everyone got one. Their mouths were stained bright red with juice as they chattered, âIâve never seen strawberries this big before!â","It wasnât only the children who had never eaten strawberries that size. The adults hadnât either.","The first crop was quickly picked clean by the people who had stayed behind.","Song Jingshuo took one look and realized that this amount of strawberries was nowhere near enough to go around. He was preparing to force a second crop when Zeng Qiang came over.","âTry seeing if you can artificially force the strawberry runners to reproduce.â","He explained to Song Jingshuo what strawberry runners were.","This required controlling the plants so that they would not flower or bear fruit, but instead put all their energy into growing new plantlets.","Song Jingshuo had never tried such targeted control before.","Under Zeng Qiangâs guidance, he began experimenting.","It worked perfectly. The strawberries sent out long runners, and little plantlets grew along them.","Normally, strawberry runners had to be secured with tools and given a certain amount of time to develop. But things werenât normal now.","Zeng Qiang simply pressed them down with his hand. âMake that plantlet put down roots in the soil. Yes, just like that. Good. Thatâs enough. Break them off here, here, and here, so they become separate plants.â","They didnât even need scissors. With a thought from Song Jingshuo, the runners snapped automatically at the nodes where they needed to be separated.","The rooted plantlets became individual plants.","The strawberry field expanded several times over.","Zeng Qiang said, âIt worked. Go ahead and force them to grow.â","He squatted beside the strawberry field and watched Song Jingshuo force an entire expanse of strawberries to grow, each one as large as a pear.","It was enough to make anyone envious and jealous.","Zeng Qiang angrily ate another one and stuffed himself.","The team returned in the evening.","There were far fewer students at the private school than at the public one, so there were relatively fewer zombies as well. They brought back more than thirty middle school students and two teachers.","Song Jingshuo went up to them and asked about the situation.","Jiang Cheng said, âItâs a little troublesome. Their homes arenât in the Technology New District.â","The private school was a boarding school, and the childrenâs families were scattered throughout different parts of the city.","Song Jingshuo asked, âAre they staying in our residential complex?â","Jiang Cheng replied, âNo need. Old Zhou took them in.â","Zhou Wang had taken responsibility for the more than thirty middle school students and the two teachers, leading them to Jixiang Jiayuan.","The population of Jixiang Jiayuan was severely skewed, with the elderly making up the vast majority. Zhou Wang brought these young people, who had been stranded in the Technology New District, into his residential complex.","They were only half-grown kids, but they were still a labor force.","He had reached an agreement with the two teachers: Jixiang Jiayuan would provide them with food and lodging, while they joined the community, followed Zhou Wangâs arrangements, and participated in community labor.","The little ones ran over and tugged at Li Jiangbing.","âUncle! Uncle! Come eat strawberries! Theyâre huge and delicious!â","Li Jiangbing hurriedly said, âDonât touch me, donât touch me. Iâm filthy.â","The girls who had returned from the fight quickly went upstairs to shower and change.","A lot of the men were too lazy to bother and simply shouted to Li Jiangbing, âJiangbing! Jiangbing! Letâs take a bath!â","They pushed Li Jiangbing toward the fountain pool.","The water in the fountain pool was actually reclaimed water. It wasnât drinkable and wasnât suitable for contact with skin.","But the water Li Jiangbing extracted was purified waterâcompletely clean.","The ball of water transformed into a column, spinning with a loud whoosh.","Li Jiangbing said, âItâs cold. Iâm warning you, I wonât be responsible if itâs cold.â","It was already evening, and the buildingâs shadow blocked the sunlight. The fountain pool had not received any sun, so the water was a little chilly.","âNo problem,â everyone said.","The first person charged in. Standing in the middle of the water column as it spun around him, he looked as though a washing machine had been stripped of all its hardware, leaving only the swirling water behind.","It actually worked. The grime and sweat clinging to his armor, clothes, and arms were all washed away.","As soon as he jumped out of the water column, Li Jiangbing immediately reached out through the air and pulled a ball of water from his body.","His clothes dried instantly.","Even his underwear was dry.","It was just a little cold.","The man shivered, then shouted, âThat feels great!â","The group burst into laughter. They were all strapping young men who could sleep on a cold brick bed without complaint. One after another, they jumped into the water column to bathe.","Wu Jiancheng watched several people âshowerâ in succession. He went over and tested the temperature with one finger, then went to whisper with Cui Haiyang.","Cui Haiyang nodded. In half a minute, he made a large iron barrel right there on the spot. He tapped it and shouted, âJiangbing!â","Li Jiangbing said, ââ¦Huh?â","He directed the purified water into the large iron barrel.","Wu Jiancheng immediately sent roaring flames beneath it.","Cui Haiyang said, âDonât heat it until itâs boiling. Warm is enough.â","âGot it,â Wu Jiancheng replied.","Wu Jiancheng could now control the temperature of his flames. The temperature of a single flame could vary by a huge margin.","A minute was enough.","Wu Jiancheng called out, âJiangbing!â","âComing!â Li Jiangbing replied. âWait a second. Iâll go first! Let me try it first.â","Warm water flowed out in a column. Li Jiangbing jumped in and immediately shouted, âDamn, that feels amazing!â","How was this any different from soaking in a warm bath?","Everyone who tried it afterward cried out in delight. Some even took the opportunity to bend over and wash their hair.","Aunt Pan said, âDry him off quickly. The windâs getting chilly. Heâll catch a chill in his head!â","Li Jiangbing laughed and cursed the man for being so crafty, then reached through the air and pulled out all the water clinging to his hair and body. He was completely dry.","The children stared in amazement, constantly going, âWowâ¦ wowâ¦â","Only the few people who had taken cold-water baths earlier stood there in silence.","What a bunch of jerks!","Song Jingshuo asked, âWhat about the two kindergartens?â","Jiang Cheng shook her head.","There were no survivors at the kindergartens either.","There was nothing they could do. The children in kindergarten were simply too young.","The elementary school students had been pushed into their classrooms by their teacher to hide. They knew it was dangerous outside, and they could endure their hunger without going out. They also knew not to make any noise that might attract the zombies.","Kindergarten children couldnât do that.","After fighting all afternoon, everyone came back to a hot meal, and each person was given strawberries as well.","The strawberries were so large that one was enough to fill you up.","Everyone went to visit the strawberry fields, marveling that they would soon be able to enjoy strawberries whenever they wanted.","Jiang Cheng had already drawn up a list of the areas to be cleared next. Tomorrow would be a full day of fighting.","That evening, everyone went back to rest, while the people in the cafeteria began working overtime to make flower rolls and steamed buns.","Steamed buns were plain and had to be eaten with side dishes. Flower rolls were seasoned and could be eaten on their own, so they would make convenient lunches for everyone the next day.","The cooksâthe uncles, aunties, and older sisters who had come from Jixiang Jiayuanâdidnât actually receive any payment.","But the group of them were happy and fulfilled doing the work.","They told Auntie Jiang and Auntie Ma, âOh, itâs enough just to have something to do. Itâs still better than staring at an empty residential complex.â","It gave them something to hold on to.","They felt that even in their old age, they could still make a contribution to so many people. They were still useful.","On September 3, many people woke up that morning with the feeling that they were getting ready for work.","They dressed, washed up, went downstairs, greeted people they knew, and headed to the cafeteria together.","âThereâs soy milk today!â","Just hearing the words âsoy milkâ brought a rush of happiness.","As it turned out, Zeng Qiang had earned some credit too.","After Song Jingshuo had grown soybeans the day before, he handed them over to the cafeteria and left the rest to them. He only handled the planting; the cafeteria took care of all cooking and preparation.","The cafeteria workers even thought that using fresh beans to make soy milk would be easier since they didnât need to soak them first.","What they called fresh soybeans were actually edamame.","Edamame were soybeans picked when they were about seventy to eighty percent mature, still inside their pods.","Edamame were a common food. In summer, a plate of boiled edamame and peanuts served with beer was one of the most familiar sights.","Since edamame could be eaten, the cafeteria workers naturally assumed that soy milk made from fresh beans would be perfectly safe to drink as well.","None of them had ever used fresh beans to make soy milk before. They were simply taking it for granted.","It was Zeng Qiang who ran over to the cafeteria to confirm that they were planning to make soy milk and gave them a quick lesson.","âYou could get poisoned.â","Fresh soybeans contained trypsin inhibitors and phytohemagglutinin. Unless they were kept at a rolling boil for eight to ten minutes, they could cause food poisoning.","Fresh soybeans also contained a lot of saponins. When heated, they produced so much foam that it looked as though the liquid were boiling, which could be very deceptive. It was a false boil.","Anyone who didnât know that might assume the beans had boiled long enough.","The older cook was rather stubborn and refused to believe it. He insisted on trying it for himself.","He boiled a small pot and drank some. Zeng Qiang didnât stop him, only saying, âDonât drink too much.â","It wouldnât be fatal, after allâjust nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea. The old man made several trips to the bathroom before he was finally convinced.","He couldnât help with making the steamed buns that evening and went home early, clutching his stomach.","The next morning, the aunties were extremely careful while preparing the soy milk. Following Zeng Qiangâs instructions, they made sure to bring it to a thorough boil.","Zeng Qiang had gotten up especially early to come over and supervise.","Later, everyone else woke up and gradually arrived for breakfast. Each person held a bowl of soy milk, sipping noisily and happily.","Zeng Qiang walked out of the clubhouse with his hands clasped behind his back and looked up at the deep blue autumn sky and the snow-white clouds.","He sighed.","âThe truly skilled leave no spectacular victories behind.â","Farmers had always been this way."]},{"number":140,"title":"Chapter 140: 0140","paragraphs":["The solution to the soybean problem was actually quite simple.","They could have just asked the cafeteria workers to dry the beans in the sun.","But there was an even easier way. Zeng Qiang told Song Jingshuo, âJust let them ripen completely and dry out on their own.â","Song Jingshuo had never tried anything like that before, but when he did, it actually worked.","The pods visibly turned yellow and brittle. Shake one, and the beans inside rattled.","Zeng Qiang sighed. âThat was fast.â","In ordinary circumstances, it took twelve to twenty days for soybeans to go from their plumpest stage of ripeness to the point where the pods and beans had dehydrated and hardened.","With a superpower, it took only a few minutes.","The team gathered again and headed out.","For some reason, everyone had started killing zombies with the weary air of people clocking in at work.","Gao Yuxuan and Guo Jun had given up the two suits of full-body metal armor, which were inconvenient to move around in. They had put their regular armor back on.","Those who remained in the neighborhood waved goodbye to the team, but they were hardly idle themselves.","There was no dedicated cleaning staff anymore, so sanitation within the neighborhood had been assigned among the residents who were not part of the team.","Everyone was registered now. Song Jingshuo had the roster and had drawn up a work schedule.","Some residents swept the courtyards. Others hauled away garbage, accompanied by earth-type superpowered individuals. They took it to the street-side park outside the west gate, opened up the soil, dumped the garbage in, and buried it.","Song Jingshuo rose from his vegetable plot and gazed across the fairly clean and orderly courtyards of the neighborhood. A thought suddenly occurred to him.","Maybe living like this forever wouldnât be so bad.","He asked Zeng Qiang, âHave I gone crazy?â","Where were his promotion, his raise, his luxury apartment? Where was the life that was supposed to rise steadily toward its peak?","Zeng Qiang had now become Song Jingshuoâs regular work partnerâa senior agricultural technology specialist.","He crouched in the field and chuckled.","The schools and kindergartens had been listed as the top priority. Clearing them out and rescuing survivors had put everyoneâs minds at ease.","Today, they began patrolling the residential areas.","Overall, there were very few zombies in the residential district.","Any scattered zombies they encountered on the streets were dealt with along the way.","Most of the residential compounds had already cleared out the zombies within their own walls over the past few days.","The situation in each compound was much like that of Auspicious Garden: the vast majority of residents were elderly.","They also ran into the students rescued from Gaoxin Middle School two days earlier.","Wearing the metal armor donated by Cui Haiyang and the others and carrying weapons, the students became excited when they saw the familiar 535 truck and ran over.","âItâs you guys! What are you doing here?â","It had only been a day since they last met, yet it felt like they had been apart for ages.","Jiang Cheng told them that several residential compounds had joined together to establish the High-Tech District Provisional Government.","The students immediately began talking over one another.","âOur neighborhood wants to join too!â","In practice, though, it would be rather inconvenient. This group of neighborhoods was some distance away from theirs.","The children said, âWe have bicycles! We want to join the team!â","Jiang Cheng neither agreed outright nor rejected them bluntly. Instead, she said, âFirst, get your own neighborhood organized. Choose someone to take charge. Are there any adults managing things right now?â","At that, the students grew indignant.","The population structure of this compound was similar to that of Auspicious Garden. But its current situation was closer to that of Imperial View Gardenâin other words, no one had stepped up to take the lead.","Imperial View Garden was close to Youth Apartments and Auspicious Garden. Thanks to the influence of those two communities, someone had at least been willing to shoulder the responsibility there. They had joined the High-Tech District Provisional Government and managed to keep up with everyone else.","But in this compound, the few able-bodied adults had quickly realized that if they took charge, they would become responsible for all the elderly residents.","The elderly were seen as a burden.","No young adults were willing to step forward. After looting the nearby convenience supermarkets and stocking up on enough supplies, everyone simply shut their doors and settled into living on their own.","In the end, it was the elderly who took matters in hand.","When the children came back and found that their parents were gone, it was the elderly who organized things and cooked for them.","More than twenty children, armed and wearing armor, took on the responsibility of clearing out the zombies. They hunted down every zombie lurking in corners or locked inside rooms throughout the compound.","The old and the young clung to one another for warmth and support.","Jiang Cheng nodded. âIf the adults wonât take charge, then you do it. Consider yourselves adults.â","The students tightened their grips on their weapons and nodded hard.","âOkay!â","Most of the elderly had no armor, and their weapons were little more than kitchen knives and the like.","After counting the residents, Cui Haiyang brought metal-type superpowered individuals over to make armor on the spot.","The goal was to ensure that everyone had armor and everyone had a weapon.","That way, everyone could fightâor at the very least, protect themselves. The High-Tech District team would not need to spare people to protect them.","Jiang Cheng told them, âGet the neighborhood organized. Your main priorities are sanitation and security. Either elect a general leader or establish a committee to manage things collectively. You also need to appoint someone to maintain contact with us. Can you get online? The specific contact information is posted on our neighborhoodâs residentsâ forum. We have a dedicated thread open to everyone. Youâll know it when you see it.â","âDoes your neighborhood have a wood-type superpowered person who can provide a steady supply of food? If not, contact us and weâll find a way to help.â","Jiang Cheng could sense that she herself had changed.","Two months ago, she might have helped the neighboring Auspicious Garden at most. After all, it was close by, and the two communities depended on each other.","Back then, supplies had been scarce. She had insisted on an exchange of benefits for everything and absolutely refused to do anything for free.","But things were different now.","Was it because they still had plenty of supplies?","When the government she had admired so much failed to appear again, and when she decided to shoulder the banner of âgovernmentâ herself, all her logic and principles had changed.","Responsibility had come crashing down on her.","It was heavy.","But that was all right. She could carry it.","And it was interesting.","She was a time-traveler, after all. She wanted to see how far she could go in this world.","The students looked as if they had been injected with a shot of strength. The light in their eyes shone even brighter.","It was hard to believe that these children had all lost their parents.","And yet they were still so strong. They held their weapons and smiled.","Everyone climbed into the vehicles, preparing to head to the next neighborhood.","Someone said, âIâll call them first.â","They had classmates there. After returning two days earlier and clearing out the zombies in their own neighborhood, the students had also managed to get in touch with them.","The students did not have cell phones. Phones had not yet become common enough for everyone to own one. At most, college students might have them. Middle school students generally did not.","But they knew how to use the communication software Jiang Cheng and the others relied on, so they could stay in contact with their classmates.","Afterward, they found several phones in the neighborhood.","That gave everyone a way to contact one another.","âXu Enâs mother is in charge over there now,â one student said. âSheâs pretty capable.â","Apart from Wang Yunyaâs mother, Xiao Dan, there had been several other parents at the school that day. Xu Enâs mother was one of them.","Those parents had all shown courage and a willingness to take responsibility.","Unfortunately, this neighborhood had no one like that.","By the time the convoy arrived, Xu Enâs mother was already leading a group of people outside.","âOur neighborhood doesnât have any zombies left,â she said.","She was astonished to hear that Youth Apartments had taken the lead in establishing the High-Tech District Provisional Government.","She looked a little lost.","âAre there really no officials left in our development district government? Itâs completely gone?â","âNothing else.â Jiang Cheng glanced at the time. âWe finished much sooner than expected today. Next, weâll check Deqingli and Shanshui Yayuan. Depending on how things look over there, if we have time this afternoon, weâll go take a look at the Development Zone government offices.â","Xu Enâs mother asked a few questions about the situation, then fell silent in thought for a moment.","Xu En was a boy with a faint fuzz of hair on his upper lip. He, too, wore silver metal armor, and he was an earth-type esper.","He called out, âMom!â","After looking at each other for a moment, his mother finally nodded. Turning back to Jiang Cheng, she said, âLet my boy join you too.â","Xu Enâs mother had already taken charge of managing the residential complex, which was excellent.","And Xu En was an esper. Jiang Cheng jerked his chin toward the large buses. âGet on!â","Xu En was a little excited. âWhich bus is the cat on?â","Everyone laughed. âThat one.â","Xu En boarded the bus Mo Li was on and became a member of the temporary governmentâs zombie-clearing squad in the New Technology District.","As soon as he got on, he saw Wang Yunya. âYouâre here too?â","Wang Yunya grinned. âHee-hee.â","The people of Deqingli still remembered Jiang Cheng.","They had been hoping for the government to come, never expecting that Jiang Cheng would be the one to arrive instead.","Four large buses rolled in. Everyone wore armor and carried standard-issue weapons, giving the whole group an imposing air.","The people of Deqingli immediately regarded them as their salvation and rushed to ask for help.","âThere are two zombies!â","âThese zombies have actually developed some intelligence. They can run!â","âWeâve been trying to catch them for days, but theyâre too fast.â","âWeâve dealt with all the other zombies. These are the only two we canât catch. Now nobody dares go outside alone.â","No one knew where the two zombies were lying in wait. Several people who had gone out alone had been attacked and eaten. Those zombies had been dealt with, but the two culprits still couldnât be caught.","It was driving everyone crazy.","If someone had told them this two months ago, they would have found it hard to believe. Even the elderly were no longer afraid of zombies.","A few sets of armor had completely turned the tables.","Humanity had started chasing zombies instead.","People really were astonishingly adaptable.","From the sound of it, these two were third-generation zombies. They had developed intelligence.","Li Jiangbing hoisted his crescent shovel onto his shoulder and shouted toward the bus, âWeâve got work!â","âBrother Zhou, quit dozing off and wake up! Itâs your turn to work!â","âLittle Huang, yes, you too.â","âOh, look at our Mo Li! Heâs already darting outâhe knows thereâs work to do, huh? Wow, youâve gotten so big! So cute, so cute, so cute!â","Spring made people sleepy, and autumn made people sluggish. Zhou Wang was suffering from the autumn version. Rubbing his eyes, he got off the bus.","First, he stretched lazily. Then he bent to the left, bent to the right, twisted backward to the left, and then twisted backward to the right.","After that, he stretched his legs.","Li Jiangbing was speechless.","Zhou Wang complained, âThese lousy bus seats are killing my back and my ass.â","âDonât you carry your own cushion?â","âItâs still uncomfortable. I canât stretch my legs out, and sitting all scrunched up is miserable.â","Zhou Wang was a successful middle-aged professional with a private car. He hadnât ridden a bus in many years.","This was torture.","Once he had stretched enough, he took a breath, and the air currents began to gather around him.","With a whoosh, he vanished.","Deqingli was a truly enormous residential complex.","Unlike commercial developments such as Jixiang Jiayuan and Yujing Xiangyuan, which consisted of only a few buildings, Deqingli occupied a vast area.","Little Huang wasnât as fast as Mo Li or Zhou Wang, so he borrowed a bicycle from the residents and rode around the complex.","The people of Deqingli were left speechless.","This wasnât how they had imagined things would go.","They had pictured four busloads of people splitting into teams, wearing armor and carrying weapons, their faces stern as they conducted a thorough, methodical search of the complex.","Instead, they got a middle-aged office worker, a junior-high-school boy, andâ¦ was that a cat or a leopard?","Before long, the black cat that had previously been the size of a leopard returned in a form as large as an elephant.","It had a zombie clenched in its jaws.","At that size, carrying one didnât hinder its movements.","In its leopard-sized form, the zombie would have been dragged along the ground. It generally used that form inside buildings, where agility was more important.","As for its maximum size?","That form was mainly for making a dramatic entrance.","After waiting a while longer, everyone began to get bored. Some people had even started dozing off.","Several students from Deqingli were catching up with Xu En and Wang Yunya, telling each other about everything that had happened during the past two days since they had parted.","Suddenly, Little Huangâs voice rang out in the distance.","âAaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaahâ!â","Everyone sprang to their feet!","Had Little Huang run into danger?","But then they thought about it and realized that couldnât be right. Little Huangâs superpower was avoiding danger.","He was a young powerhouse who could move through a horde of zombies as easily as walking through an empty street.","Everyone was baffled."]},{"number":141,"title":"Chapter 141: 0141","paragraphs":["That cry came rushing closer, fast as the wind, and then swept in with a gust.","Little Huang was riding a bicycle, but the pedals werenât taking any pressure at all.","Anyone who has ridden a bicycle knows that when the pedals offer no resistance, pedaling feels strangely weightless. It means the bicycle has gone out of control.","Too fast!","Because Zhou Wang was pushing from behind.","The bicycle was completely beyond Little Huangâs control. It was thrilling, like riding a roller coaster. Even someone as steady as Little Huang couldnât stop himself from yelling.","When the bike stopped in front of them, Little Huang planted his foot on the ground, yet he still felt a little light-headed. His heart was pounding.","âUncle.â Little Huang took a deep breath. âLetâs not do that again.â","Zhou Wang pointed at him from a distance. âYou need more practice.â","How was he supposed to practice? By taking the stairs instead of the elevator and jumping straight out of the building like you, Uncle?","Their leader was getting on in years and had started doing extreme sports!","A zombie corpse was strapped to the bicycleâs rear seat.","Zhou Wang called out to the people from Deqingli, âTake a look. Is this the one?â","Before becoming zombies, zombies had all been human. Humans had faces, so although a zombieâs skin changed color, it could still be identified by its features.","The people from Deqingli confirmed it. âThatâs him.â","With both major threats dealt with, the people of Deqingli finally relaxed.","Jiang Cheng spoke with them for a while and confirmed that there were no other zombies left in Deqingli.","The residential complex was huge, so it was normal if one or two people happened to be locked inside their homes.","The people of Deqingli said, âAs long as they arenât the kind that can run around and think like humans, weâll deal with them ourselves.â","Everyone still remembered what Deqingli had done back then.","After the zombie disaster ended, the people from Shanshui Yayuan had gone to the police and reported them, resulting in the arrest of quite a few people.","Those arrested were the direct perpetrators. But in reality, the incident had been a collective action. That meant everyone had taken part.","Even those who hadnât personally lifted a hand had undergone a complete change psychologically during that incident.","Everyone in the complex had developed a fierce streak, even the elderly.","They all carried the attitude of, âWorst comes to worst, Iâll die,â and, âIf you want me dead, Iâll take you down with me.â","Jiang Cheng had originally planned to visit Shanshui Yayuan next, since it was right next door.","But the people of Deqingli waved it off. âThereâs no need. Their complex is empty.â","Everyone was stunned.","Shanshui Yayuan had originally been a low-density villa community, with far fewer residents.","The zombie virus outbreak had killed some of them.","The massacre at Deqingli had killed another group.","Those who survived until the disaster ended had all reported the incident to the authorities and then moved away.","The houses couldnât even be sold after being listed. Nearly every development had suffered deaths, but not all deaths were the same.","Shanshui Yayuan was unquestionably a haunted housing complex.","The people of Deqingli explained, âTheir property management company pulled out, and then zombies showed up again.â","Even the property management company had withdrawn. The entire complex was now completely empty.","In that case, there was no need to go to Shanshui Yayuan. It was about time for lunch.","They parked the vehicle by the roadside.","Aunt Pan set up a stove on the spot. Its firebox was connected, with eight burners in all.","The steamers and roasting racks had been prepared in advance, polished to a gleaming silver. They had been stored in Jiang Chengâs spatial ability, along with the steamed buns and flower rolls, which had already been arranged and packed away.","Now Jiang Cheng took everything out and set it on the stove.","The fire-element ability users sent flames roaring forth. Five burners were used for steaming, and three for roasting.","They had counted everyoneâs preferences beforehand, and more people had wanted steamed food.","In any case, everyone took what they wanted and got to eat hot steamed buns and flower rolls.","Autumn really did make people sleepy.","After everyone had eaten their fill, Jiang Cheng gave them some time. âRest for half an hour. Take a nap.â","The vehicle was soon filled with sleeping people. Some were even snoring.","They slept until the alarms they had set on their phones went off. All sorts of polyphonic ringtones rang out together.","Jiang Cheng opened his eyes as well.","Half an hour of sleep had done a good job of restoring everyoneâs energy.","Everyone stretched.","Jiang Cheng walked to the front of the vehicle and said to the driver, âLetâs go. Weâre heading to the Development Zone Government offices.â","The Development Zone Government offices were a place they had to visit.","After surveying the residential areas in the eastern district, Jiang Cheng had even abandoned plans to visit the western district for the time being, choosing instead to prioritize the Development Zone Government offices.","There were still people who refused to believe that the government had truly vanished. They had to see it with their own eyes.","So they would go and see.","The Development Zone Government offices were crawling with zombies, making the place an ideal training ground for everyone.","Supernatural abilities grew stronger with practice.","The vehicle drove on, gradually leaving the residential complexes behind. Before long, they saw the Bailiang River.","The Development Zone Government offices, which managed the entire High-Tech New District, stood beside the river.","The grounds were spacious, and the five-story building was square and symmetrical. Even from a distance, its design clearly marked it as a government building.","Everyone put away their relaxed expressions and straightened up.","This was different from the other places they had visited. It wasnât merely a matter of clearing out zombies.","Although they called themselves a provisional government, many people still felt, deep down, that they were just an unofficial ragtag outfit. They were still hoping that the legitimate government would emerge and take charge.","The people of this country had an almost unimaginable devotion to the idea of legitimacy. It had been that way since ancient times.","Little Huang stared fixedly at the building.","Zhou Wang looked at the building, then at Little Huang beside him. He leaned closer and whispered, âHow about you stay in the vehicleâ¦â","Little Huang turned his head. âIâm fine, Uncle. Iâm fine.â","He gazed at the building as it drew closer and closer.","When they were almost at the entrance, Little Huang said softly, âIf we run into her later, Uncle, donât attack. Let me handle her.â","Zhou Wang placed a hand on the back of Little Huangâs head and rubbed it hard.","Their established battle formation was activated. Dao Cart and Mo Li went in first.","The zombies surged out.","Once most of them had been killed, the members of the battle team charged inside as well.","Today, Gao Yuxuan was going to conduct another experiment.","One of the most important guiding principles in Gao Yuxuanâs work was cost-effectiveness.","If something had excellent performance but cost too much, making it poor value for money, then he would still abandon it.","That way of thinking had taken root in his mind.","When people saw an electrical ability, they naturally assumed it should become an offensive power, like fire or metal abilities.","Gao Yuxuan had always felt that this wasnât cost-effective.","Yesterdayâs experiment hadnât been particularly successful, but it had given him inspiration. Who said electrical abilities had to be offensive?","Why couldnât they be support abilities instead?","He always carried an electric pen with him. Yesterday, he had already measured several sets of data.","After weighing everything, he chose what he considered the most cost-effective output level.","Today, he had basically brought the problem of accidentally leaking electricity under control. Charging himself with high-voltage electricity had been a little reckless, but it had genuinely worked. His supernatural ability was now much stronger than before.","He could fire several streams of electricity simultaneously, even weaving them into a net.","He controlled his output strictly according to the data he had measured. At this level, the electricity could no longer paralyze zombies as it had the day before. However, it still disrupted the activity of their brains.","The result was a loss of coordination and reduced speed.","The ordinary zombies tripped over themselves and fell outright.","The second-generation zombies were clearly suffering from impaired coordination as well, their movements becoming sluggish.","Game skill: ControlâSlow.","Because his supernatural ability had grown so much stronger, Gao Yuxuan could now slow an entire group with a single move.","This technique was especially useful inside buildings.","As soon as they entered the corridor, the zombies came charging toward them in a tightly packed mass.","Skill activated: ControlâSlow.","Li Jiangbing immediately led a group of people forward and launched into a wild assault with their shovels.","The combination was highly efficientâand much safer.","Gao Yuxuan tirelessly studied their abilities, and finally figured out the most cost-effective way to combine their attacks.","Su Yu had also worked out a new way to use her superpower: domains.","After advancing and upgrading, her superpower could cover a much larger area than before, and she could control its shape at will.","She enclosed all her teammates in the barrier and led them into the corridor. Then she expanded the barrier to match the shape of the corridor.","Not only did it crush the zombies in the corridor against the walls, it also blocked the zombies inside the offices at their doorways, keeping them from getting out.","The zombies frantically slapped at the protective barrier blocking their path.","Once the people inside the barrier reached an office doorway, they used a few shovelfuls to chop the heads off the zombies packed together there.","Their efficiency might not have matched that of Li Jiangbing or Gao Yuxuanâs team, but their safety was unquestionably second to none.","Aunt Pan and Zhao Yi had also developed a new skill: interception.","The two of them pressed their hands against the wall, and the smooth surface began to ripple like waves.","Before long, horizontal âfencesâ extended from the wall, dividing sections of the corridor into several prison cells. The zombies were trapped inside.","They cleared the corridor one section at a time, retracting each section of âfenceâ after the zombies inside had been dealt with.","Their efficiency was nothing special, but they had the advantage of being very safe.","Speaking of which, this wave of enthusiasm for developing practical methods of using superpowers had all been sparked by Gao Yuxuan.","Zhao Yi leaned more toward theory. He liked studying the origins of superpowers and the reasons behind the emergence of their various branches.","Gao Yuxuan preferred to explore more practical techniques.","By the time they finished clearing out the government building, it was already past four in the afternoon.","Jiang Cheng was in the district chiefâs office.","The district chief was the head of the development zoneâs government. Since the development zone was wealthy, his office was spacious and imposing.","Behind the desk and office chair stood an entire wall of bookshelves, filled with many weighty tomes.","Jiang Cheng narrowed her eyes and studied them for a moment before walking over. She extended a fingertip and slowly ran it along the spines of the books.","Many of these books were renowned works. They embodied the mainstream values and worldview of the country and formed the theoretical foundation upon which it had been established.","With âJiang Chengâsâ memories, Jiang Cheng of course knew how important these books wereâworks such as Xxxxx Thought and the Xxx Quotations.","But âJiang Chengâ had never truly read those imposing volumes. She had merely learned some general summaries of their ideas at school.","When Jiang Chengâs fingertip reached the most important works, those books vanished into thin air.","The building had five floors. Although there was an elevator, there was no need to crowd inside it.","People on each floor simply threw the zombie corpses out of the windows and into the courtyard.","Down below, Zhou Wang used a layer of air currents to catch the falling corpses and slow their descent, preventing zombie fluids from splattering everywhere when they hit the ground.","Little Huang had been using his eyes to search the entire time, but he still hadnât found his mother by the end. After all, with so many heads crammed together, there was no way to lift them one by one for a closer look.","They dealt with the bodies by burying them on the spot.","Aunt Pan, Zhao Yi, and several other earth-type superpowered individuals worked together to dig an enormous, extremely deep pit in the middle of the courtyard.","If it was deep enough, there would be no need to disinfect the area separately.","Although supplies were currently abundant, that was only because there were so few survivors. No new supplies were coming in at the moment, so they still had to conserve whatever they could.","When the pit had been filled in again, Zhou Wang glanced secretly at Little Huang.","But Little Huang was remarkably calm.","It was the adults who seemed grief-stricken. Many of them had finally accepted the fact that there were no survivors in the development zoneâs government building.","Jiang Cheng stood on the steps at the entrance, watching everyone finish up.","Suddenly, someone approached her.","Jiang Cheng turned her head. It was Zhao Yi.","âThere isnât a single person,â Zhao Yi said. âWe checked everywhere, including the underground cafeteria and the civil-defense shelter. Not one survivor.â","From a probabilistic standpoint, it made no sense.","There had been survivors in the middle schools.","There had been survivors in the elementary schools.","Yet in such a large government building, there wasnât a single one.","Jiang Cheng said, âI told you from the beginning.â","She had said that an outside force had specifically targeted the government for elimination.","Zhao Yi was now inclined to accept that conclusion.","But he still challenged her. âJiang Cheng, how did you come up with the idea of a targeted purge?â","The conclusion was far too specific.","It was difficult for anyone to reach a correct judgment based on such a small sample sizeâunless she had concealed some of her observations, or possessed other information that no one else knew.","Deep down, Zhao Yi vaguely felt that Jiang Cheng definitely knew something others did not.","After all, the Chosen Protagonist couldnât possibly be that simple. She must be keeping something in reserve.","For example, she had hidden the fact that her physique had been enhanced and that she had become stronger.","Or she had concealed Mo Liâs mutation.","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan had searched online for keywords related to animals becoming infected or mutating. In the process, they discovered a post on another forum in which someone had asked whether animals could mutate.","Gao Yuxuan had minored in computer science and was a top student.","He precisely traced the posterâs network address to S City, the Technology New District, Youth Apartments, Building Two.","The post had been published on June 19.","That early. So very early.","Jiang Cheng had kept Mo Li hidden until the Cao family tried to seize power, only then bringing Mo Li out into the open.","But that was fine. The Chosen Protagonist was supposed to be this incredible.","Both Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan accepted it. In fact, they were delighted by it, feeling that it was only fitting for her.","But Zhao Yi truly wanted them to share information. He desperately wanted to know what exactly Jiang Cheng knew that no one else did.","Of course, there was no way Jiang Cheng could tell him the truth.","She gazed at the people busying themselves in the courtyard and said only, âA womanâs intuition.â","I, a memory-lost person, did not cross into another world of my own volition.","Someoneâor some forceâmust have sent me here.","That force clearly possessed the ability to kill me, yet chose to let me live.","It made me face a world suffering from a zombie outbreak.","Clearly, this was a test or trial meant for me.","The first time, I won.","But the trial was not over. Clearly, my opponent had no intention of letting me win.","So the government, which had played such a major role in the first stage, was specifically wiped out.","Because only by doing thisâ","could the second stageâ","increase in difficulty."]},{"number":142,"title":"Chapter 142: 0142","paragraphs":["On the way back, they first dropped Xu En off, then went to refuel the car.","The gas station had already been cleaned out the last time they came for fuel.","Someone brought up the issue of how much gas they had left. âHow long will it last?â","There was no solution to that.","For now, the collective power of the group was enough to unite everyone and seize a place to survive. They could even use their supernatural abilities to grow foodâprovided land resources were inexhaustible.","But fuel for vehicles was beyond their abilities.","Fortunately, hardly anyone in the Technology Development Zone drove anymore, and the gas station was used only by them. Their fuel consumption was still relatively low.","When they returned to the residential compound, however, they saw an unexpected visitor.","Brother Dong was squatting beside the vegetable plots, chatting with Zeng Qiang.","When he saw everyone come back, Brother Dong slowly stood up. âYo, your equipmentâs all been upgraded. Not bad, not bad.â","Everyone was surprised. âWhat are you doing here?â","Jiang Cheng asked, âHow are things at home?â","âSame as ever,â Brother Dong said.","What exactly did âsame as everâ mean?","Brother Dong had come alone. If there had been anyone left at home, he would never have traveled all the way to the Technology Development Zone by himself.","His chin was clean-shaven, clearly shaved only recently, but his eye sockets were deeply sunken. His whole person seemed to carry an air of lifelessness.","Everyone understood.","Brother Dong hadnât been as lucky this time as he had been before.","He had lost his phone and couldnât contact his family, so heâd asked Cui Haiyang, Gao Yuxuan, Guo Jun, and the others to help him get a vehicle. He drove back home, smashing through the zombies along the way.","But when he arrived, there were four zombies standing neatly in the courtyard.","His father, his mother, his wife, and his child.","Brother Dong had killed them all, dug a large pit in the yard, buried them together, and raised a mound over the grave.","What was he supposed to do next? Keep living, of course.","After checking the house, he found that it was stocked with a considerable amount of rice, flour, cooking oil, and other supplies. A newly purchased chest freezer was packed full of meat.","His mother had planted vegetables in the yard, and they were growing lush and green.","He could easily hide there alone and live like he was in a secluded paradise.","And that was exactly what Brother Dong had done.","Until today, when he didnât wake up until almost noon. He opened his eyes and stared at the ceiling for who knew how long.","Then he got up and looked in the mirror. The man in the reflection had a scruffy beard and deeply sunken eyes.","He looked neither human nor ghost.","Brother Dong realized that he couldnât live that kind of solitary life.","He had to live alongside other survivors. He needed the presence of other people.","After shaving, Brother Dong got into his car. He thought for a while, then drove to the Technology Development Zone to seek refuge with them.","âI didnât come empty-handed,â Brother Dong said. âMy car is packed with rice, flour, cooking oil, and other supplies. I brought over as much as I could.â","He was a despicable, treacherous man.","The young people at Youth Apartments had a clear sense of love and hate. Nobody liked himâeven though he was a powerful ability user.","Jiang Cheng looked toward Zhou Wang.","Zhou Wang went over and patted Brother Dong on the back. âCome on. Come with me.â","Brother Dong joined Auspicious Garden.","Before dinner, they held a meeting to discuss the situation at the Development Zone government offices.","The mood was bleak.","âLetâs go into the city and take a look.â","âSee how things are at City Hall.â","Everyone said the same thing. In the end, they still couldnât bring themselves to give up hope.","Even now, there had been no word from the television at all.","âAll right. Tomorrow weâll make a circuit through the western district first,â Jiang Cheng agreed. âThen weâll head into the city.â","âAunts, Iâm afraid weâll have to trouble you to prepare tomorrowâs lunch.â","âAnyone whoâs free can go help out in the cafeteria.â","After dinner, many people strolled around the courtyard.","Strawberries hung from the plants in the strawberry field, and anyone who wanted some could pick them whenever they liked.","A small apple tree had also appeared in the compound. It was short, with fruit hanging all over it. There were no pesticides, so the apples could be picked and eaten straight away.","But they were nowhere near as popular as the strawberries. Most of the people wandering around had a strawberry in hand.","Recently, a new group of lunatics had appeared in the compound: the pet owners.","Their main symptom was muttering endlessly at their animals.","âWhen are you finally going to transform?â","âIâm not asking for anything huge. Just transform a little so I can see what you look like.â","Some people even carried their female cats over to Mo Li.","âMate with mine, mate with mine! Sheâs beautiful.â","Two female-cat owners spat at each other over whose âdaughterâ was prettier.","Mo Li was driven to distraction. With a whoosh, she vanished.","Jiang Cheng was at home, reclining in a comfortable chair. A tall stack of books was piled on the floor beside her.","They were all weighty tomes she had helped herself to from the district government offices that day.","As society had grown prosperous, it had also become increasingly restless and superficial. Young people found it difficult to sit down and read books like these.","But Jiang Cheng had managed to get through them.","As someone from another world, she found them completely absorbing.","Everyone slept quite well that night. The zombies in the Technology Development Zone were becoming fewer and fewer as they were cleared out. Deep down, everyone knew that there were hardly any zombies left in the surrounding area. They also knew that with a beast like Mo Li guarding the compound, even a cunning third-generation zombie couldnât get in.","It was extremely safe.","They were well fed, had plenty to drink, and even got fruit after meals.","A house, food, and drinkâwasnât that all anyone really wanted out of life?","They slept soundly.","Who could have guessed that when they got up and went downstairs the next morning, they would find water covering part of the compound?","An underground pipe had burst.","Everyoneâs first thought was, What a headache. This would require a professional to repair, and where were they going to find a professional worker now?","But then they realized something.","That way of thinking belonged to the old world. Things had changed.","Several earth-element ability users got down on their knees and crawled around, searching. It didnât take long before they found the spot.","âItâs here! Itâs underneath me!â","Once they had located it, all that remained was to dig.","Many people brought out bowls of hot porridge and ate it with pickled vegetables while watching the ability users repair the water pipe.","They broke up the paving bricks and dug into the soil. Then, suddenly, a column of water shot into the sky!","Li Jiangbing hurried over and brought it under control.","The water that had already sprayed out condensed into a huge ball floating in midair, while Li Jiangbing forcibly controlled the water still inside the pipe.","âDamn it, hurry up! This pipeâs got some serious pressure!â Li Jiangbing shouted.","Of course the pressure in the main line was immense.","Someone called out, âShut off the water valve! The main valve!â","The idea was sound. The problem was, who knew where the main valve was?","Manager Wang didnât know. He was the manager.","Little Fang didnât know either. He was only a security guard.","Even Aunt Pan didnât know. She handled the cooking.","Yang Xinyan was even less likely to know. She was just a clerical worker.","Only someone like Master Luo from the engineering department would know. But there was no one left from the engineering department.","Li Jiangbing gathered his strength and shouted, âFine! Hurry up! I can still hold it!â","Cui Haiyang jumped into the pit.","A water pipe couldnât just be made from any old piece of metal. It would rust within days.","They had to use the original material.","The fragments from the rupture had to be picked up piece by piece.","Cui Haiyang pressed his hands against the pipe and activated his ability. The fragments fused back together with the pipe.","After a while, Cui Haiyang released his hands. âAll right. Try it.â","Li Jiangbing withdrew his power, and the water in the pipe began flowing normally again.","Cui Haiyang climbed out of the pit and had Li Jiangbing give him some water to wash his hands.","Aunt Pan and several others refilled the hole with soil and put the paving bricks back in place. They added just the right amount of dirt, leaving not even a trace of loose soil. The area looked as clean as if it had just been swept.","Jiang Cheng came over to ask what had happened.","Cui Haiyang said, âThink of it this way: there wasnât enough of this particular color of paint, so I borrowed some from the more concentrated color beside it and spread it over. It looks about the same, but in reality, the whole thing has been diluted.â","That was the problem.","They had no way to restock the gas station.","Nor could they replace the pipes beneath their feet.","Their superpowers could patch things up here and there, but they couldnât solve the fundamental problems.","Despite a minor incident that morning, the team still set out on time.","Xu En arrived early on his bicycle, and two children from another neighborhood came with him.","They had all been told to take care of their own neighborhood first.","The children stuck out their chins and declared, âWeâre superpowered too! Xu En joined, so we want to join as well!â","âIf you donât let us go, weâll ride our bikes and follow you!â","Their fearless, stubborn refusal to listen made everyone at the Youth Apartments suddenly realize that they were getting old.","Wang Yunya said nothing. Little Huang shot her a glance.","Little Huang and Wang Yunya were neighbors in the same residential complex, though Little Huang attended a prestigious middle school downtown.","Xu En and the others were Wang Yunyaâs classmates.","That guilty look on Wang Yunyaâs face made it obvious she had known about this since last night. She had either failed to stop themâor hadnât tried very hard. More likely, she was an accomplice herself.","The children made Jiang Cheng laugh. âAll right, get on.â","âHave you eaten breakfast?â","âHere, have a steamed bun!â","âDrink a bowl of porridge before you go. Weâve got some hard labor ahead of us.â","The adults all started feeding them.","The two children had snuck out without telling the elderly people in their neighborhood, and they really hadnât eaten anything.","They wolfed down the food with loud slurps, clearly enjoying it, and even took two steamed buns with them before boarding the vehicle.","They were at that age when growing boys could eat a family out of house and home.","The western district of the New Technology Zone was filled with newly built apartment complexes, most of them with very low occupancy rates.","As the vehicles drove through, they saw only a few scattered zombies and almost failed to find any living people.","At last, they found a young couple who had moved in just after the previous disaster.","âWeâd planned to move in June, but then the zombie outbreak happened and delayed us for several months. At least it gave the new apartment a few extra months to air out.â","âThat day, he happened to take the day off to go with me to my prenatal checkup, so we were home. We were really lucky.â","As the young wife spoke, her face filled with the sense of lifeâs unpredictability and the gratitude of having survived a catastrophe.","âBoth our parents are gone. Now itâs just the two of us left in this world.â","âWe just hope the baby can be born safely.â","Everyone looked at her belly, feeling dazed.","There were hardly any children left to be seen. The youngest people around them were elementary school students.","They truly couldnât see any babies anymore.","Jiang Cheng asked, âWould you like to move in with us?â","The western districtâs commercial facilities had yet to be developed. The people who lived there had to go to the eastern district and rely on Mai Duoduo for their regular shopping.","The young couple exchanged a glance, but still declined.","âWe stocked up on a lot of supplies beforehand, like a couple of hamsters. And there really arenât many zombies around here. We hardly ever go downstairs.â","âWe feel safer here.â","âBesides, my husband has a superpower. We didnât realize so many people had powers now. Thatâs wonderful.â","The husband had an electrical ability.","The couple believed that the western district of the New Technology Zoneâwith its empty streets, homes, and foodâwas a safe haven cut off from the rest of the world, and they didnât want to leave.","Jiang Cheng didnât force them. She simply left them her contact information and told them to seek out the Youth Apartments if they ever needed help.","The couple waved goodbye and thanked them for clearing out the surrounding area. Now they could safely go downstairs.","Everyone boarded the vehicles again and continued into the city.","Someone sighed, âThereâs still going to be a child born.â","The numb acceptance ofâor perhaps indifference toâlife and death that had become so familiar suddenly cracked open, and their reverence for life began to take root again.","Li Jiangbing twisted around from the front row to speak to Jiang Cheng. âJiang Cheng, Iâd like to discuss something with you.â","âGo ahead,â Jiang Cheng said.","âI was thinking that we could take a look at the municipal government offices today, then find some time to clear out Renxin Hospital when we get back.â","âExactly!â someone immediately agreed.","There was a child on the way.","The adults wanted to see that child born safely.","Zhang Le thought even further ahead. âWe need to clear out the hospital. If she has complications and needs a C-section, I can perform it while sheâs conscious and then use my power to heal her. But she shouldnât have to endure it without pain relief. She needs anesthesia.â","Protecting a new life was what everyoneâs hearts were calling for.","Jiang Cheng smiled and agreed. âAll right.â"]},{"number":143,"title":"Chapter 143: 0143","paragraphs":["The vehicles made their way into the city. Outside the Fifth Ring Road, there were very few zombies.","Once they entered the area inside the Fifth Ring, the number of zombies gradually increased.","The 535s performed far better than ordinary buses. Once the accelerator was pressed, they shot forward like the wind.","The convoy did not stop to deal with the zombies along the road. Their main purpose in coming into the city today was simply to take âa lookâ at the municipal government offices.","The municipal government was located in the old city within the Second Ring Road.","The convoy planned to drive straight into the city center via Radiation Road.","After entering the Fourth Ring Road, there were noticeably more vehicles on the streets.","These vehicles from the Technology New District had been modified by metal-element superpowered users. Their front ends were especially reinforced against collisions. As long as they did not run into a large truck, they simply rammed forward, shoving smaller cars aside.","Even so, their speed clearly began to drop.","The zombies on the road were drawn to the commotion.","The people inside the vehicles felt a little horrified. Several of the middle school students had gone pale.","There were simply too many of them.","Even the schools and district government offices in the Technology New District had never seen zombies this densely packed.","After all, S City was a major metropolis with a population of twenty million.","The blades on the blade cars shot out and retracted in rapid succession, at an extremely high frequency. Even so, zombies still managed to slip through from time to time.","Su Yu stood up. âHow about I take care of them? The four vehicles would need to drive closer together, though.â","The vehicles were too large, and with the gaps between them, she could only cover all of them if they moved closer.","âWait for now,â Jiang Cheng said.","She pressed herself against the window and observed for a while. Then she picked up the radio.","âAll vehicles, pay attention. Try fixing the blades in place so they extend from both sides of the vehicles like wings. The front as well. Adjust the height as appropriate.â","âI was thinking the same thing!â Cui Haiyang said.","He had only just come up with the idea himself, and Jiang Cheng had said it first.","The blade cars stopped constantly shooting their blades out and pulling them back in. Instead, they grew a ring of âlittle skirts,â as though the vehicles had been fitted with bladed trim.","The âskirtsâ were half a meter wide. Their outer edges were as thin as cicada wings and razor-sharp.","This was something they had to thank Security Guard Little Wang for.","Before Young Wang had accidentally taken the wrong path while following Cao Jiacai, he had actually worked very well with the other metal-element superpowered users.","He had come from the countryside and made a living as a craftsman. He was a genuine blacksmith. His affinity with iron was even stronger than Cui Haiyangâs. In his hands, metal was truly as pliable as modeling clay.","Perhaps he could not create moving joints and connections like Cui Haiyang, but when the two of them sharpened weapons together, Young Wangâs edges were far keener.","Cui Haiyang had humbly asked him for advice.","Young Wang was just a young rural man who had come to the city to find work. Being treated like a teacher by a university student from the city left him both flattered and proud. He did not keep anything to himself and shared his feelings about using his superpowers.","The other metal-element users worked with iron every day, kneading it as if it were modeling clay. With Young Wangâs guidance, they quickly grasped the finer points.","Everyoneâs precision and control improved considerably.","Now, all four 535 buses had grown rings of blades around them, and they were incredibly sharp.","The ones chasing the vehicles were all fast second-generation zombies. They sprinted after the buses and lunged forwardâ¦","Only to have their heads sliced off.","The superpowered users inside the buses did not even need to exert themselves. The zombies were decapitated by the speed and force of their own leaps.","One short zombie lost only half its head. A taller zombie had its neck and shoulder sliced off along with its head.","The roads behind the buses were drenched in dark-brown fluid.","This was not quite like the heroic scenes the middle school students had imagined, where someone hacked off a zombieâs head or burned one to death.","Several of the students were beginning to lose it. Some stared at the ceiling, some at the floor, and some closed their eyes and muttered under their breath.","Only Little Huang remained completely calm. Sitting by the window, he watched the zombies throw themselves to their deaths like moths flying into flames, as though he were admiring the scenery.","Then Little Huang suddenly turned his head.","âWatch out.â","Two seconds after he spoke, a zombie smacked against the window.","It happened to be the window beside Xu En, who let out a terrified screech.","It was clearly a third-generation zombie. It had observed how the blades around the vehicle worked and leaped directly onto them, using the blades like steps.","It gripped the metal bars outside the window with its hands. Its pitch-black eyes stared at the living flesh inside the bus.","A flash of white light surrounded Su Yu. Her protective barrier expanded in an instant, then contracted again.","The third-generation zombie was flung away.","The middle school students had seen this protective barrier before, but even now, they still thought it was unbelievably cool.","Jiang Cheng picked up the radio.","âAdd another ring higher up.â","One after another, the four vehicles âgrewâ another ring of blades at a slightly higher level. This time, even the third-generation zombies could no longer jump onto them.","Xu En let out a long breath and sighed. âHumans really do need to use tools.â","Having a superpower made people feel pretty impressive. Dealing with one or two stray zombies was indeed no problem.","But if they were caught in the middle of this many zombies, their superpowers suddenly did not seem like enough.","They would probably be killed before they even had the chance to exhaust themselves.","Whenever a child said something, the adults laughed.","But after laughing, they felt a certain weight in their hearts. Things really were different now. The adults had been through countless battles, after all.","This was not the first time any of them had faced zombies. During the previous zombie disaster, most of these children had probably been confined to their homes and forbidden from going outside, protected by the adults the whole time.","Their experience was obviously far more limited than the adultsâ.","The vehicles, now fitted with two rings of blades, drove all the way into the Second Ring Road.","As soon as they entered the Second Ring, they passed several square, symmetrical buildings. Some belonged to bureaus, others to ministriesâall government offices.","At last, they arrived in front of the municipal government offices.","Everyone looked through the windows.","âHuh? Why is there such a huge steel gate? Iâve passed by here before. I remember it being the kind that retracts like an accordion.â","âThere is one, I think.â","âThere is. I once came here with a superior. During registration, I was bored and noticed that the gate slid to both sides during the day and only closed at night.â","âThen why is it closed during the day?â","That question hit the heart of the matter.","âThere may be people inside,â Jiang Cheng said.","A spark suddenly appeared in everyoneâs eyes.","But it could also have been closed before the people inside died.","Jiang Cheng kept that thought to herself, not wanting to dampen their spirits.","There were plenty of zombies on the road as well. Once the buses stopped, even the original zombies could lunge at them. One came, and a head fell. Another came, and another head fell.","The middle school students had become numb to it.","âCanât these zombies be a little smarter?â","âDonât tempt fate,â Li Jiangbing scolded.","Of all things, they had to wish for smarter zombies.","Mo Li had slept through most of the journey. Even when a third-generation zombie clung to the window, he merely glanced at it before going back to sleep.","Sunlight streamed through the window and fell across him. He had been sleeping wonderfully.","Now that they had reached their destination, he finally got up.","At the bus door, he stretched lazily, raising his arms high above his head.","Li Jiangbing watched him and felt that he somewhat resembled Zhou Wang.","The front of the bus was enveloped in Su Yuâs protective barrier.","Su Yu did not make it especially large. It covered only the front of the bus and the front door, creating a bit of space outside the doorway.","Superpowers were like a personâs physical strength: they could run out.","Besides, Gao Yuxuan had always been dedicated to instilling the concept of cost-effectiveness in everyone. At home, it did not matter how much energy they used during practice. Once they exhausted themselves, raising their upper limit was beneficial.","But once they were outside, they had to learn to pursue cost-effectiveness and conserve their strength.","Especially today, things in the city proper were far worse than in the Technology New District. They had to conserve their supplies and use them only where they mattered most.","As soon as the vehicle door opened, a small patch of ground outside was covered by the protective shield, forcing the zombies back.","But the instant the door opened, Mo Li shot out.","Those sitting by the door saw that, at the moment Mo Li leaped into the air, he was still a small kitten. But when they looked out through the window again, a black panther had already pierced through the protective shield and pounced into the dense horde of zombies. By the time he landed, his body had swollen to the size of an elephant.","The middle schoolers pressed themselves against the windows, squealing excitedly.","Mo Li let out a thunderous roar, like the tiger king of the mountains, like the lion king of the grasslands.","Several third-generation zombies instinctively turned and fled.","But the countless primitive and second-generation zombies could do nothing but charge forward.","Mo Li lunged into them. His body spun, his long tail lashed out, and his claws smashed through them. With a single bite, he could crush several heads at once.","In an instant, the area beside the lead vehicle was cleared.","The middle schoolers cried, âHoly crap!â","Su Yu led Cui Haiyang out of the vehicle. Cui Haiyang walked up to the gate and touched it. The huge door rolled open to both sides like an egg roll.","Sure enough, there were many zombies in the courtyard. But before they had a chance to rush out, the buses charged inside!","Anything that touched the blade-edged vehicles died instantly. They were far more efficient than the bladed cars had been at harvesting heads one by one.","There were simply too many zombies outside. The vehicles could not remain in the street.","All four buses filed inside.","Su Yu and Cui Haiyang entered as well. The egg-roll-like gate unfolded again, returning to its original shape and isolating the zombies in the streetâand Mo Liâoutside.","Mo Li rampaged through the street, killing nearly all the zombies in front of the government compound. Then he turned and leaped onto the wall. By the time he landed on top of it, he had already become a tiny black cat.","He stared down at the situation in the courtyard.","Before they got out of the vehicles, Jiang Cheng had already warned him telepathically not to get too close. The new blade-edged vehicles were different from the old ones, and approaching too closely could easily result in accidental injury.","There were quite a lot of zombies in the courtyard. Four large public buses drove in circles around the open ground, linked nose to tail. Su Yu and Cui Haiyang could not get through either, so the two of them crouched by the gate and watched, protected only by a small shield.","One of them said, âAre there any survivors?â","âProbably. Look, someone closed the gate.â","âThen Jiang Cheng was wrong.â","âWouldnât that be even better? Jiang Cheng herself hopes sheâs wrong.â","As they spoke, the weapons in their hands suddenly extended, killing the zombies that came running out of the guardhouse.","Unfortunately, Jiang Cheng had been right. There were no survivors in the municipal government building.","Just like the Development Zone government office in the Technology New District.","Not a single survivor.","Everyone had left home at seven-thirty in the morning. Clearing the western district had not taken long, and they had set out from the Technology New District for the city proper before noon.","By the time they finished clearing the municipal government complex, it was already three in the afternoon.","Everyone was starving. They truly had not been able to stop for a meal along the way.","They had not worked this hard in days.","Compared with todayâs brutal battle at the municipal government, the Technology New District had been far too easy.","This was the cityâs central administrative hub. From morning till night, countless people came here every day to handle business, collect and deliver documents, and attend meetings.","It had been an extremely busy place.","Jiang Cheng carried Vice Mayor Zhengâs head downstairs.","âHe was an excellent leader,â she said.","She paid her respects to him, then placed his head with the bodies of the other zombies.","The earth-type superpowered individuals would dispose of them all together.","The fire-type users were already heating up the food. The smell of meat pies had begun to spread, and everyone was about to die of hunger.","Gao Yuxuan planted his hands on his hips. âWho closed that gate, anyway? We thought there were survivors. What a disappointment.â","Someone else sighed. âWhat was the point of closing it?â","Inside the gate were zombies. Outside the gate were zombies too.","Across the broad courtyard, Jiang Cheng gazed from a distance at the imposing steel gates.","âBecause they couldnât see what was happening outside, and they didnât have time to think about it,â she said softly. âBut they could see what was right in front of them, and everything in front of them was zombies.â","âSo they closed the gate.â","The office door could not be shut. A zombieâs arm had gotten caught in it, wedging it open. More and more zombies were gathering outside.","Their colleagues desperately braced themselves against the door while Vice Mayor Zheng pressed the intercom number for the guardhouse.","âClose the main gateââ","âI order you to close the main gate!â","âDonât let the zombies get out!â","But they could not hold it any longer. The office door burst open, and the zombies poured inside.","Zhao Yi was beginning to want to give up thinking altogether.","The more he thought, the more terrified he became.","Jiang Cheng had been right about everything. The municipal government had also been deliberately purged.","Everyone had accepted Jiang Chengâs prophecy by now.","But how had the targeting been done?","Had more of the virus been released in the municipal government than elsewhere?","Or had some miraculous method been used?","This âtargetingâ was something one absolutely could not think too deeply about.","But Zhao Yi did not ask Jiang Cheng again.","He had a feeling that she would brush him off as usual.","She would certainly say, âHow should I know?â","That would truly be unfair to Jiang Cheng.","She did not know the exact method either.","Just as she did not know how her memories had been locked away, or how she had been sent into this world in the first place.","Everyone began eating lunch.","The meat pies were delicious, but several of the newly arrived middle schoolers could barely eat.","The images of the tall zombies they had cut apart on the wayâhearts tumbling out of their chestsâwould not leave their minds.","It had ruined their appetites.","Jiang Cheng bit into a meat pie, chewed, and swallowed.","âEat,â she said. âIf you canât eat, then donât come out with us tomorrow.â","âWe still have to fight later. You canât do that without the strength.â","Everyone stopped and looked at her.","Jiang Cheng glanced at the sky. âItâs still early. Going home now would make this trip a terrible return on investment.â","The moment she said âreturn on investment,â everyone burst out laughing.","Gao Yuxuan put his hands on his hips and thrust out his chin. âWhatâs so funny? Think about how much fuel four vehicles burn for one trip! Once itâs gone, itâs gone!â","Jiang Cheng laughed too.","When the laughter subsided, she said, âThatâs why weâre going to take back the television station.â","âIt isnât far from here. Itâs also within the Second Ring Road.â","Although one was beyond the western section of the Second Ring Road, and the other beyond the eastern section.","Well, all right."]},{"number":144,"title":"Chapter 144: 0144","paragraphs":["Everyone had eaten their fill and was dozing in the vehicles.","The middle school students slept with their heads leaning against one anotherâs shoulders.","There were plenty of zombies on the Second Ring Road too. Not a single living person could be seen outdoors.","Cui Haiyang occasionally opened his eyes to take a look. After all, the zombies chasing the vehicles would throw themselves onto the blades.","Only the driver had it hard, since he couldnât sleep at all.","When the television stationâs antenna came into view in the distance, the driver shouted at the top of his lungs, âWake up! Wake up, everyone! Weâre almost there!â","Everyone sat up, bleary-eyed.","Some hurriedly wiped the drool from their mouths.","The moment Jiang Cheng opened her eyes, she saw the television station in the distance.","This television station had a long history, and its design looked quite old-fashioned.","In fact, a new television station was already under construction on the East Fourth Ring Road. According to the schedule, the station would be able to move into the new building next year.","But now, all of that had come to a halt.","Compared with the massive steel gates of the municipal government compound, the television stationâs gates were wide open. Only the barrier arm meant to stop vehicles had been lowered.","The truck smashed through the barrier and charged inside.","Little Huang furrowed his brow and gazed up slightly at the old-fashioned television station building.","After thinking for a moment, he still issued a warning. âEveryone, be careful. I donât feel good.â","The people in the vehicle were all rather surprised.","Jiang Cheng asked, âDo you sense danger?â","Little Huang nodded.","This wasnât Little Huangâs first time going out to kill zombies. He was practically a veteran by now. He hadnât said anything when they went to the school, the district government, the urban area, or the municipal government.","This was the first time he had warned everyone.","The two new middle school students were one boy and one girl.","The boy was named Li Guxing, and the girl was named Chang Jiaxin.","Chang Jiaxin asked in a low voice, âWhatâs wrong with him?â","Wang Yunya answered quietly, âHis superpower is danger prediction.â","The newcomers suddenly understood.","Li Guxing whispered, âSeeing how amazing his footwork is, I thought he was a wind-type user.â","âWind-type users just run fast,â Wang Yunya said.","Jiang Cheng immediately notified the other vehicles over the radio. âEveryone, be careful. Little Huang senses danger! Stay alert and donât let your guard down!â","All three vehicles replied over the radio: âUnderstood!â","âWhy arenât there any zombies in this courtyard?â Zhao Yi asked.","It was true. There had been so many zombies in the government compound, so why couldnât they see any in the television stationâs courtyard?","Of course, they couldnât see any living people either.","Someone guessed, âDid they all run outside? The main gate isnât closed either.â","With only a vehicle barrier arm in place, it seemed like it would be easy for zombies to leave.","âNo.â Zhao Yi pressed against the window and looked outside. âIf they could get out, then the zombies outside should also be able to get in. The odds should be even.â","Everyone instinctively looked toward the gate. Only then did they realize, âThe zombies outside have scattered!â","The vehicles were huge and thundered loudly as they drove. Zombies were highly sensitive to sound, especially when there was so much fresh flesh and blood on board. They had all been chasing the vehicles.","That was why, at the municipal government compound, they had needed Mo Li to hold back the zombies outside. Once the convoy entered the compound, Cui Haiyang restored the steel gates to keep the zombies outside from coming in and causing trouble.","But now, the zombies that had gathered together in pursuit of the convoy had scattered.","They hadnât followed the vehicles inside, nor had they clustered around the entrance. They had simply dispersed.","Everyone exchanged glances and reminded one another, âBe careful.â","Since there were no zombies, they could get out of the vehicles directly. But Jiang Cheng still had Mo Li go down first.","Mo Li leaped out of the vehicle and transformed upon landing into a leopard the size of a large dog.","This change in size meant that there was at least no special danger nearby that differed from what they had encountered before. From that perspective, Mo Liâs perception and Little Huangâs were still distinct.","âMo Liâs perception is closer to something biological. Or we could call it physical perceptionâlike radar,â Zhao Yi summarized simply. âLittle Huangâs isâ¦ more metaphysical.â","âMore or less,â Jiang Cheng said with a nod.","Cats and dogs could sense movement or smells from a certain distance away. They could detect things before humans could hear or see them.","After Mo Li mutated, that ability had been strengthened.","Little Huangâs danger perception belonged to an entirely different system.","It was very metaphysical, almost like fortune-tellingâbut it was accurate.","âMo Li.â","Mo Li let out a âMeow~â and dashed into the television station.","A living reconnaissance unit.","âIâll go take a look,â Zhou Wang said.","He darted inside, then darted back out a moment later, his face filled with astonishment. âThere are no zombies in the lobby. Not a single one!â","Everyone looked at one another. Jiang Cheng was the first to walk toward the entrance, and the others followed one after another.","The first-floor lobby had an extremely high ceiling and was lavishly decorated.","Facing the entrance was a spacious, imposing reception desk. Corridors and security gates leading farther inside stood on either side.","There was no one behind the reception desk. The entire first-floor lobby was emptyânot a single zombie, and naturally, not a single living person either.","But the floor was covered in patches of different-colored stains.","Some were dark brown, some light brown.","They were probably a mixture of zombie blood and human blood. Zombie blood was thick and sticky, like paste, and darker in color. Even after both kinds had dried, zombie blood remained darker than human blood.","There were large swaths of discoloration, drag marks, and handprints.","It was easy to imagine the chaotic scene that had taken place here.","People screaming. Zombies tearing into them.","But where had both the people and the zombies gone?","Suddenly, loud panting came from behind them!","The people walking in front turned around one after another in astonishment.","Little Huang was panting heavily!","He sounded as if he had just finished a long-distance runâor as if he had suddenly been frightened and was suffering from an extreme stress response.","His breathing was rapid and panicked.","Jiang Cheng asked in a low voice, âLittle Huang?â","Little Huang struggled to close his open mouth and tried to breathe through his nose, but his breathing remained harsh and heavy.","After forcing himself to calm down, he said, âWait.â","He turned and walked outside. The people behind him hurriedly moved aside to let him pass.","Little Huang took one step through the entrance and reached the open space outside.","That feeling disappeared in an instant.","Little Huang steadied his breathing, then stepped back inside.","The suffocating, oppressive sense of danger instantly wrapped around him again!","Little Huang sharply inhaled.","Jiang Cheng did not urge him on, and no one else dared to make a sound.","Little Huang took two deep breaths and said, âThe moment I come in, the sense of danger increases dramatically. As soon as I go out, it gets much betterâwithin a range I can tolerate.â","Yet he was standing just inside the entrance. Going in or out was only a single step.","Zhao Yi pondered for a moment, then looked up. âThe terrain and environment.â","Everyone turned to look at him.","Gao Yuxuan let out an âAh,â clearly understanding.","Several others in the group also gradually realized what he meant. They were all young people.","Someone like Zhou Wang, a middle-aged man, was left completely baffled.","Gao Yuxuan explained to Jiang Cheng, âItâs like fighting monsters in a game. Depending on the monsterâs attack attributes, a particular area might be extremely unfavorable for the player. Usually, youâd find a way to lure the monster out into another area. Once the terrain and environment changed, theyâd favor the player instead of the monster.â","Everyone understood.","They couldnât help looking up and examining their surroundings.","Gao Yuxuan thought for a moment. âItâs probably because itâs easier to run outside, and there are vehicles. The chances of survival are higher, so the difference in perception between inside and outside is so extreme.â","That explained the huge disparity Little Huang sensed despite moving only one step.","Little Huang had calmed down by now. âSister Jiang Cheng, letâs go.â","Jiang Cheng nodded.","The group walked to the reception desk and saw the floor directory posted on the wall.","There were eleven floors in all. The very top was the equipment level, with antennas and the like.","The middle floors were office space.","The broadcasting halls and similar facilities were on the lower floors.","Everyone took the stairs up.","The stairwell doors should all have been fire doors, but now both halves of each pair lay toppled on the floor.","As they entered the stairwell, someone remarked, âItâs really wide.â","The staircase was enormousâtwice as wide as the stairwell in a youth apartment building, at least. The space was much more open as well.","When they reached the second floor, they found that the fire doors there had also all been knocked down.","Jiang Cheng frowned and paused for a moment.","Someone else noticed it too. âWas it the zombies?â","Second-generation zombies possessed tremendous strength. If these were the work of second-generation zombies, they could probably have knocked the doors down by charging into them.","But where were the zombies?","The second floor was deathly silent.","During the first zombie disaster, everyone had basically cleared out office buildings and mixed-use residential towers like this one. Back then, there had been relatively few zombies in office buildings, just as there had been few in residential buildings this time.","But this time, there was no way the office-building zombies could be so sparse.","People had been at work when the disaster struck.","A building this large should have been like the municipal or district government offices, with hordes of zombies wandering through the corridors.","Gao Yuxuan and Guo Jun were at the very front. They had shifted from the main attacking force to support roles, focusing on crowd control and slowing groups of enemies. It worked extremely well.","Once the two of them restrained the zombies, the people behind them could charge forward and coordinate their attacks.","The moment Little Huang stepped into the second-floor corridor, his breathing grew ragged. His face went pale, and sweat appeared on his forehead.","Wang Yunya was beside him and noticed that he seemed ready to collapse. She quickly grabbed his arm. âAre you all right?â","Little Huang breathed heavily. âItâs here!â","Jiang Cheng turned to look at him.","Little Huang said, âItâs on this floor!â","But no one saw anything. The corridor was completely empty.","Everyone grew suspicious and uneasy. Although they often joked that third-generation zombies were the sort that âknew to run home when it rained,â the truth was that their intelligence was somewhat greater than that.","Third-generation zombies could not only preserve their lives and escape dangerâthey could also lie in ambush and launch sneak attacks.","Deqing had been thrown into chaos by two third-generation zombies alone.","Little Huang had no way to describe what he was sensing.","Before, it had always been a sense of âdanger.â This time, it was a pure feeling of âdeath.â","Influenced by Old Huang, Little Huang had read some books on feng shui and the occult. He had a basic understanding of concepts such as life gates and death gates.","After reviewing his experiences, he had concluded that his ability to sense danger and position himself accordingly meant that every step he took landed on a life gate.","But now, he felt suffocated.","Every path ahead was a death gate.","There wasnât a single life gate.","Even if he wanted to dodge, there was nowhere to go.","But the others could not possibly turn back simply because Little Huangâs premonition was so strong.","They had come out to kill zombies in the first place knowing that they were risking their lives.","Jiang Cheng could only say, âEveryone in front, be careful.â","Gao Yuxuan said, âIâll use maximum output in a moment! Highest voltage! Strongest current!â","He was no longer concerned with efficiency. Staying alive came first.","They continued advancing while talking.","The corridor was empty, and the rooms on either side stood open and vacant as well.","It was deeply unsettling.","Those rooms were all functional spaces. Each one was enormous, with sets and equipment visible inside.","Naturally, the doors were wide tooâdouble doors in every case. Now they had all torn free of their frames and fallen to the floor.","They were nearly at the end of the corridor. A turn waited ahead, and beyond it should have been another stretch of hallway.","The farther forward they went, the harder it became for Little Huang to breathe.","âDonât go any farther!â he finally shouted. âStop! Itâs right ahead!â","The floor suddenly began to tremble.","A massive creature poked its head around the corner.","It had a hideous, enormous face.","Its gigantic body pressed against the ceiling, forcing its huge head forward. Its proportions were not remotely human; it looked more like a cat or a dog.","Its enormous body formed a wall of flesh, filling the entire corridor as it scraped against the ceiling and walls.","It moved like a baboon or gorilla, planting two massive fists on the ground to help propel itself forward.","Every time one of its fists struck the floor, the entire building shook.","Little Huang finally understood the suffocating sense of death that had rushed toward him.","He had survived among the zombies by moving with pinpoint precision. But this giant zombie had sealed off the entire corridor with its body. There was nowhere to move.","There was no life gate, so naturally every path was a death gate.","Once his movement skills became useless, Little Huang was nothing more than a lean, somewhat frail middle-school student.","The Giant Zombie clearly possessed intelligence as well. It had been lying in wait around the corner.","If Little Huang had not stopped Gao Yuxuan from advancing, Gao Yuxuan might already have been inside the monsterâs mouth!","It had revealed itself only after hearing everyone stop.","That enormous, ugly face actually twisted into a smile, grotesque and terrifying.","The wall of flesh pounded the floor and charged toward them.","âHoly crap, fall back! Fall backâ!â","Gao Yuxuan shouted frantically while unleashing a wild burst of electricity.","But even the combined maximum-output attacks of Gao Yuxuan and Guo Jun, the two strongest electricity users, could not stop the wall of flesh from charging forward.","Aunt Pan reacted just as quickly. In an instant, she raised a wall to seal off the corridor.","The next moment, the monster smashed it to pieces.","Jiang Cheng shouted, âSu Yu!â","Su Yu stepped forward, crossed her hands, and thrust them out. White light gathered, and a white shieldâor rather, a wall of lightâshot forward.","The giant monster roared as it collided with the wall of light.","Jiang Chengâs voice rang out, calm and commanding. âFall back in formation! Donât run!â","With so many people packed into the corridor, panic would immediately lead to a stampede.","They had to retreat.","A monster like this could no longer be dealt with through sheer numbers. As Zhao Yi had pointed out, the terrain was completely unfavorable to the humans.","In a corridor like this, only the people at the front could engage the monster directly. Everyone behind them was blocked.","Fortunately, the past few days had truly hardened everyoneâs nerves. They had also grown somewhat numb to the prospect of death, and no one panicked or fled blindly.","Even ordinary civilians had begun to display something of a soldierâs discipline.","Everyone remained calm and retreated quickly and in orderly fashion.","Gao Yuxuan and Guo Jun also stopped using their abilities. Since their attacks were ineffective, there was no point wasting their energy. They too were able to retreat rapidly.","But Su Yu had difficulty moving backward.","Her wall of light was braced against the giant monster, and she could not turn around to retreat.","Li Jiangbing roared, âSu Yu, hold it steady!â","He rushed over. Knowing that Su Yu could not turn around, he twisted his body, crouched in front of her, and hoisted her onto his shoulder in one swift motion.","âKeep it steady! Weâll cover the rear together!â","Su Yu felt Li Jiangbingâs powerful arms supporting her. Sitting on his arm, she wrapped one arm around his neck to steady herself, while the other remained extended forward, continuously controlling the wall of light.","Carrying Su Yu, Li Jiangbing began to run. Only then did Jiang Cheng turn and start retreating himself.","But as the three of them withdrew, Su Yuâs wall of light moved with them. This was the farthest distance Su Yu could control it from.","The giant monster could not break through the wall of light. It pounded against it furiously while pursuing them without pause.","Every time it struck, a dull pain throbbed in Su Yuâs chest.","When the barrier is operating at full power, it can automatically negate attacks and impacts. But clearly, the giant monster was simply too strong. The barrier couldnât cancel everything out in a single blow, and the residual force still rebounded onto Su Yu.","As everyone retreated, they kept looking back. The giant monster was being held back entirely by Su Yuâs wall of light, but it just wouldnât shake loose!","How much longer could Su Yu hold on?","What would happen if she couldnât?","Just then, many people felt as though someone had stepped on the tops of their heads.","When they looked up, there was already no sign of the figureâit had been far too fast.","Mo Li was incredibly fast!","She had charged past by stepping on everyoneâs headsâ"]},{"number":145,"title":"Chapter 145: 0145","paragraphs":["The last thing Mo Li stepped on was Li Jiangbingâs head.","Using it as lightly as a dragonfly touching water, he launched himself into the air. In an instant, his body began to swell, growing enormous at incredible speed!","Mo Li rarely grew huge inside buildings.","When scouting alone, he took the form of a small cat, able to avoid the paths meant for humans and take all kinds of shortcuts, such as ventilation ducts.","When fighting inside a building, he usually appeared in a leopard-sized formâswift and agile.","He hardly ever grew huge indoors. This form was even larger than his elephant-sized body outdoors.","Everyone stopped retreating.","The Giant Zombie was no longer visible. Mo Liâs body filled the entire corridor, just like the wall of flesh the Giant Zombie had formed earlier.","This time, it was a gigantic feline shield on humanityâs side.","They couldnât see what was happening. All they could hear were the sounds.","The cat was yowling. The zombie was roaring. The floor trembled, and the ceiling shook.","There was no way to imagine how two enormous creatures were trading blows face-to-face. All they could tell was that both sides were worked into a frenzy.","Everyone stopped retreating.","Su Yu lowered her shield as well. Hugging Li Jiangbingâs head, she stared at Mo Liâs enormous rear without daring to blink.","Even though she couldnât see a thing.","Li Jiangbingâs mouth hung wide open, and he was tense with anxiety.","Suddenly, there was a tremendous crash!","It sounded as if something had collapsed.","Mo Li let out a loud cry. His massive body suddenly sprang upward and disappeared.","Dust billowed through the corridor.","Zhou Wang promptly controlled the airflow and blew the dust away. Only then could everyone see the huge hole in the ceiling, through which they could see the third floor!","The Giant Zombie had smashed through the ceiling to escape upstairs, and Mo Li had gone after him.","The floor above them trembled again and again.","Since he was running away, that meant we had the advantage! Everyoneâs spirits rose.","âLetâs go up and take a look! Come on!â","With Mo Li on our side, what was there to fear? Everyone charged noisily up the stairs.","âDonât push!â","âYou stepped on my foot!â","âPut that shovel away! You nearly poked me in the face!â","âHold your shovel up higher! Donât scratch anyone!â","During breaks, the metal-element superpowered users would sharpen everyoneâs blades again, keeping their weapons in the best possible condition.","The crescent shovels in particular had become increasingly popular, with more and more people abandoning other weapons in favor of them. They could be used either to shovel or to smashâtwo functions in one!","So everyone held their shovels above their heads to avoid accidentally injuring their own people.","As Li Jiangbing ran, Su Yu suddenly realized that she was still sitting on his shoulders!","No wonder her view had been so good.","âPut me down!â","âOh!â","Su Yu climbed down and followed everyone upstairs.","Jiang Cheng and Li Jiangbing brought up the rear.","The moment they reached the third floor, everything felt different.","The entire structure was different. The corridor was especially wide and tall, almost as if it consisted of two floors with the dividing level removed.","The third floor was the broadcasting-studio level, which had special functional requirements. The corridors had to be tall enough for large sets, props, and equipment to be moved through.","No wonder the monster had come to this floor. It could finally stand upright here.","On the second floor, it had moved like a gorilla, using both fists to support itself because it couldnât stretch out. Its entire body had been hunched over.","Here, it stood upright and looked even more like a giant.","Or rather, there was no need to say âlike.â It was a giant.","No wonder Mo Li had grown so large. Only a body that size could withstand the Giant Zombieâs strength.","The giant cat and the giant crashed into each other and rolled across the floor, locked in a terrifying struggle.","Everyone could only stand far away at the opposite end of the corridor. Not a single person dared to approach.","Fortunately, this area was spacious, almost like a small plaza.","At the far end stood a large door, tightly shut. It looked like the entrance to a theater, which was probably the broadcasting studio.","That explained the open space in front of it. Back on the lower floors, everyone had glanced at the information posted on the walls. The broadcasting studio could accommodate 1,200 spectators, making it essentially the same as a theater.","With a thunderous crash, the black cat was hurled away. It smashed through a large hole in the outer wall beside the stairs, revealing the road and the overpass outside. Wind came rushing in with a howl.","The black cat swept its long tail, and the Giant Zombie crashed to the ground.","The giant cat pounced, bit down on the Giant Zombieâs shoulder, and twisted its neck! It tore one of the giantâs arms clean off!","This was a house-sized giant cat! Its bite and tearing force were terrifying beyond belief!","Many people suddenly realized that when Mo Li had transformed into a house-sized giant cat and bitten Cao Jiacai to death, it had truly been like using a sledgehammer to crack a nut.","This enormous form was meant to be used against a Giant Zombie.","âGo, Mo Li! Go!â","âMo Li, you can do it!â","The Giant Zombie roared, the sound making everyone cover their ears.","The one-armed Giant Zombie fought back desperately, but when it came to speed, how could a human compare with a cat? Humans became stronger after turning into zombies, but mutated cats became stronger too.","Mo Li clamped his jaws around the giantâs throat, his sharp teeth piercing deep!","But the Giant Zombie was no Cao Jiacai. Piercing its throat was not enough to kill it.","The giant rolled, but the cat refused to let go! The two of them wrestled and rolled together.","They kept rolling until suddenly they came toward the crowd!","Oh no! Anyone crushed beneath them would be dead!","Everyone turned and ran for their lives.","After running a few steps, they looked back and saw that Mo Li and the monster had rolled away again.","So everyone ran back.","It was like the tide receding and then surging back inâbouncing back and forth with remarkable elasticity.","At last, accompanied by the teeth-grinding sound of bones crackingâcrack, crack, crackâthe giant cat suddenly exerted its strength and twisted the giantâs head into a grotesque angle.","The giant cat released its bite. The Giant Zombie crashed to the ground and lay motionless.","Its enormous, ugly head was still attached to its body, but it looked like a screw twisted crookedly out of place.","The brain could no longer command the body, and the body could no longer sustain the brain. It was thoroughly dead.","The giant cat turned around and stared at them.","Everyone held their breath, their eyes filled with awe.","Then the terrifying giant cat suddenly let out a squeaky little âMeow~,â completely mismatched with its enormous body.","Everyone: ââ¦â","Mo Li and Li Jiangbing were close enough that Mo Li could lie on top of Li Jiangbingâs head while Li Jiangbing carried him around the neighborhood to bask in the sun. Li Jiangbing immediately began clapping his huge hands.","âGood job, good job, good job! Our Mo Li did such a good job!â","Giant cat: âMeow~â","Apparently, that still wasnât enough.","Li Jiangbing gave a loud cough.","Everyone came back to their senses. They immediately understood and burst into applause.","âGood job, good job, good job!â","âGreat job, great job, great job!â","âMo Li is the best! What a good kitty!â","The giant cat was satisfied. It strutted toward them with a catlike sway, shrinking a little with every step. By the time it reached Jiang Cheng, it had transformed back into a little black cat.","It sat down in front of Jiang Cheng and raised one paw toward him.","âMeow.â","A packet of wet wipes appeared in Jiang Chengâs hand. She pulled one out and wiped Mo Liâs paw, carefully cleaning between his toes as well. He had gotten far too much disgusting stuff on them. The wipe changed color completely.","Zhou Wang turned his head and asked Little Huang, âHow is it?â","Little Huang relaxed all over. âThereâs no danger anymore.â","The building was extremely quiet. Aside from the Giant Zombie, they had yet to see a single ordinary zombie anywhere from the first floor to the third.","Now that the Giant Zombie was dead, Little Huang could no longer sense any other danger.","Only after his paws had been cleaned did Mo Li jump onto Jiang Chengâs shoulder.","Jiang Cheng gently scratched his little head. âYou worked hard.â","But Mo Li only replied:","âMeowââ","âA survivor? A lot of them?â Jiang Cheng turned toward the doors of the studio. âTheyâre inside?â","âHow many?â","âA whole lot?â","Chang Jiaxin leaned over and whispered to Wang Yunya, âCan she understand cat language?â","Wang Yunya was a cheerful, outgoing girl. After spending the past two days with the older boys and girls, she had already heard plenty of rumors about Jiang Cheng and her black cat. She whispered back, âI heard they have some kind of telepathic connection.â","âWowâ¦â","Jiang Cheng walked over and stored the Giant Zombieâs corpse in her storage space.","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan exchanged a glance.","The two of them had been making all kinds of observations, records, and analyses. They also knew that Jiang Chengâs storage space had a limit based not on volume, but on weight.","There were still plenty of other things inside it. Even the things they knew about included the cookware she took out to prepare hot meals for everyone. There might be many more things they knew nothing about.","The Giant Zombie was clearly not merely large in volume. To support such a massive body, its muscles and bones had to be far denser than normal. Its total weight was probably at least one ton.","If its bone density was comparable to that of a crocodile, it could easily weigh close to two tons.","How much had Jiang Chengâs storage space expanded by now? She had just put the Giant Zombie away with ease.","In any case, it certainly wasnât small.","And compared to the Giant Zombie, Mo Li was even more terrifying.","Fortunately, it was our cat.","Jiang Cheng led everyone to the doors of the studio.","A row of connected seats had been wedged diagonally across the doors.","There were rows of seats along both walls as well. This spacious, plaza-like area was where the audience could wait and rest before entering.","The row of seats had been jammed against the door handles, locking the doors shut. Clearly, neither the people nor the zombies inside had been able to get out.","Jiang Cheng stored the seats away.","Two tall, powerfully built boys pushed open the heavy double doors.","A wave of foul air rolled out!","The people at the entrance nearly gagged from the stench.","It was an indescribable mixture of odors.","The smell of feces and urine. The body odor of people who hadnât bathed in days. The stench of zombies. The reek of decomposing corpses.","Everyone was already familiar with the latter two after enduring two zombie outbreaks, and they could identify them immediately. But when all those vile smells blended together, they struck the back of everyoneâs skull like a physical blow.","Covering their mouths and noses, the group walked inside.","It was a vast, column-free space with an exceptionally high ceiling. Black electrical cables sprawled across the concrete floor. Overhead, countless lighting rigs and curtain tracks crisscrossed the ceiling, suspending dozens of enormous lamps. All kinds of expensive equipment lay scattered across the floor, some of it smashed beyond recognition.","The walls had been built as a room-within-a-room structure, with a seismic isolation layer hidden beneath the concrete floor. Even the doors they had just opened were thick, soundproof security doors.","The studioâs soundproofing requirements had been extraordinarily high. Once the doors were shut, the battle between the monster and the giant cat outside had been completely inaudible within.","In the foul-smelling space, the broadcast stage stood ahead of them, while opposite it were audience seats capable of holding twelve hundred people.","High above the seats at the back was a huge wall of glassâthe control room overlooking the entire studio. Now, that enormous window had been stained a murky brown, turning it opaque.","The studio was full of people.","People lying down. People sprawled facedown. People leaning against the walls. People huddled in corners. People clinging to one another. People keeping their distance from the center.","All kinds of people lay among feces, urine, and corpses. Some appeared to be barely alive. Others looked as though they were already dead.","The floor was littered with empty mineral-water bottles and countless identical packages.","They appeared to contain bread, braised chicken legs, marinated eggs, pastries, and pickles.","The members of the High-Tech New Districtâs Zombie Cleanup Team were utterly stunned.","Not a single survivor at the district government offices.","Not a single survivor at city hall.","No one had imagined that there would be hundreds of living people inside the television stationâs studio!","Seven days.","It had been seven days since the second zombie-virus outbreak.","How had they survived?","And how had they ended up trapped inside with the Giant Zombie?","Why had they been locked in there?","Where were the other zombies?","Among so many people, wasnât there even one superpowered fighter capable of putting up a fight?","The middle school students began to vomit.","Because the stage lights illuminated everything far too clearly.","There were numerous severed limbs scattered across the stage. From the differences in skin color, it was possible to tell that some had belonged to zombies, while others had belonged to humans.","They lay strewn across the stage, like scraps of food consumed carelessly and left behind without a thought.","Zhao Yi slowly turned around and stared at the scene.","âThis canât beâ¦â","Everyone looked at him.","Zhao Yiâs teeth chattered softly, clicking against one another as his mind reeled from the shock.","âIt canât be,â he forced out with difficulty. âThisâ¦ this isnât a granary, is it?â","In an instant, everyone was covered in gooseflesh."]},{"number":146,"title":"Chapter 146: 0146","paragraphs":["The survivors were all so hungry that they no longer had the strength to run or resist.","When the people from the Technology New District charged in, many of them simply closed their eyes and waited to die.","After a moment, when nothing happened, they cautiously opened their eyes. What they saw was not the monster, but a group of young people wearing armor and carrying strange weapons. There were even children among them.","Everyoneâs minds had grown sluggish. After staring blankly for a while, someone finally asked in a hoarse voice, âYouâ¦ youâ¦â","Someone else hurriedly asked, âWhereâs Director Guo? Have you seen Director Guo?â","The question made no sense. Who knew which Director Guo they were talking about?","Jiang Cheng asked, âWho is Director Guo?â","âHeâsâ¦â someone said. âA monster.â","âA giant.â","âAn especially huge zombie.â","Oh. Now everyone understood. So Director Guo was the giant zombie.","âThat giant zombie? Weâve already taken him out.â","Mo Li was Jiang Chengâs cat.","Jiang Cheng was their leader.","By several degrees of separation, that meant we had taken him out.","Mo Li puffed out her belly proudly. Weâre amazing!","âHeâs dead?â","âDirector Guo is dead?â","âHeâs dead! Director Guo is dead!â","Only then did light return to the survivorsâ eyes. Only then did they finally believe they had been saved.","âDo you have anything to eat?â","âDo you have food?â","âI need water! Please, give me some water!â","Their eyes gleamed with a hungry, almost feral light. Sometimes, starving people were more frightening than zombies.","Jiang Cheng took out several large barrels of drinking water.","They were water-cooler jugs collected from empty houses. The water inside had been purified from tap water by Li Jiangbing and was safe to drink directly.","Li Jiangbing drew circles in the air with his finger.","The water in several jugs floated out, forming several circular rings in midair. They rotated slowly, positioned at about neck and chin height.","âDrink,â Li Jiangbing said.","The thirsty, starving survivors rushed toward them with shining eyes, stumbling as they went. Some of them reached through the water rings and fell flat on the ground.","âHey, hey, stand up and drink! Donât throw yourselves at it!â Li Jiangbing called.","The others stood outside the water rings and opened their mouths to âbiteâ into the water. Gulp, gulp, gulp!","Several of the water rings disappeared almost instantly. Many people still had not gotten a drink, so Li Jiangbing condensed several more.","He noticed that some people who had already drunk were still trying to push their way forward. With a little cunning, he formed the next water rings among those who had not yet had any and shouted, âStop pushing! Let the others drink too!â","People kept asking, âDo you have anything to eat?â","Everyone looked toward Jiang Cheng.","Some of the people who were starving noticed where everyoneâs attention was focused and charged straight at her.","âPlease, give me something to eat!â","âStop them,â Jiang Cheng said.","The members of the combat team formed a line in front of her and stretched out their arms to block the survivors.","They couldnât push them away. One shove and they would fall over; everyoneâs legs were too weak. All they could do was hold them back with their arms.","Jiang Cheng did have food.","But she couldnât simply hand it over to them.","The emergency supplies she kept in her spatial storage were compressed biscuits.","After the previous disaster at the youth apartments, Jiang Cheng had retrieved the supplies from the basement. The rice, flour, cooking oil, and other staples had already been put to use.","No one had been willing to eat the compressed biscuits, so Jiang Cheng had stored them in her own home.","Her home had now been opened up and connected to Rooms 0304 and 0302, making three rooms in total. She had accumulated quite a lot of supplies there.","As for compressed biscuitsâemergency rations meant to keep people aliveâshe stored some in her spatial storage whenever she went out, just in case.","And now, they had finally come in handy.","She couldnât give them directly to the survivors because they were far too hungry. If they ate too much, they might die from overeating.","She took the biscuits out and handed them to her own people.","âBreak them into pieces. Give each person only a small piece. Donât give them too much.â","Just how potent were compressed biscuits? A normal adult could eat half of one, drink a cup of water, and feel full.","They were genuinely awful to eat, but they were also genuinely effective.","If these starving people ate too much, their stomachs might burst.","Everyone received a small piece of compressed biscuit.","Some ate the biscuit first and then drank water. Others drank first and ate the biscuit afterward. It didnât matter. Once everything reached their stomachs, it would all mix together and the biscuit would quickly swell.","Some of the people were wearing clothes that were wrinkled and filthy, but it was still obvious that they had once been expensive designer brands. They clearly came from comfortable financial backgrounds.","Yet now, those well-off people were sitting on the floor with their legs sprawled out, sighing that there was nothing in the world more blissful than eating a crumb of compressed biscuit.","Gold and silver meant nothing compared to food and water.","If Song Jingshuo had been there to hear that, he probably would have attained enlightenment.","The hall was unbearably stinky. It was an enclosed space without even a window.","With the doors wide open, Zhou Wang controlled fresh air, drawing it in through a hole in the outer wall and sending it all the way into the studio. The foul air was gradually forced out.","Only then did the hall finally become breathable.","Jiang Cheng and Zhao Yi began communicating with the survivors.","There were more than five hundred of them.","Those wearing badges were television-station employees. The rest were members of the studio audience who had come to participate in the recording of a program.","âDirector GuoâGuo Liwei. You really havenât heard of him?â the employees asked, gradually regaining the strength to speak.","Of course Jiang Cheng had never heard of him. Neither had Zhao Yi. But someone else had.","âOh, him.â","Why had they heard of him? Because the tabloids had reported that Director Guo had slept with a great many female celebrities.","âWas that true?â","The employee nodded blankly. âMost of it was true.â","A member of the combat team asked, âThe tabloids also said he had powerful connections?â","That was true as well. Director Guo had powerful backing, which was why he had exploited so many people through unspoken rules, including actresses, female hosts, female reporters, and female employees.","He was notorious for taking a cut of everything.","But his backer had died during the first zombie disaster, along with his entire family.","Director Guo had lost his influence.","Everyone knew the station director was going to take him down.","Director Guo wasnât merely a lecher. He was also a massive embezzler. He kept everything for himself and abused his authority.","The station director had wanted to deal with him for a long time. Now that his backer was gone, the director was finally preparing to make his move. Rumors were flying throughout the station that Director Guo the Great Embezzler would soon be dismissed and sent to prison.","Who could have known that before that happened, the zombie virus would erupt again?","With so many people at the station, naturally a large number of zombies appearedâfirst-generation, second-generation, third-generation, and all the rest.","And thenâ¦","âDirector Guo ate them.â","âAfter that, he became bigger than the other zombies. Then he ate even more zombiesâand people too,â they said.","They spoke with wooden, emotionless faces.","Because there had originally been far more people in the studio.","Guo the Great Embezzler had dragged every living person in the building inside. But he needed to feed every day. After eating for so many days, these five hundred or so people were all that remained.","Zhao Yiâs guess had been right. He had been using the studio as a granary.","Zhao Yi asked, âSo he became that huge by constantly eating zombies and people?â","âNo,â one of the survivors replied. âHe was already quite big. From the very beginning, he was larger than the other zombies. He was like a giant corpse swollen by decomposition. You know what that looks like, right?â","âI know, I know,â Zhao Yi said.","Survivor: âThen he ate a lot of other zombies and people, and grew a little bigger. But the reason he became this huge was because he ate Shen Yuehong.â","Several anguished cries rose from the members of the team.","âWhat? He ate Shen Yuehong!â","âShen Yuehong was eaten by him?â","âAhhhhhhh, Shen Yuehong!â","Shen Yuehong had been a young TV host who rose to fame over the past two years. She was beautiful and sweet, with a warm, approachable personality.","Her fans ranged across every age group.","There were fans of hers in the young adultsâ apartment building too. When they heard she was dead, they were devastated.","Zhao Yi asked, âHow can you be sure he became like this because he ate Shen Yuehong?â","âBecause we watched it happen,â the survivor said. âHe ate Shen Yuehong right in front of everyone. Heâd been slowly growing larger every time he ate a zombie or a person, just a little bigger each time. But after he ate Shen Yuehongâhe must have been especially satisfied, I guessâwe watched him swell up like a balloon. It only took a few minutes for him to become a giant.â","Zhao Yi asked, âWas Shen Yuehong a zombie too?â","âNo. She never turned into a zombie. She was alive when Director Guo ate her.â","Zhao Yi had to understand the logic and cause-and-effect behind all this. He asked, âWhy did eating her turn him into a giant? Do you know the reason? Was there anything special about the two of them?â","Naturally, the survivor had no idea.","They had been trapped there since the afternoon of August 29.","At the time, a live program was scheduled to be recorded in the studio. Programs like that never lacked an audience; they were always packed. Everyone wanted to see celebrities, actors, and hosts up close.","In reality, though, recording a program took far longer than the version viewers saw on television.","It was perfectly normal for some celebrity or host to throw a tantrum and arrive two or three hours late.","The twelve hundred audience members could only sit there on their hard chairs and wait.","The television station had plenty of experience dealing with this kind of thing. Each audience member was given a plastic bag containing a bread roll, a bottle of mineral water, a vacuum-packed braised egg, a braised chicken leg, a packet of pickled vegetables, and a chocolate pie.","Many of the audience members hadnât eaten them at the time.","Later, those provisions became the lifeline of the people trapped there.","Now, torn wrappers littered the floor. Every last trace of oil and sauce had been licked clean from the packages that had held the braised eggs and chicken legs.","Eventually, there was no water left to drink. Even wealthy audience members dressed in designer clothes had been willing to drink urine.","Everyone reeked.","The surviving staff members didnât know what had caused the mutation, but they did know about the grudge between Director Guo and Shen Yuehong.","Director Guo had always wanted to force Shen Yuehong into sleeping with him.","Shen Yuehong looked sweet and approachable, but in reality she was proud and strong-willed. She had always refused him.","The station had high hopes for her and wanted to groom her into one of its leading stars, while the station chief had protected her.","Still, Shen Yuehong had certainly suffered at Director Guoâs handsâperhaps he had taken advantage of her in some way. In any case, she hated him bitterly.","Director Guo had already lost his influence and was clearly on the verge of collapse.","One day, Shen Yuehong had humiliated him harshly in front of a large crowd.","Director Guo no longer had the power to fight back and could only endure it, but he had surely come to hate her.","When he began randomly selecting people from the crowd as food, he discovered Shen Yuehong hiding among them.","âHe made this sound. It was terrifying.â As the surviving staff member recalled and described the scene, his eyes were empty. âOnly later did I realize that he was laughing. Zombies can laugh too.â","âHe ate Shen Yuehong alive right in front of us. He started with her feet, then ate her limbs, then her stomachâ¦â","âShen Yuehong never died.â","âHe did it on purpose. He could bite off most peopleâs heads in one bite. He did it on purpose.â","âHe was taking revenge. Heâd already turned into a zombie, so how could he still take revenge?â","Zhao Yi sighed. âThe zombies have evolved. Third-generation zombies have developed intelligence.â","âThird generation?â","Zhao Yi said, âHe canât really be considered third generation. He underwent a complete mutation. Heâs a monster.â","âExactly. Thatâs what we called him tooâa monster. Zombies arenât actually that frightening. Everyoneâs killed them before. But he was a monsterâ¦â","The survivors murmured, âHe was a monster.â","Zhao Yi and Jiang Cheng exchanged a glance.","Many of the survivors looked as if they had gone insane. Who wouldnât? In a situation like this, going mad was the normal reaction.","Did Zhao Yi really seem like a normal person to you?","Did Gao Yuxuan seem like a normal person?","Brother Dong had come to seek refuge yesterday. He looked alive, but his soul was already gone.","The survivors gradually came back to life after eating and drinking.","But they stank terribly.","Li Jiangbing brought water over from the restroom in the hallway. This was a high-end television station, and the restrooms had both hot and cold water. He brought the hot water straight over.","Several water spheres as tall as people spun and whirled with a whooshing sound.","Li Jiangbing shouted, âEveryone, wash yourselves! Wash yourselvesâyou stink! Donât bother taking off your clothes. Hold your noses and step inside. Stay in there for at least a minute. When you canât hold your breath anymore, stick your head out and take a breath.â","The water spheres were large enough to enclose a personâs head.","Because these peopleâs heads smelled unbelievably bad. The stench was enough to make someone retch.","There was no laundry detergent or shampoo, but at least they could rinse themselves with clean water and make the smell less unbearable.","Once they had rinsed themselves, Li Jiangbing would reach out and dry them completely with a single grab.","One of the staff members asked Zhao Yi, âDo a lot of people have special abilities now?â","Zhao Yi said, âYou still donât know anything? This waveâ¦both humans and zombies have evolved. These days, when we hunt zombies, the people with superpowers take the lead. Theyâre incredibly useful.â","âI see.â The staff member licked his cracked lips again and again. âActuallyâ¦â","He rubbed his fingers together. A tiny electric current appeared at his fingertips, flickering with a faint light.","âI have one too.â","Zhao Yi: ââ¦â","âI didnât dare say anything.â","âWhen the people who had special abilities first revealed themselves, they were the first ones to be eaten.â","âAfter that, no one dared say anything, even if they developed an ability.â","âItâs just this tiny little spark. How could it beat any zombie, let alone Director Guo?â","Only those with extraordinary innate talent had powerful abilities from the moment they awakened.","For most ordinary people with superpowers, their abilities were actually extremely weak at first. For example, when Li Jiangbingâs ability first awakened, he could control only a small water sphere about the size of a ping-pong ball.","Later, everyone had to risk their lives practicing or break through and advance during actual combat.","But the survivors hadnât even dared reveal their abilities. Director Guo would pick them out and eat them first. Everyone kept their abilities hidden.","They were also afraid that someone else would inform on themâbecause people really had done so.","Otherwise, how could Director Guo have discovered Shen Yuehong among so many people? It was because a member of the television station had been caught and shouted, âDonât eat me! Donât eat me! Eat Shen Yuehong! Shen Yuehong is over there!â","The survivors with superpowers kept them hidden. They hadnât even had a chance to practice.","The people in the Technology New District, meanwhile, had already become a force of powerful superhuman fighters. The survivors here were still stuck at the level they had been when their abilities first awakened.","âRight,â the staff member added. âAfter Director Guo turned into that giant, all the other zombies started obeying him.â","Zhao Yi and Jiang Cheng exchanged another glance.","Jiang Cheng asked, âWhat do you mean?â","The staff member said, âThose zombies would come over whenever Director Guo crooked his finger. When Director Guo grabbed them and ate them, they didnât run away either. They were like puppets.â","âDirector Guo ate every last one of them.â","Zhao Yi muttered, âFuck, it evolved again. Is this ever going to end?â","A lot of questions had been answeredâso many that they almost wished they hadnât known. They might as well have never gone to the TV station.","Without anything to compare it to, they would never have felt that the New Technology District was paradise.","But going to the TV station was something they had to do sooner or later.","Because yesterday, the entire assembly had passed a resolutionâ","If they confirmed tomorrow that no one was left in the municipal government, then they would be the only government remaining in S City.","And since they were a government, they had to shoulder the responsibilities of a government."]},{"number":147,"title":"Chapter 147: 0147","paragraphs":["Everyone had their own assignment.","Although Little Huang said he could no longer sense any danger in the building, Cui Haiyang and Wu Jiancheng still led their teams in searching the floors one by one.","Li Jiangbing and Su Yu took people to look after the survivors in the broadcasting hall.","Of the more than five hundred survivors, over a hundred were staff members.","âWe all worked on the upper floors. We were dragged down here.â","Jiang Cheng gathered the staff together and asked, âCan you broadcast live?â","Then she added, âIf not, a recorded broadcast will do.â","The staff member who had been answering their questions was named Yue Chao. He asked, âWho exactly are you people?â","Everyone was wearing armorâsome of the old white kind, some made of gleaming silver metal. Many of them carried identical weapons that looked like ancient polearms.","If not for the zombie outbreak, seeing them in the television stationâs corridors would have made him think they were performers about to go onstage.","They were well organized, but they were not an army. They still fell far short of an armyâs discipline and structure.","âAre you a militia?â he asked.","More than a month ago, S City had had a great many militia members. Among his colleagues, relatives, and friends, there had been plenty of people who served in the militia.","âNo,â Jiang Cheng replied. âWeâre the Provisional Government of the High-Tech Development Zone.â","âWe were established by the residents living in the Technology Zone.â","âBecause there are no survivors left in either the municipal government or the Development Zone government.â","Yue Chao stood there blankly for a moment. âNone left?â","The survivors in the broadcasting hall all seemed slow and numb to some degree, probably because of the physical hunger and psychological terror they had endured over the past seven days.","It was hard to blame them. Without protection or weapons, ordinary humans were nothing but meat when facing zombies.","One bite from a zombie meant: humans -1, zombies +1.","They had searched the broadcasting hall as well, but could not even find a chair that could be used as a weapon. All the seats were fixed in connected rows across multiple tiers.","A school would have been better. At least there, you could swing a chair around to defend yourself.","Jiang Cheng asked, âCan this place broadcast live?â","Yue Chao took a moment to react. âHere? No. Director Guo tore out all the cables.â","He pointed at the floor. Only then did everyone notice that many of the black cables lying there had been severed, exposing the metal inside.","Zhao Yi pressed him further. âWhy did he do that?â","âIâve wondered about that too,â Yue Chao said. âMaybe he was afraid weâd call for help? I donât know. Anyway, he understands human speech. He really has evolved.â","He gestured with his hands. âHe was already this tall from the beginningâtwo heads taller than me. He looked just like that guy over there, only even taller and stronger.â","The âguyâ he pointed to was none other than Li Jiangbing, who was famous for his massive build.","âBut actually,â Yue Chao continued, âDirector Guo was only 168 centimeters tall.â","For a man, that was undeniably short.","âHe was different from the other zombies right from the start. He was unusually tall and powerful from the beginning.â","Zhao Yi wanted to ask more, but Jiang Cheng cut him off. âWeâll talk about that later.â","She told Yue Chao and the other staff members, âI want to make an announcement to everyone in the city. Youâll operate the equipment. Live or recorded, either is fine. Just like the former Emergency Response Committee didâlike Vice Mayor Zheng.â","Everyone understood at once.","âOh, this room wonât work. Thereâs another studio downstairs.â","Together, they went down to the second floor. Yue Chao and the others found a studio.","âThis one will do.â","When they entered, it was much smaller than the broadcasting hall upstairs and had no audience seating. But it looked extremely familiar.","Gao Yuxuan glanced around. âIsnât this where they broadcast the news every day?â","A closer look confirmed it. No wonder it had seemed familiar.","Back at their familiar posts, with their hands on the familiar equipment, the staff seemed to gradually regain their souls. Their spirits and bodies finally began to fall back into sync, and the numbness slowly faded.","They busied themselves for a while, and numerous screens lit up.","Jiang Cheng stood behind the desk where the daily news was usually broadcast. Her image appeared on all the screens.","âRemember, this is a live broadcast,â Yue Chao reminded her.","Jiang Cheng nodded.","âAttention. Three, two, oneââ","Yue Chao lowered three fingers one by one.","âBegin!â","On the screens, Jiang Cheng raised her eyes.","Technology Zone, Youth Apartments.","Everyone was packed into the clubhouse.","âWhy hasnât it started yet?â","After the team seized the municipal government building, they had contacted the apartments. Everyone already knew that the municipal government had been completely wiped out. They also knew that Jiang Cheng had led everyone toward the television station and planned to take it today.","Just moments ago, they had received a call from Wu Jiancheng informing them that the television station had been secured.","âDamn, the zombies evolved again. If not for Mo Li today, we wouldâve lost at least dozens of people there.â","âThere are two things to handle. First, we have to bring everyone back today and prepare a proper meal for them.â","âSecond, Jiang Cheng is about to appear on television.â","The municipal government and the district government really had been wiped out exactly as Jiang Cheng had said.","Song Jingshuoâs emotions were complicated. He stayed with everyone in the clubhouse, craning his neck to stare at the television mounted on the wall.","While they waited, Zeng Qiang and Brother Dong kept talking.","Brother Dong was not in good shape mentally, and neither Jiang Cheng nor Zhou Wang approved of him joining the team.","They could simply leave him at home. He was considered a strong fighter now, and the team had enough people. Let him stay behind and guard the place.","Song Jingshuo turned his head and exchanged a few words with them as well. Then someone suddenly shouted, âItâs on! Itâs starting!â","Everyone looked up.","On the television, Jiang Cheng raised her eyes.","âTo all the citizens of S City, hello. My name is Jiang Cheng.â","âIâm sorry that I have to be the one to deliver this news.â","âToday, September 4, at 3:00 p.m., my companions and I eliminated every zombie in the S City municipal government compound.â","âI regret to inform you that there are no survivors in the municipal government.â","âVice Mayor Zheng and every municipal government employee have perished.â","Jiang Cheng paused after saying this, giving the people in front of their televisions time to understand and absorb the news.","Even the residents of the Youth Apartments, who had already been warned in advance, were left dazed and bewildered as they heard Jiang Cheng confirm it with her own mouth.","The government was truly gone.","âEven earlier, we confirmed that there were no survivors left in the government of the High-Tech Development Zone.â","âTherefore, led by the residents of the Youth Apartments in the Technology Zone, and with the joint participation of the residents of Auspicious Garden and Imperial View Garden, we established the Provisional Government of the High-Tech Development Zone.â","âUnfortunately, as a provisional government formed by ordinary citizens, we have no way to contact the central government or the military to request assistance.â","âWe have only ourselves.â","âAt present, we have formed a combat force of two hundred people. Our team has eliminated most of the zombies in the residential areas of the Technology Zone and cleared the zombies from the district government.â","âIf we had not needed to confirm whether the municipal government still existed, we should have been clearing the zombies from the Development Zoneâs technology park today.â","âToday, we eliminated every zombie in the municipal government compound. We have also essentially regained control of the S City television station and are currently cleaning up the battlefield and confirming the results.â","The senior high school section of S City No. 14 High School.","Five days ago, the high school and middle school students who had finally reunited in the streets had, with only a few exceptions, remained on campus.","Most of them had been unable to contact their parents. Even those who had managed to get through found that their parents were either not at home or not in a safe place.","Under these circumstances, going home was pointlessânever mind the number of zombies along the way.","At the teachersâ urging, everyone stayed in the high school section.","The school had iron fences and gates. They might not be enough to stop second-generation zombies that could jump, or third-generation zombies that had developed intelligence, but at least they could keep out the mindless original zombies.","There were still supplies in the cafeteria. Although the fresh vegetables were gone, the staple foods and frozen meat could last for quite some time.","On the second day, a parent arrived.","He was the parent of a high school student, and had only managed to reach the school after awakening a superpower and surviving countless brushes with death.","The teachers realized that middle school parents might also come looking for their children, so they organized a team to return to the middle school campus. Using chalk, they wrote the following message in prominent places:","âThe survivors are at the high school section on Huachen North Road.â","Sure enough, several more parents arrived in succession. Some had children in high school, while others had children in middle school. The middle school parents had found their way there after seeing the messages.","Some of these parents found their children. Others did not.","For those who could not find their children, it was almost certainâone hundred percent certainâthat they had perished.","But none of these parents left.","Given the current situation, home did not necessarily mean safety, and the journey there was even more dangerous.","So everyone stayed.","These parents were either superpowered, clever, or exceptionally brave in battle. They also had one thing in common: they all loved their children deeply.","The arrival of these adults was a tremendous help to the teachers.","For the past few days, everyone with a superpowerâadults and children alikeâhad been training desperately, striving to improve and advance.","The few metal-element users in particular had been working especially hard.","Wu Shuchen, a middle school student with metal powers, had already stopped wearing his little glasses. His constitution had improved, and, like Zhao Yi, he no longer needed them.","His superpower was now on an entirely different level. He had become one of the main workers among the metal-element users.","Every day, he made armor from the moment he opened his eyes. He would take breaks when exhaustion overcame him, but otherwise he worked until nightfall.","The selfless contributions of these metal-element users had given every student, teacher, and parent at the school armor and weapons. At the same time, the high-intensity output, exhaustion, recovery, and repeated use of their abilities had helped their own powers advance by leaps and bounds.","Two of the parents had served in militia units and were exceptionally experienced at killing zombies. They organized the children into training groups and taught them techniques for fighting zombies.","Middle school students were at the age when their blood ran hot. Once they had armor and weapons, their enthusiasm burned even brighter, and they clamored to go outside and kill zombies.","The adults agreed.","Looking back now, the first zombie outbreak seemed almost like a rehearsal.","After the nationwide mobilization during the first outbreak, when people had left their homes and fought back, everyone understood that they could not simply wait for death. Humanity had to take the initiative and reclaim its right to survive.","Naturally, the first choices for the teams going outside were the older students and the stronger people.","Adults and students, ordinary people and superpowered individualsâbolstered by their armor, they left the school together. Step by step, they cleared the streets around the campus.","For the past two nights, everyone had slept much more soundly.","The children did not think too deeply about things. They were immersed in the exhilaration of âI can kill zombies too!â","But the adults grew heavier-hearted with each passing day. The cafeteria television had been left on all day, every day, for many days now, yet they were still waiting in vain for any announcement from the government.","Then, todayâSeptember 4, the seventh day since the second outbreak of the zombie virusâa student helping in the cafeteria suddenly rushed outside and shouted:","âCome quickly! Hurry! Someoneâs appeared on television!â"]},{"number":148,"title":"Chapter 148: 0148","paragraphs":["Everyone rushed into the cafeteria in a frenzy.","âIs that Vice Mayor Zheng?â","Vice Mayor Zheng had earned the peopleâs deep respect during the last zombie disaster. The citizens who had survived adored him.","Unfortunately, the person appearing on the television was not the mayor who had risen to the occasion and performed outstandingly in the crisis. Instead, it was a young woman in her twenties, and she was very beautiful.","She raised her eyes, her gaze so sharp that it startled the children.","ãâ¦My name is Jiang Cheng.ã","ãâ¦The Technology New Districtâ¦Jixiang Jiayuan.ã","âTechnology New Districtâs Jixiang Jiayuan?â While the adults were mourning the apparent annihilation of the government, a middle school girl suddenly said, âHuang Xuetao lives in that residential community.â","The middle school students all turned around.","âReally?â","They were clearly very concerned about this person named Huang Xuetao.","The high school students asked, âWhoâs that?â","Wu Shuchen reminded them, âHeâs our Student Council Presidentâthe senior who led us in fighting the zombies. He can predict danger. We told you about him.â","The high school students said, âOh, him!â","Wu Shuchen continued, âHe went back to save his mother. I donât know whether he managed to save her.â","Wu Shuchen admired Huang Xuetao greatly. He had something of a fledglingâs attachment to him and kept hoping that Huang Xuetao would be able to save his mother.","Even though Wu Shuchen himself had been unable to contact his own parents.","S City Television Station, news studio.","Jiang Cheng stared directly into the camera in front of her, looking straight at everyone watching the live broadcast.","ãâ¦I believe everyone has already noticed that this wave of zombies is different from the last one.ã","ãClearly intelligent zombies have appeared. They can flee, trick their enemies, lie in ambush, and launch sneak attacks. We call them âthird-generation zombies.âã","ãToday, we even encountered a mutant zombie at the television station. We are unable to classify it for now, but I believe this is not an isolated case.ã","ãHowever, everyone, please do not panic because of this.ã","ãBecause there must also be superpowered individuals among you.ã","ãAs the zombies mutate, humanity is evolving as well.ã","ãAt present, we know of the five elemental abilities associated with metal, wood, water, fire, and earth, as well as two elemental abilities outside the five elementsâwind and electricityâand the special ability known as the mental type.ã","ãRegardless of which type of ability you possess, please take note of the following: superpowers can be improved and advanced through constant practice and repeated use.ã","ãUsing your ability at high frequency can effectively improve your control and precision. Prolonged use, or pushing your ability to its limits with extremely high output, can increase its upper limit.ã","ãThe side effects include headaches, nosebleeds, pain and bleeding in the eardrums, pain in the eyeballs, and bleeding from the eyes. Headaches and nosebleeds usually occur first, while bleeding from the eyes occurs last.ã","ãSo far, there have been no reported cases of anyone dying from bleeding from all seven orifices. However, we recommend that you stop practicing once your eyes begin to ache or your vision becomes doubled.ã","ãThe above is a summary of the experiences of all the superpowered individuals in the Technology New District. We hope it will be helpful to everyone.ã","ãAt this time, I would like to say something to all superpowered individualsâã","ãHeaven has granted us the opportunity to evolve and given us superpowers. We were not given these gifts so that we could hide in a corner and merely scrape by.ã","ãI urge every superpowered individual to do everything in your power to help protect others.ã","ãIn particular, I urge metal-element users to step forward and use your abilities to provide armor for as many people as possible.ã","ãYes, the armor Iâm wearing is exactly what I mean. It was made for everyone by our metal-element users.ã","ãThe zombie virus spreads through blood with extreme efficiency. This puts humanity at an unfair disadvantage.ã","ãArmor allows us humans to fight the zombies on equal footing.ã","ãEvery suit of armor you make gives us one more comrade-in-arms, and humanity one more soldier.ã","ãEvery person has a purpose. Metal-element users, you bear a tremendous responsibility!ã","ãFinally, with no survivors in the municipal government and no way to contact any of the other governments, the temporary government of the Technology New District is currently the only government in existence.ã","ãUntil a formal government of higher authority emerges, we will do our utmost to shoulder the responsibilities of government.ã","ãAt present, the central urban areas appear to contain enormous numbers of zombies. The Technology New District has essentially completed its cleanup and also has a large number of vacant homes.ã","ãAny survivors who have nowhere to go may come to the Technology New District for shelter.ã","ãFor anyone trapped and in need of rescue, the following three numbers are emergency contact numbers.ã","Jiang Cheng announced three mobile phone numbers.","Earlier that day, they had collected a large number of phones from the municipal government and planned to take them back with them. They belonged to public servants who had perished.","While they were eating, they had found some chargers and plugged the phones in.","Gao Yuxuan finally had a chance to try charging a phone.","He had actually wanted to try it for a long time, but he only owned one phone himself. A phone was not merely an expensive electronic device; it was also a vital means of communication.","He hadnât dared to experiment with his own phone. If he broke it, he would be in serious trouble.","Now that he had so many unclaimed phones, he could finally practice.","During the meal, he blew out three phones before finally finding the right balance. After that, he was able to charge phones steadily.","When he tried increasing the output, he discovered that he could charge them even faster than a regular chargerâhe was practically a living fast charger.","Jiang Cheng selected three phones from the pile and announced those three numbers as hotlines.","ãThese three numbers will begin operating tonight. We have not yet completely finished our current operations, so we do not have time to answer calls.ã","ãPlease send requests for help by text message whenever possible. Include your location, the surrounding conditions, and the number of survivors.ã","ãWe have limited manpower. We will not answer calls to mobile phones; we will only answer calls made to landlines.ã","Those with mobile phones could send text messages requesting help.","Only those who had lost their phones would have no choice but to call a landline.","ãI call on the surviving governments in each district to gather their forces as quickly as possible.ã","ãI also call on all survivors to remember: Heaven helps those who help themselves, and salvation begins with self-rescue.ã","ãPlease make use of every resource around you and stand together.ã","ãAbove all, survive.ã","The children of No. 14 Middle School all began to cry.","Heaven helps those who help themselves. Salvation begins with self-rescue.","Yes. Yes, they were people who had helped themselves and rescued themselves. That was why they had survived!","The boys and girls wiped away their tears and rallied their spirits.","âCome on! Letâs practice our superpowers!â","âThere are so many of us! We donât need rescuing!â","âThatâs right!â","The parents and teachers exchanged glances.","They would wait and see.","It wasnât that they were afraid to act, nor that they distrusted the resolute-looking young woman on television.","It was simply that they were only a group formed by combining the residents of several communities. How much strength could they really have?","They would wait and see.","Several adults were responsible for protecting so many minors. They could not make decisions lightly.","For now, the school appeared to be a relatively stable safe zone.","There were actually quite a few survivors still trapped inside the office buildings in the city center.","More than a dozen people were trapped in one company office.","The company had been burglarized before. In a fit of anger, the owner had installed a steel security door outside the companyâs main entrance. During the second zombie outbreak, it became a barrier between life and death.","More than twenty survivors had hidden inside the office.","For the past several days, they had been drinking from a few barrels of bottled water and the water in the ownerâs luxurious fish tank.","They had tomatoes and celery to eat.","All the office plants were rented. Ownership belonged to the landscaping company, which was also responsible for their maintenance and upkeep.","As it happened, on August 29, a landscaper had finished tending the plants at several companies in the same building and then arrived at this one. That was how he ended up trapped inside with the people there.","This rural middle-aged man awakened a wood-type superpower.","Even luckier, the administrative manager had seen someone selling vegetables by the roadside on her way to work that morning. The vegetables were cheap and fresh in the morning, so she had bought a bagful of tomatoes and celery.","The wood-type uncle began propagating the tomatoes and celery to make food for everyone.","But by the next day, he could no longer propagate anything.","If this had been Song Jingshuo, with no one there to guide him, he would have been completely stumped.","Fortunately, the uncle wasnât some finance guy from a major city. He had gotten a job at the landscaping company precisely because he was good at growing plants.","After thinking it over, the uncle understood. Rapid propagation had depleted the nutrients in the soil of the plant pots. They needed fertilizer.","The boss had survived too.","The uncle gave him a choice: everyoneâs urine and fecesâor the arowana in his fish tank.","The boss didnât want to eat shit, so, suppressing his heartbreak, he chose to sacrifice his beloved arowana.","The employees: âBoss, your contribution is immeasurable.â","And so, they managed to hold out for seven days.","On the seventh day, everyone sat in the reception area, watching Jiang Cheng speak on the television mounted on the wall.","The boss sighed and stood up. âAll right. Time to save ourselves.â","âBut we only have one person with a wood-type superpower. How are we supposed to save ourselves? We donât even have any decent weapons, let alone armor.â","Armor was the most important thing.","You could grab a chair and, at a stretch, call it a weapon.","But without armor, humans and zombies were on completely unequal footing.","âAhem!â the boss said. âIf we donât have armor, then weâll just make some.â","With one hand resting on an abstractly designed metal chair, the boss suddenly made it begin to change shape. Slowly, it formed the shape of a suit of armor.","The employees: ââ¦â","The boss: âI actually just realized I had a superpower.â","The employees: ââ¦â","Yeah, right.","Heâd just been saving all his scheming for office politics.","Truly, no businessman was free of treachery. He kept his trump card hidden until the very last moment.","What a sly old fox.","They already had the materials needed to make armor and weapons.","The company had a fitness room, and all the equipment inside was made of metal. There was more than enough.","After all, working out was also known as âpumping iron.â","And the boss was a fitness fanatic.","But while everyone watched the boss huff and puff as he made the armor, someone said, âEven with armor, itâll still be dangerous. Can we make something like a turtle shellâa cover we can carry over our heads while we walk?â","âThat would be so heavy. Would we even be able to move?â","âWhat if we attached the wheels from the office chairs?â","âHuh?â","The boss stopped and thought for a moment. âLetâs try it!â"]},{"number":149,"title":"Chapter 149: 0149","paragraphs":["The anti-theft steel door that had been closed for seven days swung open.","Out rolled several inverted pen holders.","They really resembled pen holders, made of iron with ventilation holes all over them. However, they were turned upside down, and beneath them were wheels taken from computer chairs.","One could see people's feet.","There were probably four or five people in each \"pen holder\".","It couldn't hold more. If it did, the \"pen holder\" would have to be made bigger, and it might not fit into the elevator.","If there were fewer people, more \"pen holders\" would be needed, and the total amount of iron in the fitness room would be insufficient. They also needed it to make weapons and armor.","The boss had made a total of six \"pen holders\" in all.","As the door opened, the \"pen holders\" gingerly rolled out. There were no zombies in sight outside. The few zombies from a few days ago were nowhere to be found.","Just as they thought this, they rounded the corner at the end and found out: Oh, they were all gathered in the elevator hall.","Damn it!","Several zombies rushed forward and slammed into the \"pen holders\".","\"Ouch! Ouch! Ouch!\"","The boss had installed handholds inside the \"pen holders\" so that everyone had something to grab onto. Fortunately, this way, the people inside the \"pen holders\" that were hit didn't fall over.","\"Form the formation!\" the boss roared.","Before going out, everyone had a brainstorming session on what to do if they encountered zombies while rolling around in these \"pen holders\".","They had already come up with a set of countermeasures.","Several \"pen holders\" shouted in unison to synchronize their steps and rammed into other zombies.","Two \"pen holders\" joined forces to ram a targeted zombie: \"Push harder! Push harder!\"","The people inside used all their strength to pin this zombie against the wall: \"Mr. Xu! Mr. Xu! Hurry up!\"","While the other \"pen holders\" blocked the other zombies, the \"pen holder\" where Mr. Xu was in quickly rolled up to the pinned zombie.","Suddenly, a shovel-like blade protruded from the \"pen holder\" and shot out horizontally, directly slicing off the zombie's head.","They followed this method one after another. First, the crowd worked together to subdue the zombies, and then Mr. Xu, who had the gold-based superpower, was responsible for beheading them.","Soon, all the zombies in the elevator hall were taken out.","There were four passenger elevators, and each could only accommodate one \"pen holder\". But it didn't matter. When they pushed open the fire door beside it, there was a spacious cargo elevator inside that could hold two \"pen holders\" at the same time.","Everyone got into the elevators.","As the elevators descended, everyone's hearts were pounding a bit. After watching so many horror movies, they always thought there would be monsters as soon as the elevator doors opened.","Fortunately, life isn't a movie. When the elevator doors opened on the third basement floor, there were really no zombies in sight.","Everyone heaved a sigh of relief.","But they relaxed too soon.","As the \"pen holders\" started moving, the wheels made a huge scraping noise on the garage floor!","And there was a huge echo!","From afar, they could see zombies running towards them.","Everyone: \"...\"","\"Damn it!\" Mr. Xu, who usually boasted about having studied abroad and liked to mix foreign words into his speech, cursed in his hometown dialect. \"Come here!\"","The \"pen holders\" rushed to gather together, and several of them quickly merged into a giant \"pen holder\".","It was like a small house, and all the colleagues met up inside.","Mr. Xu really thought there was no hope.","In a company, if only the boss is working and the employees just stand by and watch, what hope is there?","\"Well, you're the only one with superpowers,\" the employees showered him with flattery. \"You're destined to be the boss, the leader, the one who will lead us to victory!\"","\"That's the capable taking on more responsibilities!\"","\"So that's why someone like you can start from scratch and become a self - made millionaire.\"","Mr. Xu was pleased by the flattery and crafted a crescent shovel.","There was a girl named Jiang Cheng on TV who also held a crescent shovel.","She wore shiny silver armor, and the crescent shovel glowed under the studio lights. It was both retro and sci - fi.","Everyone thought the shovel looked very practical at the time and suggested that Mr. Xu make a copy.","\"Here, yours,\" Mr. Xu said as he finished making one and handed it to an employee.","He made another one and handed it over, saying, \"Here, yours!\"","The zombies in the distance stopped moving because the noise had stopped. Since they were far away, they gradually stopped in their tracks and wandered around in place.","Mr. Xu was extremely busy inside the small iron house. He made one after another.","At first, they had planned to make all the weapons before going out. But after the \"pen holders\" were made, they found that carrying these weapons inside could easily hurt others, so they asked Mr. Xu to put them away.","Now they were being made on - the - spot.","Mr. Xu was so tired that he was sweating profusely. As he was making them, his head started to hurt, and his nose started to bleed.","Immediately, seven or eight employees took out tissues from their pockets and wiped the blood from Mr. Xu's nose. \"You're going to level up, Mr. Xu. Hold on! They said on TV that this is how you level up! This is the prelude to your leveling up!\"","Good employees are supposed to urge their boss to grow.","Mr. Xu made the weapons until his ears hurt. Finally, he finished making them for everyone.","Everyone had armor and a weapon.","Alright, guys, follow me.","The \"small house\" opened, and everyone walked out cautiously.","\"Mr. Xu, where's your car?\"","\"In Area 4.\"","\"That's a bit far. Mine is in Area 1.\"","Everyone planned to escape by car.","Suddenly, the supervisor pulled Mr. Xu aside. \"Mr. Xu, look at that car!\"","Everyone looked over, and their eyes lit upâthere was a 16 - seat medium - sized bus!","Wasn't this much better than everyone driving several small cars separately?","Mr. Xu said, \"We don't have the keys.\"","The supervisor said, \"Aren't you a gold - based superpower user? The lock is also made of metal. Give it a try.\"","Mr. Xu said, \"But just opening the door isn't enough. How can we start the car without the keys?\"","The supervisor went, \"Hey!\" and said, \"Strange, I seem to have superpowers too. Let me try to start the car.\"","The supervisor smiled obsequiously and held up a finger, with a small cluster of electric current crackling at the tip.","Mr. Xu: \"...\"","The employees: \"...\"","The gardener: \"...\"","If you're not from the same company, you won't be in the same boat.","They were all about mutual mistrust, lack of unity, and scheming against each other.","Wasn't this a kind of corporate culture?","The door opened smoothly, and the supervisor sat in the driver's seat and tried to start the car with his \"newly - awakened\" electricity - based superpower.","Everyone sat in the car and started discussing. \"There are so many zombies outside. We need to add some protection to the car.\"","\"Use iron nets to protect the glass.\"","\"The iron net has no offensive power. Use iron spikes. You know what iron caltrops are like. Make it look like a hedgehog or a porcupine.\"","\"That won't work. Zombies don't feel pain. Even if they're pierced, it doesn't matter. They might even get stuck on the car. We have to be able to decapitate them.\"","Human wisdom is the same everywhere.","Although they hadn't seen the \"Blade Car\" that Jiang Cheng and the others had later modified, their discussion result was to make a blade - equipped car.","Mr. Xu had two wads of tissue stuffed in his nostrils and was sitting in the passenger seat, taking a rest.","As long as he stopped, the superpower he had just consumed would gradually recover.","He squinted at the supervisor, who kept failing again and again. \"Can you do it?\"","The supervisor was also sweating profusely. \"Don't be impatient. I'll try again.\"","The engine started up and then died out again and again.","In the distance, that zombie was attracted by the sound and staggered forward, stopping and starting repeatedly. Finally, when it got closer and spotted these fresh pieces of flesh, it began to pounce forward.","The employees found the crescent shovel useful the first time they used it.","The strong - built ones could chop off a zombie's head with a single strike.","\"Who invented this? It's so useful!\"","\"You're stupid. This is an ancient cold - weapon.\"","\"Sorry, I meant who discovered its effectiveness. Not every ancient weapon is suitable for chopping off zombie heads.\"","After dealing with the zombie, the employees opened the passenger - side door. \"Mr. Xu! Mr. Xu!\"","Mr. Xu, who was still pinching his nose and hadn't fully rested, was helped out of the car by the employees. \"You'll have to endure a bit more hardship.\"","Mr. Xu let out a long sigh to the sky.","Mr. Xu transformed the car into a blade - equipped vehicle.","The windows were also covered with iron mesh.","These weren't difficult tasks. The hard part was sharpening the blades.","He was on the verge of exhaustion. The delicate operation was extremely tiring! Finally, he managed to make the \"blades\" around the car body sharp, and it was as if he had almost lost half his life.","His ears were killing him.","The director finally managed to start the car!","He had been hiding his ability and hadn't practiced much. His superpower was really weak.","But precisely because it was weak, unlike Guo Jun, he didn't damage the car's circuit board with an overly strong electric current at once.","He tried again and again, gradually increasing the electric current, and finally got the car started.","The employees cheered, as if they had landed a huge order.","Wiping the sweat from his forehead, the director said sincerely with admiration, \"It still has to be you. You're so powerful right after awakening. Look at me, I'm so weak.\"","Both of them had their own independent offices. These days, they had been sleeping in their offices.","In the dead of night, Mr. Xu quietly practiced his gold - based superpower without making a sound.","The director couldn't do the same because the electric current would make a crackling sound when it got a little stronger, which was especially noticeable at night.","As a result of hiding and not practicing, one was weak, and the other was even weaker.","\"Let's go! Let's set off!\"","The car started moving.","Except for the one they had just dealt with, there were hardly any zombies in this area. They even thought there were no zombies in the underground garage.","Who would have known that near the exit, there was a huge crowd of them!","There were also several overturned cars, which had crashed into the neatly parked ones.","The bloodstains had turned a dark and deep color.","It turned out that some people had been trying to break out. Unfortunately, small cars were easily climbed on by second - generation and third - generation zombies.","The cars overturned, and the people died.","More and more zombies kept appearing...","The wisdom of the masses is powerful.","The blade - equipped vehicle showed its might. From the side window, one could see zombie heads flying off, and the dark - brown viscous blood splashing all over the window.","When this minibus successfully broke out of the underground garage and saw the setting sun outside, everyone burst into cheers again!","\"Charge! Charge!\"","\"Which way should we go?\"","\"North! The high - tech new area is in the north!\"","\"Which road should we take?\"","\"Any road will do. First, get on the Fifth Ring Road! The exit at Wan'an Bridge!\"","\"What was the name of that community?\"","\"Youth Apartment!\"","\"Yes, Youth Apartment.\"","\"Alright, let's go! Our destination is the Youth Apartment!\""]},{"number":150,"title":"Chapter 150: 0150","paragraphs":["Of the more than five hundred people rescued from the television station, some said they wanted to go home.","Li Jiangbing asked just one question: âHow are you planning to get there?â","No one had anything to say after that.","It simply wasnât realistic.","Even those who wanted to go home would have to wait until later.","These people were all weak in the legs, with vacant stares. Some kept muttering to themselves, while others cried and laughed for no apparent reason. None of them looked entirely sane. If they were allowed to leave on their own, they would be dead the moment they stepped outside the television station compound.","For now, the people from the High-Tech New District planned to take all five hundred of them back to the development zone. The first problem was transportation.","The two hundred members of the High-Tech New District team had driven four large 535 buses, each carrying fifty people.","Each bus could squeeze in as many as one hundred and fifty to two hundred passengers. Without packing them in too tightly, another fifty people per bus would be no problem. That would take care of two hundred more.","Yue Chao said, âThe station has shuttle buses.â","The television stationâs employees lived in various districts across S City. The station had opened sixteen routes in total, with sixteen shuttle buses. All of them were thirty-six-seat coaches.","Counting the aisle, each one could manage fifty people without a problem.","After a final discussion, they decided to take six coaches.","There were too many vehicles, and fuel would only be wasted. They would pack as many people as possible into each bus.","Just then, when they looked outside through the large hole in the second-floor wall, they saw several zombies wandering into the courtyard after Director Guoâs death.","Earlier, when the convoy from the High-Tech New District had entered, the vehicles had made a tremendous racket, but the zombies had not followed them in. They had simply scattered on their own.","âMind control,â Zhao Yi said.","Gao Yuxuan agreed. âThe range probably isnât small either. It covers a certain area and has already formed a domain.â","Zhou Wang felt that he wasnât actually that old, and he had no trouble communicating with the other people from the Youth Apartments.","The problem was that he often couldnât understand what these two were saying. They were always tossing out strange terms he had never heard before.","Su Yu used her protective shield as an example and explained it to him. Zhou Wang more or less understood. He rubbed the back of his neck and said, âThis isnât science anymore. What are these things, demons and monsters?â","Gao Yuxuan said, âWhy does it have to be demons and monsters? This is the evolution of the human brain. Brother Zhou, you should read more science fiction. What do you usually read?â","Zhao Yi was firmly on Gao Yuxuanâs side. âIâve always believed that human beings never stopped evolving. The next direction of human evolution should be the brain. I never imagined Iâd live to witness it with my own eyes. If you trace our superpowers back to their source, they all come from the brain.â","Zombies had brains too.","A zombie was basically a dead thing. The only part that seemed alive was its brain, directing that dead body as it walked beneath the sun.","The human brain had developed superpowers, and the brains of zombies had advanced as well. The newly mutated zombies could now control ordinary zombies.","Zhao Yi was deeply worried.","Wu Jiancheng led people in searching every floor. They found more than a dozen additional survivors on the upper levels.","Ironically, their survival was thanks to Director Guo.","Director Guo had eaten all the other zombies. They had nowhere to hide. Whenever he summoned them with his mental power, they obediently came to him and allowed themselves to be eaten.","As a result, there were no zombies left upstairs, giving these people room to survive.","Director Guo was enormous, and he made an especially loud commotion whenever he moved. Whenever he went upstairs, the survivors would immediately hide. There were many nooks and crannies that Director Guoâs huge body couldnât enter, so he missed these people.","Besides, he had an entire granary of people to eat at his leisure.","In the end, all four 535 buses and all six coaches were crammed full of people.","Cui Haiyang and the other metal-element superpowered individuals modified the coaches into blade vehicles as well. Then everyone set off together for the High-Tech New District.","They had come from the city government building, but they took a different route back.","There were zombies everywhere along the road. The drivers were thrilled, flooring the gas and plowing straight into them. Heads burst into the air one after another, while corpses fell to the ground and had their intestines and chunks of feces crushed out by the tires.","Gao Yuxuan and Cui Haiyang spent the entire journey sitting together and discussing how to turn the vehicles into new weapons.","During the previous disaster, they had also driven large vehicles around, ramming and crushing zombies. Now that they had seen how effective blade vehicles were, they realized they were especially suited to clearing areas in the city center where zombies were densely packed.","They were absolutely devastating weapons for attacking groups.","Even small cars could be modified this way. Gao Yuxuan badly wanted to drive a small car covered in blades alone, charging into a horde of zombies and fighting his way back out.","Just imagining it made his blood race.","When they passed a gas station, the convoy stopped to refuel.","The people from the High-Tech New District had become fuel hoarders. Whenever they saw a gas station, they were certain to fill up.","There were two gas stations in the development zone, and they needed to conserve their own fuel. Whenever possible, they used fuel from the city first.","Zhao Yi asked Jiang Cheng, âCan you store fuel in your space?â","âThere has to be a container,â Jiang Cheng said.","Jiang Cheng had already tested it. Things like water and fire could not be placed directly into her storage space.","But a bottle or bucket of water could be stored.","If someone lit a ball of paper in a bowl, she could store the bowl and the flame together.","However, a puddle of water on the ground, or a ball of flame held by a fire-element superpowered individual, could not be stored.","[Unable to define the boundaries.]","That was the information that floated through her mind.","Before her memories had been locked away, she must have been extremely familiar with her storage space and known all its rules. Now, however, she had to figure everything out from the beginning.","When the bowl was taken back out, the fire had gone out.","Jiang Cheng deduced that this was because there was no oxygen in the space, so the fire could not continue burning.","The large steamed buns the aunties had made that morning were still lukewarm when they were taken out at noon. Heat dissipated, and time did not stop flowing inside the space.","Zhao Yi began seriously contemplating the nature of Jiang Chengâs space.","Watching him, Jiang Cheng suddenly felt that everything happening now was very strange.","If time had gone back two months, Jiang Cheng felt that she would never have casually revealed her superpower. At the very least, she would not have let anyone know its limitations.","She would have kept every advantage in her own hands and made sure no one knew her trump card.","Yes. That was the kind of person she was.","But now, she had calmly told Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan everything, trusting them completely.","When had she changed?","â¦Unable to define.","Jiang Cheng could not determine exactly how she had changed.","Some changes had no specific event or point in time. They happened unconsciously, little by little, through imperceptible influence.","Even so, everyone managed to find a large number of fuel drums in the gas stationâs storage room. They filled them all and had Jiang Cheng store them in her space.","There was even a giant zombie in that space of hers.","It could really hold a lot, Zhao Yi thought admiringly.","The convoy of ten large vehicles returned to the High-Tech New District in grand fashion.","The people who had stayed behind felt as if they were facing a formidable enemyâfor now, they had to prepare dinner for seven hundred people.","Song Jingshuo looked a little exhausted.","Of course he was exhausted!","âTry preparing food for several hundred people sometime,â Song Jingshuo said mournfully. âAnd you only get three hours to do it.â","It had nearly cost Song Jingshuo his life.","Everyone who had stayed behind was mobilized. Even the elderly men and women from Auspicious Garden came to help.","The stoves in the clubhouse were obviously not enough. The earth-element superpowered individuals set up cooking stoves directly in the small square, the metal-element superpowered individuals quickly made cooking utensils, and the fire-element superpowered individuals were responsible for stoking the flames.","Every potato and eggplant that Song Jingshuo had forced into rapid growth was as big as a basketball.","Everyone was given a vegetable peeler to peel the potatoes and eggplants. The potatoes were steamed and mashed, then sprinkled with salt and pepper. The eggplants were steamed into a mash and topped with garlic sauce.","The survivors lined up to receive metal mess tins.","Each person got a scoop of mashed potatoes, a scoop of mashed eggplant, a piece of braised pork, a scoop of rice, a bowl of seaweed soup, and a strawberry as large as a pear.","Compared with a proper meal, it was a little plain, but considering how many people there were and how little time they had, it was already quite good.","These five hundred people had even drunk urine before. What right did they have to complain?","They had eaten a small piece of compressed biscuit that afternoon. It had expanded in their stomachs and served as a good stopgap, giving their stomachs time to adjust. Now they were hungry again, so it was time to eat.","As a result, almost everyone refused the braised pork. Some even threw up.","The uncles and aunties were completely baffled.","âJust give the meat to our people,â Jiang Cheng told them with her arms folded. âItâs fine. Let them eat vegetarian for now. They may have to eat vegetarian for quite a while.â","Possibly for the rest of their lives.","Some memories simply couldnât be forgotten, no matter how hard one tried.","Song Jingshuo quietly asked Gao Yuxuan what had happened, and Gao Yuxuan told him.","Song Jingshuo had already learned from Wu Jianchengâs earlier phone call that a zombie had mutated into a giant, but he hadnât expected there to be so much more to the story.","These survivors were now refugees in the Technology New District.","The refugees found spots wherever they could and sat down right there to eat. No one complained about the dirt on the ground.","Compared with the broadcasting studio where they had spent seven days, the ground here was practically spotless.","Jiang Cheng asked Song Jingshuo, âHave you arranged somewhere for them to stay?â","âItâs arranged,â Song Jingshuo said with a nod. âTheyâll all be staying at Jixiang Jiayuan. We donât let outsiders into this area easily.â","Song Jingshuo was indeed dependable.","There were plenty of vacant apartments in the Youth Apartments, of course, but neither Jiang Cheng nor Song Jingshuo intended to let just anyone move in.","The Youth Apartments were the core of the entire Technology New District, and many things had to be carried out there. The unity and understanding among the four hundred residents had been forged through two waves of zombie disasters. It was best not to introduce any destabilizing elements.","Zhou Wang was also willing to take these people in.","He now understood ancient rulers especially well. After waging war, they had to let the country recover and give the common people time to have children.","Population. Population was incredibly important.","There was no way for Zhou Wang to make the more than one hundred elderly residents of the complex disappear, so he could only bring in people from outside to help share the burden.","The last time, they had accepted more than thirty middle-school students and two teachers from a private school. This time, there were another five hundred able-bodied adults, and they already knew that several of them had supernatural abilities.","There were probably more. Many people were in poor mental condition and werenât speaking up yet.","They could let them recover first.","At the food distribution station, a group of people holding metal plates were swallowing hard and asking pitifully, âCould we have another piece of meat?â","The aunties were delighted!","They had assumed that these refugees hadnât eaten properly in six or seven days and had felt so sorry for them that they had gone to considerable trouble to cook all this braised pork. Yet the refugees hadnât appreciated it at all. One after another, they insisted on eating vegetarian food and couldnât even stand the smell of meat.","All the auntiesâ kindness had gone to waste.","It was enough to make anyone lose heart.","Then, all of a sudden, a group of people showed up who wanted meat. The aunties couldnât have been happier.","âHere you go, here you go! Iâll give you a few extra pieces. Is that enough?â","Mr. Xu was practically in tears. âEnough, enough.â","Mr. Xu, who normally ate so much lobster and sea cucumber that he was sick of them, never imagined that one day he would shed tears over a few pieces of braised pork.","This group was Mr. Xu and his companions, who had struggled their way out of an office building and driven over to seek refuge in the Technology New District.","They had driven straight toward the Technology New District, but since they werenât familiar with the area, they followed the road signs and ended up at the industrial park.","Fortunately, the zombies there were all inside the various companiesâ buildings or factory courtyards, so the roads themselves were relatively safe. Their blade vehicle fought its way through, only to take a wrong turn and end up in the western section of the residential district.","There was no one in the western section.","There werenât even any zombies. The place looked like a ghost town, a vision straight out of the apocalypse.","It was nearly dark by the time Mr. Xu and the others finally reached the eastern section. They made their way to Deqingli, asked for directions, and eventually managed to find the Youth Apartments.","There were so many people around the Youth Apartments. What were they all doing?","So many of them were holding metal plates. Werenât those the kind used in cafeterias?","They looked around and spotted a young man in a security guardâs uniform among the crowd.","âHey, young man! Young man!â Mr. Xu and the others went over to speak to Little Fang. âCould we ask youââ","Little Fang turned around and nearly gagged from the smell.","One look told him everything. Their clothes clearly hadnât been changed in days. Their faces were reasonably clean, but every time one of them opened his mouth, the stench of seven days without brushing their teeth came rushing out. They were obviously refugees.","âOver there, over there. Get your plates there,â Little Fang said, pinching his nose as he pointed. âThen go over there for food. Someone will handle lodging later. Eat first.â","And that was how Mr. Xu and his companions, in a daze, joined the ranks of the refugees in the Technology New District.","They ate braised pork with tears in their eyes."]},{"number":151,"title":"Chapter 151: 0151","paragraphs":["After dinner, Mr. Xu and the others lined up with everyone else to collect towels, toothbrushes, toothpaste, soap, and underwear.","The women were also given sanitary pads and bras.","Everything had been purchased in bulk through Pinduoduo by the people who had stayed behind, after they received calls from the front lines. They had driven forklifts out to collect the deliveries.","Mr. Xu had never worn this kind of supermarket underwear before, but at least he had something clean to change into. The pair he was wearing had been on him for seven days and had gotten shit on them.","Once they had collected their supplies, they were led out through the communityâs east gate.","âWait, werenât we told there were plenty of vacant apartments?â they asked.","The people maintaining order at the scene were mostly elderly residents and children. The children looked like middle school students. One of them answered, âThere are. Just follow us.â","They led the newcomers across the road outside the east gate and straight through the west gate of the community opposite.","âThis is Jixiang Gardens. Everyoneâs being housed here for now.â","âArenât we staying at Youth Apartments?â Mr. Xu asked. âWe thought everyone was staying there.â","âI wish I could live at Youth Apartments too,â the child said.","Mr. Xu: â?â","He had no idea what was going on.","The children were students from the private boarding school they had rescued earlier.","By now, the students had figured out the situation. They understood that Youth Apartments was calling the shots in this area.","Among the middle school-aged residents who owned apartments in Jixiang Gardens, there were two peopleâa boy and a girlâwho both had superpowers. They had also joined the team based at Youth Apartments. Everyone was envious of them.","In everyoneâs eyes, Youth Apartments was a place to yearn for, somewhere they all wanted to join.","But apparently, they didnât accept just anyone. Sure enough, this latest group of survivors was entirely taken in by Jixiang Gardens.","The plan was to fill Jixiang Gardens first, then move on to Yujing Xiang Gardens.","The locks on the doors of the vacant apartments had already been opened.","The elderly residents and middle school students assigned everyone their apartments. Generally, people were allocated by beds: however many people could sleep in an apartment was how many people were assigned to it.","Among the refugees from the television station were several couples. They were assigned master bedrooms with double beds, while single people were sent to spare bedrooms.","If they were unlucky, they might end up in a childâs room decorated in a princess or comic-book theme.","When it came to Mr. Xuâs group, they were asked what their relationship was. Once the elderly resident learned that they were familiar colleagues, he assigned Mr. Xu and the director to a master bedroom with a double bed.","The apartment was a fairly spacious four-bedroom unit. Apart from the study, all three bedrooms had double beds.","In the end, six people from the company were assigned to the apartment. The others were housed on the same floor, and the gardener was placed with them as well.","During the assignment process, one of the elderly residents kept a written register and asked, âDoes anyone have superpowers?â","It turned out that there was one metal-type, one electric-type, and one wood-type ability user. The elderly man was delighted.","âThe wood-type one has to start working tomorrow. Good heavens, thatâs a lot of mouths to feed. Xiao Song, Old Lin, and Old Qian have been worked half to death, forcing all those potatoes to sprout for you.â","The gardener had no objections and nodded.","He had been a rural laborer who came to the city to find work. Luckily, instead of having to haul bricks on construction sites, he had found a position at this landscaping company thanks to his experience growing crops.","It was actually work he enjoyed.","In the past, when he moved from office building to office building for various jobs, all those men and women had treated him like he was invisible. Almost no one had ever greeted him or spoken to him.","Now, everything was different. In just these seven days, everyone had been fawning over him.","The gardener had already figured it out: these days, food and drink were the real hard currency.","Back at Youth Apartments, once all the refugees had been taken away and there were no outsiders left in the complex, the east gate was shut and locked. Jiang Cheng then took out the giant zombie.","The team members had all seen it with their own eyes, but although the people who had stayed behind had heard about it, seeing it in person still scared them half to death.","âHoly shit.â","Everyone gathered around the enormous creature, and a chorus of âHoly shit!â rose from the crowd.","Song Jingshuo sighed. âIs heaven trying to wipe out humanity?â","âOf course not,â Jiang Cheng said. âIf it wanted humanity wiped out, it wouldnât have given us superpowers.â","Song Jingshuo: ââ¦Fair point.â","News of Shen Yuehongâs situation was passed along to the people who had stayed behind by the team members, causing another uproar.","Shen Yuehong had fans everywhere. She was warm and approachable, and men and women of every age liked her.","Several of the young women at Youth Apartments learned the whole story and angrily kicked Director Guo.","âThat bastard! Heâs not even human!â","âWeâll have to start rescuing people everywhere,â Song Jingshuo said.","âWe have to,â Jiang Cheng replied.","Everyone had already reached a consensus on this at the previous meeting.","This was a human world. First and foremost, there had to be people for a society to exist. Only with enough people could a complete society be rebuilt.","The moment everyone agreed to establish a government, they also accepted the responsibility that came with it.","Song Jingshuo folded his arms and watched everyoneâs commotion.","âIâm honestly surprised youâre this kind of person.â","He meant it.","Selfless and devoted to the greater good.","Song Jingshuo had never imagined that Jiang Cheng would go this far. He had never expected her to be this sort of person.","âWhatâs wrong with your brain?â Jiang Cheng asked.","Song Jingshuo: ââ¦â","He turned to look at her.","Jiang Cheng rolled her eyes. âI already became friends with you.â","Donât you know what kind of person you are?","Song Jingshuo: ââ¦â","For once, he had no way to argue.","The two of them had been the first to realize that they were kindred spirits.","They had quickly set aside their rivalry and formed a powerful alliance. Smart people like them knew that one plus one was greater than two.","Li Jiangbing possessed a keen understanding of how to survive in society. He knew that life would be easier if he followed smart people.","As it happened, Jiang Cheng was a woman who wanted to hold the authority among a large group of men, and she needed someone to back her with force.","And so, one plus one plus one was born.","At the beginning, the Iron Triangle had come together purely because of mutual benefit.","Only after facing zombies again and again did they gradually come to understand one another, develop trust, and ultimately become true friends who would risk their lives for each other.","But they also had to remember what kind of people they truly were.","Jiang Chengâs eyes were deep and dark.","Song Jingshuo was silent for a moment.","âThen youâ¦â","âThose in a position must attend to the duties of that position,â Jiang Cheng said frankly. âI simply want this position.â","It was a reason Song Jingshuo could completely understand and accept.","Even if the position offered no material benefits, the sense of control it provided was itself an accomplishment in life.","Song Jingshuo had once been that kind of person too. But perhaps because he now had Jiang Cheng, he no longer had any desire to seek power.","In fact, he was entirely satisfied with the current situation.","As it was confirmed that no one had survived in the government, he increasingly understood that this time there would be no government support like before, with endless supplies being transported in from elsewhere.","Now, they couldnât even reach the various government departments outside S City. No one answered the phones.","This time, they were clearly in it for the long haul.","He hadnât become a farmer. He had gained control over everyoneâs food supply.","Aunt Pan had been right.","Once all the unnecessary splendor and excess of society had been stripped away, the most important people were the ones who made things and the ones who grew things.","Even the superpowers humanity had been granted seemed to possess an underlying logic.","âWhat are your thoughts on supplying food in the future?â Jiang Cheng asked.","âPotatoes,â Song Jingshuo replied.","âWeâre refugees now. We canât still be dreaming about delicacies, can we?â","âPotatoes are the greatest blessing in times of famine.â","âThereâs one more thing,â Song Jingshuo said quietly. âIn a couple of days, Iâll have the strawberry fields plowed under under the pretext of planting some other crop.â","âFruit will be rationed from now on.â","âAs a luxury item and a reward.â","âWeâll adjust it depending on the situation. Vegetables might be rationed too.â","Jiang Cheng glanced at him, the corners of her lips curling upward as she held out her fist.","Song Jingshuo lightly bumped his fist against hers.","The best teammates were those who didnât need to say much. A hint was all it took.","More likely, they simply happened to give voice to thoughts the other had already considered.","âI discussed this with Zhou Wang all the way here today,â Jiang Cheng said. âLetâs give these people a day off for now, so they can adjust.â","âAfter that, weâll need to change things. Communal meals definitely wonât work.â","âRight.â Song Jingshuo nodded. âHistory has already proven that.â","A society could not be flat.","People could be equal in terms of rights, but they could never receive exactly the same treatment.","That was because the contributions each person made were destined to be different.","Those who were capable could do more, but doing more had to mean receiving more.","A stable society necessarily needed clearly differentiated levels and a structured hierarchy.","Jiang Cheng said, âWe have to guarantee better treatment for our own people.â","âNo problem,â Song Jingshuo replied.","The residents of the Youth Apartments had already settled into a working system during the first disaster.","This time, four hundred people had left their posts without hesitation and defied their superiors to return to the Youth Apartments simply because of a single mass message from Jiang Chengâand survived as a result.","How could that not count as a selection process?","Those who had not trusted Jiang Cheng enough, or who had been too weak and hesitant to act, had been filtered out.","The four hundred residents who had returned were incomparable to the others in terms of organization, discipline, trust in Jiang Cheng, and willingness to obey her.","It was no longer just a triangle of power.","There were Cui Haiyang, Su Yu, Wu Jiancheng, Zhang Lesi, Zhao Yi, Gao Yuxuan, and Aunt Pan.","As well as outside support from Guo Jun, Zhou Wang, and Little Huang.","Together, they had formed a solid structure, with everyone finding their own place within it.","The four hundred people from the Youth Apartments were both their foundation and their core.","Beneath them, priority could be given to the original residents of Jixiang Jiayuan. There werenât many of them, and most were elderly. Besides, they had a certain sentimental bond with the place.","The superpowered individuals and able-bodied laborers among the refugees would have to earn better treatment or status through their own efforts.","Those who had nothing would not starve. They would have potatoes to eat, and they would not be bitten to death by zombies, because they were protected by the collective.","Under the circumstances, simply being alive was already something to be grateful for.","After the day ended, Jiang Cheng returned to her apartment, took a shower, and changed into comfortable clothes.","She switched on the floor lamp beside the recliner and picked up the top book from the stack on the floor, continuing to read from the place marked by a folded page.","Mo Li leaped onto her lap, then squeezed through the gap beneath the book and settled against her chest.","The longer small animals were raised, the more attached they became to the people who cared for them, much like children.","Jiang Cheng gently scratched the catâs head with her fingertips. Mo Li began to purr contentedly.","Jiang Cheng stroked the cat and read her book.","She had not told Song Jingshuo everything she was thinking.","Why, exactly, did she want to claim that position?","Jiang Cheng suspected that the zombie virus had most likely followed her into this world.","She had been sent here to undergo a trial.","The first time, she had not even left the Technology New District.","The second time, the governmentâwhich had played a major role in the first disasterâhad been specifically wiped out.","So what, exactly, would count as victory this time?","It absolutely could not mean merely scraping by alone, or with a small group of people.","Absolutely not.","Jiang Cheng did not believe that the organization that had sent her into this world could have such a narrow vision.","She needed to broaden her horizons and think on a grander scale.","The government was gone. Then she would take its place, shoulder that responsibility, and become the person others followed.","Everything was for the sake of victory."]},{"number":152,"title":"Chapter 152: 0152","paragraphs":["Although he had to squeeze into the same bed as the director, Mr. Xu slept more comfortably that night than he had all week.","He brushed his teeth, took a shower, and changed into clean underwear.","He slept soundly until dawn without a single dream.","The next morning, some middle school students went door to door, announcing, âCome downstairs to collect rice. One share per household. Bring a bowl.â","Everyone poked their heads out and greeted one another.","âHow did you sleep last night?â","Their dirty clothes were beyond wearing, so everyone rummaged through the original homeownersâ wardrobes for something to wear. Not every household had clothes in suitable sizes, and people inevitably ended up dressed in all sorts of odd combinations.","Once they were dressed, they took their bowls downstairs.","Zhou Wang presided over the distribution while the elderly residents helped portion everything out.","Zhou Wang picked up a megaphone. âPlease cherish every grain of rice. Today is a day for everyone to rest and recover, and itâs also the only day youâll be able to collect rice.â","Mr. Xuâs ears immediately perked up. âWhat about tomorrow?â","âStarting tomorrow, weâll be providing potatoes,â Zhou Wang said. âEveryone needs to understand one thing: this is no longer your home. You canât go back to your homes because theyâre overrun by zombies. In the old days, what weâre doing would have been called fleeing from disaster. These days, weâre all refugees.â","âNo oneâs going to starve. Potatoes are filling.â","âDonât worry about too much just yet. Collect todayâs rice first. Youâve all been through a lot, so take the day to rest. Weâll discuss the details tomorrow.â","Everyone lined up to collect their rice.","At Auspicious Garden, they didnât serve meals from one communal kitchen. Every apartment had its own kitchen, stove, cookware, and tableware. Once people received their rice and vegetables, they could take them home and cook for themselves.","Each apartment housed three to five people.","Those who didnât know how to cook could team up with their neighbors. They would have to work that out among themselves.","Zhou Wang couldnât wipe everyoneâs backs or play nursemaid to them.","At most, he would look after the elderly and children. As for the adults, they had all been out in society long enough to take care of themselves. If anyone was still naÃ ̄ve enough to cling to fantasies, Zhou Wang would be the one to snap them out of it.","âIâll call out the names of the people who are to come downstairs and see me after theyâve eaten,â Zhou Wang said, raising the megaphone again.","The first person he called was the horticulturist who had come with the people from Mr. Xuâs company.","After breakfast, Jiang Cheng went down to the underground parking garage with Song Jingshuo.","The storage area that had once been used for supplies was back in operation.","âIâve been waiting for you to come take a look,â Song Jingshuo said, both hands in his pockets.","The space was packed to the brim. It wasnât the only one, either. Several blast doors had been put into use, carving out multiple spaces to serve as warehouses.","In fact, once everyone had started working in teams and Song Jingshuo had left the field team to remain behind and handle logistics, he had already begun dispatching people to transport supplies here from Mai Duoduo bit by bit, like ants carrying food.","âBefore, we only had to consider the people already here.â Song Jingshuo looked around, surveying the results of his work. âNow, all of a sudden, we have so many more people. And thereâll be even more in the future. They need all kinds of things.â","He was tall, handsome, and carried himself with an arrogant, cocky air.","Jiang Cheng gave him a thumbs-up. âJingshuo, youâre amazing. Youâre the most handsome man in the whole complex.â","Nothing about his face, physique, or future made her happier than seeing him actually get things done. That was what truly deserved her praise.","Song Jingshuo had already seen right through her. He turned his head away. âTsk.â","Yang Xinyan felt terrible.","She and two other homeowners were responsible for the three hotline phones. Since last night, the text messages had been pouring in nonstop.","There were too many pleas for help to count.","âWeâre at Huasheng Building. There are eighty-two of us, and weâve secured the seventeenth, eighteenth, and nineteenth floors. Please help us!â","âIâm alone at Tianlong Center! Iâve been hiding everywhere I can. Please save me! There are zombies everywhere! Please, Iâm begging you!â","âIâm a teacher at Haifan Elementary School. I have seven adults and more than sixty children here, all elementary school students. Please save the children!â","Every message sounded like a desperate scream.","Some people called directly. As Jiang Cheng had instructed, calls from mobile numbers were hung up immediately. Calls from landlines were answered, questioned, and documented.","That was even harder to bear than reading the messages.","The people on the phone often had hoarse voices, and all their panic and desperation came through loud and clear.","But the message that affected Yang Xinyan most wasnât even a plea for help.","âThis is my fatherâs phone number. He worked for the municipal government. Is he still alive?â","Yang Xinyanâs fingers stiffened as she typed her reply.","âIâm sorry. No one from the municipal government survived. We found this phone and are using it as a communications tool. Iâm sorry.â","The other person replied soon after.","âOkay. Itâs all right.â","âLittle Yang? Little Yang?â","A hand waved in front of her face, then finally landed on her shoulder with a pat.","Yang Xinyan looked up and saw Manager Wang.","Manager Wang was carrying a bucket. These days, he did every odd job under the sun, always going wherever he was needed. But most of the time, he served as Song Jingshuoâs assistant.","âAre you all right?â Manager Wang asked with concern. âYou look out of it. Didnât sleep well last night?â","Yang Xinyan wiped at her eyes. âReading these messages is getting to me.â","Manager Wang leaned his large head over to take a look at the computer. He sighed and tried to comfort her. âYou canât think about all that. You need to think about how well weâre doing here.â","He pulled a strawberry from his pocket. âHere, eat this. Xiao Song says the strawberry fields are going to be cleared tomorrow. After that, fruit will be rationed.â","For the past two days, everyone had been free to pick strawberries.","âWhy?â Yang Xinyan asked.","âWe need to grow real food. Strawberries donât fill your stomach,â Manager Wang said. âDonât worry. Theyâre moving the strawberries into the south-facing apartments, so weâll still be able to eat them. We just wonât be able to pick them whenever we want.â","Manager Wang then asked about her work. âHow are you holding up?â","Yang Xinyan had been working hard for the past few days. She wasnât a homeowner but a property management employee, so she had to handle the basic duties of property management.","There was no one left in property management.","Aunt Pan had already left the property management team and become part of the combat force and labor pool for the complex.","That left Manager Wang, Little Fang the security guard, and Yang Xinyan handling property management.","The homeowners also took on work around the complex, but they rotated through different assignments. They might do one job today and another tomorrow. The three of them, however, were permanent staff. Yang Xinyan in particular was assigned a great deal of physically demanding work, and it was exhausting.","When Jiang Cheng said they needed someone to keep a close eye on the messages coming through the phones, Manager Wang immediately took the opportunity to put Yang Xinyan forward.","Yang Xinyan pointed at the computer. âJiang Cheng told me to sort them by location and start by selecting the areas with the largest groups of people.â","Manager Wang glanced at the endless stream of messages on the screen and hurried away. âIâm not looking, Iâm not looking.â","Anyone who read them would feel awful.","No wonder the girl looked so dazed.","Only people as tough as Jiang Cheng, Song Jingshuo, Li Jiangbing, and Zhao Yi could withstand it.","The Youth Apartments still served meals in a cafeteria.","The cafeteria was different from communal meals. The main reason the Youth Apartments had a cafeteria was that nearly everyone there was single, and cooking individually would waste too much time, so they ate together.","Almost no one in the Youth Apartments was idle. Even the combat team had a reserve unit, and everyone had to take turns resting.","Little by little, everyone was finding their own place in the new ecosystem.","The complex remained clean and orderly. When a lightbulb burned out, someone replaced it. When a pipe became clogged, someone cleared it.","Seeing the refugees in wrinkled clothes, with foul breath and vacant eyes, made everyone understand even more clearly just how difficult it was to maintain this seemingly ânormalâ life.","After breakfast, everyone went off to take care of their own tasks.","Zhou Wang arrived with Auntie Lin, Auntie Qian, and a middle-aged man. All three of them were wood-element superpowered people.","âThis is Master Luo. Master Luo is also a wood-element superpowered person.â","The way he addressed him as âMaster Luoâ left everyone in the Youth Apartment momentarily dazed.","Aunt Pan was squatting nearby with a bowl of porridge, helping Song Jingshuo turn over the soil as she ate. At the words, she turned her head and stared for a while before facing forward again.","It felt as though a very long time had passed, but when they thought about it carefully, it had only been seven or eight days.","People had already adapted. They had already begun to forget.","They quickly came to an agreement with Master Luo.","He could move into the Youth Apartment.","Zhou Wang and Jiang Cheng had already reached an agreement: several wood-element superpowered people would work together, and all the food cultivation for both residential compounds would be handled here at the Youth Apartment.","Because of this decision, Xiao Dan had pulled Zhou Wang aside for a private talk that morning.","Xiao Dan wondered why everything had to be handed over to the Youth Apartment. Why couldnât they keep it in their own hands?","Zhou Wang sighed. âIâm exhausted. How about I leave everything here for you to manage?â","Xiao Dan immediately fell silent.","The reason was simple: Xiao Dan had no superpowers. Under the current circumstances, a leader couldnât be weak. If they were weak, they wouldnât be able to keep everyone in line.","Although her daughter, Wang Yunya, was a fire-element superpowered person, she was too young. Besides, she spent all day with the people from the Youth Apartment.","Actually, Zhou Wang could understand Xiao Dan.","Once people got a taste of power, it was very easy for them to become distorted by it.","During the previous disaster, Xiao Dan had merely been a key memberâs family member in Auspicious Garden. This time, she had become a key figure herself.","She had a strong personality, and people with strong personalities naturally tended to have a greater desire for control than ordinary people.","When that desire for control grew large enough, it was called a lust for powerâor ambition.","âThis is your first time taking part in something like this,â Zhou Wang said. âYou havenât experienced how difficult it really is to manage so many people.â","âYou think it isnât difficult right now only because the Youth Apartment is taking on so much of the burden. We donât feel the difficulty because weâre simply benefiting from their efforts.â","âIf you really separated from the Youth Apartment, youâd immediately realize how hard it is.â","âDo you dare?â","Xiao Dan certainly didnât.","However, when Zhou Wang went to find Auntie Lin and Auntie Qian, Xiao Dan tested the waters with her daughter.","Wang Yunya rolled her eyes. âOf course we should listen to the Youth Apartment. Who else would we listen to? Isnât the Youth Apartment organizing everything? Werenât we rescued by them too?â","âDonât make breakfast for me anymore. Iâm going to eat over there. It sounds like weâre going into the city today.â","âFrom now on, you donât need to make breakfast for me at all. Iâll eat over there. Team members can eat in the cafeteria. Xu En and the others eat there too.â","âIâm off!â","The fire-element girl fastened her armor and ran off at top speed."]},{"number":153,"title":"Chapter 153: 0153","paragraphs":["The cafeteria auntie who had survived at Guangxiu Districtâs No. 14 High School told the teachers and parents, âWeâre running out of meat.â","If anyone was to blame, it was the principal.","The new principal, who had taken office after the first disaster, wanted the children to eat fresher food. He had ordered them to use up the frozen meat in the cold storage as quickly as possible and to buy chilled meat whenever they could.","Now the meat was almost gone.","A bunch of middle schoolers ate like growing boysâenough to bankrupt their parents.","The teachers and parents discussed the matter and decided to make a trip to the nearby market to stock up.","The nearest market was four blocks from the school. The students had already cleared out most of the streets around the school. Expanding their patrols a little farther would bring them to the market.","The survivors of No. 14 High had no plans to flee to the Science and Technology New District right away, but neither did they intend to hide on campus forever.","The children in particular were in remarkably high spirits. In the midst of such a disaster, they displayed a vigorous will to live and a fearless courage.","The children with superpowers practiced their abilities every day.","The ordinary children practiced formations and teamwork every day.","And the less physically robust children spent each day dreaming up all sorts of wild ideas to make the superpowers more useful and help everyone kill zombies more efficiently.","Everyone took turns helping in the cafeteria and cleaning, doing their best to maintain a ânot too badâ living environment.","Everyone agreed that they should go out.","They needed to replenish their food, of course, but they also needed clean clothes and detergent. Besides, September had arrived and the temperature had noticeably dropped. The adults were already thinking about how to keep warm.","The market had a food market on the first floor, while the second and third floors sold clothing and various other small commodities. It ought to have everything they needed.","And so everyone set out, all of them wearing armor and carrying weapons.","They cleared the zombies from the streets along the way.","The children had already encountered three generations of zombies. Third-generation zombies really were cunning. Some hid inside buildings along the street, while others stood openly in the road, pretending to be ordinary second-generation zombies and lulling people into carelessness. But the children had also accumulated plenty of combat experience.","The superpowered ones had support personnel.","The ordinary people used three-person teamsâa system proven through the fires of modern history to be the most effective combination. It was extremely practical.","The idea had been proposed by a high school student who was a military enthusiast. After plenty of practice and real-world testing, everyone had adopted it.","The childrenâs growth was astonishing.","The student army soon reached the market.","It was called a market, but its full name was Hongâan Market.","There were far fewer zombies inside than they had expected. August 29 had not been a busy time of day for shopping.","The elderly had already finished buying their groceries early that morning, while office workers would only stop by to shop for vegetables after getting off work.","At this hour, most of the zombies were the market vendorsâthe hard-working people who had gotten up at three in the morning to buy and prepare their stock.","Even so, no matter who they had been in life, once they became zombies, they were zombies. There was nothing anyone could do about that.","The students were completely fearless. Working closely together, they spent more than an hour clearing all the zombies from the first floor.","The teacher put his hands on his hips. âThatâs a lot of vegetables. What a shame theyâre not very fresh anymore.â","After all, they had been sitting there for a week. And at the end of August, there had been several especially hot days, practically summer weather. It had only just started to cool down.","A lot of the vegetables had rotted.","Everyone lamented the waste.","âCome on, there are still the second and third floors.â","âUpstairs!â","As they climbed, everyone exchanged their experiences. âThis shovel really comes in handy.â","After seeing the crescent-shaped shovel in Jiang Chengâs hands on television, Wu Shuchen had copied it. By now, half the people had bravely switched to shovels, while the other half were accustomed to using iron rods and refused to change.","The shovel seemed to be winning out. Once sharpened, it could cut through things; turned sideways, it could also smash them flat. It did both jobs well.","At the front of the group was a fire-powered student. Even though he had a superpower, he still carried a crescent shovel. Superpowers could run out of strength, after all. A weapon was still necessary.","He had tried it himself just now, and the crescent shovel really was useful. As they reached the bend in the stairs, he heard someone beside him say, âIf Iâd known, I wouldâve switched too.â","He turned to the person and said, âI told youââ","Before he could finish, several people shouted, âWatch out!â","The fire-powered boy felt a sudden tightness around his neck. In an instant, he couldnât breathe. His body was lifted off the ground and then slammed onto the stairs, where he was dragged down step after step with a series of loud bangs. His metal shoulder armor screeched against the steps.","His head jolted up and down until he was dazed. He had no idea what had happened.","All he could hear were people shouting around him.","âHold on to him!â","âCut it! Cut it!â","Suddenly, his body stopped moving.","There was a flurry of footsteps around him as his classmates charged upstairs. âAfter it!â","A few students came over and clumsily untangled the thing wrapped around his neck. âAre you all right?â","The boy sucked in a deep breath and immediately began coughing violently.","Several people patted his back and helped him catch his breath.","âAre you hurt?â","The armor had a raised, shell-like piece at the back of the neck to protect the neck, the back of the head, and the ears. Thanks to the armor, he had avoided being scraped, but bruises from the impact were unavoidable.","After finally regaining his breath, the boy stared fearfully at the section of blue-green thing lying on the floor. âWhat was that? A snake?â","âNo.â Someone prodded it several times with an iron rod, then crouched down to examine it more closely. Finally, he understood. âHoly shit!â","He stood up, cupped his hands around his mouth, and shouted to the people upstairs, âEveryone be careful! Itâs a tentacle! Not a snakeâitâs a tentacle! A tentacle!â","When the students had been climbing the stairs, the fire-powered boy at the front had turned around to speak. That was when many of them saw a long, blue-green, rope-like object shoot down from above. With a snap, it slipped into the gap between the boyâs armor and the back of his head and wrapped around his neck.","Their first thought had been: snake!","The âsnakeâ coiled around the fire-powered boy and dragged him toward the second floor.","Everyone reacted at once, each person doing something different. Some reached out to grab him, others gave chase, and still others shouted warnings.","In the end, the person running at the front managed to cut through the âsnakeâ with a crescent shovel and rescue the fire-powered boy. The whole group surged after it.","âDonât let it get away!â","The second floor sold all kinds of everyday odds and ends: buckets, washbasins, brooms, mops, plastic stools, hardware, bedding, Buddhist statues, framed art, and countless other things. The shops stood in rows, each separated by partition walls, while the ceiling overhead was open and connected throughout.","But there were far fewer zombies on the second floor than everyone had expected.","By the time the group caught up, the âsnakeâ had vanished.","They were searching for it when their classmates below shouted, âItâs not a snake! Itâs a tentacle! Itâs a tentacle!â","Everyone looked at one another. âWhat?â","Suddenly, a girl let out a scream. She was knocked off her feet and began sliding across the floor, the metal armor on her body scraping loudly against the ground.","The tentacle had wrapped around her ankle and was dragging her away. It was astonishingly fastâeven knocking over two zombies as it went.","The students raced after it, killing the zombies blocking the corridor as they ran. Fortunately, they were all primitive zombies, slow and clumsy.","The girl screamed as she was dragged along. When the tentacle pulled her around a corner, she suddenly grabbed hold of the wall of one of the shops.","The aluminum-alloy partition wall was very thinâthin enough to grip with one hand.","The girl screamed, âHelp me!â","A classmate who had come racing after her raised a crescent-shaped spade and was about to chop down when the âtentacle,â as if it had learned its lesson, suddenly released the girlâs ankle before the sharp spade could reach it. Then it lashed out like a whip, smacking the classmate across the face and sending him spinning like a top. The spade flew from his hand and clanged to the floor.","What incredible strength.","That one blow had knocked the classmate senseless.","The girl also managed to scramble up, and the two of them sat on the floorâone dazed, the other gasping for breath.","The âtentacleâ had already vanished.","The corridors between the shops formed a grid, crisscrossing in every direction.","The studentsâ scattered footsteps could be heard everywhere.","âOver here!â","âIt disappeared again!â","âItâs on our side!â","âOwâthereâs a zombie!â","There were only a few scattered zombies on the second floor, and they were relatively easy to deal with.","Suddenly, someone shouted, âItâs gone up to the third floor!â","Everyone rushed toward the third floor in a noisy wave.","The third floor sold clothes. The shops were packed even more tightly than on the second floor, and the passageways were narrower.","At a glance, they couldnât see a single zombie.","The students split into several groups and spread out along different routes. They gripped their weapons tightly and kept their eyes fixed on the floorâthe âtentacleâ was elusive, sliding along the ground like a snake with a slippery shhh-shhh.","Suddenly, someone shouted, âOver here!â","Everyone thundered toward the sound.","The boy bringing up the rear of one group suddenly felt something tighten around his neck. He opened his mouth to shout, but something immediately clamped over it, preventing him from making a sound.","The weapon in his hand fell to the ground with a clatter. Unfortunately, the students in front were running and shouting so loudly that no one noticed.","The boy was dragged along the floor, watching helplessly as the shops on either side seemed to shoot backward.","He desperately clawed at the âtentacleâ wrapped around his mouth and neck. But although the thing looked soft, its outer skin was actually extremely tough, and its strength was terrifyingly immense. It squeezed so tightly that he was on the verge of passing out.","Iâm done for. The boyâs heart sank. Iâm going to die.","Just then, a sharp crescent-shaped spade came crashing down. It landed perilously close to the boyâs head and severed the âtentacle.â","It was the girl from the second floorâthe one whose ankle had been caught and dragged away. Frightened, she had sat on the floor gasping for a while before following the boy who had been sent spinning like a top to catch up with the main group.","As soon as they reached the third floor and hurried inside, she saw, at the intersection ahead, a âtentacleâ sliding swiftly across the floor.","She reacted quickly. Before she had time to think, she charged forward and chopped down with her spade, severing it cleanlyâand landing the blow right above the head of the boy being dragged away.","If she had been even a moment slower, she might have struck him in the face instead.","âOver here!â the boy who had come with her shouted. âItâs over here! Itâs got someone!â","A great many people came running over.","The girl helped the boy on the floor free the âtentacleâ wrapped around his neck and mouth. âAre you all right?â","The sensation in his mouth was disgustingly nauseating.","The boy might have been the first person to touch a zombie with his tongue. It was revolting beyond words.","He scrambled to his feet and vomited up his breakfast. Afterward, he wiped his mouth and snarled viciously, âWhereâs my spade? Whereâs my spade? Iâm going to turn this thing into sizzling squid tentacles!â","He searched everywhere for his spade.","Everyone tried to surround and cut off the âtentacle,â but it was incredibly cunning and terrifyingly fast. It also kept ambushing whoever fell behind.","They chased it again and again, but couldnât catch it.","In the end, the two students with electrical superpowers discussed the situation and stepped forward.","âEveryone move back. Get to the stairs.â","The teacher wanted to stop them, but the two students said, âThereâs no other way.â","One of the parents said, âLet them try.â","Another parent advised, âDonât hold back. Start at maximum power.â","The two students nodded and walked resolutely into the depths of the market.","Wu Shuchen tightened his grip on his spade.","Senior Huang Xuetao, can you see this?","The other seniors are all so brave, too.","So am I."]},{"number":154,"title":"Chapter 154: 0154","paragraphs":["Shouts rang out from deep inside the third floor.","Everyoneâs heart clenched, and they charged over with a thunderous rumble.","Fortunately, the shouts werenât cries of pain. They were battle cries as people exerted themselves.","Two students with electrical superpowers had lured the âtentacleâ into a trap by using themselves as bait. The moment one of them was caught, the student with the electrical ability immediately unleashed electricity at full power.","Electricity worked on any living organism with some remaining biological activity. In fact, even corpses could conduct electricity.","The tentacle did indeed begin twitching and slowed down, but it still hadnât come to a complete stop.","The other student caught up, grabbed hold of it, and shouted, âAaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa!â as he poured out every last bit of his strength.","Superpower at maximum output!","The tentacle writhed a few times before finally dropping to the floor, motionless.","The student hurriedly freed the other student from the tentacle strangling his neck.","The rescued student gasped for breath and began coughing.","The students, teachers, and parents all came running over.","âCheck whether itâs pretending to be dead,â the teacher said.","This tentacle was extremely cunning, so nobody dared let their guard down. Everyone carrying a shovel rushed forward and hacked at it, one blow after another, as if they were chopping vegetables with cleavers.","The tentacle was cut into many pieces, yet it still didnât move.","After all, it had been hit with the full-power output of two students with electrical superpowers.","Following the tentacleâs trail, everyone found a curtain shop.","No wonder it had been so cunningâit had hidden itself beneath a huge pile of curtains and fabric stacked on the floor!","Who could possibly have found it there? What a nasty thing!","Several groups had already passed right in front of this curtain shop without noticing a thing.","The cunning tentacle must have retracted itself at the time.","When everyone scrambled to pull away all the curtain fabric and saw what was underneath, they were utterly stunned.","The boy whose mouth had just been wrapped by the âtentacleâ turned deathly pale.","He spun around and vomited again. âBlaaaarghââ","That was just tragic. His classmates all felt terribly sorry for him.","Because someone had shouted âtentacleâ first, everyone had been imagining an octopus monster from a horror movie.","But in reality, this was a person. Noâthat was too generous. She had once been a person, but now she was a zombie.","It was an old woman.","âOld womanâ was a concept as understood by middle school students.","After all, to a middle schooler, anyone in their twenties was already ancient.","In reality, she was a vigorous, middle-aged auntie.","How vigorous was she? The kind of vigorous that could knock you off a crowded bus during rush hour if you happened to ride with her.","The âtentacleâ wasnât a tentacle at all. It was the auntieâs tongue.","Her mouth had split sideways all the way toward the roots of her ears. Her tongue had become wide, thick, and incredibly long, stretching out from her mouth and trailing across the floor for more than a hundred meters. Judging from what had just happened, it might be able to extend even farther.","What kind of monster was this?","The auntie was dressed in flowers.","Her top had a tiny floral pattern, and so did her pants. Looking at her made everyoneâs eyes feel dazzled.","The teacher walked over and took a careful look.","âOh. Itâs her.â","The students were astonished. âYou know her?â","The teacher sighed. âThis is Hong'an's Quarrel Queen, famous throughout the area.â","The teacher rode a bicycle to work. Every day, when passing through Hong'an Market, she would first go in to buy groceries, carry them to school, and then take them home after work.","The produce was best in the morning. If she waited until after work to buy it, all the good stuff would already have been picked over.","The teacher had worked at No. 14 Middle School for many years, so she had also been a regular at Hong'an Market for many years. She was extremely familiar with âHong'an's Quarrel Queen.â","This auntie was a terrifyingly gifted scolder, unbeatable throughout Hong'an Market.","The teacher had heard all sorts of gossip about her while buying groceries. At home, she had scolded her daughter-in-law so relentlessly that the woman wanted to jump off a building, and she had driven her own daughter to leave home. At Hong'an Market, she had cursed out every vegetable vendor and gotten into fights with many of the clothing-shop owners on the third floor.","One of the parents pulled out a cellphone. âTeacher, move aside for a moment. I want to take a picture.â","It was a new model with a camera.","This zombie was far too unusual. Nobody had ever seen anything like it before, so they had to take a photo.","The students began discussing it among themselves.","âIs this a third-generation one?â","âDefinitely not. Third-generation zombies know how to run away and use tricks. This isnât even the same level.â","âA mutant zombie! Didnât that auntie on television say something about mutant zombies?â","âRight, right, I remember that too. She said mutant zombies.â","The children had no idea how lucky they were.","This mutant zombie was merely a sharp-tongued, foul-tempered ordinary woman from the neighborhood. Unlike Guo the Great Embezzler, who had seen the wider world and harbored grand ambitions, she had never aspired to anything beyond her own little corner.","No matter how fierce and quarrelsome she had been, all that had happened was that she had turned into a long-tongued monster. Although she was somewhat difficult to deal with, she wasnât truly that dangerous.","They had been very lucky.","Everyone searched the market and found several survivors in the small general store on the first floor.","The shop owner had promptly pulled down the metal rolling shutter, cutting the store off from the zombies in the produce section. There had been food and drink inside, allowing everyone to hold out.","The only problem was that they had used basins and buckets whenever they needed to relieve themselves. Even though they had deliberately placed them in a corner, the stench had still been overwhelming.","But the students didnât mind.","The shop owner, an older woman who had survived the disaster, waved her hands generously.","âTake whatever you want. Go ahead, take it. Itâs free. What use is money now?â","The students cheered and rushed into the store to grab things.","Outside, the teachers and parents found several flatbed cargo tricycles, along with the kind of three-wheeled carts elderly people rodeâones with a large rear compartment for carrying passengers or cargo.","The meat displayed outside the butcher shop had all gone rotten, with flies buzzing everywhere.","But the meat in the freezers was still frozen solid. All of it had to be transported back to the school.","The students had already started eating snacks and drinking soft drinks.","The past seven or eight days had been miserable, and everyone was desperately craving something to eat. They needed to replenish themselves.","Only when the teachers called them over did the students reluctantly wipe their mouths, stuff snacks into their pockets, and go back to work.","Most of the vegetables were no longer fresh, and many had already rotted.","The adults searched through them and picked out whatever was still edible, mostly things like radishes and potatoes.","âThese potatoes have sprouted. We can plant them,â one parent said.","The teachersâ hands all paused.","The unspoken meaning was that they would have to prepare for a prolonged struggle.","Sigh.","The students went up to the second floor of the market and carried down many handcarts, one for each person.","The teachers instructed them to carry food first and get other things on the next trip. Even so, many students secretly took items they needed.","For example, the girls quietly went up to the third floor and took underwear.","In the end, several tricycles of various sizes were packed to the brim. Everyone had a handcart.","They had returned with a full load.","The shop owner and the few lucky customers had nowhere else to go. They wouldnât have dared take to the road on their own, so they followed the students from No. 14 Middle School back to campus.","By the time the large group transported the meat and vegetables back to school, it was already noon, and the cafeteria had finished preparing lunch.","After eating, everyone rode the tricycles back to Hong'an Market to âstock up.â","The school had housing for faculty and staff, and there was a bathhouse on the first floor where everyone could wash. But they needed clean clothes. There were also countless other necessities, such as toothbrushes and toothpaste.","The teachers needed to find quilts and bedding for everyone.","Over the past few days, all the metal parts of the desks had been taken apart and turned into armor and weapons.","The desktop panels had been joined together to make bed boards, while schoolbags served as pillows. Everyone had been sleeping in their clothes.","That had been fine a few days ago, but the temperature had clearly dropped over the last couple of nights. It was too cold now.","They had to find quilts and bedding.","The bedding and clothing stores in Hongâan Market had been completely stripped bare. The curtain shop hadnât been spared either. Curtain fabric wasnât exactly comfortable, but it was thick, and folded into several layers, it could serve as bedding.","The second trip was loaded up too. If they wanted anything else, theyâd have to make another trip.","âDonât rush,â the teacher said. âWeâll have to come several more times. We can come again tomorrow.â","There was simply too much they needed.","Everyone dragged their handcarts back. Then someone suddenly turned around and narrowed their eyes.","âHuh? Whatâs moving over there?â","It was across the road.","And not just some little streetâit was a major thoroughfare, broad and divided by iron railings. On the other side stood a building that housed the vehicle administration office.","One of the upstairs windows was open. Someone was leaning out and frantically waving a curtain they had torn down.","It was too far away to shout. They didnât dare risk attracting the zombies. If that person hadnât torn down the curtain and waved it like a flag, they would have been almost impossible to spot from such a distance.","âSomeoneâs calling for help!â Everyone understood at once.","What should they do?","They looked at one another, exchanging glances.","Before the teacher or any of the parents could say a word, the students had already dropped their handcarts, rolled up their sleeves, and gripped their crescent-shaped shovels.","âLetâs goâ! Weâre rescuing them!â","Heaven helps those who help themselves; heaven saves those who save themselves.","They didnât need to wait for someone to rescue them. They could save themselves.","They could even save other people!","New Tech District.","Zhou Wang arrived with Auntie Lin, Auntie Qian, and the new Master Luo to meet up with Song Jingshuo.","Everyone had already reached an agreement. Although the refugees would all be housed at Auspicious Garden, everyoneâincluding the original residents of Auspicious Gardenâwould be placed under the unified management of the temporary district government.","In simple terms, everyone would be relying on the district government for food.","All the wood-type superpowered people would be assigned to work at the Youth Apartments, and their food supplies would be distributed through the Youth Apartments.","Xiao Dan had still failed to think things through.","There were few original residents at Auspicious Garden. Although it had several superpowered people, its overall fighting strength was insufficient.","What would happen if so many people suddenly moved in? If the crops were kept inside their own housing complex, what if these newcomers refused to follow orders and simply tried to seize them by force?","During the first zombie disaster, whenever anything happened, it was always the men who stepped forwardâas long as a family still had a man in it.","That was why, during all the incidents last time, it had been Wang Yunyaâs father, Xiao Danâs husband, who had dealt with matters outside while Xiao Dan stayed home to look after Wang Yunya.","She had eventually learned what had happened, but she had never faced it directly.","She had never confronted the distortion of human nature firsthand, and lacked the experience.","Her thinking was still rooted in the rule-of-law society of the past.","Song Jingshuo took the others to a meeting.","In fact, Imperial Scenery Garden also had a wood-type superpowered person. But its population was currently small, and it was self-sufficient, so that person did not need to be called up for now. They would remain there to help their own community.","From now on, the old, small-workshop approach of planting whatever they felt like eatingâand planting it the day they wanted to eat itâwas over. From now on, everything had to be properly planned.","The staple crops would be potatoes and sweet potatoes. The main vegetables would be radishes and napa cabbage.","These crops not only produced high yields but were also easy to store. They needed to be planted on a large scale and stockpiled in advance, in preparation for the refugees they would take in later.","The peanuts needed to be planned out as well. They would provide cooking oil.","The beans needed to be planned too. The cafeteria aunties had said they could be used to make bean paste and brew soy sauce.","In fact, all vegetables could be planted, as long as priorities were clearly established.","Fruit would be strictly controlled.","There also had to be clear tiers in the benefits people received.","Jiang Cheng said to Zhou Wang, âYou donât have to go today. You can stay here.â","More than five hundred refugees had entered Auspicious Garden, and Jiang Cheng felt that Zhou Wang ought to remain behind. If anything happened, at least they would have someone dependable to take charge.","Zhou Wang placed both hands over his stomach. âItâs fine. Xiao Danâs here.â","His eyes flickered.","âAnd Xiao Song is here too. She has plenty of management experience. If anything happens, she can go to Xiao Song.â","The look in his eyes made it obvious that something had happened.","Jiang Cheng didnât want to involve herself in Auspicious Gardenâs internal problems. As long as nothing major went wrong, it was none of her concern.","She nodded. âAll right. Then go.â"]},{"number":155,"title":"Chapter 155: 0155","paragraphs":["Several people at Mr. Xuâs company knew how to cook. Since they all lived on the same floor, they got together to prepare a meal.","The rice they had been allocated was rationed by headcount, enough for one day. Everyone took out a portion to cook porridge. They rummaged through the refrigerators in several vacant, ownerless apartments and found things like salted duck eggs, fermented tofu, and pickled vegetables. There was meat, eggs, and fresh produce, too. Though the vegetables had been kept in refrigerators, too much time had passed, and they had already wilted.","No one mentioned the supplies in those apartments. Everyone simply took it for granted that they now belonged to the people who had moved in.","While they were cooking the porridge, Mr. Xu and the director went downstairs for a stroll.","âWeâll be eating potatoes every day from now on,â Mr. Xu said. âThat wonât do.â","âIt should be the basic level of support,â the director said. âBut surely not everyone is being treated the same way. I donât believe the people in the upper echelons are eating like this, too.â","Mr. Xu said, âThe Youth Apartment complex is probably on an entirely different level from this place.â","All the refugees had been sent here to live, while not a single person remained over there. It was entirely occupied by âtheir own people.â","The middle school students yearned to go there.","The old people said that all the wood-element users who grew vegetables were working there.","These bits of information were already crystal clear.","That morning, when they turned on the television, S Cityâs municipal station was repeatedly broadcasting a speech by a young woman named Jiang Cheng. She had said, âLed by the Youth Apartment.â Did they understand? Led by the Youth Apartment.","That was why Mr. Xu and the director had come downstairs for a stroll: they wanted to go over there and take a look.","When doing business, clients had to be won over through oneâs own efforts. Even as refugees, they had to fight for better treatment themselves.","Who could just sit at home and wait for good things to fall from the sky?","As the two men wandered around, they spotted Xiao Dan in the residential complex.","Xiao Dan was quite busy. Several hundred people had suddenly moved in, and all sorts of problems had cropped up after just one night.","Some wanted to change apartments. Some complained that they felt unwell. Others made all kinds of demands.","Xiao Dan had just sent one group away after another. She had barely finished dealing with a few people asking whether vehicles could be provided so they could return home when two middle-aged men approached her.","Mr. Xu was exceptionally polite, with a cosmopolitan air about him. âHello, maâam. Weâd like to ask what people with superpowers can do for this community.â","Xiao Danâs eyes lit up. âWhat kind of superpowers do you have?â","âIâm a metal-element user, and heâs an electricity-element user.â","Xiao Danâs eyes lit up even more. She said enthusiastically, âWelcome, welcome! Our community welcomes all superpowered individuals!â","Mr. Xu asked, âWhat do we need to do?â","âThereâs nothing at the moment,â Xiao Dan said. âYou should rest first. Which building and room are you staying in? Iâll make a note of it.â","Mr. Xu did not tell her. Instead, he said, âWe already registered yesterday.â","Xiao Dan paused. âThatâs all right. Iâll record it again.â","Mr. Xu smiled. âThereâs no need to trouble yourself. If anything comes up, just use the information from the registration to find us.â","The director said, âThen weâll go get some rest. We really are feeling awful. We hid out at the company for seven days, and now we feel weak all over. Four of our colleagues turned into zombies. Sigh, weâd worked together for years, but we had no choice except to put them down. Sigh. You go ahead and take care of your business. Weâll just walk around for a bit. Go on, go on.â","After hearing that, Xiao Dan could hardly insist on keeping them there. She could only nod. âYou two should rest properly for a couple of days. Iâll notify you when thereâs an assignment.â","Mr. Xu said, âThank you for your hard work. Thank you.â","The two men turned and slowly wandered off. They were in no hurry, strolling along at an easy pace as if they were simply out for a walk.","One was a metal-element user, and the other was an electricity-element user. Both were powerful offensive abilities. Xiao Dan thought that she would have a good talk with Zhou Wang later and find a way to keep these two superpowered individuals here. Then Jixiang Garden would have a force capable of standing on its own.","Mr. Xu and the director strolled side by side toward the west gate of Jixiang Garden.","âShe has no operational authority,â Mr. Xu said.","When he had asked what arrangements would be made for them, she had only said that they should rest first. She could not say anything else. In other words, she simply was not the one making the decisions.","âShe doesnât have personnel authority, either,â the director said.","The previous night, while assigning apartments, someone had registered everyoneâs superpowers. Clearly, there was a unified system for coordinating and managing them. Xiao Dan had also asked which building and floor they lived in, intending to record it. That meant the registration information was not in her hands.","âShe was quite enthusiastic,â Mr. Xu said.","When she heard that they were metal- and electricity-element users, her eyes had lit up, and her attitude had grown noticeably warmer.","âThat means she needs them,â the director said.","âShe canât do a damn thing for us. Come on, letâs go take a look over there.â","With neither operational nor personnel authority, she probably could not decide anything about their treatment, either.","If they wanted better treatment, they had to find the person who actually had the power to make decisions.","The two men wandered out through Jixiang Gardenâs west gate and crossed Jixiang West Street. Directly opposite stood the east gate of the Youth Apartment.","The gate was closed. A sheet of paper had been pasted onto one of the gateposts:","Strict management. All entry and exit must be registered. For assistance, contact security. â","An arrow pointed toward the security booth.","The two exchanged a glance.","See? This side actually had management.","The gate was locked, which meant there was something valuable inside that needed to be kept separate from unrelated people.","The two men poked their heads around and saw a security guard sitting in the booth, holding a stainless-steel basin and eating oversized steamed buns.","The guard looked only nineteen or twenty. He had quite an appetite; the buns were stacked high in his basin.","Mr. Xu and the director fell silent.","Both men could not help smacking their lips.","They looked delicious.","It was all right. Once they went back, they would have plain porridge to drink, too.","Yes. That was pretty good as well.","Looking in through the gate, they could see only a straight, paved path. The surrounding buildings completely blocked the view of the rest of the complex.","The two looked around.","âOver there. Letâs go take a look over there.â","They headed south. After passing the building, they could finally see into the complex through the gap between the buildings.","But first, they spotted someone familiar on the strip of landscaping between the building and the outer fence.","âMaster Luo! Master Luo!â","The two grabbed the iron bars and squeezed their faces through them as they called out.","They looked like prisoners behind bars who had just seen a beloved relative.","The area between the buildings and the outer fence consisted entirely of landscaped greenery. The original shrubs and flowers had now been pulled out and piled to one side. The gardener who had come to the Technology New District with Mr. Xu and the othersâthe new Master Luoâwas crouching on the freshly turned soil with another young man, working on something.","Hearing the voices, Master Luo looked up. When he saw the two men, he stood and came over to speak with them.","âOh, itâs you two.â","Mr. Xu asked, âMaster Luo, what are you doing here?â","âThere arenât many wood-element users, so we all have to work,â Master Luo said. âSo many people are waiting to be fed. Iâm in charge of planting peanuts now.â","Master Luo was full of emotion as well. âSuperpowers are really convenient. You donât even need a hoe to turn the soil anymore. A soil-element user can do it directly for you. And heâs a university student, too.â","The soil-element user was a resident of the Youth Apartment. He was also quite young, in his twenties. Hearing that, he said helplessly, âDonât remind me. I finally escaped the countryside and started living the life Iâd always wanted. Then heaven saw fit to give me a soil-element superpower.â","It seemed the heavens had seen right through his origins.","The director felt terribly sorry for him. âMaster Luo, youâve worked hard. Youâve really worked hard.â","Mr. Xu felt sorry for him, too. âOnce youâre done here, hurry back and eat. Weâve got porridge cooking at home, and there are salted duck eggs, too. We saved some for you. Ah~â","He even added an especially heartfelt âAh~.â","Master Luo wasnât moved in the slightest.","He had been taking care of the greenery at Mr. Xuâs company for three years, and this was the first time heâd ever spoken to Mr. Xu.","Before this, Mr. Xu had never even noticed him.","Maybe Master Luo had some kind of invisibility superpower back then. Who knew?","Master Luo ruthlessly poured cold water on the two of them. âIâve already eaten here. I had steamed buns. Iâm not going back. Theyâve assigned me a room here, so Iâm staying here tonight.â","Mr. Xu and the directorâs hearts went ice-cold. âYouâre not coming with us?â","Their food supply was gone.","Master Luo could see how disappointed they were. He didnât have much of a relationship with themâjust the small bond forged through seven days of sharing hardships.","For the sake of that tiny bond, he gave them some advice. âGo find the guard at the east gate and tell him youâre superpowered. All the superpowered people here have work. The foodâs good, too.â","The young earth-type man behind him came over as well. âYou two are superpowered too? What kind of abilities do you have?â","After learning that one of them was metal-type and the other was electric-type, the young man asked, âHow are you two feeling now? If you still havenât recovered, rest for a while. If youâve recovered enough, get to work. Thereâs plenty to do. Whether you join logistics or the combat team, everyone who works eats on our side.â","The director squeezed his face between two bars of the gate and asked, âAre there any steamed buns left?â","Mr. Xu gave him a hard kick. How utterly shameful!","The earth-type young man laughed. He pulled a walkie-talkie from the small of his back. âIâve got two superpowered people hereâone metal-type and one electric-type. They want to work in exchange for food.â","A voice came through the walkie-talkie. âSend them to the east gate. Iâll have someone pick them up.â","The earth-type young man asked, âAre there any buns left? They havenât eaten yet.â","There was a pause on the other end.","âThere are. Theyâre still hot. Hurry and bring them in to eat.â","Mr. Xu and the director jogged over to the east gate. The guard had already opened it, and he still had half a steamed bun hanging from his mouth.","The closer they got, the better it smelled.","There had been too many people yesterday. They remembered this young guard, but the guard didnât remember them. Biting into his bun, he said, âCome in, come in. Thereâre people inside.â","The two of them entered, and the guard, Little Fang, closed the gate again.","As Mr. Xu and the director walked farther in, they met a young man and woman coming toward them. The woman was holding a folder, while the man carried some kind of deviceâa small case in one hand and a pen-shaped object in the other, connected by a wire.","âYou two are the newcomers, right?â the woman asked. âWhich one of you is metal-type?â","Mr. Xu stepped forward. âI am.â","âMetal-type abilities can be used either in the combat team or in logistics,â the woman explained. âThough people in the combat team often have to help with logistics too. Metal-types have it relatively hard. The more capable you are, the more work youâll have to do.â","Mr. Xu said, âWe just got here and arenât familiar with anything yet. Iâll start with logistics.â","âSure.â","The young man turned to the director. âYouâre electric-type, right? Then youâll have to join the combat team.â","If an electric-type superpowered person only worked in logistics, they were basically no different from an ordinary person. At present, there was no logistical work that required the use of electric-type abilities.","The director was still hesitating when the young man raised the electric pen in his hand. âHere, letâs test you. Give it everything youâve got. Donât hold back.â","Mr. Xu reminded him, âGive it everything youâve got.â","Their treatment depended on this. There was no point hiding his strength now.","The director gave it his allâbut his all amounted to only so much.","The young man looked at the reading on the device and seemed a little speechless. âThatâs such a tiny current. Did you really give it your all?â","The director truly had, but that really was all he could manage.","Seeing the young manâs faintly disdainful expression, he grew worried that he wouldnât even get any steamed buns. He hurriedly said, âIâll try again. Let me try one more time.â","This time, he squeezed out every last bit of strength he had. The result was only slightly stronger than before.","The young man frowned. âThis wonât do. To provide auxiliary support, you need to produce at least fifty milliamps of current and maintain it for more than ten seconds. If you canât do that, you wonât even be able to use the slowing assist. To kill a zombie outright, you need a current of at least one hundred and fifty milliamps. At your level, itâd be like scratching a zombieâs itch.â","Fifty milliamps of alternating current was already enough to kill a living person. But zombies could take far more punishment than living humans, so that level of current was only enough to activate the control skillâSlow.","To directly electrocute and destroy a zombieâs brain, they needed one hundred and fifty milliamps.","These figures had all been personally tested by Gao Yuxuan, who had fought his way into groups of zombies to gather real combat data. They also had to take into account a superpowered personâs total energy reserves and stamina. That was why he had concluded that electric-types were more cost-effective as control support than as direct attackers.","The young man said, âJudging from your endurance and total energy pool, you donât seem to be doing very well in those areas either. At this level, you canât join the combat team.â","The director was deeply disappointed. âSoâ¦ does that mean I donât get any steamed buns?â","His unwavering devotion to steamed buns made the woman burst out laughing.","Mr. Xu felt like he had completely lost face.","The young man laughed too. When he was done, he said, âYou canât join the combat team for now. Youâll need to train first. Forget itâletâs take you to breakfast. After you eat, Iâll take you to training.â","The directorâs eyes lit up. âReally?â"]},{"number":156,"title":"Chapter 156: 0156","paragraphs":["Mr. Xu and the director no longer remembered how much lobster and sea cucumber they had eaten in the first half of their lives. All they knew was that the steamed buns in front of them were so delicious they could bring tears to their eyes.","The security guard, Little Fang, no longer recognized them, but the cafeteria auntie recognized them at a glance. âItâs you two!â","The refugees had shown no appreciation for the braised pork she had painstakingly prepared the night before. Some had even vomited on the spot. Only these two and the companions they had brought had eaten with relish.","âHere, there are plenty of steamed buns. Eat, eat! Slow downâdonât choke.â","They were in the middle of eating when a call came in. It was an employee. âCome back for dinner! The porridge is ready!â","Mr. Xu said, âYou eat. Donât worry about us.â","âHuh? You two arenât coming to eat?â","Mr. Xu replied, âWeâre going to talk to the person in charge about our future prospects. You eat. Donât worry about us. The important thing is to take care of yourselves.â","âOh, all right. Thank you for your hard work, Mr. Xu.â","âItâs nothing. Itâs for everyone.â","After hanging up, the employee turned to the others and said, âThose two bastards must have found a way to live the good life without us!â","Everyone agreed. They couldnât help feeling anxious. âTheyâd better not ditch us.â","The young man in charge asked the director, âHow long ago did your superpower awaken?â","Mr. Xu turned his gaze toward the distance.","The director hemmed and hawed. âNot long ago.â","The young man understood. âNo wonder youâre so weak. After awakening, thereâs a period of rapid growth. You have to practice hardâthe improvement during this stage is especially fast. After that, youâll hit a bottleneck. Thatâs when everyoneâs talent and effort will begin to show, and the gap between people will become especially obvious. You have to work hard!â","Once they had eaten their fill, the two men went their separate ways.","The girl took Mr. Xu to find the metal-element superpower users. When they arrived, everyone was already working in full swing.","The open ground was piled high with iron railings dismantled from the roads.","One group was responsible for purification. Whenever painted or rusty iron came into their hands, the paint and rust would instantly turn into powder and fall to the ground, leaving behind gleaming metal. That was then passed on to the next stage.","They had made many narrow, elongated tables and stools, all shining brightly.","The girl said, âYesterday was too rushed, and everyone had to sit on the ground to eat. We canât keep doing that. Today, weâre making tables and stools so everyone will have somewhere to sit.â","Elsewhere, several people were making armor and weapons.","Mr. Xu took a look and saw that everything was being done on an assembly line. One person made shoulder armor, another made arm guards, and another made leg guards.","The crescent-shaped shovels were made the same way. Some people specialized in making the blades, while others made the handles. The handles even had threads carved into them to prevent peopleâs hands from slipping.","Even so, once people received them, they would still wrap the handles with strips of cloth, electrical tape, or something similar.","Mr. Xu joined the crescent-shovel production line, taking responsibility for sharpening the blades.","Sharpening required delicate precision, and delicate precision was by no means easy. After working for a while, Mr. Xu was already sweating all over his forehead.","Someone beside him glanced over and said, âYour efficiency is too low. Practice more.â","âThe teams will be coming back tonight, and weâll have to repair everyoneâs weapons. Hurry up and practice.â","A shovel could easily become dull after a dayâs use, so all the weapons had to be repaired together at night to keep them sharp.","On the other side, the young man took the director to find several electricity-element superpower users.","A row of iron crosses stood there, with a light bulb fixed to the top of each one. The electricity-element users generated power from a distance and lit the bulbs.","Some bulbs stayed brightly lit for a long time. Others were too dim, while one flickered on and off.","The young man led the director over. âYou can practice here. Thereâs a vacant spot.â","The others were all young people, residents of the Youth Apartments. They turned to look at him.","âRefugee?â","The director was very polite. âYes. And you are?â","âWe live here.â","âOh, I see.â","âWhen did your power awaken?â","âNot long ago.â","âGive it a try. Letâs see what you can do.â","The director had never tried firing his power from a distance before. So far, he had only managed to hail a taxi once, and even that had taken an enormous amount of effort.","So the director gathered his strength from his core and imitated the young people beside him, firing electricity through the air.","A current extended from his fingertip and crackled for a few moments before disappearing.","The light bulb did not turn on.","Everyone fell silent for a moment before bursting into laughter.","âUncle, did your power just awaken?â","âUncle, you need to practice!â","âHahahahahaha!â","The director was displeased. âWhy are you calling me âuncleâ? You all look old enough to be working already. You shouldnât lower your seniority in the workplace. Colleagues should address one another as equals. No matter how old someone is, you should still call them brother or sister.â","That was true. Everyone understood the principle. They had only been teasing him on purpose just now, and they promptly changed the way they addressed him.","âBrother, you need to practice.â","âBig Brother, what should we call you?â","The director replied, âMy surname is Yu.â","âBrother Yu, let me explain how this works.â","The group did not hold anything back. They shared everything they knew.","They explained how to perform delicate operations, how to use a test pen to sense the differences between various voltages and currents, how to aim when discharging electricity, and how to build an electrical grid.","Director Yu said, âYou all look like you only awakened your powers recently, but you certainly know a lot.â","Everyone laughed. âWe have someone who specializes in researching this stuff.â","It was September 5. Only eight days had passed since August 29. These people were already this professional. Director Yu felt a deep respect for the Youth Apartments.","As he practiced and chatted with the young people, he soon got a rough understanding of the basic situation at the Youth Apartments.","There were two central figures: the woman was called Jiang Cheng, and she handled external affairs. The man was called Song Jingshuo, and he handled internal affairs.","There were also several other key members.","And thenâ¦","âA cat?â","âThatâs right,â everyone said. âOur neighborhoodâs Guardian Cat.â","âItâs incredibly powerful.â","âYouâll see it once you join a team.â","It sounded as though electricity-element superpower users were required to join the combat teams.","Director Yu cautiously asked about all sorts of things related to the teams.","âDonât be afraid,â the others reassured him. âYouâre new, so theyâll definitely have you stay toward the back. Weâll be in front.â","These people who were still practicing had already been the main fighters against the zombies before their powers awakened. However, since their abilities had suddenly awakened one after another, they had to hurry and practice them first.","After all, judging from the situation so far, superpowers really were useful.","âThis is evolution.â","Everyone repeated Zhao Yiâs theory to Director Yu. Director Yu nodded along as he listened. âThat makes sense. That makes sense.â","Then he asked, âWhat are those people doing?â","The residential complex consisted of six buildings arranged in a circle, with a courtyard in the middle. The courtyard was actually quite large, but it was now packed with activity.","The areas that had clearly once been landscaped greenbelts had been stripped of their original plants. The earth-element superpower users were turning over and preparing the soil, while several people seemed to be applying fertilizer. Two older women and a young man were each tending several plots and planting things.","Mr. Xu was sitting on a metal chair with several metal-element users on the other side, making various items. Everyone was arranged in a line, working like an assembly line.","Well, looking closely, it really was an assembly line.","Mr. Xuâs speed was obviously not keeping up, and a pile of unfinished items was accumulating beside him.","Some people were sweeping the courtyard and hauling away garbage. They were all very young. It was easy to guess that they were residents of the complex. After all, this development had been designed to profit off young people, with tiny apartments that were practically unsuitable for marriage, marketed to them as a way to take advantage of their limited finances.","It appeared that everyone had been assigned a position. More likely, they were operating on a rotation system.","It looked as though no one had any complaints. If people were assigned permanently to jobs like sweeping floors and taking out the trash, anyone would eventually wear their grievances plainly on their faces.","There were also some people working out. Others were lined up, running laps around the courtyard in neat formation.","The âpeopleâ Director Yu had asked about were the ones running and exercising.","âYou have to train your body. Physical fitness is the foundation of evolution.â","âNo one knows how long the window for awakening superpowers will remain open. Everyoneâs working themselves to the bone, hoping to awaken.â","âExactly. I awakened yesterday.â","The speaker was the man whose lightbulb kept flickering.","His words drew a round of laughter.","âYou call that awakening?â","âYou just got scared awake.â","This man had originally thought he had no hope of awakening and was prepared to remain an ordinary member of the team. But yesterday, after being frightened by Guo the Great Embezzler at the television station, he had unexpectedly awakened.","He put his hands on his hips. âWho cares how I woke up? The point is, Iâm awake. Iâve evolved!â","Then he casually patted Director Yuâs belly. âBrother Yu, you should exercise too. Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan said it themselves: the body is the foundation. If the foundation is weak, itâll definitely affect your superpower.â","âThatâs right. Weâll go running later too.â","âLetâs train a little longer.â","âCome on, Brother Yu. Join us.â","After working on an assembly line for long enough, a personâs mind gradually went blank. Their hands became more and more skilled, while their thoughts became emptier and emptier.","Mr. Xu didnât know how long his mind had been blank when he suddenly came to his senses.","It turned out that everyone around him was laughing.","âKeep it up, big brother! You can do it!â","He turned his head and followed everyoneâs gaze.","ââ¦â","Old Yu?","Why was Old Yu running with a group of young people?","Old Yu was already exhausted, running like a dying dog.","He was practically about to collapse.","Young people along the entire route cheered him on.","Old Yu refused to admit he was getting old. Unable to bear losing face, he clenched his teeth and forced himself to keep going.","Served him right.","Mr. Xu was a serious weightlifter who kept himself in excellent shape. If he hadnât been, it would have been impossible for him to withstand the sudden increase in workload yesterday as he created armor and weapons for everyone.","The office buildingâs rent was so expensive, yet he had still been willing to set aside a separate gym and work out there with his employees.","Only Old Yu spent every day slacking off and refusing to train.","Served him right.","âWhat kind of superpower does he have?â","âSeems to be electricity.â","âOh, electricity. Then he really does need to train. Heâll have to join the team in the future.â","The team had already left for the day.","The three phones had been bombarded with calls and messages last night. Things only eased up toward midnight, but as soon as morning came, another barrage of text messages began.","Clearly, some people hadnât seen the livestream right away yesterday. They had only seen the replay when they turned on the television this morning.","Yang Xinyan, her eyes red from lack of sleep, handed the organized and printed materials to Jiang Cheng.","They had been sorted beautifully: locations, numbers of people, surrounding conditions, and contact information, categorized by district and arranged from north to south.","There was far too much. The stack was several pages thick, so Jiang Cheng distributed it among everyone for them to read together.","Li Jiangbing quickly dodged away, waving both hands. âDonât give me any! Donât give me any! My eyes hurt just looking at it!â","He couldnât stand such densely packed information.","This was Song Jingshuoâs strong suit. His eyes darted across the pages, and he finished reading them in the blink of an eye. He had read the most and the fastest.","Everyone exchanged information.","âThereâs a group of forty in Guangxiu District.â","âThereâs one of sixty in Chaoyang District.â","âThese office towers are next to each other, all in the same business district.â","Too many people were calling for help. Who should they save first, and who should they save later?","It was like that hypothetical moral dilemma: at a railway junction, one track would kill a young student, while the other would kill ten elderly people. Which would you choose?","At a moment like this, you realized that not everyone was capable of making the decision.","In truth, everyone else was merely a passenger on the train. They could only close their eyes and leave the choice to the driver.","Jiang Cheng was the driver."]},{"number":157,"title":"Chapter 157: 0157","paragraphs":["But Jiang Chengâs choice surprised Song Jingshuo.","In the most recent batch of messages from Guangxiu District, Jiang Cheng chose a group that had relatively more people but fewer superpowered individualsâand was on the verge of collapse.","Song Jingshuo raised his eyes.","This wasnât like him.","His way of thinking was very close to Jiang Chengâs, so this choice didnât seem like something she would make, either.","There were plenty of groups that had already stated they controlled an entire building, or at least several floors, and had a certain number of superpowered individuals.","If he were choosing, he would prioritize those groups. Bringing them in would mean adding combat power and dependable allies.","Prioritizing the strongâthat was his logic, and it should have been Jiang Chengâs logic as well.","Why was Jiang Cheng doing the opposite?","He didnât know that if she were considering only the matter of saving people, Jiang Cheng would indeed have made the same choice as him.","But Jiang Cheng couldnât think only about saving people itself.","She had seriously reflected on the relationship between herself and this world.","And on the mysterious force manipulating and toying with everything from behind the scenes.","Jiang Cheng was keenly aware that she was, in fact, being manipulated and controlled.","This world was both her trial ground and her prison.","She was, in truth, a prisoner.","Whatever had happened between her and that faction before, it was obvious that she had lost.","That meant her previous methods and logic had been flawed.","She had to change.","At its core, Jiang Chengâs logic was the same as Song Jingshuoâsâ","Recruit the strong and eliminate the weak.","The two of them had originally been people who thought this way.","But if acting according to that logic had led to failure the last time, then Jiang Cheng had to take a different path this time.","Jiang Cheng wasnât considering the act of âsaving peopleâ itself. She was playing a game against the force behind this entire catastrophe.","Everyone wore a different expression. Some were clearly thinking, âThatâs wonderful,â and even looked moved.","Some had no opinion at all.","Others seemed to have different ideas, but lacked the drive or determination to insist on them.","Since they knew they werenât capable of being the driver and had tossed all the difficult decisions to the driver, they might as well follow the driverâs lead.","Song Jingshuo didnât voice any objections, either.","This wasnât a life-or-death decision where one side had to win and the other had to lose. Perhaps it wouldnât achieve the maximum benefit he wanted, but so what?","Lookâquite a lot of people actually supported Jiang Chengâs choice.","Many genuinely believed that the weak should be rescued first. The strong could hold out for a while longer, while the weak might die if they couldnât hold on.","The logic behind this choice was essentially the same as the triage system used in hospital emergency rooms:","Save those who are closest to death first.","Once the decision was made, the team set out.","This time, they took not only four 535s, but also two buses from the television station.","Guangxiu District was the district closest to the Science and Technology New Area. No. 14 Middle School, where Little Huang attended school, was also located there.","The Blade vehicles cut through the zombies along the roadside as easily as knives through vegetables.","âKeep this up, and eventually the roads into and out of the city will be cleared completely.â","âHumans really do need to make effective use of tools.â","The first floor of the target building was occupied by a dental clinic. When the people outside came into view, the zombies inside began ramming themselves against the glass doors.","Gao Yuxuan started rolling his wrists and rotating his ankles.","The zombies smashed through the glass doors in a few blows and surged out in a swarm.","Gao Yuxuan spread both arms wide, looking like a perverted lecher trying to grope someone, while a crackling sheet of electricity spread from him.","The zombies immediately became sluggish.","Li Jiangbing led a group of people forward, taking down one head with each shovel strike.","With his hands clasped behind his back, Guo Jun looked like an old man taking a leisurely stroll.","âCome on, come on. Letâs get inside.â","In commercial skyscrapers twenty or thirty stories tall, it was impossible to lure all the zombies out at once. They could only enter and clear the building floor by floor.","According to the collected information, two floors in this building had sent out distress messages. The survivors had lived on snacks stockpiled in their officesâsupplies their colleagues had developed the habit of storing after the initial outbreakâbut those supplies were nearly exhausted.","The team cleared the building floor by floor, already familiar with the process. Little Huang and Mo Li showed no abnormalities, and there were no mutated zombies inside the building.","Not every company or floor had a television. Besides the two floors that had sent distress messages, they also found several survivors on other floors, all of them so starved that their cheeks had sunken in.","There were more than sixty survivors in total.","They all smelled awful, and every one of them looked listless.","Each person was given a piece of steamed potato. The potatoes were as large as basketballs and had been cut into neat, square chunks. A little salt was sprinkled over them.","They werenât particularly tasty, but they were still better than having nothing to eat.","No one complained. They all wolfed the food down.","They couldnât make a trip into the city just to deal with a single building.","After checking the distress-message records, they found two more buildings in the commercial district and went to clear those as well.","There were also survivors in nearby buildings who hadnât seen the television but had spotted the team from their windows. They called out for help through the glass.","By the time they finished, they had rescued more than two hundred people from several buildings in the area.","Jiang Cheng also looted the convenience stores, restaurant kitchens, and upscale supermarkets in the commercial district. Food, drinks, ingredients, toilet paper, sanitary padsâshe didnât leave behind a single consumable. Wherever she passed, the shelves were emptied.","Everyone sincerely felt that Jiang Chengâs spatial ability was incredibly useful.","If only everyone could have one.","There was also a shopping mall nearby.","The mall hadnât been part of the original plan, but they went anyway because they wanted what was inside.","They found more than a dozen survivors scattered throughout the mall.","After all the zombies had been cleared out, everyone began taking things. Getting supplies from the mall had been the whole reason they came.","Jiang Cheng even told the more than two hundred survivors rescued from the office buildings, âTake whatever you need. Especially clothes. Everyone should take at least one autumn or winter coat. Ideally, take several.â","The mall had a very standard layout.","The basement level housed a supermarket and a food court. The first floor sold shoes, bags, skincare and cosmetics, watches, and jewelry. The second floor was devoted to fashionable womenâs clothing. The third floor carried mature womenâs clothing. The fourth floor sold underwear, athletic wear, menâs clothing, and outdoor gear. The fifth floor carried bedding, childrenâs clothing, and digital products.","Jiang Cheng went straight to the third floor.","There were many women from both the team and the group of survivors on that floor, all searching for clothes. At Jiang Chengâs reminder, everyone consciously looked for winter cotton-padded coats and down jackets.","Jiang Cheng went directly into the storerooms of the various brands and collected entire bundles of winter coats into her space.","Then she went to the fourth floor and took winter clothes for men.","After that, she went to the fifth floor to collect bedding and childrenâs clothing.","She continued until her storage space was completely full. She compressed and packed everything as tightly as possible, but eventually there was no room left at all.","She called Li Jiangbing and had him bring people upstairs to carry away all the autumn and winter clothing, cotton-padded coats, and bedding they could collect.","They had brought six vehicles today, so there was enough room.","Everyone was working enthusiastically. Each person loved this feeling of taking whatever they wanted without paying. It gave them an inexplicably satisfying thrill.","Jiang Cheng leaned against the railing of the central atrium and looked down through the open space.","There were people on every floor, taking all kinds of things.","Many people on the first floor were changing their shoes. Fighting zombies had worn shoes out surprisingly quickly, and many peopleâs shoes were so dirty that they could no longer be washed clean. Some of the shoes people wore every day were also unsuitable for walking such long distances.","The vast majority of them changed into athletic shoes.","Some had taken bags, too. Double-strap backpacks and crossbody bags were the most popular choices, since they could carry a bit of food and water with them when they went out.","Clothes were what most people took. Thin ones, thick ones, underwear, outerwearâpeople took all kinds.","Those were the mainstream choices. There were non-mainstream ones, too.","Someone had gone to the laptop section on the fifth floor and taken a computer. When asked, his answer was that his own computer wasnât good enough, so he had taken a better one home to play games.","Someone else had taken a digital camera along with an entire box of memory cards.","âIâll carry it with me from now on and take more pictures. Maybe one day, my photos will end up in the history books.â","Li Jiangbing had changed into a new pair of outdoor shoes. Clomp, clomp, clompâhe came looking for Jiang Cheng. âEverythingâs been loaded into the car. What are you looking at?â","Seeing Jiang Cheng staring intently downstairs, he leaned over the railing to look as well.","On the first floor, two people were rummaging through the display cases of a jewelry store, stuffing gold necklaces and bracelets into their pockets.","Li Jiangbing: ââ¦â","âWhat a pair of idiots,â Li Jiangbing cursed. âThose two morons.â","Jiang Cheng curled her lips. âHow interesting.â","The difference between people could really be that enormous.","Li Jiangbing cursed again. âEven with my limited education, I know that in the future, food and water will be the only things worth anything. Can a huge gold bracelet be exchanged for a steamed bun?â","The vehicles were packed to the brim on the way back.","By the time they returned to the Young Adultsâ Apartments, it was already dark.","The cafeteria had prepared meals according to the number of people listed on the notice. This time, they no longer had to sit on the floor to eat. Long tables had been arranged in rows, each with chairs, so everyone had a seat.","Mr. Xu and Director Yu had already eaten with the residents of the complex, but neither of them had gone back. They had found a place to sit, chatting while observing the situation.","Director Yu sighed. âNo oneâs invited the two of us to move in.â","Mr. Xu comforted him. âMaybe the people in charge arenât here. Letâs wait until theyâre done with their business and see what happens.â","Director Yu knew that was only consolation. That handsome man surnamed Song was obviously in charge. Whenever the team went out, everyone in the complex followed his instructions and arrangements. Whenever anything happened, they all went to him.","Handsome Song certainly knew that two new superpowered people had arrived. That morning, he had been the one to say over the walkie-talkie, âIâll send someone to meet them at the east gate.â","But Handsome Song hadnât come over to invite them in with tearful pleas, urging them to move into the Young Adultsâ Apartments and enjoy better treatment.","Not like Master Luo.","Master Luo had been taken away first thing that morning and moved directly to a new place.","The two men silently ate strawberries, neither willing to admit that their powers were simply too weak and that they werenât worth recruiting.","In fact, the two of them had made a lot of progress after practicing all day. Mr. Xu in particular had started with a much better physique than Director Yu. His only disadvantage was that he had spent too little time practicing over the past few days.","Mr. Xu suddenly nudged Director Yu with his elbow. âThatâs Jiang Cheng.â","Director Yu looked over. Yes, there was no mistake. They had both seen her on television before. The young girl talking to Handsome Song was definitely Jiang Cheng.","âThe big guy next to her must be Li Jiangbing.â","âThose two should be Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan. They match the descriptions.â","âAnd the two talking to themâare they Shield and Doctor? I canât tell which is which.â","âItâs easy. Shield is on the left, and Doctor is on the right.â","ââ¦How can you tell?â","âWasnât Doctor supposed to be someone you didnât want to mess with? Look at the girl on the rightâsheâs punched that young man twice in the three sentences sheâs said. All right, the one getting beaten has to be Gao Yuxuan. That makes the calmer one Zhao Yi. Now we can tell the two of them apart as well.â"]},{"number":158,"title":"Chapter 158: 0158","paragraphs":["âSix groups came by during the day, twenty-one people in all. Theyâd all seen us on television and come looking for us,â Song Jingshuo briefed Jiang Cheng on what had happened in the complex while she was away. âTheyâve all been settled in.â","âTwo superpowered people came over from Jixiang Jiayuanâone metal-type and one electrical-type. The metal-type one is decent. The electrical-type one is mediocre.â","âBut heâs got a good head on his shoulders,â Song Jingshuo added approvingly.","He had come over from there first thing in the morning, which showed that he was quick-witted.","âI didnât deal with them right away. I left them waiting,â he said. âWe shouldnât go looking for them. We need to make them come begging to us.â","Master Luo had been brought over first thing that morning because there were too few wood-types. With so many people waiting to be fed, they couldnât work Song Jingshuo to death, so they had recruited him in an emergency.","None of the other superpowers was particularly indispensable.","Jiang Cheng smiled.","She and Song Jingshuo were perfectly in sync.","Song Jingshuo handed Jiang Cheng a stack of printed pages.","Jiang Cheng quickly skimmed through them, then handed them back. âLooks good. I have no objections.â","The performance-assessment system Song Jingshuo had spent a whole day and night designing had been approved by the two of them just like that.","The second floor of the clubhouse had also been cleared out, and the people staying behind were helping move things in.","The team had brought back a great deal of supplies: padded coats, quilts, all kinds of clothing, snacks, drinks, and chocolate.","It was impossible not to sneak a piece of chocolate or open a bottle of soda while carrying everything in.","Everyone understood that these things were meant to become benefits for everyone in the future. If an organization couldnât offer decent benefits, how could it motivate people to work?","The people from the Youth Apartment werenât worried in the slightest.","There were no idle people in the Youth Apartment. Nearly everyone had something to do.","With so many people living together, there were endless little matters to deal with. People were needed everywhere:","Cleaning, repairs and maintenance, helping in the cafeteria, keeping order, looking after children, fertilizing the fields, and harvesting ripe crops.","The cafeteria alone required a great many people now.","And they were different from everyone else. The status of âYouth Apartment homeownerâ had already begun to carry an air of something like official tenure.","Now that so many outsiders were arriving, the entire Youth Apartment had effectively become Jiang Chengâs inner circle.","Jiang Cheng never let her own people suffer losses, and everyone felt secure because of it.","Song Jingshuo and Jiang Cheng went upstairs to the clubhouse together.","The metal-types had built a great many shelves. The young people were orderly and efficient, and all kinds of items had been sorted and stored neatly.","Once everyone had gone downstairs, Jiang Cheng began taking things out.","Song Jingshuo watched her.","She had already taken out a large amount of frozen meat in the cafeteria.","Now she was taking out clothing, bedding, and daily necessities.","She kept taking things out.","And taking things out.","And taking out more and more.","She continued until Song Jingshuo went from completely composed to visibly stunned.","âJiang Cheng,â Song Jingshuo finally asked, âhow big is your storage space now?â","Everyone knew that as long as a person was willing to work hard and endure the physical pain, a superpower could be improved.","But quite a lot of people couldnât withstand the physical agony of breaking through their limits. It was truly unbearable. Some had tried pushing themselves until their eyes began to hurt, feeling as though they were about to go blind.","If they didnât stop, it felt as though their eyeballs were being gouged out alive.","The clearest example was Li Jiangbing.","Li Jiangbingâs water-type superpower wasnât like those of Zhou Wang, Guo Jun, or Aunt Pan, whose abilities had been powerful from the moment they started. When he first awakened, his superpower had been very ordinary, no different from everyone elseâs.","But now, he could manipulate water with astonishing skill.","A few days earlier, his eyes had been bloodshot every morning when he showed up. All the medicine was with Zhang Lesi, and he had asked her for several boxes of eye drops. Song Jingshuo knew all about it.","It was just that water-type abilities were noncombat abilities, so after everyone grew accustomed to them, they no longer seemed particularly impressive.","Unlike Guo Jun and Aunt Pan. Whenever either of them made a move, everyone would let out a collective gasp of admiration.","âI donât know,â Jiang Cheng said. âThereâs no way to quantify it.â","At first, the storage space Jiang Cheng could âseeâ had seemed about the size of a bathroom. But that was merely a visual projection produced through her mental link.","Jiang Cheng soon discovered that the space couldnât actually be measured by volume.","The visual projection she could see hadnât changed much over the past few days, but her spatial ability had continued to improve.","Moreover, Jiang Cheng had noticed something rather incredible.","Today, her storage space seemed to have reached a breakthrough.","She wasnât entirely sure.","The spaceâs capacity increased every day, and she hadnât deliberately kept track of how much it could hold before the previous two days.","Compared with what she could âsee,â the sensations she received through the mental link were closer to reality.","By the time the two of them went downstairs, the complexâs core staff had already gathered in the lobby.","Song Jingshuo explained the performance-assessment system he had designed.","Someone listened with a blank stare. âWhy does this feel like Iâm back at work?â","Everyone burst out laughing.","Put simply, the system meant that there could be no âegalitarian pot.â","The consequences of everyone sharing the same pot had already been proven by history. So compensation would be based on work performed.","Of course, the first priority was to guarantee everyoneâs basic survival needs: they would be fed.","Song Jingshuo said, âAs long as conditions allow, weâll do our best to guarantee everyoneâs meals.â","He also guaranteed that all Youth Apartment homeowners, along with those granted equivalent homeowner status, would receive fruit every day as a fixed benefit.","However, the snacks, drinks, clothing, and other supplies collected from outside would all be placed under rationing and control starting tomorrow.","Every position would generate performance points, whether it involved going out with the team to rescue people or performing various kinds of labor at home. Every job would earn performance points.","Naturally, the rescue team would earn the most. No one objected to that; everyone considered it reasonable, since they faced danger.","Performance points could be used like wages to âpurchaseâ any controlled supplies.","Someone immediately said, âIsnât this the same as the work points used in rural areas decades ago?â","Song Jingshuo: â...Itâs not that old-fashioned.â","Song Jingshuo had always projected an upscale, cosmopolitan image, so it couldnât be called work points. They had to be performance points.","Only then would it sound sophisticated, cosmopolitan, and suitably in line with his personal style.","Everyone roared with laughter.","That night, after washing up, Jiang Cheng lay in bed with her eyes closed, concentrating as she seriously tried to sense her storage space.","If she had done this the night before, she could have confirmed the unusual change that had appeared early that morning. But since she hadnât paid attention at the time, she couldnât confirm it now.","She would have to wait until tomorrow.","Mr. Xu and Director Yu returned to their âhomeâ in Jixiang Jiayuan.","As soon as they stepped through the door, they found everyone gathered in the four-bedroom apartment. The moment they saw them, the group surged forward.","âYouâre back! Youâre back!â","âMr. Xu, Director Yu, youâve worked so hard!â","Everyone hustled the two men over to the sofa and pressed them down onto it.","Some brought tea, others massaged their shoulders, and everyone fussed over the two men with excessive warmth and concern.","Mr. Xu/Director Yu: â...â","âAll right, all right. Enough with the act.â Mr. Xu waved them off and handed the plastic bag in his hand to one of the employees. âThese are for you.â","âWow, strawberries!â","âTheyâre huge again! Hurry up and divide them!â","âAs expected of Mr. Xu. Where did you get these?â","There were eight strawberries in the plastic bag.","For the past two days, everyone had been free to pick strawberries, and some people at the Youth Apartments had ended up eating so many that they were sick of them. At dinner, even one strawberry per person felt like too much.","As it happened, two newcomers had arrived: Mr. Xu and Director Yu.","Mr. Xu worked diligently, earnestly learning from experience and humbly listening to everyoneâs advice.","Director Yu, a chubby middle-aged man, was also going all out to improve his fitness, running laps alongside the younger people.","Everyone had a good impression of the two of them. They had heard the pair say that there were still more than twenty people in their âhome,â all of whom had shared hardship and risked their lives together. Once they had gotten familiar with a few people, those people gave their own portions of strawberries to them.","Everyone cut the strawberries into pieces with knives and shared them around.","âEat up,â Director Yu said. âStarting tomorrow, things will get difficult. They arenât going to provide fruit for us anymore. Itâs going to be rationed.â","No one was surprised. They had already been told that morning that potatoes would be the only food provided in the future.","Something as luxurious as fruit was bound to be placed under control.","Everyone gathered in a circle around the sofa. âMr. Xu, what did you find out today? Tell us about it.â","Mr. Xu and Director Yu straightened up and grew serious. âAll right, then. Weâll tell you.â","âThe Youth Apartments are at the very heart of this provisional governmentâs organizational structure. All the authorityâcommand, personnel, and administrationâis concentrated there.â","âOld Yu and I have successfully integrated ourselves today. Although we havenât entered the management level yet, the path upward is very clear, and thereâs plenty of room for advancement.â","Mr. Xu paused, then took a reserved sip of tea to moisten his throat.","Everyone applauded.","Mr. Xu set down his teacup and continued. âThe difference in treatment between the two sides is obvious. For now, it looks like theyâre still in the early stages of setting up this makeshift organization, so there may be a period when things arenât very rigorous. But the few young people over there seem genuinely capable. I expect theyâll adjust and get everything on track soon.â","âWeâre classified as refugees right now. No, more accurately, you are. Youâre currently considered refugees, and in the future youâll only receive the minimum resources necessary to survive. Your food allowance will be potatoes.â","âBut donât panic. Given the current situation, they canât rely solely on the few hundred people next door. The core team is certain to expand. If everyone wants better treatment, you need to seize the opportunity. The moment they begin expanding and recruiting, join immediately.â","âSeniority. Remember this: seniority is very important in any collective. From what I can tell, the provisional government is preparing to go into the city every day to bring people back. There will be more and more people in the future. The earlier you join a collective, the more benefits youâll enjoy.â","Everyone asked, âMr. Xu, why are only we considered refugees? What about the two of you?â","Director Yu spread his hands. âWeâve already integrated ourselves.â","Everyone fell silent.","âOh, right,â Mr. Xu said. âDonât prepare meals for the two of us. Weâre already signed up for all three meals over there.â","Zhou Wang returned from the Youth Apartments with Little Huang. Xiao Dan had been waiting for him at the entrance, peering into the distance.","When she saw the two of them, Xiao Dan went to meet them. âWhy are you back so late? Our girl already went back to sleep.â","âWe had a meeting,â Zhou Wang said.","Little Huang stayed by Zhou Wangâs side. Although he was young, his superpower was far too unusual, so he was completely different from Wang Yunya and the other children.","He was counted as core personnel.","Xiao Dan gave Zhou Wang a report on the dayâs work. âTwenty-one new people arrived today. I got all of them settled.â","âThey made all sorts of demands. Thereâs no way we can satisfy them all.â","âThere was even a fight. I had to call people over from the Youth Apartments before we could stop it.â","Zhou Wang was surprised. âHow did they end up fighting?â","Xiao Dan was exasperated. âDonât ask. They said they were coworkers from a television station and had some old grudge between them. Then they happened to be assigned to the same apartment, and they started fighting today. Weâve already moved them to separate rooms.â","As soon as people saw that someone had been given a room change, several others who werenât satisfied with their accommodations also demanded to be moved.","âI refused them all. We canât open the door to that sort of thing. They have somewhere to live and food to eatâwhat more do they want? Do they think weâre a wishing well?â","Zhou Wang praised her. âYou handled it well.â","Xiao Dan hadnât held a regular job in many years. After her daughter grew up, she had run a few small businesses and even sold insurance. Though she hadnât made a fortune, she had earned a modest incomeâno less than she would have from a regular job.","Overall, she was quite a capable person.","Zhou Wang handed her several sheets of paper. âTake a look at this.â","Under the streetlamp, Xiao Dan quickly flipped through them.","A complete system had been established, and it was fairly comprehensive. Every aspect had been taken into consideration. Even the calculations and distribution of performance points appeared reasonably balanced and acceptable.","Zhou Wang specifically pointed something out to her. âYouâre in a management position. Management positions are classified as fixed posts, so the benefits are quite good.â","Xiao Dan knew that she couldnât have come up with such a detailed plan in such a short time. In truth, she had no experience managing people. She simply liked taking charge and organizing things.","She considered herself a very energetic person, but by the end of the day, she felt utterly exhausted.","Managing people really was exhausting. It was no easier than fighting zombies."]},{"number":159,"title":"Chapter 159: 0159","paragraphs":["Jiang Cheng opened her eyes and woke.","Mo Li leaped onto her chest, sniffed the tip of her nose, then sat quietly and stared at her.","Jiang Cheng closed her eyes and focused on what she was feeling.","She had sensed it repeatedly before going to sleep the night before, forcing herself to memorize the sensation.","There was no mistaking it. Her storage space had definitelyâ¦ leveled up again.","Zhao Yi hadnât even swallowed his first mouthful of breakfast when Jiang Cheng called him aside to talk.","Watching from a distance, Zhang Lesi nudged Su Yu with her elbow. âLook at Zhao Yi. Why does he always seem so nervous around Jiang Cheng?â","Su Yu glanced over. âHeâs afraid of Jiang Cheng, I guess.â","Zhang Lesi: ââ¦?â","Su Yu actually understood him pretty well, but she couldnât explain it to Zhang Lesi. Someone as carefree as Zhang Lesi could never empathize with people like them, who tended to keep everything bottled up inside.","Biting into her flatbread, Zhang Lesi said, ââ¦Zhao Yi isnât in love with Jiang Cheng, is he?â","ââ¦â Su Yu replied firmly, âNo.â","âI didnât think so either.â Zhang Lesi said, âIsnât Jiang Cheng dating Song Jingshuo?â","Su Yu was firm again. âNo.â","Zhang Lesi: ââ¦How do you know?â","âYou can tell after spending enough time with them.â","The hormones between two people who were attracted to each other should be something hazy and sticky, something that clung to them so tightly they could never pull apart.","Not something where, whenever the two of them drew near, a spreadsheet seemed to appear in the background: You enter one string of numbers, I enter another.","The grid lines were crisp, the values precise.","And they haggled over every last decimal.","Zhang Lesi said, âTheyâre looking over here. Are they looking at you or me?â","Su Yu looked up. Sure enough, the two of them glanced in their direction, then turned back and continued talking.","She turned to look at Zhang Lesi, who was biting her lip.","Now that was more like it. When someone who had always been bold, brisk, and decisive became anxious, clingy, and uncertain, that was what hormones looked like.","Zhao Yi said, âIt must be related to mental and psychological factors. All the samples display this characteristic. Look at Su Yuâsheâs the most typical example.â","Jiang Cheng and Zhao Yi turned to look at Su Yu in the distance.","Su Yuâs closest friend had once been He Tian. After He Tian was gone, Su Yu and Zhang Lesi had started partnering up. Their personalities were worlds apart, yet they got along harmoniously. They complemented each other quite well.","Of course, aside from Aunt Pan and Jiang Cheng, they were also widely acknowledged to be the two strongest, most unusual, and most useful superpowered women. It was only natural that they would end up together.","Humans were social creatures. Everyone needed a companion.","Zhao Yi asked, âHave you suffered some kind of mental shock? Experienced a major psychological change? Did Director Guo frighten you?â","Jiang Cheng shook her head. âThat sort of thing canât scare me.â","[That sort of thing canât scare me.] What a heroine line!","Zhao Yi fought hard to keep his expression under control.","He tried so hard that, from a distance, Zhang Lesi and Su Yu couldnât help but find him rather tense.","Still, it was better than losing control and grinning like an idiot, only to have people mistake him for one.","Zhao Yi tried to guide her from a professional angle. âHave you overcome something? Defeated some aspect of yourself? Made some kind of change?â","Jiang Cheng lifted her eyelids.","A change?","That was certainly true.","At the television station, she had decided to accept more than five hundred refugees who looked as if their souls had already left their bodies. She had announced during a live broadcast that the High-Tech New District would open its doors to refugees.","From that moment on, she had already begun to change.","She was no longer accepting only the strongâthe âuseful.â She was taking in the weak as well.","The theories she had read about in books were quite interesting. She wanted to try them.","In truth, they ran counter to her own beliefs. Even Song Jingshuo had noticed that.","The day before yesterday, five hundred refugees had moved in. Yesterday, she had been astonished to discover that her storage space could hold so many things.","Yesterday, she had saved a group of people who would have died if she hadnât intervened. Today, when she woke up, the space had clearly leveled up again.","But this wasnât quite the same as what had happened to Su Yu, whose brain had exploded into action after undergoing a tremendous psychological shock.","This felt more like some kind ofâ¦ reward for getting the answer right.","Jiang Cheng folded her arms. âDonât you think that theory is rather vague and insubstantial?â","Zhao Yi became energized at once. âHumanity has yet to develop even ten percent of the brain. We canât deny infinite possibilities simply because our technology hasnât reached that level. We can say, with awe, that it belongs to the realm of the gods, but we canât simply dismiss it.â","The realm of the gods.","Putting a personâs soul into another world did sound like something only a godâor someone with divine powersâcould accomplish.","A god was manipulating her.","A god was watching her.","A god was pleased with her.","âI understand.â Jiang Cheng nodded. âGo eat your breakfast before it gets cold.â","Jiang Cheng turned and walked away.","Wait, waitâ¦ So what exactly was the reason? He wanted to know too!","Disappointed, Zhao Yi turned around. The moment he looked up, he saw Zhang Lesi standing in the distance with her arms folded, staring at him.","Zhao Yi: ââ¦â","She was another person he was somewhat afraid of.","Zhao Yi hurriedly looked around for Gao Yuxuan.","Where the hell had he gone? He had to be taking a dump!","âYou were right,â Zhang Lesi said. âThis really isnât like me.â","Su Yu had just pointed out the state she was in.","Zhang Lesi continued, âIâm going to ask him directly later.â","âIf he likes Jiang Chengâ¦â she said, âIâm not giving up that easily.â","Su Yu almost choked on her porridge.","âWhy are you reacting so strongly?â Zhang Lesi said. âEven if he likes Jiang Cheng, Jiang Cheng isnât dating him. Of course I have to fight for him. If thereâs something you want, you have to fight for it yourself. How can you just give up?â","Su Yu sighed. âThe two of us really are different.â","Zhang Lesi teased her, âRight. Youâre just waiting for the rabbit to run into the tree, arenât you? Youâre staying home and waiting for the other person to make the first move. If they happen to be the same kind of person as you, the two of you can wait for each other for ten thousand years.â","Su Yu fell silent.","She simply stared at Zhao Yi until he finished eating and returned his tray.","Zhang Lesi stood up. âWish me luck.â","âGood luck! You can do it!â Su Yu cheered.","She went to return her tray. When she turned around, she saw Zhang Lesi in the distance with one palm planted against the wall, forcibly blocking Zhao Yi in.","She looked incredibly domineering.","Su Yu couldnât help laughing, though she felt a little envious as well.","There was no point in being envious. She simply wasnât that kind of person, and she couldnât imitate it even if she tried.","The refugees at Auspicious Garden had come downstairs early in the morning.","They had nothing to do, and since they had gone to bed early, they had woken up early too. They had also been informed the day before that they needed to come downstairs early to collect potatoes. There was another announcement to be made, and everyone had to attend.","Standing at a higher spot with a loudspeaker in hand, Zhou Wang looked out at the enormous crowd.","The refugeesâ spirits really couldnât compare with those of the local residents. Even after a full day of rest, they still looked like this.","Zhou Wang raised the loudspeaker. âThose who moved in yesterday can take today off and join the group activities tomorrow. But donât leave after collecting your potatoes. Watch for a while first, so I wonât have to repeat everything tomorrow.â","âTo those who came from the television station the day before yesterday: rested enough? Good. Then weâre getting ready to work.â","âNo one is obligated to support other people for free. Our provisional government was established by residents from several neighborhoods, and everyone has put in a lot of time and effort. So letâs not sit around doing nothing while eating and drinking for free.â","âOf course, if youâre genuinely too sick or weak to do anything, donât panic. As we said, potatoesâenough to fill your stomach! At any rate, no one is going to starve to death.â","âBut if you want to live a little better, then we need to get moving and put in some work.â","âWork is glorious!â","Zhou Wang announced the performance-point system created by Song Jingshuoâthe points assigned to each position, the work required, the supplies that could be exchanged for them, and so on.","Zhou Wang shouted at the top of his lungs, âI wonât waste time with unnecessary talk. A household can only thrive when everyone contributes. Weâre one big family now, so everyone has to do their part if we all want to live better!â","âAll right, letâs start by handing out potatoes.â","âSign up at the table over there. Anyone registering for a squad, move to the frontâthe squad is about to depart, so hurry!â","The reason Song Jingshuo had chosen potatoes, of course, was their astonishing yield.","Every single one was as big as a basketball.","The metal-type ability users had made waist-high iron cages to hold them. Forklifts carried the potatoes from the Youth Apartments to Jixiang Jiayuan.","A long line had already formed in front of the registration table.","The squads offered considerably better benefits than the other positions, which made them highly appealing.","With armor, zombies were actually nothing to fearâas long as you didnât run into some kind of super-mutated one.","Besides, there were plenty of formidable people in the temporary government of the Technology New District, along with a super-powerful God-Cat.","But the main reason wasâ¦","Nobody wanted to eat potatoes every day!","All the men from Mr. Xuâs company went to sign up for the squads.","Mr. Xu had generously set up a gym at the company, so everyone was in fairly good physical shape. The squads also issued armor and weapons. With so many people around, anyone afraid of dying could simply blend into the middle and slack off a little. It wasnât as if that were impossible.","The administrative manager and the HR assistant wanted to sign up too. Since they were all on the same side, they figured they could at least watch each otherâs backs even if they had to fight zombies.","Who could have guessed they would be turned down?","âAt present, the squads are only accepting women with special abilities.â","Ordinary people without special abilities would have to rely entirely on brute strength. And when it came to brute strength, the men were sufficient for the time being, so they were accepting men first.","The two women were somewhat disappointed.","Then the administrative manager turned her head and spotted the woman in charge of Jixiang Jiayuan, who was so busy she could barely keep up with everything. Her eyes lit up. She grabbed the HR assistant and went over to offer their services.","âWe handle administration and human resources at the company. Weâre good at management and organization.â","That was exactly what Xiao Dan needed, so she hired them on the spot.","Excellent. The first people from the company to work their way into the management team were neither Mr. Xu nor Director Yu, but the administrative manager and the HR assistant.","After listening to Zhou Wangâs speech, Mr. Xu and Director Yu herded all their employees off to register, then went to the Youth Apartments for breakfast.","Many people at the Youth Apartments had already finished eating.","Some had already started working, sweeping the courtyard and clearing away trash.","A group of little children finished breakfast and followed the young auntie assigned to look after them that day in doing morning exercises.","They werenât getting a free meal, either. A pile of child-sized brooms sat nearby. Once their exercises were done, each child picked up a small broom and carried it off to sweep the corridors.","Mr. Xu and Director Yu watched.","Mr. Xu nodded. âNot bad.â","He had barely finished speaking when someone came over and threw an arm around his shoulders.","âBrother Xu, have you eaten yet? You havenât? Then eat first. Weâre going out to kill zombies today!â","Mr. Xu said, âWait a second, Iâ¦â","âWait for what? Stick with us. Donât be scared.â","âCome on, come on!â","âWeâre splitting into teams today. There are too many people asking for help, so we have to divide into several squads to rescue them. Everyone has to pitch in!â","âOur metal-type ability users have to go with the vehicles. They canât do without us.â","âIâm telling you, you earn a lot more work points with the squads.â","âDonât say âwork pointsâ again, or Old Song will come after you.â","âHahahahahaha!â"]},{"number":160,"title":"Chapter 160: 0160","paragraphs":["Director Yu could only watch helplessly as his boss was carried away by the others.","Some young men came over to greet him. They were the lightning-element guys he had met yesterday. Nervously, he asked, âD-Do I have to go with the team too?â","Some of the young men said, âYouâd better sit this one out. Get some more practice first.â","Others said, âWhy not send him straight into battle? A little stimulation might help him break through.â","But in the end, they still didnât let Director Yu go. His superpower was rather weak, and he was a little overweight too. They were worried he wouldnât be able to keep up.","Most of the survivors had been trapped in high-rises in the city. Taking the elevators was unsafe, so they had to climb the stairs floor by floor.","Just climbing the stairs would be a struggle for Director Yu.","One of the young men warned him, âWhen weâre gone, you have to run on your own. You absolutely have to run.â","His stamina and lung capacity had to improve.","Everyone said, âEven if zombies are chasing you, youâll need to be able to run for your life.â","They were curious. âHow did you survive last time?â","Director Yu chuckled. âI was on vacation.â","He had gone to a grassland ranch resort where there werenât many people.","There had been only two or three zombies, and everyone had worked together to kill them. After learning that the entire country had fallen, the tourists had been too afraid to leave.","The resort had plenty of stored food, and most importantly, it had lots of sheep.","In the later stages, everyone ate mutton every day. It traumatized Director Yu so badly that even now, he barely touched lamb.","Mr. Xu was dragged by the metal-element users over to a young man named Cui Haiyang.","âThis is the guy. He should be pretty good.â","Cui Haiyangâs eyes lit up. He immediately started manhandling Mr. Xu, squeezing his arm and patting his chest.","âBig bro, those are some nice muscles.â","With a grand wave of his hand, Cui Haiyang declared, âYouâre on my team.â","And just like that, Mr. Xu had been assigned.","After breakfast, Mr. Xu collected his armor and crescent shovel, then listened as Cui Haiyang gave him a brief explanation of the job.","Metal-element users were unquestionably the most hardworking among all the superpowered people. They could both fight and work.","Their main task on the road was maintaining the sharpness of the vehicleâs âBlade,â keeping it in such good condition that any zombie foolish enough to ram into it would lose its head.","âWe metal users do more work, so we earn more too,â Cui Haiyang explained. âEvery day, on top of the teamâs performance points, we also get a fixed amount of extra performance points. And if thereâs any temporary overtime, we get overtime performance points as well.â","ââ¦â Mr. Xu looked at him. âWhy is there overtime?â","âOf course there is. Sometimes we suddenly need something, or a large group of people shows up and we have to rush out a large batch of armor.â","âOh, I see.â","âIâm telling you, metal-element users are the most valuable of all. The gold standard. Work hard, Brother Xu.â","The teams really were treated well. Just before they boarded the vehicle, the driver handed each person two chocolate bars.","They were meant to replenish their energy during battle.","Mr. Xu tucked his into his pocket.","As a newcomer, Mr. Xu still wasnât used to fighting with his superpower.","âItâs fine,â Cui Haiyang said. âWith muscles like yours, you donât even need a superpower.â","Mr. Xu reached over and tugged on the chains wrapped around Cui Haiyang. âWhatâs with this outfit?â","The young manâs armor was wrapped in coils of what looked like chains, giving him a punkish, post-apocalyptic-movie vibe.","Cui Haiyang grinned. âYouâll find out soon enough.â","When they reached their destination and entered the building, Mr. Xu tightened his grip on the crescent shovel.","He might have been getting on in years, but he had spent many years lifting weights and working out. He didnât want the younger guys to look down on him.","At the same time, he was afraid of losing his life and wanted to hide in the back and slack off.","He was torn.","Inside the corridors, the doors to some offices stood open. The zombies heard the noise and came rushing over.","Mr. Xu began to tense up.","Cui Haiyang walked at the front. He slapped a hand against his body, then flicked two fingers forward.","Several chains shot into the air like snakes.","They wrapped around a zombieâs neck and began spinning at high speed. The zombieâs head dropped cleanly to the floor.","The headless zombie collapsed.","Those werenât chains.","They were chainsaws. Actual saws!","Mr. Xuâs mouth fell open and refused to close. So this was another way to use a superpower?","What theâ?","His plan to slack off and avoid danger vanished completely.","His blood began to race.","What had he built all these muscles for? This was exactly the kind of situation they were meant for!","Mr. Xu charged at the zombies with his crescent shovel, shouting. Before he even reached them, the shovel automatically extended and thrust forward.","A head rolled to the floor.","What a rush!","People like Cui Haiyang, who had relatively powerful abilities, had already begun leading teams on their own.","Cui Haiyang led one team, Guo Jun led another, Aunt Pan led one, Gao Yuxuan led one, Su Yu led one, and Wu Jiancheng led one.","By now, everyone had tacitly accepted that, at least within the teams, superpowered people were expected to take the lead. Ordinary people had to take a subordinate position.","Li Jiangbing was also superpowered, but his ability couldnât be used in combat, so he didnât lead a team by himself. He stayed with Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Chengâs ability wasnât combat-oriented either, but she had Mo Li.","Mo Liâs combat power was so overwhelming that none of the other superpowered people dared claim they could stand against him.","After all, Director Guo had died in Mo Liâs jaws.","Today, Jiang Cheng also kept Zhou Wang and Little Huang at her side instead of letting them form their own teams. The destination assigned to her team was known to contain a mutant zombie.","The emergency message read: âIt looks like a spider. It can climb walls and walk across ceilings. Itâs incredibly fast!â","Little Huang sensed it as soon as they entered the building.","âItâs a little dangerous.â","But the danger was nowhere near that of Director Guo.","Whether that meant they were incredibly lucky or incredibly unlucky was hard to say. They had encountered Director Guo on their very first day of battle, which had raised everyoneâs expectationsâand their danger thresholdâfar too high.","Even Brother Dong had come along today.","The emergency message had mentioned something being âfast,â so Jiang Cheng had Zhou Wang drag Brother Dong over as well.","Brother Dong had rested for two days and felt that some of his energy had returned.","As long as a person lived among other people, they could absorb at least a little of the vitality around them.","The two wind-element users quickly located the âspider zombieâ described in the message.","It really did look like a spider. It had eight legsâ","No, six legs and two arms.","Those six legs were actual human legs. Two of them still had trouser legs attached. Although the fabric had rotted away from the body, it was clear that they belonged to the zombie itself.","The other four legs were completely bare, and two of them appeared to be womenâs legs.","When the zombie crawled along the floor, its belly faced downward and its back faced up.","Its two arms were at the front, while the six legs behind it all bent downward. It truly looked like a spider. The person who sent the message hadnât exaggerated.","It couldnât spin webs, since it wasnât a real spider. But it could climb walls, and when it crawled upside down across the ceiling, it moved so quickly it looked like a fading shadow, effortlessly defying gravity.","Watching the zombie skitter across the ceiling, Li Jiangbing grew frantic. He kept urging Mo Li, âSweetie, get in there! Come on, get in there!â","Mo Li only glanced at it.","âMeow~â","Jiang Cheng fell silent.","Li Jiangbing asked, âWhat did he say?â","Jiang Cheng replied, âHe said, âThereâs no need for me to go.ââ","Li Jiangbing: ââ¦â","Was Mo Li actually looking down on the zombie for being too weak?","As it turned out, Mo Li really wasnât needed. The spider zombie was fast, but Zhou Wang and Brother Dong were fast too.","The two of them chased after it like the wind, hacking off its legs one by one. The spider zombie grew slower and slower, until finally they cut off its head as well.","It was completely dead.","Everyone gathered around the monster, sighing. âHow can a person become something like this?â","Jiang Cheng also stared at the hideously deformed zombie.","If âGodâ was testing her, then did âGodâ also turn humans into monsters?","âGodâ wasnât even satisfied with ordinary zombies anymore, but had begun creating creatures like this for the sake of sheer novelty.","During the lunch break, Jiang Cheng took out her phone, which was still on silent, and noticed a missed call from the property management office. It was probably Yang Xinyan.","Jiang Cheng called back. â...Is that so? Thatâs great. All right, give me their number and Iâll call them.â","After hanging up, Jiang Cheng raised an eyebrow. âApart from us, someone else has established a provisional government.â","Everyone was astonished.","The call went through immediately.","âHello?â","Jiang Cheng said, âHello, Iâm Jiang Cheng from the Science and Technology New District.â","The other party sounded delighted. âHello, Jiang Cheng. Weâve finally managed to get in touch with you.â","Jiang Cheng said, âCould you tell me about your situation?â","The other person composed himself before saying, âWeâre in Shilong District. Weâve confirmed that there are no survivors at the Shilong District Government Office. Weâve established the Shilong District Provisional Government. We hope to receive your advice and assistance on what to do next.â","Jiang Cheng carefully asked about their circumstances.","More than a hundred people had gathered there, half of them coworkers from the same state-owned enterprise. The rest were people they had encountered and gathered along the way over the past few days.","They had originally taken control of an old residential compound and settled there. Then they saw Jiang Chengâs televised broadcast. They no longer wanted to hide away and had decided to step forward as well.","Jiang Cheng and the others had already visited the municipal government office, and the government they had established was also a district-level government.","So today, the group went to the Shilong District Government Office, where they were currently located, and confirmed that there were no survivors. Following the example of the Science and Technology New District Provisional Government, they established the Shilong District Provisional Government on the spot.","Jiang Cheng asked, âDo you have a sustainable source of food?â","âYes,â the other person replied. âWe cleared out a supermarket and stocked up on quite a lot of food. We also have someone with a wood-based superpower. Sheâs already started growing vegetables.â","As long as they had someone with a wood-based ability who could provide a steady source of food, they had the foundation for development.","Everything else could be acquired gradually.","Jiang Cheng said, âHow about we meet? At the television station?â","The other party sounded surprised.","Jiang Cheng continued, âFirst, itâll be easier to discuss things in person. Second, weâve received a huge number of distress calls. Today, weâve expanded our team and divided it into seven groups to rescue survivors. But given the size of S City, weâre still far too stretched thin.â","âNow that youâre here, I hope you can take over the rescue operations in Shilong District. If thatâs acceptable, letâs meet at the television station. If everything checks out, we can hold a live broadcast, announce your information, and officially hand over the affairs of Shilong District to you.â","âI also hope this will encourage more capable people to step forward.â","âWith the government gone, weâll establish one ourselves.â","The other person seemed to have caught fire as well. âAll right, Jiang Cheng. See you at the television station!â"]},{"number":161,"title":"Chapter 161: 0161","paragraphs":["The survivors they had just rescued were, as a rule, in terrible condition.","Jiang Cheng quickly discussed the situation with everyone. In the end, they decided that Li Jiangbing would lead a team and drive the large truck back to the New Technology District with the survivors so they could be settled there.","The others found a business van on the street. Jiang Cheng and Zhou Wang took several people with them and headed for the television station in S City.","Three of those accompanying them were technical staff from the station.","There was no such thing as a traffic jam or traffic lights anymore. They sped along the empty roads and arrived at the television station half an hour later, where they met the people from Shilong District.","It looked as though nearly all of the districtâs more than one hundred people had come. At the front was a middle-aged man whose words and bearing carried a certain authority. He was part of the management of their state-owned enterprise.","Jiang Cheng shook his hand. âIâm Jiang Cheng.â","âMy surname is Zheng. Zheng Junwei.â The middle-aged man sighed. âJiang Cheng, Iâve finally met you in person. Youâre even younger than we imagined.â","âIn the current situation, age is no longer a standard by which anyone can be judged,â Jiang Cheng replied. âBrother Zheng, letâs go up to the third floor and have a proper talk.â","The third floor contained a large broadcasting studio with plenty of chairs, enough to accommodate so many people.","As everyone looked up, they saw a huge hole in the wall of the second floor.","âWhat happened here?â","Jiang Cheng said, âThere was a mutated zombie in the television station. It had grown to an enormous size, and it took quite a bit of effort to kill it.â","The people from Shilong District clicked their tongues in astonishment. âThat must have been one terrifying zombie.â","âWeâve encountered mutated zombies too,â they said.","Everyone sat down in the broadcasting studio on the third floor and had a thorough discussion.","Jiang Cheng kept nothing to himself. He took out several sheets of paper and handed them to Zheng Junwei. âThis is the system weâre currently implementing.â","Zheng Junwei was thoroughly familiar with administrative matters. He only needed to glance through the pages before understanding the general framework.","âCan you give this to us?â he asked.","âItâs for you,â Jiang Cheng replied.","Zheng Junwei was delighted. âThatâs wonderful. We can just copy your homework.â","The structure of a system was one thing. The key was maintaining a balance among all the figures within it.","If the differences in performance between various positions and the price differences among various supplies failed to reach a balance, the entire system would quickly descend into chaos.","Zheng Junwei praised them. âYou clearly have an experienced financial professional on your team.â","Jiang Cheng smiled. âWe do. Someone with a background in finance. Theyâre very good at this sort of thing.â","There was truth in the saying that every profession had its own specialty. But in these chaotic times, being able to identify professionals among a crowd and put them in charge of what they were good atâthat was the ability of a leader.","Being a leader was never easy.","Zheng Junwei understood that.","Jiang Cheng gave him one instruction in particular. âYou must maintain order. Even if it means using force, even if blood has to be shed.â","âYou must protect the elderly, children, and women. If you can protect those three groups, youâll establish the atmosphere of order for the entire community.â","âOtherwise, once the strong begin preying on the weak, it will spread like an infectious disease.â","Zheng Junwei sat with both hands resting on his knees, his posture broad and imposing. His expression grew solemn.","âI understand. Itâs like corruption in a company.â","âIf that happens, what you establish wonât be a government. Itâll be a gang.â","âJiang Cheng, you can rest assured. If weâre willing to step forward, it means we have the right convictions. Donât underestimate us middle-aged men.â","The atmosphere finally lightened, and everyone laughed.","Jiang Cheng took out several more sheets of paper. He looked through them first, then selected a few and handed them to Zheng Junwei.","âThese are for Shilong District.â","They were all pleas for help that Yang Xinyan had compiled and printed.","This was not a transfer of power, but a transfer of responsibilityâa handing over of human lives.","Zheng Junwei accepted the papers solemnly.","The blood of middle-aged men could run hot too.","Yue Chao came upstairs. âJiang Cheng, everythingâs ready downstairs.â","But Jiang Cheng suddenly had another idea.","âYue Chao, can we put this information on television?â","âHuh?â","Jiang Chengâs eyes shone. âWhen I was just handing things over to Brother Zheng, I suddenly realized that there must still be people in different parts of the city who can protect themselves and even have strength to spare. If thatâs the case, letâs broadcast all the pleas for help. We can ask those who have the means to help rescue people too.â","âInstead of relying on our own limited strength to do little more than put out a few cups of water on a blazing fire, we might as well let sparks spread across the entire plain.â","Guangxiu District, No. 14 Middle School.","âTeacher Wang! Teacher Zhang!â A student ran out of the cafeteria and shouted, âThereâs something new on TV!â","âThat Jiang Cheng is on again!â","âHurry up and come over!â","The teachers and students all rushed into the cafeteria.","The content that had been playing on repeat for two days had finally been updated.","Jiang Cheng appeared again.","But this time, many other people appeared on the screen as well.","[The Shilong District Provisional Government has been established.]","[All pleas for help from Shilong District have been handed over.]","âHello, everyone. Iâm Zheng Junwei, formerly the general manager of the XX Division of XXXX Company. Iâm now the person in charge of the new Shilong District Provisional Government.â","The man surnamed Zheng announced a hotline for requesting assistance, as well as the address of a residential compound in Shilong District.","They had occupied the compound and turned it into their base. Anyone could seek refuge there, regardless of which district they came from. Just like the New Technology District, it was open to everyone.","From now on, there were two safe zones people could take refuge in.","The difference was that the Shilong District Provisional Government would handle Shilong Districtâs affairs, relieving the New Technology District Provisional Government of the burden of managing an entire district.","One of the students turned around in surprise. âTeacher Wang, why are you crying?â","Teacher Wang wiped her eyes. âItâs nothing.â","Children of that age might not have been able to understand.","But adults could understand one another.","When the New Technology District Provisional Government announced that the district was secure and open to anyone seeking refuge, parents and teachers did not immediately take the children there.","Doubts still remained in their hearts.","They were afraid that the young peopleâs enthusiasm would fade. Afraid that this was merely the result of personal heroism, and that once the initial excitement wore off, they would be unable to hold on.","But now, one small flame had ignited another.","How could that not bring tears to peopleâs eyes?","Especially when Jiang Cheng spoke again afterward:","[Our strength is limited and faint, but when countless limited and faint strengths come together, they become powerful.]","[Does anyone still remember these words? I didnât say them. They were spoken by Vice Mayor Zheng during a speech at the time of the previous zombie disaster.]","[Vice Mayor Zheng is already gone. We tried to contact the central government and the other governments, but we lost contact with all of them.]","[But it doesnât matter. Weâre still here.]","[Right now, we have only two provisional district governments. Compared with the number of survivors across the entire city, that is nowhere near enough.]","[I call on everyone who can already protect themselves and still has strength to spare to lend a hand to those around them.]","[Every survivor we rescue gives us one more comrade to fight beside us and one more partner with whom we can work.]","[No one can live entirely alone.]","[Please, look around you.]","Before the broadcast, Jiang Cheng had already called Yang Xinyan and asked her to send the electronic versions of the compiled pleas for help to Yue Chaoâs email address.","They had now been edited into captions.","After Jiang Cheng finished speaking, the captions began to scroll slowly across the screen. The pleas for help, categorized by district and street, were displayed for every viewer to see.","Jiang Cheng also emphasized that if a mutated zombie was involved, the person sending the plea for help had to make that clear in the message, so that rescuers could organize an appropriate team.","A student suddenly shouted, âThere are people from Guangxiu District!â","âThat building isnât far from us! I ride past it on my way to school every day!â","âThere are more than a dozen people trapped inside.â","âWhereâs a pen? Quick, write down the floor and the phone number!â","Yesterday, the students had not only successfully taken down Hongâan Market, killed the long-tongued mutated zombie, and rescued the survivors trapped in the nearby vehicle administration bureau.","Those survivors were now staying at No. 14 Middle School as well. Their group had grown.","Over the past two days, both the adults and the children had gone out together. Like ants carrying food back to their nest, they had nearly emptied Hongâan Market.","Conditions at the school had improved, and everyoneâs quality of life was much better than before.","Not a single child had considered seeking shelter in one of the safe zones.","The school was their safe zone.","Not a single child felt that they were people in need of rescue. Instead, they had reached the astonishingly unanimous conclusion that they were people capable of protecting themselvesâwith strength left to spare!","They were people who could go and save others!","Taking it a step further, some students had already begun asking, âTeacher, why canât we establish a provisional government for Guangxiu District? We have quite a lot of people!â","The teachers had only just wiped away their tears when the students hit them with such a soul-searching question.","For a moment, the teachers had no answer.","The adults looked at one another.","âBecauseâ¦â one teacher began, carefully choosing their words. âBecause we still donât know whether anyone from the Guangxiu District government is left.â","âWhat if no oneâs left?â","âIf there were someone, I think they would have come forward and said something by now.â","âExactly, exactly. Thatâs what I thought too.â","âSo if no oneâs left, then we can do it, right?â","The adults were speechless again.","Why couldnât they? No one had said they couldnât. Who had the authority to say they werenât allowed?","A spark was lit in the childrenâs hearts.","Today, besides these reports, the television also showcased the blade car and the crescent shovel, explaining in detail how useful they were.","That was because Jiang Cheng and the others had discovered that the vehicles used by the people from Shilong District merely had their windows covered with metal grilles. They had never thought of an invention like the blade car.","Sometimes, something one person took for granted might be something another person could never have imagined.","Jiang Cheng had become aware of the differences in knowledge between individualsâand even between different groupsâso he had taken the opportunity to introduce both the blade car and the crescent shovel during this broadcast.","Wu Shuchen and several ninth-grade students were practically pressing their faces against the television.","The high school students stared at them in confusion. âWhat are you doing?â","Wu Shuchen hurriedly waved them off. âWait, wait!â","They stared fixedly at the television screen, patiently waiting for the current loop to finish before the broadcast began again.","They waited until the scene changed to show a large group of people, then watched the screen with intense concentration.","Suddenly, the middle school students cried out, âThere! We saw him!â","âItâs him!â","âHeâs still alive!â","The middle school students jumped and cheered, celebrating wildly.","The high school students asked, âWho?â","âSenior Huang Xuetao! We saw Senior Huang Xuetao!â","âHeâs alive!â","The high school students finally remembered. âOh, that guy!â","Many people were already putting on their armor, forming up, and distributing weapons.","No. 14 Middle School was now divided into several teams. Each team included adults, high school students, and middle school students.","The superpowered individuals were distributed as evenly as possible, too.","The cafeteria was filled with bustling activity.","âA shovel! I still donât have a shovel!â","âIâm missing one leg guard! Who took an extra one? I need a small!â","âIâve got a medium! Make do with this for now!â","Armor was strapped on, and weapons were taken up.","âLetâs go! Move out!â","âWhen we have strength to spare, we study!â","âNow that we have strength to spare, we save people!â","âHahahahahaha! I hereby appoint you two as representatives for Chinese class!â"]},{"number":162,"title":"Chapter 162: 0162","paragraphs":["Seven large trucks went out in the morning. By evening, ten large trucks and six smaller vehicles had returned.","They had brought back more than nine hundred survivors and refugees.","Splitting up the teams had indeed boosted their efficiency dramatically.","Several more burners had been added to the earthen stoves in the small square of the Youth Apartment complex. Otherwise, there would not have been enough.","Among the refugees who had already been settled in, many of those without superpowers had signed up to work in the cafeteria. Just peeling potatoes and mashing them required a great many people.","Aside from potatoes, the vegetables they had selected were mainly eggplants, Chinese cabbage, bok choy, cucumbers, radishes, garlic sprouts, and chives. Soybeans and peanuts were reserved for special purposes.","The central greenbelt and all the surrounding greenbelts in the Youth Apartment complex had been reclaimed as vegetable plots.","In the process, quite a few people had gotten red in the face arguing over whether the garlic shoots should be called âgarlic sproutsâ or âgarlic scapes.â Each side insisted that the term from their own hometown was the correct one.","Although they had rescued a large number of people today, with Song Jingshuo in charge at the Youth Apartment complex, everything proceeded in an orderly fashion despite the chaos.","Looking down from one of the higher floors, one would have seen the courtyardsâespecially the small squareâswarming with dark heads. Teams moved back and forth, now heading east, now west.","They looked like diligent little bees.","The refugees were given a meal to keep them alive, and after they had been fed, they were transferred to Xiao Dan at Jixiang Jiayuan.","Today, Xiao Dan had recruited two very capable assistants: an older woman named Wu Yan and a young girl named Tao Xiaoxiao. By the end of the day, Xiao Dan knew she had made the right choice.","The two women were exceptionally good at organizing and keeping things in order. They left her miles behind.","Xiao Dan was quite capable when it came to working alone and handling things independently, but she was not very good at organizing, coordinating, assigning tasks, or making plans within a group.","Those, however, were Wu Yan and Tao Xiaoxiaoâs strengths.","Xiao Dan immediately felt as if a huge weight had been lifted from her shoulders.","Her voice had gone hoarse from exhaustion over the past two days.","After dinner, Jiang Cheng would usually organize a brief work meeting to review the dayâs successes and failures.","Today, Jiang Cheng and Zhou Wang had not yet returned, so Song Jingshuo chaired the meeting.","Everyone summarized the dayâs situation.","Every team said the same thing: âItâs still much easier when we go out with Jiang Cheng.â","Jiang Cheng had a storage space, so all kinds of miscellaneous items and suppliesâincluding food and cooking equipment for lunchâcould be stored with her. It was incredibly convenient.","After the teams split up, each team could only carry its own supplies.","Although there were earth-, fire-, and metal-powered ability users who could work together to prepare meals, all those items took up space in the vehicles and had to be loaded and unloaded repeatedly. And along the way, people could not always resist sneaking a bite here and there.","Besides, this meant they could only bring essential supplies. Anything extra was inconvenient to transport. Jiang Cheng, on the other hand, could keep a little of everything on hand.","Back when everyone had formed one large group, almost all of them had been people from the Youth Apartment complex. Even Aunt Pan counted as one of them. The outsiders were people like Zhou Wang and Little Huang, neighbors from nearby whom they had already worked with and gotten to know during the previous disaster.","The few children who had joined later had also been rescued from schools by the group. They were obedient and did whatever they were told.","Whenever something needed to be done, the people who were good at it would take charge, while everyone else simply followed instructions.","Now that the group had split up, every team included refugees who had only just been recruited. They were unfamiliar with one another, and unlike obedient children, they were all adults.","Although each team leader was a powerful superhuman, having strong abilities did not mean being good at everything else. Once they had to stand on their own, everyoneâs strengths and weaknesses became obvious.","Aunt Pan took the initiative to say, âIâm not very good at this.â","Aunt Pan and Master Luo were both honest, down-to-earth people who were not good with words. They had no children, and back in their hometown, people looked down on them because of it. They could not even win an argument. That was why they had given up their few mu of farmland and gone to the city to work.","The big city was far more accepting. No one mocked or looked down on them for not having children.","But Aunt Pan truly was not good at managing a team or assigning tasks. She would simply keep her head down and do her work honestly.","When she was asked to lead a team on her ownâespecially when someone asked what should be done about one thing or anotherâshe had no idea how to respond.","What Aunt Pan meant was that she did not want to be a team leader anymore. She only wanted to follow the others and kill zombies. Someone else could be the leader; she would obey orders.","But Song Jingshuo did not go along with her request.","Instead, he assigned her a reliable deputy while still allowing Aunt Pan to remain the nominal team leader.","People who were too honest were easily bullied.","When Master Luo had still been around, he had not been good with words either, but he understood people and social situations. Aunt Pan had never suffered because she had always had her husband to shield her.","Now that Master Luo was gone, there was no one to protect Aunt Pan from petty, malicious people.","Of course, Aunt Panâs superpower was extremely formidable, so no one dared bully her openly. But Song Jingshuo understood all too well the little tricks and hidden schemes people could use.","Jiang Cheng and Zhou Wang only returned after the meeting had ended.","The cafeteria had saved them some food and reheated it for them.","Song Jingshuo sat with them while they ate and gave Jiang Cheng a brief report on the dayâs work meeting.","By the time they finished eating, it was already completely dark, and everyone went their separate ways. Zhou Wang, Little Huang, and the people from the television station returned to Jixiang Jiayuan.","Song Jingshuo asked Jiang Cheng, âWhy are you in such a good mood today? Is it because of the Shilong District government?â","Jiang Cheng asked, âWas it that obvious?â","âNot exactly obvious. It was justâ¦ natural,â Song Jingshuo said. âYou really look happy.â","Song Jingshuo admitted that the establishment of a provisional government in Shilong District was indeed something uplifting.","Everyone had visibly perked up after seeing the new live broadcast on television today.","But the happiness showing in Jiang Chengâs eyes and brows seemed somehow different from everyone elseâs. If he had to describe it, she looked a little like a child who had just been given candy.","It was not an emotion one would expect from someone as rational as Jiang Cheng.","âJingshuo, after you became an adult, did you ever try changing yourself?â Jiang Cheng asked in return.","Song Jingshuo raised an eyebrow. âFor example?â","âFor exampleâ¦â Jiang Cheng thought for a moment. âTrying to become a saint?â","Song Jingshuo: ââ¦Are you calling me a social Darwinist?â","Jiang Cheng denied it. âNo. I mean trying to become someone completely different from who you used to be.â","Song Jingshuo pondered for a moment, then said with certainty, âIsnât that still calling me a social Darwinist?â","Jiang Cheng pressed a hand to her forehead.","Song Jingshuoâs phone rang. He answered it. âI know. Iâve finished eating. Iâm coming right over. Iâll go back and get it first. You guys have fun.â","Jiang Cheng asked, âWho was that?â","âGao Yuxuan asked me to go play games.â","Jiang Cheng said, âSee? Isnât that a very good attempt at changing yourself?â","It was true.","Song Jingshuo had never played video games before.","In his mind, a man who was addicted to games was someone who lacked ambition.","Song Jingshuo said, ââ¦Theyâve led me astray.â","Jiang Cheng and Mo Li went home and enjoyed a satisfying hot shower.","Then Jiang Cheng curled up on the sofa with Mo Li in her arms and continued reading.","It really was difficult to change oneâs way of thinking after reaching adulthoodâunless one finally encountered a powerful ideology that saw through the true nature of the world, pointed directly to the truth of society, and clearly showed the way forward.","Why was Jiang Cheng so happy?","Because she had found happiness.","It was no longer merely a matter of killing zombies. One could even say that the zombies had become tools.","She had learned an entirely different way of thinking. She had put it into practice with an experimental attitude, only to become increasingly convinced of its validity as she continued.","The joy of it was indescribable.","The local natives probably couldnât understand it. After all, it was something they had been exposed to since childhood.","Just like in âJiang Chengâsâ memories: the ideas were clearly there, yet they had no sense of presence. Being exposed to something for too long made it formalized and hollow, making it difficult to feel the brilliance within.","But to Jiang Cheng, an outsider from another world, this was without a doubt a way of thinking she had never encountered before.","There was always something fresh and fun about a first experience.","It really was like a child getting candy.","Gao Yuxuanâs family had more than a dozen game consoles. He owned all six of the latest models released that year. Every penny he earned went into buying them.","Gao Yuxuan, Li Jiangbing, and Song Jingshuo had their feet propped up on the coffee table, each holding a controller as they battled furiously.","They were so engrossed that their sheet masks nearly fell off.","Naturally, the sheet mask belonged to Song Jingshuo.","It had started when Gao Yuxuan had gone up to Song Jingshuo and asked him to his face, âYou really use sheet masks?â","Song Jingshuo had fallen silent for a moment before slowly replying, âDo you think theyâre cheap?â","Later, Song Jingshuo had pressed him to reveal who had told him about the sheet masks, but Gao Yuxuan had been loyal to the end and refused to give him up.","Now, all three of them were wearing Song Jingshuoâs supposedly expensive sheet masks. Gao Yuxuan said, âActually, this feels pretty good. Hey, how much does one cost?â","Song Jingshuo calmly named the price.","ââ¦â Gao Yuxuan stared at him. âHoly crap?â","Gao Yuxuan declared, âIâm wearing this for another hour! Iâm even going to sleep with it on!â","Li Jiangbing hurriedly patted the mask flatter. âDamn, thatâs expensive! Just like you. Even the ones girls use arenât this pricey, are they?â","Song Jingshuo said, âTheyâre specially supplied to luxury clubs. Not the kind you can buy at a shopping mall. You have no idea how expensive it is to spend money at that club. Even I canât afford it. The few times I went, I was either tagging along with my boss or entertaining clients on the companyâs dime. I only bought a few sheet masks to use myself.â","Song Jingshuo began promoting them. âThereâs a reason they cost so much. This stuff really is excellent. If I have an important meeting that day, Iâll put one on first thing in the morning before heading out. My complexion looks great afterwardâI look completely refreshed.â","Gao Yuxuan said, âThatâs fine. We donât have meetings that important. I just sneak off to sleep in the back row.â","Li Jiangbing burst out laughing. âHahahahahaha!â","Song Jingshuo asked curiously, âWhereâs Zhao Yi? Why isnât Zhao Yi here?â","Gao Yuxuan had specifically brought four sheet masks so Zhao Yi could try one too, but Zhao Yi hadnât shown up. Werenât he and Gao Yuxuan practically joined at the hip?","Li Jiangbing said, âYou really know how to bring up the sore spot. Heâs been cursing about this all night.â","â...?â","Gao Yuxuan flew into a rage. âYou tell meâdoesnât he deserve to be cursed?â","âThis morning, he came rushing to me in a panic, saying Zhang Lesi wanted to date him. He was scared out of his mind and asked me what he should do.â","âAs his true friend, of course I told him the honest truth!â","â...â Song Jingshuo asked, âWhat did you say?â","Gao Yuxuan said, âI strongly advised him that when looking for a girlfriend, you absolutely mustnât choose a tigress like that! Otherwise, sheâll control everything you do. What fun would life be?â","âHe even nodded and said I had a point!â","âAnd then?â","âAfter dinner, I went looking for him everywhere. And what do I see? He was walking around the courtyard hand in hand with Zhang Lesi!â","Who could understand the pain of being torn apart from oneâs inseparable best friend?","And this kind of betrayal was even more infuriating!","Gao Yuxuan was practically turning into an angry little bird!","Li Jiangbing said, âYour sheet maskâs wrinkled! Itâs all crumpled up!â","Gao Yuxuan hurriedly patted the ridiculously expensive mask flat again.","It was far too expensive. Wasting even a single drop of essence was heartbreaking."]},{"number":163,"title":"Chapter 163: 0163","paragraphs":["âWhen someone asks you, âAm I pretty?â they want to hear you praise them. The only correct answer is yes, youâre pretty.â","âWhen someone tells you that someone confessed to them and they donât know what to do, theyâre rubbing their romance in your face. The only correct response is to immediately express your envy, jealousy, and resentment so they can feel satisfied.â","âAs for how you really feel or what you really think, that doesnât matter,â Song Jingshuo patiently explained. âPeople have eyes and mirrors. They know perfectly well whether theyâre pretty or not. And when someone confesses to them, no one knows better than they do whether they like that person or have feelings for them.â","âEveryone comes with a clear purpose. Theyâre expecting you to say what they want to hear. No one wants to hear the truth.â","Gao Yuxuan suddenly understood. âNo wonder girls were always hitting me!â","It had taken him all these years.","He had finally solved one of lifeâs great mysteries.","Li Jiangbing was laughing so hard he was shaking.","âDonât laugh.â Embarrassed and furious, Gao Yuxuan turned his fire on Li Jiangbing. âYouâre not any better than me. You keep playing dumb in front of Su Yu. What, are you waiting for Su Yu to confess to you first? Iâm telling you, Su Yu isnât Zhang Lesi.â","Li Jiangbing immediately stopped laughing. âDonât talk nonsense. Donât go spreading rumors about a girl. Doesnât that little girl have a reputation to protect?â","Gao Yuxuan refused to back down. âHow am I spreading rumors? Everyone has eyes.â","You couldnât hide who you favored.","You saved her the best seat in the car.","You helped her carry anything heavy.","Whenever something good came along or things were being handed out, she was the first person you thought of.","As long as it was within your power, you did whatever you could to make things easier for her.","Some things didnât need to be said aloud. They showed in your actions.","The clearest sign was giving up benefits and power for someone else.","Yet precisely when Su Yu tried to show her feelings, he pretended not to notice, leaving her completely at a loss.","Even Song Jingshuo encouraged Li Jiangbing. âYou said it yourselfâSu Yu isnât like Zhang Lesi. A girl like her will never take the first step. You have to pursue her.â","Li Jiangbing stared at the television screen. âPursue her? You want me, a technical-school graduate, to pursue a woman with a masterâs degree? Even if you gave me ten times the courage, I couldnât do it. This relationship is impossible from the very beginning.â","The room suddenly fell silent for a moment. The only sounds were the little characters on the television firing bang bang bang and the villain shrieking in agony.","Song Jingshuo and Gao Yuxuan both froze for a beat.","They fought zombies every day and saw the same familiar faces every day. They had actually forgotten that, in normal society, they were allâ¦ very different from one another.","Gao Yuxuan pursed his lips, desperately trying to think of something to smooth things over. But no excuse came to him, so he could only look to Song Jingshuo for help.","Song Jingshuo said, âWhat use are degrees and money now?â","Exactly! It was still Old Song who knew what to say!","Gao Yuxuan quickly chimed in. âThatâs right! Who cares about that anymore? If you ask meââ","âDonât say anything. Just shut up,â Li Jiangbing said irritably.","âBy your logic, that makes it even more impossible.â","âIn a normal, peaceful time, someone like her would never have fallen for someone like me. So why does she like me now? Because things arenât peaceful.â","âFor her, this is a wealthy heiress fallen on hard times.â","âFor me, itâs taking advantage of someoneâs misfortune.â","âIf I did something like that, my mother would beat me to death.â","âBullshit.â","Li Jiangbingâs face was covered with a sheet mask. He kept his eyes on the television and refused to look at them.","Song Jingshuo and Gao Yuxuan couldnât see what expression he was making.","Mr. Xu returned humming a little tune, a bag slung over his shoulder.","When he saw the employees, he handed over the bag. âHere. Take these and eat.â","Everyone cheered.","There were potato chips, chocolate, and drinks. They poured the two bottles of drinks into cups and divided them among themselves, each person getting only a sip.","But even that was satisfying.","Some of the other employees who had joined the teams had brought things back as well. Seeing Mr. Xu contribute everything he had brought, they took out their own goods and shared them too.","Wu Yan and Tao Xiaoxiao even brought out several enormous grapes, each one as big as an orange.","There were no grapes at Youth Apartment. They were a special feature of Auspicious Home. A resident on the first floor with a private courtyard had grown them there, with the help of Xue and Qian, the two wood-element ability users, who had accelerated their growth.","They could be forced to ripen and picked on the spot. The ones left unpicked still hung from the vines as tiny green beads and werenât ready to eat yet. Even if someone wanted to steal them, there would be nothing to steal.","For now, they were an exclusive benefit of Auspicious Home, available only to original resident homeowners.","Sister Wu and Xiaoxiao held management positions, so their current benefits were equivalent to those of Auspicious Home homeowners.","Mr. Xu summed it up. âSee? I told you not to become marginal members. Either go out on the front line or join management.â","Being on a team meant more than just earning a lot of performance points. There were all kinds of unseen benefits when they went outside as well. Anything collected collectively was managed and distributed as a group, but anything you scavenged yourself belonged to you. That was why everyone went out carrying two shoulder bagsâthey wanted to bring back as much as possible.","Mr. Xu hadnât prepared anything on his first day and had been dragged along with the others, so he had picked up a bag on-site.","âEveryoneâs had something to eat. Come on, letâs have a meeting.â Mr. Xu clapped his hands.","It was much like the work meetings at Youth Apartment. Everyone talked about which position they had taken, what they had done, whether it was tiring, how many performance points they had earned, whether there were any benefits, and so on.","Director Yu said, âThe management here is pretty good, especially at Youth Apartment. I had time to talk with that Song Jingshuo today. Guess what company he used to work for? Shengda! He was the one who came up with the performance-point system.â","Shengda was a leading company in the financial industry. Anyone who could get into Shengda was an outstanding talent.","Mr. Xu suddenly understood. âNo wonder.â","After some discussion, Mr. Xu said, âFirst of all, I think that although the temporary district government in the Technology New District is young, itâs heading in the right direction in every respect. It has room for continued development. We should settle down here for the long term.â","There wasnât anywhere else they could go anyway.","âSecond, we canât split up. The company may be gone, but the more unfamiliar our surroundings become, the more important it is for us to stick together. No one can survive alone.â","Everyone nodded. In fact, several people even breathed sighs of relief.","What everyone was truly worried about was that Mr. Xu and Director Yu, as ability users, might abandon them.","There was already an indistinct line forming between ability users and ordinary people. The youthful, close-knit atmosphere at Youth Apartment had merely kept that line from becoming too obvious.","But no one in Mr. Xuâs company was stupid. They were all vaguely aware of it.","In the end, they reached a unanimous agreement.","The company might never return, but from now on, they were a familyâa single household.","Everyone had to contribute to this âfamilyâ and do their part. Aside from the two people permanently assigned to cooking because they were good at it, everyone else should take positions and earn performance points whenever possible.","The cooks would be paid out of the groupâs collective performance points.","Since Mr. Xu and Director Yu were ability users, and Big Sister Wu Yan and Little Sister Xiaoxiao had entered management and earned more than everyone else, those four would be exempt from household chores.","Everyone else would take turns handling chores such as cleaning.","A small group that was reasonably stable and united had taken shape.","In the future, as the number of refugees grew, more and more groups like this would emerge, brought together by blood, affection, or shared interests.","Just as Jiang Cheng had said:","No one could survive alone.","It took the Youth Apartment two days to get the large-scale cultivation plans sorted out, and Auntie Xue and Auntie Qian were finally able to relax and catch their breath.","When Auntie Xue saw that Song Jingshuo had cultivated several kinds of fruit seedlings but no grapes, she brought him a section of vine on the morning of September 7, complete with leaves and a cluster of unripe grapes.","âTake it home and plant it.â","Song Jingshuo thanked Auntie Xue and took the cutting home, planning to grow it in a pot first.","The people in the residential compound had helped him collect a great many flowerpots and foam boxes. His home was now packed with seedlings.","Only some of them had been selected for large-scale cultivation. Many others were simply being raised for now, to be dealt with if the need arose.","The agricultural researcher Zeng Qiang specialized in fertilizers.","Zeng Qiang complained that Song Jingshuoâs wood-type superpower had made his entire field useless.","For example, if fertilizer had not finished fermenting, it would normally scorch the roots and kill the plant. But with the support of a wood-type superpower, the plant would not die. It could forcibly absorb the nutrients and continue growing.","If that was the case, what did they need a scientific researcher specializing in fertilizer for?","Still, complaints were only complaints. Zeng Qiang continued to carefully prepare excellent potting soil for Song Jingshuoâs seedlings using whatever materials they could find.","With proper potting soil, Song Jingshuo no longer had to check the seedlings several times a day. He could simply leave them at home, and they would grow naturally without needing his attention.","They only had to grow strong and healthy by the time humanity needed them.","When Song Jingshuo received the grape cutting, he asked Zeng Qiang, âWhat kind of fertilizer should I use?â","âDuring the seedling stage, nitrogen fertilizer is the priority. Go back and look around. I remember there should still be some left.â","Song Jingshuo returned to his house and searched around. There were still several boxes of soil he had not used. After rummaging through them, he found a foam box marked âNitrogenâ in permanent marker. He poked a hole in the soil with his finger and planted the cutting inside.","There was no technique to it whatsoever.","No pruning, no angled cuts, no consideration of temperature or moistureânone of it.","He simply stuck it into the soil. Then he activated his superpower, and roots immediately sprouted, anchoring themselves firmly in the earth.","It would have been enough to make any agricultural researcher green with envy.","A tiny cluster of green grapes was still hanging from the vine. Song Jingshuo casually accelerated their growth, wanting to taste them.","Even he was beginning to get tired of eating strawberries. It was time for a change.","The little green grapes grew visibly larger.","Naturally, Song Jingshuo controlled the process so that only the grapes matured, preventing the vine itself from shooting upward.","But as he fed the vine his superpower, he sensed its powerful urge to spread.","It wanted to grow larger, to grow longer, to become thick and sturdy, to wind itself around something.","This was the first time Song Jingshuo had accelerated the growth of a climbing plant, and the experience was indeed fascinating.","The other vegetables were all focused on growing leaves and trying to flower.","A thought suddenly flashed through Song Jingshuoâs mind: What would happen if he used his superpower to accelerate the vine itself instead of the fruit?","Once the idea occurred to him, he could not resist trying it.","Song Jingshuo used his superpower to its absolute limit every day. When he grew tired, he rested; once he had recovered, he started again. From morning until night, with no days off.","But since his superpower, like Li Jiangbingâs, was noncombat-oriented, few people paid attention to just how powerful it really was.","Only Auntie Qian had remarked beside him the day before, âYou make things grow so fast. Itâs good to be young.â","Song Jingshuoâs thoughts shifted, and a surging tide of superpower rushed into the vineâs veins.","The vine instantly shot upward toward the ceiling!","It stopped there, needing no support. It tangled around itself, twisting into something like a pillar wedged between the foam box and the ceiling.","Proud. Forceful.","Completely different from those little green vegetables sprawled across the ground.","Song Jingshuo squatted on the floor with one hand braced against his knee.","He stared upward for a long while before finally reaching out to touch the vineâ¦"]},{"number":164,"title":"Chapter 164: 0164","paragraphs":["That evening, after the team returned with the survivors they had rescued, they held a work meeting at the clubhouse after dinner.","While the others were speaking, Jiang Cheng noticed that Song Jingshuo kept reaching for his left wrist with his right hand. He was wearing something there.","He used to wear his name-brand watch on that wrist. Now, what he wore looked like a wooden bracelet.","Jiang Cheng narrowed her eyes and studied it more closely. It wasnât wood. It was vine.","Several slender vines were twined together in a circle, resembling a bracelet. There was even a tiny green leaf attached.","The leaf was so small that she wouldnât have noticed it without looking carefully. She only spotted it when Song Jingshuo unscrewed his water bottle and secretly poured some water over his wrist.","So it was alive.","Jiang Cheng knew it definitely wasnât a âbracelet.â","The opening was too small, hugging his skin almost completely. It couldnât have been âput on.â","â¦It must have grown directly onto him.","Song Jingshuo wore a watch because it was a symbol of a successful man. But he wasnât the kind of man who wore jewelry.","What sort of thing, and for what reason, would someone need to keep wearing on his wrist?","Jiang Cheng narrowed her eyes.","She knew Song Jingshuo too well. He would never do anything unnecessary or useless.","When she looked up, her eyes met Song Jingshuoâs.","Clearly, Song Jingshuo had noticed her scrutiny. He raised his left hand to his chest, rotated his wrist, and crooked the corner of his mouth at her.","Jiang Cheng raised an eyebrow.","Song Jingshuo immediately knew that she had guessed most of the truth.","Splitting the team into separate units and having them operate independently had greatly improved efficiency. After two days, the various unit leaders and their membersâespecially the newly recruited onesâhad mostly worked out their differences and settled into a rhythm.","Jiang Cheng decided, âTomorrow, Iâll lead a team to clear out Renxin Hospital.â","She had been considering the matter of Renxin Hospital for several days.","Now that their population was growing, Zhang Lesi no longer went out with the team. Instead, she stayed at home and âsaw patients.â","Her diagnostic ability had made her a âmiracle doctor,â but her healing ability could only treat external injuries. It was useless against illnesses.","Fortunately, the people who had been found to be sick over the past few days only needed to take medicine.","But sooner or laterâthat much was certainâamong so many residents, there would be people who needed surgery. They would need anesthesia, medical instruments, a sterile environment, and so on.","They had to prepare in advance. They couldnât wait until the need arose before taking action. By then, it would be too late.","The next dayâs assignments had all been distributed. The meeting was adjourned.","Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo left separately. Neither asked about the vine ring on the otherâs wrist, and neither brought it up.","Instead, Li Jiangbing caught up with Song Jingshuo and threw an arm around his neck. âWhat was all that meaningful eye contact between you and Jiang Cheng just now?â","There was no way they could leave him out of anything.","Song Jingshuo pried his thick arm away. âCome on. Iâll show you something.â","The two of them found a secluded corner of the neighborhood, and Song Jingshuo showed it to him.","Li Jiangbingâs mouth hung open for a long while before he finally closed it, utterly speechless. âEven you tooâ¦ Jiang Cheng has Mo Li tooâ¦ Why am I the only oneâ¦â","Heaven was so unfair. Of all people, he should have become the main combat force. How had he ended up with a water-based ability?","He asked Song Jingshuo, âSo, are you going to join the team?â","âNo.â Song Jingshuo hadnât even considered it.","The days when they needed to rely on combat strength to establish authority within the group during the first disaster had long since passed.","Their organizational structure was already in place.","The team had more than enough members, and they were recruiting more every day. New refugees were admitted daily. They were given one day to adjust, and on the third day, they had to come out and work. They didnât lack one more fighter.","Everyone only needed to find their own place.","Song Jingshuo was now widely recognized as the second-in-command of the temporary government in the Development Zone, as well as the person in charge of all resource management.","Everyone knew that his superpower had no offensive capability, yet no one failed to follow his arrangements and instructionsânot even those powerful ability users.","All of this had come about under Jiang Chengâs leadership and through everyoneâs joint efforts: they had established a miniature society governed by order.","When order existed, there was no need to suppress others through force.","Of course, that order had nearly been destroyed by Cao Jiacai. At the time, everyoneâs abilities were still undeveloped and had not reached their current level. Cao Jiacaiâs combat strength had been on an entirely different tier.","But Jiang Cheng held the greatest trump card, the most terrifying killing move.","If Cao Jiacai hadnât stepped forward, Jiang Cheng might never have released Mo Li. Or perhaps Jiang Cheng had been waiting all along for Cao Jiacai to make his move, giving her an excuse to bring Mo Li into the open.","In any case, if they insisted on discussing combat strength, Mo Li was more than merely in a class of its own. Mo Li existed on an entirely different levelâand was absolutely loyal to Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng possessed the greatest force. She had no desire to become queen or ruler.","What Jiang Cheng wanted was order.","That was everyoneâs good fortune.","On the morning of September 8, Jiang Cheng led her people in seizing and clearing Renxin Hospital.","A group from Changxing District contacted Jiang Cheng.","âWeâve established the Changxing District temporary government.â","Once again, this confirmed that the government had been deliberately wiped out.","Jiang Cheng had been certain of it for some time.","If there were still anyone left in the government, there was no way there wouldnât have been even a single announcement by now.","If there were still anyone left in the government, they should have mobilized the military. No matter how many soldiers were still alive, they would have been stronger than ordinary civilians.","Li Fengâs phone could no longer be reached.","Jiang Cheng guessed that he was dead.","Even if he was still alive, it would be very difficult to contact him.","The Eastern Military District was not in S City. In fact, it was closer to N City and J City than to S City, not to mention the various counties and towns scattered between them.","It was only because S City was so important that, the last time around, they had abandoned the surrounding cities, sacrificed the smaller counties and villages, and diverted their main manpower and supplies to S City first.","Jiang Cheng would not spend even a second dwelling on missing Li Feng. In truth, she did not miss him.","He was merely a partner she had worked with briefly.","Every single one of her companions in the Youth Apartments was closer to her and more important than he was.","That afternoon, Jiang Cheng met with the people from Changxing District at the television station. They broadcast a live announcement declaring the establishment of the Changxing District temporary government and updated the subtitle message that had been playing on a loop.","Thinking of broadcasting all the rescue messages on television on September 6 had truly been an inspired strategy.","Just yesterday alone, they had received countless text messages saying things like, âWeâve rescued the people trapped in such-and-such building.â","One after another.","Yang Xinyan entered the new information into the system while crying.","When asked why she was crying, she said she didnât know either.","The updated information meant that those capable of rescuing people would not waste time rushing to places that had already been cleared.","Yue Chao and several other television station employees had also created an electronic map. They marked the safe zones in Shilong District, Changxing District, and the Technology New District in green.","Compared with the Technology New District, the strongholds in Shilong District and Changxing District looked like tiny green beans.","The entire residential area of the Technology New District was a green safe zone.","They also consolidated messages from the text alerts, such as, âWeâve cleared out such-and-such building. There are no more zombies,â and, âWeâre using such-and-such shopping mall as our base. Any survivors nearby can come here for shelter.â","The messages were broadcast as subtitles while the locations were marked on the map.","Green dots, scattered here and there.","Like sparks from a prairie fire.","The half-grown boy scouts from No. 14 Middle School became anxious when they saw the new broadcast.","Because when they went out to rescue others that morning, they ran into another group that had come to help as well. Both sides were there to rescue the same people.","Although the two groups cooperated happily and bravely, there was still one problemâ¦","âIf we donât establish the Guangxiu District government soon, someone else will beat us to it!â","âThatâs right! We have more people. Those others only had a few dozen today. Since we have more people, we should be the ones to form the government!â","The students were frantic with worry, afraid that someone else would establish the district government before them.","Their minds were filled with just one thought: âWe have to be the government!â","They put their heads together and studied how they could establish a government.","First, they had to confirm that everyone in the district government was really dead. After that, the people could establish a new government on their own.","âWhere exactly is the Guangxiu District government?â","âI know! On Huairou Road!â","âAnd whereâs Huairou Road?â","Even middle school students born and raised in the city did not really know the different districts all that well.","Many of them were only familiar with the route from home to school, along with the commercial areas they occasionally visited with their classmates.","Once they left their own neighborhoods, they were completely lost in the vast city.","Fortunately, they had a map.","After confirming the location, they had to deal with the problem of transportation.","âHow are we going to get there?â","To wipe out the zombies inside a district government building, they would have to send out a large force. They couldnât possibly walk there.","It was a little far.","âTeacher Zhang, you can drive, right?â","Everyone hoped that Teacher Zhang would go out onto the streets, find a public bus, and bring it back for them to use as transportation.","Look at the people in the Technology New District. Their incredibly cool âBlade Vehicleâ was a public bus too. You could even see the route number on it: Route 535.","But Teacher Zhang firmly refused.","âNo.â","âYouâre all still minors. Weâve already discussed this. Weâre going to stay here and focus on ensuring your safety and taking care of your daily needs.â","âEstablishing a government isnât something children should be worrying about. Stop daydreaming and let the adults handle it. In a district as large as Guangxiu, there are bound to be capable people who will step forward.â","But we are the capable people! Why couldnât the teacher understand that?","The âweâ Teacher Zhang referred to included not only the teachers, but also several parents.","In other words, the adults had discussed it among themselves and completely rejected the studentsâ idea.","The middle schoolers were terribly discouraged.","It felt like getting an excellent score of ninety-eight out of a hundred, proudly showing it to your parents, only to be scolded for losing two points and told to reflect on your mistakes.","As the âadultsâ of No. 14 Middle School, the teachers and parents were now so busy looking after the refugees they had rescued that they barely had time to breathe.","They thought that their firm rejection had put an end to the matter.","But they had forgotten that children of this age were at their most rebellious.","That night, the cafeteria was still lit.","Teacher Zhang went over to take a look and found many students kneading dough.","During this period, everyone had to take turns helping out in the cafeteria. Many of the students had learned to cook, and they had even learned how to steam mantou.","âWhat are you doing?â the teacher asked.","One quick-witted, silver-tongued student immediately replied, âThere are too many refugees. Weâre making some mantou for them.â","âOh.â Teacher Zhang was a little touched.","Their idea was wildly impractical, but they really were good kids.","The teacher reminded them, âDonât stay up too late. Go to bed early.â","The students agreed.","But Teacher Zhang had forgotten that when children this age set their minds on doing something, there was no stopping them.","The next morning, the teachers and parents woke to discover that the school was strangely quiet.","Only the cafeteria staff were in the dining hall. Confused, they said, âAre they all still asleep? Why hasnât anyone come for breakfast?â","Teacher Zhang realized something was wrong and ran to the classrooms where the students slept.","They were empty.","A parent came running over. âI checked. A huge number of bicycles are missing from the bike shed! Those little rascals!â","Some of those little rascals were their own children too. Their wings had grown strong enough to fly.","The autumn morning wind was already a little chilly.","The road was filled with sneezes, but there was even more laughter.","And the crisp ringing of bicycle bells.","No cars? Then they would use bicycles.","They built metal cages, each one enclosing seven or eight bicycles, all linked together.","Students who couldnât ride sat on the connecting bars between several of the bicycles.","The outside of the metal cages was modeled after the âBlade Vehicle,â covered with blades arranged all around them like skirts.","But bicycles werenât fast enough to produce the Blade Vehicleâs effect of instantly slicing off a zombieâs head.","That didnât stump the children.","Their young minds quickly came up with a solution: they could adjust the blades and make the blades shoot out on their own to kill the zombies.","The people in the Technology New District had evolved from âBlade Carsâ to âBlade Vehicles.â","The students couldnât successfully imitate the âBlade Vehicle,â so they explored on their own and came up with a âBlade Car.â","They cut down zombies all along the way.","As luck would have it, Guangxiu District was in the north, making it the closest of the cityâs eight districts to the Technology New District, which lay on the outskirts.","That meant every time the Technology New Districtâs convoy entered the city, it had to pass through Guangxiu District.","Over the past two days, the convoy had repeatedly expanded, adding more vehicles. Each unit took a different route.","They entered the city in the morning and left in the evening. With every trip in and out, they slaughtered large numbers of wandering zombies on the streets.","The students saw countless headless zombies and severed heads rolling everywhere.","âUgh, it stinks!â","âSo gross!â","It might have smelled awful, but the breeze brushing against their faces as the teenagers raced toward their goals and ideals was cool and gentle beyond words.","A journey taken in youth was better than any luxury or budget trip.","When young people wanted to do something, they simply went out and did it.","Wait until they grew up, and it would be too late!"]},{"number":165,"title":"Chapter 165: 0165","paragraphs":["Jiang Cheng had never imagined that even she could run into something so baffling.","Some of the distress messages they received contained reports of mutated zombies. Those mutated zombies now fell under Jiang Chengâs jurisdiction.","Because of the special nature of their abilities, Zhou Wang, Little Huang, and Brother Dong had joined Jiang Chengâs team to deal with the mutated zombies.","They had taken down one that morning, then hurried to another location at noon to deal with a second. They had just finished in the afternoon when Yang Xinyan called to say that someone in Guangxiu District had established a provisional government and wanted to get in touch with them.","Jiang Cheng called the number back.","The person who answered had a rather deep male voice. Though he sounded rushed and not particularly steady, there was no telling his age from his voice alone.","Jiang Cheng arranged to meet them at the television station later. From the other end of the call came bursts of cheering.","There were both male and female voices, mixed with the childish voices of young children.","After hanging up, Jiang Cheng frowned.","âWhatâs wrong?â Zhou Wang asked.","âThey seem to have children with them,â Jiang Cheng said.","âWhy would they bring children along?â","That was exactly what had made Jiang Cheng frown.","If they didnât even have a safe base where children could stay, what were they planning to use as the foundation for a government? The responsibilities a government had to take on couldnât be handled with empty words.","âWeâll see what theyâre like first,â she said.","Under normal circumstances, the trip took an hour and a half. Now, with no traffic and no need to obey traffic lights, they could usually get there in twenty or thirty minutes.","When they arrived, the others still hadnât shown up.","Jiang Cheng and the other core members waited on the first floor of the television station. The driver took the vehicle around the nearby area. They had been to the station several times, and every time they came, they drove back and forth along the surrounding streets to clear out the zombies.","By now, if anyone wanted to see a zombie near the television station, they would have to go at least four streets away.","Half an hour passed. The vehicle returned, but the others still hadnât appeared.","Jiang Cheng called them. âWhere are you?â","The only thing she could hear through the phone was the howling wind. The man shouted, âI have no idea where this is! Where are we? Liu Gang, go take a look at that road sign!â","He was shouting at the top of his lungs.","Jiang Cheng: ââ¦â","âOh, it says Zuoliang South Road. Do you know where that is?â","Jiang Cheng: ââ¦â","This was getting harder and harder to describe.","âYouâve only just gotten there?â Jiang Cheng asked. âAt this rate, itâll take you at least another half hour.â","âRight, right, that sounds about right. Wait for us, okay? Weâll definitely make it!â","That last sentence sounded more like he was trying to encourage himself.","After hanging up, Jiang Cheng told everyone, âThereâs a problem.â","They all had a very, very unreliable feeling about this.","Everyone had heard it too. They exchanged looks.","While they waited, they cleared several floors of zombies from a building next door.","They didnât go any higher. It would look bad if the others arrived and found no one there. After clearing a few floors, they came back down and returned to the entrance of the television station to wait.","Fortunately, Jiang Cheng carried a great deal of supplies with her. She took out drinks and handed them around.","The sun was shining down, and they were drinking cold beverages. It was an unexpectedly rare moment of leisure.","More than ten minutes later than expected, the other group finally appeared.","From far away, their main force could be seen emerging onto the road.","A bizarre metal cage covered a bizarre multi-person vehicle powered by foot.","There were quite a few people, and the whole thing was made of metal. Rolling toward them, it even created the illusion of an iron cavalry charging forward.","That was, until they huffed and puffed their way to the entrance of the television station.","Everyone: ââ¦â","They had really worn the students out.","That metal cage was no lightweight. They had set out early that morning and pedaled all the way to the Huairou Road district government office.","They had spent the entire morning killing zombies, which had drained a tremendous amount of their strength.","At noon, they drank tap water and gnawed on toasted mantou.","They found some ham sausages, biscuits, chocolate, and other food in the district government offices. The first zombie disaster had practically given everyone a hoarding disorder. This time, many people had managed to survive in office buildings by relying on all sorts of instant noodles, cookies, chocolate, biscuits, and even compressed biscuits that people had kept in their workplaces.","Then they went on a frantic search for phones.","The children didnât have phones, so they picked up a huge pile at the district government office. Now everyone had one.","Nobody wanted the black or silver-gray high-end business phones. Everyone scrambled for the ones with bright, attractive, or stylish cases.","Phones with cameras and music functions were especially popular.","Some even had to be assigned through rock-paper-scissors or odd-or-even hand games.","Then they cycled from the Guangxiu District government office to the television station.","Guangxiu District was way up north! Only after looking at a map did they realize that the television station was over by the West Second Ring Road!","A car could maintain its speed, or even floor the accelerator and race along. A bicycle carrying a huge metal cage, however, could only get slower and slower.","After all, human stamina was limited, and by the end of the day, they had nearly exhausted theirs.","The fire- and metal-type ability users were especially listless.","They had also needed to kill zombies along the way.","The electric-type ability users were doing somewhat better. But because the metal cage conducted electricity, they were afraid of accidentally electrocuting their classmates, so they hadnât dared use their abilities on the road.","In short, by the time they reached the television station on the West Second Ring Road while pedaling that metal cage, the students were utterly spent.","Little Huang could hardly believe his eyes.","It wasnât until the group of strange geniuses âopenedâ the metal cage and emerged one after another, looking utterly exhausted, that he was finally able to confirm it.","âNumber Fourteen Middle School?!â","The students had actually brought back plenty of clothes from Hongâan Market, but for the sake of looking impressive when they acted as a group, they all wore their school uniforms whenever they went out.","They looked incredibly neat and their spirits were lifted.","A short boy who looked like an elementary school student rushed forward.","âSenior Huang Xuetao!â","Several others ran over after him.","âHuang Xuetao!â","They threw their arms around Little Huang, laughing and crying at the same time.","Little Huang had lost his father on the very first day of the first zombie disaster. After that, everyone had instinctively treated him as an adult.","They had been doing so for so long that they had grown used to it.","Only now, seeing Little Huang embrace a whole crowd of children of every size, tears of excitement in his eyes, did everyone suddenly realizeâ","He was still just a kid.","And there werenât just one or two children.","They were all children.","Older boys whose voices had already changed, and younger ones whose voices had not.","The smallest few looked practically like elementary school students.","Jiang Cheng: ââ¦â","Everyone fell silent.","Jiang Cheng stepped forward and asked, hands clasped behind her back, after scanning the crowd, âAre you the ones who want to establish the Guangxiu District provisional government?â","The students all knew her.","Whenever this auntie appeared on television, she wore silver armor and carried a crescent-shaped shovel. When she spoke, her eyes seemed to pierce through the television screen and stare directly at every single person.","The students thought she was incredibly cool and had all been looking forward to meeting her in person.","But only after facing her for real did they understand how much pressure she could bring to bear.","Her pitch-black eyes swept over them, and none of them dared meet her gaze.","Leader.","The concept surfaced naturally in everyoneâs mind.","So this was what someone had to be like to lead other people.","âAh, yes, yes. Thatâs us,â said a tall, burly boy, stammering.","A thick layer of black fuzz covered his upper lip.","The others, meanwhile, were all staring at the drink cans in the adultsâ hands or lying on the ground nearby, secretly swallowing.","They had carried a huge metal cage and ridden bicycles for an hour. They had drunk all their water, and their throats were parched!","Jiang Cheng nodded without immediately pressing for more details. In a gentle voice, she said, âIt must have been exhausting riding all this way. Have something to drink first.â","She pointed, and everyone quickly moved aside. In the middle of the plaza outside the television station was an inflatable swimming poolâbrightly colored and printed with cartoon designs.","Large chunks of ice floated inside, drifting slowly with the current. Even more drinks were bobbing along with the ice.","The people from the Youth Apartments had practically cleared out Mai Duoduo.","They had hauled away large quantities of freezers, including commercial ice-making machines. The fish in the aquatic section had been scooped out first, and the tanks, water and all, had been stored in Jiang Chengâs space. The purifiers and water-circulation oxygenators had been transferred to the Youth Apartments as well.","Basically, anything that might be useful had been carried away. Take it all, take it all.","There were now people specifically assigned to raise the fish.","When they had left that morning, they had loaded the tanks with huge blocks of ice.","Jiang Chengâs space could not prevent heat from escaping, but it lost heat more slowly than an ordinary space would. Even now, there were still plenty of large ice chunks in the water, glittering beneath the sunlight.","The sight left the students, whose throats felt ready to burst into flames, staring wide-eyed.","They were led over to collect drinks. Though everyone was desperately thirsty, they still lined up properly. Once they received their drinks, they passed them to the people behind them first.","The boys gave theirs to the girls, and the older students gave theirs to the younger ones.","Those who received drinks said thank you.","They were polite and orderly.","The adults took it all in, realizing that these were good kids.","After all, they were all top students from a prestigious secondary school. Not only did the school have strict discipline and an excellent atmosphere, but its students had already been selected from among countless others.","Only after the children had gulped down their ice-cold drinks and seemed to come back to life did Jiang Cheng turn to the student leader and ask, âDo you have a safe base?â","âYes. Weâre staying at the school.â","âDo you have food?â","âYes. We cleared out a nearby produce market.â","âDo you have anyone with wood-based abilities who can provide a steady supply of food?â","ââ¦Ah, no.â","âHow have you arranged the management of your supplies? How do you prevent warehouse managers from abusing their positions? How do you deal with theft and embezzlement?â","âAh?â","âHow do you coordinate the distribution of supplies between refugees and the local residents? How do you determine the ratio of supplies allocated to combat personnel and noncombatants?â","âAh?â","âHow do you encourage and attract refugees to participate in collective action and labor? What are you offering them as compensation?â","âAh? No, weâ¦ They just stay thereâ¦ Weâre the ones doing all the workâ¦â","It was not surprising in the least.","Jiang Cheng nodded and asked, âSo, do you still want to be this provisional government?â","The students fell silent.","In truth, many of them had already begun to lose heart halfway through the bike ride.","What was stranger was that back at school, when they faced a few teachers and parentsâand even the survivors they had rescuedâthey had never felt like children. Instead, they had thought, Weâre amazing.","But once they arrived at the television station and stood face-to-face with Jiang Cheng, the feeling that she was an adult and they were children became overwhelmingly strong.","The grand, surging confidence they had possessed that morning had mostly faded by afternoon.","No one said a word.","Jiang Cheng began by offering them some encouragement. âEverything youâve done up to this point is astonishing. Youâve already taken on far more than anyone your age should have to.â","Praise finally allowed the students to straighten their backs a little, and their morale recovered somewhat.","âBut the responsibilities a government has to shoulder are enormous, and there are far too many problems it has to face.â Jiang Cheng began to turn the conversation in another direction.","By this point, the students no longer felt especially disappointed. After everything they had gone through that day, by the time they reached the television station, they had already begun reassessing themselves.","âAre there no adults at the school?â Jiang Cheng asked. âRefugees donât count.â","âThere are. Three teachers and nine parents.â","Jiang Cheng hit the nail on the head. âYou came out without permission, didnât you? The adults disagreed with you, didnât they?â","The students looked up at the sky, down at the ground, scratched their heads, and cleared their throats.","Jiang Cheng smiled.","They really were still children. They had not truly been tempered by society. Even if they were adults by age, their minds were still those of children.","Jiang Cheng extended an olive branch. âCome back to the High-Tech New District with us.â","But the children exchanged glances, communicated their decision without words, and still refused.","âWe still want to stay in Guangxiu District. We may not be able to run a government, but our school is large, and there are lots of empty classrooms. We have plenty of clothes and quilts, and we can shelter many people.â","âWeâll do our best to rescue them.â","âAuntie Jiang, is that okay?â"]},{"number":166,"title":"Chapter 166: 0166","paragraphs":["Those pairs of eyes had not lost their brightness in the face of disappointment.","Although they still lacked the ability to shoulder the responsibilities of government, they were still wonderful, werenât they, adults?","They were truly a pleasure to watch.","Jiang Cheng couldnât help smiling.","Technology New District, Youth Apartments.","Someone called out to everyone, âJiang Cheng is livestreaming!â","Everyone stopped what they were doing and hurried to the common room to watch.","âWhich district has established a government this time?â","Every day brought something new to get excited about.","âSounds like Guangxiu District. I heard Xinyan mention it at lunch.â","âGuangxiu District is close by. It can link up with Technology New District.â","Everyone watched the livestream expectantly, but what aired was not what they had imagined.","ãFirst, a safe base.ã","ãSecond, a wood-type superhuman who can continuously supply food.ã","ãThese are the two most basic and essential conditions for establishing a government.ã","ãAfter that, a set of principles must be established as soon as possible. Systems for managing supplies and distributing compensation for jobs must be clearly defined.ã","ãWithout these things, it will be difficult for a base to expand. As the population continues to grow, all kinds of disorder will appear.ã","ãLater, the rules and regulations of Technology New District, along with the detailed provisions, will be shared with every district for reference.ã","ãMore than forty groups of survivors were rescued yesterday. The information will be updated later.ã","âHuh? Why are there suddenly so many requirements? What happened to the new government in Guangxiu District? I wanted to see what the people there looked like.â","Everyone began buzzing with discussion.","Song Jingshuo guessed, âThey must have run into people who didnât meet the requirements. Otherwise, they wouldnât have suddenly brought all this up.â","At first, there hadnât been any requirements at all. If you were capable, you could simply step up and do it.","ãIn addition, it has been confirmed today that no survivors remain in the Guangxiu District Government. Guangxiu District has yet to establish a new government institution.ã","ãHoweverâã","Ah, here came the turning point.","Everyone perked up their ears.","ãThe senior division of S City No. 14 High School, located on Firearms Camp Road in Guangxiu District, has been jointly established as a safe zone by more than three hundred surviving students, teachers, and parents.ã","ãThe students have successfully rescued more than one hundred survivors. This morning, they eliminated all the zombies inside the Guangxiu District Government Building.ã","ãAt present, the school can provide classrooms and bedding for communal living. Its food reserves are still sufficient.ã","ãGoing forward, it will also receive material support from the temporary government of Technology New District.ã","ãSurvivors who are homeless may go there for shelter.ã","ãSurvivors who have not yet escaped danger may also seek help from the students of No. 14 High School.ã","ãThe following are the contact numbers for the students of No. 14 High Schoolâ¦ã","A huge group of students appeared on camera.","Every one of them wore gleaming silver armor and a neatly pressed school uniform. Each held a crescent-shaped shovel and stood with their chests thrust out, struggling to maintain a stern expression.","Song Jingshuo: ââ¦â","Everyone: ââ¦â","All right. Now they understood everything.","The television station had sixteen shuttle buses in total. At the beginning, Jiang Cheng and the others had driven away six. Later, Changxing District and Shilong District took another five between them, leaving five behind.","The metal-type superhumans had removed all the seats, leaving only the bus compartments.","There were simply too many children from No. 14 High School. They couldnât all fit if they had to sit in the seats.","The lower sections of these buses could be opened, revealing large luggage compartments.","The âcagesâ were all collected and stored away. The bicycles that had been linked together were separated as well and stuffed into the luggage compartments. They crammed in as many as they could.","The adults had originally suggested simply leaving the bicycles behind, but the children couldnât bear to part with them.","Many of them were riding their own bicycles, beloved possessions they were unwilling to abandon.","Besides, the bicycles were a means of transportation. They might need them again in the future.","The adults did their best to accommodate them. Once the storage space was full, Jiang Cheng put the rest away herself.","âLetâs go.â","They drove several buses and took the children back to No. 14 High School in Guangxiu District. It was on the way back to Technology New District, too.","The teachers and parents had already seen their children on television. Their anxious hearts finally relaxed, leaving them both furious and proud.","They had never expected that the âJiang Chengâ from the television would personally bring the children back.","Several teachers and parents came to shake Jiang Chengâs hand.","âThank you. Thank you so much. Weâve caused you a lot of trouble!â","Jiang Cheng briefly explained to the adults the agreement she had reached with the children.","âTechnology New District will continue to support your supply of materials and treat this place as a safe base.â","Although the children had failed to establish a government, the adults were still overwhelmed with emotion at the remarkable achievements they had managed to accomplish.","Jiang Cheng inspected the food stores in the cafeteria.","The grain reserves were indeed still abundant and seemed capable of lasting quite a while.","But Jiang Cheng noticed that the refugees being sheltered there were freely coming and going in the cafeteria. One person lifted the lid of a large steamer and took two steamed buns.","No one said anything. Only the cafeteria auntie looked displeased when the person left the lid crooked, muttering as she walked over to set it straight again.","Jiang Cheng said nothing either.","Some lessons couldnât be taught. People had to put them into practice themselves and learn by running into the wall.","Still, she called the four students in charge aside and spoke with them privately for a while. Only then did she wave goodbye to everyone, get into the vehicle, and leave.","The people in charge were two boys and two girls.","These boys and girls were at precisely the age when the sexes divided into opposing camps and competed with one another over everything. Everyone insisted that the genders had to be equal, so they had elected two boys and two girlsâfour students in totalâas the main people responsible for the student body.","All four were superhumans to begin with, and powerful ones at that.","They were also class officers or members of the student council and had some experience with management. As a result, people were relatively willing to follow them.","After the adults from Technology New District had left, the studentsâ excitement still hadnât settled down. They surrounded their own teachers and parents, chattering away.","âTeachers, do you know what Auntie Jiangâs superpower is?â","âItâs âspatial storageâ!â","âItâs the kind of concept you only see in science-fiction novels!â","âAnd it isnât ordinary spatial storage. She has her own personal space that she carries with her and can put tons and tons of things inside.â","âSheâs insanely awesome!â","âShe was so cool! She put her hands behind her back and glanced over, and I immediately stood up straight.â","âMe too!â","Everyone was talking at once, their excitement running high.","At that moment, someone noticed that the four people in charge were unusually quiet, their expressions somewhat dazed.","âWhatâs wrong with you guys? What did Auntie Jiang say to you privately?â","One of them came back to himself. âOh, nothing.â","âYeah, she just told us to manage things properly and stuff.â","After brushing off the curious students, the four boys and girls glanced at one another without saying a word.","ãIf anyone commits an assault against a woman, donât hesitate. Once the crime is confirmed, kill them.ã","ãIf you truly canât bring yourselves to kill someone, contact me directly. Iâll handle it.ã","ãThere are still plenty of supplies, so there shouldnât be any killings over the struggle for resources.ã","ãSo the collapse of order will certainly begin with the violation of women.ã","ãIn troubled times, harsh measures are necessary.ã","ãMaintaining order is difficult, but destroying it is easy.ã","ãKeep an eye on the younger girls, especially those in junior high. Theyâre too young and donât understand anything. They think everyone is a good person.ã","ãYou four are different. Youâre seniors in high school, so youâre adults now, right?ã","ãFrom this moment on, learn to be adults.ã","The four of them looked at one another, all feeling somewhat dazed.","How naÃ ̄ve. She actually thought she could run a government.","Only now did she understand that this was truly something only adults could do.","Being an adult sounded terrifying.","Tech New District.","Xiao Dan had finally recovered somewhat over the past couple of days.","Wu Yan and Tao Xiaoxiao had been a great help. They had borrowed a laptop from the Youth Apartments, and once they put everything into spreadsheets, it all became quantifiable and manageable.","Everything was clear and orderly at a glance.","When people were too busy and exhausted, they had no time to think about anything else. But now that Xiao Dan had caught her breath, she had started thinking again.","She waited for Auntie Xue and Auntie Qian to finish work.","Every day, Auntie Xue and Auntie Qian were assigned a certain amount of work to complete. Once they finished it, they could leave.","But they both enjoyed the atmosphere at the Youth Apartments. Their coworkers there were all tall, handsome young men with impeccable taste in clothes and refined manners. How could that not be enjoyable?","They often stayed there for a long time.","As a result, Xiao Dan had to wait for ages. It was already evening before she finally saw them.","The three of them went to a pavilion in the residential complex to talk.","âI was thinking,â Xiao Dan said, âthat we should grow some things here in our own neighborhood too. We donât have to plant muchâIâm worried about tiring you two out. But we should at least grow something. We canât keep asking them for everything over there.â","Auntie Qian looked surprised. âAre we short on anything here? Donât we have enough vegetables to eat?â","The residents of Auspicious Home had fewer basic benefits than the residents of the Youth Apartments, but they were hardly reduced to the level of refugees who received only one potato a day.","Residents of Auspicious Home were allotted vegetables, meat, and fruit.","Zhou Wang had negotiated all of that. After all, Auspicious Home had taken in the refugees and provided housing for a large number of them.","The people at Auspicious Home felt that their treatment was quite acceptable. There were many elderly residents, after all, and they did not contribute as much as the young people at the Youth Apartments. The fact that those young people were willing to support and provide for them without complaint was already quite good.","But Xiao Dan was not satisfied.","In her mind, things were still divided much as they had been during the first disaster: the âYouth Apartmentsâ were one group, and âAuspicious Homeâ was another.","As far as belonging was concerned, she was part of Auspicious Home.","And now that she had become the person in charge, she desperately wanted to secure more benefits for Auspicious Home.","âEnough is enough, but having only âenoughâ is such a miserable feeling,â she said. âI was thinking that if we had some supplies of our own, weâd have a lot more flexibility. We wouldnât have to ask them for everything or let them hold all the power over us.â","Auntie Qian and Auntie Xue couldnât relate to her at all.","Their own benefits were exceptionally goodâthey belonged to the first tier.","The young people at the Youth Apartments were also highly capable, and they treated the two older women with great respect and affection.","If one compared it to a school, the two of them were like distinguished retired experts brought back on special appointment: their supplies were abundant, and their status was highly respected.","Whenever Xiao Song assigned them work, she did so in a soft, gentle voice.","They had never felt that they were begging anyone or being controlled by anyone.","But Xiao Dan had made a living doing odd jobs and selling insurance. She was not someone who would easily give up or retreat. She would do everything she could to persuade the other side.","In the end, Auntie Xue couldnât hold out any longer and was won over.","She agreed to establish a vegetable garden in the residential complex. There was no need to encourage the plants to grow at the same high efficiency as those at the Youth Apartments. Here, she could maintain an ordinary garden. She would simply give the plants a little boost in the morning before leaving and again after returning at night, making them grow faster than normal.","It wouldnât be particularly tiring.","After Xiao Dan left, Auntie Qian said to her, âArenât you working against Xiao Songâs arrangements by doing this?â","Auntie Xue gave an awkward little smile. âWeâre only growing some vegetables. Look, I didnât agree to fruit. I understand that benefits have to be tiered in order to manage people properly.â","The matter of restricting fruit and establishing different levels of benefits was something Song Jingshuo had specifically discussed with them and with the new Master Luo.","Both women had lived through historical periods in their youth, and they understood perfectly well that egalitarian âbig potâ distribution could not work. Once Song Jingshuo explained it, they were able to understand and support it.","âI just felt sorry for Little Xiao,â Auntie Xue said. âSheâs having a hard time too.â","Auntie Xue really did open several vegetable plots in the garden. She gave them a boost twice a day, once in the morning and once at night. It was easy and took almost no effort.","Every day, Xiao Dan watched the vegetables in the garden grow a little larger, and she was delighted.","Having supplies she could control herself made her feel more secure and more satisfied.","On the evening of the third day, Auntie Xue gave the vegetables another boost and told her, âOne more boost tomorrow and they should be ready.â","Xiao Dan was thrilled.","It turned out she had celebrated too soon.","After sleeping through the night, she woke up on the morning of the fourth day to find that every vegetable in the garden had been stolen.","Xiao Dan was furious.","When Zhou Wang came home that evening, she hurried after him, complaining, âCanât we get the surveillance cameras in our complex fixed?â","The surveillance system at Auspicious Home had âbroken downâ during the first zombie disaster, in order to cover up certain things.","âIf the cameras werenât broken, I could find the culprit right now,â she said.","Zhou Wang had noticed the vegetable plots several days ago. He had simply chosen not to say anything.","Sure enough, exactly what he had expected had happened.","Hearing her say this, Zhou Wang stopped and sighed. âFortunately, the cameras are broken.â","Xiao Dan stared at him in astonishment.","Zhou Wang turned around. âIf the cameras werenât broken, and you found out who stole them, what would you plan to do?â"]},{"number":167,"title":"Chapter 167: 0167","paragraphs":["Xiao Dan was furious. âOf course we make them return the vegetables they stole!â","âBut what if the stolen vegetables have already been thrown into the pot?â Zhou Wang asked. âOr even if they return them, how do you plan to punish the thieves afterward?â","Xiao Dan suddenly fell silent.","Because she had no idea how to punish the people who had stolen the vegetables.","She might not even have considered the question.","Zhou Wang asked her, âDo you know Cao Jiacai?â","Xiao Dan hesitated. âIâve heard of him.â","Zhou Wang continued, âThat day, when you called me from school for help, Cao Jiacai blocked me from going. Do you know how Jiang Cheng handled it?â","Zhou Wangâs eyes were dark and distant.","After all, she was the person who had once led an entire apartment complex in weathering a zombie disaster.","Xiao Dan said, âI heard she let a black cat bite him to death.â","âWhen the first zombie outbreak began, there was a cleaner in their property-management office who went on strike during the first few days and refused to work. Have you heard about that?â","Xiao Dan had.","No one had mentioned it during the first zombie disaster.","Later, Cao Jiacai reported the matter to the police. The police, worn down by his persistence, called Jiang Cheng to verify the story, which had worried everyone at Youth Apartments.","When the zombies broke out again this time and Mo Li directly bit Cao Jiacai to death, everyone realized that this outbreak was different from the last one.","People stopped hiding things behind euphemisms. Instead, deliberately or otherwise, they began revealing the truth to outsidersâthe people who had joined the apartment complex later, neighboring partners, and others.","Jiang Chengâs companions were no longer worried that this would be considered a âcrimeâ in peacetime.","That was how Jiang Cheng handled things.","It was evidence that offered a glimpse into her character and methods.","âDo you know when that was?â Zhou Wang asked. âThere were zombies everywhere outside, and Jiang Cheng drove that man out. She was sending him out to die.â","âYou found the people who stole the vegetables using the surveillance footage. Can you drive them all out to die?â","Zhou Wang delivered the question like a blow straight to the soul.","There was no need to think about it. Xiao Dan blurted out, âHow could I do that?â","She had neither the authority nor the ability.","Several large fields had been stripped bare. It could not have been the work of just one or two peopleâthere had to be at least a hundred.","And forget a hundred; even if it had only been one person, she could not drive a refugee out to die just for stealing vegetables.","âJiang Cheng dares to let people die,â Zhou Wang said. âThatâs why, ever since the incident in June, several thousand people have listened to her. Have you ever seen anyone dare to ignore her?â","âBut you want to drag all these people out into the open, and you have no way to deal with them. Do you still plan to run things? Iâm definitely going to replace you.â","âBecause after this, no one will listen when you speak. You wonât be able to manage anything anymore.â","âYouâre used to working on your own, I know. You have a sharp tongue, and most people canât win an argument with you.â","âBut managing a group is different.â","That night, Xiao Dan went home in a daze and fell asleep the moment her head hit the pillow.","The next morning, while everyone was collecting their potatoes, Zhou Wang gave a speech.","With both hands resting on his stomach, he had the air of a corporate executive. âItâs good that everyoneâs been able to improve their lives.â","âBut if you want to improve your life, you have to put in the work. This is the only time youâll get something for free. There wonât be a next time.â","âEither come out and work for performance points, or find a way to feed and clothe yourselves.â","âSuperpowers are useful, sure, but humanity survived for thousands of years before anyone had superpowers.â","âThere are only a handful of wood-element users. Are you just going to sit around and wait for them to grow everything for you? If a wood-element user doesnât plant your food, are your own hands suddenly useless?â","âFind some plastic or foam boxes. Iâll also find some earth- and metal-element users and ask them to make a batch of planters for everyone.â","âSister Xue and Sister Qian have already agreed to raise a batch of seedlings for everyone. Take them home and grow your own food.â","âDonât just sit around waiting for someone to put food in your mouth.â","There was no way to stop people from growing vegetables individually.","Jiang Cheng and Song Jingyu had already discussed the matter in their meetings. In fact, they encouraged everyone to do so.","The primary reason for rationing fruits and vegetables was that supplies were genuinely scarce. The first priority was to secure basic necessitiesâin other words, to make sure everyone had enough potatoes to keep from going hungry.","The secondary purpose was to use them as rewards to encourage people to participate in collective work.","But they were not trying to coerce or suppress anyone with food.","Xiao Danâs plan for large-scale cultivation would undermine the authority of the temporary government, and that was absolutely unacceptable. But if ordinary residents wanted to grow a few vegetables on their balconies to improve their lives and make efforts to save themselves, they should be encouraged and supported.","Xiao Dan had exhausted herself pleading with Auntie Xue to open up the vegetable fields, yet no one remembered her contribution.","Zhou Wang solved the problem by getting everyone a batch of planters, boxes, and seedlings. Everyone thought he was capable and thanked him with smiles and praise.","Watching everyoneâs happy faces and hearing their gratitude toward Zhou Wang, Xiao Dan vaguely felt that she had somehow been set up.","But she could not say how she had been set up, or who had done it.","Every step had been her own idea. She had done everything herself. Even when others tried to advise her and she refused, she had ignored them.","She had caused the whole mess herself. So who, exactly, had set her up?","She could not figure it out. She felt lost.","As a full-time mother, she had always believed she was still connected to society.","The products and insurance policies she sold required her to constantly seek out customers and persuade them to buy. She had interacted with so many peopleâhow could she possibly have become disconnected from society?","But even if you met many people while working sales on your own, each relationship was still a one-on-one connection.","Be a little more forceful, a little thicker-skinned, and you could close the deal.","But the essence of âsocietyâ lay in the interactions among multiple people.","Only within a group did complicated, multilayered relationships emerge. You had to see through peopleâs motives, goals, and circumstances; sort out the connections among them; react quickly; adapt on the spot; and constantly adjust your approach.","Without that kind of environment, people gradually became dull in some ways, while becoming stubborn in othersâwithout realizing it themselves.","That was the true meaning of becoming âdisconnected from society.â","Although everyone from Mr. Xuâs company had been assigned a job, they still had to line up for their basic supplies.","They stood among the crowd and listened to Zhou Wangâs speech. Once it was over, they went their separate ways.","Mr. Xu said to Director Yu, âAll that work for nothing.â","There had really been a huge number of people stealing vegetables the night before. As soon as everyone heard that the vegetables were almost ripe and would be harvested the next day, they had all taken plastic bags downstairs.","The apartment complex had been practically haunted the previous night.","Even when people saw acquaintances, they did not greet them. They simply kept their heads down and stole vegetables.","It was eerily quiet.","Mr. Xuâs group had strength in numbers and managed to steal quite a lot.","Only Wu Yan and Tao Xiaoxiao had insisted on wrapping scarves around their faces, saying, âIt would be so embarrassing if Xiao Dan saw us.â","That did not stop each of them from tucking four large heads of cabbage under an armpit and tiptoeing upstairs.","The vegetable-field affair had passed just like that. The two of them had now gone to comfort Xiao Dan.","That was how the workplace worked. The person joining you in cursing someone else might very well be that âsomeone else.â","Director Yu rubbed his face. âHa, I figured that out ages ago.â","Mr. Xu was starting to lose patience with him. âAre you done yet?â","Director Yu chuckled. âYouâre jealous of me.â","Climbing stairs really was one of the fastest ways to lose weight.","After training, Director Yuâs superpowers had improved by leaps and bounds, and he had already begun taking part in team missions.","After climbing stairs for just a few days, he had already lost a whole round of weight.","His jawline had even emerged!","Every morning and evening, he occupied the bathroom for ages, gazing into the mirror and admiring his jawline.","Whenever he spoke, he would unconsciouslyâor perhaps quite deliberatelyâtilt his chin upward.","Mr. Xu sneered. âIâm a muscular hunk. Why would I be jealous of a fat guy like you?â","Director Yu replied, âBeing fat is only temporary. The face is eternal.â","He used to claim that he had been the campus heartthrob back in school, with countless girls chasing after him. Everyone always said he was full of it.","Now that he had slimmed down, everyone finally believed he hadnât been boasting.","Even Wu Yan and Tao Xiaoxiao had become much gentler when speaking to him, and their smiles were far more sincere.","They were no longer the superficially flattering remarks and insincere smiles that praised him on the surface while mocking him underneath.","On the map produced by Yue Chao and the others at the television station, green points were gradually increasing in number.","Not only were there more safe zones capable of taking in and sheltering people, such as No. 14 Middle School, but temporary district governments had also been established one after another in three urban districtsâFuyang District, Wuxing District, and Shennan Districtâas well as one suburban district, Yaohu District.","Zheng Junwei, the head of the temporary government of Shilong District, watched Jiang Cheng appear on television time and time again. Rubbing his chin, he smiled.","âInteresting.â","What was interesting?","The process of establishing a temporary government.","First, you had to confirm that no one from your district government had survived.","Then you and a group of capable people established a government on the spot.","Was that the end of it?","No, no, no. The most interesting part came nextâ","You had to obtain recognition from Jiang Chengâs temporary government of the Technology New District. Only then could your government be considered successfully established.","Everyone throughout S City agreed on one thing: only a temporary government recognized by Jiang Cheng was a genuine temporary government.","Was it because Jiang Cheng controlled the television station?","That was certainly one factor, but it wasnât the only one.","Jiang Cheng and the people of the Technology New District had already become the âorthodoxâ authority in the hearts of S Cityâs residents.","You needed Jiang Chengâs personal seal of approvalâshe was practically a living imperial sealâto join the ranks of the legitimate governments.","Otherwise, you were an unorthodox faction, a local armed force, or at best a self-proclaimed local ruler. No one would acknowledge you.","Yaohu District was a distant suburban district, yet its people had driven for two hours into the city just to meet Jiang Cheng, receive her official recognition, and be granted the proper credentials.","The district governments were supposed to be equals within the administrative structure.","Zheng Junwei, a former general manager of a state-owned enterprise, found the whole situation very interesting.","He had met plenty of capable young subordinates before.","But within a large organizational structure, capable young people might be allowed to become top salespeople or senior technicians. It was far more difficult for them to rise into the upper levels of management.","That was because, within an organization, ability was only one factor. Seniority and the traditional order of advancement also played a major role.","Jiang Cheng was too young.","That was Zheng Junweiâs first impression when he saw her: too young.","Her skin looked impossibly flawless and elastic.","Wrinkles were the true certificates of experience.","Yet the moment he interacted with her, he sensed the sharpness within her.","It was impossible to suppress.","In times of chaos like these, she was exactly the sort of person who ought to rise to prominence.","It was a perfect example of the saying: heroes are made by the times.","The Technology New District.","Auspicious Garden kept taking in refugeesâboth those rescued by the district and those who had come seeking refuge on their ownâand it was finally full.","The new refugees began to be sent to Imperial View Garden.","The wood-element superpowered individuals at Imperial View Garden were recruited, and the community began to fall under the management of the Technology New District.","Because Auspicious Garden had already provided a successful example, the recruitment of Imperial View Garden went smoothly.","In fact, the people there were even happy to be brought under the districtâs administration.","âIt just feels more secure this way,â they said.","On September 15, a district government was established in Chaoqing District in the urban area. In the suburbs, a district government was established in Yunshan District.","On September 16, student representatives from No. 14 Middle School in Guangxiu District called Jiang Cheng. Their voices were filled with dejection.","âAuntie Jiang, can we come seek refuge in the Technology New District?â"]},{"number":168,"title":"Chapter 168: 0168","paragraphs":["When the children innocently suggested setting up a provisional government for Guangxiu District, the teacher stopped them, saying that some capable adults would come and take care of it.","The teacher genuinely believed that.","But the teacher was wrong. To this day, no one in Guangxiu District had managed to step forward and organize a provisional government.","The reason was laughable: Guangxiu District bordered the Tech New District and was simply too close to it.","From the very beginning, that had made Guangxiu District the area most frequently reached by the Tech New Districtâs rescue teams, and the area from which they had taken away the largest number of survivors.","Several large groups of survivors had already been evacuated. The small groups left behind were too scattered to form any effective force.","No. 14 Middle School, by contrast, could be considered a force in its own right.","But the students were too innocent and naÃ ̄ve.","Jiang Chengâs voice turned cold. âWhat happened?â","The student said, âNothing major, itâs justâ¦â","It was one grievance after another, one upsetting incident after another. Nothing was pleasant. Nothing was going the way they had imagined.","The things Jiang Cheng had solemnly warned them about had not happened.","That was because after Jiang Cheng left, the four student representatives had held a discussion. They called all the boys and girls together for separate meetings.","The boysâ meeting centered on protecting the girls, especially the younger female students.","The girlsâ meeting focused on being wary of all âuncles.â No one was to be alone with any âuncle.â","There were no elementary school students here. Middle schoolers already understood certain things, and the school had given them some education on the subject.","The problem was that the children couldnât connect the concept of a âcriminalâ with the âuncleâ standing in front of them.","For example, the children knew that there were hooligans in society.","But it simply did not occur to them that someone they had worked so hard to rescue might try to take advantage of them.","The two concepts could not overlap in their minds.","This gap in perception existed everywhere, especially for children.","Every child knew from an early age that they had been born from their father and mother.","But quite a few children seemed to suddenly wake up one day at a certain age and realize: Holy crap, so Dad and Mom had to have sex to make me! So Dad and Mom have a sex life!","Jiang Chengâs warning was meant to bridge that gap in their understanding.","Sure enough, one first-year middle school girl later reported that one day, an uncle had asked her to help find some bedding because he couldnât locate it.","The girl was confused. How could the bedding be missing? Didnât everyone sleep in the classrooms together?","The aunties slept in one classroom, and the uncles slept in another.","The girl had almost gone with the uncle. She had just taken a step when she suddenly remembered the meeting the older girls had held. So she said, âIâll bring a few people with me.â","The uncle immediately said, âNo, no, itâs fine. I just remembered where it is.â","Then he walked away.","The girl reported the incident to the senior girls, two of the four student representatives. The girls found the other two representatives, and the four of them discussed it. They all felt that something was wrong.","But when they asked the younger girl to identify which uncle it had been, she couldnât recognize him.","All the middle-aged men looked more or less the same: greasy hair, unshaven faces, and wrinkled suits.","There were so many people like that that, after one glance, the younger girl couldnât tell them apart.","In the end, they couldnât find the man to confront him. But the older girls held another meeting for the younger girls and reminded everyone to stay vigilant.","So nothing particularly terrible happened.","But every single day was still exhausting.","Some people demanded to switch classrooms. They said the north-facing classrooms were too gloomy and wanted to move into the south-facing ones.","Naturally, the people in the south-facing classrooms refused.","The matter was actually very simple. The school had plenty of classrooms. Everyone had started living on the first floor; once it was full, they had moved to the second floor, and once that was full, to the third.","There were still empty classrooms farther up. Why not just move up one floor?","Because the school building had no elevator. Moving upstairs meant climbing more stairs every day.","The people in their thirties and forties claimed that they were too old to climb, insisting that the students on the first floor give up the south-facing classrooms. They said the students were young and could climb a few extra stairs without a problem. They also accused the students of being selfish for occupying the best classrooms on the first floor.","The students were furious. What did they mean, âoccupyingâ the best classrooms? This was their school in the first place. When the zombies appeared, they had been trapped here and forced to sleep in the classrooms.","The students refused to switch.","But when they returned from a rescue mission, the classrooms had already been reassigned.","A group of adults had moved downstairs and dumped the studentsâ bedding in the hallway. They had not even bothered to help carry it upstairs.","The students were so angry that they couldnât help arguing with the adults.","But the adults were very skilled at talking.","âWe thought you were good people. We thought you would help others and take care of them. Youâve really disappointed us. Why canât you take care of people older than you? Is this how your teachers taught you?â","The students were trapped.","They felt as if they were being roasted over a fire.","Of course they wanted to be good people. But why did being a good person have to be so miserable?","The teachers and parents came out to smooth things over as well.","The students could only swallow their anger, gather up their bedding, and go sleep in the north-facing classrooms upstairs.","Then one of the cafeteria aunties came to complain that someone was wasting food. They had thrown away half a steamed bun without finishing it.","As more rescued people and refugees arrived, the aunties calculated the amount of food needed every day with painstaking precision, terrified that even the smallest amount might be wasted.","Seeing someone leave half a bun behind broke their hearts. But when they went over to say something, they were cursed at instead.","The aunty felt deeply wronged.","There was also a vegetable garden at the school. The cafeteria aunties and the security guards had set it up long ago. The principal thought it added a touch of rural charm and would help the children learn about vegetables, so he had allowed them to keep it.","After the zombies appeared, it became the schoolâs source of fresh vegetables. But the garden was too small. It could only provide a little variety and improve the meals; it was nowhere near enough to feed so many people.","Then the refugees arrived and discovered the garden. They immediately began breaking off tomatoes, twisting off cucumbers, and pulling up radishes.","All of those vegetables could be eaten raw.","Picking some vegetables would have been fine, but this group of city dwellers had no idea how to treat them with care. They tore the vines, trampled the soil, and damaged the garden.","The aunty was so angry that she burst into tears.","Over the phone, the students told Jiang Cheng, âItâs justâ¦ this feeling that weâre powerless to do anything.â","Their voices were filled with exhaustion.","âIt feels like this isnât our school anymore.â","âThey donât listen to us at all, and they refuse to help with the work. Weâre the ones doing everything. Only a few adults came to help. Then they stopped coming, too.","âAnd there are several people saying that weâre just children and shouldnât be in charge anymore.â","âThey insist on taking over the storage room. We told them no. One of them turned out to have fire powers, and we had no idea. Heâd been here for several days and had never said he was an ability user. He hadnât helped with anything, either. Then, all of a sudden, he threw a fireball and burned Xiao Yunshuâs braid. Xiao Yunshu was so angry she cried.â","Jiang Cheng asked, âDid you hand the storage room over to them?â","The student said, âNo. We didnât. But whenever we go out, they force their way into the storage room and take whatever they want.â","âThe people left behind are all younger students or people without abilities, and even the teachers canât stop them.â","The teachers had never been particularly forceful people to begin with.","And among the refugees, there were several people especially skilled at using moral blackmail.","What truly crushed the studentsâ spirits was the news that âtwo of the studentsâ parents have superpowers. Yesterday afternoon... they left.â","Those two parents had taken their children away.","One family was from Changxing District, and the other was from Wuxing District. Their children had both been admitted to No. 14 Middle School through the Math Olympiad competitions.","Both districts now had their own district governments, and the two families had gone to seek refuge with them.","The two adults who had fought alongside everyone and worked hard to survive from the very beginning had, through their actions, denied the children of No. 14 Middle School.","It was devastating.","The children were hit especially hard.","Jiang Cheng asked, âWhich one are you? Duan or Li?â","The student replied, âIâm Duan Junqi.â","âAll right, Duan Junqi,â Jiang Cheng said. âIâll give you one hour. Make me a list.â","âEveryone whoâs been stirring up trouble.â","âThose whoâve been seizing supplies.â","âThose whoâve bullied the students.â","âThere have to be at least ten people. More is fine. Anyone you dislikeâput them all on the list.â","âWait for me. Iâll be there in an hour.â","After Duan Junqi hung up, everyone crowded around him.","âWell? Did Auntie Jiang agree?â","Duan Junqi looked at them. âNo. She didnât.â","A wave of disappointed sighs swept through the group.","âBut,â Duan Junqi continued, âshe said sheâd be here in an hour.â","âShe told us to make a list.â","It was still quite early.","The fact that those two parents had taken their children away the day before had truly broken the studentsâ hearts.","That evening, they had held a long meeting before finally deciding: âForget the school. Letâs go seek refuge with Auntie Jiang in the Technology New District.â","It had been too late to call her then, so they had gotten up early today and called Jiang Cheng before even having breakfast.","That worked out well. At this hour, the teams from the Technology New District had not yet set out; everyone was still eating breakfast.","Jiang Cheng immediately used the radio to issue instructions to the cafeteria staff: âTell all the team leaders that todayâs arrangements have changed!â","Jiang Cheng went straight to the cafeteria at the clubhouse.","No matter how urgent things were, they still had to eat first.","They held a meeting while eating, then gathered their weapons and equipment.","âLetâs go.â","Guangxiu District, No. 14 Middle School.","The students lingered at the school gate, constantly looking outside.","One of the adults they disliked came over with his hands on his hips. âWhy arenât you going out today?â","Student: âWeâre not going out today.â","Adult: âAre there still enough supplies in the cafeteria? You need to go out and find more. Donât let everyone starve.â","Why werenât you going out to find supplies? All you did was stand here and bask in the sun.","The students seethed with anger.","âYouâre sulking now?â the adult sneered. âKids really are unreliable.â","âYouââ one student began, unable to hold back, but Duan Junqi stopped him.","Duan Junqi said, âWe have something to do today.â","The adult clicked his tongue.","Suddenly, Duan Junqiâs phone rang. He hurriedly answered it.","âHello? Good! Good!â","After hanging up, he said, âTheyâll be here soon!â","The studentsâ spirits lifted.","Suddenly, the school broadcast crackled to life.","âEveryone report to the front plaza immediately! Everyone report to the front plaza immediately! There is an important announcement. Come downstairs at once!â","Some of the refugees complained, âSo noisy. What is it now?â","They had finished breakfast and had nothing to do. They had been planning to go back to sleep, but then they thought they might be handing out supplies. Afraid of missing out, they hurriedly got up and went downstairs.","Men and women streamed out in a dense crowd and gathered in the plaza in front of the schoolâs main building, filling the air with a constant buzz.","Many people asked the students, âWhatâs going on?â","âWhat happened?â","Even the teachers came over to ask.","âXiao Yunshu, whatâs the matter?â","But Xiao Yunshu only looked toward Duan Junqi, who was on the phone. She waved to the teacher, signaling her to wait and say nothing for now.","Duan Junqi hung up and shouted, âOpen the gate!â","The older students went over and opened the school gates.","A rumbling sound seemed to be approaching from far away.","âWhat is that?â","âWhat are they trying to do?â","âAre more people coming? I hope not too many. We wonât have enough food as it is.â","But gradually, everyone realized that something was wrong.","Rumble, rumble.","It sounded like enormous, heavy vehiclesâmore than one of them. The noise grew louder and louder as they drew near.","Soon, they came into view.","They were the Blade vehicles everyone had seen in the television announcements.","They were much larger and taller than ordinary buses.","After undergoing countless transformations and extensions, their paint had peeled and become mottled. Everyone had complained that they looked ugly, so the metal-element users had simply stripped the paint from the entire vehicles.","Now their bodies gleamed silver from end to end.","The blades flashed in the sunlight.","From the moment they appeared in the distance, they radiated an oppressive presence.","Silver light flickered regularly through the gaps between the campus railings, dazzling everyoneâs eyes.","At the school gate, the vehicles swung around the corner and drove into the plaza.","The driver was Zhang Kuang. He slammed on the brakes at high speed.","The screech of the brakes made everyoneâs teeth ache.","Many people stumbled backward in fright, terrified that they would be run over and lose their heads on the blades.","One vehicle.","Then another.","Then another.","Before long, numerous vehicles had lined up across the school plaza.","Their killing intent was overwhelming.","The entire plaza fell utterly silent."]},{"number":169,"title":"Chapter 169: 0169","paragraphs":["When the vehicle doors opened, the people who stepped out were all young and strong.","Their daily regimen of intense physical labor and climbing stairs had given every one of them a well-proportioned, sturdy build, brimming with strength.","Their standardized silver armor gleamed brightly, while the sharp crescent-shaped shovels at their sides flashed with a cold, dangerous light under the sun.","Regardless of what they had done before or what kind of personalities they had possessed, decapitating people day after day and growing accustomed to the sensation of sharp blades severing flesh, muscle, and bone had naturally instilled a terrifying bloodlust in them.","Several of the women carried an even more frightening aura of violence than the men.","What had happened at the school had enraged the women, whose sense of morality was stronger.","A few of them were even middle-school girls. They glared furiously at these adult parasites.","The crowd shrank back.","Many people instinctively retreated, bunching toward the center.","As though standing in the middle would make them safer.","A black cat leaped from the vehicle. The instant it landed, it had already transformed into a sleek black panther, drawing a chorus of startled cries from the crowd.","A young woman stepped down from the vehicle. Her silver armor fit her perfectly, her eyes were cold, and her stride was strong and agile.","The last person to get out was a tall young man with a handsome face. He was the only one among them who wore neither armor nor weapons. His long legs were wrapped in suit trousers, his white shirt sleeves rolled up, and his black leather shoes gleaming.","With his handsome features and languid bearing, he carried an air of nobility.","He stood behind the young woman, with the black panther on her other side, like a pair of attendants.","Jiang Cheng stepped forward, her cool eyes sweeping over the crowd.","No one dared meet her gaze. Everyone instinctively looked away.","âAuntie Jiang!â","âAuntie Jiangââ","The middle-school students took two steps forward and called out to her.","Their voices were filled with grievance, and for some reason tears began to well up in their eyes.","They regarded her as an idol because they had seen her on television. They always felt that the reason they had been unable to establish a government was simply that they were too young and inexperienced.","But they had still worked hard to do everything properly, braving danger and never caring about the cost. They wanted her approval.","Yet somehow, things had turned out like this. Everyone had clearly worked so hard, risking their lives without complaint.","How had it come to this?","Jiang Cheng held out her hand.","Duan Junqi hurriedly called out, âShao Yingchuan!â","The name sounded grand, but the person who stepped forward was a small, fair-skinned girl who had not even finished growing. She was only in middle school.","The girl hugged a hardcover notebook and trotted over, handing it to Auntie Jiang with both hands.","She did so with great solemnity.","Jiang Cheng opened to the first page. Three striking words caught her eye:","âGrudge Book.â","Shao Yingchuan was still young and had no special abilities, but she possessed beautiful handwriting, so she had been assigned to record incidents and manage the residentsâ accommodations.","Day after day, she had to deal with these adults.","She had suffered plenty of abuse and wiped away her tears countless times.","But even the older students could do nothing about these adults, and the teachers had only told them not to make an issue of it.","How could she not hold a grudge? It was only that she lacked the ability to settle those grudges for the time being.","The little girl loved writing and had always kept a diary. Every day, she recorded all the unpleasant things that happened.","The time, the place, the people involved, the cause, the process, and the outcome.","She had even mockingly named it the âGrudge Book.â","It had merely been a way to vent her grievances. Who could have imagined that it would one day become useful?","Her handwriting was beautiful, and her records were so clear and detailed that everything was immediately apparent.","Jiang Cheng skimmed through the pages. She could not help casting the little girl an appreciative glance.","When she looked up again, her eyes were devoid of warmth and frightening to behold.","At last, she spoke. âThereâs no need for me to introduce myself, is there?â","Indeed, there was no need. No one in S City failed to recognize herâJiang Cheng.","The acting district chief of the temporary government in the Science and Technology New District.","The leader of S Cityâs anti-zombie forces.","The fightersâ idol. The survivorsâ hope.","Jiang Cheng did not waste a single word.","âThose whose names I call will step forward on their own. Donât wait for my people to make you.â","The first was a man who had wasted food in the cafeteria and insulted one of the aunties.","âZhang Bohong.â","Zhang Bohong froze. He wanted to hide in the crowd, but then he saw a massive, powerfully built young man bend down to listen. The little girl who had presented the notebook was already pointing in his direction.","There was no way he could hide. That girl in charge of the records had an exceptional memory for faces.","Zhang Bohong had no choice but to brace himself and step forward. Trying to remain polite, he asked, âM-May I ask what this is about?â","Jiang Cheng ignored him and continued calling the next name.","The second was a man who had destroyed the vegetable plots and made one of the aunties cry.","âHong Zhenzong.â","The third was a man who had shoved the warehouse administrator, causing a young middle-school boy to fall and scrape his knee, then forced his way into the warehouse and taken supplies without permission.","âLÃ1⁄4 Hao.â","The fourth was a woman who had led the seizure of the studentsâ south-facing classroom on the first floor and thrown the childrenâs bedding into the hallway.","âYan Yiwen.â","Several hundred fully armed young men and women glared menacingly at the crowd.","The students pointed out more offenders.","No one dared remain where they were. Those whose names were called stepped forward one after another, steeling themselves and huddling together anxiously.","There had been far too many petty incidents that had angered the students, so Jiang Cheng selected only a few people to name.","She chose those responsible for the more serious incidents, and those who had led the others.","Even so, she called out more than thirty people.","When Jiang Cheng finally closed the hardcover notebook with a sharp snap, the hundreds of remaining refugees felt as though they had been pardoned.","Many of them had broken out in a cold sweat across their foreheads and backs.","Because none of them were fools. In truth, every one of them knew perfectly well what they had done and what they had taken part in.","They had merely bullied the children because the youngsters were naÃ ̄ve, innocent, kindhearted, and easy to manipulate.","But once genuinely decisive adults arrived with armed forces, everyone immediately became an obedient citizen who followed the rules.","If they had joined the Science and Technology New District from the very beginning, under strict and systematic management, perhaps every one of them would now be working diligently, contributing their labor, obeying discipline, and living harmoniously with the others.","âI hereby announce this.â Jiang Chengâs gaze swept over them. âSince Guangxiu District does not meet the requirements for establishing a temporary government, it will now be incorporated into the Science and Technology New District and placed under unified management.â","âThe thirty-seven people named above have refused to obey the rules. They will now be repatriated.â","âOn humanitarian grounds, you will be provided with armor and weapons and sent back to your places of origin.â","âGoing homeâ was something that could happen only in a dream.","In reality, there was no way they could return home.","Once they went back, who would continue providing them with food?","Who would guarantee their safety?","How were they supposed to survive?","Were they really going to go out every day on their own, kill zombies, rummage for supplies, and search for food?","The thirty-seven people panicked.","Some immediately began begging for mercy. âWe know we were wrong! Weâll change! We wonât do it again!â","See? Jiang Cheng had not even announced what their âcrimesâ were, yet they already knew exactly what they had done wrong.","Every one of them understood it perfectly.","Others raised their voices and shouted angrily, âYou have no right to do this!â","Or they simply started acting shamelessly. âIâm not leaving! Iâm not going anywhere!â","Some began throwing tantrums and playing the victim, wailing, âYouâre sending us to our deaths!â","It was precisely because they were so shameless and thick-skinned that the student children had been helpless against them.","Listening to them was irritating enough.","Su Yu frowned.","Suddenly, a force erupted from behind those people, spreading like a shock wave.","The various wails and screams cut off abruptly.","The sudden burst of force sent everyone sprawling forward, face-first into the dirt.","Protective Barrier: Ejection.","The protective barrier was one-way. People could leave from the inside, but nothing could enter from the outside.","âInsideâ and âoutsideâ were defined by Jiang Cheng.","The barrier could appear all at once, enclosing the people it was meant to protect. Or it could start small, expanding from a single âpointâ into a field in an extremely short span of time.","The shorter the time, the greater the impact of the expansion on the outside world.","An instantaneous expansion was essentially an explosion.","The crowd cried out and shuffled backward again, beginning to pack tightly together.","But no one complained. If anything, they wanted to press even closer. That was the only way to feel safe.","Duan Junqiâs breathing grew heavy. He clenched his fists and struggled to control his emotions, trying to keep his face as impassive as the adultsâ.","He glanced at Xiao Yunshu, and happened to catch her looking at him too.","Xiao Yunshu was also doing her best to keep her expression under control.","But the delight shining in her eyes was impossible to hide.","Some of the younger kids couldnât restrain themselves at all. They clenched their fists and waved them excitedly in the air!","Jiang Cheng merely lifted her chin slightly, and the people in silver armor carrying weapons sprang into action.","They walked over, hauled up those lying dazed on the ground, and asked, âWhich district are you from? Where do you live?â","Then they dragged them toward the vehicles and stuffed them inside.","Cry, scream, begâit didnât matter. Those tricks might work on children, but what use were they against people who decapitated others every day?","Zombies had human forms too.","After killing enough of them, a personâs heart really did grow hard.","Most peopleâs resistance was completely ineffective in the hands of the fighters.","But there was one case where the resistance was genuinely effective. Just as a man was about to be hauled away, two columns of flame shot up from the ground, forcing the two fighters to retreat in haste!","Jiang Cheng remembered this man. His companions had shoved aside the little boy guarding the warehouse and forcibly taken supplies.","When the older kids had rushed over to stop them, this man had conjured a fireball and burned Xiao Yunshuâs braid.","She had looked terrible the moment they got out of the vehicle.","Her high ponytail had been burned off. Once it came loose, the hair at the back of her head formed a slanted plane.","Now she had barely managed to tie it up, leaving her with this ridiculous-looking head of hair.","No wonder she was furious enough to cry.","The corners of Jiang Chengâs lips curled upward.","Things would be boring if no one put up a fight.","She asked, âAre you trying to force us to take action?â","The fire wielder cursed, âForce your mother! What gives you the right to do this? Who gave you that authority? What law says you can drive us out?â","Flames roared in both his hands, radiating waves of heat that kept anyone from approaching.","Out in the world, he would have been considered a fairly powerful fire-type ability user. He had come to seek refuge on his own, but had never mentioned that he possessed an ability, which was why Xiao Yunshu had been caught off guard.","He was also one of the people who had plotted to seize the schoolâs supplies, refusing to let the children take charge.","They relied on his powerful fire ability.","He had observed the situation carefully. His ability was stronger than those of every student with an ability. If a real fight broke out, he had excellent odds of winning.","Jiang Cheng said, âPower is something you seize for yourself.â","Not again. Not again!","Song Jingshuo folded his arms and stared straight up at the sky.","Several people who were close to Jiang Cheng began to avert their eyes.","After spending enough time with her, people gradually came to understand what Jiang Cheng was really like.","She wasâ¦ extraordinarily intolerant.","If she ignored you, it was probably because whatever you had done was too insignificant to even earn her dislike. You werenât worth the effort of a glance.","You should be grateful she couldnât be bothered to look at you.","Because if she was willing to face you directly and speak to you in an even, reasonable tone, you were in serious danger.","Jiang Cheng might be intolerant, but she respected basic legal principles, moral standards, and due process.","Those were the framework that held an orderly society together. Jiang Cheng did not lead by acting on her personal likes and dislikes; everyone was required to abide by that framework.","That was how order was formed and maintained.","But Jiang Chengâ¦ found minor evils and minor punishments far too boring.","She liked it when people committed major evils.","Once someone did something truly wickedâsomething that, by common moral standards, warranted severe punishmentâshe had every justification she needed to act.","Listen to her voice. It was practically seductive.","Sure enough, those words stirred the fire wielderâs ambitions.","He had originally wanted to seize control of the school. It was just that he had been able to lie around eating and drinking without lifting a finger, watching the student brats scurry about like diligent little worker bees. As for the supplies in the warehouse, he could simply take whatever he wanted, since the students were powerless to stop him. So he had never actually made his move.","But now, facing the adults, it was time to seize true power!","Capture the ringleader first!","Decapitation was the greatest blow one could deal to a groupâs morale. If he could kill the leader in a single strike, intimidate the rest, and frighten them into standing down, he would win immediately!","It could only be said that he was far too naÃ ̄ve.","The television broadcasts Jiang Cheng and the others produced had always focused on politics, administration, and practical experience.","They had never once shown any footage of combat.","No one had any idea how powerful the armed force under Jiang Chengâs command truly was.","But one thing should not be forgotten: supernatural abilities grew stronger the more they were used.","Day after day, the teams in the technology district never stopped training.","When the fireball erupted and shot toward Jiang Cheng, most people merely raised their eyebrows.","There was no need for a combat-type ability userâor Su Yuâto intervene.","Even Mo Li seemed too lazy to move.","A water shield formed in the open space between Jiang Cheng and the fire wielder, blocking the fireballâs path.","It was not a single, cookie-shaped shield. Experiments had already shown that such a water shield could not withstand a powerful fireball. A sufficiently strong fireball would merely be weakened once before breaking through the shield and continuing toward its target.","So the water shield that appeared out of thin air was shaped more like an ice-cream cone.","The fireball was like a scoop of ice cream. It burrowed into the âcone,â rapidly shrinking until it vanishedâin the blink of an eye.","In the blink of an eye, an attempted sneak attack and assassination had failed.","Li Jiangbing had noticed that one of the people they needed to deal with was a fire wielder, so he had taken up a favorable position as soon as he got out of the vehicleâright beside the fountain pool in the school plaza.","At last, he had a chance to participate in combat with his ability instead of relying on his muscles to shovel heads around.","He was delighted.","Jiang Cheng turned her head and asked Wu Jiancheng, âHow powerful was that fireball?â","Wu Jiancheng was spectacularly oblivious. âPretty average, I guess.â","Jiang Cheng had no choice but to give him another hint. âCould it have killed me?â","âOh!â Wu Jiancheng finally caught on. âAbsolutely.â","Jiang Cheng said, âSo that makes it attempted murder?â","Wu Jiancheng nodded emphatically. âYou bet!â","âGood.â Jiang Cheng was delighted too. âGo, Mo Li.â","The black panther leaped into the air and pounced!","Gasps rose from the crowd.","One of the team members had been recording everything with a digital camera.","Jiang Cheng had told him to film it before they came.","She had said, âWe happen to need a sample.â"]},{"number":170,"title":"Chapter 170: 0170","paragraphs":["Forcibly expelling those who refused to follow the rules had only made everyone wary.","What truly terrified them was Mo Li ignoring the fire wallâs defenses, charging straight into the flames, and biting through the fire-type superhumanâs neck.","That was a personânot a zombie.","A living person!","This Jiang Cheng really dared to kill.","Mo Li hadnât even needed to grow any larger. In its current form, it had ended the life of a superhuman.","Why was Mo Li on an entirely different level?","Everyone had sparred with Mo Li before.","Against Zhou Wang and Brother Dong, it could match their speed.","Against Guo Jun and Gao Yuxuan, it could withstand high-voltage electricity.","Against Wu Jiancheng, it was impervious to the scorching flames, swallowing them in one bite and extinguishing them with a sweep of its tail.","No one had dared test it against the metal-type superhuman. They were afraid they would be killed by a single swipe before their blades could even reach Mo Li.","Mo Li carried the fire-type superhumanâs body over, dropped it at Jiang Chengâs feet, and released it.","Jiang Cheng clasped her hands behind her back and swept her gaze over the remaining refugees.","They could feel the chill of the autumn wind now. The sun was bright, yet everyone felt cold.","âIâll skip the unnecessary talk,â Jiang Cheng said.","âThe Fourteenth Middle School shelterâs trial operation is over. Starting today, we are entering formal operation.â","âThe management regulations will be announced shortly.â","âFrom now onâfollow the rules.â","Jiang Cheng paused.","Everyone thought that was the end of it, but then she spoke again.","Her icy gaze rolled over the crowd.","âIâve heard that an adult man claimed he couldnât find his bedding and called a middle-school girl to help him look for it?â","Everyone froze.","How could bedding go missing? They all lived together in the classrooms, and everyone had exactly the same things. How could one personâs bedding disappear?","What did she mean?","âYou know who Iâm talking about.â","âYou can keep hiding in the crowd.â","âIâll make this clearâthere are a lot of little girls in this school.â","Jiang Cheng placed particular emphasis on the word âlittle,â issuing a death warning:","âIf anything happens to one of these little girls, Iâll turn you into a human pig.â","In an instant, all the adults understood. The teachersâ faces went pale.","When Jiang Cheng finally said, âDismissed,â everyone ran off as fast as they could.","Even those living on the upper floors no longer minded the exhausting climb. They scrambled upstairs in a hurry.","They only felt a little safer once they were hiding inside their classrooms.","Many people hid behind the curtains and peered down at the scene below.","On the ground floor, Jiang Cheng turned to face a group of students, along with several teachers and parents.","Everyone lowered their heads slightly, as though they had done something wrong.","Jiang Cheng sighed and said, âLet me introduce someone.â","She pointed her thumb at the handsome man beside her. âThis is Song Jingshuo. He designed our current management system. Today, heâll be conducting your training.â","Everyone else wore sneakers and combat uniforms. Only Song Jingshuo was dressed well enough to chair a meeting and take a beautiful woman on a date afterward.","With both hands in his pockets and his long legs standing casually apart, he looked like a rich young master with his bodyguard.","Why was everyone willing to put up with Song Jingshuo showing off today?","Because the troublesome task of educating the children had been dumped on him.","Everyone had been that age once. They knew perfectly well how much of a headache teenagers could be, and no one wanted to take on the job.","Not even Jiang Cheng.","They had practically forced Song Jingshuo out into the field.","Once the matter was settled, the group split up.","Some people escorted the expelled refugees away.","Others went to search for survivors according to the original plan.","Jiang Cheng inspected the warehouse and cafeteria, left the Fourteenth Middle School with enough potatoes to last a week, and departed as well.","The cafeteria auntie was stunned by the basketball-sized potatoes.","In the auditorium, the students sat in neat rows.","Onstage stood a folding chair. Song Jingshuo sat beneath the lights, one ankle resting on the opposite knee.","âTell me,â he said. âWhy?â","Several student representatives responsible for managing things stood with their heads bowed.","The teachers and the few parents who had stayed behind had no superhuman abilities. The parents with abilities had left, while those who remained were only helping with logistics and administration.","The students had become the main force handling the most important tasksâsearching for supplies and rescuing survivors.","âOn September ninth,â Song Jingshuo said, âwe already broadcast the general principles and detailed regulations on television, specifically so everyone could use them as a reference.â","âItâs the sixteenth today. That section has been playing on a loop ever since.â","âHow did you manage to pick up the sesame seeds while throwing away the watermelon? How could you fail to implement the most important partâthe distribution system?â","âYouâthe tallest one. You answer.â","The student called on was Duan Junqi.","There was no way for Duan Junqi to avoid it, so he answered through gritted teeth. âItâs justâ¦ the meals. Weâ¦ couldnât do it.â","He nudged Xiao Yunshu with his elbow. Xiao Yunshu shared his misfortune and spoke up as well. âIt was justâ¦ making ourselves eat the good food while giving them the bad food. That felt a littleâ¦ you know. We couldnât bring ourselves to say it.â","Song Jingshuo sneered sarcastically. âYou thought you were being a great person, didnât you? Thought you were so kind and compassionate. Thought the adults were all villains for coming up with such an evil system, right?â","Everyone lowered their heads even further, looking dejected.","Becauseâ¦ truthfully, they had thought that way.","Sometimes, they really did wonder if the adults were being a little unkind.","How could they give everyone else nothing but potatoes?","Song Jingshuo asked, âDo you understand now?â","The students hurriedly nodded.","Song Jingshuo said, âIf you understand, sit down. Iâll explain it to you.â","âThe basic operating principle of a society is that when a person contributes labor, they receive compensation.â","âBut money is useless now. If you want someone to work, what can you use to compensate them?â","âWhat can serve as hard currency?â","âOnly something everyone needsâsomething no one can do without.â","âIn our current situation, that can only be food.â","Song Jingshuo continued, âDid everyone just lie down and refuse to do anything from the very beginning? Was there not a single person willing to help at first?â","There was a moment of silence before people gradually answered.","âThere were.â","âThere were people at the beginning.â","âLaterâ¦â","Later, they saw that helping earned them nothing, while those who lay around in the sun had food and drink just the same. The shameless troublemakers who refused to contribute even managed to eat more and take more. Gradually, no one was willing to help anymore.","âWe all learned about the communal feeding system in history class,â Song Jingshuo criticized. âYou just couldnât connect it to what was happening right in front of you, could you?â","The countryâs education system was actually quite comprehensive.","Chinese, history, and civics worked together to instill political awareness and a sense of the bigger picture in citizens from childhood.","All of that knowledge had already been absorbed into their minds.","âWhat you learn isnât meant only to be written on an exam,â Song Jingshuo said. âIt has to be applied to reality.â","The studentsâ biggest problem was that they only kept what they learned in their headsâthey couldnât put it into practice.","That day, Song Jingshuo sacrificed half a day to explain everything to them, breaking it down into the smallest details.","He even went through each incident one by one: what the other party was thinking, what their intentions were, and how they should respond.","It had been a long time since he had spoken so much. One of the students handed him a bottle of mineral water, and Song Jingshuo drank half of it in one go.","At the end, he said, âGood people canât become leaders, because leaders have to shoulder a great many burdens and make ruthless decisions so that ordinary people can go on being good.â","He did not forget to add sarcastically, âAnd they have to face accusations from all those ordinary âgood peopleâ that they arenât kind enough, right?â","âThose who manage contribute their brains. Those who work contribute their strength. Those who fight risk their lives. Naturallyâand rightfullyâthey should receive better food and supplies than others.â","âStarting tomorrow, everyone gets one potato a day. Steam it, roast itâwhatever you like. Sprinkle on some salt and eat it.â","âAnything else must be earned through labor.â","âNo one is allowed to reap without sowing.â","âTo serve the people means allowing more good people to survive, not letting a handful of good-for-nothings ride on the heads of decent people and crap on them.â","That uncle crossed his long legs, his black leather shoes gleaming beneath the lights.","His gaze was cold as he looked down at the crowd below.","âIf you donât have the means to wield thunder, then donât pretend to have the heart of a bodhisattva.â","Jiang Cheng was not idle, either.","Sometimes, when so many things happened at exactly the right moment, it was not coincidence. It meant they had accumulated to the point where an eruption was inevitable.","It had been more than half a month since the second outbreak of the zombie virus.","It wasnât just the temporary governments in the various districts that had taken in large numbers of survivors at their bases. S City had also developed countless shelters, large and small, like Fourteenth Middle School, that took in survivors on a smaller scale.","Some survivors, after escaping dangerous areas on their own, had sought refuge in places like these.","Wherever there were people, there would be conflict. So many strangers gathered together became miniature societies.","And not every place had abundant supplies.","Once supplies ran short, or the power to maintain order was lost, all it took was for one person to step forward and lead the way before human nature could easily slide into the abyss.","It was time to put a public security management system in place.","Fourteenth Middle School would serve as an example.","S City Television was broadcasting Jiang Cheng again.","Everyone who had access to a television gathered in front of their screens to listen to Jiang Chengâs recommendations for implementing detailed public security regulations.","[Guangxiu District shall be placed under the unified administration of the Tech New District.]","[The following public security regulations shall be implemented:]","[Premeditated murder, including attempted murder: death penalty.]","[Gang rape and rape, including attempted rape: death penalty.]","[For lesser offensesâincluding assault resulting in injury, disturbing the peace, embezzlement, dereliction of duty, and theft of public property, especially essential survival suppliesâflogging shall be imposed according to the severity of the offense.]","[Theft of private property: upon discovery, the stolen goods must be returned twofold, accompanied by a verbal warning. After three accumulated warnings, flogging shall be imposed.]","[Special provision: when the victim is a minor, especially a child under fourteen, the punishment may be escalated without limit.]","The people from the temporary governments in every district were watching the new broadcast.","When they heard this, they looked at one another in dismay.","âEscalated without limit?â","âTheyâre already sentenced to death. How can it be escalated any further?â","Among the crowd gathered around the television at Fourteenth Middle School, a scruffy, unshaven middle-aged man remembered Jiang Chengâs mention of turning someone into a âhuman swineâ and began to tremble.","While everyone was watching the broadcast, he quietly slipped away, stole a suit of armor and a weapon, then climbed over the wall and left the school.","He left of his own accord.","The television showed footage from Fourteenth Middle School. Those who refused to obey the rules were forcibly expelled, while those who tried to kill Jiang Cheng were executed on the spot.","Everyone who had met Jiang Cheng knew about that black cat. Some had only seen it in its feline form; others had seen it take the shape of a leopard.","But regardless of its form, it was always as docile as a pet when it stood beside Jiang Cheng.","Who would have thought that at a single command from Jiang ChengââGoââthe pet could instantly become a ferocious beast that killed without hesitation?","Zheng Junwei of Shilong District said, âI told you she must have some formidable abilities, especially at her age.â","The fire-type superhuman instantly raised a wall of flames to protect himself. He truly did not look weak.","But the black cat, shaped like a leopard, passed through the flames unharmed and killed him with a single strike.","Everyone began asking, âDoes this count as a superpower? What kind is it? Animal control? Has anyone else ever had an ability like that?â","No. This was the first time anyone had seen anything like it.","Jiang Chengâs face appeared on the screen again.","[Given the current circumstances, this is precisely the time to employ severe measures in troubled times.]","[Under the pressure of survival, we do not have the manpower to imprison criminals or reform them through labor.]","[There is a clear line between the death penalty and other forms of punishment. Every person of normal intelligence can understand where that line is.]","[There is no ambiguity.]","[The purpose is not to kill anyone, but to reduce the cost of enforcement and make the deterrent more immediate and obvious.]","[To preserve the survival of the collective, prevent systemic collapse, and deter acts against humanity.]","[Today, the students of Fourteenth Middle School asked me to abandon the school base and let them enter the Tech New District base to live.]","[I refused their request.]","[The Tech New District is currently the largest safe zone. It can indeed still accommodate many more people.]","[But we have never intended for the Tech New District to become an isolated island.]","[Accepting refugees into the Tech New District is only a temporary measure to help the survivors currently under our protection stay alive.]","[We have never intended to give up on this city!]","[Please do not forget: in this city, countless people have risked their lives to exterminate zombies, rescue their fellow citizens, and establish safe zones. They have never done these things so that they could abandon the city and leave it behind!]","[Nor have they done so to carve out their own territories and establish armed fiefdoms!]","[Everyone must remember that our ultimate goal is to reclaim our city, reclaim our homes, and reclaim our lives!]","[To let everyone return to the way things were!]"]},{"number":171,"title":"Chapter 171: 0171","paragraphs":["This time, when the zombie virus broke out, the internet was eerily quiet.","The only posts anyone could see were pleas for help, and there were such posts from almost every major city.","The largest forums were national in scope, so it was clear that, just like the last outbreak, this disaster had spread across the entire country.","Even those well-known forums only saw a new post every now and then.","Someone might ask, âIs anyone still out there?â After a long while, someone else would reply, âIâm in T City. What about you?â","After that, there would be no further word.","It was as though the frantic online chatter during the first outbreakâwhen everyone had been trapped at home and could only contact one another, communicate, and exchange information over the internetâhad all been nothing more than a dream.","Ever since the first disaster began, no information from overseas had appeared online.","The âForeign Newsâ sections on the major news portals had stopped updating as well, and even after the disaster ended, they never resumed.","The news reported by the state was entirely about restoring production and rebuilding the country.","There had been no visits from foreign heads of state, nor had any of the countryâs leaders traveled abroad.","The only mention of foreign affairs came in the form of import and export figures. Judging by the data, all imports and exports had come to a complete halt.","In fact, Jiang Chengâs company had also lost contact with its overseas clients, causing a trade fair that had originally been planned to be canceled and seriously affecting business.","In the past, Mr. Peng might have had to lay off employees just to keep the company running.","But after the disaster, there were hardly any employees left to begin with, so there was no need for layoffs. The company simply limped along as it was.","Usually, the television was left tuned to the national station rather than the local channels.","Deep down, everyone still hoped that the state would have someoneâanyoneâstep forward and tell ordinary citizens, âWeâre still here.â","But that never happened, and little by little, everyoneâs heart sank.","They sometimes switched through the channels from other regions as well, but all they found were prerecorded programs.","The only provincial channels available were satellite TV stations. Those were different from actual local stations.","For example, the city station in S Cityâthe one Jiang Cheng used for livestreams and public announcementsâcould only be received in some nearby areas, such as N City. People in the capital could not watch it.","The phone numbers of government departments in other regions, obtained through the municipal government, went unanswered.","Every so often, one would actually connect, only for the person on the other end to say, âI donât know. We donât know either. Thereâs no one left here!â","They sounded like ordinary people who had simply broken into a government building.","Under such circumstances, once the internet stopped being active as well, it became nearly impossible to know what was happening in other regions.","On September 17, twenty days after the second disaster began, Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo finally agreed to Zeng Qiangâs âfertilizer plan.â","The main reason was that Zeng Qiang had been eating vegetables grown with zombie fertilizer for so many days, and there had still been no signs of mutation.","Another reason was that the fertilizer shortage had become too serious.","There were too many people waiting to be fed. With farming on such a large scale, the soil simply could not keep up.","If it could have, Song Jingshuo would never have wanted to eat food grown with zombie fertilizer.","He was extremely particular. In the past, he had bought organic vegetables even when shopping at the supermarket.","Now, the food really was organic in the truest sense.","They had no shortage of zombie corpses, and zombie bodies were incredibly rich in nutrients. There was more than enough fertilizer to go around.","It was just that the whole idea made people feel a little queasy.","That was why they chose to bury the zombies as fertilizer at night, working overtime after everyone else had gone to sleep.","Of course, everyone knew that the logistics team was using zombies as fertilizer. But as long as they didnât see it with their own eyes, they could continue eating with a clear conscience.","The night air was cool. They mobilized all the earth-type ability users, along with some of the other available labor.","First, they dug sufficiently deep pits at each location, then buried the collected zombie corpses inside.","The key was to dig deep enough. Only then could they prevent the smell and keep maggots from breeding.","The drawback was that if the pits were too deep, surface plants would have trouble absorbing the nutrients. But that didnât matter. This wasnât normal farming to begin with.","During the accelerated growth process, the roots could simply be driven straight down.","Song Jingshuo had tested it. In just a few seconds, the roots reached the zombies below, and the plants suddenly came alive, greedily devouring the nutrients.","The fertilizer was incredibly potent. Small bok choy grew as large as cabbages, while cucumbers became the size of winter melons. The cafeteria staff didnât even know how they were supposed to cook them.","Under these circumstances, everyone held a meeting and decided to release a limited amount of fresh vegetables from time to time to improve peopleâs lives.","Feeding everyone potatoes wasnât meant to deprive anyone. It was simply a way to keep more people alive under limited conditions.","The ultimate goal was still to help everyone survive. They could never afford to lose sight of that.","After much discussion, they decided that cucumbers would be the first vegetable distributed.","The cucumbers were so huge that they could no longer be counted by the piece. They had to be counted individually as âone cucumber.â","Each household received one.","It was too large to carry in oneâs arms without making it difficult to walk, so people had to hoist it onto their shoulders and carry it home.","The cafeteria ladies had developed a soybean paste as well.","There hadnât been enough time for it to ferment properly, so it wasnât traditional bean paste. Still, the ladies had done their best.","Song Jingshuo also tried to provide various seasonings, including scallions, ginger, garlic, chili peppers, and peanuts.","In the end, they managed to produce a sauce that tasted pretty good, especially when mixed into mashed potatoes.","The sauce immediately became the best-selling item. Everyone rushed to exchange performance points for it.","The cafeteria ladies who had worked so hard were rewarded with performance points as well, and their lives became rather comfortable.","Jiang Cheng also discussed the use of zombies as fertilizer with the heads of each district.","The method could effectively encourage every district to clear the zombies from its streets.","The areas around human settlements would naturally be cleared first. Even the zombies killed around No. 14 Middle School had been buried.","But many zombies killed by the blade vehicles along the roads outside the settlements had simply been left behind in the city streets, where they rotted and bred maggots.","S City had once been a model city for civilization and sanitation. Now, large swarms of rats could already be seen.","Some people in smaller safe zones couldnât obtain meat and had even begun catching rats to eat.","The potential health risks were enormous.","Most of the settlements in each district were located in residential areas.","Wherever residential buildings were densely packed, there were usually several small parks or green belts nearby.","If zombie corpses were used as fertilizer, these areas could be developed into food-growing zones, dramatically increasing food production.","The urban environment could be cleaned up at the same time.","Over the past few days, cars other than those belonging to the provisional government had occasionally begun appearing on the city streets.","Many belonged to small safe zones established by small groups of survivors. When they saw vehicles from the provisional government, they would pull over and wave hello.","People from the Technology New District had asked these survivors whether they wanted to move there or seek refuge in a larger safe zone, such as No. 14 Middle School.","Many had refused.","They said that although their safe zones were small, they had everything they needed. There were usually several ability users among them, and they had the means to find food and protect themselves.","They had already developed a sense of security and a dependence on their own communities, and they didnât want to move to an unfamiliar place.","The people from the Technology New District did not pressure them. They only asked them to stay in contact and seek help from the provisional government if necessary.","The same situation was unfolding in every district.","Like wild seedlings sprouting from wasteland.","Although many parts of the city were still crawling with zombies, life had gradually begun to return.","The vitality of humanity was truly astonishing.","By the end of September, the city looked completely different.","On the main roads, only a scattering of zombies could occasionally be seen.","There were occasional cars on the streets, but there were still no pedestrians in sight.","The entire New Technology District had taken in more than forty thousand refugees.","To solve the problem of feeding so many extra people, Culture Park in the New Technology District had been completely transformed into a food-production base.","The base mainly grew staple crops such as potatoes, sweet potatoes, corn, and soybeans. It also produced a few basic vegetables, including cucumbers, eggplants, and yardlong beans.","More delicate vegetables were still grown within the residential compounds of the Youth Apartments.","The daily consumption was staggering.","The zombiesâ conversion into compost had made an enormous contribution.","Zeng Qiang was truly a great benefactor.","After Jiang Cheng announced the New Technology Districtâs Disaster-Time Public Security Management Measures on television, the district chiefs from the various areas called her one after another.","Jiang Cheng not only kept in contact with those district chiefs; through her efforts, the chiefs also established contact with one another, especially those from neighboring districts that shared borders.","The so-called âdistrictsâ were administrative divisions from the old days, but in reality, their boundaries were no longer particularly strict. One could even say that there were no boundaries at all.","They were simply groups of the strongest and most principled people in each administrative area, raising the banner and doing their best to save everyone nearby whom they could reach.","Because they agreed with Jiang Cheng and the New Technology Districtâs principles, they too had stepped forward under the influence of Jiang Cheng and the New Technology District.","Shared beliefs brought them closer together.","Especially after Jiang Chengâs speech on the sixteenth, contact between the districts grew even tighter. They helped one another and exchanged supplies.","On several occasions, the New Technology District had been invited to join other districts in hunting down difficult-to-kill mutants.","The most difficult of all was Binhe Sports School.","Binhe Sports School was located in Changxing District. The Changxing District provisional government had lost quite a few people trying to eliminate the dangerous mutated zombies inside.","Since the invention of protective armor, it had become rare for so many combat personnel to be lost at once while fighting zombies in armor.","It was truly heartbreaking.","The sports school contained a great many super-speed zombies. Their speed was comparable to that of wind-type superpowered individuals.","Changxing District had no choice but to ask the New Technology District for assistance.","The people from the New Technology District arrived, and Zhou Wang and Brother Dong went inside to investigate. They nearly failed to make it back out, which gave them quite a fright.","Little Huang was already unable to hold on mentally once he reached the street outside the sports school. His speed was only ordinary, and against such a large number of super-speed zombies, there was practically nowhere he could dodge. Every path was a dead end; there was no way out.","They sent Mo Li inside. Mo Li was not afraid of those creatures and could keep up with them.","However, the zombies knew how to hide and flee. There were too many of them, they were too fast, and they also knew that Mo Li was dangerous, so they avoided confronting her head-on.","Mo Li made one circuit inside and managed to drag only a dozen or so of them out.","The people from the two districts met up and discussed the situation.","Zhao Yi analyzed it. âJudging from the way they avoided Mo Li, they seem to be highly organized. I suspect thereâs a psychic-control-type zombie in there.â","Director Guo from the television station had been able to control other zombies with his mental power.","Although they had never encountered a second one afterward, that didnât mean another one couldnât exist.","Everyone held a meeting, pooling their ideas and brainstorming a battle plan.","In the end, they settled on one strategy: slowing them down.","They contacted the other districts, and in the end, nearly all the electricity-type superpowered individuals in the city were assembled. Gao Yuxuan held a briefing for everyone and explained the battle strategy.","As for the armor, they had originally planned to have the combat personnel wear full-body armor. But full-body armor was troublesome to manufacture and made movement less agile.","Mr. Xu reminded Cui Haiyang of the âpen holdersâ they had used during their escape back then. In the end, they adopted pen-holder-style armor.","They found many office chairs in the nearby office buildings and removed the wheels to use with the pen-holder armor.","This time, there was one pen holder for each person, with four wheels on the bottom. Movement was fairly smooth.","Once everyone was equipped, the electricity-type superpowered individuals began entering the school.","Sure enough, with Mo Li absent, the cunning zombies emerged as soon as they saw that those entering were all human.","Each one was as fast as lightning.","But on this planet, humans had always been the most cunning of all."]},{"number":172,"title":"Chapter 172: 0172","paragraphs":["In the eyes of the zombies, these were all âpeopleââflesh and blood.","Though each of them was wearing a âpen holder,â the zombies still poured out in force.","Many of them were six-foot-plus athletes. They shot over one way, then shot back the other.","They were too fast to see.","At first, there werenât many of them.","The humans wearing pen holders released only weak currents. They sent electricity back and forth, but couldnât hit the athletes who were moving at lightning speed.","After a while, the zombies suddenly began to multiply.","They all came out.","Sure enough, something had been watching from the shadows.","Some of the zombies even toyed with the humans. They darted around at high speed, deliberately ramming into the âpen holdersâ and sending them skidding all over the place.","The entire field was filled with countless blurs.","One of the people inside a âpen holderâ was Gao Yuxuan. He roared, âNow!â","Suddenly, the humans who had only been able to produce weak currents began unleashing their full powerâ","Blue and purple electricity crackled through the air.","The electric-type superpowered people had deliberately spread themselves out. Now, their currents intertwined and converged, forming an entire electrical grid across the area!","The speed zombies seemed to have been hit with a pause button. They writhed and struggled, or simply collapsed to the ground.","Mo Li had been lying in wait on top of the wall.","At last, it was time for him to make his entrance.","The black cat leaped into the air. In an instant, he transformed into a black panther and sprang into the electrical gridâ","He went numb.","Every hair on his body stood on end.","Mo Li: ââ¦â","That was how hard Gao Yuxuan and the other electric-type superpowered people had pushed themselves this time!","Mo Li shook himself and transformed!","His body began to grow enormously!","There. As long as his hide was thick enough and his flesh tough enough, he wouldnât get numb anymore.","The only problem was that he was too big to use his mouth properly.","So he started swatting with his paws. Each swipe could kill several zombies at once.","The only issue was that the zombies died in extremely unpleasant ways.","Everyone had been informed about Mo Liâs situation beforehand, so they were mentally prepared for his transformation.","Although his enlargement had gone beyond their expectations, he was still an allyâs fighting strength. The electric-type superpowered people from the other districts could do little more than exclaim, âHoly crap!â","But watching him swat zombies to deathâespecially zombies that were still standingâwas a little beyond what ordinary people could handle psychologically.","Mostly because it was awful not only to look at, but also because the remains went everywhere!","Liquid! Solid chunks! Bits and pieces! Everything was flying!","The pen holders had ventilation holes. It would have been one thing if the debris had merely smacked against them with a series of rapid thuds, but liquid could pass through the ventilation holes!","That was enough to drive anyone insane!","The zombies on the outskirts began to flee.","They fled as a group. There was no need to guessâeven a glance was enough to tell that someone was directing them.","The electrical grid was withdrawn, and everyone gave chase.","Each âpen holderâ had four casters underneath.","There were also handles inside the âpen holdersâ to keep the occupants from falling when they were hit.","As everyone chased the zombies while wearing their âpen holders,â they soon discovered that if they ran for a short distance first, then grabbed the handles and lifted their feet off the ground, they could glide along.","The superpowered people: ââ¦â","This was fun!","The main force outside received the message Gao Yuxuan sent from within and began entering the campus as well.","They found the electric-type superpowered people in front of a building.","It looked like some kind of gymnasium. There were several gymnasiums on the school grounds, and nobody knew what this particular one was used for.","In any case, after studying it for quite a while, they spotted a faucet and a length of hose nearby.","Gao Yuxuan called out, âJiangbing! Come here!â","And so they began spraying water everywhere.","Under Li Jiangbingâs control, the tap water flowing across the ground moved as if it were alive, worming its way through the gap beneath the main entrance.","Gao Yuxuan urged him from the side, âMore! Put in more!â","Once the water had spread across the entire floor of the building, they would release the electricity and finish off the zombies inside!","But just then, a hoarse, desperate voice rang out from within the building:","âDonât use electricity! Donât use electricity! There are living people in here! Donât use electricity! Iâm inside!â","Everyone was stunned.","When they came to their senses, they began shouting, âOpen the door! We have to save him!â","Hadnât the zombies hidden inside? How could there be a living person in there?","Jiang Cheng suddenly shouted, âEveryone, back away!â","Jiang Cheng had always commanded great respect. When she told them to retreat, everyone did so despite their eagerness to rescue the person.","Jiang Cheng had Li Jiangbing call out, âCan you come out? Weâre about to release the electricity!â","The door opened from the inside, and a middle-aged man staggered out.","âHelp! Help! Theyâre all zombies!â","Jiang Cheng immediately shouted, âHaiyang!â","Cui Haiyang flicked his fingers. The chains shot through the air like a snake and wrapped around the man, binding him tightly from head to toe.","The man fell to the ground.","Everyone raised their weapons toward the open entrance, but no zombies came out.","Jiang Cheng walked over and asked the man lying on the ground, âWhere are the zombies?â","Someone helped the man to his feet. Everyone could now see that he was a middle-aged man who looked fairly strong.","The man said, âInâin there?â","He was still racking his brains for some lie with which to deceive them, but Jiang Cheng had already seen through him.","âYouâre the one controlling the zombies?â","So many zombies had run inside. How could a living person have survived in there?","They had never encountered anything like this before, but simple logic was enough to reach the conclusion: he was the one controlling the zombies.","Upon realizing that he had been exposed, the manâs eyes flashed viciously.","The zombies hiding inside the gymnasium suddenly began roaring. They charged toward the entrance.","Gao Yuxuan shouted, âJiangbing!â","The water on the ground surged rapidly into the gymnasium!","Gao Yuxuan twisted his shoulder. His right hand traced a circular arc from behind him to the front, then slapped down onto the water with a sharp crack.","Electricity shot forward like a snake, traveling along the water!","It looked incredibly cool!","The speed zombies slowed down. With a howl, Mo Li sprang into the gymnasium and began slaughtering them!","Director Yu quietly told Mr. Xu, âDo you know how many times he practiced that?â","The move where Gao Yuxuan twisted his right arm, swung it around in a circle, slapped his palm onto the ground, dropped onto one knee, and swept his left arm up and back in an absurdly cool poseâDirector Yu had seen Gao Yuxuan practice it countless times.","But Director Yu didnât mention that he had secretly practiced it himself as well.","Once all the speed zombies had been eliminated, Changxing District and the Science and Technology New District held a joint trial.","Someone spotted a photograph on the schoolâs bulletin board. The man turned out to be the sports school principal.","Zhao Yi said, âItâs a mental-type superpower.â","The sports school principalâs ability was to control zombies.","When he first discovered this, he had been ecstatic, believing that he could use it to become a tyrant.","What ultimately limited him was the range of his mental power. There was no such thing as a perfect ability. The greatest limitation of this one was distance. Once he was too far away, it became difficult to use.","So the principal made the school his base.","First, he sacrificed all the teachers and students who had survived, turning them into zombies.","Living people would not obey him. Zombies would.","That way, the entire school became a world of zombies.","It wasnât that he had never considered keeping a few of the girls alive. It was simply that the limited control range made them too troublesome to manage.","In the end, he turned them all into zombies.","He was probably the first man in the world to enjoy the company of zombies.","He had already been demoted and sent to work as the principal of a sports school after molesting a female athlete.","A personâs desires, all his life, came down to eating, drinking, relieving himself, and that one other thing.","Even after evolving supernatural abilities, humanity had failed to evolve its soul.","What the principal had done amounted to a crime against humanity.","The two districts carried out a joint execution, broadcasting the entire process live on television.","The death penalty.","On October 2, Yang Xinyan came jogging over to Jiang Cheng. âYou need to look at this text message.â","It had been a long time since they had received a distress message.","By now, nearly everyone who could be rescued from the urban districts had been brought out, while many others had managed to save themselves.","The industrial area in the development zone had also been cleared, and the scattered survivors had all been rescued.","As for the rest, most of them had probably died.","Yang Xinyan was in charge of several communication phones, and they had not received a single distress message for several days.","Jiang Cheng took the phone and looked at the messageâ","[Help us! Jitou Village, Taiping Town! They claim to be the government, â¡â¡ women, seize the food, and burn villagers alive! Theyâre also raising zombies and releasing them to bite people! Help us! Donât call! Iâll delete this message later! Whatever you do, donât call!]","No one knew where Taiping Town was. No one had even heard of it.","Several people took out several maps and searched separately and together until their eyes nearly went blind.","Finally, Su Yu found it. âHere! Here!â","It was practically off the map, in a remote suburban area, and very far away.","Taiping Town consisted of two villages: Jitou Village and Jijiao Village.","After the zombie virus outbreak, some people gained supernatural abilities.","Unfortunately, many of those who acquired such abilities were local thugs and village tyrants.","At first, everyone managed to get along peacefully and worked together to fight the zombies.","But after three or four days, people began muttering, âWhy hasnât the government done anything yet?â","The last time, the government had taken action on the third day.","They kept waiting and waiting, until September 4, when a girl named Jiang Cheng announced on television that the S City government had been completely wiped out.","The people of their xx District established a provisional government of their own.","Two days later, oo District established a government as well.","The government had been wiped out, so they would become the government themselves.","The thugs and gangsters announced on the spot that they were the government.","Naturally, some of the villagers refused to accept it. They were set alight by someone with fire-based supernatural abilities.","The villagers desperately fought the flames and managed to rescue the victim, but most of his body had already suffered severe burns.","The people at the township clinic had all turned into zombies too, so there was no one who could treat him. The man soon died.","When the thugs watched television, they had already noticed that the people in the development zoneâthe ones who had established the earliest governmentâseemed rather fond of meddling in other peopleâs affairs. They had even publicized a rescue hotline.","After burning the man alive, the thugs went from house to house and cut the wires to every television.","They confiscated all the phones.","From then on, they lived in that remote rural area far from the city, bullying men and abusing women as they pleased.","They had never been law-abiding citizens to begin with. During the previous zombie disaster, they had even gotten blood on their hands. They had simply silenced the witnesses, so no one knew what they had done, and no one reported them.","The murderers continued living peacefully.","When the second zombie disaster struck, the murderers became the local emperors of their villages."]},{"number":173,"title":"Chapter 173: 0173","paragraphs":["What do heavenly soldiers and generals look like?","Probably like a convoy of gleaming Blade vehicles traveling all that way for you.","This was the outer suburbs, practically beyond the administrative boundaries of S City and almost touching the neighboring province.","They had to study the map painstakingly to find their way. They must have taken a wrong turn somewhere along the way, since the entire convoy had to reverse.","To arrive before noon, they must have set out at daybreak.","With a thunderous roar, they surrounded the village.","At first, the bullies asked, âWho are you? What are you doing here?â","But when the young woman who frequently appeared on television stepped out of one of the vehicles, the bullies understood.","The footage had been edited off everyone elseâs television, but the televisions in the bulliesâ homes could still receive the broadcasts. They had watched almost every episode.","They had been extremely pleased with themselves for being so clever, cutting off the villageâs channels for receiving and sending information from the very beginning.","But the auntie who cooked for them came and went, and she could see what was happening.","Every time she returned, the auntie told the others. Acting on everyoneâs pleas, she risked stealing a phone while they were eating and sent out that message.","Everyone had assumed they would have to wait desperately, straining their eyes for help.","Who could have guessed that the very next day, a large convoy of silver Blade vehicles would come roaring in?","The village bullies knew perfectly well why the convoy had come. Just two days earlier, this woman had executed a principal.","What that principal had done was not much different from what they had done.","People like that would never surrender meekly.","The interesting thing about them was that every one of them wanted to strike at Jiang Cheng directly, going straight for the head.","Jiang Chengâs face was simply too recognizable. Everyone knew her, and everyone knew that she was the central figure.","There was no need for this battle at all.","Several streaks of purple electricity pierced the air at once. The bulliesâ fireballs, weapons, and bolts of electricity had only just begun to take shape when they were zapped away.","Every one of them collapsed to the ground, convulsing.","When the electricity vanished, Gao Yuxuan blew on the tips of all ten fingers.","There were not actually many genuine village bullies. Six in total. The other seven were lackeys who had followed them because they saw an opportunity to profit.","The bullies with supernatural abilities were dragged up like dead dogs, while the lackeys trembled so violently their legs nearly gave way.","They tried to slip away quietly, but the villagers had suffered at their hands for far too long. How could they possibly let them escape? They rushed forward and grabbed hold of them.","Someone struggled desperately, shouting, âYouâyou people from that new district! What right do you have to interfere? Weâre not under your jurisdiction!â","Jiang Cheng ignored him and announced directly to the villagers, âI am a representative of the provisional governments of the Science and Technology New District and Guangxiu District. These seven are representatives of the provisional governments of the other seven urban districts.â","âThis is joint law enforcement by all eight urban districts of S City.â","âYou may now report what happened to you.â","After receiving the message and confirming the location, Jiang Cheng had contacted the provisional governments of the other seven urban districts and proposed joint law enforcement.","All seven districts had agreed without hesitation.","No single district should be allowed to grow too powerful on its own. Of course, the Science and Technology New District was the strongest in terms of raw power, but when it came to public authority, all the districts should stand on equal footing.","Zheng Junwei especially admired Jiang Cheng for initiating joint law enforcement.","She had not tried to keep all the power in her own hands. Instead, she acknowledged the law-enforcement authority of every district.","That allowed them to restrain one another. If the leader of any district dared to abuse their power, the provisional governments of all the other districts would have the authority to enforce the law against them.","The purpose of deterrence had never been to use it, but to prevent trouble in the first place.","The moment Jiang Cheng finished speaking, a tremendous wave of crying broke out among the crowd.","It was not just one or two people. It was many, many people.","There was no need to go into detail about the bullying, sexual violence, and abuse. The villagers led the enforcement team to the zombie pit.","The pit was nearly three meters deep, filled with a mass of zombies and covered by an iron grating arranged in a grid.","An old man pointed at one of them, crying, âThatâs my son!â","Young men who had resisted the village bullies had been thrown into the pit with the zombies.","More than twenty women had been assaulted, ranging in age from eighteen or nineteen to their thirties.","The perpetrators included all six village bullies and all seven of their lackeysâa total of thirteen people.","The nature of the crimes was exceptionally vile.","All eight district representatives unanimously approved the death penalty.","The villagers asked, âCan we carry out the executions ourselves?â","Their hatred ran too deep.","Everyone agreed.","The thirteen men were beaten to death by the villagers with hoes and iron shovels.","Zhang Lesi had come along as a doctor, and as expected, some villagers needed medical treatment. Jiang Cheng had thought of everything.","Zhang Lesi asked the villagers, âWhy didnât you run?â","This was already the countryside, where the density of zombies was far lower than in the urban areas.","Aunt Pan sighed. âYou city girls donât understand.â","The villagers explained to Zhang Lesi, âHow could we run? If one family fled, several other families would be dragged into it.â","Many people in the village were related. If your family ran, your eldest uncleâs family, your second uncleâs family, and your third auntâs family would all suffer because of it.","Even if an entire clan fled, the neighbors would still be implicated.","In fact, even the village bullies were related to many of the villagers. But being relatives had not spared any of them from the bulliesâ cruelty.","Su Yu murmured, âHow could anyone be so evil? How could they be so evil?â","Aunt Pan said, âThatâs how the countryside is. You young girls must never go to the countryside. You have to go to the big cities instead. The big cities are much better. They have room for people.â","After the executions, the villagers asked Jiang Cheng, âWhat are we supposed to do now?â","Jiang Cheng said, âYouâre too far from us. This distance makes it difficult to manage your affairs. It would be best for you to govern yourselves. Elect a village committee.â","One advantage the countryside had over the cities was that the villagers did not have to worry about their food supply.","Jiang Cheng had one particularly important question. âDo you have any wheat or rice seeds?â","The villagers replied, âWe have wheat. Rice wonât grow here; thatâs a southern crop. We do have upland rice, though. Do you want some?â","Jiang Cheng was overjoyed. âYes! Weâll take all of it!â","A problem that had plagued the Science and Technology New District for a long time had finally been solved: their staple food supply.","In the urban areas, they had only found sweet potatoes, potatoes, and cornâfoods that could barely be considered staples. But genuine staples like rice and flour came from rice plants and wheat, and they had never been able to obtain seeds for either crop.","The villagers each went home and brought out large quantities of seeds for the enforcement team.","âIs this enough? If it isnât, we have more!â","Aunt Pan knew how to farm, so she inspected the seeds. âItâs enough, itâs enough.â","The eight districts divided the seeds among themselves and began the journey back to the city.","Even after the vehicles had gone a long way, the villagers could still be seen gathered at the entrance to the village, waving and wiping away their tears.","Su Yu sighed. âPeople are worse than zombies.â","After leaving the suburbs, they reached the fork in the road leading into the city. Since everyone was heading in different directions, they stopped their vehicles to say goodbye.","When Zheng Junwei shook hands with Jiang Cheng, he said, âJiang Cheng, we should put the formation of a municipal government on the agenda.â","Jiang Cheng nodded. âAll right.â","On the way back, Zhao Yi asked quietly, âAre we going to establish a municipal government?â","But Jiang Cheng said, âLetâs wait and see. Right now, Iâm thinking about resettling the residents.â","The Science and Technology New District had taken in far too many residents. The burden on its food supply was enormous.","Now that the urban environment was gradually becoming safer, Jiang Cheng was considering sending the residents back to their own homes.","If the residents were dispersed among the various districts, the pressure on the Science and Technology New District would be greatly reduced.","But that was only one of the reasons. Whenever Jiang Cheng thought about âestablishing a municipal government,â she always felt that something was off.","Was that really all there was to it?","It looked as though she had won again.","This trial she was being put through still seemed far too easy.","The first time, she had regarded the zombies as her greatest opponents.","But this time, she was gradually coming to realize that the zombies might merely be tools.","The real difficulty lay with people.","She decisively changed course. Rather than doing everything in her power to wipe out the zombies, she focused on solving the problems people were facing as best she could.","If that counted as winning, it still felt a little too easy.","As it turned out, Jiang Chengâs instincts had been right.","Things were never that simple.","And people were very prone to overlooking what was right under their noses.","Every day, they thought about solving all kinds of problems and accomplishing great things, yet neglected the most basic necessities.","That was also because, although they called themselves a âgovernmentâ and were doing some of the things a government was supposed to do, they ultimately were not a real government and lacked experience.","Someone called Yang Xinyan and was connected to Jiang Cheng.","âIs this Jiang Cheng? Weâre from the water treatment plant. We canât hold out much longer.â","Even someone as quick-minded as Jiang Cheng felt her thoughts grind to a halt for several seconds when she heard those words. Her mind rang with a loud roar.","The water treatment plant!","How could she have forgotten something so fundamental?","It was probably because of habit.","When the first zombie crisis broke out, after Vice Mayor Zheng secured control of the situation, he had immediately dispatched people to guarantee basic public services such as water, electricity, gas, and communications.","As a government official, he had naturally possessed access to a great deal of information and had many resources at his disposal, including the forces of the Eastern Military Region and enormous supplies of provisions.","His administration had operated from the top down.","Jiang Cheng was different. The first problem she had faced was survival. She had to leave her home and fight the zombies first.","First the courtyard, then the building. After that, she had to find food and make sure she could stay alive before she could think about anything else.","She had worked from the bottom up.","Working from the bottom up meant surviving first. With no information and no resources, everything had to be done by oneself.","During the early stages of the second zombie disaster, every day had been unbearably hectic. She had either been rescuing people or on her way to rescue them.","The early days of any disaster were always the busiest period for rescue efforts.","Day after day, she had been busy from the moment she opened her eyes in the morning until she closed them at night.","By the time everything had finally fallen into order in the middle and later stages, she was already supporting more than a thousand refugees.","At that point, it was not only Jiang Cheng, but everyoneâincluding the residents and refugees in the Technology New District, as well as the people in all the other provisional governmentsâwho had completely overlooked the basic necessities of life.","The reason was that Vice Mayor Zheng had done such an excellent job safeguarding those necessities the first time around. Water, electricity, and gas had never been cut off. That sense of stability had carried over into this crisis, as though everyone simply assumed that uninterrupted utilities were a matter of course.","Ordinary people were ordinary people in the end. It was difficult for them to imagine how much effort the government had poured into maintaining that âuninterruptedâ service.","And the real government was already gone.","Jiang Cheng was, in the end, only an imitator."]},{"number":174,"title":"Chapter 174: 0174","paragraphs":["Jiang Cheng had no idea why, but there was a roaring noise in her ears.","Her head throbbed as if it were splitting apart.","The people and things around her had blurred into indistinct shapes.","It felt as though there had been an earthquake. She could not shake the sense that the ground was swaying beneath her feet.","But the voice on the phone dragged her back to reality.","âWeâve only got enough coagulant and disinfectant to last another week. If we canât replenish our supplies, the water we produce wonât meet the required standards.â","There had been no earthquake.","Everything around her was perfectly calm. People were doing what they were supposed to do, each of them composed and clear-headed.","Jiang Cheng shook her head to clear it and asked, âMay I ask your name?â","âMy surname is Yu.â","âEngineer Yu, letâs discuss this in person.â","He should not have been called Master Yu. Engineer Yu was the proper title.","The water treatment plant was located on the outskirts of the city, near a reservoirâthe primary source of drinking water for S City.","Jiang Cheng brought her people to meet Engineer Yu. There were only a few workers left, but they had held their posts and managed to keep the water supply running for the public.","âWeâve already been through this once,â Engineer Yu said.","Because they had experienced it before, they had kept the weapons and protective gear issued to them for the later stages of the disaster in order to protect the plant. The relief supplies they had received were also still stored in the warehouse.","This was a critical facility, and Vice Mayor Zheng and Secretary Sun had allocated them a very generous amount of supplies. Whatever had not been used at the time had simply been put into storage. This time, they had not needed to obtain anything from outside.","Engineer Yu and his people had endured one dangerous moment after another: the power system had failed, bearings had overheated, and seals had begun leaking. They had been through it all.","They had survived thanks to this group of technical staff.","Jiang Cheng asked, âWhy didnât you contact us?â","Engineer Yu hesitated, but finally decided to tell her the truth. âWeâre not an ordinary facility. A facility like ours canât just be handed over to anyone. You claim to be the government, butâ¦â","During a crisis, important public-service facilities like theirs might even be placed under military protection.","They could not simply hand everything over to a group of unknown people who claimed to represent the government.","Engineer Yu and the others had been waiting for the real government.","The entire S City government had been wiped out, so they had been waiting for the central government instead.","It was just thatâ¦the central government had never arrived, and now the water treatment plant was about to run out of options.","âIâve tried calling the No. 2 Plant, No. 3 Plant, Beijia Plant, and Datian Plant, but I canât reach any of them. That means weâre probably the only facility still supplying water,â Engineer Yu said. âLuckily, total water consumption has dropped drastically. Otherwise, we wouldnât have been able to keep going.","âIndustrial and commercial water use has stopped completely.","âThe only people still using water are the survivors who remain alive.","âThe population was already reduced by a huge number during the first zombie outbreak. This time, itâs been reduced again.","âThe amount of water the remaining survivors use would barely register on a statistical report under normal circumstances.â","Zhao Yi spoke with Engineer Yu for a while, then knitted his brows, looking deeply troubled.","Jiang Cheng asked, âCanât we procure these things ourselves?â","Coagulant and disinfectant.","There had to be suppliers. The plant would certainly have records showing where to obtain them.","But Zhao Yi rejected the idea. âI disagree, Jiang Cheng. I disagree.â","Jiang Cheng stared at him.","Zhao Yi continued, âThese arenât products sitting neatly, cleanly, and safely packaged on a supermarket shelf. Theyâre chemical agents. Every step, from production and transportation to actual use, has to be carried out by trained professionals. A mistake at any stage could lead to a major disaster.â","Even the drivers who transported chemical products had to undergo special training.","Jiang Cheng respected every one of the technical workers.","She folded one arm across her chest, pressed her fist against her lips, and paced back and forth a few times. Then she looked up and asked, âWhere does the water come from?â","Engineer Yu answered, âS Cityâs drinking water mainly comes from surface water in the Qinzhuang and Qilishan Reservoirs.â","Jiang Cheng asked, âThen if we stop using coagulant and disinfectant and simply supply the water as it is, would that basically make it natural water from the wilderness?â","Zhao Yi and Engineer Yu exchanged a look.","âYou could put it that way,â Zhao Yi said.","Engineer Yu added, âIt would still pass through grates to screen out larger debris and then undergo sedimentation. After standing still for a while, it would contain significantly less mud, sand, insect eggs, and suspended matter than water found in the wild. But from a biological safety perspective, it would still be considered natural water. The bacteria, viruses, algal toxins, and colloidal particles would all remain. None of them would be removed.â","Jiang Cheng asked, âWould it be safe to drink after boiling?â","âIn the absence of any other clean water source,â Engineer Yu said, making sure to add that condition first, âyes.â","âIt just wouldnât taste very good. The earthy, fishy smell couldnât be removed. The water would also turn yellow or green, so the difference in appearance would be obvious.â","Engineer Yu actually wanted to say that long-term consumption was not recommended, but that advice belonged to peaceful times. Given the current situation, people would be grateful for any water they could get.","So Engineer Yu kept silent.","Jiang Cheng said, âThe people in the countryside donât use tap water either, do they?â","At Jitou Village in Taiping Town, she had seen households using hand-pumped wells.","Engineer Yu explained, âThatâs groundwater. Itâs naturally cleaner than surface water, with fewer bacteria and even fewer algae.â","Jiang Cheng said, âBut itâs still natural water. They boil it before drinking.â","Engineer Yu could only nod. âYes.â","Jiang Cheng said, âThen letâs continue supplying water. Weâll skip the step involving coagulant and disinfectant and provide natural water that has undergone only basic physical treatment.â","âThe water in the tap-water system will mainly be used for daily needs: washing clothes, flushing toilets, and growing plants.â","âWeâll consolidate the smaller safe zones as much as possible. At the water-use terminals in the major residential areas, weâll set up storage containers, and water-element ability users can extract purified water for drinking!â","âEngineer Yu, what do you think? Will that work?â","The young woman was clearly not a technical specialist.","But after pacing silently and considering the problem, the solution she proposed and the arrangements she made helped Engineer Yu understand why she was the leader.","The facility Engineer Yu worked for was not an ordinary company. It was a place tied to the livelihood of the entire nation.","He had been keeping an eye on the people appearing on television, but unlike ordinary citizens, he had watched them with caution.","If the television station had still had someone like him holding the fort, when Jiang Cheng and the others arrived, they would not have opened the doors to welcome them. They would have refused them outrightâand might even have resisted with weapons.","But now, looking into the young womanâs calm eyes, Engineer Yu began to place his trust and hopes in this so-called provisional government.","This young woman was genuinely thinking about how to solve problems and how to keep ordinary people alive.","Engineer Yu nodded solemnly. âIt will!â","On the way back, Zhao Yi turned to look at Jiang Cheng several times.","Jiang Cheng kept biting the knuckles of her fingers.","He had never seen her like this before.","Jiang Cheng had always given people the impression of being calm and unflappable. Whenever people saw her, they felt reassured, as though they had someone to rely on.","If the sky fell, Jiang Cheng would be there to hold it up.","What was it that had her brows drawn so tightly together?","Zhao Yi could not help asking, âJiang Cheng, what are you thinking about?â","Jiang Cheng stopped and looked up. âWater, electricity, gas, and communications. Water is taken care of for now, and communications arenât a problem. What about the others?â","Communications were still functioning because, during the previous disaster, the authorities had suspended service cutoffs for unpaid phone bills. Vice Mayor Zheng had later announced that the suspension would be extended for another three months, so that people searching for missing family members would have more time to contact them.","The three months had not yet passed when the second zombie virus emerged. That was why everyone could continue making calls without paying their bills, and their service would not be cut off.","But what about electricity and gas?","Only after meeting Engineer Yu today did she realize that all of this required manual maintenance. If Engineer Yu hadnât led several people in holding the fort day and night, everyone would have run out of water long ago.","[The technology here is so backward.]","The thought flashed through Jiang Chengâs mind.","â¦So, am I from somewhere with highly advanced technology?","Zhao Yi said, âThen we need to contact the power company and the gas company right away and see if thereâs anyone leftââ","Before Zhao Yi could finish, the vehicle suddenly began to shake.","Everyone clearly felt the tremor.","They exclaimed in shock, âWas that an earthquake?â","Jiang Cheng gripped the back of the seat in front of her.","An earthquake?","She had felt a strange tremor when she first received Engineer Yuâs call. But when she came to her senses, it seemed no one else had noticed.","After hanging up, she had even asked, âWas that an earthquake just now?â","The people beside her had replied, âNo.â","But the tremors before her now were undeniably more pronounced, more real.","Everyone felt them.","No one was particularly afraid. City S wasnât located in an earthquake zone, and the occasional tremors it experienced were usually seismic waves traveling over from earthquakes in other regions.","But Jiang Cheng didnât know that this wasnât a real earthquake.","On the western outskirts of the city lay an area surrounded by open wasteland and farmland. Yet at its center stood a sprawling, complex industrial zone.","Tall fences, an intricate network of orange-yellow pipes, enormous filtration and pressure-regulating equipment, and the distinctive spherical gas storage tanks.[Note]","This was the city gate station of the natural-gas company.","It was also known as the cityâs âgas shutoff valve.â","At that moment, the flames shooting into the sky were not even the most terrifying thing. The enormous shock waves exceeded anything a human being could imagine.","One explosion followed another, forming an unbroken chain. The intense heat melted everything in its path.","The main pipelines were filled with high-pressure gas. When a pipeline ruptured, the pressurized gas burst out and ignited, forming a gigantic torch.","In theory, emergency shutoff valves were installed at regular intervals along the pipelines. But monitoring the pressure and remotely closing the valves required human operators.","Now, the technicians who had held their posts at the natural-gas gate stationâpeople like Engineer Yuâhad already been consumed by the flames. No one remained to carry out the shutdown.","The flames raced along the pipelines, spreading rapidly in both directions: upstream along the long-distance high-pressure transmission lines and downstream toward the cityâs gas-consuming terminals.","Inside the vehicle, everyone had just finished saying things like, âWhere exactly was that earthquake?â and âIt feels like it was pretty close. Could it have been over by City N?â when they heard explosions approaching from a distance.","Everyone turned to look.","Manhole covers shot into the air as flames erupted from underground.","The glass windows of shops shattered.","Cars parked along the street were sent tumbling.","Bang! Bang! Bang! Bang! Bang! Bang!","The explosions came in a continuous chain, spreading along the pipelines in every direction throughout the city!","Red light reflected off the windows and burned itself onto everyoneâs retinas.","Before they even had time to react, the world turned upside down.","Impact. Agony. Vertigo.","Zhao Yi gasped desperately, using every ounce of strength to try to crawl out. But the vehicle had overturned, and he was wedged helplessly between the seats.","Fortunately, it was standard procedure for a metal-element superpowered individual to travel with the group.","Jiang Cheng had brought several key personnel with her today.","Wu Jiancheng and Cui Haiyang were both in the vehicle.","Enduring the excruciating pain of his injuries, Cui Haiyang tore open the metal body of the vehicle and released the metal locking the seats in place. He shouted hoarsely, âGet out! Hurry!â","Li Jiangbing was the first to crawl out. He immediately turned around and began pulling the others free, one after another.","Those who had already escaped turned back to pull out the people still trapped inside.","Only a few seconds after the last person crawled out, the vehicle exploded.","At that critical moment, Wu Jiancheng reached out and took control of the flames. The fire roared, burning backward in defiance of the laws of physicsâthen abruptly went out.","No one was burned.","Zhao Yi collapsed onto the ground, completely drained, and began gasping for breath.","His forehead had struck something, and blood blurred his vision.","When he tilted his head back, he saw Jiang Cheng upside down through the red haze of blood.","Zhao Yi struggled to roll over. The world righted itselfâand Jiang Cheng righted herself with it.","Years later, even on his deathbed, Zhao Yi would never forget what he saw.","Jiang Cheng stood there, blood streaked across her face, forcing herself upright as she faced the city engulfed in flames.","In the distance, explosions continued without a momentâs pause.","In the firelight, Jiang Cheng smiled.","Her smile was filled with mockery.","Because Jiang Cheng knew that all of this had happened because of Zheng Junwei.","Zheng Junwei should never have said those words.","âGodâ was watching.","âGodâ was listening.","âGodâ was smiling.","Zheng Junwei had said that Jiang Cheng ought to consider establishing a municipal government.","âGodâ had heard him.","âGodâ had made His move.","The difficulty level had just gone up.","[Note: The water-treatment technology mentioned here was based on information found online.]"]},{"number":175,"title":"Chapter 175: 0175","paragraphs":["No one knew when the sky had clouded over. The clouds should have been layered thickly overhead, but the entire city was burning, twisting and warping the sky above it.","The clouds were tinged purple.","But no one noticed.","The first time, no one knew what was about to happen. No one paid attention.","The second time, after hearing Jiang Chengâs explanation, everyone tried to recall what they had seen. Even so, most people only remembered that it seemed to have been cloudy. It was difficult to remember something you had never noticed in the first place.","This was the third time. The sky had turned purple again, and still no one noticed.","There were explosions and fires everywhere.","Ten minutes after the gas station exploded, the main upstream pipeline chain-reacted and blew up.","Thirty minutes later, the explosions reached the cityâs medium-pressure gas network. The moment someone using the gas turned on a flame, it triggered another blast.","The Youth Apartments in the High-Tech District.","After the last incident, when a burst water pipe had left everyone scrambling because no one knew where the main shutoff valve was, Song Jingshuo had urged Manager Wang to produce the complexâs blueprints. He had then handed them over to several people with civil-engineering experience so they could identify the key valves in every system.","When the apartment complex exploded, Song Jingshuo realized that the natural-gas pipelines had gone wrong. He immediately shouted, âShut off the valves! Shut off the valvesâ!â","Someone sprinted off to do it!","The clubhouse cafeteria exploded. The cook, a big man whose food had always been delicious, died on the spot. So did a woman who had come over from High-Tech Middle School.","Fortunately, fire-type ability users made up the largest group among all the superpowered people.","The fire users rushed forward to put out the flames. Zhang Lesi plunged into the smoke before it had even cleared and rescued the remaining injured women.","When the women opened their eyes, they were dazed. The explosion had rattled their minds senseless. They could not speak, only gasp for breath.","The special nature of the Youth Apartments revealed itself once again. Everyone ate at the cafeteria; no one cooked in their own homes.","As a result, the buildings remained safe.","The moment Song Jingshuo realized this, he immediately ordered, âGo next door! Go next door and help!â","The neighboring complexesâAuspicious Garden and Imperial Scenery Gardenâwere now packed with refugees.","Many of them had been cooking. It was not yet dinnertime, but the cafeteria had begun using its stoves early because it had so much food to prepare.","There was no guarantee that no one in the neighboring complexes had started cooking early as well.","With fewer missions outside the compounds, people had gradually settled into staying indoors.","Large numbers of fire-type ability users rushed toward the neighboring complexes.","Several manhole covers on Auspicious West Street had blown off, flames shooting upward from underground.","People with civil-engineering backgrounds shouted, âEarth types and metal types! Cut off the underground pipelines! Cut them offâ!â","Without the blueprints, there was no way to know where the valves on the streetâs medium-pressure gas lines were. The best solution was to sever the pipelines with their abilities.","Song Jingshuo heard them and immediately called the leaders of the other districts. The instant someone answered, he gave the same concise order:","âEarth and metal typesâsever the underground gas pipelines!â","The entire city exploded.","Flames consumed the city.","Then, all of a sudden, someone told you what to do.","The people answering the calls did not even have time to see who was calling. They were already shouting, âCut off the underground pipelines! Earth types! Metal types! Cut off the underground pipelinesâ!â","Sure enough, several floors of Auspicious Garden exploded. Some residents had started cooking early.","Especially after outside missions had become scarce, many peopleâs schedules had fallen apart. They slept until late in the day before getting up.","Their mealtimes had become irregular too. It was afternoon nowâperhaps they were making lunch.","That was exactly what had happened.","Mr. Xu and his group had fallen into an erratic routine. They were making lunch.","The kitchen of the apartment where they were cooking exploded.","A human torch came staggering out, screaming horribly.","Only after everyone worked together to put out the flames did they discover that it was Tao Xiaoxiao.","Someone shouted, âSister Wu is still inside! Old Zhao! Old Qin!â","They had a large group, occupying several apartments on the same floor.","Sister Wu and Tao Xiaoxiao had just finished chatting with them in another apartment and gotten up to leave. Sister Wu had said she was going to check on the kitchen. Tao Xiaoxiao, tempted by the smell of food, had followed her.","They had only been gone a moment when the explosion happened!","Everyone panicked. They soaked blankets with water, and several people wrapped themselves in the wet blankets before charging inside.","After a while, they carried someone out together. It was Sister Wu, burned so badly that smoke was still rising from her body.","âOld Zhao and Old Qin are gone!â","Mr. Xu had no time to grieve. He bellowed, âMove! Weâre taking them to Zhang Lesi!â","Mr. Xu carried one injured woman on his back, while Director Yu carried the other. Together, they rushed downstairs.","Mr. Xu was a muscular man to begin with. Director Yu had followed the team up and down stairs every day, not only slimming down but also building up considerable strength in his legs.","Together, they carried their two injured female colleagues downstairs.","Clearly, the Youth Apartments had once again acted faster. The moment they rushed out of the building, they saw many familiar faces charging over from that direction.","Mr. Xu shouted, âWhereâs Zhang Lesi?â","One of the fire-type ability users running ahead called back, âBehind us!â","Then he continued forward and rushed upstairs to put out the fire.","Zhang Lesi was running behind them.","Mr. Xu ran toward her, while Zhang Lesi ran toward him. As they approached, she shouted, âPut them downâ!â","Everyone hurriedly laid the injured women on the ground.","Wu Yan and Tao Xiaoxiao were burned beyond recognition, barely clinging to life.","It did not matter. As long as they still had a breath left in them, Zhang Lesi could drag them back from deathâs door!","Zhang Lesi dropped to her knees between them and pressed one hand against each woman.","The charred skin began to repair and regenerate before everyoneâs eyes, as if by a miracle.","Why did such a miracle exist in this world?","No one had time to think about it. They could only regard it as a miracle.","Wu Yanâs eyelids had just begun to move when Zhou Wang shouted from nearby, âZhang Lesiâ!â","Zhang Lesi looked up.","Zhou Wang and Brother Dong had already rushed over like afterimages, tossed two people whose bodies were still steaming and smelled of roasted meat onto the ground before her, and then sped away like the wind.","Every second counted. Saving people was what mattered.","Zhang Lesiâs superpower consisted of diagnosis and external-injury treatment.","She most often used her diagnostic ability, examining people day after day as if she were clocking in for work.","Her external-injury treatment could only be used on a living organism that was still alive when it was injured. She had tested it on frozen pork from the cafeteria, but it had not worked. The subject had to be alive.","Diagnosis was an ability that functioned almost passively. Using it consumed very little energy. After examining one person, she only needed to take a drink of water and catch her breath before she could recover.","Zhang Lesi had never used her healing ability at such an intense rate before.","People kept bringing the injured to her. Others dragged away those she had already saved, people who were still dazed and confused.","After healing one person, Zhang Lesi crawled on her knees toward the next.","She did not look at their faces or even check who they were. She relied only on the sensations transmitted through her palms:","About to dieâwonât dieâalmost thereâhealedânext!","Blood began to trickle from Zhang Lesiâs nose. Her eardrums throbbed as if pierced by needles, and it felt as though her eyeballs were about to burst.","And inside her mind, the source of her superpower was churning and boiling!","I can still save people!","I can save even more!","Iâ","I canâ!","Amid the shocked cries of those around her, two sprays of blood burst outward.","Zhang Lesiâs eyeballs exploded.","No one knew that the source of the superpower in Zhang Lesiâs mind had contracted to its absolute limit before rapidly expanding again.","Only Su Yu had experienced something similar.","But Zhang Lesiâs condition was far more dangerous.","She was far luckier than the metal-type superpowered individual who had died at the military camp during the second outbreak of the zombie virus.","She had possessed her superpower for a month already, and her frequent use of it had allowed her body to become completely attuned to it. When she pushed past the safety limit, the foundation of her physical body was able to withstand the power sourceâs eruption.","âConnect them! Connect themâ!â","There were countless sounds in her ears: explosions, screams of terror, sobs, and footsteps.","Zhang Lesiâs face was covered in blood, and she couldnât see a thing. But with one hand pressed against each of two injured people, she sensed the presence of three peopleâone of the injured people had pressed against another victim waiting nearby for treatment!","Zhang Lesi shouted hoarsely, âMake them touch! Make their bodies connectââ","Many people were still too shocked by the sight of Zhang Lesiâs eyeballs bursting to react.","Mr. Xu and Director Yu were the first to understand!","They rushed over and pushed and dragged the injured people scattered across the floor closer together. âConnect their bodies! She wants to treat them all at once!â","The employees sprang into action!","There was strength in numbers.","In Zhang Lesiâs perception, countless living beings appeared.","The superpower that had just erupted within her surged outward like a tidal wave. It traveled through the bodies pressed tightly together, through every patch of contacting skin, passing into every person and every cell!","More injured people were constantly added to the chain, while others beside her were carried away and replaced.","In the end, Zhang Lesi knew nothing more.","Just before she passed out, the only thing she remembered was repairing the last damaged cell.","She had told them she could do it!","All across the city, fires were raging.","Manhole covers lay scattered everywhere, while flames shot up from the open shafts.","The fires caught the cars parked along the roads, and the vehicles exploded in turn.","Some cars had alarms installed. When falling manhole covers struck them, they began emitting shrill alarms.","The zombies in the city were drawn toward the noise and charged into the flames, their burning bodies clearing the streets instead.","On the road, Jiang Cheng bent over, bracing her hands on her knees as she gasped for breath.","She turned her head and saw Zhao Yi lying on the ground, staring at her in a daze.","He had seen her lose control of her emotions just now, hadnât he?","She had been so furious that she had actually laughed.","Jiang Cheng walked over and held out her hand to Zhao Yi.","Zhao Yi pulled himself to his feet with her help, and then he looked up at the sky.","âJiang Chengâ¦ is that what you meant by purple?â he asked.","âProbably,â Jiang Cheng said.","Because Jiang Cheng wasnât sure what this celestial omen meant either.","Did it mean that someone among them was going to turn into a zombie again?","She didnât think so.","Reusing the same trick over and over was pointless.","If that was what it intended, then âGodâ was underestimating her far too much.","âIs everyone all right? Is everyone here?â Jiang Cheng asked, looking at the group.","Li Jiangbing was sitting on the ground, panting as well. âEveryoneâs here. Everyoneâs here.â","But after scanning the group once, Jiang Cheng suddenly asked, âWhereâs Mo Li?â"]},{"number":176,"title":"Chapter 176: 0176","paragraphs":["Mo Li had actually been feeling unwell since that morning.","He was a cat, so of course he couldnât say what was wrong. He didnât even have any concept of expressing that he felt unwell.","Cats had an astonishing tolerance for discomfort.","When Jiang Cheng was about to head out, Mo Li still followed her as usual despite feeling sick.","There was nothing dangerous about this trip.","There were occasionally zombies wandering along the roadside, but these days, even humans wearing armor no longer considered them much of a threat.","On the way back, Mo Li felt even worse. His head was heavy and foggy.","When Li Jiangbing teased him, he didnât respond.","Li Jiangbing even said, âSleeping in broad daylight? Thatâs all you know how to do.â","What did he know? Cats were supposed to sleep more and bask in the sun during the day!","Mo Li was groggy. He wanted to swat Li Jiangbing with a paw, but he couldnât even lift one.","When the first âearthquakeâ struck, he was the first of them all to realize that something was wrong.","He wanted to warn Jiang Cheng, but he couldnât open his mouth.","Then the vehicle overturned. Explosions spread, and heat rushed in from every direction.","All the humans got out of the vehicle.","Mo Li did not.","He was still trapped beneath it.","Actually, he wasnât really crushed. For a small cat, there was plenty of room beneath the vehicle.","He simply couldnât move. He wanted to unleash his strength, but it seemed he was just a tiny bit short.","The vehicle exploded.","It was warm and comfortable. His fur spread open, greedily absorbing the heat.","His body seemed to be growing.","He hated Wu Jiancheng for putting out the fire so quickly.","Because of that, Mo Li had to curl up and stretch beneath the vehicle, allowing the energy to seep through his entire body. Only after quite a while did he finally feel completely relaxed and refreshed.","That was when he heard everyone shouting, âMo Liâ!â and âMo Li, where are youâ?â","Iâm right here.","âCould he have been thrown out through a window when the vehicle overturned?â","No, Iâm right here.","âHe couldnât have been. Mo Li is so strong.â","Thatâs right. Iâm very strong.","â¦","â¦","Why could he suddenly understand everything they were saying?","Mo Li slowly opened his eyes. Through a gap, he could see everyoneâs shoes moving around.","Yes, he could understand every word perfectly.","It wasnât like Jiang Chengâs telepathy.","Nor was it merely recognizing simple sounds and actions.","He could understand everythingâclearly and completely.","âMo Li~â","âMo Liââ","Everyone was still calling for him.","Jiang Cheng was also calling out to him through telepathy.","[Mo Li, where are you?]","Mo Li replied through telepathy, [Under the vehicle.]","Jiang Cheng froze, then spun around. âMo Li is under the vehicle!â","Li Jiangbing cried out in alarm. âWas he hurt? Cui Haiyang! Cui Haiyang!â","Why call Cui Haiyang? I can get out by myself.","Mo Li tried to push the vehicle up with his head, but it didnât feel quite right. Without thinking, he raised both front paws and braced them against the underside of the vehicle. Then he exerted his strength and lifted it.","Li Jiangbing called for Cui Haiyang. Cui Haiyang came jogging over, intending to break the vehicle apart and find Mo Li.","Before he could even touch the vehicle, it suddenly shifted.","âWait!â","Cui Haiyang took a step back.","âItâs Mo Li, right?â","âIt has to be!â","They had been driving a sixteen-seat minibus that day.","The vehicle weighed roughly three and a half to four tons.","Aside from Mo Li, they couldnât think of anyone who could possibly lift it.","Sure enough, Mo Li was beneath the vehicle.","And sure enough, he was unharmed.","After all, he was that strong.","Everyone took another step back and waited for Mo Li to grow larger, lift the vehicle, and crawl out on his own.","The several-ton vehicle rose into the air.","Mo Li could see everyone clearly now. He knew every single one of them so well.","Whenever they approached him, he didnât even need to distinguish their scents. Just by listening to their footsteps, he could tell who was who.","He called out to the person most important to him.","âJiang Cheng.â","But Jiang Cheng didnât answer.","She stared at him without even blinking.","Everyone else was doing the same, staring at him without blinking.","It was as though they had forgotten the flames filling the street and the explosions in the distance that popped like firecrackers.","They could see nothing but him.","What was going on?","Mo Li suddenly exerted himself and flung the vehicle behind him. With a thunderous crash, it sent shards of debris and clouds of dust flying.","He habitually wanted to lick his paw, but what he saw instead was a handâsnow-white skin, sharply defined knuckles, and long, slender fingers.","Mo Li froze.","He lifted his other paw. It was a hand too.","Only then did Mo Li realize that he was standing upright on his hind legs, just like Jiang Cheng and the others.","He seemed to have gained a new transformation form.","He had to show Jiang Cheng right away.","âJiang Cheng!â he called happily, running toward her.","âHoly crap, stop!â","Li Jiangbing was finally the first to recover from his shock. He hurried forward to block the completely naked pervert.","âStop! Thereâs a woman here! Holy crap!â","Li Jiangbing quickly stripped off his shirt, bent down, and tied it around the young manâs waist. He even pulled it down carefully, afraid it might expose anything that shouldnât be exposed.","Then he took a step back and stared at the stranger who seemed to have appeared out of nowhere.","In fact, Jiang Cheng was the only woman there that day.","Zhang Lesi was a doctor and had to stay home to see patients, so she rarely went out with them.","Su Yu was taking her turn looking after the little ones.","The group was smaller than usual that day, but according to the principle of the Five Elements, each element was supposed to have one superpowered person accompanying Jiang Cheng. Zhao Yi, being a technical specialist, had to go with them, so Aunt Pan, who had earth-based abilities like him, stayed behind.","Gao Yuxuan was stunned. âWho are you? Where did you come from?â","He had asked what everyone else was thinking.","Because standing before them was not the giant version of Mo Li they had imaginedâthe one who had just lifted a vehicle weighing several tons.","The overcast sky lent the scene a bleak air, while the flames on all sides added an eerie quality.","Amid the gloom and strangeness stood a handsome young man.","He appeared to be eighteen or nineteen, at that vague point between boyhood and young adulthood.","Not only was his face delicate and striking, but his shoulders, back, and waist were also perfectly proportioned. His powerful body was nearly flawless, like a sculpture carved from marble.","If they had to pick a flaw, it would be that his skin was too paleâpaler than many girlsâ.","If he had been properly dressed and possessed even a little taste, a young man like this would have looked like a celebrity walking down the street.","But right now, everyone was staring at him as if he were an idiot.","Because what normal person would stand stark naked in the middle of the road, facing the gazes of so many people without the slightest trace of embarrassment?","The only thing covering him was Li Jiangbingâs shirt, wrapped around his waist.","The young manâs eyes were clear. He seemed unable to understand why these familiar people were looking at him like that and keeping their distance.","Fortunately, Jiang Cheng stepped forward.","After studying him for a moment, she walked toward him.","The young man brightened. He opened his arms and hugged Jiang Cheng, draping his entire body over her shoulder. His arms dangled loosely across her back.","Li Jiangbing shouted, âHey, hey, hey, hey!â","Gao Yuxuan was stunned. He turned to look at Zhao Yi, who was also turning toward him.","The two men, connected by an unspoken understanding, both wore expressions of disbelief.","They simultaneously grabbed Li Jiangbing, who was about to charge forward.","Li Jiangbing tried to shake them off. âLet go! That pervertââ","âJiangbing, itâs all right.â Jiang Cheng reached out and hugged the young boy, then gently pushed him away and turned to face everyone. She introduced him: âThis is Mo Li.â","Li Jiangbing froze.","Everyoneâs mouths fell open.","The Technology New District.","The fires in the surrounding area had all been extinguished, including those on the upper floors and around the ground-level pipelines.","Every pipeline that could be shut off had been cut off.","They had also called the heads of several other housing developments. Some metal- and earth-type ability users had already been sent over, cutting off the pipelines as they went. The fire-type users had headed that way to help put out the flames.","There was nothing they could do for those who had already died. Most had been killed instantly in the explosions.","As for the injured, anyone who was carried to Zhang Lesi before taking their last breath had been saved.","Zhang Lesi couldnât move now.","She had given everyone quite a scare this time.","The little ones had first been entrusted to someone else, while Su Yu stayed by her side the entire time.","Things had more or less settled down. Song Jingshuo called Jiang Cheng and briefly explained the situation.","âZhang Lesi is out of danger. Tell Zhao Yi not to worry.â","Then he asked, âHow are you?â","âOur car was blown onto its side, so we found another one,â Jiang Cheng said. âOnly, wellâ¦â","âWhat is it?â","âItâs hard to explain,â Jiang Cheng said. âThereâs a minor situation. Iâll tell you when we get back.â","Half an hour later, Jiang Cheng and the others returned.","Zhao Yi came running over. âWhereâs Lesi?â","âSheâs over there.â Song Jingshuo pointed toward her. âSheâs out of danger now. Donât worryâ¦â","The rest was unnecessary. Zhao Yi had already taken off toward her at a run.","No one dared stay inside the building anymore.","Everyone remained in the courtyard.","Someone carried a mattress out of an empty first-floor apartment for Zhang Lesi to lie on, while someone else brought bedding to cover her.","Aunt Pan built a little shelter with three walls to keep the wind off her.","Su Yu was taking care of her. She had already wiped the blood from Zhang Lesiâs face, but she didnât dare touch her eyes.","Su Yu hadnât gone with them to the neighboring site, so she hadnât seen what happened herself. But she had heard the others talk about it.","She had secretly trained her supernatural ability with great diligence, so she knew very well how painful it was to reach the point where oneâs eyeballs began to hurt.","Almost everyone who trained hard enough stopped at that stage, unable to force themselves any further.","She couldnât imagine what it would feel like for oneâs eyeballs to burst.","Zhao Yi came rushing over. Su Yu hurriedly gave up her place to him and warned him, âDonât touch her eyes.â","Then she stepped away, watching from a distance.","Zhao Yi sat on a small stool and looked at Zhang Lesi, who lay beneath the blankets with her eyes closed.","Zhang Lesi was energetic and bursting with power, and she had always been fiercely proud. Zhao Yi had never seen her this weak, her face pale as gold paper.","He carefully took her hand.","Zhang Lesi moved slightly. Her voice was hoarse. âZhao Yi?â","âItâs me. Do they stillâdoes it still hurt?â","Zhang Lesi grinned with her eyes closed. She didnât answer his question.","Instead, she said, âZhao Yi, Iâm freaking awesome!â","âI know. Youâre awesome, like the heroine of a comic book.â Tears fell as Zhao Yi spoke.","Zhang Lesi mocked him in her hoarse voice. âWhat a crybabyâ¦â","Meanwhile, Song Jingshuo explained the details of the situation to Jiang Cheng again, along with all the measures he had taken and the arrangements he had made.","Jiang Cheng nodded. âItâs lucky you were here. Youâve worked hard.â","At that moment, Song Jingshuo couldnât help shifting his gaze toward the young boy.","âWho is this?â","He was a handsome little guy, but there was something strange about him.","His eyes held a clear, unmistakable innocenceâalmost stupidity.","He wore an iron vest on his upper body and a skirt-like suit of iron armor below.","It was obvious that he wasnât wearing anything beneath the armor.","He was even barefoot, standing directly on the ground.","Jiang Cheng paused. She didnât answer. Instead, she said, âYou two should compare heights and see if youâre about the same.â","As expected, they were nearly the same height.","Jiang Cheng entrusted the boy to him. âFind him two sets of your clothes so he has something to wear for now.â","Li Jiangbing, Gao Yuxuan, and the others returned after checking on Zhang Lesi. They grabbed Song Jingshuo and dragged him away.","âCome on, come on. Letâs find him some clothes first. Weâll tell you who he is later.â","At Song Jingshuoâs house, Cui Haiyang âundressedâ the boy, removing his iron skirt armor.","Li Jiangbing pushed him into the shower, turned on the hot water, and washed him.","The hot water gathered into a whirling column, whooshing as it spun. Li Jiangbing even worked shampoo into the boyâs hair, and after washing it, casually scratched under his chin.","The boy tilted his head back and let him.","The two of them were remarkably at ease with each other.","They wrapped him in a large bath towel and carried him out. Several people then bustled around, helping him put on the clothes Song Jingshuo had found, underwear included.","Once everything had been sorted out, Song Jingshuo sat with one hand on his chin and half his face covered, staring at the bewildered young boy crouched on his sofa. The boy had his knees tucked to his chest, both hands pressed in front of his feet.","Song Jingshuo still couldnât fully process the information he had just received.","âYouâre sayingâ¦ this is Mo Li?â","Song Jingshuo rubbed his face and asked, âHow did you accept this so easily?â","How had they managed to take it so calmly?","A cat had turned into a human.","That made even less sense than a cat turning into a gigantic creature the size of a house.","Actually, everyone had asked Jiang Cheng the same question in the car at the time.","âYou already knew he could turn into a human, didnât you?â","Jiang Cheng denied it. âNo. This should be the first time.â","âThen why are you so calm?â","Jiang Cheng looked out the window and asked in return, âIs there anything left that we canât accept now?â","Outside the window, flames soared into the sky all along the road.","The city was burning.","It looked like a scene from hell.","Compared with that, a little cat turning into a human was nothing at all."]},{"number":177,"title":"Chapter 177: 0177","paragraphs":["Because they were afraid there might be more explosions, no one dared stay upstairs. Everyone gathered on the ground floor.","Jiang Cheng went next door to take a look. Every building bore signs of burning. The exteriors were blackened, and an overwhelming sense of ruin filled the air.","Wu Yan and Tao Xiaoxiao had been rescued, but their spirits had yet to return. Both looked utterly dazed, trembling at the slightest sound.","There were quite a few others like them.","They had all suffered dozens of seconds, even several minutes, of being burned alive while fully conscious.","The pain had temporarily separated their souls from their bodies.","Mr. Xu and the other men found it inconvenient to help, so they carried over a pile of supplies they had pooled together and negotiated with several older women in the neighborhood, asking them to help look after the two girls.","Xiao Dan also came over, helping with tears in her eyes.","The superpowered individuals sent out on missions returned one after another.","The utility pipelines in the Technology New Districtâs residential area had basically all been shut off. The flames shooting from the manholes in the streets gradually weakened before finally going out.","However, on the government-office side, the industrial district across the river was still engulfed in raging flames. Some of the materials piled outside the factories were flammable, and had caught fire.","There were simply too many combustible materials in the entire industrial district. When darkness fell, the flames across the river lit up the sky.","After hearing the reports, Jiang Cheng suddenly remembered that a married couple lived in the western district of the residential areaâand the wife was pregnant.","Zhang Lesi had always said that she had devoured a massive obstetrics and gynecology textbook and was fully prepared to deliver this womanâs baby when the time came.","She went to check on the pregnant woman once a week to make sure that both mother and child were safe.","Jiang Cheng searched through her contacts, found the young coupleâs number, and called.","The phone was turned off.","With a terrible premonition, she sent people over to investigate. Sure enough, in the otherwise empty western district, theirs was the only building on fire. Flames roared as they consumed half the building.","By then, putting out the fire was already meaningless.","The people sent there stood below, craning their necks upward.","They watched as the flames and thick smoke swallowed the building.","When they returned and reported to Jiang Cheng, she could sense how low their morale had fallen.","Dozens of people had already died, but the death of a pregnant woman and an unborn child was more devastating than any of the others.","Everyone had truly been looking forward to that childâs birth.","Jiang Cheng said, âDonât tell Lesi yet.â","Everyone nodded in silence.","The power was gone, and no water came from the taps.","Questions about coagulants and disinfectants no longer mattered.","The water and electricity had simply been cut off.","That made Jiang Chengâs meeting with Engineer Yu seem like a joke.","Engineer Yu called her. âItâs no use. We have to evacuate.â","The explosions had not only destroyed much of the cityâs underground water network; the water treatment plant had also failed to survive the disaster. More than half of its buildings had burned down.","When Engineer Yu called Jiang Cheng, his face was lit orange by the roaring flames.","Some of the technicians were crying.","They had endured so many crises over the course of a month, only for everything to be reduced to ashes in the end.","How weak and helpless humanity was in the face of disaster.","Jiang Cheng consoled Engineer Yu instead. âItâs all right. We still have water-based superpowered individuals. Donât stay there. Come over here. Do you have a vehicle? Can you make it here today? Do you know the way?â","Engineer Yu replied, âWe wonât go today. Weâll find somewhere safe to lie low first. Tomorrow, send a few people who can drive heavy trucks over to take the water tankers away. They should come in handy.â","Of all the bad news, this was the only remotely positive bit. It could hardly even be called good news.","Only after they confirmed that the residential area was safe did everyone gradually return upstairs.","The water, electricity, and gas were all cut off.","Humanity groped its way forward through the darkness, stumbling at every turn.","While everyone else went upstairs to rest, Li Jiangbing and Jiang Cheng could not.","A metal-based superpowered individual quickly made a massive water tank with a faucet.","Late that night, with all the streetlights extinguished, everyone drove to the government offices.","Li Jiangbingâs water-based superpower finally found its most useful purpose.","The nearest natural source of water to the Technology New District was the Bailiang River, which ran alongside the government offices and separated the Technology New Districtâs residential area from the industrial park.","The firelight from the industrial district across the river dyed the water red.","Jiang Cheng released the water containers, and Li Jiangbing raised a hand. The river water immediately began to surge.","A dragon of water soared into the sky. Clean, drinkable water separated itself from the natural river water and flowed into the storage containers on its own.","Everyone had been worried whether Jiang Chengâs storage space could hold so many water tanks. The weight of a single tank was terrifyingâwhat if it burst the space?","As it turned out, their concerns had been completely unnecessary.","Jiang Cheng merely walked over, and the storage tanks vanished one after another.","Those enormous storage tanks.","That tremendous weight.","The capacity of Jiang Chengâs storage space seemed bottomless.","The water tanks were delivered to the various residential compounds overnight as emergency supplies.","Only then could the group finally rest.","When Jiang Cheng returned home, a boy leaped off the bed in the darkness and walked straight up to embrace her.","âJiang Cheng.â","Calling it an embrace was not entirely accurate.","Mo Li did not really understand the concept of âhuggingâ Jiang Cheng. He was actually draping himself over her shoulders, just as he had when he was still a kitten.","But he was now a tall young man standing six foot one.","Jiang Cheng could not support his weight.","She patted his back, signaling for him to stand up straight, and asked, âAre you hungry? Do you want something to eat?â","All the cat food and litter they had prepared at home had gone to waste.","Mo Li had barely touched either of them over the past few months. Now that he had taken human form, Jiang Cheng did not know whether he needed to eat human food.","Mo Li said, âIâm not hungry. I just need to bask in the sun.â","When Mo Li had first transformed into a human that day, his speech had still been rather jumbled.","Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo had been busy, so they handed him over to the talkative Gao Yuxuan.","Apparently, choosing the right teacher really did make a difference. By the time Jiang Cheng finished her work and returned, Mo Liâs use of language had already become basically fluent.","Jiang Cheng nodded, lit a candle, and motioned for Mo Li to sit with her on the sofa.","But as soon as she sat down, Mo Li lifted one enormous foot and tried to place it on her thigh, preparing to sprawl across her lap just as he used to.","Jiang Cheng: ââ¦â","He had absolutely no awareness of how large he was now.","Jiang Cheng pushed him away and patted the seat beside her, indicating that he should sit there.","She then had to teach him to sit on his bottom instead of crouching with his knees drawn up and all four limbs pressed against the sofa.","âMo Li,â Jiang Cheng asked, finally voicing the question she most wanted answered. âAre you a transmigrator?â","Mo Li did not reply. He merely looked at her quietly, blinking his dark, shining eyes from time to time.","Jiang Cheng knew then that he had not understood.","When a cat did not understand something, it would not ask questions or respond with another question. It would simply stare quietly at the person who had spoken.","Therefore, even if Mo Li had also transmigrated, he either did not possess human-level intelligence or his memories had been suppressed. He had no understanding of the concept whatsoever.","Although she could not confirm whether he had transmigrated, Jiang Cheng knew that Mo Li was one of a kind.","At least in S City, he was the only one of his kind.","âThen what are you now?â she continued. âA human or a cat?â","Mo Li said, âA human and a cat.â","He had chosen both options.","He was both human and cat.","Jiang Cheng thought for a moment, then ordered, âTry turning back into a cat.â","Song Jingshuoâs designer casual clothes collapsed to the floor, and the handsome, spirited young man instantly shrank into a cat before Jiang Chengâs eyes.","As long as he could transform back, Jiang Cheng could finally breathe a sigh of relief.","Mo Li shrugged off the clothes covering her and nimbly climbed onto Jiang Chengâs lap, curling herself into a round little ball. Content, she went, âMeow~â","Mo Li had realized that being a kitten was the most comfortable form. She could drape herself over Jiang Cheng, snuggle against her whenever she pleased, and generally stick close to her.","Whenever she was in human form, Jiang Cheng never let her do that.","Jiang Cheng had also realized that Mo Li had always been able to freely control the size of her body.","Whenever she went outside, she transformed into the form of a leopard. Clearly, that size was the most suitable for outdoor activity.","After all, when it came to running, the difference between long and short legs was rather significant.","But whenever she was by Jiang Chengâs side, she always maintained the form of a small black cat, specifically so she could perch on Jiang Chengâs shoulders, burrow into her arms, or curl up on her lap at any time.","Kittens just loved cuddling.","And Mo Li loved cuddling with Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng was exhausted today as well.","The fact that the boy could still turn back into a kitten was a comfort to her.","That way, after they washed up and went to bed, she could continue holding the kitten in her arms.","They slept soundly through the night.","â¦","When Jiang Cheng woke the next morning, she discovered that she was being held in the boyâs arms.","As far as Jiang Cheng remembered, the last time she had been held like this was when she was a child.","Oh. That was a memory belonging to the original Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng turned over to face Mo Li.","The kitten had woken up long ago and had been quietly watching her with his eyes open.","Considering that he had refrained from planting his enormous body on her chest, that alone was a huge improvement.","The boy leaned close and sniffed Jiang Chengâs face. After confirming that she was still alive, he happily touched his nose to hers.","That was how a kitten woke a human up.","Except that he was human now too.","After Jiang Cheng got out of bed, the naked young man, completely lacking any sense of shame, tried once again to drape himself over Jiang Chengâs shoulders, only to be firmly rejected.","Jiang Cheng pointed at the clothes on the sofa. âGet dressed. Donât turn back into a cat. Stay like this and put your clothes on. They taught you how to dress yourself, didnât they? Put that down. Underwear first, then trousers.â","Mo Li had been observing all sorts of human behavior for a long time and was not unfamiliar with any of it.","It was just that this was his first time trying these things himself, so he was not quite used to them yet.","Still, human hands were remarkably nimble. After a little instruction, he was able to wash his face and brush his teeth with ease.","Once they were both cleaned up, Jiang Cheng took Mo Li downstairs.","Downstairs, everyone was lining up to draw water from the enormous storage tank that had been set up in the courtyard the previous night.","There were too many people, and the line was moving too slowly. Cui Haiyang had added more taps to the tank. There were taps all the way around it, thirty in total, allowing thirty lines of people to collect water at the same time. Efficiency immediately improved.","The natural gas supply was gone, but the earthen stoves in the courtyard of the Youth Apartments had always been in use, so the transition was seamless.","After enjoying a period of relative leisure, everyone had begun busily working as they had before.","The fire-element ability user had joined the cafeteria team and would probably remain in that position until they found another solution.","Several of the aunties were still recovering from the shock they had suffered. The others who knew how to cook had been called upon in an emergency and were shouldering the heavy responsibility of running the cafeteria.","Su Yu was among them.","The moment Gao Yuxuan saw Jiang Cheng come downstairs, he hurried over to report, âLesiâs eyes have healed, but she still canât see.â","Zhang Lesiâs eyeballs had completely healed. They looked dark, bright, and just as beautiful as before.","But she truly could not see. She was completely blind at present.","âStay calm. Donât panic.â Zhang Lesi was a doctor herself. âIt should be a psychological issue.â","âI know perfectly well that my eyes have healed, but mentally, Iâm still stuck at the moment when I was blind.â","âDonât worry. You should recover after some time.â","She remained calm enough to make fun of herself. âIâve always studied the effects psychological factors can have on the body. But when it actually happens to you, you realize just how completely the conscious and subconscious mind can be separated.â","No one knew how much pain she had suffered in that moment, or how deep her terror had been.","Zhang Lesi had never imagined that one day she would be so frightened that the shock would leave her psychologically blind. She huffed angrily, âIâm pathetic.â","But no one else saw it that way."]},{"number":178,"title":"Chapter 178: 0178","paragraphs":["After breakfast, Jiang Cheng sent people to pick up Engineer Yu and the others, along with the water plantâs water tanker.","Emergency water tankers were meant to provide drinking water during natural disasters, large-scale events, and brief water outages.","Once the tanker returned, transporting water between the residential area and the Bailiang River would be much more convenient. Jiang Cheng would no longer need to go along herself.","The temporary government of the High-Tech New District held a meeting, attended by key personnel from all the communities in the district.","Since June, they had endured two zombie outbreaks. It was the first time they had held a meeting with morale this low.","Everyoneâs eyes looked a little empty.","They were deeply discouraged.","Jiang Cheng glanced around the room and spoke. âFeeling dispirited? That wonât help. We still have to solve the problems in front of us.â","There was no time to be discouraged. Every problem before them was brutally realâfar too real.","The first was the water supply.","There were only three water-type ability users in the entire High-Tech New District.","Gao Yuxuan was holding his laptop.","He turned his head and looked around, then spotted Zhao Yi taking care of Zhang Lesi. Zhang Lesi could no longer see, but she was still attending the meeting as an observer.","Gao Yuxuan turned back and stared blankly at the laptop screen.","He and Zhao Yi had been compiling statistics on the ability users.","Both of them were highly sensitive to data, and they had long known that there seemed to be an underlying balance in the proportions of the various ability types.","They had mentioned it to Song Jingshuo before. Song Jingshuo was even more sensitive to data; he had glanced over their spreadsheet and agreed with them immediately.","At the time, however, all the necessary infrastructure was still functioning, so the pattern had not been especially obvious.","Now that the water, electricity, and gas had all been cut off, the âbalanceâ in the ability-user data suddenly stood out.","Fire, electricity, metal, and earth were the most common types. They were the most ordinary, the most practical.","Wood-type ability users, who were directly connected to everyoneâs ability to fill their stomachs, dropped sharply in number. There were only a precious few of them.","Once the water stopped flowing, they suddenly realized: Why were there so few water-type ability users?","With both water and wood in short supply, Gao Yuxuan could see that line of balance even with his eyes closed.","It kept people alive.","But only barely alive.","The water problem involved far more than drinking.","There was drinking, cooking, and bathingâand one especially crucial matter: flushing toilets.","How could modern toilets function without water?","The situation meant that life with modern toilets would soon be leaving them behind.","That was deeply painful and depressing.","âThen weâll do this.â Jiang Cheng made the final decision. âDrinking water will be supplied centrally. Weâll run a trial first, then decide whether to impose quotas.â","âAll residential communities are to stop using their toilets and switch to dry latrines.â","âSet up communal bathhouses.â","âEstablish centralized cafeterias.â","These measures would address the problems caused by the loss of water and gas.","âThere are still plenty of vacant apartments. Everyone should move downstairs. If necessary, open several communal dormitories on the lower floors.â","This was because without electricity, the lights and elevators could no longer be used. Living on the upper floors had become extremely inconvenient.","Song Jingshuo was one example. He lived more than twenty floors up.","The electricity problem also needed a solution.","Gao Yuxuan raised his hand. âRenxin Hospital.â","To guarantee uninterrupted power for surgeries and intensive care, the hospital had to maintain a continuous electricity supply.","Hospitals usually had diesel generators and battery banks.","Many factories had them as well, but the industrial park had burned too fiercely the previous night. People had already been sent there to assess the situation, but they still did not know whether the fires had gone out.","âDiesel generators?â Jiang Cheng rested a hand against her chin and thought. âBring them over first. Weâll figure out the rest afterward.â","The heavy vehicles all ran on diesel.","The gas stations in the High-Tech New District had already been emptied by their group. Later, when they went into the city, they had found fuel tankers.","Fortunately, the main people still using vehicles were the temporary governments in the various districts. Their consumption was negligible compared with the cityâs total reserves. At least for now, they were not facing an immediate fuel shortage.","Even so, Jiang Cheng asked, âCan the generators be modified? Wind power? Hydropower? Human power? Can the battery banks be charged directly by electricity-type ability users?â","âWeâll have to test all of them,â Gao Yuxuan said. âWind power isnât feasible, and hydropower would be difficult under the circumstances. I have the most confidence in human power.â","Someone said, âDamn, are we going to have to build a human-powered charging array?â","Gao Yuxuan disagreed. âWhy build a human-powered array? There are so many abandoned cars outside. Differential gears, pulleys, rear axlesâwe can dismantle them. There are more than enough. Letâs build one ourselves! As long as we have a single generator, the efficiency will absolutely surpass that of a human-powered array.â","âThe precision requirements are too high.â","âHaiyang, say something! This is your field!â","âI support Yuxuan. We can give it a try. Iâll draw up a design first.â","Jiang Cheng did not interrupt the arguments and discussions among the engineers.","In fact, as the arguments and discussions grew more heated, morale gradually began to recover.","That was a good thing.","In the end, they decided to try building a transmission aggregation system.","After a long discussion, the emptiness had disappeared from everyoneâs eyes. The young people were beginning to regain their natural spark.","When the meeting ended, everyone got busy.","Some tasks had to begin immediatelyâ","The civil engineer quickly sketched out a simple diagram and explained every detail to Aunt Pan.","Since they had no tools for drawing lines on the ground, several people simply separated and stood at the key points to serve as human markers for Aunt Pan.","âAuntie, from there to meâyes, straight across, then turn.â","âDeeper. Wait, let me squat down and try it, to see whether the compartments are far enough apart.â","The metal-type ability users urged them, âHurry up and decide the distances. We need to build the frames.â","The people who had gone to inspect the Bailiang River returned. âItâs still burning. It looks like it wonât stop for several days.â","After considering the matter, they decided not to send the fire-type ability users to put out the flames in the industrial area. Who knew what those factories contained?","âThere are explosions all the time. Itâs too dangerous to go in. Weâll wait for it to burn itself out.â","The generator and battery bank at the hospital were too heavy to move by human strength alone. This was where Jiang Cheng had to step in.","Before leaving, Jiang Cheng searched around the courtyard and found Mo Li.","The handsome young man was squatting on the ground, both hands resting in front of his paws, sitting exactly like a cat.","The little children crowded around him.","âIs that really Mo Li?â","âLook at his eyes!â","âIt is Mo Li!â","The handsome boyâs eyes looked black at first glance, no different from anyone elseâs. But when the sunlight struck them, their green color became visible.","Once the children confirmed that it was Mo Li, they all marveled.","A small hand reached up to touch his head. âMo Li, where did your pointy ears go?â","Mo Li lifted a foot, intending to scratch his ear, but discovered that the bones and joints of his new body were not suited to the movement. So he scratched it with his hand instead. âThey became like this.â","âMo Li, can you still turn into a big cat?â","âYes.â","âCan you still carry us around the courtyard?â","âI can.â","âThen right nowââ","âNot right now.â Jiang Cheng hurried over to stop them.","She told Mo Li, âIf you want to change into cat form, go inside first. And when you change from cat form back into human form, go inside first too. When youâre in human form, you have to put on clothes before seeing anyone. You canât see people while naked.â","Mo Li said, âOh!â","âIâm going out for a while.â","Mo Li made as if to stand, but Jiang Cheng pressed him back down. âStay here and play with everyone. Iâm going to Renxin Hospital.â","There were no zombies left anywhere within the High-Tech New District. It was a clean, safe zone, so Jiang Cheng did not need Mo Li to accompany her.","The little ones had been badly frightened yesterday. Several of them had looked pale with fear.","They had cried when they saw what Zhang Lesi looked like. They all liked Zhang Lesi very much.","Now Mo Li was playing with them, and it was clear that the children were feeling much better.","Cats had always been the best at soothing people.","Interestingly, the thing people had accepted most readily was animals turning into human beings.","But the absence of flush toiletsâand having to use pit latrines in the futureâwas enough to make many people feel as though the sky were falling.","When Engineer Yu arrived at the youth apartments with the technicians, he found the place bustling with activity.","The main framework and pits for the pit latrines had already been completed. The civil engineers and Aunt Pan had finished their work and withdrawn.","The metal-element superpowered people had taken over, starting on the partitions and the flooring around the pits.","The gleaming footboards had been fitted with nonslip ridges, and the doors had bolts.","There were separate menâs and womenâs toilets.","They looked no different from ordinary public restroomsâapart from the fact that they were pit latrines.","This was the most urgent task.","They would build the bathhouse after this was finished.","At the moment, though, everyone was discussing whether to build a boiler themselves or get one from somewhere else.","With Jiang Chengâs storage space, transporting large equipment was unbelievably convenient.","The earthen stove had been expanded and modified further. From now on, it would be the main kitchen.","The fire-element users got the flames going, and the temporary cooks had already begun preparing lunch. The aroma was already wafting through the air.","A huge water tank stood there, with faucets running all the way around it. People kept coming over with cups, bottles, buckets, or kettles to collect water.","A gigantic cat, as huge as an elephant, carried a group of little ones around the courtyard on its back.","It was the same cat they had seen on televisionâand the one they had seen yesterday. But yesterday, it had still looked like an ordinary kitten. Today, they had finally seen it in its giant form.","Song Jingshuo came over and clasped Engineer Yuâs hands in both of his, greeting him solemnly. âThank you for all your hard work over the past month or so!â","Engineer Yu only said, âIt was what we should do.â","Then he added, âAll twelve water trucks have been driven back.â","Song Jingshuo tightened his grip. âThatâs exactly what we need.â","With the water trucks, Jiang Cheng no longer needed to accompany them personally.","The water tanks would not need to be moved either, and they could build several more to increase their storage capacity.","Song Jingshuo said, âThe rooms are ready. Since thereâs no electricity now, weâve prepared rooms on the second floor.â","Engineer Yu had no particular demands. âAs long as theyâre habitable.â","When he went up to see them, he found that the conditions were actually quite good. The youth apartments had originally been fully furnished.","The fashionable young people had also furnished them with decent furniture and appliances.","Several young people helped carry water upstairs for him.","The buckets they had stockpiled through Buy More More were finally proving extremely useful.","Engineer Yu thanked them.","When it was time to eat, someone called him downstairs for a meal.","No matter what happened, people still had to eat.","Engineer Yuâs spirits were somewhat low, but he still had to go downstairs for lunch.","Once he got there, he found that almost everyone was young, and every one of them was eating heartily.","They chatted as they ate.","âLetâs go take a look at the private schools. Arenât they boarding schools? They have dormitories and bathhouses, and usually their own boilers. We can just bring one back.â","âLetâs scout the place first. Once we know what itâs like, weâll report back to Jiang Cheng and go move it together.â","âLetâs hurry. If we canât bathe much longer, Zhang Lesi is going to start yelling at us.â","âHahahahahaha!â","For some reason, Engineer Yu found that he had an appetite after all.","So what if there was no water, electricity, or gas?","Wasnât this simply the way the country had lived several decades ago? Wasnât it the same kind of life he had experienced as a child?","It was nothing serious.","As long as there were people around, that was enough."]},{"number":179,"title":"Chapter 179: 0179","paragraphs":["There was another very serious problem today: the phones had lost their signal.","Right after the explosion yesterday, the signal had still been working. Song Jingshuo had even called the other seven districts, and had spoken with Jiang Cheng as well.","Jiang Cheng had spoken with Engineer Yu.","But today, there was no signal.","No water meant losing the toilets.","No electricity meant losing communications.","The explosions and fires had destroyed a huge number of power lines, causing widespread blackouts across nearly the entire city.","The base stations had gone down too.","Thinking about it now, they were lucky to have contacted Engineer Yu yesterday. Otherwise, getting in touch with him today would have been difficult.","At the same time, everyone realized that this meant every district had become an isolated island.","Jiang Cheng and the others returned after lunch.","As soon as Song Jingshuo saw them, he asked, âDid you get it?â","Jiang Cheng nodded. âWe did.â","A diesel generator and a bank of lead-acid batteries.","Gao Yuxuan and the others had also dismantled all sorts of equipment from here and there, and Jiang Cheng had packed everything up to take back.","It felt like rats raiding a granary.","Song Jingshuo said, âEngineer Yu has already arrived. He had lunch in the cafeteria and is resting now. Jiangbing and the others went to fetch water. Also, these are the locations of the other water plants that Engineer Yu brought with him.â","This was information they needed to share with the other districts.","But sharing anything had become difficult now.","Previously, they had exchanged email addresses. They could still find the electrical-type ability users to charge the computers, but the network was gone.","Jiang Cheng frowned. âWe have to find a way to contact everyone. Also, we need to bring the children from No. 14 Middle School over as soon as possible. How many people do they have there now?â","Song Jingshuo said, âAbout twelve hundred, including students and refugees.â","The biggest problem at No. 14 Middle School was that they had no wood- or water-type ability users.","In mid-September, Jiang Cheng and the others had fought their way into No. 14 Middle School and restored order there. Song Jingshuo had personally taught them how to manage things.","For the following week, someone went there every day to oversee operations, until the children gradually became familiar with the management procedures.","Because they had no wood-type ability users, the Technology New District had continued supplying them with provisions, mainly potatoes.","But now, there was no water, electricity, or gas. The gas was not a serious issue, since fire-type ability users were everywhere. But having no water was truly life-threatening.","âWe have to hurry. They must be in a panic. Letâs go this afternoon.â","âAll right. Iâll make the arrangements. Go say hello to Engineer Yu first.â","Jiang Cheng went to see Engineer Yu. âHave you settled in? Are you getting used to things?â","âItâs great,â Engineer Yu said. âThe steamed buns are delicious. I havenât had buns like these in ages. These days, all you get are those big, snow-white buns, stuffed with whitening agents.â","Jiang Cheng smiled. âWe grew the wheat ourselves and milled it ourselves.â","The wheat seeds had come from Taiping Town.","Gao Yuxuan, Cui Haiyang, and the others had no idea where they had dismantled an electric motor from, then tinkered with it until they had built an electric grain mill.","The flour it produced was yellowish, and the steamed buns made from it were yellowish too.","A group of city kids had made a huge fuss, asking why the steamed buns werenât white.","Aunt Pan had looked down on them for it.","Engineer Yu nodded. âI heard you planted rice too.â","The food supply could now be developed over the long term.","The water problem was also being addressed.","One issue after another in peopleâs daily lives was being resolved.","Even without water, electricity, or gas, their standard of living could still be higher than that of the countryside where he had grown up.","Jiang Cheng chatted with Engineer Yu for a little while, without any particular topic or purpose.","She was doing it purely because of the overwhelming frustration and helplessness Engineer Yu had displayed during their phone call the day before.","She understood that feeling all too well.","Who didnât?","It was just that not everyone could adapt as quickly as Jiang Cheng, adjusting themselves almost immediately.","A few words of casual conversation were simply meant as comfort.","She still had plenty of things waiting to be done, so she got up to leave.","Just as she was about to step out of the room, Engineer Yu suddenly called after her. âJiang Cheng.â","Jiang Cheng turned around.","Engineer Yu said sincerely, âYouâve already done very well.â","Jiang Cheng smiled and nodded. âThank you.â","I know.","Of course Iâve done very well.","Otherwise, why would that person keep raising the stakes again and again, suppressing me again and again, destroying my efforts?","â¦Or was this some kind of perverse amusement?","Was that person some kind of twisted psychopath who enjoyed watching others fail and despair?","Two teams were sent out that afternoon.","One team had only a single vehicle. They went to check on the governments of the other districts, see how everyone was doing, and share whatever information or response measures the Technology New District had with them.","The other team consisted of twelve vehicles and headed straight for No. 14 Middle School.","Driving now required more caution than before, because too many manholes no longer had covers.","Most of those manholes had stopped spewing fire.","But some buildings had already caught fire, and a high-rise could burn for a day or two.","Smoke filled the sky everywhere along the roads. Vehicles lay overturned on the ground. The scene had the atmosphere of an apocalypseâ","There had already been two zombie outbreaks. Only now were people finally beginning to feel as if the end of the world had truly arrived.","The teachers and students of No. 14 Middle School saw the convoy from the Technology New District and reacted as if reinforcements from heaven had arrived.","They cheered and ran toward them.","âYou came!â","âWe knew youâd come!â","âWe couldnât get through on the phones!â","âWe were so worried!â","Jiang Cheng had come in person. The first thing she asked was, âWas anyone injured yesterday?â","The students began to cry.","âThe aunties died.â","âIt exploded all of a sudden.â","âAfter we put out the fire and went inside, they were alreadyâ¦â","Those wonderful women.","From the very beginning, they had wielded huge iron ladles and fought alongside everyone else.","As the number of refugees grew, they had counted the food on their fingers every day, terrified of wasting even a little.","Then one explosion had taken everything.","It was more frightening than zombies. Zombies were no longer frightening at all.","They werenât even afraid of mutated zombies.","But the sudden loss of human life was terrifying.","The complete helplessness of it.","When they saw Jiang Cheng, they could no longer hold back their tears.","The students followed Jiang Chengâs arrangements.","The refugees, however, began buzzing among themselves, and many hesitated.","The main reason was that many of them were unfamiliar with the Technology New District. That was how big cities were. Even though Guangxiu District bordered the Technology New District, many people from Guangxiu District might never have visited it even once.","Jiang Cheng did not force them. âYou can go to another district if you want. These are the base locations for each district. Weâll post them on the wall in a moment. Anyone who doesnât know the exact locations can go and check. Those who want to come with us should start packing now.â","In truth, they did not have much to pack. They already had bedding and toiletries there. They could bring those along, so they would not have to go through the trouble of gathering everything again after arriving in the Technology New District. Things were chaotic enough as it was. Anything that saved them a little effort was worth doing.","Suddenly, two people came running over, shouting Jiang Chengâs name.","âJiang Cheng! Jiang Cheng!â","They were both extremely excited.","âThe staff dormitory has a bathhouse! It has a boiler!â","âLetâs take the boiler with us!â","Jiang Cheng followed them there with several metal-type ability users.","After a great deal of work, they dismantled all the fixtures holding the boiler in place and separated it from the building.","âJiang Cheng, put it away!â","Jiang Cheng stored it. It was an excellent find. They could take it back and use it to build a bathhouse for the residential compound.","She asked, âAre there any other places that might have things like this?â","âA lot of places. Schools, government officesâlarge institutions like that usually have them.â","Jiang Cheng instructed them, âKeep thinking. Whenever you remember something we might be able to use, and that we can actually find, letâs take it all with us.â","Everyone laughed.","Jiang Chengâs practical, down-to-earth attitude was impossible not to appreciate.","In the end, more than eight hundred people were brought back to the Technology New District.","They also ran into three separate groups trying to stop their vehicles on the way.","Each group consisted of a dozen or twenty people who had claimed a place as their base and were living there on their own. There were quite a lot of these small safe zones scattered throughout the urban area.","The city still had plenty of surviving resources, and the area considered safe was steadily expanding. Some people simply refused to attach themselves to a larger group.","But by this point, anyone without a wood-type ability could still survive by searching for food left behind in the city.","Those without a water-type ability, however, could no longer make it.","The vehicles were far too distinctive. Anyone entering or leaving the city had to pass through Guangxiu District, not to mention that this was the only route to and from No. 14 Middle School.","Everyone knew they belonged to the Tech New District, so people stopped them to ask to join.","They accepted them all.","Construction in the Tech New District was proceeding in full swing.","Having water trucks made things much easier.","Every residential compound had added water-storage tanks. For now, the plan was to ensure that each compound had twenty tons of reserve water per day.","They would see whether that was enough and make adjustments later.","At present, the two most urgent tasks in every compound were building toilets and constructing communal kitchens with makeshift wood-burning stoves.","It was no longer possible for every household to cook separately. They could only adopt a communal-cafeteria system.","The more than eight hundred people brought back from No. 14 Middle School were assigned differently.","There were more than three hundred teachers and students. The children had already undergone education and training, and their organization, discipline, and obedience were all much better than those of the adults. In Jiang Chengâs eyes, they were reserve troops.","They were assigned rooms in the Youth Apartments.","As for everyone else, they were given arrangements similar to those made for the refugees before, and distributed among residential compounds that still had room.","The children couldnât sit still. The Youth Apartments were undergoing a major renovation, and they all ran over to watch.","After watching for a while, they began taking part themselves.","Engineer Yu looked at the young people in the Youth Apartments and felt that they were full of vitality.","But in the eyes of the Youth Apartmentsâ residents, the children who had just joined them were the truly energetic ones.","Morale was gradually recovering.","The team that had gone into the city to contact the other administrative districts did not return until nightfall, bringing bad news with them.","âFuyang District has fallen into chaos!â","The leader of Fuyang District was dead.","When a loosely organized group formed spontaneously among ordinary people had yet to establish a sufficiently balanced structure, it sometimes depended entirely on the personal charisma and ability of its leader to hold everyone together.","The groupâs central figure had died in the explosion. Flames had engulfed the city, making it seem like the apocalypse itself.","Peopleâs hearts instantly fell apart, and the collective quickly disintegrated. In just one day, the situation had deteriorated to the point where several factions began fighting over supplies, and blood was being shed.","The people who had returned were deeply shaken. âIt only took one day. One day!â","It was as hard to build something as it was quick to collapse.","Shilong District and Changxing District were both doing fine. Everyone there still appeared to have a strong sense of community, and they had already begun rebuilding on their own.","The people from the Tech New District shared the addresses of their respective waterworks with them, along with various construction plans for the Youth Apartments.","Zheng Junwei of Shilong District asked, âAre you still holding together?â","The people from the Tech New District thought about it, then nodded firmly.","âWe are!â","Zheng Junwei was deeply moved.","âThe people from Changxing District suggest that we use radios to stay in contact from now on. This is the frequency they gave us.â","The returning team handed Jiang Cheng a slip of paper with a series of numbers written on it.","Jiang Cheng asked, âWhere are we supposed to find a radio?â","No one knew.","Jiang Cheng asked, âWould an ordinary radio work?â","At least someone knew the answer to that. âNo. It canât receive amateur radio signalsâthe operating frequencies are different. Ordinary radios generally use the 87â108 MHz band, while amateur radio usually operates between 430 and 440 MHz.â","Jiang Cheng asked, âCan it be modified?â","That would not work either. It would be equivalent to building an entirely new machine by hand.","There was a fundamental hardware gap between a radio receiver and a two-way radio, and there was nowhere to find the necessary components anyway.","Jiang Cheng had no choice but to abandon the idea. âThere has to be somewhere we can find one of these things.â","Just then, Song Jingshuo arrived.","âWhatâs going on?â","Everyone explained the situation to him.","âOh.â Song Jingshuo said, âTake the one out of my car.â","Everyone: ââ¦â","âWhatâs so strange about that?â Song Jingshuo said, both hands in his pockets. âWeâre into off-road driving, and pretty much everyone in that hobby uses radios.â","Great. The rich guy was showing off again."]},{"number":180,"title":"Chapter 180: 0180","paragraphs":["Su Yu moved the little ones to a new place.","The floor they had been living on was far too high. It was unbearable to make the little ones climb so many flights of stairs every day.","A communal dormitory was reopened for them on a lower floor.","The new public toilets had been hastily repaired, and they were already in use by the time Jiang Cheng returned from Renxin Hospital.","Everyone found using them rather miserable.","âWhatever you do, donât look down.â","âUgh.â","Still, it was better than using the toilets in their own homes. There was no water for flushing anymore, and people living on the tenth, fifteenth, or twentieth floors couldnât very well carry buckets upstairs just to flush the toilet.","Using the public toilets disgusted everyone else. Using the toilets at home disgusted only themselves.","Aunt Pan shook her head with a smile, then conducted an experiment.","Afterward, she told Song Jingshuo, âIt worked.â","Song Jingshuo had spent years enjoying outdoor activities, so he was actually quite tolerant of dry latrines. Even so, he sincerely said, âThank you for your hard work.â","Everyone soon discovered that whenever Aunt Pan walked once around the public toilets, the pits inside became much cleaner.","If they saw Aunt Pan walking away from the public toilets with her hands clasped behind her back and heading toward the vegetable fields, they knewâ","Aunt Pan was transporting feces.","Beneath everyoneâs feet, underground, the soil began to churn on its own, coiling around everyoneâs waste like an earthworm and burrowing through the earth until it reached the ground beneath the vegetable fields.","There, it became fertilizer.","The agricultural researchers were full of conflicting emotionsâadmiration one moment, sorrow the next.","âThese supernatural abilities seem to have been designed specifically to help us survive in an environment like this,â Zeng Qiang remarked.","The speaker meant nothing by it, but the listener took it to heart.","Zhao Yi was strolling slowly with Zhang Lesi in his arms. When he heard those words, he turned his head and glanced at Zeng Qiang.","After saving themselves, the temporary governments in each district also mobilized earth- and metal-type ability users to go out into the streets and sever the gas pipelines, putting an end to the underground wells that were spewing flames everywhere.","But in the end, all they could do was cut off the networks around their own bases.","Compared with the city as a whole, the surviving humans were far too few, and the supernatural ability users among them were fewer still.","The fires raging through the rest of the city had already surpassed humanityâs ability to control them.","Humanity had done everything it could, but the entire city continued burning for four days before the flames finally went out completely.","At that point, the key to whether the existing organizations could continue was unexpectedly the presenceâor absenceâof water-type ability users.","Water-type abilities had no combat power and had always been regarded as useless, underwhelming abilities.","Only then did everyone realize how rare water-type ability users actually were.","At a safe settlement, having even one water-type user could solve a major problem.","Unfortunately, neither Chaoqing District, Fuyang District, nor Guangxiu District had a single one.","Guangxiu District was backed by the Science and Technology New District. The people in the small safe points there abandoned their own little shelters one after another and sought refuge in the Science and Technology New District.","The main reason Fuyang District descended into chaos in just one day was that its central figure was gone. Then, when the water shortage arose, conflicts broke out among the people.","What everyone was fighting over when they fought over supplies was bottled water.","The fighting escalated, and the district splintered into pieces.","Chaoqing District fared slightly better than Fuyang District, partly because of its location.","S City had a river to the north and another to the south, while the old city center was encircled by an ancient moat.","Chaoqing District was relatively close to the river south of the city. The people organized themselves to collect river water, let it settle, and boil it before use.","For the moment, at least, they had solved their most urgent water problem.","Over the radio, the districts came back online one after another. At last, they were able to contact one another again instead of remaining isolated islands.","After holding out for several days, Zheng Junwei of Shilong District was the first to take the lead.","âWeâre moving.â","Why had civilizations so often arisen beside water in ancient times?","Because people simply could not survive without it.","Several districts were too far from natural water sources. Even when they managed to obtain water trucks from the municipal waterworks, transporting the water required too much manpower and time.","They also had to consider the future supply of fuel. The cityâs fuel reserves were still sufficient for now, but sooner or later, they would be exhausted.","Each district moved in a different direction.","Some headed for the moat in the old city center.","Others moved south or north, toward the two major rivers.","Tens of thousands of survivors began a mass migration.","They rolled up their quilts, dragged their suitcases, and carried their pots, bowls, and other household goods.","Large buses arrived one after another to pick people up.","The vehicles from the Science and Technology New District also went out to help.","Although their bases had only been home for a month, many people cried when the time came to abandon them and leave.","Someone sobbed, âWhen will this ever end?â","âWeâd finally started getting betterâ¦â","Zheng Junwei also felt dazed when he heard that.","Yes. Things had clearly begun to improve.","There were no more zombies across the vast area surrounding the base.","That girl Jiang Cheng had even begun discussing the return of residents with him. They had talked about converting the green belts in the urban districts into farmland.","He had proposed establishing a municipal government.","He had been full of ambition, dreaming of joining forces with Jiang Cheng to truly manage the city.","How had things suddenly turned out like this?","He turned his head and saw that many buildings had burned into ruins.","The people were fleeing.","Jiang Cheng had once said on television, âWe are not giving up on this city.â","Who could have known that Heaven itself would force them to abandon it?","Zheng Junwei closed his eyes. Everything felt like a dream.","Before Heaven, human abilities and ambitions were as insignificant as ants.","From that point on, S City, as a city, existed in name only. Only the old city center still had a large population of survivors living along the moat.","The base in Chaoqing District remained unchanged.","Every other district abandoned its original base and moved elsewhere.","Because of the water shortage, all the small safe points lost the ability to survive independently. They voluntarily merged with the streams of people and joined the migration.","S City thus became a dying city, barely clinging to life.","The Science and Technology New District, however, was thriving.","The mechanical power aggregation system developed by Gao Yuxuan, Cui Haiyang, and the others had succeeded.","Using automobile rear axles, differentials, and belt pulleys, they combined the strength of many people to drive a single high-power generator.","It was more efficient than a human power array and suffered less energy loss.","Once the fires in the industrial district went out on their own, they went there to search and found several generators and battery banks that could still be used.","In the end, thanks to everyoneâs efforts, every residential compound in the Science and Technology New District acquired its own power-generation and energy-storage equipment.","To make this possible, they collected every bicycle throughout the entire Science and Technology New District.","Since the district was far from the city center, aside from students, not many people there had ridden bicycles. Most residents had commuted to the city by private car or public transportation.","So they had no choice but to enter the city and haul the bicycles back to the Science and Technology New District, carload after carload.","A community the size of Auspicious Home needed three hundred bicycles, with three hundred people pedaling continuously from morning until night to generate electricity.","That allowed them to provide two hours of electricity at night so everyone could have light.","No one could pedal for eight hours a day. Even fitness enthusiasts couldnât manage that.","So having âthree hundred people pedaling at the same timeâ meant that over the course of a day, between one and two thousand people had to take part in power generation.","This solved two major problems for the entire Science and Technology New District: the potential security risks caused by having too much idle labor, and the shortage of jobs.","Back when zombies still roamed everywhere, the most plentiful jobs were in the teams.","As the urban districts grew cleaner, the number of survivors waiting for rescue dwindled, and the population of the resettlement communities increased, a problem began to emerge: too many idle people and too few jobs.","It was only because Jiang Cheng had a harsh temperament and an iron-fisted approach, daring to impose severe penalties in troubled times, that no major public-order problems arose.","In the later stages, executions were almost unheard of.","But flogging was surprisingly common.","The emergence of electricity-generating jobs greatly eased the problem.","People simply couldnât be allowed to sit idle. They needed something to do.","If they had too much free time, they could go pedal bicycles. They would expend energy, generate heat and electricity, earn performance points, and exercise at the same time.","The electricity-generating stations were extremely popular in every community.","Li Jiangbing gave up all his other work and devoted himself entirely to water supply.","Twenty tons of water a day was more than enough for the Youth Apartments if it was used only for drinking, but in the other communities, the supply was somewhat tight.","The Youth Apartments, however, also had extensive vegetable-growing operations.","The park farm likewise required a great deal of water.","And water for drinking wasnât the only concern. There was also water for bathing.","In fact, Li Jiangbing had once pointed out that used bathwater could be purified. It could even be used for drinking.","He had sworn that it would be absolutely clean.","But everyone had strongly objected and shut down the idea.","With water trucks delivering supplies, purifying bathwater wouldnât improve efficiency by much. The whole thing was simply that Li Jiangbing wanted to show off his skills.","Song Jingshuo spent several days getting a clear picture of the actual figures, then established water quotas for every community.","After a trial run, the quotas landed right on the line of âbasicallyâ meeting everyoneâs needs.","A new demand was born.","Every community opened its bathhouses for free two days a week, allowing residents to bathe without charge.","Anyone who wanted to bathe on other days had to pay, using performance points to purchase bath tickets.","Drinking water was rationed as well.","Each person received enough basic drinking water free of charge to meet their essential needs.","Any additional water had to be purchased.","Since there were no elevators, some people even took on odd jobs delivering water upstairs. Business was surprisingly brisk.","Gao Yuxuan also opened a game room in the Youth Apartments, with several televisions and game consoles.","It did not use the public power supply. Instead, electric-type superhumans were hired as living batteries.","The fees were expensive, and customers had to reserve a time slot each day.","Public cafeterias were established in every community, but some people still disliked eating in a large communal dining hall.","Those people could collect ingredients and cook for themselves at small private stoves.","The stoves were rented by the hour, with fire-type superhumans providing the heat.","All kinds of private businesses began to emerge as well.","Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo not only failed to oppose them but actively supported them.","And so, by creating new jobs and new demands, they got people moving of their own accord. A virtuous cycle formed, and a miniature society came alive.","More and more people continued to flee the city and seek refuge there, and the population of the Technology New District kept growing.","But Zhang Lesiâs eyesight still had not returned. Zhao Yi lived with her and took care of her daily needs.","Although Zhang Lesi could no longer see, her other senses had become much sharper. One day, Zhao Yi was simply lying there without making a sound, yet she sensed that something was wrong.","âWhatâs the matter? Canât you sleep?â","Zhao Yi was silent for a moment.","Zhang Lesi asked, âWhat happened?â","When faced with the person closest to him, Zhao Yi finally revealed what was weighing on his mind.","âIâm scared.â","Zhang Lesi was startled. âScared of what?â","They had all been through so much together. Zhang Lesi couldnât imagine what could still frighten Zhao Yi. He wasnât a timid or weak man.","Zhao Yi stared at the ceiling. âYou know that our government... was specifically targeted for elimination.â","âOf course. Havenât we known that for a long time?â","This was no secret among the leadership. Jiang Cheng had openly told them about her âtheory,â and it had since been confirmed.","That was why the governments of the cityâs eight districts and the surrounding suburbs had later been established independently.","Zhao Yi fell silent again for a long time. Only after Zhang Lesi nudged him did he speak.","âBut do you know just how precise this âtargetingâ was?â","Fear appeared in Zhao Yiâs eyes.","It had all started with a chance conversation. The other personâs family member had been a civil servant.","âHe was sent out on assignment that day. He even called me to say heâd be home in the afternoon and could pick up our child, so I didnât need to worry about it.â","That civil servant and his child had both died.","Up to that point, there was nothing unusual about it. So many people had died back then. It was perfectly normal.","But then the person continued:","âWe lived in government-subsidized housing, and all our neighbors were people in the system. The neighbor next door was home on sick leave that day. She ended up mutating and bit her parents-in-law to death. I never expected to run into her husband here. Sigh... itâs already lucky if one person from a family survives.â","It sounded like nothing more than a coincidence.","If anyone else had heard it, they probably would have let it pass.","But the person who heard it was Zhao Yi.","Zhao Yi had always thought differently from everyone else.","âI borrowed Jiang Chengâs name and privately asked the people in charge of logistics at each community to investigate whether any of the refugees were civil servants or relatives of civil servants.â","âI also had them record how those civil servants had died.â","âThe results confirmed my theory.â","Most civil servants had died at their posts, inside their workplaces.","There were all kinds of ways to explain it. For example, government buildings were large, crowded, and interconnected. If one person mutated and bit several others, they could all have died in the end.","It wasnât impossible to make that explanation fit. But that was the story you told ordinary people.","A more convincing explanation was Jiang Chengâs: targeted elimination.","At the time, Zhao Yi had wondered how that targeting had been carried out.","People always wanted an answerâsomething rational, something they could convince themselves of. Only then could they suppress their unease.","âI thought that perhaps the virus concentration had been increased inside government buildings, raising the probability of mutation. Or perhaps the buildings had been deliberately sealed off so no one could escape.â","âFrom a logical standpoint, that explanation made sense.â","âBut...â","But how could you explain the civil servants who had been out of the office, on leave, or away for any number of other reasonsâyet not a single one of them had survived?","How could you explain that?","As long as the mark of âcivil servantâ was attached to your identity, your death on August 29 was already decided."]},{"number":181,"title":"Chapter 181: 0181","paragraphs":["Zhang Lesi found it unbelievable. âWhat are you talking about?â","âIsnât it all just coincidence?â she said. âYouâve only got a few samples, and youâre already drawing conclusions? The development zone is so far from the city center. Maybe the surviving civil servants are all somewhere else. Your conclusion doesnât hold up at all. The sample size is too small.â","Zhao Yi knew that not everyone could understand.","He didnât insist that Zhang Lesi do so.","Now that Zhang Lesi couldnât see, she was bound to have fears of her own.","They had all wanted her to find an empty room on the first floor so she wouldnât have to climb up and down the stairs. She had refused.","Because she couldnât see, her other senses had become more sensitive. She didnât want to go somewhere with completely unfamiliar surroundings and scents. She felt safer staying in her own home.","He rolled over and hugged her. âYouâre right. I was just letting my imagination run wild.â","Zhang Lesi scoffed. âYouâve just read too many comics. If what youâre saying is true, what kind of power could do something like that? If a foreign power were really that incredible, it could just wipe out our country. Why go to all this trouble? What would be the point? Do they want our land? Our resources? War reparations? There has to be something theyâre after, right?â","What Zhang Lesi said wasnât unreasonable.","But Zhao Yi had another, even more absurd theory in mind.","If Zhang Lesi couldnât even accept this possibility, then there was no way she would accept the even more absurd one.","He gently patted her back and coaxed her to sleep.","As for this matter, Zhao Yi felt that he could only discuss it with Gao Yuxuan.","When Gao Yuxuan saw him, he asked, âWhereâs Lesi?â","âSunbathing.â Zhao Yi glanced back.","Zhang Lesi had set up a chair and was basking in the sun. Whenever Zhao Yi was working, Zhang Lesi would sunbathe.","Her friends were all around her, so there was no need to worry.","Besides, being unable to see didnât stop her from treating other people. She could still use her superpowers.","Gao Yuxuan asked, âWhatâs wrong?â","This sort of thing wasnât suitable for discussing in broad daylight. But Zhao Yi didnât have time at night, so he could only find whatever spare moments he could.","He told Gao Yuxuan all the information he had gathered, along with his own thoughts.","Under the sunlight, Gao Yuxuan met his eyes.","Zhao Yi waited for him to digest it all.","Unlike Zhang Lesi, Gao Yuxuan didnât dismiss the idea outright. Instead, he followed Zhao Yiâs line of reasoning and continued extrapolating.","âTo be capable of doing something on this scale, it couldnât possibly be any Western country, let alone any of the countries around us. There are only so many countries in the world, and everyone knows what theyâre like. Soâ¦â","Gao Yuxuan lowered his head and thought it through aloud. âSo this is a power beyond every country on Earth. Which means itâs a power beyond this planet. Which means it can only be an extraterrestrial civilization.â","Anyone else hearing such a statement would have burst out laughing, but neither of them did.","They werenât joking. This was a serious discussion, made in earnest and with careful consideration.","It was something Zhao Yi could only discuss with Gao Yuxuan.","With Li Jiangbing, he would probably have to spend ages explaining everything.","With Song Jingshuo, he might already be rubbing his forehead and laughing helplessly.","Only Gao Yuxuan could truly match his wavelength, their imaginations moving in sync.","Zhao Yi said, âThereâs another possible direction.â","Gao Yuxuan lifted his eyes. âDimensional reduction from a higher-dimensional world?â","Zhao Yi said, âExactly.â","Gao Yuxuan asked, âSo weâre living in a lower-dimensional world?â","âPossibly.â","âFuck.â","Zhao Yi let out a long breath.","Gao Yuxuan put his hands on his hips and sucked air through his teeth. âJeez. Jeezâ¦â","He kept saying it for a while.","Zhao Yi asked, âYouâre not afraid?â","Gao Yuxuan kept his hands on his hips. âAfraid of what? Whatâs there to be afraid of? At worst, we die. Weâre damn hard to kill, anyway!â","The fear in Zhao Yiâs heart suddenly dispersed.","âTrue,â he said, relieved. âAt worst, we die.â","They had already witnessed so many deaths and brushes with death that, when he thought about it, there really wasnât much left to fear.","The fear heâd felt before had mostly come from the unknown. Fear born from imagining what might be hidden in the unknown was the greatest fear of all.","Now that he had realized the worst that could happen was death, he was no longer afraid.","Gao Yuxuan noticed the way he lowered his eyes.","In just a few short months, they had gone from being unfamiliar neighbors to comrades fighting side by side, and then to kindred spirits who understood one another.","Now, they were close friends.","Gao Yuxuan saw through him at a glance. âThereâs something else you havenât told me, isnât there?â","Zhao Yi looked into the distance.","Following his gaze, Gao Yuxuan saw several people gathered around Jiang Cheng, talking to her.","âThereâs something I thought Jiang Cheng would mention,â Zhao Yi said. âBut she didnât, so I donât know whether I should bring it up.â","âIf thatâs the case, donât tell anyone else. ButââGao Yuxuan changed tackââIâm not âanyone else.â Out with it!â","Zhao Yi was silent for a long time before saying, âThe sky was purple that day. Did you see it?â","ââ¦â Gao Yuxuan asked, âWhich day?â","âOctober fifth.â","October fifth was the day they had thought they were finally seeing the light at the end of the tunnel, only to suddenly plunge back into darkness.","The entire city had been rocked by massive explosions. S City had burned in a sea of flames and been reduced to ruins.","Gao Yuxuan said, ââ¦The kind of purple sky Jiang Cheng mentioned?â","Jiang Cheng had said that the sky had turned purple during both the first and second outbreaks of the zombie virus. She had also experienced something strange, which was why she had dared to conclude, presumptuously, that the zombie virus had returned.","People could accept the idea that something was wrong with their bodies.","But when it came to omens in the sky, many people had secretly refused to believe it. It sounded too superstitious. After hearing it, they hadnât taken it to heart.","âHoly shit! I didnât see it!â Gao Yuxuan couldnât believe it. âWhat did I miss? I actually missed it!â","âNo, waitâwhat was I doing at the time?â","âOh, right, right! We crashed! The car exploded!â","âMo Li even stood up naked and flashed his junk at us!â","âWho the hell would be looking at the sky under those circumstances?â","At the time, the city had been a sea of fire, explosions going off one after another. Everyone had been injured and bleeding.","A black cat had transformed into a human.","Every single thing that happened had been enough to seize anyoneâs attention.","Even so, Gao Yuxuan was still annoyed with himself for missing such an important moment. He turned his frustration on Zhao Yi instead.","âWhy didnât you tell me then? You bastard!â","He had actually kept the sight all to himself!","But Zhao Yi was completely innocent.","With so many things happening at once, how could he have gone over and grabbed Gao Yuxuan by the collar to say, âHey, look! The skyâs turning purple!â","By the time they had finished finding a new vehicle, making Mo Li a skirt and armor to cover his nakedness, and examining him from every angle while holding him by the arms and ears, the sky had already returned to its normal overcast gray when Zhao Yi looked again.","Zhao Yi explained, âMainly because I thought Jiang Cheng would mention it.â","But Jiang Cheng hadnât said anything at the time, nor had she mentioned it on the road.","Then Zhao Yi found out that something had happened to Zhang Lesi. He hadnât had the slightest capacity left to think about the color of the sky.","Jiang Cheng hadnât brought it up after she returned, either.","Zhao Yi had assumed that there had simply been too much going on at the time, and that she would mention it later.","In the blink of an eye, it was already the end of October.","Jiang Cheng clearly had no intention of saying anything.","And everyone else, just like Gao Yuxuan, had focused only on what was happening right in front of them and had failed to notice the sky.","Only he and Jiang Cheng knew that the omen had appeared again.","âSo you held it in all this time, and now that you finally couldnât hold your shit anymore, you remembered I existed, huh?â Gao Yuxuan complained. âFrom now on, Iâm calling you Old Turtle.â","With his hands on his hips, Gao Yuxuan squinted and ground his teeth as he glared at Jiang Cheng from a distance.","Mo Li went over.","He walked up behind Jiang Cheng and spread his arms, clearly intending to drape himself over her shoulders.","Jiang Cheng swung around and smacked him across the forehead.","Mo Li looked aggrieved.","He obediently stood off to the side.","The clothes Mo Li was wearing had been personally picked out for him by Song Jingshuo from the storeroom.","They werenât exactly designer brands, but the outfit was well coordinated. Combined with his incredible physique, Mo Li looked exceptionally handsome.","Besides, the high school girls called Mo Li âMo Li,â while they called Song Jingshuo âUncle Song.â","After all, youth was the most precious thing of all.","âIf I were Jiang Cheng, I wouldnât say anything either,â Gao Yuxuan said. âJust think about what happened the first time, and what happened the second time. Then what about the third time?â","The first time, someone became a zombie for the first time in human history.","The second time, the virus erupted again. Not only did the zombies become more powerful, but humans also began to evolve.","But the third timeâ¦","The third time, Mo Li evolved into human form.","The first two incidents concerned all of humanity.","But by the third, the focus had suddenly narrowed.","To Gao Yuxuan and Zhao Yi, it didnât seem like a big deal. As the heroineâs summoned beast, Mo Li was incredibly powerful. Continuing to evolve was simply his destiny.","But not everyone would see it that way.","There would definitely be people saying, âCould sheâitâbe the calamity that brought the zombies here?â","Throughout history, people who thought that way had actually been in the majority.","âKeep your mouths shut,â Gao Yuxuan said.","âYou too,â Zhao Yi said.","Zhao Yi continued, âActuallyâ¦ I just want to know whether our world is real.â","Compared to the human world, a comic was a lower-dimensional world, and so was a novel.","People in a higher-dimensional world could manipulate the development of a comic or novel with nothing more than a pen.","âI just want to knowâ¦â Zhao Yi said. âAm I real?â","âWhat a load of crap,â Gao Yuxuan said. âReality and unreality are relative.â","âTo us, a comic is fictional.â","âBut to the characters in that comic, this is their âreality.ââ","âYou donât have the ability to shatter the void and ascend to a higher-dimensional world, so just honestly be ârealâ in this world of yours. Stop daydreaming about impossible nonsense.â","Zhao Yi gazed at Zhang Lesi in the distance.","She had her eyes closed, quietly basking in the sunlight.","She seemed to be glowing.","She was so beautiful.","Then he turned his head and looked at Gao Yuxuan.","Silly.","Loud.","But still his soulmate and his closest friend.","He had once been nothing more than a lonely otaku working away from home in a big city.","Despite being well past his youth, he was still criticized by his parents and older relatives for âwatching things meant for children and playing with childrenâs toys.â","Every day, he went to the office and pretended to be an adult.","Then he returned home to eat alone, keeping himself company with his figurines.","But now, he had a lover, a dear friend, and a whole group of companions who trusted one another.","If some person in a higher-dimensional world was writing all this into existence, then he was grateful for every stroke of that personâs pen.","He felt happy. He felt blessed.","Why obsess over whether any of it was real?"]},{"number":182,"title":"Chapter 182: 0182","paragraphs":["On Jiang Cheng and Mo Li Living Together","Back when Mo Li was just a kitten, no one thought there was anything unusual about it. Later, when Mo Li learned to transform into a giant cat and became overwhelmingly the strongest fighter of them all, everyone could do little more than envy him.","But now Mo Li was human. Although he could still turn into a cat, Jiang Cheng had ordered him to stay in human form whenever he had nothing to do during the day, so that he could get used to being human.","Everyone felt as though they had an itch they couldnât scratch!","They all wanted to know whether Mo Li was human or a cat at night!","Computers could still be used, but there was no internet anymore, so people could no longer create dozens of small chat groups and discuss things to their heartsâ content as they had in the past.","They could only exchange a few whispered words during breaks at work. They were as furtive as the old aunties who used to gossip at the entrance of a village.","Women, from middle-school girls to elderly aunties, generally accepted the situation quite readily.","He was so tall, so handsome, and had such a good figure. Who cared what kind of animal he had been before?","The men, meanwhile, were more interested in whether Mo Li was stronger in human form or in his giant-cat form.","Some people even went to ask Mo Li directly.","âTheyâre both me,â Mo Li replied.","In any case, they were both him. He could transform however he pleased.","Mo Li was clearly different with Jiang Cheng. With other people, he didnât refuse when familiar acquaintances patted his head or scratched under his chin.","Strangers, on the other hand, were strangers. They could look all they wanted, but they werenât allowed to touch him.","Mo Li also kept trying to perch on Li Jiangbingâs head as he had in the past.","Li Jiangbing refused with absolute determination.","He could accept a pair of adorable cat bells on his head, but he absolutely would not accept those belonging to a human male.","Ever since Mo Li had become human, the rumor that âJiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo are datingâ had collapsed on its own.","Song Jingshuo suddenly found himself with a great many more admirers.","As for Jiang Chengâ¦ things remained just as they had been before.","First there had been Song Jingshuo, and now there was Mo Li.","Even those who liked Jiang Cheng would take one look at the competition, make a realistic assessment of themselves, and quietly give up.","A great many temporary couples appeared among the refugees.","It was much like the couples formed on construction sites in the old days.","Whether they had lovers or were already married before, if two people happened to hit it off now, they simply got together and made a life.","Working together to earn performance points and exchange them for supplies was much more economical than doing it alone.","With Jiang Chengâs approval, the teachers from No. 14 Middle School opened a school.","It was mainly for the little children.","Middle-school studentsâespecially high-school studentsâhad already completed their basic education. Even the younger middle-school students had learned most of the general knowledge they needed.","But if the little ones werenât educated, they would grow up illiterate.","There were very few forms of entertainment left. Fortunately, the library in the Development Zone had not been burned down. After being tidied up, it reopened.","It was crowded every day.","After losing television and computers, humanity began returning to books.","Most peopleâs work involved physical labor. With their minds free to wander, they lived simple lives from day to day and, strangely enough, didnât feel that the work was especially hard.","Sometimes, they felt that life wasnât impossible after all.","They even felt that things were going fairly well.","Changxing District, which had first proposed using radio communications, had someone skilled in amateur radio who upgraded the equipment into a shortwave radio station.","The amount of information they received increased dramatically.","Some broadcasts came from other cities and regions. Some were even in languages no one could understand, presumably from foreign countries.","That person drove specially to the major residential areas and delivered the new equipment he had tinkered together to each district.","The Tech New District also acquired a shortwave radio station and could now receive all kinds of information.","It feltâ¦ as though an isolated island had suddenly reached the shore.","They learned that there were still people alive beyond S City.","Everyoneâs circumstances were different.","In some places, the water and electricity had stopped around forty-eight hours after the second zombie-virus outbreak, and people had been struggling desperately from the very beginning.","Other areas, like S City, had well-organized communities and capable leaders who guided everyone in saving themselves.","Some of the people transmitting over the radio represented organizations, while others were individuals.","Organizations like the one in S City mostly exchanged useful information: where resources could be obtained, where water sources and arable land could be found, what plants were suitable for cultivation, and where to locate a particular piece of equipment when a problem required it.","Many genuine difficulties and problems were solved over the radio.","But there was even more useless information.","There were plenty of lunatics and crazies, too. In any case, they were mostly not right in the head.","Some sounded as though they lived alone, as if there wasnât another living person around them. They seemed determined to chatter endlessly over the radio twenty-four hours a day without saying a single useful thing.","They sounded as if they had already gone mad.","But even mad people had an audience.","Somehow, there were listeners who enjoyed them, saying that the broadcasts helped them unwind.","Amid the large crowd of rambling lunatics, one frequency stood out and unexpectedly attracted a considerable audience.","There was a man and a woman on it. The manâs voice sounded old, as though he were elderly. The woman was somewhat younger.","The two did not seem to have any connection, nor did they appear to be in the same location. Whenever the old man was broadcasting, however, the woman often cut in.","The two of them held lengthy discussions about the zombie problem.","They debated constantly and often argued.","It sounded like a talk show, yet it was extremely popular, and many people enjoyed listening.","By coincidence, the time they most loved to argue was exactly the period when the Youth Apartments had electricity every evening.","At everyoneâs request, during that time each night, the radio station was connected to the buildingâs broadcast system so that everyone could hear the âprogramâ echoing through the corridors.","It became the Tech New Districtâs most popular âshow.â","The old man seemed to have the surname Jiang, so everyone called him Uncle Jiang.","The somewhat younger woman appeared to have the surname Mao, and people called her Sister Mao.","Many of Uncle Jiang and Sister Maoâs theories about zombies and superpowers aligned with those of Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan. Zhao Yi, in particular, loved listening to them.","During that time, the lights were on, every household left its door open, and people listened to the debates coming through the corridor speakers.","It was much like the days decades ago, before televisions had become widespread, when neighbors crowded together to watch a television set.","One day, Uncle Jiang said, âItâs getting cold. A major drop in temperature is coming.â","He said this at the end of October, around the time Zhao Yi had told Zhang Lesi and Gao Yuxuan about his fears.","The temperature suddenly began to fall.","Since it was already the end of October, the drop was normal enough. Winter was coming, after all.","Everyone spent their performance points exchanging them for padded clothing and thick quilts.","But surviving the winter could not depend on individuals alone. Otherwise, a great many people would probably freeze to death.","The temporary government of the Tech New District held several meetings, pooling everyoneâs ideas and trying to find a way to solve the problem of winter heating.","Fortunately, the Tech New District had its own heating company, which provided centralized heating for the residential area.","Because the explosion on October 5 had destroyed many of the underground pipes, centralized heating was no longer possible.","But the heating company had coal.","A heating company did not wait until autumn to hurriedly transport in the coal needed for winter. The coal for winter was prepared during the summerâindeed, it had even been stockpiled before the first zombie disaster.","Ever since the disaster in June, the heating company had been nothing but an empty compound. There had been no living person left there, and no one had returned to work after the disaster passed.","There were simply too many things that needed dealing with at the time. Arranged by urgency, the Development Zone government clearly didnât consider the heating company a priority. Or perhaps it was already somewhere on the list.","Heaven had still left everyone a way out.","On October 5, the day of the massive explosion, underground wells in the heating companyâs yard had also erupted in flames, but they were far enough from the coal piles that the fire never reached them.","Besides, the heating company was right next to a residential area. The superpowered people were dispatched to cut off the underground utility lines, and before long they had brought the fire in the Technology New Districtâs residential zone under control.","No one had been thinking about the heating company, but somehow its entire yard of coal had been saved.","So those who save themselves are saved by Heaven.","Now, that coal could finally be put to use.","The plan they ultimately settled on was to provide each household with an individual iron stove, burning coal briquettes or honeycomb briquettes.","A vigorous campaign to build stoves and manufacture fuel began.","The design for the iron stoves came from Engineer Yu.","He sighed. âWeâve gone back to the old days.â","And it wasnât just Engineer Yu. Many of the younger people had experienced the era of burning honeycomb briquettes when they were children.","They really had gone back to the old days.","When travel was slow, and people had time to spare.","Metal-type superpowered people worked together with the mechanics to develop crushers and coal-briquette presses.","Honeycomb briquettes were laid out to dry all over the heating companyâs yard and along the roads outside.","A great many new jobs were created.","Besides padded clothes and thick quilts, old-fashioned kettles, vacuum flasks, and hot-water bottles also became hot-selling items.","Song Jingshuo watched the inventory dwindle at a frightening speed.","Aunt Pan said, âI wonder if the wholesale market in Yuezhuang is still there. Or whether it burned down.â","Before all this, Song Jingshuo had never known anything about one wholesale market or another.","When he bought name-brand clothes, they had to be from the current season. He wouldnât buy anything from an out-of-season sale, much less from an outlet store.","There were plenty of wealthy people in his circle. You could tell at a glance.","They immediately organized people and vehicles to go there.","Fortunately, the wholesale market had taken good fire-prevention measures. The warehouses stood separately, with firebreaks between them.","Two warehouses had burned down, but several others remained completely intact.","A wholesale market really did have everything.","It was a huge haul.","They brought it all back and began an extensive exchange program using merit points.","The merit points everyone had saved up finally became useful.","The iron stoves were distributed to households free of charge.","Pairs of earth- and metal-type superpowered people went door to door to install them.","They had to punch a hole through the wall and extend the chimney outside. That required the earth- and metal-type users to work together.","Zhao Yi was also so busy during this period that his feet barely touched the ground.","There was no need to worry about Zhang Lesi, though.","She had to see patients, and they had assigned her a personal aide to accompany her during the day.","She still couldnât see a thing, which worried everyone terribly. She herself, however, was the least concerned.","She calmly analyzed the situation. âMaybe Iâve been living too comfortably. Being unable to see hasnât affected me, so psychologically I donât have a strong enough desire to recover.â","Then she boasted, âI have excellent taste in men.â","Coal was allocated according to the number of people in each household. Anyone who wanted more had to exchange merit points for it. If you wanted to make it through the winter warmly, youâd better not be lazy. Go to work.","At the same time, communities throughout the area began building free public warming rooms.","Some were made with glass, others with plastic sheeting.","Fire-type superpowered people took shifts keeping the warming rooms heated.","There were so many fire-type superpowered people that they werenât worth much. The pay for this job was fairly good, so competition was fierce.","Once inside, you would often see a fire-type user sprawled in a deck chair, dozing.","Several small-to-medium-sized fireballs floated in the air.","If they were too large, they might burn someone. If they were too small, they wouldnât provide enough heat, so there had to be quite a few of them.","The job demanded extremely fine control over the fireballs, which was why it paid well.","Sometimes, when you saw the fireballs suddenly shrink as though they were about to go out, you knew the fire-type user had nearly fallen fully asleep while dozing. You had to hurry over and kick the deck chair, jolting him awake.","The fireballs would swell up again.","It was so warm and cozy that it really did make people sleepy.","During the day, if they had no work, people could save coal at home by staying in the public warming rooms. Many liked to spend their time there.","In an era when entertainment options were scarce, the warming rooms became social hubs, much like public restrooms had been several decades earlier.","The warming rooms had little stools, though people were also welcome to bring their own more comfortable chairs.","Some even brought bedding, swept a clean corner with a broom, and lay down to sleep.","Buckets of peanut shells were carried outside one after another.","That was because roasted peanuts were provided free of charge.","They not only gave everyone something to occupy their mouths while listening to gossip, but also supplied plenty of calories to help ward off the cold.","No one knew exactly how many zombies Song Jingshuo and Zeng Qiangâs group had buried underground. In any case, ever since they started using zombies as fertilizer, the peanut harvest had become absurdly abundant. Now the peanuts were being distributed as a public benefit.","They had manure fertilizer now, too. According to Auntie Xue and Auntie Qian, their superpowers made handling it particularly easy.","Xiao Dan stuffed Wang Yunya into a heating shift at the warming room. The pay was high, and the work was easy.","Every day, the young Wang Yunya listened to all kinds of gossip until her eyes went wide.","âWhat happened yesterday?â","âThe first wife brought the mistress and the second mistress along to catch the fifth mistress in the act.â","âWow. Did they fight?â","âThey did.â","âThen didnât they all get whipped?â","âNo. The first wife took the whole beating herself. He was the only one who got whipped. The fifth mistress even hugged him and cried, saying she was sorry.â","ââ¦What happened afterward?â","âAfterward, they picked dates and made arrangements so that no oneâs schedules conflicted.â","âExactly. As long as thereâs no conflict, itâs fine.â","Under these special circumstances, the institution of monogamy had lost its power to restrain people.","Many were, in practice, living in multi-partner relationships.","Both men and women.","As long as you excelled in one areaâlooks, figure, superpowers, or specialized knowledge and skills that could earn merit pointsâas long as you had one outstanding strength, it was easy to find a partner.","Because the fights over catching people cheating in these multi-partner relationships never ended, there was always an opening in the whipping-execution post.","To avoid being whipped, everyone now advocated not resorting to violence. Catch your cheating partners civilly."]},{"number":183,"title":"Chapter 183: 0183","paragraphs":["The weather had turned cold, and farmers from the outskirts were driving their flocks of sheep into the city to sell.","The Tech New District had originally been a suburban area, mostly farmland. Later, a huge tract of land was designated for development and turned into the Tech New District. Outside the residential area and industrial park, it was still countryside.","In the past, the sheep herds raised by nearby villagers had wandered onto the roads of the Tech New District several times, even making the news.","Ever since the massive explosion on October 5, the power had been out.","The Tech New District had immediately assigned an electric-type ability user to keep the cafeteriaâs freezers running, and had quickly managed to put together some generators. But there was nothing they could do about the situation in the urban districts.","They could no longer go into the city to search the frozen-meat stores and cold-storage warehouses.","All the meat had gone rotten.","With the prospect of having no meat to eat, Brother Dong said, âWhy donât we take a look around the outskirts?â","Brother Dongâs parents lived in the suburbs. When he had left home, he hadnât planned on ever going back, so he had given all the chickens and ducks at home to his neighbors.","He knew the rural area around there very well.","âSomeoneâs bound to have livestock. Letâs go look.â","Even if the owners had died or turned into zombies, there was a chance their cows, sheep, chickens, and ducks were still around. They could pick them up for free.","Of course, nothing was ever truly free.","The livestock and poultry belonging to dead farmers had already been taken in by their surviving neighbors.","When people from the Tech New District really did find some, they had to negotiate a price.","Performance points meant nothing to the villagers. Trading had returned to the level of barter.","Fortunately, the Tech New District had all kinds of supplies, and in the end they managed to reach agreements and purchase sheep, chickens, and ducks.","They had found a source of meat for the Tech New District, though the supply was so limited that rations had to be strictly controlled. Still, it was better than having none at all.","Gao Yuxuan and the others also rigged up the power grid to send electricity into the Bailiang River and catch fish.","That was how everyone managed to keep having meat to eat.","Now that the weather had turned cold, the farmers knew they lacked the strength to get so many animals through the winter. They drove them all to the Tech New District, hoping to sell them.","The Tech New District took them all in.","They did not slaughter everything at once. Instead, they built pens, set up stoves to keep the animals warm, and raised them while slaughtering them gradually.","As time went on, one of the ewes even gave birth to a lamb.","When the little children learned that the lamb would eventually be eaten too, they cried.","The unexpected bonus was that the chickens laid eggs every day.","Zeng Qiang strongly recommended raising chickens on a large scale to ensure a steady supply of eggs.","The farmers wanted to sell their animals before the weather became even colder because they were on their own, and winter feed could no longer be obtained. They had to cut their losses in time.","But for the Tech New District, which had wood-type ability users, this was not difficult.","The real reason the Tech New District had never considered animal husbandry was that its core members were all a bunch of urban young people.","They had started farming because they had been blessed with wood-type abilities.","But animal husbandry depended entirely on human labor, so it had never even occurred to them.","Aunt Pan understood this, actually.","But she was superstitious about educated people. Since all these youngsters were educated and none of them had brought it up, she assumed it must not be necessary.","So she kept quiet.","And so, although the process was a little bumpy, after developing agriculture, the Tech New District finally embarked on the path of animal husbandry as well.","In the end, everything had to depend on their own production.","Jiang Cheng remembered a slogan from a book: âDo it yourself, and youâll have enough food and clothing.â","That slogan had been coined more than sixty years ago. Back then, conditions had been far worse than they were now.","Yet those people had still made it all the way to prosperity before the disaster.","So we can do it too.","Because shortwave radio could cover such vast distancesâeven spanning continentsâit picked up all kinds of communications.","At first, no one paid attention to one particular transmission.","It was Uncle Jiang who said to Sister Mao first:","âDo you believe it?â","Sister Mao replied, âGive me a reason to.â","Uncle Jiang said, âI have one, but itâs hard to explain.â","âIf you have one, then say it.â","âI already told you, itâs hard to explain.â","Sister Mao gave a cold laugh. âStop being so cryptic.â","Since the two of them had a large audience at the youth apartments, everyone was drawn to the discussion they were having and began listening to the broadcast in question.","Among the mutterings, curses, doomsday theories, and religious preaching of all sorts of lunatics and psychotics, they found the voice of a middle-aged man. It was deep and low, and seemed to be a recording, because it repeated the same words over and over:","âEveryone, be prepared. Extreme weather is coming soon.â","âEveryone, be prepared. Extreme weather is coming soon.â","âEveryone, be prepared. Extreme weather is coming soon.â","â¦","It sounded no different from the ravings of the other lunatics.","If not for Uncle Jiang and Sister Mao, everyone would probably have skipped past it while tuning the radio.","But Uncle Jiang and Sister Mao were seriously discussing the possibility of extreme weather.","Uncle Jiang firmly believed the man, claiming that he had a reason for doing so, but refusing to say what it was.","The more he acted that way, the more intriguing it became.","Jiang Cheng called a meeting of the districtâs key personnel.","âWhat do you all think?â","âSounds like a charlatan to me.â","âWeâve tried calling him, but Uncle Jiang never responds. He only responds to Sister Mao.â","Even so, the two of them played off each other so well that they were extremely captivating.","Jiang Cheng said, âLetâs first discuss what extreme weather might actually mean and how it would affect us.â","Everyone was surprised. âYouâre taking it seriously?â","âYes,â Jiang Cheng said. âLetâs discuss it as if it were real.â","Jiang Cheng never joked about serious matters, nor did she waste meeting time on jokes.","Everyone became serious.","Someone spoke first. âFirst, we need to define âextreme weather.â The lowest temperature in S City during winter is usually around minus fifteen degrees Celsius, right? In my hometown, it gets down to minus thirty. If that happened in S City, wouldnât that count as extreme weather?â","âMy God, Iâd freeze to death at minus thirty! I hate the cold most of all.â","âThatâs why youâre a fire-type, haha.â","âThank heavens Iâm a fire-type. Seriously, I sleep with a fireball burning beside me now. I can keep it from changing even after I fall asleep.â","Song Jingshuo said, âStay on topic.â","âOh. So, low temperatures, freezing conditions, hail, freezing rain, things like that?â","âMore or less,â Jiang Cheng said. âWhat impact would those have on us?â","This time, everyone gave serious answers.","âGoing outside would become difficult. Heavy snow and ice would make both walking and driving extremely hard. If we needed supplies, even going out to look for them would be difficult.â","âIf the low temperatures continued, we couldnât let the stoves inside the buildings go out. At the temperatures in my hometown, people would freeze to death if the fires stopped.â","âThe soil would freeze solid, and no one could work outdoors. Farming would definitely have to stop, which would affect our food supply.â","Those were more or less all the likely consequences.","Jiang Cheng asked, âWhat countermeasures do we have?â","Song Jingshuo said, âIf the roads freeze, we can put snow chains on the tires. Theyâre simple enough to make ourselves.â","Someone else said, âWeâll have to see how cold it gets. If itâs truly severe, weâll either need to burn more coal or house everyone together.â","The most important point was this: âWe have to make sure thereâs enough food. Thatâs the most important thing.â","Jiang Cheng reported the subject of the meeting to the other districts over the radio.","âEven if the man is a charlatan, weâre the government. We should still prepare an emergency plan.â","âIf it really happens, failing to respond in time could get people killed.â","After the radio communication ended, someone sighed.","âShe still thinks sheâs the government.â","Under the immense pressure of survival, the high spirits many people had possessed when they first established the temporary government had nearly been worn away.","The person beside him was silent for a moment before saying, âForget everyone elseâbut her, she deserves it.â","Everyone regularly exchanged updates and shared whatever information they had.","They all knew more or less what was happening in the Technology New District. It was the largest survivor settlement in S City by population. It should have been under the greatest pressure to survive, yet it was actually the best-managed of all the settlements.","It could even be said to have enough food and clothing.","With the water, electricity, and gas all cut off, the residents somehow still looked remarkably spirited.","In a way, the Technology New District had become everyoneâs spiritual pillar.","Whenever they felt exhausted and wanted to throw in the towel, they only had to think of the Technology New District to feel that perhaps they could keep going after all.","On certain difficult roads, what people needed was comrades by their side.","Zheng Junwei of Yuanshilong District called his people together for a meeting and said, âJiang Cheng is right. We should have had emergency plans in place from the start. Letâs get ours ready too.â","On November 14, they began receiving broadcasts from Uncle Jiang early in the morning:","âGo listen! Everyone, go listen!â","They switched frequencies and found the low voice of a middle-aged man.","He kept repeating:","âThereâs going to be a major temperature drop today. Extreme weather is coming. Everyone, get prepared!â","âThereâs going to be a major temperature drop today. Extreme weather is coming. Everyone, get prepared!â","âThereâs going to be a major temperature drop today. Extreme weather is coming. Everyone, get prepared!â","Someone immediately reported it to Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng furrowed her brows slightly. After a moment, she decided, âNotify every residential compound to implement the cold-weather emergency plan.â","Then she added, âGet in touch with all the districts and remind them as well.â","After the communications towers went down, mobile phones became useless. For several days, it was extremely difficult for the residential compounds to contact one another, and people had to deliver messages in person.","Later, with Song Jingshuoâs guidance, they searched everywhere for off-road vehicles with large numbers pasted onto their rear windows and antennas mounted on top. They removed the radios from these vehicles and installed one in each residential compound. At last, their communications evolved from the primitive civilization of shouting back and forth into the modern civilization of radio.","Every compound received the warning.","At Jixiang Jiayuan, Mr. Xu went from room to room inspecting things.","âHave you all added enough coal? Add more. Fill it up. Leave the stove opening uncoveredâdonât close it.â","âMake do for now. Stop complaining. Whatâs wrong with squeezing together?â","âListen to the government.â","Each household had only one iron stove, without exception installed in the living room. The temporary government of the Technology New District required everyone to sleep in the living room.","Mr. Xu and Director Yu had long since become familiar faces around Jiang Cheng. They were even qualified to sit in on some meetings.","They could also speak up and offer suggestions, and several of their proposals had been adopted.","The longer they stayed together, the more they trusted Jiang Cheng.","As a company manager, Mr. Xu knew very well that the people below had to be properly supervised if instructions were to be carried out without problems. So he inspected every room, forcing the employees to follow Jiang Chengâs requirements.","The four of them had also moved their mattresses into the living room. They pushed the coffee table aside and joined the mattresses together, sleeping squeezed up against one another.","The living room was indeed much warmer than the bedrooms.","Looking up at the ceiling, Mr. Xu said, âActually, I think we could sleep like this all winter. Itâs warmer.â","It was warmer, all right, but everyone still woke up freezing in the middle of the night.","Sneezes rang out everywhere.","âFuck, why is it so cold?â","âDid the fire go out?â","âGet up and check.â","Shivering, they lit a candle and climbed to their feet to take a look. The fire hadnât gone out. The stove was still burning, yet the room was cold.","The temperature really had dropped sharply.","There was a thermometer on the wall of the apartment. Mr. Xuâs teeth were chattering as he carried the candle over to look at it.","It was November 14. In previous years, central heating in S City usually began on November 15.","At this time of year, the lowest nighttime temperature in S City should normally have been one or two degrees Celsius. It was rare for the temperature to fall below zero so early in the season.","Every time Mr. Xu opened his mouth, white vapor poured out and fogged the thermometer.","He reached out and wiped the vapor from its surface.","The round thermometer had a fan-shaped temperature scale. The right side was red, with a maximum temperature of fifty degrees. The left side was blue, with a minimum of minus thirty degrees.","By the candlelight, Mr. Xu saw the needle hanging limply on the left, below the blue â-30,â in the empty space beneath it.","Mr. Xu felt cold all over.","Cold from the inside out."]},{"number":184,"title":"Chapter 184: 0184","paragraphs":["At that moment, Mr. Xu felt almost the same fear Zhao Yi had experienced.","A vague foreboding, an indescribable unknown.","The next moment, Mr. Xu abruptly turned around. âXiaoxiao!â","He set the candle on the table and hurriedly put on his clothes.","Director Yu asked, âWhatâs wrong with Xiaoxiao?â","Mr. Xu said, âIâm afraid she didnât listen. Iâm going to check on her again.â","Of their entire group, only Wu Yan and Tao Xiaoxiao were women.","The young girlâs endurance hadnât been tempered to the same degree as that of the older women.","Back when they had been trapped in the company, everyone had greasy hair and foul breath. She had secretly hidden a bottle of mouthwash and rinsed her mouth with it every day.","She thought no one knew.","During the nightly room inspection, Tao Xiaoxiao had also been very reluctant to sleep in the living room.","The stove was burning there, and a pile of honeycomb coal was stacked nearby, so the floor was inevitably dirty. She hated it.","She had agreed in front of Mr. Xu, but he was afraid she would say one thing to peopleâs faces and do another behind their backs.","He knew his employees far too well.","He pounded on the door.","The male employee who opened it was shivering violently from the cold. âW-Whatâs going on? Holy crap, why is it so cold?â","Mr. Xu asked, âWhereâs Xiaoxiao? Did Xiaoxiao sleep in the living room?â","The man stammered, âShe, she didnâtââ","Mr. Xu shoved him aside and rushed in with Director Yu and the others.","Sure enough, there were only two mattresses on the floor, one double and one single.","The two male employees were sleeping on the double mattress, while Wu Yan occupied the single one. They all sat up with their blankets wrapped around them, exhaling clouds of white vapor through their open mouths.","Mr. Xuâs expression changed. âXiaoxiao didnât come out to sleep?â","Wu Yan said, âSheâ¦â","Tao Xiaoxiao was young, sweet-tongued, and good at winning people over. Even Wu Yan usually indulged her. Since she didnât want to, Wu Yan hadnât forced her.","Tao Xiaoxiao was still sleeping in her own room. Fortunately, she hadnât been completely foolishâshe knew enough to leave the door open so that the heat could spread through.","Even so, in the short distance from the living room to Tao Xiaoxiaoâs doorway, Mr. Xu could already feel the change in temperature on his face.","It was icy.","The instant he stepped into Tao Xiaoxiaoâs room, the cold pierced straight to the bone.","The size of the doorway and the distance between the rooms ultimately limited how much heat could travel.","Tao Xiaoxiaoâs lips were as pale as gold paper. She had already lost consciousness in her sleep from the cold.","Everyone hurriedly carried her into the living room.","âAdd more coal! Get the fire burning hotter!â","They placed two blankets beneath her and covered her with two more.","Everyone on the same floor was woken up, and all their hot-water bottles were stuffed around her.","The men rubbed her hands, feet, and ears.","Wu Yan knelt above her head, reached one hand inside her collar, and frantically rubbed her abdomen and chest to generate heat through friction.","Someone else poured hot brown-sugar water into her mouth.","That was how a whole group of colleagues dragged Tao Xiaoxiao back from the brink of death.","By the time Tao Xiaoxiao was able to open her eyes, everyone else was utterly exhausted.","What a remarkable girl.","Though still so young, she had experienced two completely opposite brushes with death: nearly being burned alive and nearly freezing to death.","Both times, they had forcibly pulled her back from the gates of hell.","At the Youth Apartments, everyone slept in communal dormitories.","Most of the apartments there were basically single large roomsâbedroom and living room combined, without any partitions. The spaces were relatively large, which made them inefficient to heat.","The emergency plan for dealing with the cold was to create large communal dormitories.","They connected several apartments, removed all the unnecessary furniture, filled the rooms with beds, and set up more stoves. The heating efficiency immediately improved.","The rooms couldnât be too large, either. Generally, three apartments were connected to form one dormitory, and people were packed into them one dormitory at a time.","Jiang Cheng, of course, stayed with the girls. They also brought along the little girls from the childrenâs group.","The boys followed the uncles.","Mo Li tried to sneak into the womenâs dormitory in cat form, but Li Jiangbing grabbed him by the scruff of the neck and carried him away.","Adults had been assigned to both the boysâ and girlsâ middle-school dormitories, while some children were staying with the adults as well.","The children chattered away.","They all said it felt as if they had returned to their school days, when everyone had crowded together and slept in the classrooms.","The bed boards beneath them were made by piecing together classroom desks, and they were hard enough to make anyone sore. It had only been a month, yet they already missed those days.","Someone sighed. âWhy does time pass so quickly and so slowly at the same time?â","When Jiang Cheng woke up, she immediately felt the chill at the tip of her nose.","The temperature had really dropped.","Fortunately, there were more stoves and more people in the communal dormitory, so no one had frozen.","Several fire-element girls released fireballs, and the temperature in the dormitory quickly rose.","Everyone held their clothes around the fireballs to warm them before daring to put them on.","When they went to the windows and wiped away the white frost, they were all stunned.","âCome and look!â","Everyone crowded around the floor-to-ceiling windows.","The courtyard outside had already become a world of white.","They could see the public toilets and cafeteria, as well as the heated corridors that had been hastily constructed over the past few days to connect the various buildings, the toilets, the cafeteria, and the communal heating rooms.","Because they had been built in a rush to ward off the cold, the heated corridors had not been made particularly tall. Still, they had been high enough for a six-foot-tall person to walk through.","But now, the corridors were almost completely buried in snow.","In other words, the snow was more than a person deep.","The girlsâ dormitory buzzed with excited chatter.","Because the provisional government had issued an early warning and made thorough preparations, everything had been arranged properly. Everyone was surprised and excited, but no one was afraid.","Su Yu helped Zhang Lesi get dressed.","Zhang Lesi asked, âWhereâs Jiang Cheng?â","Su Yu turned her head and saw Jiang Cheng standing beside the floor-to-ceiling window, gazing outside.","The middle-school girls, excited beyond measure by the heavy snow, stood around her.","Jiang Cheng stood among them, as if a still image had been embedded in an animated scene.","What was Jiang Cheng looking at?","What was she thinking?","Su Yu called out, âJiang Cheng?â","Jiang Cheng turned to look at them, then came over to help Zhang Lesi get dressed.","Winter clothes were too thick and difficult to put on.","âWere you cold last night?â she asked.","Zhang Lesi replied, âNot really. I could feel the cold, but I didnât freeze. Whatâs it like outside?â","Jiang Cheng said, âThe snow has buried the heated corridors.â","Su Yu and Zhang Lesi both paused. âThe heated corridors?â","Zhang Lesi shoved Su Yu. Su Yu ran to the window and took a look, utterly shocked.","Jiang Cheng helped Zhang Lesi into her pants. âLift your leg. Theyâre buried. Almost completely. The snow is nearly as high as a person.â","Zhang Lesi said, âI remember Zhao Yi saying the corridors were designed to be two meters high?â","Jiang Cheng replied, âThatâs right.â","Zhang Lesi found it unbelievable.","Su Yu came back. âThe corridors are almost invisible. The snow is higher than a person.â","Zhang Lesi angrily pounded the bed. âWhy canât I see it too!â","She was from southern China and had always dreamed of seeing heavy snow.","Su Yu said nothing. She had seen it with her own eyes, and the sight had shaken her to the core.","She glanced at Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng lifted her eyes and looked back at Su Yu.","Su Yu hesitated, unsure how to begin.","Jiang Cheng shook her head.","âGo ahead,â she said. âWhat kind of person do you think he is?â","The person who had warned them in advance about the extreme drop in temperature.","It had turned out that he wasnât crazy.","If anything, he had become famous in a single battle.","The girls worked together to fill hot-water bottles and basins, then poured water into them to wash up.","After a while, someone knocked on the door to announce, âYou can go downstairs to use the bathroom now.â","The fire-element ability users on duty that day had already gotten up and gone downstairs.","There were stoves in the public toilets, but at this temperature, they might as well not have existed.","The fire-element users first used fireballs to warm the entire restroom before daring to let everyone in. Otherwise, they were afraid peopleâs urine would freeze to their bodies.","The hastily repaired enclosed walkways connected the buildings in the center of the courtyards.","Stoves had been placed in the middle of the walkways as well.","But no one had any experience with temperatures this low. It was only when the bitter cold truly arrived that they realized there werenât enough stoves.","More stoves were added on the spot.","Fire-type superpowered individuals were already heating the communal warming rooms. There were others in the cafeterias, and even in the public restrooms.","With all that, the web-like network of enclosed walkways finally grew warm enough. People could move through them without suffering frostbite from the extreme cold.","Before noon, the statistics from each residential compound came in.","Even with all those warnings and arrangements, there were still people who refused to follow instructions.","People like that existed everywhere. But this would be the last time they disobeyed.","Jixiang Jiayuan had 71 people freeze to death.","Yujing Xiangyuan had 130.","The other residential compounds reported their numbers one after another, most ranging from several dozen to two hundred.","Deqingli had more than 300 deaths, because it was densely populated and housed more people.","The entire Science and Technology New District was sheltering more than 30,000 refugees. In total, more than 900 people had frozen to death the previous night.","There were no deaths at the Youth Apartments, only one case of frostbite.","It was a man who had been unable to hold it in and had gone downstairs to take a dump in the middle of the night.","Halfway through, he realized something was wrong. If he didnât get upstairs immediately, he might not be able to make it back at all. He hurriedly pulled up his pants and sprinted upstairs.","By the time he got back, he had already suffered frostbite.","His roommates carried him to Zhang Lesi, who treated him.","The man kept his entire face wrapped in a scarf the whole time, refusing to show even his eyes.","That way, no girl would see the face of âthe man who froze his butt while taking a dump in the middle of the night.â","Everyoneâs butt looked more or less the same anyway. Hiding his face was enough.","Mo Li appeared in the form of a black cat, but he was different from beforeâhe had turned into a long-haired cat.","Everyone almost failed to recognize him.","Li Jiangbing praised Mo Li enthusiastically. âGood cat!â","It turned out that Mo Li transformed into a long-haired cat at night.","When he heard Li Jiangbing say, âItâs so cold,â he began to grow, transforming into a hugeâan absolutely enormousâlong-haired cat.","Cats had higher body temperatures than humans, and a giant catâs body temperature was even higher. On top of that, he had long, insulating fur.","A group of grown men fought to sleep pressed against Mo Li. It was warm and cozy beyond description.","They were happy, but Mo Li was not happy in the slightest.","How could he possibly be happy when he couldnât cuddle up and sleep with Jiang Cheng?","The little catâs face clearly showed the words: Iâm not happy.","But because of the cold, it was better for him to stay in his long-haired cat form to retain body heat, so Jiang Cheng stopped forcing him to maintain a human form.","Mo Li could finally perch on Jiang Chengâs shoulder again, and he became happy once more.","âMo Li, get a little bigger,â Jiang Cheng said.","Mo Li: â?â","Mo Li didnât understand, but he did as he was told.","âA little bigger. Just a tiny bit is enough.â","Mo Li grew slightly larger.","âGood. Just like that,â Jiang Cheng said.","Jiang Cheng draped Mo Li around the back of his neck, then pulled his front and hind legs across his chest and crossed them there.","A genuine fur stole that was practically a living radiator.","With that fur stole draped around his neck, Jiang Cheng went to the radio station.","It was no longer possible to calculate the situation by administrative district. Several districts had already begun merging and had become a handful of major refugee settlements.","The Science and Technology New District had received the mysterious manâs prediction yesterday and immediately used the radio to warn people in the other districts.","Yet even those who had made preparations just like the Science and Technology New District still suffered massive losses to the cold.","Almost every settlement had a death toll comparable to that of the Science and Technology New District.","And that was despite the fact that the Science and Technology New Districtâs population was one and a half to three times larger than theirs.","At that moment, nearly every settlement leader wanted to ask the same questionâ","Who exactly was the man who had predicted the extreme cold?","Naturally, there was no answer.","Perhaps Uncle Jiang knew. After all, he often hinted that he was actually familiar with the mysterious manâs background.","But on closer thought, they realized that no one had ever really known who Uncle Jiang wasâor who Sister Mao was, for that matter.","They tuned the radio to the right frequency. On November 15, the mysterious man was still broadcasting:","âIt wonât be over anytime soon. Give up your fantasies.â"]},{"number":185,"title":"Chapter 185: 0185","paragraphs":["The lowest temperature shown on the left side of the thermometer was -30Â°C.","Everyone tried taking the thermometer outside. The needle drooped helplessly into the blank space below -30Â°C, then froze and cracked outright.","So, in reality, no one knew just how cold it was outside.","As Aunt Pan put it: âYou couldnât even move shit.â","In the end, with the help of the fire-type ability users, they managed to thaw the ground and transport it anyway.","If they didnât do it regularly, then within just a few hours everyone would be facing the horrifying prospect of having a mountain of feces stabbing them in the ass.","Luckily, the sheep and chickens had already been moved out of the pen and into the buildings. They stank horribly, but the sheep had their wool, and the chickens burrowed beneath the sheepâs bellies.","With the furnaces as well, they all survived.","There was still meat, eggs, and goatâs milk.","Even those who froze to death were not wasted.","Since a cultivation room had been built inside the buildings ahead of time, and soil and crops had already been transported in, the dead were buried directly in the earth, contributing to everyoneâs survival.","The Technology New District began a massive infrastructure project.","In just a few days, numerous âsky corridorsâ appeared, crisscrossing the space between the buildings.","The main reason was that people couldnât stay cooped up indoors all day. But whenever everyone went out, they had to pass through the courtyards, public restrooms, greenhouses, and canteens on the ground floor. The heated corridors became far too congested.","So several sky corridors were built.","One even connected to Auspicious Garden.","The two residential compounds were neighbors, and Auspicious West Street between them was actually not very wide.","A corridor was built between the two buildings closest to each other in the two compounds. Each of those buildings was then connected to the other buildings in its own compound.","Imperial Auspicious Garden followed suit and connected itself to Auspicious Garden.","The three neighboring compounds now looked incredibly cyberpunk and futuristic.","Since no one could go outside, even more people scrambled for jobs at the power generators.","They were no longer doing it to earn performance points. They simply wanted something to do.","Many people couldnât sleep and had their days and nights completely reversed, so there were people working the generators both day and night. As a result, electricity was actually more plentiful than before.","Besides Gao Yuxuanâs game room being packed, there were also many private cinemas of various sizes, stocked with pirated discs.","The electricity-type and fire-type ability users were busy from morning till night.","Some men even secretly opened members-only mini cinemas, admitting male guests only and contributing their private collections from their computers.","Apart from the power-generation jobs, there was another position that required a great deal of manpower: picking and harvesting crops.","The main crops were wheat and peanuts.","While seriously treating the mysterious manâs words as prophecies and making contingency plans, the provisional government had decided during a meeting that, in an extreme situation, they would provide food with a higher calorie content.","Compared with potatoes, steamed buns were more calorie-dense.","It wouldnât do to feed everyone nothing but potatoes. The body needed more energy than that.","Fortunately, the Youth Apartments had plenty of vacant rooms, and several floors had been cleared out specifically for farming.","The provisional government abandoned its plan of using potatoes to regulate prices.","That had been an approach suited to peacetime. When temperatures fell so low that even thermometers could no longer measure them, prices no longer mattered. The goal was to keep as many people alive as possible.","Steamed buns were unlimited, but wasting them was strictly forbidden. Anyone caught wasting food would immediately receive a whipping.","Peanuts were available without restriction.","Given the circumstances, the provisional government chose peanuts to save lives. In the canteens, dormitories, and sky corridors, baskets of fried and roasted peanuts were everywhere, free for anyone to eat.","It wasnât about indulging cravings. It was about constantly supplying the body with sugar, oil, and fat, allowing it to generate enough heat to withstand the cold.","With the choices available, peanuts were the best possible lifesaving food.","The snow was higher than a person.","Obtaining water on-site had become the easiest thing of all. They didnât even need Li Jiangbingâs water-type ability anymore.","They could simply collect snow and boil it.","But every ten days, they had to transport food to the more distant residential compounds.","The quantities were enormous.","And it was extremely difficult to start the vehicles. Even if one managed to get running, a fire-type ability user had to accompany it.","Faced with these difficulties, the best transport method was Mo Li and Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng stored all the food that needed to be transported in her storage space, then bundled herself up from head to toe against the cold.","The fire-type ability users specially made charcoal.","The metal-type ability users made small heaters.","Hot water wouldnât do. The tiny amount of heat from hot water couldnât possibly withstand the cold. They needed charcoal that would burn and release heat on its own.","The charcoal was stuffed inside their clothes.","Mo Li grew enormous and crouched down on the ground. Jiang Cheng climbed onto his back.","Several others climbed onto Mo Liâs back as well. They tied his long fur into knots, securing Jiang Cheng in place.","Once Jiang Cheng had settled herself and been fastened down, everyone worked together to comb his fur smooth, then buried her in the long, thick coat.","The earth-type ability users quickly opened a section of wall so the gigantic Mo Li could get out.","Once Mo Li and Jiang Cheng disappeared into the blizzard, they rapidly restored the wall to keep out the cold.","When enlarged, Mo Li could walk through the snow with half his body exposed.","As he charged forward, the snow was thrown into the air and transformed into swirling mist. Viewed from the upper floors of the buildings, he looked like a long snow dragon winding across the earth.","That long fur really was an incredible defense against the cold. Hidden inside it, Jiang Cheng didnât feel cold at all.","Following the carefully planned optimal route, they delivered food to every residential compound.","All the compounds had undergone massive construction projects. With various sky corridors spanning the area, they looked especially surreal amid the endless white snow.","In some windows, they could see firelight, which meant that fire-type ability users were inside.","It was easy to imagine people gathered around fireballs for warmth.","Human beings had to band together if they wanted to struggle onward and survive.","Contact with other districts revealed that conditions everywhere were far from good.","People froze to death from time to time.","Water, at least, was not in short supply because of the snow.","Everyone followed the Technology New Districtâs advice and planted large quantities of wheat and peanuts.","Peanuts saved lives.","But hardship wore away at peopleâs willpower.","From November through March, the various settlements had gritted their teeth and endured for more than four months, yet the extreme cold still had not passed.","During that time, they experienced blizzards, freezing rain, and hail.","Every time, the mysterious man announced the disaster in advance over the radio.","Every time, his prediction came true.","Gradually, people no longer dared call him a quack.","Many began to believe in him almost religiously.","Meanwhile, many of the fortune-tellers and crackpots who had constantly rambled over the radio fell silent. Ever since the extreme cold arrived, the chaotic world of the shortwave radio seemed to have been suddenly swept clean. The world had abruptly grown quiet.","No one wanted to think too deeply about it. Doing so made their chests feel heavy.","Uncle Jiang and Sister Mao were both still alive and well.","The two of them were extremely tight-lipped. No matter how much you chatted or debated with them, you couldnât tell what kind of environment they were surviving in, or whether they lived alone or in some kind of settlement.","But it was clear from their voices that both of them were definitely in safe environments.","Safety, however, did not mean a person couldnât go insane.","Sometimes Sister Mao spoke as if she were muttering in a delirium.","Uncle Jiang sounded even more like a crackpot than the mysterious man.","Yet what made the two of them so compelling was that, amid all the arguments, debates, and pointless chatter, they would often offer remarkably accurate opinionsâor even information that ordinary people had no way of obtaining.","For example, the massive zombie outbreak in T City.","That news had been confirmed by the radio expert in Changxing District through wireless transmissions from M City.","The zombie situation in T City had completely spiraled out of control, and large numbers of mutated zombies had appeared. Their combat abilities were exceptionally powerful. The survivors had suffered a total collapse and fled in every direction, with many escaping to M City.","Several radio stations in City M confirmed the incident.","This proved that Uncle Jiang and Sister Mao truly had access to certain channels of information beyond the control of outsiders.","All of this happened before the extreme cold arrived.","At the time, everyone had their theories.","âSatellite surveillance?â","âMaybe they have connections to some high-ranking officials. There must be survivors among the upper ranksâsurely they couldnât all be dead. And where did the military go?â","âThere must be some remnants of power. Sister Mao sounds like she has access to some special channels too.â","But Uncle Jiang and Sister Mao refused to respond to any of it. No one knew the answer.","All they knew was that the two of them would occasionally release bits of information.","Then there was the mysterious man, who made prophecies.","After the extreme cold struck, many people came to believe in them. There were even faint signs that it was developing into a religion.","One had to understand that religionâespecially a religion born under such brutal conditionsâwas never a good thing.","They were almost always cults.","And cults did sinister things.","It had always been that way.","But Jiang Cheng was utterly ruthless.","She had already wiped out two cult strongholds in succession.","In front of all the residents, she exiled the cult leaders and their followersâto the courtyard.","People stood at every window on every floor.","Everyone watched as Mo Li swept those people out of the building with her tail, sending them tumbling into the snow.","They struggled to get back on their feet, but within just a few minutes, they froze to death.","Among them was a minor.","A middle school student.","Many people couldnât bear it and pleaded for mercy, hoping Jiang Cheng would spare the boyâs life.","But the boy had been brainwashed too deeply. He shouted, âThis is divine punishment! Divine punishment! Humanityâs sins are too great, so Heaven is cleansing the earth and restoring purity to the world! We must confess our sins! Why wonât you confess yours? Youââ","He was beyond saving.","Jiang Cheng remained unmoved.","âBlack Panther.â","The Black Panther sprang forward, bit down on the boy, and threw him outside.","When his body crashed through the heavy quilted curtain, a blast of frigid air swept inside, stinging everyoneâs faces.","From floor after floor, people watched helplessly as the boy died too.","Everyone had always known that Jiang Cheng was hard-hearted.","Again and again, Jiang Cheng proved just how cold her heart could beâand how ruthless her methods were.","Some people cowered fearfully within the crowd.","The two cults Jiang Cheng had eliminated were the most extreme ones.","Of course, she knew that all kinds of other religious groups, large and small, were hiding throughout the residential complex.","She turned to the people who had watched the execution in the cafeteria and said, âPass my words on to everyone.â","Her gaze swept over the entire crowd, crushing them beneath its weight.","âI will do everything in my power to help more people survive.â","âBelieve in whatever you want.â","âBut donât cause trouble.â","Su Yu returned to the dormitory from the cafeteria and told Zhang Lesi what she had seen.","Zhang Lesi hadnât gone downstairs, but she already knew roughly what had happened. The girls in the dormitory had also been pressed against the windowpanes, watching.","When those people froze stiff, they had all cried out in shock.","Many of them said, âServes them right!â","Those people believed in divine punishment and wanted to secretly kill virgins as sacrifices to Heaven.","They had set their sights on the middle school studentsâeven the little children.","That boy had nearly tricked one of his female classmates into going to her death.","He had even planned to sacrifice himself.","He thought his love was boundless and that he was incredibly noble."]},{"number":186,"title":"Chapter 186: 0186","paragraphs":["Zhang Lesi sneered. âWell, thatâs got everyone behaving themselves now, hasnât it?â","âA bunch of idiots. So what if that person can predict the future? In the end, werenât we all saved by our own efforts? Itâs not like he could crawl out of the radio and rescue us!â","âIf youâre going to deify someone, you might as well deify Jiang Cheng!â","âSeriously, if it hadnât been for Jiang Cheng, put anyone else in her place and they might not have been able to keep this many people alive!â","âExactly. Who else couldâve done it?â","Zhang Lesiâs voice was especially loud.","Su Yu knew she was saying it deliberately for the people in the dormitory to hear.","There were a lot of young girls here. At that age, their minds were still immature and easily influenced.","Zhang Lesi asked again, âWhereâs Jiang Cheng?â","Su Yu looked back. âWe were walking back together just nowâ¦ She doesnât seem to have come up?â","Jiang Chengâs bunk was empty.","An open book still lay facedown on it.","âHer bookâs here,â Su Yu said.","She picked it up and sighed. âSo Jiang Cheng reads books like this.â","Zhang Lesi knew what sort of books Jiang Cheng read.","After living together in the communal dormitory for several months, there werenât many secrets left between them.","Jiang Cheng read the kind of books that made peopleâs jaws drop. In Zhang Lesiâs view, those massive volumes were impossible to get through without settling down and focusing completely.","Most people simply couldnât calm their minds enough to read them. They didnât possess that level of insight, nor did they want to shoulder that kind of responsibility.","Su Yu flipped through the book to the page Jiang Cheng had left facedown and saw several lines underlined in red:","âDo not be intimidated by the enemyâs bluster.â","âDo not become disheartened by difficulties that can still be endured.â","âDo not lose heart over temporary setbacks.â (Authorâs note)","Su Yu read them in a daze.","But why had Jiang Cheng underlined these particular lines?","Could someone as unyielding as Jiang Cheng also become disheartened and lose heart, just like the rest of them?","What was going on? Jiang Cheng had once been nothing more than an ordinary neighbor, just like the rest of them.","When had they started taking it for granted that Jiang Cheng could withstand anything, that she would never experience any negative emotions like everyone else?","How could that be possible?","Jiang Cheng was human too.","Jiang Cheng was human.","That was why she hadnât returned to the communal dormitory.","She had gone back to her own place, lit the stove, and had sex with Mo Li.","Their bodies were slick with sweat.","The pressure was released.","Before the extreme cold arrived, Jiang Cheng and Mo Li had lived together and slept in the same bed, so they were already intimately familiar with each otherâs bodies.","But they had never actually had sex.","Mo Li was male, after all.","Cats had their own characteristics: a female had to go into heat before a male would enter it in response.","Since Jiang Cheng never had, Mo Li never had either.","This was their first time.","When Jiang Cheng returned to the communal dormitory, she found Su Yu reading to Zhang Lesi.","She passed by their bunks and greeted them on the way.","Zhang Lesiâs expression suddenly became rather peculiar.","âWas that Jiang Cheng just now?â she asked, lowering her voice to a whisper.","Su Yu answered, âYes.â","After finishing his work, Zhao Yi came to take Zhang Lesi for a walk in the hallway. Zhang Lesi couldnât keep it to herself and leaned over to whisper in his ear.","No one could resist the allure of gossip.","Especially gossip about Jiang Cheng.","Zhao Yi asked cautiously, âAre you sure?â","Zhang Lesi said, âI can recognize it with one sniff.â","Jiang Cheng was radiating the unmistakable scent of sex.","Zhang Lesi tugged at him. âWho do you think it was?â","She was dying of curiosity. She just had to know.","âThere are only two possibilities,â Zhao Yi said.","Zhang Lesi shoved him. âGo find out! Hurry! Tell me as soon as you know!â","It was actually very simple.","The timeline was clear: it had happened after the execution that day.","Jiang Cheng had obviously been emotional at the time, and then things had progressed from there.","Zhao Yi found out after asking just one question.","After the execution, Song Jingshuo had gone back to work. He had been with the older women.","Case closed!","Zhao Yi hurried off to report back to Zhang Lesi.","This was exciting.","It wouldnât have been nearly so exciting if it had been Song Jingshuo.","No matter how handsome Song Jingshuo was, he was still just a human man.","This time, it was a beastman.","There was simply too much to discuss!","The two of them found a corner and whispered together for quite some time.","At last, Zhang Lesi said insincerely, âDonât tell anyone else.â","Zhao Yi gave an equally insincere promise. âOf course. You either.â","Exactly.","To Zhang Lesi, Su Yu wasnât âanyone else.â","To Zhao Yi, Gao Yuxuan wasnât âanyone else.â","And to Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan, Li Jiangbing wasnât âanyone else.â","But they were all in complete agreement that Song Jingshuo was âsomeone else.â","He was the one person who absolutely must not be told!","So everyone who needed to know found out, with the sole exception of Song Jingshuo.","Unfortunately, Song Jingshuo discovered it himself.","Someone greeted him in passing and casually mentioned that Zhao Yi had been asking about him.","Zhao Yi hadnât come looking for him. He had asked where Song Jingshuo had been at a particular time.","The moment Song Jingshuo heard that, he knew something was suspicious.","He found Zhao Yi and pinned him against the hallway wall.","âWhatâs going on?â","Zhao Yi stammered, âW-What do you mean, whatâs going on?â","âCut the crap.â Song Jingshuo didnât bother being polite. âWhy were you asking where I was this afternoon?â","Zhao Yi averted his gaze.","Oh. There was definitely something going on.","âDonât make me use force,â Song Jingshuo warned.","Zhao Yi was no match for Song Jingshuo. After glancing around to make sure no one was nearby, he leaned in and whispered the whole story into Song Jingshuoâs ear.","Song Jingshuoâs expression turned grave.","Zhao Yi was extremely worried.","Why hadnât he told Song Jingshuo? Because Zhao Yi considered Song Jingshuo an âinvolved party.â Even if he hadnât technically been involved, he was at least connected to the matter.","The losing party.","They were afraid heâd take it badly.","Entirely unnecessary.","A womanizer and a hopeless romantic simply lived in completely different worlds. To Song Jingshuo, sex between consenting adults was no different from eating or drinking.","Song Jingshuo released Zhao Yi and sighed.","Zhao Yi cleared his throat, intending to offer him a few words of comfort.","But Song Jingshuo said, âWas she really under that much pressure?â","Zhao Yi was stunned.","Song Jingshuoâs brow furrowed.","âOf course,â he said. âWe donât feel the pressure as keenly because sheâs the one carrying it for us.â","She made every final decision.","She determined the direction they would take.","And if that direction was wrong, the consequences were unimaginable.","Everyone had overlooked just how much pressure that represented.","They simply took it for granted that she could handle it.","No one stopped to consider how many people had gone mad, how many had committed suicide, how many had sunk into sex addiction, how many had binged on food, or how many had fallen in with cults.","The refugees had been dwindling continuously, becoming nothing more than fertilizer.","The next day, while eating in the cafeteria, Song Jingshuo found Jiang Cheng.","âIâd like to say something to Jiang Cheng,â he announced.","Everyone immediately took the hint and moved to another table, leaving the two of them alone.","Jiang Cheng lowered her head and drank her hot soy milk. âWhat is it?â","Song Jingshuo said, âIâm reminding you to be careful about contraception.â","Jiang Cheng didnât even look up. âYou found out pretty quickly.â","She thought for a moment. âZhang Lesi, I assume.â","She had guessed it in one try.","Bathing was inconvenient these days, and Zhang Lesiâs senses were exceptionally sharp. This wasnât the first time she had smelled out an affair.","Jiang Cheng clearly wasnât one of the hopeless romantics.","Just as Song Jingshuo had thought, it had been nothing more than a way to relieve stress.","Nearly ten months had passed since the time at the clubhouse gym when she had said coolly, âWe havenât reached the point where sex is necessary to alleviate and soothe the psychological stress caused by the threat of death.â","Now, for her, they had finally reached that point.","âWhatâs gotten into you?â Song Jingshuo asked. âWhy are you so irritable? Is it because of those people?â","âYes.â Jiang Cheng raised her eyes. âTheir weakness disgusts me.â","The weakness of the human heart.","They thought they were being so noble. In reality, it was their inner weakness that allowed heretical ideas to take root in their minds and made them believe them as truth.","When an entire group displayed such foolishness and weakness, it was truly repulsive to her.","The corner of Song Jingshuoâs mouth twitched.","Jiang Cheng said, âIf you have something to say, say it.â","Song Jingshuo put it bluntly: âAn elitist mindset.â","Jiang Cheng was momentarily taken aback.","Song Jingshuo said, âI think weâve both changed a lot over these ten months. Youâve changed a great deal too. And yet this elitist mindset is still there.â","Elites often pretended to be part of the masses, one of the masses.","But in truth, they looked down on the masses. They believed themselves to be superior, convinced that they were a cut above the rest.","Sometimes, they even despised the masses.","The disgust Jiang Cheng spoke of was, to a certain extent, contemptâa revulsion born of contempt.","Elites considered themselves outstanding, even perfect, and always viewed the massesâ lack of excellence and their imperfections with a harsh, critical eye.","Jiang Cheng stared blankly at the half bowl of soybean milk left in front of her.","After a long while, Song Jingshuo finished his soybean milk. Jiang Cheng let out a long breath.","She said, âItâs really hard to put knowledge into practice.â","It was all too easy to lose touch with the people.","She looked up. Walkways jutted diagonally between the buildings, crisscrossing one another.","She turned around. Someone was dragging a gray, wheeled ash bin, going floor by floor to clear the ashes from the stoves in the heated corridors and stairwells and replenish their coal, ensuring that the entire building stayed warm.","None of this could have been accomplished by her alone.","It had clearly been accomplished by everyone.","Yet because of a small handful of foolish people, she had overlooked the greater whole.","She had actually allowed herself to be controlled by such emotions.","Just as Jiang Cheng lifted the remaining half bowl of soybean milk to her lips, she suddenly stopped.","A realization struck her.","So this was what they had been waiting for.","They had trapped everyone inside like burrowing animals beneath the cover of this bitter cold, waiting for this momentâ","Waiting for her state of mind to collapse.","Jiang Cheng raised her eyesâ¦","But what if her state of mind did not collapse?","Jiang Cheng held on to her composure. Three days later, the mysterious man on the radio finally changed his tune.","He said: âItâs going to end.â","The words quickly spread through every residential compound, throwing the residents into an uproar.","âHe said itâs ending. Is that true?â","âIs he talking about this hellish weather?â","âProbably. He was the one who predicted it in the first place.â","And so, the night before, everyone had still remembered to add coal to the stove before going to bed.","But at dawn, they were all woken by the heat.","Everyone was bewildered. They had not added any extra coal, so how had it suddenly become so warm?","Wearing only her long underwear, Jiang Cheng got out of bed and walked to the window. With a swish, she pulled open the curtains.","Everyone instinctively raised a hand to shield their eyes.","Snow reflected the sunlight, making it painfully dazzling.","But they soon realized that something was different.","Someone else, wearing slippers, climbed out of bed and ran to the window. Standing beside Jiang Cheng, they stared out at the scene without moving.","Suddenly, she whirled around and shouted, âThe snow is melting! The snow is melting!â","Everyone went mad, crowding toward the windows to look.","The snowdrifts that had stood higher than a person when they went to bed the previous night had all melted.","Mud and meltwater covered the ground.","Sunlight streamed through the windows, warm against their skin.","There were already specks of green on the treetops and branches.","The world had gone from a bitterly cold winter to a spring teeming with new life in the space of a single night.","Jiang Cheng gave the rising sun a cold smile.","Note: From Quotations."]},{"number":187,"title":"Chapter 187: 0187","paragraphs":["When the sky turned purple for the third time, raging flames engulfed the city, Mo Li transformed into human form, and all water, electricity, gas, and communications were cut off. Humanity was forced to abandon the city and move elsewhere.","Jiang Cheng was confused by these events and assumed that this was the third stage.","It was not until Song Jingshuo pointed it out that she realized the truth.","Sure enough, the moment she steadied her mind and made sure her emotions did not collapse, the extreme cold vanished.","The sun came out. The sky cleared. Spring arrived.","She was being observed.","She was being seen.","She was being watched.","Jiang Cheng sneered.","Sure enough, everything was happening because of her.","Were the people watching from behind the scenes treating her and everyone else here as some kind of entertainment?","Like crickets in a jar.","Like fighting roosters in a cage.","Everyone poured out of the buildings.","The earth-element superpowered individuals dismantled all the covered walkways in the courtyard. The courtyard became spacious again.","People took off their down jackets, padded coats, and cotton trousers, then stomped wildly through the muddy water, laughing, shouting, and celebrating.","Song Jingshuo tossed several saplings into the mud.","Strawberries, grapes, apples, mangoes, and pears quickly took root, grew, and bore fruit.","Clusters and piles of them.","Everyone swarmed over to pick and eat them, juice running down their chins.","They sang, danced, and threw mud.","Then someone came to his senses and warned, âStop throwing it. There might be shit mixed in.â","Everyone fell silent.","Then an overwhelming barrage of mud flew straight at him!","The collective dormitory in the youth apartment complex was disbanded. Everyone began moving back into the homes they had lived in before.","At Auspicious Garden, everyone was also in high spirits as they carried their mattresses back into the bedrooms. No one had to squeeze together and sleep in the living room anymore.","The windows were opened for ventilation, and the air was fresh and clean. The rooms no longer reeked.","It felt as though they had returned from merely âbeing aliveâ to actually living.","From the outbreak of the extreme cold in October to its end in March after the New Year, the population of the Technology New District had fallen from more than thirty thousand to twenty-four thousand.","Half of those lost had committed suicide.","Everyone regretted that those people might have survived if only they had held on a little longer.","But human beings could be weak and fragile sometimes.","Besides, who said that holding on until the end meant victory?","The mysterious man said: âRun! Run! If you donât get away now, itâll be too late!â","Uncle Jiang said: âThey might as well drive everyone to their deaths.â","Sister Mao said, âWhatâs coming this time? It sounds like they just donât want anyone to live.â","That was everyoneâs question too. What was coming next?","The mysterious manâs broadcast cooled everyoneâs celebration of having âwon.â","Everyone was on edge.","Who exactly was this person? A prophet?","If so, what was coming that people would not be able to escape from?","Zheng Junwei and the leaders of several settlements communicated with Jiang Cheng by radio.","Everyoneâs mood was heavy.","No one knew where the next disaster would come from or what form it would take.","The unknown was the most terrifying thing of all.","Zhao Yi and Zhang Lesi also moved back into Zhang Lesiâs house.","Zhang Lesi stretched out across her own bed in a starfish position and sighed. âMy own bed really is the most comfortable!â","The quality of life in the collective dormitory had been truly terrible.","Everyone had stunk.","Zhao Yi and Zhang Lesi had both gone to the bathhouse to wash today.","The women had scrubbed each otherâs backs, and now they were all clean, fresh, and fragrant.","Zhang Lesi and Zhao Yi had also finally been able to have uninhibited sex again after such a long time. Both of them were still bursting with vitality.","They were young, after all.","Or perhaps it was the craziness that came before an unknown danger.","After all, no one knew when death would come knocking.","For example, if the extreme cold suddenly made a comeback right now, the two of them would freeze to death in their own home.","So Zhang Lesi said, âWe still have to get dressed. Even if death means the end of everything, I still donât want anyone to find me dead naked.â","Zhao Yi said, âActually, when they bury you, theyâllââ","âShut up!â","Zhao Yi obediently shut his mouth.","The two of them still put on proper clothes before going to sleep. They decided against sleeping naked, just in case they died in an undignified pose.","After lying there for a while, Zhang Lesi asked, âIf things really are as you said, then after we die, will we go to another world?â","Before Zhao Yi could answer, she continued, âMaybe aliens will come and capture us all. Right?â","Over the long months, Zhao Yi had told Zhang Lesi all his conjectures and theories.","As expected, Zhang Lesi could not resonate with him instantly the way Gao Yuxuan had. But she liked his capacity for âimagination.â","Zhao Yi asked, âDonât you believe me?â","Zhang Lesi stubbornly replied, âIâm just saying, hypothetically.â","âMaybe,â Zhao Yi said.","Zhang Lesi was silent for a while before finally admitting, âIâm starting to believe it a little.â","In the span of one night and one day, they had gone from extreme cold straight into spring.","Zhang Lesi was a medical student, a top scholar. She would never foolishly put her faith in a cult, but she understood very clearly that while the spread of the zombie virus had still fallen within the realm of human capability, the sudden arrival and disappearance of this extreme cold were absolutely beyond human control.","And yet the traces of human manipulation were so strong and obvious.","It was a force beyond known science, beyond the government, beyond this planetâa higher level of power.","The two possibilities Zhao Yi had proposed were both plausible.","Aliens, or a higher-dimensional world.","âWhatever. Iâm telling you, if we suddenly croak and wake up in some higher-dimensional world, donât even think about running away.â Zhang Lesi huffed. âIâll find you even if you run to the ends of the earth.â","Zhao Yi laughed and turned over to embrace her. âWhy would I run?â","He gently kissed her hair and held her tenderly as they fell asleep together.","Everyone was asleep. After months of oppressive, grueling living conditions, everyone had finally returned to their own beds, and they slept more comfortably than ever.","The clock on the wall ticked on.","Tick.","Tock.","At four oâclock, Little Huang suddenly opened his eyes!","Danger!","Danger!","The boy wanted to warn everyone, but his superpower erupted violently.","His ability was to sense danger.","Danger filled the world from every direction!","There was no way out. Everywhere was death!","Death!","Little Huang opened his mouth like a drowning fish. He wanted to shout and scream, but no sound came out.","He died with his mouth hanging open.","If Zhang Lesi had been there, she would have described Little Huangâs death as fear triggering a massive surge of stress hormones such as adrenaline and cortisol, accelerating his heart rate and shortening diastole. The heart muscle received less oxygen, eventually causing cardiac arrest.ãNoteã","In laymanâs termsâ¦","He had been scared to death.","At four in the morning, while everyone else slept soundly, Little Huang was frightened to death by his own superpower.","His mouth hung open, his eyes remained wide, and his face was filled with terror.","â¦","A few minutes later, cement structures cracked and steel bars groaned.","The earth roared like a gigantic beast awakening!","Mo Li opened his eyes only two minutes after Little Huang.","In an instant, he shot upright, scooped up the sleeping Jiang Cheng around the waist, and leaped through the floor-to-ceiling window from the third story!","Jiang Cheng woke the moment he was lifted. The enormous sound of shattering glass and the sensation of weightlessness followed immediately.","The next second, Mo Li landed safely with her in his arms.","Jiang Chengâs hand sank into the wet mud. She raised her head, just about to ask what was happening, when she lost her balance and fell to the ground.","The earth was shaking so violently that standing was impossible.","The ground tilted, and Jiang Cheng rolled toward the lower side, her body completely beyond her control.","Mo Li sprang lightly into the air, scooped Jiang Cheng up into his arms, and leaped high to avoid the sudden upheaval and rupture of the ground.","Reinforced concrete shattered. Buildings collapsed. The courtyard caved in, exposing the densely packed bones of zombies buried beneath it!","In an instant, the deeper layers gave way, and the zombie remains plunged into the underground parking garage!","Then the depths collapsed again. Bones and private cars tumbled toward a pitch-black fissure with no visible bottom!","Many people were claimed by death before they even had time to wake.","The roar of destruction and the screams of the living merged in the night.","There was no electricity. Darkness swallowed everything.","An unseen god of death harvested lives in the darkness.","No one knew which fire-element superpowered person began conjuring fireballs, but at last there was light.","One fireball after another flared to life, swaying in the air. Some were snuffed out and vanished.","Countless voices cried out amid the rumbling, but no one could make out what they were saying.","The shockwave left people temporarily deaf.","The ground flexed like the plastic ruler they used to bend with a fingertip in school, then release. It trembled and rebounded in waves.","People were flung into the air as easily as though they had lost all weight, smashed against walls, and rolled to the ground, where falling chunks of concrete crushed them into bloody pulp.","The world was being torn apart.","From the tops of skyscrapers to the depths underground.","Screams came from everywhere.","The ground tilted, and floor slabs snapped one after another.","People clawed at the concrete until their fingernails split and bled, but there was nothing for them to grip. Floors buckled upward, gravity dragged bodies across them, and people screamed as they slid into the cracks and fell.","One after another, like dumplings dropping into a pot.","âHold on tight! Tighter!â Su Yu shouted.","Because of the mysterious manâs rambling prophecy, she had felt uneasy and had taken the initiative to sleep with the little ones that night.","Everything happened too quickly. In the instant they opened their eyes, some of the children had already lost their lives.","There was no time. There simply wasnât.","The protective barrier she threw up in an instant could shield only four girls.","They clung tightly to Su Yu in a single bundle because the barrier had an âinsideâ and an âoutside.â","From the âinside,â they could pass freely through the barrier to the âoutside.â","But if they were thrown away during the massive quake, they would leave the protection of the barrier.","Su Yu alone could not be forced out of it, so everyone held on to one another. No matter how violently they were tossed about, none of them would be flung free.","Su Yu glanced up.","A massive concrete floor slab came crashing down, ready to flatten them into bloody pulp.","Su Yu stared at it without blinking.","White light burst in every direction, illuminating the night.","Song Jingshuo also lived on one of the upper floors.","The shaking was so violent that he could not even crawl. He struck his head, and blood streamed down his face.","Song Jingshuo slapped his left hand against the blood dripping onto the floor. The vine bracelet around his wrist, patterned with a single green leaf, absorbed the human blood and suddenly grew explosively.","Roots as fine as threads shot toward every planting container in the room, burrowing into them and drawing out their nutrients.","The vines thickened until they were as large as dragons. With a thunderous crash, they tore through the already-crumbling walls, wrapped around Song Jingshuo, and carried him out of the building as they spread wildly downward.","Zhao Yi dragged Zhang Lesi along as he ran!","He knew he could not let go. Zhang Lesi could not see!","In truth, he could not see either. The stairwell was pitch-black. But the darker it was, the more tightly he had to hold Zhang Lesiâs hand.","The reinforced concrete twisted and writhed.","Humans were as helpless as leaves caught by the wind.","The two of them were hurled against the ceiling, then slammed brutally back onto the floor.","Zhao Yiâs head rang. His shoulders, back, chest, and knees all throbbed with pain. He instinctively tightened his grip, but his hand closed on empty air.","âLesi!â Zhao Yi opened his eyes and looked up. âLesi!â","There was light now. Fireballs of every size floated above, below, and outside the building, their glow spilling in through the gaps.","The building had split vertically. He was on one side, Zhang Lesi on the other, with the middle collapsing between them.","She lay facedown at the edge of the break, as though she had lost consciousness.","âLesiâ!â Zhao Yi shouted.","He struggled to his feet and activated his superpower. The concrete floor rapidly extended toward Zhang Lesi, forming a bridge.","Amid the violent shaking, Zhao Yi ran toward her. âLesiâ!â","Zhang Lesi had followed Zhao Yi as they fled for their lives, and she hated herself for it.","Why couldnât she see yet? Why had she become a burden to someone else?","The tremendous force sent waves surging through the ground, tossing her and Zhao Yi against the ceiling before hurling them back onto the floor.","Zhang Lesi was battered to the brink of unconsciousness.","She heard someone shouting her name.","âLesiâ! Lesiâ!â","Zhang Lesi struggled to raise her head and saw light.","Everything shifted from a blur into focus.","The man she loved was screaming her name with all his strength. He had built a bridge of concrete across the gap and was racing toward her.","âLesiâ!â","It was exactly like the love she had always imagined.","Love was supposed to be grand and earth-shaking.","Zhang Lesi smiled.","Then she watched, eyes wide open, as the half of the building behind Zhao Yi tilted and collapsed.","The concrete bridge broke apart.","Zhao Yi ran, leaped, and launched himself into the air.","âLeâsiâ!â","He reached out toward her.","Zhang Lesi pushed herself up and reached out toward him as wellâ","But in the end, their hands never met.","Everything seemed to slow to a crawl. Zhang Lesi blinked once.","Zhao Yi fell.","Then time suddenly sped up again.","The next instant, Zhang Lesi jumped after him.","Without the slightest hesitation.","If they were going to die, then so be it. It was worth it.","She had always said she had excellent taste in men.","[Note: The medical descriptions in this passage are based on information gathered from online sources.]"]},{"number":188,"title":"Chapter 188: 0188","paragraphs":["In a disaster like an earthquake, earth-type users were probably the hardest to kill.","Zhang Lesi leapt after Zhao Yi.","At last, their hands clasped. Zhao Yi pulled Zhang Lesi into his arms.","He stretched out his other hand. The collapsed floor slabs and shattered concrete surged and grew wildly, chasing the two of them as they plunged downward. The concrete reached diagonally beneath them.","Zhao Yi slapped his hand against it.","All superpowers could be used at a distance, but activating them through direct contact caused almost no loss of energy and was the most efficient method.","They were falling too fast! The concrete chased after them in a frenzy!","It caught their shoulders.","Then their backs.","Then their waists.","Then their legs.","Changing the angle! Slowing their descent!","The concrete slide Zhao Yi created with all his strength finally brought the two of them safely to the ground.","But it immediately broke apart and came crashing down on top of them.","Zhao Yi was horrified. Acting on instinct, he pulled Zhang Lesi tightly into his arms.","A hand reached out.","The enormous building debris vanished into thin air.","Zhao Yi opened his eyes.","Jiang Cheng yanked Zhang Lesi away and shouted at Zhao Yi, âGo save people!â","They desperately needed an earth-type user now.","Zhao Yi roared, âKeep an eye on her!â","Then he turned and ran.","Buildings collapsed. Debris fell. Dust billowed everywhere.","Jiang Cheng screamed with all her might, âGet over here! Get over here!â","She raised both hands above her head. A black dot quickly expanded into a disk, then, in the next instant, erupted into a gigantic black disk dozens of meters across.","People could see the âblackâ because it was suspended high overhead, where it could be viewed in its entirety from below.","It was a bottomless blackness.","The surrounding night was already dark, yet this blackness was so stark and distinct.","But if someone could look at it from the side, at the same height, they would see nothing at all.","Its thickness was zero.","The enormous wreckage of the collapsing buildings thundered downward and vanished into the black disk.","It looked like an invisible bottomless pit.","And it truly was a bottomless pit, because this was the visible manifestation of the entrance to Jiang Chengâs extradimensional space.","Everyone knew that Jiang Cheng was a space-type superhuman with a higher-dimensional storage space.","Normally, that space needed no âentrance.â Whenever Jiang Cheng wanted to store something, it vanished inside in an instant.","But now, in front of everyone, Jiang Cheng had opened the entrance to her extradimensional space. With a diameter of dozens of meters, it was large enough to shelter many people.","Shattered concrete and twisted steel bars came crashing down, all of them swallowed up.","It was like a black hole.","The people hid beneath it and were finally safe.","At that moment, white light lit up on the other side of the courtyard.","A holy protective barrier rose into place, equally enormous, sheltering the survivors.","Some people ran toward the light. Others ran toward the black hole.","Those who were too slow were crushed to death beneath falling concrete.","Two buildings collapsed completely. Four others were reduced to half-buildings, swaying precariously.","People cried and screamed as they hung from the ruins or plunged downward, convinced they were going to die.","A huge slide made of packed earth rose from the ground.","Those who landed on its slope were in excruciating pain, but they survived, sliding all the way down to the ground.","Thick vines burst from the soil as if they had come alive, writhing like monstrous serpents. Countless tendrils stretched out and wrapped around one person after another, rescuing those clinging to broken walls and on the verge of falling.","Water was drawn out of the muddy wetlands formed by the melting snow. It gathered into a watery dragon, spiraling upward like a tornado.","Those who fell were swept into the water dragon. Spinning rapidly, their downward momentum was canceled, and they landed safely.","âOver there! Go over thereââ Li Jiangbing bellowed.","Those who landed safely scrambled away, either running toward Su Yu or Jiang Cheng to seek shelter.","Metal rods thrust up from the ground one after another, piercing into buildings that were about to collapse.","The survivors slid down the rods one by one.","Mo Li had already transformed into a giant cat.","He was huge, yet still agile. He leapt into the air and caught a falling person in his jaws, then set them down after landing.","Then he charged toward the shattered walls and rubble. In the blink of an eye, he climbed more than a dozen stories, carrying survivors down in a blur.","Everyone with the ability to help was rescuing people.","Aunt Pan and Zhao Yi, both earth-types, Song Jingshuo, a wood-type, Cui Haiyang, a metal-type, and Li Jiangbing, a water-type, all gave everything they had. Even Mo Li was doing his part.","The fire-types lit fireballs to illuminate the darkness.","They continued until the sun rose, and the morning light stabbed into Jiang Chengâs eyes.","The night receded.","All six buildings had collapsed. The high-rises that had once stood tall had become enormous heaps of rubble, and there was no longer any danger raining down from above.","Jiang Cheng withdrew her spatial portal. Su Yu withdrew her protective barrier.","Both of them collapsed to the ground.","Zhang Lesi examined the two of them and healed the bruises they had sustained from falling and colliding with things. âTheyâre fine. Theyâre just exhausted.â","She was exhausted too.","Everyone formed a line and waited for her treatment. Many people had broken bones and could not move, so they lay in the mud and waited for her.","Those who had already been healed stood barefoot in the mud and among the broken pieces of concrete, staring around blankly. Everywhere they looked, the high-rises were gone.","The Youth Apartments, Jixiang Jiayuan, Yujing Xiangyuanâeven Mai Duoduo Supermarket.","And the overpass in the distance.","Everything had become ruins.","Zhou Wang also sat on the rubble, staring blankly.","Mr. Xu had survived. After searching for a long time, he found only Wu Yan.","Everyone else was dead.","Death had taken Tao Xiaoxiao once. Then it had taken Tao Xiaoxiao a second time. This time, it had finally taken her away for good.","Everyone was lost.","That feeling of numb bewilderment was shared by all.","Jiang Cheng was the first to wake up.","Mo Li had already returned to human form, and Li Jiangbing had found him some clothes.","His human form was certainly less effective in battle than his cat form, but when it came to taking care of Jiang Cheng, a human was obviously better than a cat.","Jiang Cheng swallowed the ball of water Li Jiangbing tossed her. Her first question was, âHow is Su Yu?â","Li Jiangbing said, âSheâs fine. She passed out from exhaustion, just like you.â","The impact of the collapsing building had been tremendous. In fact, every bone in Su Yuâs body had been fractured.","Zhang Lesi had healed her. Now they were simply waiting for her to wake up.","Jiang Cheng nodded and, leaning on Mo Li, stood up.","Her bare feet were covered in mud. She stepped on steel bars and concrete, climbed to a slightly higher position, and looked as far as she could in every direction.","Everyone who was still alive looked at her.","Their eyes had lost all their spirit.","In the distance, Jiang Cheng could even see people from Jixiang Jiayuan looking in their direction.","With the high-rises gone, the world seemed to have suddenly opened up, vast and boundless.","From one place to another, everything looked so far away.","Someone approached and asked, âJiang Cheng, what are we supposed to do now?â","Jiang Cheng looked into those lifeless eyes.","Her companions had once been so passionate, so optimistic, so full of vitality.","She wanted to say something impassioned and inspiring to encourage everyone.","But what could she say?","Should she tell them, âThe misfortune you suffered today was all caused by my existenceâ?","Jiang Cheng closed her eyes.","âFirst, we survive,â she said.","When she opened her eyes again, they were calm and utterly still.","âWater.â","âFood.â","âShelter.â","âWarmth.â","âIn that order,â she said.","When people were lost and bewildered, being given instructions made them begin to move mechanically.","Cui Haiyang was still alive. He began building water tanks.","Li Jiangbing was still alive. He drew pure water from the mud and the moisture in the air.","Song Jingshuo was still alive. He walked barefoot through the muddy ground, stopping every so often. Each time he did, a plant pushed its way out of the soil beside his feet.","One plant found. Then another.","Aunt Pan and Zhao Yi were still alive. They quietly discussed where they should build houses.","The entire residential compound was filled with ruinsâbroken walls and shattered remnants of buildings several stories high.","Most importantly, the ground had split open. The depths of the fissures were pitch-black and seemed unfathomably deep. A massive crack cut diagonally through the entire residential complex, extending all the way to Jixiang Jiayuan.","âLetâs take a look at the road,â Jiang Cheng said.","They exited through the east gate and headed north along Jixiang West Street, toward the road directly opposite the entrance to the Maiduo Supermarket.","The government of the High-Tech New District had spared no expense, so the road was exceptionally wide.","Of course, the east gate was gone now, and so was the supermarket.","After the metal-type superpowered individuals yanked out all the railings dividing the middle of the road, the broad avenue, now without its barriers, looked more like a plaza.","Aunt Pan and Zhao Yi went over to inspect it. Although the road was covered in cracks and large sections of asphalt had buckled upward, there were nowhere near as many collapsed walls and ruins as inside the residential complex, where the debris had piled up like mountains.","It was considerably flatter, all things considered.","Aunt Pan and Zhao Yi called Cui Haiyang over to build a shelter.","Nothing elaborateâjust four walls and a roof would do.","Everyone else searched through the ruins for food, clothing, or survivors.","It was unlikely that there were any survivors left.","But everyone clung to that last sliver of hope.","Suddenly, someone called Jiang Chengâs name. âJiang ChengâJiang Chengâcome listen to this!â","Jiang Cheng stood up, her hands and legs going weak.","Mo Li carried her on his back and bounded across the ruins, reaching the spot where the voice had come from in just a few leaps.","The person there said, âListenââ","Everyone who had followed them held their breath and dared not make a sound.","Gradually, they all heard it.","That familiar voice, buried beneath the ruins.","ãRunâã","ãEndâã","Jiang Cheng stared at the rubble and told Mo Li, âBring Aunt Pan over.â","Mo Li hurried off, then hurried back with Aunt Pan slung over his shoulder.","Zhao Yi and Cui Haiyang followed behind, panting. âWhat happened?â","Once they arrived, they understood what they needed to do.","Aunt Pan crouched down and listened carefully. After confirming the location, she placed her hand on the ground.","The rubble and chunks of concrete parted to either side until one corner of a room was exposed.","It was, at least, one corner that had remained intact.","A shortwave radio lay in the triangular space, crackling with static.","ãIt isnât over yet.ã","ãYou must escape.ã","The mysterious person repeated the same words again and again:","ãI told you to run. Why arenât you running? It isnât over yet. You have to get awayâquickly. If you donât run, youâll die. Youâll die.ã","Everyone stood at different heights amid the ruins, their faces expressionless as they listened to the mysterious voice.","Were they afraid?","Fear had its limits, and theirs had probably already been exhausted.","So they could no longer feel fear. All that remained was numbness.","Jiang Cheng stared at the shortwave radio and suddenly called out, âGao Yuxuan.â","Gao Yuxuan was lost in thought and started when he heard his name. He stepped forward. âJiang Cheng?â","Jiang Cheng asked, âCan this thing still make noise without power?â","âOf course not. We specially modified it to run on a car batteryâ¦â Gao Yuxuanâs voice trailed off.","They had modified the shortwave radio to use a car battery as its power source.","But now the wires were severed, and the battery was nowhere to be found.","Yet the radio continued to operate.","The mysterious person kept repeating:","ãI told you to run. Why arenât you running?ã","So youâre dropping the act now, huh?","Jiang Cheng laughed.","âWho are you?â she asked.","Of course, one couldnât actually speak to a radio like that.","It was a radio, not a phone on speaker mode.","This was a simplex radio. One party had to finish speaking before the other could respond.","Someone had to press the button.","Gao Yuxuanâs lips moved slightly.","The mysterious voice answered through the radio:","ãWho I am isnât important. What matters is that if you donât leave now, youâll all die. Get out of here.ã"]},{"number":189,"title":"Chapter 189: 0189","paragraphs":["Every country has its own circumstances.","From the very beginning, everyone knew that they could never flee in the way families did in foreign disaster moviesâjumping into their cars and driving away at the first sign of trouble.","Not every household in the country owned a private car, and there was nowhere for them to escape to anyway.","From the start, everyone had agreed without question on the fundamental principle:","Defend their homes.","From the first Youth Apartments, to the second expansion that encompassed the entire Tech New District, to the various districts responding in turn and establishing several survivor settlementsâ","Now the mysterious man wanted to force them to leave.","To make them abandon the base they had defended for so long.","[Difficulty increased.]","Then how exactly would this trial determine victory or defeat?","Or did victory and defeat even exist?","Perhaps the result did not matter at all.","Perhaps the only thing that mattered was watching the process.","Zhao Yi stepped forward and fired off his questions. âWhat do you want? What are you trying to get from us? What are your demands?â","Unfortunately, the shortwave radio no longer answered him. It began repeating in a loop:","[It isnât over yet. Escape from here.]","Zhao Yi was deeply disappointed.","He had desperately wanted to make contact with a higher life-form.","He was intensely curious about another civilizationâor another world.","No one dared approach the shortwave radio.","For it to make a sound without any power sourceâby the standards of the Chinese people, that was obviously a haunting.","Only Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan were unafraid. Together, they carried the thing to a newly built house beside the road.","Zhao Yi even built a stand for it and placed it right in the middle of the room.","Inside the empty house, the crackle of electrical interference continued without pause as the mysterious man repeated the same words again and again.","People from the surrounding area began drifting toward the house.","By noon, survivors from the other residential compounds had arrived as well.","The people who had survived had no idea what they should do or where they should go, so they instinctively made their way to the Youth Apartments.","All this time, the Youth Apartments had been like a lighthouse.","Whenever people did not know what to do, they naturally came here.","A rough count showed that the Tech New District had originally housed twenty-four thousand people. Just over four thousand had survived.","Twenty thousand were gone.","Many familiar faces were missing.","At the Youth Apartments, two of the old core members, Wu Jiancheng and Guo Jun, were nowhere to be found.","Of the original property-management staff, only Aunt Pan remained. Manager Wang, Yang Xinyan, and Little Fang were all gone.","Of the little children, only four girls and two boys remained.","Zeng Qiang and Master Luo were nowhere to be found either.","When they said someone was ânowhere to be found,â they meant that there was neither a living person nor a corpse to be found.","Brother Dong from Auspicious Garden had not made it out in time.","As a wind-type ability user, he should have had one of the highest chances of survival. Zhou Wang had survived by jumping straight out of a window.","But Brother Dong had traded for alcohol the day before. He had drunk far too much and was still suffering from a hangover.","When the earthquake struck, he had not woken up at all.","Little Huang was dead.","His death had been confirmed because Zhou Wang and Little Huang had always lived together. One had lost his parents, while the other had lost his wife and child.","The two of them had been like father and son.","When the earthquake struck, Zhou Wang had rushed into Little Huangâs bedroom and dragged him out with him before jumping from the building.","He had never let go.","It was only after the earthquake stopped that he realized Little Huang had died long ago.","Auntie Xue, a wood-type ability user, was nowhere to be found.","Auntie Qian had survived.","She was elderly and slept lightly for only a few hours at a time. She had been awake when the earthquake struck.","Knowing that her legs were too weak to run, she had used the vines she kept indoors to form a ball around herself, then curled up in the corner.","The triangular space formed by three intersecting walls was structurally stable.","The shortwave radio had also been found in such a triangular space.","In any case, Auntie Qian had survived.","Of the more than twenty people at Mr. Xuâs company, only he and Wu Yan had survived.","Uncle Eighty, a metal-type ability user, had survived at first, but died while rescuing others.","Wang Yunya had been rescued, but her mother, Xiao Dan, was nowhere to be found.","Many people were like Wang Yunya, walking around as if their souls had left their bodies.","Jiang Cheng took food out of her storage space, and the people from the Youth Apartments distributed it to everyone.","Many survivors did not even know to line up. They wandered aimlessly like ghosts, some muttering incoherently under their breath.","The people from the Youth Apartments had to force the food into their hands.","âEat!â","They lowered their heads and ate.","The houses had already been built.","They were extremely simple, box-shaped structures. Inside, there were only two rows of bare, hard bunk beds.","Each room could accommodate thirty or forty people.","Several long rows of houses stood along the main road, looking like matchboxes.","After everyone had eaten their fill, Li Jiangbing called out âJianchengâ twice in a row. When no one answered, he remembered that Wu Jiancheng was gone.","If someone was nowhere to be found, they were most likely dead.","Li Jiangbing stood there in a daze for a long while.","It was only when another fire-type ability user tactfully approached and asked, âDo you need fire?â that Li Jiangbing finally gave a small nod.","âHeat some water so everyone can wash,â he said.","Everyone was filthy. They were barefoot, covered from head to toe in mud and dirt.","By then, the survivors had already recovered a great deal of clothing and footwear from the ruins. Some of it had even been stripped from corpses.","The temperature was around seventeen or eighteen degrees Celsiusâthe temperature of spring. Under normal circumstances, people would still have needed light jackets.","Many were wearing pajamas or autumn undershirts and long johns.","Li Jiangbing had already rinsed and dried all the clothing and shoes.","But at this temperature, no one could wash with cold water, so he had called on the fire-type ability users to heat it. It did not need to be hotâjust warm was enough.","They had not done this in a long time. Going through the motions again actually made them feel a little nostalgic.","Most of the refugees had washed this way back then, and they all knew what to do. They lined up, one after another, stepped into a warm ball of water, rolled around in it for a while, then came out. The water was drained from their bodies immediately, and they collected clothes before finding shoes in a suitable size.","For many people, they had to be herded over to the washing area.","But after washing themselves, finding clean clothes and shoes, and keeping busy, the survivors gradually seemed to regain their senses.","At temperatures in the teens, the rooms were actually colder than outdoors.","Each room had been equipped with an iron coal stove.","Jiang Cheng took out coal.","In the past, the temporary government of the Tech New District had maintained its own large warehouse. But all the core members knew that Jiang Chengâs storage space was their backup supply depot.","It contained nearly every basic survival necessity imaginable.","The only thing people did not know was how much she actually had.","Song Jingshuo was probably the only one who had a rough idea.","Temporary toilets had also been built.","They were out in the open, surrounded by walls, with no doors and a screen wall for privacy.","Drinking-water storage tanks had been constructed as well.","Song Jingshuo found watermelon seedlings and immediately grew dozens of large watermelons.","After the heavy snow brought by the extreme cold melted, the ground was muddy everywhere and the air was saturated with moisture. This made it very convenient for Li Jiangbing to conjure water from thin air, and for Song Jingshuo to grow fruits with such a high water content.","They quenched thirst and replenished sugar.","Eating sugar made it easy for people to relax.","Under the organization of the Youth Apartments, the basic necessities required for survival were all provided in an extremely short period of time: the water, food, shelter, and warmth Jiang Cheng had demanded.","Once people had eaten their fill, put on warm clothes, and sat inside a clean, roofed room with a fire burning in the stove, they began to feel as if they had come back to life.","Their eyes slowly regained focus and vitality.","They were still alive. That was all that mattered.","Most people had mainly been frightened out of their wits. But in reality, when they had first arrived here several months earlier, they had already been refugees.","Those who had suffered the loss of loved ones, like Wang Yunya, were actually in the minority. Most people had already lost their loved ones several months ago.","Of course, some temporary couples, friends they had made later, and couples who had gotten together during the ordeal were grieving too.","But this wasnât their first time experiencing it.","Once everyone had gotten their bearings, they naturally entered a state of standby, waiting for Jiang Cheng of the Youth Apartments to give them their next instructions.","That was how things had always been.","There had to be someone to tell everyone what to do and how to do it.","And that person had always been Jiang Cheng of the Youth Apartments.","Jiang Cheng and all the surviving core members were in the room where the haunted radio was broadcasting.","No one had tuned it in. The radio had switched over to Uncle Jiang and Sister Mao by itself.","ãYou canât go north. The north has split open into a massive canyon, turning it into an impassable chasm.ã","ãYou canât go south either. The southern continental shelf has sunk, pushing the coastline inland by hundreds of miles. The rivers have all been flooded backward by seawater.ã","ãGo west, toward the plateau. You can survive there.ã","ãSurvive my ass! The cold air has shifted over there. If we go there, weâll have to endure freezing weather and a miserable life all over again. Weâre practically about to become cave-dwelling humans!ã","ãItâs still better than the east. Donât you know a Corpse Emperor has appeared over there? He controls the zombies by the thousands.ã","ãIâd rather fight zombies than freeze. I canât stand being cooped up indoors.ã","ãThen go.ã","ãDo we really have to leave?ã","ãOf course we do. He said it isnât over yet. The shaking will continue.ã","ãIs he going to shake us to death?ã","ãIf you donât leave, youâll die. He wants you to go. If you refuse, heâll simply make you die.ã","Jiang Cheng asked, âSo who is he?â","Everyone abruptly turned to look at her.","She stared impassively at the radio that seemed to be haunted.","Donât pretend.","Youâre all in cahoots.","ãHeh heh.ã Uncle Jiang chuckled. ãYouâll know when you meet him.ã","Sister Maoâs voice turned shrill. ãDonât go see him! Donât go!ã","So they really could hear them.","This wasnât communication through the shortwave radioâs microphone or radio signals. It was some kind of supernatural ability?","Everyoneâs hair stood on end, and they were covered in gooseflesh.","Li Jiangbing swallowed, his eyes darting nervously from side to side.","These temporary structures had been built to give everyone a place to shelter from the wind and rain.","There were no glass windows. Instead, narrow openings had been made high up in the walls. They couldnât really be called windowsâjust ventilation holes.","The room where everyone rested was very dim.","This room, however, had several fireballs burning overhead with a whooshing sound, lighting the place.","Peopleâs shadows were cast across the walls, swelling and shrinking as they swayed.","Li Jiangbing was terrified of things like this.","He pressed himself tightly against Song Jingshuo.","ãYou mustnât see him! Once you doâ¦ youâll never be able to come back!ã Sister Mao sounded as though she were struggling to suppress her fear.","Her acting was remarkably convincing.","Jiang Cheng remained unmoved. âWhy? Will he kill me?â","ãHeh heh.ã Uncle Jiang said, ãGuess.ã","The radio fell silent. After several seconds of crackling static, it switched to the mysterious manâs voice.","ãIt isnât over yet.ã","ãYou must escape.ã","They were forcing the people to abandon the base they had fought so hard to maintain.","Jiang Cheng said, âTurn it off.â","Gao Yuxuan said, âHuh?â","This thingâ¦ technically wasnât even on.","It didnât have any power.","It was haunted. How were they supposed to turn it off?","Jiang Cheng said, âIf you canât turn it off, smash it. Donât let it make another sound.â","With that threat, the haunted radio obediently fell silent.","The mysterious man and the static disappeared.","It was as though the radio had turned itself off.","It would probably turn itself back on the next time it was needed.","Zhou Wangâs mind felt like a complete mess. He couldnât make sense of any of it.","Mr. Xu considered himself a highly educated member of humanityâs elite, but even he had begun to question his entire understanding of life.","Jiang Cheng asked, âZhao Yi, what do you think?â","Zhao Yi was still lost in his own confusion. âTheyâre actually working together.â","Thinking back, wasnât that exactly what had been happening?","The mysterious man played the role of a prophet, while worrying that people might not believe him or understand what he meant.","Uncle Jiang and Sister Mao provided commentary, singing in perfect harmony.","This was completely different from the advanced, detached, mysterious higher civilization Zhao Yi had imagined.","It was more like the sort of con artists one might encounter in everyday life.","They were so down-to-earth that Zhao Yi found the whole thing utterly disillusioning.","Zhang Lesi asked, âSo their ultimate goal is to force us to leave? What happens if we refuse?â","Gao Yuxuan said, âThey already made that perfectly clear.â","If they refused to leave, the shaking would continue.","Zhou Wang interrupted their speculation. âWait, wait, wait! Little Jiang! Take care of us old folks here! My brain canât keep up! Explain whatâs going on first!â","He was genuinely confused.","And he wasnât the only one who still didnât understand what was happening.","Jiang Cheng called on someone. âZhao Yi, you explain.â","Zhao Yi sighed and stood up to face everyone.","âThis started out as a wild guess of mine. I never expected it to come true.â","âWe all know that the zombie virus might have been released by an external hostile force to destroy us.â","âBut this âexternalâ hostile forceâ¦ isnât the foreign power everyone has in mind.â","Zhao Yi had intended to explain his entire theory, including the two possible directions it could take.","But then he saw Zhang Lesi subtly shake her head at him.","Couples developed a certain tacit understanding.","Zhao Yi understood what she meant.","After hearing his theory, she had told him, âI can accept aliens and all that. Anyone whoâs been educated knows how vast the universe is. Itâs impossible that our planet is the only place with intelligent life. Even if aliens really did appear, that would still be consistent with science.â","âBut this whole high-dimensional-world, low-dimensional-world thing? Forget it. Thatâs way too much like an anime.â"]},{"number":190,"title":"Chapter 190: 0190","paragraphs":["Even though Zhao Yi had simplified his theory, leaving out the parts about higher- and lower-dimensional worlds and speaking only of âaliensâ and âalien civilizations,â Zhou Wang was still left staring at him, eyes wide.","Mr. Xu stood there with his mouth hanging open.","That was how most people looked the first time they heard the theory.","They were dumbfounded.","Zhou Wang felt as though the top of his skull had been pried open and his brain tossed into a wok with Sichuan peppercorns and spices, then stir-fried to a crisp.","The middle-aged man vigorously rubbed both sides of his head, trying to make sense of it. âSo they made the zombies, wiped out all the governments, and they can even control the weather?â","He raised his head and practically shouted, âWhat the hell do they want?â","With technology that advanced, they could do anything they wanted.","Why torment a bunch of puny humans?","If they didnât like humanity, why not just wipe everyone out?","Why go to all this trouble?","âMaybe itâs fun,â Jiang Cheng said. âLike us squatting by the roadside watching ants. Didnât you ever do that when you were a kid?â","Gao Yuxuan closed his eyes. âFuckâ!â","When he was little, he could squat on the ground and watch them for half an hour.","Then, when he got bored and was ready to leave, he would stand up, unzip his fly, and piss all over the anthill.","That stream of urine was a city consumed by raging fire.","It was an ordeal of bitter cold.","It was the earth splitting open and buildings collapsing.","The room fell utterly silent.","After a long while, someone suddenly let out a laugh.","A pause, then another two laughs.","Another pause, and then more laughter.","There wasnât enough breath between any of the laughs.","They sounded as if they were dying, as if they had gone mad.","Who could possibly stay sane?","Mr. Xu bent over and buried his face in his hands. After a long while, he sat upright again. âJiang Cheng, which way are we going?â","Jiang Cheng glanced at him.","He was one of the two smartest people among the first batch of refugees.","Before she had even recruited them, the two of them had already sensed which way the wind was blowing and proactively come to join her. Thanks to their sharp minds, they had risen all the way into the management team.","Unfortunately, the one surnamed Yu had disappeared as well.","Jiang Cheng did not answer him at once.","She lowered her eyes.","No one spoke. They remained silent, waiting for her to think it through.","Li Jiangbingâs thoughts were simple: whichever direction Jiang Cheng chose, he would follow.","Jiang Cheng raised her eyes.","Everyone held their breath.","âWeâre splitting up,â Jiang Cheng said.","Everyone was stunned.","âWeâll split up. Half of us will go east, and the other half will go west,â Jiang Cheng said. âWeâre splitting up so they canât wipe us all out in one fell swoop.â","âIt doesnât matter which side survives. As long as one side makes it.â","Half of the people would obviously go with her. But what about the other half? Who would lead them?","Jiang Chengâs gaze swept across the people before her.","In the end, she chose the person she believed was best suited for the job.","âSu Yu, Iâll take half, and you take the other half.â","Su Yu was a unique superpowered individual, unlike anyone else, and extraordinarily powerful.","Her protective barrier could withstand the collapse of half a building.","She was a kind girl, a universally acknowledged good person.","Perhaps because of her unusual ability, there was a sacred, almost salvific aura about her.","The human heart was actually fragile and easily hollowed out.","That was why cults found it so easy to ensnare people, slipping into the emptiness at just the right moment.","Most ordinary people had to fill that emptiness with something in order to keep themselves standing.","Song Jingshuo was certainly an excellent administrator, fully capable of shouldering the responsibility of leading a group.","But in everyoneâs eyes, Song Jingshuo was ultimately just an ordinary man.","Under the current circumstances, when so many peopleâs souls had been reduced to empty shells, Su Yu was the better choice.","Su Yuâs vision blurred.","She had never expected Jiang Cheng to entrust her with such a heavy responsibility.","She fought back the tears gathering in her eyes and nodded firmly as she accepted the burden. âAll right.â","Li Jiangbing opened his mouth. He looked at Su Yu, then Jiang Cheng, then Jiang Cheng again, then back at Su Yu.","As for which way they should goâ","Gao Yuxuan said, âHow about one group heads south and the other heads north? I refuse to believe we have to play by their rules.â","Defiance was the name of the game.","âIt wonât work,â Zhao Yi said. âTheir abilities are practically divine compared to ours. If they donât want us going south or north, they have the power to stop us.â","âEven if there werenât natural barriers to the north and no coastline pushing inland from the south, they could simply create them.â","That was true.","A massive fissure had appeared on the site of the old Youth Apartments. Half the courtyard had collapsed into it.","It ran diagonally through the entire residential complex, even extending into Auspicious Garden.","It was bottomless.","They had given humanity two choices: east or west.","To the west, the terrain rose, forcing them to face the extreme cold.","To the east, zombies had gathered, and one of them had already evolved into a Corpse Emperor.","Neither destination was remotely appealing.","Clearly, they were just toying with humanity.","As for who should go where, Jiang Cheng said, âLetâs roll the dice.â","She had Cui Haiyang make a die with three sides marked âeastâ and three sides marked âwest,â giving them even odds.","Jiang Cheng asked Su Yu to roll.","Su Yu rolled âwest.â","âAll right, youâre going west,â Jiang Cheng said. âIâm going east.â","Then she asked, âWhat about the rest of you?â","She was speaking to the people in the room.","Song Jingshuo didnât need to think. âIâm with you.â","Sweat covered Li Jiangbingâs forehead. He couldnât come up with an answer.","Zhao Yi exchanged a glance with Zhang Lesi, then another with Gao Yuxuan.","The three of them understood one another perfectly.","âYou roll,â Zhang Lesi said. âIâll go with you.â","âYou roll,â Gao Yuxuan said. âIâll go in the opposite direction.â","The lovers had decided not to separate. They would stay together.","The partners had decided to split up, because each side needed someone to witness what happened with their own eyes. The two of them would each serve as that witness for one side.","Zhao Yi rolled âeast.â He and Zhang Lesi would follow Jiang Cheng.","Gao Yuxuan would go west with Su Yu.","Li Jiangbing couldnât make a choice. He gritted his teeth. âIâll roll too.â","He would leave it to fate.","Fate sent him east with Jiang Cheng.","Li Jiangbing closed his eyes for a moment and accepted his destiny.","Some people found it easy to make a decision. Aunt Pan was one of them. âIâll go with Little Su.â","Jiang Cheng had always given people the impression of being powerful and forceful.","Compared with her, Su Yu seemed much gentler.","Older women instinctively felt more protective toward the vulnerable. Su Yu was not vulnerable in the slightest, but Aunt Pan felt that Jiang Cheng already had plenty of strong people around her, so she would go with Su Yu.","Cui Haiyang rolled for Su Yu and high-fived Gao Yuxuan.","Zhou Wang also rolled for Su Yu, deciding to leave it to fate.","Mr. Xu didnât roll at all. He chose Jiang Cheng directly.","The girl surnamed Su was a good person, and her superpower was useful. But not everyone could make him willingly submit to a subordinate position.","Auntie Qian chose Su Yu.","âThere are zombies to the east. If they come, I canât run, and Iâll only hold you back,â she said. âIâll go with Little Su. Itâll be colder, but at least it should be safer. Iâll focus on growing crops for everyone. Xiao Song can go with you, and Iâll go with Little Su. That works out perfectly.â","Quite a few fire-type ability users chose Su Yu.","Their abilities would be even more useful in the extreme cold.","This was not a falling-out. The companions were simply testing their luck together, sharing the risks, and searching for a way to survive.","Everyone stepped out of the little house and gathered all the survivors.","Jiang Cheng climbed onto the roof and used the tin megaphone Cui Haiyang had made to announce to everyone that they would be splitting up and heading in opposite directions.","âChoose for yourselves,â she said. âIf you canât decide, roll the dice.â","Someone asked, âCanât we stay here?â","âFine. We respect everyoneâs personal choice.â Jiang Cheng had never forced anyone to stay alive. She only saved those who wanted to live.","But she also laid out the risks honestly. âS City may continue to suffer earthquakes until it becomes uninhabitable.â","The vast majority of people would undoubtedly choose to leave with them.","Most people were obedient by nature and tended to follow the crowd. They were afraid of being left alone.","Besides, the water-, wood-, and numerous fire-element ability users were all leaving. These three types of abilities played an importantâindeed, crucialârole in survival under the current circumstances.","Without them, staying alive would become extremely difficult.","âWe leave tomorrow,â Jiang Cheng said. âMake your decision by then at the latest.â","Everyone began murmuring among themselves.","The truth about the zombie disaster and the catastrophes that followed soon spread as well.","Some people broke down completely. Some refused to believe it no matter what. Others felt as if they were trapped in a dream.","Yet somehow, everythingâthe zombies, the raging fires, the extreme cold, and the supernatural abilitiesâcould finally be explained.","Some people made their choice.","Those who couldnât decide for themselves could roll the dice.","At first, they rolled one by one. Later, they grew tired of that and simply had a whole group roll together, with one person representing everyone.","That way, no matter which side they ended up on, they could stay with people they knew and gain at least a little sense of security.","Many people had already begun working.","They searched for vehicles.","They combed through the ruins for anything useful.","Especially useful plants.","Song Jingshuo and the others successfully found the remains of the cultivation level and recovered several crucial crops.","He and Auntie Qian divided the plants between them.","That night, everyone slept in temporary matchbox-like houses.","Another earthquake struck in the middle of the night.","Everyone hurried outside.","âThis house should be fine unless the ground splits apart,â Zhao Yi said.","The house had been built through the combined efforts of earth- and metal-element ability users. Steel reinforcement had been embedded inside specifically to make it earthquake-resistant.","But Zhao Yi was remarkably good at tempting fate. The moment he finished speaking, the earth split open.","A crack slanted across three rows of houses.","The houses did not collapse, but their walls cracked.","Zhao Yi fell silent.","He decided he had better keep his mouth shut.","âTheyâ had actually been monitoring them the entire time.","After that night, no one mentioned staying behind anymore.","At dawn, everyone began working.","Jiang Cheng transferred a batch of supplies to Su Yu.","She gave Su Yu three-quarters of her stored coal.","Since Su Yuâs group did not have the convenience of storage space, the large cargo trucks they found were given priority to them.","On one seven-meter-long freight truck, everyone first spread a layer of soil, then a layer of corpses, and finally another layer of soil, turning it into a mobile farm for Auntie Qian.","It could produce crops wherever they went.","The time to part had arrived.","They had fought side by side and endured hardship together from the previous June until now. At last, they had to go their separate ways.","Many familiar faces said their farewells, offering reminders and words of caution.","Jiang Cheng and Su Yu embraced.","One of them was cold and detached, the other reserved and introverted. Neither of them often showed her emotions so openly.","But this time, the two young women held each other tightly.","Leaning close to Su Yuâs ear, Jiang Cheng urged, âDonât hesitate when trouble comes. Kill when you have to. If you truly canât bring yourself to do it, drive them away.â","Su Yu knew her own weakness all too well. Her eyes blurred with tears as she promised, âI will.â","Zhang Lesi clasped both of Su Yuâs hands. For once, the usually outgoing girl was unable to say a word. After struggling for a long while, all she managed was, âTake care.â","âYou too.â","Gao Yuxuan and Cui Haiyang bumped fists one by one with Song Jingshuo, Li Jiangbing, Zhao Yi, and the others.","âLetâs see who can survive,â they said.","âHopefully, all of us.â","âAnd youâtry showing off a little less from now on.â","âGet lost.â","Song Jingshuo said goodbye to Auntie Qian and gently embraced the older woman.","The old lady smiled through her tears.","Zhou Wang bade farewell to Mr. Xu. The middle-aged man remained unfailingly courteous. âThank you for taking care of us these past few months.â","âNot at all. Youâre too kind.â","The young people from the youth apartments also said goodbye to Zhou Wang. âBrother Zhou, take care!â","Zhou Wangâs eyes grew misty as well.","He seemed to see that day againâthe day when the residents of Auspicious Garden had finally summoned the courage to go downstairs and fight the zombies. Back then, they had no armor and no standard-issue weapons. They had possessed nothing but the determination to live.","Just as they were about to collapse, this group of young people had arrived like heavenly soldiers descending to earth and cut their way through the zombies.","Their bond had been forged at that moment.","In the end, everyone pretended to be busy. In truth, they really were busy, loudly calling for people to board the vehicles and doing everything else that needed to be done.","They left the final moments to Li Jiangbing and Su Yu.","Li Jiangbing did not know what to say.","He did not know whether Su Yu resented him for leaving with Jiang Cheng.","But Su Yu smiled and promised him, âIâll take good care of myself.â","Li Jiangbing felt a weight lift from his heart.","âTake care of yourself first whenever something happens,â he said. âStop worrying so much about everyone else. If thereâs really trouble, stay alive first. Everything else can wait.â","Because she was important to himâmore important than anyone else.","Su Yuâs vision blurred.","Everyone boarded the vehicles.","The enormous convoy started moving. One group headed east, while the other went west.","After ten months of guarding their home together, the companions finally parted ways here, setting off in different directions to seek a path to survival."]},{"number":191,"title":"Chapter 191: 0191","paragraphs":["Jiang Chengâs convoy did not leave S City immediately.","First, they searched along the way for more vehicles to ease the strain on traffic and make things a little more comfortable for everyone.","They also needed fuel.","The first gas station they found had already exploded in the earthquake. They continued searching and found a second one. They siphoned out the fuel, filled several empty tanker trucks, and had the tankers join the convoy.","Jiang Cheng then headed for the other survivor bases. The first one was Zheng Junweiâs.","After the phones lost network access, the various districts established contact through radio stations. After the earthquake the night before, they had found only the shortwave radio, but they still couldnât locate Song Jingshuoâs vehicle radio.","The New Technology District had completely lost contact with the other survivor bases.","Zheng Junweiâs survivor base was on the eastern side, in a riverside housing development. Jiang Cheng had been there twice before.","But this time, the development was gone.","It wasnât like the Youth Apartments, which had been reduced to a mountain of rubble and a field of ruins. It was simply gone.","All that remained was a broad, empty wasteland.","The people who had been there before were stunned.","âThis is definitely the place. Look over there, see? I remember that terrain. The river channel seems a little different, but this should be it.â","Someone asked, âWhatâs that?â","In the middle of the vast wasteland stood something that looked like a small pavilion.","The convoy drove over. Only when they reached it did they discover that this âpavilionâ was far larger than a real pavilion. It merely had the shape of one; it wasnât actually a pavilion.","At last, everyone recognized what it was.","It was the decorative spire from the roof of the riverside housing development.","When it had still been on the roof, it had looked like a tiny pointed ornament from a distance. No one had realized it was actually this huge.","Everyone fell silent, then began backing away. The farther they retreated, the broader their field of view became.","From there, everything was clear.","The spire hadnât fallen onto the ground.","It had âgrownâ out of it.","Zhao Yi crouched down and pressed both hands against the soil.","After a while, he stood up and said to Jiang Cheng, âLetâs go.â","The earth had split open, swallowing the entire housing development, then closed again.","No one had survived.","In the end, they were nothing more than ants.","The convoy left the barren wasteland in silence and continued toward another survivor base.","When they arrived, the place was in complete chaos.","The backbone personnel who had once held the group together were gone. The former community had disintegrated into a scattered mob, its members turning on one another.","There appeared to be only two or three hundred people, yet corpses littered the ground.","Some of the dead women were barely clothed.","When the people at the base saw the convoy, someone recognized it.","âItâs the New Technology District! Itâs the New Technology District!â","They waved frantically, running after the vehicles.","Jiang Cheng told the drivers, âDonât stop. Keep going.â","The lead vehicle accelerated, and the others followed suit.","Some people tried to force the convoy to stop by throwing themselves in its path.","The New Technology District had always presented itself as a government, hadnât it? Then surely it could be pressured through morality.","How naÃ ̄ve.","Under Jiang Chengâs leadership, the people of the New Technology District had been through countless battles. The truck drivers had seen every kind of trick.","When Jiang Cheng said not to stop, they didnât stop.","They floored the gas and ran the people over, crushing them into bloody pulp.","After that, no one else dared to block the convoy. They could only watch helplessly as the enormous procession departed.","âWhere are they going?â","âAre they leaving S City?â","âThere must be something going on. Find a way to catch up with them!â","The New Technology District had always been the leader. They wouldnât leave S City for no reason.","The people scrambled to find vehicles, trying to catch up with the main convoy.","All the convoy left behind was a trail of dust.","Just as the mysterious person had wished, Jiang Cheng planned a route eastward.","She traveled east the entire way, with Q City as their final destination.","The distance from S City to Q City was more than seven hundred kilometers. In the past, it would have taken only a day to drive there on the expressway.","But now, not long after the convoy entered the expressway, they discovered that the road had been cut off. They had no choice but to turn around and drive back against the traffic.","Fortunately, there were no vehicles on the expressway at all. Otherwise, they would have caused an accident in minutes.","After leaving the expressway, they switched to the national highway.","The convoy traveled slowlyânot just slowly, but with extreme caution.","No one was planning to rush off to meet the Corpse Emperor. They wanted to search for a way to survive along the route.","Once they left S Cityâs administrative boundaries, they finally saw the zombies they had missed for so long.","Everyone must have gone crazy. They actually felt a sense of familiarity upon seeing zombies.","They really hadnât seen a zombie in S City for a very long time.","Many of the refugees had never joined a team or gone on an outside mission. After taking shelter in the New Technology District, they had not seen a single zombie again.","When they encountered only scattered zombies, the convoy simply ran them over.","Only when they came across a somewhat larger gathering did they stop and get out to clear them away.","Many people hadnât worn their armor in a long time. During the extreme cold, all the armor and crescent shovels had been collected and stored away. Now Jiang Cheng brought them out and distributed them again.","âLetâs get warmed up first.â","If they expected to face the Corpse Emperorâs massive zombie army in the future, they might as well get some practice now.","They had been cooped up inside buildings for months. They couldnât afford to grow sluggish.","Song Jingshuo stopped hiding his ability, too. He simply tossed a seedling onto a zombieâs corpse.","The seedling rapidly grew, blossomed, and bore fruit.","No one minded. They stepped over the zombie remains, picked watermelons, mangoes, and strawberries, then squatted by the roadside and ate.","Before setting out, the cooking team had baked a large number of flatbreads. They only needed to heat them up before eating.","The several months spent trapped inside the buildings had given the bean paste plenty of time to ferment. The aunties had finally managed to make real doubanjiang.","Jiang Chengâs space was a reserve warehouse, and since it was a reserve, she had chosen supplies that could be stored for longer periods. She had stored a great deal of doubanjiang.","Now she brought it out and spread it over the hot flatbreads, then rolled them up with the green onions and cucumbers Song Jingshuo had grown on the spot.","Everyone squatted in rows, eating flatbreads rolled around green onions.","After eating and drinking, they also took care of their bodily needs in the portable toilets.","The drivers honked their horns. Everyone climbed back into the vehicles, and the convoy set off again.","They passed through a village. There were no living people, only zombies.","The convoy stopped to look for useful supplies, but inside the houses they found human corpses instead.","The bodies were all lying in bed and had only just begun to decay.","Everyone analyzed the situation.","âThey probably froze to death.â","That had happened months ago, when the extreme cold first arrived.","During the extreme cold, the bodies had been preserved as if frozen, so they hadnât decomposed. Now that the extreme cold had vanished, the corpses had thawed and begun to rot.","If the bodies werenât dealt with, they could cause an epidemic. The people from the New Technology District buried all the corpses together.","That night, the convoy stayed in the village. It was far better than the temporary dormitories, since there were actual beds. They also gathered a great deal of miscellaneous household equipmentâpots, bowls, utensils, and other daily necessitiesâand loaded everything up the next day.","The convoy drove for another day. The villages, towns, and cities they passed that morning were all devoid of living people.","They were probably still within the area covered by the extreme cold.","The small cities contained a considerable number of zombies, including several mutated ones.","The former team members had recovered remarkably well. They had regained their familiar combat rhythm.","After leaving the small city and continuing onward, they entered another one in the afternoon.","At last, they saw signs of human life.","It was a survivor base inhabited by humans.","The people on the streets were not wearing armor or carrying weapons. Clearly, the zombies in the area around the survival base had been thoroughly cleared out and brought under control, allowing people to walk outside without weapons and feel safe.","The people inside the vehicles pressed against the windows to look outside, while the people outside stared in shock at the terrifyingly large convoy.","Every vehicle had been modified into a blade car, gleaming silver. The long line drove into the city, radiating an overwhelming sense of pressure.","The convoy chose to stop on a wide road.","Everyone got out.","The local passersby stared blankly at them.","One of the braver ones came forward and asked, âWhere are you from?â","When everyone answered, âS City,â the locals all wore astonished expressions.","âThere are still survivors in S City? Didnât that place freeze solid under the ice and snow?â","The people from the Technology New District scattered in every direction, while the locals watched them with curiosity. The two sides engaged in communication and interaction in a reasonably friendly atmosphere.","It couldnât not be friendly. The Technology New District had nearly two thousand people, and quite a number of them were wearing armor and carrying weapons. They had already regained the murderous aura they had possessed several months ago.","Besides, every one of them looked well-fed and full of strength.","No one dared attack or provoke them.","The people from the Technology New District also noticed something.","âSo many of them are so thin their cheeks have caved in,â they whispered among themselves.","âThey look malnourished.â","âA little while ago, a girl who looked about college age asked me if I had any flatbread. She said she only wanted one piece. Before she could finish, a middle-aged woman rushed over and said she only wanted half a piece. I thought they were beggars, but thenâ¦â","It turned out they were selling themselves.","One piece of flatbread for the younger women, half a piece for the older ones.","The people from the Technology New District were stunned.","In the past, everyone had complained about the Technology New Districtâs basic survival policy of giving each person one potato a day.","But now, looking at this small city, they realized that if those women had been given a potato the size of a basketball every day, they would never have needed to sell themselves.","No one was born depraved. They were simply trying to survive.","They asked the locals where they could find a place large enough to accommodate two thousand people.","The locals pointed them toward an elementary school.","An elementary school was perfect. It had buildings and classrooms, saving Zhao Yi and the others the trouble of constructing shelters themselves.","The convoy honked its horns to gather everyone, then drove to the school.","There was even a cafeteria. They did not need to build makeshift cooking pits, either; the fire-type ability users went straight to work.","The cooking team busied itself.","At noon, everyone ate scallion-filled flatbread rolls. In the evening, they made every effort to prepare a better meal.","Now Song Jingshuo was the only wood-type ability user left, but fortunately, Jiang Chengâs reserves were astonishing. Along the way, they had also collected a large number of zombie corpses to use as fertilizer for Song Jingshuo.","They did not even need the earth-type ability users anymore. Everyoneâs nerves had long since been hardened, so they simply scattered seeds directly onto the zombie corpses.","And how far had Song Jingshuoâs wood-type superpower evolved?","He no longer accelerated crops from seed to maturity in one continuous burst. Instead, he stimulated the plants into an active state, after which they would absorb nutrients and grow on their own.","Although this was not as insanely fast as growing a seed into food in two minutes, it was especially suitable for large-scale cultivation.","Once the plants had been stimulated into this state, the ability user no longer needed to manage them. As long as there was enough fertilizer, the plants would reach maturity within several hours or overnight, depending on how strongly they had been stimulated.","Large patches of crops appeared across the school field, along with enormous water-storage tanks.","The metal-type ability users polished the blades on the vehicles, preparing for the possibility of encountering a Corpse Emperor at any moment.","Everyone lined up to receive bedding. Once they had collected theirs, they went into the buildings to find classrooms and arrange sleeping quarters.","Everything proceeded in an orderly fashion. Everyone followed instructions.","The people watching from outside the fence were left utterly stunned.","The people from the Technology New District had not seen outsiders in a long time, either.","They had been cooped up for months. The moment the extreme cold receded, another earthquake struck. Now that the environment finally appeared safe, everyone wanted to go out and take a look around.","Jiang Cheng agreed.","âGo out in groups. Bring weapons. No one is to travel alone, especially women. The team leader will be held fully responsible. If you lose anyone, donât come back.â","The refugees went out in groups.","They all wanted to see what life was like beyond S City.","It was nearly dusk, and the sky had grown dim.","There was no electricity in the city. All along the streets, oil drums had been converted into fire barrels, providing only feeble illumination.","Many people were skin and bones.","The men had dangerous looks in their eyes, while the women wore timid, shrinking expressions.","Walking through streets like these, the people from the Technology New Districtâwho had always referred to themselves as ârefugeesââlooked far too healthy if they were men, and far too clean if they were women."]},{"number":192,"title":"Chapter 192: 0192","paragraphs":["Song Jingshuo activated the cropsâ growth and then left them alone to grow on their own. They should naturally ripen by tomorrow.","Li Jiangbing filled the drinking-water supply, then came over and called out to him, âLetâs go outside and take a look around.â","Jiang Cheng went with them.","They also brought Mo Li and the three little ones.","Only six of the little ones had survived in total. Jiang Cheng and Su Yu had taken three each.","Since no one could be sure which side would survive, they had divided even the children equally.","Now, Song Jingshuo was carrying one in his arms, while Li Jiangbing and Mo Li each had one riding on their shoulders.","Walking down the street, the scene looked bizarre: a beautiful young woman in front, followed by three men of entirely different styles, each carrying a child.","People along the road stared and sighed. âItâs been so long since Iâve seen children this youngâ¦â","Jiang Cheng turned her head when she heard that. Many people seemed moved by the remark, and some even had tears glimmering in their eyes.","Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo exchanged a glance.","âThereâs probably not enough food,â Song Jingshuo said.","Many people were so thin they barely looked human, hunger written plainly across their faces.","Jiang Cheng nodded. âThe water supply probably canât keep up, either.â","Most people were filthy.","The streets were dirty as well. Although many people had gathered here, the place clearly wasnât being managed very well.","Back in the Technology District, sanitation jobs had been divided into street sweeping and garbage collection. Garbage collection paid slightly more performance points.","Since there was enough manpower and everyone needed to earn performance points, the residential compounds and surrounding streets were kept very clean.","Of course, that was also connected to the fact that the water supply had always been sufficient.","The group only wandered around for a short while before heading back.","One reason was that dinner would be ready soon. Another was that there really wasnât much to see.","There were only a few street stalls, where people bartered goods.","Food was the hard currency.","Pulling out a packet of instant noodles with the casual flourish of someone producing a black card with no spending limit, one could immediately attract countless staresâand many of them were deeply unsettling.","It wasnât only women like Jiang Cheng who felt uncomfortable.","Even Song Jingshuo and the other men felt uneasy.","Some people looked so hungry they seemed capable of eating human flesh.","Those who had gone out returned one after another as dinnertime approached.","No one had stayed outside for long.","Everyone had noticed that same feeling of unease.","No one dared to go out alone, especially the women. This place offered none of the sense of security provided by the Technology District.","Dinner was ready.","The earth-element ability users had set up rows of long tables and benches on the school athletic field, and everyone ate outdoors.","They chatted and discussed what they had seen while they were out.","âShe asked me if I was an ability user. I said I wasnât.â","âThen she asked how I could be so clean.â","âI told her, âBy washing.ââ","âShe said, âWhere would we get the water? Itâs so coldâwe canât stand bathing in the river.ââ","âI told her, âHave the fire and water ability users heat the water.ââ","âShe just stared at me.â","The girl who was speaking hadnât finished her flatbread at lunchtime, so she had stuffed the rest into her pocket. When she saw a pitifully thin girl nearly fainting from hunger, she took it out and gave it to her.","That was how the conversation had begun.","The girl had said, âHow could people with special abilities do this kind of work for us?â","To the people from the Technology District, those words had been deeply shocking.","It wasnât only that girl. In the short time they had spent outside, many of them had already noticed that, in this small city, ability users and ordinary people seemed to belong to entirely different social classes.","If one saw several people walking together while the passersby hurriedly moved aside, it was obvious that all of them were ability users.","Ability users stayed with ability users, while ordinary people stayed with ordinary people.","The ability users looked well-fed. Not one of them had a sallow face, hollow cheeks, or a starving appearance.","Nor did they look timid. They walked with swagger.","By contrast, people like those from the Technology Districtâan entire group made up of both ability users and ordinary people, laughing and chatting togetherâseemed not to exist here.","They had even witnessed a fire-element ability user set an ordinary person on fire in the street.","Since Zhao Yi still had to stay at the school to oversee the infrastructure work, Zhang Lesi had gone out with some others.","Two of the girls accompanying her were fire-element ability users.","They immediately acted and extinguished the flames, while Zhang Lesi treated the injured person on the spot.","The person they had rescued fled in panic without even saying thank you.","The perpetrators looked vicious and cursed angrily, but in the end they didnât dare cause trouble for Zhang Lesi and the others.","The people from the Technology District all looked well-fed and strong.","The two fire-element girls were clearly powerful as well. With a simple grab of their hands from a distance, they had snuffed out the flames, making the others wary of them.","But the incident quickly destroyed everyoneâs interest in sightseeing, and they soon returned.","Many people ate dinner in silence.","One major reason they had left the school was to see how people outside S City lived.","Now they knew.","Life here was completely different from life in S City, and from life in the Technology District.","Yet many of them couldnât help realizing that this might be what the chaotic end of the world was really supposed to look like.","Early the next morning, everyone awoke to find that the crops on the athletic field had ripened.","After washing up, everyone threw themselves into the harvest.","Almost everyone was experienced. The moment they picked up their tools, their movements became practiced and efficient.","Food was simply too important.","At its peak, the Technology District had a population of more than thirty thousand.","All the wood-element ability users from the various residential compounds had been gathered at the Youth Apartments.","At the time, some residents from other compounds had objected. There had certainly been people who wanted to keep control of the food supply in their own hands.","But in reality, it was precisely because all the wood-element ability users had been brought together to work as one and grow crops on a large scale that the Technology Districtâs food supply had remained secure.","The ability users grew the crops, while ordinary people without abilities handled harvesting, threshing, grinding, and processing.","It didnât matter if the city residents had no prior experience. People like Aunt Pan and Master Luo taught them step by step.","Everyone received a different amount of performance points based on their position and how arduous the work was, enough to maintain a life of food and warmth.","To the people of the Technology District, this was only natural: ability users were no different from everyone else. They were simply more capable and made greater contributions, so it was only fair that they received more performance points.","Only after coming outside did they learn that things were not like this everywhere.","Hunger, a lack of cooperation, and inequality were the norm here.","A convoy of green vehicles rumbled into the city.","People along the road watched the convoy with awe. It was the largest force in the city, and no one dared provoke it.","The convoy went straight to a luxurious hotel, where someone came out to greet them.","âThe boss is back!â","Many sturdy men in camouflage climbed down from the trucks. The man known as the boss had a broad back and a narrow waist, with a thick, unkempt beard that made him look intensely masculine.","But if one looked closely at his eyes and brows, it became clear that he was actually quite young.","âNot bad. We brought back plenty of supplies. Go unload everything,â the boss said, lighting a cigarette.","Many people busily began carrying goods down from the trucks.","There was all kinds of stuff: bags of rice and flour, instant noodles and biscuits, whole barrels of cooking oil and even half-empty ones.","Toilet paper, clothes, shoes, beddingâ¦","There werenât many supplies in a small city, so they had gone out to search the nearest major city for materials.","The people who had stayed behind reported, âA convoy came yesterday. There were a lot of themâprobably around a thousand.â","The boss narrowed his eyes and looked up. âHuh?â","His subordinate continued, âThey set up camp at the elementary school on Gusi Street. I donât know if they plan to stay, but they have quite a few ability users, and many of them are strong. They all look like tough customers.â","The subordinate paused.","The boss took the cigarette from his mouth. âWhat is it?â","The man said, âTheyâre highly organized and disciplined.â","The boss was momentarily dazed.","Organization.","Discipline.","They sounded like words from the last century.","So distant.","The boss took a drag and said, âIâll go take a look.â","Then he casually asked, âWhere did they come from?â","âApparently S City. I honestly donât know how they managed to survive.â","Several months ago, they had considered going to S City themselves.","But after driving west through this small city for several hours, they realized something was wrong.","The temperature was dropping at an alarming rate. The snow on the ground was already knee-deep.","And it wasnât even snow season yet. S City shouldnât have had snow this deep at all.","Of course, they didnât know that the snow was only knee-deep because they were still far from S City.","At that time, the snow in S City was already higher than a person.","But they had realized that something was seriously wrong.","When one of their vehicles stalled and nearly failed to start again, the boss decisively ordered them to turn back.","They abandoned their plans to go to S City and returned to the small city they had passed through, settling there. Before long, they had become the largest power in the area.","It was only because they were there that the place could barely maintain the appearance of human society.","Before they arrived, things had been even worse than they were now.","They later made several trips to investigate and confirmed that S City had been plunged into extreme cold.","Eventually, this was confirmed by a local resident who operated a radio.","The man had a shortwave radio and could listen in on communications from across the country and even overseas.","He had also heard Uncle Jiang, Sister Mao, and the mysterious man.","âThey said it covers the entire central region and parts of the east,â he told them.","S City was considered part of the east, so it lay within the affected area.","âWeâre really lucky. Our city just happens to be outside the range.â","They never quite gave up on S City. Every so often, they would drive closer to see if they could get through, but each time, they turned back as soon as they saw the snow.","The temperature was simply too low. Considering that the cityâs water and electricity supplies must have been cut off, and that centralized heating was no longer available, they had always assumed that there probably werenât many survivors left in S City.","They never expected there to still be living people there.","And they certainly hadnât expected those people to come here.","Gusi Street Elementary School.","The people from the New Technology District were holding a meeting after breakfast.","This small city was called D City. Along Jiang Chengâs entire journey, it marked roughly the two-thirds point.","Although there had been zombies along the wayâand quite a few of them in some placesâthey had never encountered anything like the âzombie emperor commanding tens of thousands of zombiesâ that Uncle Jiang and Sister Mao had described.","âCould it really be in Q City?â everyone wondered, somewhat puzzled.","They had even put on their armor and taken up their weapons while still on the road, prepared to fight a massive horde of zombies at any moment.","But the journey had been far too peaceful. It was completely different from what they had expected.","Before the meeting could even finish, visitors arrived.","Several vehicles pulled up. The local powers had come together to pay them a visit.","With their numbers, armor, weapons, and ability users backing them up, the local factions were remarkably polite and friendly toward these outsiders. Everyone exchanged courteous greetings.","Jiang Cheng said, âWeâre only passing through. Weâre on our way to Q City.â","The local leaders let out a collective sigh of relief. âThatâs good. Thatâs good.â","Jiang Cheng and the others were just about to ask about the situation farther east when another group arrived.","This time, several green military jeeps drove up.","The local leaders all stood.","Their attitude changed immediately, becoming noticeably cautious.","âIs that Li Feng coming back?â","âBy my count, he should be back by now. Heâs been gone for three or four days.â","âHe must have brought back plenty of supplies again.â","The name Li Feng was so common and ordinary that everyone heard it without reacting.","They had endured too many brushes with death. Even the companions who had stayed by their sides all along were gone, while the people they had met during earlier stages of the journey had long since become nothing more than fading memories.","But Li Feng had shaved off his beard before returning.","So when he stepped out of the vehicle and stood there, his long legs carrying him down first, many of the people from the Youth Apartment recognized him at once.","Li Feng recognized them too.","Their reunion brought no cheers or joy. They simply stood there in silence, staring at one another.","Between them lay nearly ten months of timeâand countless brushes with death.","Only after Li Feng finally called out, âJiang Cheng,â did he stride forward.","Jiang Cheng narrowed his eyes. Mo Li gathered her strength.","Just as Zhao Yi and Song Jingshuo were about to greet Li Feng, he drew a gun from behind his waist and aimed it directly at Jiang Chengâs brow."]},{"number":193,"title":"Chapter 193: 0193","paragraphs":["Killing intent was impossible to hide.","From the moment Li Feng recognized Jiang Cheng, killing intent began to radiate from him. Mo Li noticed it at once.","But Jiang Cheng raised a hand to stop Mo Li.","She looked at the old acquaintance pointing a gun at her. âLi Feng?â","Li Fengâs eyes were filled with fury. âTalk! Which country sent you? Talkâ! Which countryâs spy are you?â","On August 29, the military camp suffered heavy casualties.","It was not until August 30 that Li Feng finally had time to catch his breath. He remembered to open the locker and retrieve the phone he had been required to turn in at headquarters. He wanted to contact his family and friendsâto see whether any of them were still alive.","The moment he turned on his phone, he saw the text message from Jiang Cheng.","Accidents couldnât be predicted in advance. Only planned attacks could be anticipated.","What kind of person could foresee a virus attack capable of destroying an entire nation?","Li Feng had felt ice-cold all over.","He instinctively dialed the number, but just as the phone began to ring, a comrade shouted, âLi Feng! Moveâ!â","He had no choice but to hang up and run after them.","At some point during the battles that followed, his phone was lost. He had no time to look for it, either.","Losing the phone meant losing the numbers of the people he had added at the time. From then on, he lost contact with all of them.","The next ten months were a long period of wandering and hardship.","Fighting. Surviving. Searching everywhere for an organization, only to find none.","Peopleâs hearts fractured. Everyone clung to their own opinions, and paths diverged.","When they met again, they had no choice but to personally eliminate those who had fallen.","It was easy to be a single screw within a complete organizational system. You could even become an excellent screw.","Only after the organization collapsed did you realize how difficult it was to become a leader.","The hardest thing was never the zombies. It was peopleâs hearts.","Leadership was an innate talent, and most people simply didnât possess it.","Li Feng had endured a great deal of painful growth before becoming the person he was today.","In his search for an organization, he and his comrades traveled through several cities.","But he had never forgotten Jiang Chengâs text message. He had always wanted to go to S City and ask her about it in person.","Yet when he finally set out for S City, the extreme cold that descended across the central region stopped him once again.","In the end, he returned to D City and put down roots there.","By then, D City had no law or order left.","After arriving, they clashed violently several times with the other factions in the area.","Li Feng showed no mercy, killing decisively and establishing his authority. Only then did they manage to secure their position.","With them around, the other factions no longer dared to act so recklessly.","What he had never expected was that Jiang Cheng would one day appear in this little city.","The veins in Li Fengâs forehead bulged. âTalkâ!â","In those ten months, he had seen too much darkness. The fury had seeped into his bones.","If Jiang Cheng said even one wrong word, he would shoot her dead!","He didnât know whether she had a superpower.","One personâs superpower wasnât necessarily stronger than anotherâs.","But no one could dodge a bullet.","They had tested it beforeâeven someone with an exceptionally powerful metal-based ability couldnât control a high-speed bullet in time.","Bullets might not be particularly effective against zombies, but against humans, they were the most useful weapon there was.","The local toughs gathered around to watch the spectacle.","The people from the Tech New District were deeply surprised.","Zhao Yi, Zhang Lesi, and the others didnât dare make any rash move. They were visibly tense.","Song Jingshuo understood the situation the moment he heard it.","He turned to Jiang Cheng. âYou sent him a text too?â","Jiang Cheng said, âI sent it to everyone in my contacts.â","Li Feng barked, âWhat are you two talking about!â","Song Jingshuo sighed. âShe mass-sent that message to everyone in her contacts that day. More than four hundred people from our residential compound came back.â","He continued, âHave you ever seen a spy expose their own identity like that?â","It was a powerful counterargument.","Li Feng stared at the two of them for a moment before finally lowering his gun.","Everyone breathed a sigh of relief.","The local toughs secretly regretted that the show was over.","Jiang Cheng shifted her gaze toward them and politely asked them to leave. âSorry, but weââ","The local toughs immediately said, âOh, sure.â","âWeâll head out, then.â","âTake your time.â","They left reluctantly, disappointed at having missed the rest of the spectacle.","Once there were no outsiders left, Li Feng said, âExplain.â","Jiang Cheng tipped her chin toward the road. âIn the car.â","She climbed into a Blade vehicle, and Song Jingshuo followed her.","Li Feng got in as well without hesitation.","Zhang Lesi clicked his tongue. âHeâs got quite a temper.â","Zhao Yi sighed. âHe must have been through a lot.â","Zhao Yi had been very familiar with Li Feng during that period.","But the warmhearted, passionate young man he knew was completely gone. The Li Feng standing before them now seemed like an entirely different person.","The three of them talked in the vehicle for nearly an hour.","When they got out, all three wore solemn expressions.","Zhang Lesi, Zhao Yi, and Li Jiangbing hurried over. âWhat happened?â","Jiang Chengâs face was cold. âLi Feng has never heard of the Corpse Emperor.â","Everyone turned to look at Li Feng.","Li Feng explained, âSupplies are extremely scarce in D City. Weâve been searching for supplies in the major cities nearby.â","âItâs been raining in the west for the past two weeks, so I havenât gone there recently. But the last time I went was about two weeks ago. There were zombies, yes, but I never heard anything about a Corpse Emperor.â","Everyone exchanged glances.","Li Jiangbing said, âCould he beâ¦ messing with us?â","If so, that alien was unbelievably bored.","Jiang Cheng said, âItâs not that simple.â","âTheyâ could create extreme cold. They could trigger earthquakes. They could reap countless lives as casually as if they were chatting.","Even if they were merely toying with them, it wouldnât be as simple as making them waste a trip.","This game they were playing involved human lives.","Li Feng called over one of his men. âGo bring Old Cheng here. Quickly!â","His man immediately drove off in a Jeep.","Li Feng explained, âOld Cheng is a local. He operates a radio. We brought him into the group.â","Being cut off from the world was terrifying in its own way. In D City, they had met this man surnamed Cheng, who listened to the radio using a hand-cranked generator. Li Feng and the others wanted access to the broadcasts, so they took him in.","They brought him over in twenty minutes.","Old Cheng was a middle-aged man. He looked like someone who could scrape by as long as he followed Li Feng.","He said, âThatâs right. Brother Jiang and Sister MaoâI listened to them too. Thatâs how I knew about the extreme cold in the central and eastern regions.â","âThe Corpse Emperor? What Corpse Emperor?â","âI havenât received their broadcasts for three daysâno, four days now.â","âThere was an earthquake at the time. I donât know where it happened, but we felt it here. I figured the two of them might have died in the earthquake.â","Four days ago had been the great earthquake in S City.","After that, the radio station began acting strangely.","âTheyâ had stopped pretending.","But not everything they said was a lie, because Li Feng confirmed, âThe north really has become a massive canyon.â","âWe were in E City yesterday. Some people had come there from the north.â","âThe earthquake was extremely severe. The canyon must be at least a mile wide, running east to west. I donât know how long it is. In any case, the north and south have been cut off.â","âThose people were afraid the ground would continue collapsing, so they fled south.â","Uncle Jiang had said that there was a canyon in the north, that the coastline had advanced in the south, that the extreme cold was moving westward, and that a Corpse Emperor had appeared in the east.","It wasnât frightening if everything was true.","It wasnât frightening if everything was false.","What was frightening was when truth and lies were mixed together, making you want to grind your teeth in hatred.","Since Uncle Jiang had been able to come up with a name like âCorpse Emperor,â âtheyâ must certainly have been capable of creating such an existence.","The question was, where was the Corpse Emperor?","It couldnât be that it was inâ¦","How infuriating.","Although Jiang Cheng had said that splitting the group in two would help share the risks, deep down, she still believed the danger was on her side.","She had always felt that she should be the one to face the most difficult, grueling, and dangerous challenges.","Once she drew the danger toward herself, the risks on the other side would be reduced, and their chances of survival would be higher.","She had already begun to sense that âtheyâ were toying with her.","Perhaps they simply wanted to make things more interesting.","But she had overlooked one thing: What if the way they toyed with you wasnât by playing with you directly, but by playing with the people you wanted to protect?","Jiang Cheng gritted her teeth.","It was rare to see such an expression on her face. She usually kept her emotions tightly under control.","If even Jiang Cheng lost control of her emotions, it meant the situation was truly serious.","âJiangbing! Tell everyone that weâreâno, forget everyone. Get me a team. Weâre taking one vehicle to Q City!â","Jiang Cheng had to see it with her own eyes.","Uncle Jiang had said âto the east,â and Q City was already on the coast. It was as far east as they could go.","If they reached Q City and didnât see the Corpse Emperor, that would prove they had been tricked!","Li Feng said, âWe canât get to Q City right now. Itâs been raining there for nearly half a month. The roads have been washed away.â","Jiang Cheng turned around and stared into his eyes. âIs it a disaster on that scale?â","Li Feng didnât know why she was looking at him like that. He said, âMore or less. There have been flash floods, and quite a few places have been washed away.â","Jiang Cheng turned back.","Li Feng saw her cheeks twitch slightly as she gritted her teeth.","They quickly assembled a team. Jiang Cheng told Song Jingshuo to stay behind. âYouâre in charge here.â","Song Jingshuo didnât argue. He was a wood-type ability user. Although his combat ability was actually quite strong, the responsibility of providing food was simply too important.","What happened when people didnât have enough food? D City was a ready-made example.","He nodded. âEven if it really is there, donât make contact. Retreat immediately.â","He was talking about the Corpse Emperor.","Jiang Cheng agreed, then led the group aboard the vehicle.","Li Feng climbed in as well. âIâm going with you.â","No one objected.","Q City was less than two hundred kilometers from D City. When the roads were all open, they could make the round trip in a morning by taking the expressway.","Their driver was an experienced veteran who had driven Blade vehicles for years. Once they left the urban area of D City and stopped seeing any living people, he began flooring the accelerator.","Li Feng asked, âWhat if it isnât there?â","Jiang Cheng would rather it be there.","She would rather face the Corpse Emperor herself.","âIf it isnât,â she said, âweâll turn around immediately and go after Su Yu.â","Li Feng knew she meant the other half of the groupâthe people who had headed west. During the past hour, Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo had explained everything to him.","It was a tremendous shock to his worldview.","But considering that zombies and supernatural abilities existed, what could be more shocking to the worldview than zombies and supernatural abilities?","âSu Yu?â Li Feng thought for a while. âIs she the quiet one, the girl who speaks softly? I remember she was wearing a blue-and-white striped T-shirt.â","Li Jiangbing glared at him. âYou even remember what she was wearing?â","Li Feng was baffled. âBecause it looked like a sailor shirt. Whatâs wrong with that?â","Sailor shirts were part of the navyâs training uniform.","Li Jiangbing turned his head away. âNothing.â","Mo Li rested his head on Jiang Chengâs shoulder.","He could now overcome most of his feline habits while in human form. But his obsession with Jiang Chengâs shoulder was something he just couldnât get over.","Li Feng had already noticed Mo Li.","As a man, Mo Li had an almost perfect face and physique, and his entire body radiated strength. Li Feng, who had once been a soldier, could especially sense the way Mo Li always seemed ready to spring into action.","He followed Jiang Cheng everywhere, never more than a step away. Once they got into the vehicle, he sat directly beside Jiang Cheng, and everyone else had clearly grown used to it.","There was an unmistakable physical intimacy between him and Jiang Cheng.","But even if they were a couple, Li Feng still found it jarring to see such a big man insist on resting his head on Jiang Chengâs shoulder.","Li Feng had once been attracted to Jiang Cheng, but feelings like that faded with time and physical distance.","Over the past few months, he had repeatedly suspected that Jiang Cheng was a foreign spy connected to the zombie virus. He had also endured countless painful experiences, and when all was said and done, those hardships had been caused by the zombie virus.","He had hated Jiang Cheng over and over again in his heart.","Now that he knew it had all been a misunderstanding, his hatred had faded. But it was difficult to recover the feelings he had once held.","Jiang Cheng was no longer the Jiang Cheng she had been before, and Li Feng was no longer the Li Feng he had once been.","They had been apart for less than a year, yet they could never go back to how things had been.","Li Feng simply felt uncomfortable watching an adult man behave in a way that was inappropriate for his age and gender.","He asked Li Jiangbing, âWhoâs this handsome guy? Iâve never seen him before.â","Everyone fell silent for a moment.","Everyone in the group had already grown accustomed to accepting that this handsome young man was actually a cat.","But when it came time to explain it to an outsider, they suddenly realized how difficult that would be.","Zhang Lesi leaned over from the back. âYou know him.â","Li Feng said, âHuh? Have we met?â","That couldnât be right. The man stood out so much in a crowd that he was impossible to miss. If Li Feng had seen him before, he couldnât possibly have no impression of him at all.","Zhang Lesi smiled slyly. âYou held him before.â","Li Feng said, ââ¦What do you mean?â","Hearing them talk, Mo Li raised his head and looked back.","He actually recognized Li Feng.","But the moment this man had appeared, he had shown murderous intent toward Jiang Cheng, so Mo Li didnât like him very much.","âThatâs right. You held me before,â he said. âIâm Mo Li.â","Li Feng was still trying to figure out why the name âMo Liâ sounded so familiar.","Zhang Lesi leaned close to Li Fengâs ear. âMo Li. Jiang Chengâs black cat. Remember? He evolved and became human.â","It took Li Feng half a minute to process those words.","He stared blankly at Mo Li.","Mo Li was sitting in the front and looking back at him the entire time.","Only then did Li Feng notice that, with the light shining in from the side, the young manâs eyes werenât actually black. They had a faint green tint.","Li Feng truly felt that the entire world had gone wrong.","What had the aliens done to this world?","Why?"]},{"number":194,"title":"Chapter 194: 0194","paragraphs":["Jiang Cheng ultimately never made it to Q City.","The survivors of Q City were fleeing.","An hour after leaving D City, the sky ahead began to darken. Going any farther meant entering the rain zone.","Q City was a coastal city backed by mountains, and several roads had been cut off. Some had collapsed because their foundations gave way; others had simply been washed out by flash floods.","As they continued forward, vehicles began coming toward them from the opposite direction.","Cars, motorcycles, three-wheeled vehicles, even bicyclesâthe survivors were using every means of transportation they could find to escape Q City.","âThereâs been a tsunami!â they shouted. âThe mountain floods are coming down too! Heaven itself wonât let us live!â","The Blades vehicle pushed upstream. Farther ahead, the road began to flood.","Fortunately, the Blades vehicle had been converted from a large public bus. Its chassis was high enough that it could keep moving.","Until the flood surged toward them.","Li Jiangbing stood beside the driver at the front of the vehicle. The oncoming flood split apart before them, flowing around the Blades vehicle and streaming away on both sides.","The flood carried both living people and zombies. The zombies thrashed clumsily in the water, trying to tear into the living.","The metal-element esper traveling with them transformed the blades on the vehicleâs body into handrails. People drifting past the vehicle grabbed onto them and were pulled to safety.","Jiang Cheng stared at the endless expanse of water. After a long silence, she said, âTurn around.â","She asked Li Feng whether the situation in Q City had reached the level of a natural disaster.","Now âtheyâ had given her the answer.","With flash floods and tsunamis raging right in front of her, they had answered loudly and clearly:","Yes. This is a natural disaster.","Uncle Jiang had said that the extreme cold was moving westward, while the east was raising a Corpse Emperor.","The west had natural disasters; the east had man-made ones.","But now Jiang Cheng had come east, and the east was where the natural disaster was.","The man-made disaster could only be in the west.","The Corpse Emperor was in the west.","Su Yu had headed straight toward the Corpse Emperor and his army of zombies.","Li Jiangbingâs expression had turned terribly grim.","Everyone understood now.","Jiang Cheng closed her eyes. âTurn back. Weâre heading west to catch up with Su Yu.â","At that moment, nearly 1,500 kilometers away from Jiang Cheng, Su Yu and the people traveling with her were staring at the endless sea of zombies. They too realized they had been tricked.","They had been traveling west all this time, passing through the central regions that had once been covered by the extreme cold, fully expecting the weather to grow colder the farther west they went.","The central regions still bore heavy traces of the extreme cold. Along the way, they saw many corpsesâmost of them people who had frozen to death inside shelters.","Radios were not common.","They might seem ubiquitous in foreign films, but in reality, shortwave radios were extremely uncommon in China, a niche item at best.","Not every survivor settlement had a shortwave radio.","Nor did everyone who heard the mysterious personâs warning about the âextreme coldâ believe it.","Even among those who did believe, not everyone had any real concept of what âextreme coldâ meant. They might find a couple of extra thick coats and gather some firewood in reserve, and that would be the extent of their preparations.","The only blessing was that death in their sleep was painless. They closed their eyes at night and died before morning.","The central region had once been a prosperous inland area. After the extreme cold, it became a deserted zone. The cities and towns were devoid of survivors, resembling ghost towns.","Too many corpses were rotting, and there was no one capable of dealing with them. The area would soon become an epidemic zone. It was no longer habitable.","Zhou Wang suggested that the convoy pass through as quickly as possible and reach the west as soon as they could, where they could find a suitable place to settle.","Su Yu accepted his suggestion.","Su Yu, Cui Haiyang, and Gao Yuxuan had always been the backbone of the Youth Apartments. From the Youth Apartments to the temporary government, the three of them had been highly active.","In reality, however, they were merely screws in an already established system. None of them had ever truly led a group.","Only Zhou Wang had independently led and managed a residential community.","Thus, the team naturally settled into an arrangement where Su Yu became its spiritual leader, while Zhou Wang handled the actual management.","After crossing the ghost towns of the central no-manâs-land, the terrain rose, and the mountains became noticeably more numerous.","Before long, they saw another city. From here on, they had entered the western region.","They had assumed it would be cold and had prepared themselves to face the extreme chill.","Jiang Cheng had given them a great deal of coal and many blankets and winter clothes precisely so they could withstand the cold.","Yet the western region was experiencing the full warmth of spring. It was even several degrees warmer than S City had been when they set out.","It was baffling.","âWhere did the extreme cold go?â Su Yu asked.","No one could answer her.","In truth, everyone was delighted that the extreme cold was nowhere to be seen. No one wanted to spend their days holed up for the winter. People needed contact with the outdoors; they did not want to become cave-dwellers.","Yet amid the general excitement, Su Yu sensed a faint unease in her heart.","Because of that unease, even though the cityâs high-rises were already visible in the distance, Su Yu still decided not to enter the city. They would camp that night in an open area in the countryside.","Naturally, everyone was disappointed.","Because they had feared that the rotting corpses scattered throughout the central region might spread disease, they had not stopped in any cities. They had spent two nights in a row sleeping outdoors.","Everyone desperately wanted to sleep in a real bed.","Zhou Wang stepped forward to calm them. âThere are a lot of zombies in a major city. There might even be mutant zombies. If we go in later and night falls before we have electricity, itâll be too dangerous. Weâll enter tomorrow morning. At least then weâll be able to see the zombies if they come.â","The complaints subsided.","Su Yu let out a breath of relief.","Fortunately, they had Zhou Wang. She really was not good at managing people.","If only Lesi were here. Lesi was much better with words than she was.","That night was much like the previous two. The earth-element espers constructed houses and large communal sleeping quarters.","Everyone moved the stoves into the buildings. It was still somewhat cold at night, and the temporary structures had no enclosed windows, so they still needed heating.","A few people were also assigned specifically to stand watch. If the extreme cold descended without warning, the sentries could immediately wake the fire-element espers and have them start fires to provide warmth.","Because of this, the fire-element espers were distributed very evenly among the various buildings.","Every preparation had been made on the assumption that they were about to encounter the extreme cold.","But the chill that night was merely the normal temperature of a spring night.","By dawn, the extreme cold had not arrived.","The zombie tide had.","The earth began to tremble, rousing the drowsy sentries.","At first, they thought another earthquake had struck.","Then they saw the zombies pouring out of the distant city.","The sentryâs heart-wrenching cry rang out through the dawn:","âZombies! Zombies are comingâ! Zombiââ","Everyone was jolted awake.","In an instant, white light swept over everyone, expanding outward like a huge inverted bowl and covering all the hastily constructed buildings beneath it.","Su Yuâs protective barrier was truly formidable.","After enduring an earthquake and taking the full impact of half a collapsed building, it had become even more powerful.","In the past, whenever the barrier went up, everyone felt safe.","But this time, after everyone hurriedly put on their armor and grabbed their weapons before rushing out of the buildings, the color drained from every face.","The total number of zombies they had seen over the past ten months might not even equal the number in this single attack.","They stretched across the land in a dark, surging mass.","No one had ever seen so many zombies. It seemed as if their sheer numbers alone could crush humanity beneath their feet.","Everyone froze.","Countless howls rose into the air.","Some people turned pale. Others covered their ears.","When something terrifying reaches a certain scale, it becomes horrifying beyond words.","The zombies came running, kicking up enormous clouds of dust.","All kinds of mutant zombies were already visible: serpentine ones, spider-like ones, three-headed, six-armed onesâevery possible variation, as though this were a grand exhibition of human deformities.","A cloud of dust and smoke came rolling toward them.","Gao Yuxuan and Cui Haiyang, veterans of countless battles, roared, âDonât just stand there! Get to the front! Move! We need time! Buy us timeâ!â","Why did they need time?","Because the protective barrier was being sustained by Su Yu.","It was not limitless.","It could run out of strength, weaken, and vanish.","And because it was shielding everyone, the barrier was extraordinarily large. The larger the barrier, the more superpower it consumed, which meant it could hold out for less time.","They had to buy time!","Fight!","Destroy them!","Many brave people rushed to the front, the tips of their toes pressed against the barrier.","The zombies, of course, did not stop when they saw it.","The zombie horde slammed into the barrier.","Su Yu felt as if she had taken a hammer blow to the chest.","The last time she had felt this way was on the night of the earthquake, when she had single-handedly withstood half a building collapsing on her.","The zombies pounded furiously against the barrier. With so much fresh flesh only a step away inside, how could they not go mad?","There was not a single primitive zombie among them.","They were at least second-generation zombies.","Countless mutated zombies lashed and hammered at the barrier with their tentacles and pincers.","Gao Yuxuan unleashed the highest-voltage current he could muster, striving to kill them instantly.","Cui Haiyang planted a huge iron plate upright on the ground. It rapidly transformed into an iron framework, and above it formed a long blade like a guillotine, positioned at neck height. The blade shot out and retracted repeatedly, harvesting rows of heads each time.","Many of those who had come for âExtreme Coldâ possessed fire-based superpowers.","Fireballs flew outward as if they cost nothing.","The earth-type superpowered individuals knelt with their hands pressed against the soil. Outside the barrier, stone spikes rose one after another, stabbing straight up from between the zombiesâ legs and into their brains.","And a great many ordinary people wielded crescent shovels, hacking away at the zombiesâ heads!","If someone was careless, a zombie would seize the extended shovel. If the wielder failed to let go in time, they would be dragged outside!","Su Yuâs protective barrier was one-way, divided into an âinsideâ and an âoutside.â","Physical and superpowered attacks from outside were blocked.","From inside, physical attacks and superpowers could extend outward. Human bodies could extend through it as well.","Weapons could reach out. Hands could reach out. As long as the rest of the body remained inside, they could pull themselves back in.","But once a personâs entire body had gone outside the barrier, they could not return.","Under the current circumstances, Su Yu could neither reverse the barrierâs âinsideâ and âoutsideâ for a single person nor open a small gap for them.","She had been able to do that before, when there had been fewer zombies and she could manage the precise manipulation.","But now the zombies were swarming the barrier from every direction.","Those at the front collapsed into corpses, and the ones behind them trampled over the bodies and continued charging.","There was no way to perform such fine control. None at all.","The corpses outside the barrier piled up layer after layer, but the zombies behind them kept coming without end. No one knew exactly how many there were.","Farther away stood more than a dozen giant zombies, evenly spaced apart. They did not advance, like generals commanding the battle from the rear.","Everyoneâs adrenaline surged wildly.","People were dragged outside the barrier one after another, and then swallowed by the zombies. They did not even have time to scream. It happened too quickly.","Those at the very front had already been rotated out several times.","Every person who withdrew had arms trembling with muscle spasms.","Cui Haiyang gripped the iron framework and sent the guillotine blade shooting out.","One tentacle had been waiting for this moment.","The instant the blade shot through the barrier and sliced through a zombieâs head, the tentacle darted forward like lightning, wrapped around the blade, and pulled it outward.","Cui Haiyang let go almost at once, but by the time he released it, both his hands had already crossed outside the barrier.","Another tentacle coiled around his wrist.","Cui Haiyang was dragged out.","âHaiyangâ!â Gao Yuxuan let out a shrill cry.","Gao Yuxuan pushed his superpower to a level he had never reached before.","More than a dozen bolts of electricity pierced through the barrier and struck at the heads of the zombies surrounding Cui Haiyang.","Cui Haiyang instantly reshaped the iron framework, forming it into a cage around himself. Blades shot outward from the cage as well. Roaring, Cui Haiyang rammed the iron cage in every direction, trying to carve out a path to survive.","Cui Haiyang had always been the soul of their team.","The moment they saw him trapped, the fire-, metal-, and earth-type superpowered individuals frantically unleashed their abilities at the zombies around him.","But it was useless.","The zombies closed in layer after layer.","They blocked everyoneâs view.","Layer after layer.","Soon, nothing could be seen at all.","Suddenly, a tentacle flung something into the air.","An object spun rapidly, hung suspended for a moment, then came crashing down onto the barrier before bouncing away violently.","Gao Yuxuan saw it clearly.","It was the iron cage Cui Haiyang had just formed.","Gao Yuxuan cried out in a voice torn apart by grief, âHaiyangâ!â","Despair swept through everyoneâs hearts, including Su Yuâs.","Even with so many people in front of her, she could still see the giants in the distance.","They stood there, unmoving, refusing to advance.","Su Yu knew that if so many giants joined the attack, the time the barrier could hold out would be cut in half.","Su Yuâs voice turned sharp. The girl who normally spoke softly and gently shouted, âBrother Zhou! Tell everyone to retreat! Retreat! Get everyone into the vehicles! Iâll hold them off! Fall back! Iâll hold them off!â","Zhou Wang had just withdrawn from the front line. Both his arms were trembling.","With zombies packed so densely together, even he did not dare leave the protection of the barrier. His wind-based superpower was useless here; all he could rely on was brute arm strength.","His muscles were cramping from overuse and pain.","Retreat?","Zhou Wang looked at the backs of his companions, fighting desperately at the front.","Then he turned and looked behind them.","No.","The zombies had gathered on the west side because everyone was facing them head-on. They were all concentrated there.","If they climbed into the vehicles and retreated, the commotion would be too great. The zombies would simply go around the barrier and pursue them.","There were countless speed-type zombies.","There were countless mutated zombies, and no one knew what special abilities they possessed.","And farther away stood so many giant zombies that they were enough to make anyone lose their nerve.","âLosing oneâs nerveâ could sometimes be an objective description.","That was exactly what had happened to Zhou Wang.","He looked at the densely packed front line to the west, then at the empty rear to the east.","Everything seemed to move in slow motion. The roars and screams sounded so faint in his ears, so unreal.","Zhou Wang did not want to die.","He had been given a wind-based superpower by heaven precisely so he would not die. That was how he had always understood it.","How could he die here?","Zhou Wangâs lips trembled.","âN-no, we canât. We wonât get away like that,â he said. âY-you hold on. Iâ¦â","His speech went from stammering to fluent in an instant. âIâll take some people around to the rear and draw their attention. Once I pull them away from here, everyone else can retreat.â","At that moment, Su Yu had no capacity to think.","There were too many zombies. Many of the mutated zombies were immensely powerful, strong enough to exceed what the barrier could neutralize. The excess force rebounded onto Su Yuâs body to a certain degree.","On the night of the earthquake, every bone in her body had fractured. Only Zhang Lesi had managed to drag her back from the gates of death.","Now, every part of her body hurt.","âMove faster! Faster!â she shouted.","Whatever he was going to do, he had to do it quickly!","Zhou Wang answered, âAll right! All right! Hold on! You have to hold on!â","Then he turned and ran.","Su Yu thought he had gone to âlead them away.â He had said he was going around to the back to draw the zombiesâ attention.","But Zhou Wang was simply running east.","Just as one foot stepped outside the protective barrier, Zhou Wang suddenly remembered something.","He hesitated for a moment, then turned and sped into a house.","Three little tykes were hiding inside, too frightened to make a sound.","Zhou Wang rushed in and yanked them to their feet. âCome on! Youâre coming with me!â","The flatbed cart they had used to transport the iron stove the night before was right in front of the house. Zhou Wang put the three children on it. âSit tight and hold on!â","Air currents condensed around him and rose, lifting the flatbed cart slightly off the ground as it fought against gravity.","Zhou Wang started running, dragging the cart and bursting out through the eastern side of the protective barrier.","He left everyone behindâSu Yu and Gao Yuxuan includedâand fled alone with the three little tykes.","Su Yuâs pupils suddenly widened."]},{"number":195,"title":"Chapter 195: 0195","paragraphs":["Compared with Zhang Lesi, Su Yu was a reserved and quiet girl.","Her superpower was also highly unusualâarguably one of a kind.","Since they needed to work as a team, she shared certain information with her comrades, such as the fact that her barrier had an âinnerâ and an âouterâ side.","But there were other things she knew that she had no need to tell anyone else.","For example, whenever someone passed through the barrier from the inside to the outside, it acted like a sensor and let her know who had gone throughâand how many people had crossed it.","So when Zhou Wang took the three children through the barrier, Su Yu sensed it instantly.","Her pupils dilated.","Since last June, they had endured two outbreaks of the zombie virus, a city consumed by flames, and extreme cold. What Su Yu had experienced was unity, courage, and trust. It had never occurred to her that someone within the group might deceive them, betray them, abandon them, or run away.","And it was someone they had relied on and trusted like an elder brother.","Su Yu suddenly remembered that a long time ago, when they had been chatting privately, Gao Yuxuan had mentioned Zhou Wangâs superpower.","âWind element? Thatâs really only good for running away.â Gao Yuxuan had worn a mischievous grin. âThat old broâ¦ deep down, he definitely wants to slip away and make a run for it.â","Of course, he could never say that in public. He had only said it privately among a few close friends.","Later, Zhou Wang had become an important companion and a comrade who fought alongside them. Gao Yuxuan never brought it up again.","Zhao Yi had also said that although it could be summed up as âthe influence of psychological needs on the choice of superpower attributes,â put another way, it was simply that âeverything was fated.â It seemed as if everything had been arranged in advance.","Countless zombies pounded against the barrier. There were simply too many of them, and the backlash reached Su Yu.","Her body began to hurt, but that pain was nothing compared with the blow to her spirit.","For one brief moment, her faith was almost shattered.","Then she opened her eyes and saw the backs of her comrades ahead of her.","In the cool spring morning, sweat had soaked through the backs of many peopleâs clothes.","âGet back!â someone shouted from behind, before charging forward himself.","The person who fell back dropped onto the ground, gasping for breath. Once he had recovered, he charged forward again.","And so Su Yu knew she could not break down.","How could she collapse because of one cowardly deserter when so many comrades ahead of her still needed her?","Su Yu closed her eyes and spent half a minute thinking about what to do. Then she opened them again.","âGet in the vehicles! Fall back! Weâre retreating in five minutes! Iâm taking down the barrierâ!â","Taking down the barrier meant facing the tide of zombies head-on, as well as the giant zombies in the distance that had yet to move. This was already beyond what they could handle with human strength alone.","They had to retreat.","Everyone began to turn and withdraw, scrambling into the vehicles.","Someone helped Auntie Qian into one of them.","Someone shouted after failing to find Little Squirt inside the building, âWhere are the children?â","Su Yu yelled, âTheyâve already left! Get in the vehicles, all of you! Hurryâ!â","Only then did the person climb into a vehicle with a sigh of relief.","Gao Yuxuan retreated to Su Yuâs side. âHow are you getting out?â","Su Yu gritted her teeth. âDonât worry about me. Get in the vehicle! Iâll cover the rear!â","Gao Yuxuan understood at once.","Su Yu had no intention of retreating.","There were many speed zombies among the horde, and the mutant zombies were monstrously powerful.","Without someone covering the rear, no one might make it out.","But whoever stayed behind to cover them definitely would not.","Su Yu shouted, âGo!â","Gao Yuxuan stood shoulder to shoulder with her. âIâm staying with you.â","âI canât leave on my own.â","âIf I did, how would I answer to Jiangbing?â","âThat guy entrusted you to me.â","Su Yu froze. âHeâ¦â","Gao Yuxuan said, âHe likes you. You know that, right?â","Su Yu had never been able to tell for certain whether Li Jiangbing liked her.","With a personality like hers, unless the other person expressed himself clearly, she simply could not be sure.","Sometimes she really envied Lesiâs personality, but she could never be like that herself.","Gao Yuxuan had wanted to speak for Li Jiangbing for a long time, but had never found the chance. If he did not say it now, there might never be another opportunity.","âThat idiot.â","âHe thinks he isnât good enough for you.â","âHis education level is low, while you have a masterâs degree.â","âHe said that if it werenât for this ruined world, you never would have chosen him.â","âThat youâre only settling because the world has fallen apart.â","âYou may be willing to lower your standards and settle, but he canât take advantage of your situation.â","Su Yu smiled.","Tears streamed down her face.","Idiot.","She wished Lesi could see this.","She really wanted to shout it out loud to Lesiâ","See? I have good taste in men too!","Su Yu crossed her fists in front of her forehead and gave a mighty shout. Then she yanked her arms apart.","The barrier instantly expanded from an overturned bowl into a wall stretching endlessly in both directions!","The zombies were blocked. They could not get around it!","Su Yu screamed herself hoarse.","âGo! Get out of hereâ!â","Many people ran toward the vehicles, but slowed down when they looked back and saw what was happening.","Many had already climbed into the vehicles, yet froze when they saw the scene.","Gao Yuxuan performed his signature routine: rolling his wrists and rotating his ankles.","Then he charged forward once more.","âDaddyâs here!â","Purple electricity wove into a net, pierced through the âwall,â and spread outward. A whole swath of zombies collapsed.","Behind them came the roar of engines and the screech of tires against the ground.","Go. Live.","This handsome guy will die in your place.","Gao Yuxuan gathered his strength and was just about to fire a second blast when a fireball shot from behind him, passed through the âwall,â and struck a zombie in the head. It burst into roaring flames!","Gao Yuxuan stared in astonishment.","One fireball after another flew over from behind.","He whipped around. The vehicles really had driven away, fleeing to safety.","But some people had never gotten into the vehicles at all. Others had climbed out again.","Their comrades shouted, âDaddyâs here!â as they screamed and charged back toward the âwallâ!","There were superpowered individuals among them, but even more were ordinary people. They gripped crescent-shaped shovels and used every last bit of strength remaining in their mortal bodies to hack fiercely at the zombies on the other side of the âwallâ!","Gao Yuxuanâs eyes grew hot.","So did Su Yuâs.","There was no need to be too harsh on humanity.","The âmanyâ in âwhen many hearts unite, a fortress can be builtâ had always meant manyânot everyone.","Out of a population of more than a hundred million, perhaps a million people could stand united.","Out of a population of tens of thousands, perhaps fewer than a thousand might share the same goal.","Among two thousand people, if several dozen or a hundred were willing to abandon their chance to escape and stay behind to die together, then they had not been let down!","Tears streamed down Su Yuâs face, but her heart had never been more resolute.","The comrades who had been dragged out of the barrier and killed earlier began to turn into zombies.","Many familiar faces appeared on the other side of the wall.","Gao Yuxuan saw Cui Haiyang.","Cui Haiyangâs face had been gnawed beyond recognition. He walked up to Gao Yuxuan, raised his fist, and roared as he pounded against the âwall.â","Gao Yuxuan held back his tears.","âSee you in the next life, bro!â","Purple electricity shot into Cui Haiyangâs eye socket and straight into his brain.","The âwallâ stretched endlessly to the left and right to prevent the zombies from giving chase.","But this consumed an enormous amount of superpower.","Blood began to run from Su Yuâs nose, and her eardrums throbbed with pain.","At last, the giant zombies in the distance began to move.","They ran on all four limbs, like something between gorillas and enormous hounds.","Their speed was shocking.","If Su Yuâs âwallâ had not blocked them, then at that speed, the giant zombies might well have caught up with the vehicles that had just escaped.","Boom! Boom! Boom! Boom!","More than a dozen giant zombies slammed into the âwallâ one after another.","Su Yu felt a sharp pain in her chest!","Blood burst from her ears!","The giant zombies swung their fists, pounding furiously against the âwallâ!","Blood mist burst from Su Yuâs eyes as well.","Even Gao Yuxuanâs electricity couldnât numb the giants in the slightest.","The giant zombies possessed strength beyond that of ordinary humans. Only an existence as monstrously powerful as Mo Li could stand against them.","The giants raised their fists again.","Every bone in Su Yuâs body shattered, and she fell backward onto the ground, staring up at the sky.","Li Jiangbing had urged her to protect herself first.","But in the end, Su Yu couldnât do it.","If she had, she wouldnât have been Su Yu.","The âwallâ flashed one last time before vanishing from the world.","The giant zombies raised their fists and aimed them at Gao Yuxuan.","Electricity crackled all over Gao Yuxuanâs body. He threw his head back and roared, âIâamâyourâdaââ","â¦â¦","â¦â¦","Zhou Wang actually regretted bringing the three children along. They were extremely burdensome.","But he simply couldnât abandon them.","The oldest was about the same age as his own son.","Perhaps that was a hurdle he could never overcome.","He didnât dare linger, pushing the handcart eastward at full speed.","On flat groundâespecially on smooth roadsâhis wind-based ability consumed very little energy.","Only after he was certain that the zombie horde could no longer catch up did he stop to rest at a gas station.","He found several bags of potato chips in the convenience store and handed them out to the three children to fill their stomachs.","Then he sat there in a daze, wondering what to do next. He had been resting for more than half an hour when he suddenly heard a rumbling sound. He quickly hid with the Little Squirts.","He never would have imagined that it was the people he had left behind.","They were actually still alive. How had they escaped?","Taking advantage of the crowd, Zhou Wang emerged with the Little Squirts, pretending to act naturally.","Everyone had narrowly escaped death themselves, so no one noticed him.","Many people turned their heads when they saw him, assuming he had come from another vehicle. They were even relieved that he was still alive.","And just like that, Zhou Wang slipped back into the crowd.","Many people were crying.","From their conversation, Zhou Wang finally learned how they had survivedâSu Yu, that young girl, had truly sacrificed herself for them, giving her life so the others could escape.","Zhou Wang was stunned.","He didnât notice that Auntie Qian had been sitting in a vehicle, watching him through the window with a gloomy look in her eyes.","Everyone began discussing what to do. Someone said, âBrother Zhou is still here.â","So they all came to ask Zhou Wang.","Zhou Wang was at a loss as well.","Auntie Qian suddenly spoke up. âWe should turn back and look for Jiang Cheng.â","As one of the rare wood-type ability users, Auntie Qian bore the important responsibility of providing food. She had always enjoyed a high status and special treatment.","But she rarely spoke up in discussions or participated in decision-making.","It was unusual for her to voice her opinion on such an important matter. Her suggestion also matched what everyone was thinking at the moment. Many of them wanted to go after Jiang Cheng.","Zhou Wang had no better proposal, either, so everyone decided to head east in search of Jiang Cheng.","That night, they camped outdoors. It was only when they needed ability users that they realized the situation: among several vehicles and hundreds of people, there was only one earth-type user, three fire-type users, and Auntie Qian, the wood-type user.","Where were all the other ability users?","Everyone began crying again.","After filling the vehiclesâ tanks with fuel, they slept for one night before heading east at full speed the next morning.","By afternoon, something in the distance ahead was reflecting the sunlight, shining so brightly that it hurt their eyes.","Everyone crowded toward the front of the vehicles and squinted into the distance.","From the east came a massive convoy, rumbling toward them.","Blades encircled the silver-bright vehicles.","So familiar."]},{"number":196,"title":"Chapter 196: 0196","paragraphs":["Li Feng said that seventy-three people would go with him.","Li Feng had more than two hundred people under him, but only seventy-three were willing to go with him. He was delighted.","âBecause,â he said, âthose seventy-three are all my comrades.â","The survivors from the command post had eventually gone their separate ways. Everyone had their own ideas and chose what they believed was right.","After learning the whole truth, Li Feng and his seventy-three comrades made the same choice: they chose to join Jiang Cheng.","The superpowers of these former soldiers were astonishingly formidable.","Li Feng had a fire-based ability. Wu Jiancheng and Cao Jiacai would have to combine their powers to barely match him.","Finding out what conspiracy lay behind the zombie virus had become Li Fengâs obsession.","Whether it was foreigners or aliens, he had to go and see for himself.","The convoy headed west.","They were 1,500 kilometers away. The journey was not going to be quick.","Some roads had been destroyed by earthquakes, while others had been ruined by freezing during the extreme cold. The drivers did their best, pressing the accelerator to the floor.","After driving for a day, they encountered survivors fleeing eastward the next day.","Only half of them remained.","It was the first time so many people had burst into tears upon seeing Jiang Cheng.","Li Jiangbing listened woodenly as they told him how Su Yu had stayed behind to cover everyoneâs retreat.","Zhao Yiâs lips trembled faintly.","Those who had escaped naturally had not seen what happened at the very end, but from their descriptions, it was clear that those who stayed behind could not possibly have survived.","âAll right. I understand. Everyone, get some rest first, thenâ¦â Jiang Cheng said.","Jiang Cheng thought she had kept her emotions under control quite well, just as she usually did.","But everyone was staring at her in utter silence.","Jiang Cheng was puzzled.","Even Song Jingshuo was staring at her, looking as though he wanted to say something but couldnât.","Under everyoneâs gaze, Jiang Cheng raised a hand and touched her face.","Her fingers came away wet with tears.","Jiang Cheng herself did not know who she was crying for.","She still clearly remembered that in June and July, she had not particularly liked Su Yu.","That girlâs heart was too soft. In an environment like that, being too kind and soft-hearted was, in Jiang Chengâs eyes, a burden.","When had things changed?","How many people whose names she knew had fallen behind along the way?","And what about those who had been injured on June 16, when the first group had gone downstairs to kill zombies?","Looking back now, Jiang Cheng realized how heartless she had been toward them then.","She should at least have asked their names.","At least offered them a word of comfort.","At least shown them some respect.","Every one of them had been worthy of respect.","How had she been able to remain so cold back then?","When had she become the person she was now?","Song Jingshuo led people in settling everyone down.","Amid the crowd, he spotted Auntie Qian.","Auntie Qian was watching him with a somber look.","Song Jingshuo hurried over, delighted to see her.","Auntie Qian had also narrowly escaped death.","Song Jingshuo comforted her gently.","But Auntie Qian told him to lower his head, then whispered something in his ear.","Song Jingshuoâs expression changed.","He straightened and stared at Auntie Qian.","Auntie Qian stared back without flinching.","Everything she had told him was true.","She had no personal grudge against that person, nor any motive to frame a powerful ability user.","She simply was not good at fighting, so she had always stood beside Su Yu and watched the front line. When they had been talking, she had actually been standing right behind him.","At that moment, with everyoneâs lives hanging in the balance, she had not dared interrupt them. The little old woman had gone completely unnoticed.","He had not realized that anyone was standing behind him. Auntie Qian had heard their entire conversation and witnessed everything that had happened.","Song Jingshuo turned and found Jiang Cheng, then quietly told her what Auntie Qian had said.","Jiang Cheng turned to look. Through the crowd, she met Auntie Qianâs eyes.","People walked back and forth between them.","Auntie Qian looked at the two young people in the distance and left the choice to them.","Zhao Yi asked many questions about the zombie army.","Someone said, âI donât know if I saw it wrong, but I think I saw someone I knew.â","Zhao Yi initially thought he meant that some of those who had died in battle had quickly turned into zombies and joined the zombie ranks.","âNo, thatâs not what I mean,â the person said. âIt was my neighbor. He died back in June.â","It was not just one person. Once someone had spoken up, others began saying, âI think I saw someone I knew too. I thought my eyes were playing tricks on me.â","He had seen people who had frozen to death during the extreme cold.","Many people said that during the battle, they had caught fleeting glimpses of zombie faces that looked like people they had once known.","All of those people had died one after another during the ten months since the first outbreak of the zombie virus.","They had died at different times and in all kinds of ways.","Zhao Yi stood in the open space, lost in thought for a long time.","The temporary buildings were finished, and the cadres were notified to attend a meeting.","Zhou Wang hurried over.","Everyone of any importance was there.","Auntie Qian sat in a corner.","Song Jingshuo was speaking with Li Jiangbing. They were standing so close that they were practically whispering to each other.","Li Jiangbing suddenly turned his head, his eyes red.","As soon as Zhou Wang arrived, he asked, âJiang Cheng, what do we do next? Where are we going?â","He spoke first, asked the first question, and seized the initiative.","When people felt guilty, they tended to do unnecessary things to prove that they were not.","Mo Li stood in the doorway.","Song Jingshuo toyed with the vine bracelet around his wrist, pinched off a leaf, and tossed it onto the muddy ground.","Jiang Cheng looked at him with a strange expression.","Could he be called a bad person? His contributions to the group were actually greater than those of many others.","Could he be called a good person? And yet he had done something like this.","âZhou Wang.â It was Li Jiangbing who spoke.","His voice was hoarse.","Zhou Wang knew that he was grieving. Everyone knew that Li Jiangbing had feelings for Su Yu.","Zhou Wang was about to say a few words of comfort.","But Li Jiangbing asked, âYou told her to hold on and said you were taking people to lure the enemy away, didnât you?â","Zhou Wangâs face changed drastically.","The wind-type ability user turned and ran without hesitation, only to trip and land flat on his face.","At some point, thin vines had sprouted from the ground and wrapped around his ankles. Those who knew the truth watched indifferently.","Those who did not know what was happening were utterly stunned.","They looked at Jiang Cheng, then Song Jingshuo, then at everyone else.","No one spoke.","No one wanted to defend someone who had deceived a comrade into going to her death.","âShe volunteered to stay behind!â Zhou Wang shouted. âShe volunteered!â","Li Jiangbing said, âThat happened later. It has nothing to do with what you did. Iâm asking you: did you trick Su Yu into holding on, then run away by yourself?â","Zhou Wang struggled desperately to defend himself. âShe was that kind of person! She was bound to stay behind anyway! She would have done it even without me! She was a saint!â","But in truth, at that moment, Zhou Wang had not known that Su Yu would give up her life to cover everyoneâs retreat.","He had thought she would escape with the others.","He was simply afraid they would not make it out if they fled together.","Zhou Wang had actually regretted what he did back at the gas station.","If he had known Su Yu was that kind of person, he would never have gone out of his way to do it. Then he would not have had to suffer the guilt afterward.","Li Jiangbingâs eyes were deep and cold as a frozen abyss.","âShe may have been a good person. She could choose to sacrifice herself for everyone,â he said. âBut you had no right to trick her into dying.â","A sphere of water appeared out of thin air.","A long time ago, Jiang Cheng had told Li Jiangbing that water could not kill zombies, but it could kill people.","She was always teasing and frightening him.","How could water possibly kill someone?","The sphere of water closed around Zhou Wangâs head.","Zhou Wang charged left and right, struggling to escape, but the vines held fast to his feet, leaving him no way out of the room.","And Mo Li was standing in the doorway.","Zhou Wang collapsed onto the ground and rolled around, desperately slapping at his own face, trying to disperse the water.","But the water ball followed him with deadly precision. There was no escaping it.","Before long, Zhou Wang drowned before the eyes of everyone present.","The floor opened, and his body sank into it, buried on the spot.","Suddenly, the room filled with the crackle of electric current.","Everyone turned around. Sitting on the platform specially built by Zhao Yi was the shortwave radio.","It had started again.","Playing tricks and pretending to be supernatural.","In a house where someone had just died, it was especially chilling.","The mysterious manâs voice rang out: âRun. Run now. Heâs coming.â","Jiang Cheng asked, âWho?â","âThe Corpse Emperor.â","Jiang Cheng asked, âDoes he really exist?â","âIf you donât run, youâll see him.â","âWhere should we run?â","The mysterious man laughed. âThereâs nowhere to run.â","Li Feng flew into a rage. He rushed over and smacked the shortwave radio. âWho are you? Who the hell are you?â","The mysterious man only kept muttering:","âRun. Hurry and run.â","âIf you donât run, heâs coming.â","ââ¦Heâs here.â","âIâm here.â","The room fell deathly silent.","âIâm here.â","A massive block of concrete came crashing down from above, smashing the shortwave radio into a heap of parts before vanishing without a trace.","Everyone turned to look at Jiang Cheng.","Her eyes were pitch-black.","âGo tell everyone,â she said. âThe zombies are coming again. Anyone who wants to run should leave now.â","But where could they run?","That was the question everyone asked most often.","Those who had fled from the west and those who had come from the east gathered together and exchanged information.","The north had truly split open into a vast canyon.","There was a zombie army in the west.","In the east, there were tsunamis and floods. The water had spread all the way from Q City to D City. When the people from the east left D City, the water was already up to their knees. The people of D City were scattering in all directions as well.","The central region had become a dead zone after the extreme cold. Now that the weather was warming up, it was about to become a plague zone.","No one had gone south. But since the ghost radio had said that the continental shelf was sinking and the coastline was advancing inland, it clearly had no intention of letting anyone survive.","Zhao Yiâs theory had been completely proven correct.","Everyone now understood. The people who had created the zombie virus had never intended to let humanity live.","Many people sat on the ground, sobbing uncontrollably.","Finally, someone asked, âWhereâs Jiang Cheng? Where did Jiang Cheng go?â","They still hoped that Jiang Cheng could lead them somewhereâanywhere, even the ends of the earthâas long as there was a direction to follow and some hope to cling to.","Night had already fallen. The fire-type users had lit the fire boxes and torches.","Firelight danced across Jiang Chengâs face, making her look both calm and insane.","âIâm not going anywhere,â she said. âIâm staying right here.â","âI want to see the Corpse Emperor.â","âI want to ask him why heâs toying with us like this.â","âAnyone who wants to leave, leave now.â","But they had already been driving for two days, covering at least seven or eight hundred kilometers.","If the zombie army could still catch up after traveling that distance, then it meant there was nowhere safe left in the world.","Jiang Cheng herself was extremely curious: What did the Corpse Emperor look like?","But no one had seen the Corpse Emperor.","All they had seen was the zombie armyâevery kind of grotesque, bizarre, and terrifying creature imaginable, as though they were the collective product of someoneâs entire imagination.","There were even giant zombies leading the rear guard.","The Corpse Emperor should have been somewhere behind them, but no one had seen his appearance yet.","This man who was always putting on mysterious airsâ¦","Perhaps in response to the question of what the Corpse Emperor looked like, he arrived in grand splendor at daybreak the following morning.","How grand was he?","The zombie army opened the way, an endless sea of corpses.","The giant zombies had been reduced to laborers, carrying a palace.","Yes, a palace.","It was tall, magnificent, and gilded from top to bottom, as though he were afraid Jiang Cheng might not see it.","If this were a comic, Zhao Yi would definitely have cursed at this point:","âWhat the hell is wrong with the author?â"]},{"number":197,"title":"Chapter 197: 0197","paragraphs":["Dozens of blade cars gleamed in the morning light.","Their tanks were full.","Jiang Cheng was in the lead vehicle. âLetâs go,â she said.","Engines roared, and the convoy charged forth beneath the dawn glow.","Zhao Yi thought, Isnât this just like the final battle you always see in anime?","He wanted to laugh.","Though it was hardly appropriate under the circumstances, Zhao Yi still wanted to laugh.","Because he had finally figured it all out.","Zhang Lesi asked him, âWhat are you laughing about?â","Zhao Yi clasped her hand tightly. âLesi, if we end up in another world, weâll definitely find each other, right?â","He had to hear her say it.","Zhang Lesi was utterly confident. âWhether you can find me or not, Iâll definitely find you.â","Zhao Yi was overjoyed. âAll right. Itâs a promise.â","What do you mean, itâs a promise? Idiot.","Zhang Lesi laughed too.","A promise, then.","Tens of thousands of zombies let out a collective roar.","Their synchronization was unnaturally perfect. It was obvious they were being controlled.","The Corpse Emperor controlling the zombie horde was probably hiding inside the palace carried on the shoulders of the giant zombies.","The zombies began to charge.","The blade cars rushed forward without fear.","Billowing clouds of dust rose on both sides.","Impact!","Heads went flying. Tentacles were severed. Claws punched through the cabins and pierced human bodies.","The carsâ window glass had all been removed and replaced with horizontal blades, allowing those with supernatural abilities to use their powers through the gaps.","Fireballs and bolts of electricity shot forth.","Insect-like zombies crawled beneath the cars and heaved them upward. The vehicles tilted, and the zombies seized the chance to swarm over them and flip them over.","The metal-type ability users immediately opened up the cabins. The metal bodies of the cars bloomed like flowers, flinging the zombies clinging to them high into the air.","The survivors took the opportunity to scatter from the cabins.","Armor and crescent shovels glinted in the sunlight.","This time, no one ran away.","Once they understood there was nowhere left in the world where they could survive, the despair somehow made them fearless.","Since death was unavoidable, they might as well kill a few zombies first. At least then, they would not have lived for nothing.","Some of those who had fled eastward began to regret it. Yesterday, they should have stayed behind and died fighting alongside Su Yu, Gao Yuxuan, and Aunt Pan.","But this was fine too.","Dying with Jiang Cheng now was just as good.","Zhao Yi truly saw familiar faces among the zombies.","He saw Nie Kuizhang.","Zhang Lesi saw the doctor who had supervised her training at the hospital.","Her mentor had died during the first zombie outbreak. Nie Kuizhang had died on August 29.","Zhang Lesi was shocked and uncertain. Turning to Zhao Yi, she asked, âWhatâs going on? Am I seeing things?â","Zhao Yiâs expression was remarkably calm. He did not answer her question. Instead, he reminded her once again, âYou have to find me.â","Their car was caught by an octopus-like mutant zombie.","A metal-type ability user opened the cabin and turned the vehicleâs body into blades, slicing through the octopusâs tentacles.","Stone spikes burst up on every side, sending zombies flying.","Zhang Lesi gripped her crescent shovel and shouted to Zhao Yi, âDonât worryâyou wonât be able to escape the palm of my hand!â","Then she charged into the horde.","Every blade car was abandoned.","The finest creations of the metal-type ability users.","They had proven their worth countless times on the roads, slaughtering more zombies than anyone could count.","Now their time had come.","Everyone rushed out of the cabins.","Even someone like Mr. Xu, a metal-type ability user, hadnât given himself a protective shell like a âpen holder.â Like everyone else, he wore only ordinary armor.","They had gone into this battle prepared to die together with the enemy.","Li Jiangbing slaughtered his way through the horde like a Vajra warrior in a Buddhist temple, utterly berserk.","Strictly speaking, this was Song Jingshuoâs first time taking part in a battle with his superpowers.","Thick vines burst from the ground in every direction, sweeping up zombies and hurling them into the distance, smashing their brains on impact. Or they wrapped around their necks and twisted until they snapped.","Li Feng and his comrades were terrifyingly powerful in one-on-one combat.","Yet once they were swallowed by the tide of corpses, every last one of them was overwhelmed.","âGoâJiang Cheng! Goââ Li Feng roared, his entire body engulfed in flames.","Everyone was carving a path for Jiang Cheng.","They wanted Jiang Cheng to go ask that bastard Corpse Emperor exactly what he intended to do in this world.","Mo Li transformed into a giant cat and carried Jiang Cheng toward the palace in the distance.","Anything that dared to stand in their way was bitten to death, trampled flat, or torn to pieces!","Jiang Cheng glanced back and saw her companions sinking into the tide of corpses.","She turned her head forward again and refused to look back.","The giant zombies set the palace down, sending clouds of dust billowing into the sky.","Then they charged at Mo Li, the earth trembling beneath their feet.","ãJiang Cheng, get down!ã Mo Li said. ãJiang Cheng, go!ã","After setting Jiang Cheng down, Mo Liâs body swelled once more!","The enormous beast charged forward and tangled with the giant zombies.","Jiang Cheng ran toward the palace, with Mo Liâs cries echoing behind her.","Jiang Cheng looked back.","There were too many giant zombies. They tore into Mo Liâs flesh.","Jiang Cheng turned her head forward again. The palace was right in front of her.","Her feet never stopped.","Zombies surged forward to intercept her. Massive chunks of concrete appeared in midair one after another, crashing down and flattening swaths of them.","Jiang Cheng ran with every ounce of strength left in her life.","She refused to look at her companions behind her. At that moment, there was only one thing on her mind: charge into that palace, see the true face of the Corpse Emperor, and chop off his dogâs head.","A horde of large mutant zombies appeared ahead. Jiang Cheng released an enormous block of concrete.","These were remnants of buildings she had collected during the earthquake. They had been construction materials for the earth-type users during reconstruction, but in battle, they were ready-made weapons of mass destruction.","Although Jiang Cheng could release the materials and reclaim them at the same time, the limitations of her control range meant that she kept losing usable material as she sprinted forward.","Until she reached the end of the road.","Her space was empty.","Her strength was gone, too.","Jiang Cheng fell to the ground.","Once again, Jiang Cheng felt anger rising inside her.","They had thrown her into a world like this, yet hadnât given her any combat ability.","Using objects from her space as weapons was nothing but a cheap trick! In truth, she had never gained any real fighting power.","Not fire, not lightning, not metal, not earthânot even wood!","All she had was a space and a whole assortment of safety protocols!","To hell with these safety protocols!","Jiang Cheng was so furious that her brain exploded once more.","ãSafety protocols disengaged.ã","An interface like a black hole opened before her eyes, resembling a mirror of pure darkness.","Using the last of her strength, Jiang Cheng drove her crescent shovel into the face of the nearest zombie.","She released the weapon, sprang into the air, and leaped into the black hole.","The black hole vanished in an instant, leaving no one on the ground.","Only the zombies remained, staring around in confusion.","At that exact instant, a black hole opened. Jiang Cheng leaped through space, emerged from it, and hit the ground hard.","Jiang Cheng rolled, then pushed herself up awkwardly and looked ahead.","At last, she saw the Corpse Emperor.","Jiang Cheng had broken the safety protocol, crossed through space, and entered the Corpse Emperorâs palace.","It looked terrifying from the outside, but inside it was remarkably plainâthere was nothing there.","The vast hall contained only enormous marble pillars that took two people to encircle, and a marble floor.","Straight ahead, where a throne would normally stand, was a platform raised above the ground.","That âplatformâ was probably the equivalent of a throne.","Because the Corpse Emperor had no ass to sit on.","âYouâre here,â said the Corpse Emperor.","It was the voice of the mysterious man.","The Corpse Emperor looked very oldâan elderly man with an almost kindly face.","His upper body was human, but from the waist down, he had a spiderâs body and a scorpionâs tail.","Jiang Cheng found the âCorpse Emperorâ before her utterly ridiculous.","What was ridiculous was that he looked like such a cheap patchwork creation, like the villain from a low-budget horror movie with disastrously bad design.","He simply didnât deserve the life-or-death struggle everyone outside had endured.","If Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan saw him, they would be disappointed too. The Corpse Emperor they had imagined was far cooler than this one.","âSo itâs you?â Jiang Cheng said.","She wanted to move closer, but one of her ankles was injured. Pain shot through it, and she nearly stumbled.","Dragging her injured foot, Jiang Cheng moved forward one step at a time.","âWere you the one who dropped me into this world?â","âAre you the one who wants to wipe out humanity?â","âYouâve been playing us in the palm of your hand. Is that fun?â","The sight of the Corpse Emperorâs cheap, ridiculous, utterly uninspired appearance sent her anger surging to its peak.","âTell meâwhat is your purpose?â","âIs it this world, or is it me?â","âTell me. Are the people outside suffering all this because of me?â","The Corpse Emperor actually smiled. âDo you hope they are, or do you hope they arenât?â","The old bastard even had the nerve to press further. âAre these people important to you?â","Her lips were split, and blood seeped from her teeth.","Jiang Cheng spat out a mouthful of bloody phlegm.","âI didnât come here to listen to your jokes. I want the truth!â","âThe truth...â said the Corpse Emperor.","His enormous scorpion tail reached forward and fired a beam of light, which spread into a doorway of light.","âWalk through this door, and you will see the truth.â","âBut you will never be able to turn back.â","âJiang Cheng,â the old man asked, âis the truth really that important?â","Jiang Cheng spat out blood again, then wiped the blood from the corner of her mouth with the back of her grimy hand.","âIf Iâm going to die anyway, I want to die knowing why.â","Without hesitation, she stepped into the light.","...","...","...Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng.","Someone was calling her.","Who was it?","Faces flashed before her eyes, one after another.","First Peng Ze, then Master Luo, Wu Jiancheng, He Tian, Guo Jun, Aunt Pan, Zeng Qiang, Yang Xinyan, Little Fang, Manager Wang, and the aunties.","Little Huang, Xiao Dan, Uncle Eighty, Auntie Xue, Auntie Qian, Mr. Xu, Director Yu, Brother Dongâeven Zhou Wang and Nie Kuizhang.","Jiangbing, Jingshuo, Su Yu, Lesi, Zhao Yi, Yuxuan, Haiyang.","There were too many. Far too many.","Every one of them was ordinary and imperfect. Every one of them had flawsâsome were even full of bad habits.","But every one of them was alive.","Jiang Cheng even felt as though she had never been surrounded by so many living people in her entire life.","Each of them had left an imprint on her soul, layer upon layer, shaping who she was.","ãMental power source link safely disconnected.ã","ãMemory block removed.ã","ãMental power readings normal.ã","ãVital signs normal.ã","âJiang Cheng.â","âYoung Mistress.â","âExecutor.â","All her memories came rushing back. Jiang Cheng knew that these were all names by which she had been called.","The voices sounded distant and indistinct, as though coming from the other side of something.","The probes embedded in her head detached one by one and retracted automatically, causing a faint ache.","She opened her eyes.","The world warped and blurred through the liquid.","The nutrient solution was highly oxygenated. Its nutrients seeped through the skin, while the liquid entered the lungs and exchanged oxygen atoms directly.","A pair of hands after another reached into the fluid, carefully supporting her head, neck, shoulders, and back as they lifted her from the tank.","Jiang Cheng sat up and coughed the liquid from her nose and mouth.","The nutrient solution settled and was recovered. The tank unfolded and contracted, transforming into a platform.","The people around her helped lower her legs.","Afraid that her body had grown numb from lying in the tank for too long, they massaged her from neck to calves.","They were all handsome, physically fit young menâeach one a stunning beauty in his own right.","They knew her body and habits intimately, and knew exactly how to make her comfortable.","Their hands were endlessly gentle.","âExecutor.â An old manâs voice rang out.","It was a familiar voiceâthe mysterious manâs, only older and more weathered. Yet it was still unmistakable.","It was the Corpse Emperor.","The young men stepped aside, revealing an old man behind them.","He wore an extremely old-fashioned uniform with a bow tie.","From head to toe, he embodied every clichÃ©d image of a butler.","He truly was Jiang Chengâs old butler.","That kindly, deeply wrinkled face belonged to the Corpse Emperor.","He was Uncle JiangâUncle Jiang himself.","He asked, âExecutor, did you have fun?â","Jiang Cheng found it utterly hilarious.","She couldnât help covering her forehead and laughing.","Jiang Cheng had been consumed by hatred and fury. Her murderous intent had cut to the bone as she trampled over the sacrifices of her comrades in search of the truth.","Now that the memory block had been removed, she remembered everything.","That detestable, infuriating mastermind who controlled the world, toyed with human lives, and regarded everyone as nothing more than antsâ","It turned outâ¦","Jiang Cheng raised her eyes.","It turned out that person was me."]},{"number":198,"title":"Chapter 198: 0198","paragraphs":["Jiang Cheng asked, âWhat happened to everything afterward? Itâs all such a mess. Why did you intervene personally?â","Ever since the end of the extreme cold, the story had become increasingly overblown, with increasingly flimsy logic.","The Corpse Emperorâs palace had been laughably absurd.","And making the people inside the âWorldâ realize that a third-party supernatural existence was real would itself affect the authenticity of the âWorld.â","The Old Butler wore an utterly innocent expression. âAfter the treatment was complete, we tried waking you several times, but all attempts failed. You were too deeply immersed and refused to wake up. Youâre different from the others. Your psychic source was deeply linked to the system, and forcibly severing the connection might cause further damage. We could only find a way to make you wake up on your own.â","Jiang Cheng was extremely dissatisfied. âThe latter part was far too ugly.â","Jiang Cheng had very high standards when it came to aesthetics. One only had to look at the male companions serving her to know that.","And yet the palace had been so gaudy, while the Corpse Emperor had been so ugly.","The Old Butler looked even more innocent. âThe purpose was to make you feel that something was wrong and break free. You underwent rigorous training and should have been able to distinguish reality from virtuality. I made it this excessive, and you still refused to disconnect.â","Jiang Cheng paused, then defended herself. âBecause everything before that was so realistic.â","The Old Butler rested a hand on his stomach. âOf course it was. To ensure realism, we deployed a large-scale interactive collective-consciousness matrix involving forty thousand people. Apart from us, very few organizations are capable of that.â","The handsome men used towels to wipe away the nutrient fluid remaining on Jiang Chengâs body, then helped her to her feet.","Jiang Cheng reproached him. âThe Corpse Emperor was a complete failure.â","The Old Butler was regretful as well. âActually, I designed it very carefully. I originally planned to use someone close to you as the Corpse Emperor. âSong Jingshuo,â âLi Jiangbing,â âSu Yu,â âZhao Yi,â and âGao Yuxuanâ were the first choices. I was genuinely uncertain which one to use. But when âSu Yuâ died, we detected that the fissure value in the psychic sourceâs Qilicha index was too high. To prevent you from being harmed, we had to abandon the design.â","Jiang Cheng: ââ¦â","âIt was a brilliant design,â Jiang Cheng praised. âDonât design anything like that again.â","She held up one finger. âAlso, âuncertainâ is a behavioral trait found only in carbon-based humans. Youâre a quantum cloud. You donât get uncertain.â","Uncle Jiang smiled.","If one moved around behind him, one would see that the back of his head was enclosed in a transparent casing, inside which substances like rosy clouds drifted.","They were high-density particles from the depths of space. Once activated, they became a quantum cloud.","From the moment it was activated, it became a life-form. At the same time, it was also a quantum computer.","But Uncle Jiang had worn this humanoid shell since the moment of his birth, so everyone still called him âUncle Jiang.â","In truth, he had no gender. He was simply a small quantum cloud.","Of the three quantum computers in the Gita Republic, he was the smallest.","Uncle Jiang said, âWhat you just said constitutes discrimination against my right to life. You should know that it was one of your ancestors who pushed so forcefully for the Other Life Rights Act.â","âMy great-grandmother was incredible,â Jiang Cheng sneered. âYou quantum computers must have adored her.â","âWe respect her,â Uncle Jiang said. âShe was someone who respected all life.â","Jiang Cheng sneered again. âShe respected life so much that she handed the entire family fortune over to a quantum computer.â","âStrictly speaking, we do not possess ownership of the Jiang familyâs industries.â","âYour ancestor promoted the Other Life Rights Act, confirming our existence as legitimate life-forms and granting us legally recognized inheritance rights, along with all other rights.â","âBut all the wealth still belongs to the family itself. She merely granted us the authority to supervise and appoint or dismiss executives.â","But that was precisely what Jiang Cheng feared most about them.","It was true that, as a descendant of the Jiang family, she had been able to become the operating executive of the conglomerateâin other words, its de facto headâbecause the family Mainframe had chosen her.","But at the same time, the power of appointment and dismissal held by the Mainframe was a sword hanging over the head of every executive.","The Mainframe had already dismissed two generations of executives in succession.","Then it had selected Jiang Cheng from the familyâs embryo bank and had her incubated.","At the center of the room was a circular bath. White steam drifted across the warm water.","The young men removed the clothes soaked with nutrient fluid from Jiang Cheng, revealing her beautiful body.","Compared with the Jiang Cheng in the virtual world, the real Jiang Cheng had the same face, but she was a genetically optimized human with an SS-plus genetic rating. Her body was much taller, stronger, and more powerfully built than her virtual body.","The proportions of her muscles and bones were practically perfect.","In fact, as a descendant of an ancestor who possessed the genes of a high-gravity planet, she had exceptionally high muscle and bone density. When living on ordinary planets, she needed to sleep on a gravity bed and undergo regular high-multiple gravity training to maintain her bone density.","In short, she was strong enough to knock down every man present.","In the virtual world, her strength had actually been suppressed through data restrictions; she had not been given an enhanced physique with extraordinary strength.","Soaking in the warm bath, Jiang Chengâs body finally began to relax. The numbness caused by the treatment pod gradually faded, and her body became limber again.","âLetâs discuss serious matters,â Jiang Cheng said. âFirst, how is my psychic source?â","Uncle Jiang said, âIt has recovered completely.â","During the era of the ancestor who founded the Jiang conglomerate, brainwave-control technology had already been widely used.","It was applied to everything from household appliances to weapons and spaceships.","But humanity had not stopped there. After the war between humans and beastfolk ended, humanity acquired the beastfolkâs more advanced genetic technology and made enormous leaps forward along that path.","The human brain was developed further. It took less than a century to progress from brainwaves to psychic power.","Nowadays, a great many important things required a psychic imprintâfrom loans to authorizations.","Including Jiang Chengâs authority, as the operating executive of the family conglomerate, to allocate funds.","This time, Jiang Cheng had been attacked and her psychic source had been damaged, requiring 120 hours of treatment.","Throughout the treatment, her brain had to remain active, and her psychic source could not be allowed to close.","It was like keeping a dying person hanging on to their last breath.","The most common method was to connect the injured personâs brain to a virtual world.","That was what ordinary people did when faced with such a situation.","But Jiang Cheng was not an ordinary person.","Just as the virtual-world Song Jingshuo had said, she truly was a born capitalist.","She had been selected from the familyâs embryo bank and incubated specifically to become the next head of the family.","From childhood, she had received rigorous anti-virtualization training, all to prevent her from being deceived into granting authorization if she were kidnapped and forcibly connected to a virtual world.","She could see through an ordinary virtual world in half a minute and swiftly enter the emergency-response state she had been trained to adopt.","Under normal circumstances, this effectively protected her assets from theft and prevented her authorizations from being abused. But when her psychic source was damaged, it made treatment far more troublesome.","She had to be given an extraordinarily realistic âWorld.â","Of course, that was no difficulty for the Jiang family.","The Jiang familyâs medical group routinely had two hundred thousand people undergoing drug trials and psychic experiments. They were human test subjectsâcommonly known as drug people.","After running countless calculations, the familyâs Mainframe deployed forty thousand test subjects to construct an incredibly lifelike, large-scale interactive co-consciousness matrix for Jiang Cheng, ensuring that she would neither see through it nor suffer a psychological backlash.","Before closing the life-support capsule and entering the matrix, Jiang Cheng had said, âDonât make it too boring.â","Uncle Jiang had replied, âI promise.â","âAnd donât make it too simple, either.â","âIâll monitor the whole process and make sure to raise the difficulty.â","And so, the difficulty had been raised twice afterward.","âWhat about the Tanaka family?â Jiang Cheng asked.","âTanaka Masaya, who organized this attack, has already âdied accidentally.â The Tanaka family has accepted a settlement and decided to stop interfering in this congressional election.â","Jiang Cheng gave a cold laugh. âThey got off too easily.â","Uncle Jiang sighed. âIf your ancestor knew that the two families had ended up like this, she would surely be very disappointed.â","âI hope the two of you will update your database,â Jiang Cheng said. âI know time means very little to quantum clouds like you, but according to the clan culture of ancient Earth unearthed by my great-grandmother, she was my ancestral progenitor, and Iâm already her sixth-generation descendant.â","âThatâs a very long time for carbon-based humans. It means a great deal to us.â","âDonât expect us distant descendants to inherit the friendship between two ancestors. The only things humans can inherit are wealth and power.â","The conglomerate had not originally belonged solely to the Jiang family. At the very beginning, it had been founded by two entrepreneurs and one investor.","The ancestors of the Jiang and Tanaka families had been the two entrepreneurs. According to legend, they had been close friends as well as business partners.","But, as Jiang Cheng had said, friendship could not be inherited.","Six generations later, the two families had become bitter enemies, locked in a fierce struggle over their interests.","âAll right. Is there anything else you need to report?â Jiang Cheng asked.","Uncle Jiang reported all the official business that had piled up during the 120 hours she had been away.","He was her butler, supervisor, and protector, as well as her personal computer, assisting her with every kind of affair.","A light screen unfolded before Jiang Cheng. She handled each matter in turn.","Her mental energy moved smoothly. She left her imprint with ease, approving authorizations one after another.","The treatment had worked very well.","After finishing her official business, Jiang Cheng said, âMake the arrangements. I want to see the Mainframe.â","âOf course.â","Uncle Jiang made as if to leave, then suddenly seemed to remember something. He always enjoyed imitating the behavioral traits of carbon-based humans.","âOh, right. Should the memories of the forty thousand people who participated in the co-consciousness matrix be blocked?â","Jiang Cheng hated it when Uncle Jiang set traps for her.","A large-scale interactive virtual world with such a high degree of realism could have an enormous impact on the human brain. It was explicitly prohibited by law.","In other words, this thing was illegal.","Under normal circumstances, there was no need to ask Jiang Cheng at all. The participantsâ memories would simply be blocked.","When they woke and left their capsules, they would remember nothing about what had happened in the âworld.â","As far as they were concerned, they had merely participated in a clinical trial for a medical group under the Jiang conglomerate. Once the trial was over, they would collect their money and leave.","But Uncle Jiang had deliberately asked Jiang Cheng. His intention was perfectly clear.","He and the Mainframe both knew exactly how much contraband they had smuggled into the virtual worldâand so did she.","They might be the most powerful quantum computers in the world, but Jiang Cheng was also the possessor of an outstanding SS+ genetic profile.","No one was a fool.","She said coldly, âWhy donât you erase my memories first?â","That way, all his and the Mainframeâs hard work would be for nothing.","Uncle Jiang gave an awkward chuckle, but said nothing about how the matter would ultimately be handled.","Men washed Jiang Chengâs body, applied fragrant body wash, and rubbed it over her skin.","Jiang Cheng stared into the misty steam.","If the memories were blocked, everyone would forget everything that had happened in the âworld.â","The thought alone made her angry.","âIf we donât block the memories, what impact will that have on us?â she asked.","Uncle Jiang replied, âSomeone might take the opportunity to blackmail us. Others might report us, or sue us for psychological damages.â","âThen let them sue. Our legal team isnât there to sit around doing nothing. As for the reports, all they can do is make us pay a fine. Weâll pay it.â","Uncle Jiang acknowledged the order.","But Jiang Cheng called him back again. âDonât block the memories. Just weaken them.â","The memories of the âworldâ had already been weakened when she woke up moments ago. That way, she would not confuse the virtual world with reality, nor would it have too great an impact on her real life.","Uncle Jiang acknowledged the order once more and prepared to leave.","One of the male companions moved closer and kissed Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng was a generous patron, and her male companions worked hard to please and entertain her.","As for love, they would never dare hope for it. How could a cold-blooded capitalist like her possibly possess such a thing?","The kiss suddenly reminded Jiang Cheng of something. She pushed the handsome man away and called Uncle Jiang back yet again.","âWhat was the matter with that cat? Did you arrange it?â","âMo Li?â Uncle Jiang said. âNo. He was a calculation error.â","Jiang Cheng stared at him coldly.","âEven quantum computers can make calculation errors,â Uncle Jiang explained. âIt has to do with how the rules were designed.â","Once each participantâs consciousness was connected, the kind of persona they would possess was generated through coordination between the system and that participantâs subjective consciousness.","Only an identity generated in this way would be accepted by the participantâs subconscious. The participant would recognize the âworldâ as real and would not realize that the entire world was fake.","Otherwise, if the identity assigned by the system diverged too greatly from the participantâs subjective wishes, the participant could easily develop the feeling that they were dreaming, or that something was unreal.","The key to the co-consciousness matrix lay in the word âco.â","Everyone affected everyone else. One personâs sense of unreality could spread to the others like a contagious disease.","A majority of the matrixâs nodes had to believe that the world was real in order to maintain its sense of reality.","Once enough nodes realized that the âworldâ was fake, the matrix would collapse.","âThat beastman didnât want to be human,â Uncle Jiang said. âSo when his initial identity was generated, he became a cat.â","Who could have guessed that one of the participants would possess such a powerful desire not to be human?","In reality, the moment Jiang Cheng suddenly awakened to the fact that she was a transmigrator was precisely when the virtual world began operating.","There had been no transmigration. Even the identity of a âtransmigratorâ had been created for Jiang Cheng by the system.","But he ultimately was not a real cat.","Although his conscious mind manifested as a cat, his subconscious still knew that he was human. Thus, he could barely communicate with Jiang Cheng through telepathy.","In fact, he had been the first of all the participants to interact with Jiang Cheng.","Because of Jiang Cheng, he wanted to become human again.","Every time the sky turned purple, data streams surged behind the clouds as the worldâs data was adjusted.","The first time, a portion of the people were assigned the attribute of âzombies.â","The second time, building on the first adjustment, a portion of the people were assigned the attribute of âsuperpowers.â","During the second data adjustment, the black cat that had co-adjusted itself into a data error was further enhanced. The conscious mind that was a cat could no longer suppress the human subconscious, and his communication with Jiang Cheng became smoother.","In simple terms, the âcatâ had acquired human intelligence.","The third time, this fellow had gone too far.","He wanted to become human.","For the system, there was nothing wrong with a participant wanting to âbe humanâ in the virtual world.","After all, he was human to begin with.","The system approved the request.","And so, Mo Li regained his human form."]},{"number":199,"title":"Chapter 199: 0199","paragraphs":["This planet belonged to the Jiang Consortium. It housed the research center and pharmaceutical factories of the consortiumâs medical group.","A great many legal and illegal studies were conducted here.","Large numbers of drug-test subjects underwent human experimentation on the planet. If they were unlucky enough to die, the liability waiver in the agreement they had signed absolved the company of responsibility. At most, their families received a payment to settle the matter quietly. But in this era, reproduction, sex, and marriage had all become separate matters, so quite a lot of people had no family at all. If they died, they died.","That was capitalism for you. Never harbor any illusions about capital.","Everyone living on the planet was either an employee of the medical group or an employeeâs family member.","The entire surface of the planet was covered in greenery, making it look exceptionally beautiful.","There were no âroadsâ on the ground. All routes were in the air, and daily commuting was primarily conducted through transport tubes.","Skyscrapers towered everywhere. In the spaces between them, public transit tubes crisscrossed and wound through the area less than one hundred and fifty meters above the ground like blood vessels. Public transit vehicles sped through the transparent tubes.","At the intersections, vehicles approaching from different directions frequently roared past one another with a time difference of only 0.1 seconds, creating an extremely dangerous spectacle. In reality, however, every public transit vehicle in the tubes was centrally coordinated and efficiently operated by computers. The seemingly perilous 0.1-second gap would never result in a collision.","Above one hundred and fifty meters was the airspace for private flying cars, shuttles, and airships.","Private vehicles were âhungâ outside the balconies of buildings, allowing their owners to board directly from home.","There were no underground parking garages here.","That was why, during the first zombie outbreak, when Jiang Cheng led the residents of the youth apartment complex in clearing out the zombies, they had completely overlooked the underground parking garage.","âJiang Chengâ did not own a private vehicle. She had hardly ever gone down to the complexâs underground levels.","And in Jiang Chengâs world, she had never even seen a design like an underground parking garage.","Neither of them had any frame of reference that connected to the concept of an underground parking garage.","Jiang Cheng slept soundly.","Her brain had effectively gone without rest for one hundred and twenty hours.","This was the first time she had truly slept.","After waking up, she went to the research instituteâs psychic-energy testing building. Most research and experiments involving the brain and psychic energy were carried out there.","The spacious, lofty office contained luxurious sofas facing a curved wall of floor-to-ceiling windows.","Jiang Cheng stood before the glass and gazed into the vast space outsideâ","The twenty-story-high wall was an integrated array of fluid chambers. The entire wall was densely packed with them, resembling countless coffins. A drug-test subject lay inside each one, having sold the use of their brain to a pharmaceutical company for research.","Numerous robots flew busily through the air, maintaining the integrated chamber wall.","They pulled out some chambers and inserted others.","They regulated the various drugs added to the nutrient solution and monitored the vital signs of every subject.","From time to time, a chamberâs red alarm light would flash, indicating that the experimental subject inside was in critical condition. The robots would then fly over at once to make adjustments and attempt a rescue.","Jiang Cheng sat down on the sofa. Dozens of light screens unfolded before her simultaneously.","The screens were filled with people she knew.","Although many of them looked different in reality from how they had appeared in the âWorld,â she could still recognize them at a glance.","âLi Jiangbingâ was still a huge manâmassive beyond belief.","That was because more than eighty percent of his body had already been mechanized.","Medical technology was highly advanced in this era. But advanced technology did not mean widespread access. Cutting-edge treatments came with exorbitant prices.","In this era, the average natural lifespan of a ânatural humanââsomeone born without genetic selectionâwas one hundred years.","The average lifespan of a genetically selected person was between 135 and 150 years.","For a super-selected person like Jiang Cheng, the projected natural lifespan was between 150 and 170 years.","But the rich and powerful could live far beyond 170 years. They had all kinds of methods for extending their lives to around 220 years, or even longer.","Organ replacement using biochemically grown organs cultivated from oneâs own body was the best option, but it was expensive.","Mechanical replacements were the worst option, but they were cheap.","The result was that once more than eighty percent of a personâs body had been mechanized, they automatically lost their citizenship and became subhuman.","They had no right to vote, could not participate in political elections, and could not sit for civil service examinations.","They received unequal pay for equal work. For the same job, they could earn only fifty to seventy percent of the standard salary, and they were usually restricted to low-end work.","âLi Jiangbingâ had only his head, neck, one shoulder, and one arm left. Everything else was mechanical.","His mechanical body had been designed in the exaggerated form of a muscular man. The term âexaggeratedâ was relative to a normal human body. In truth, the fact that he still retained a human shape was not particularly exaggerated.","That was simply how society worked. Employers liked those bizarrely shaped mechanical bodies. It seemed that the more inhuman the design, the more it amused them. As a result, people with grotesque mechanical forms found it easier to get jobs.","Li Jiangbingâs entire body was hard and rigid. No wonder his supernatural ability was water-based and soft.","He must have longed for a soft body.","The forty thousand subjects were released in batches.","In the plaza-like rest hall, âLi Jiangbingâ found âSu Yu.â","In the âWorld,â Su Yuâs bones had all been shattered.","The real-life âSu Yuâ was hardly any better.","She lay on a hovering bed.","At a glance, the bed was clearly a cheap, crudely assembled secondhand model.","Anyone who was willing to sell their body to a pharmaceutical company for all kinds of experiments could not possibly be financially well-off.","They became drug-test subjects precisely because they were poor.","âLi Jiangbingâ sat beside Su Yuâs bed and spoke with her.","Both of them were shy and gentle.","But Su Yuâs condition looked terrible. She could not even raise the bed into a sitting position like an ordinary patient.","Her entire body was limp, bones included.","Jiang Cheng asked, âWhatâs Su Yuâs condition?â","She looked like she was about to die.","Uncle Jiang pulled up her records. âShe was an elementary school teacher. When the accident occurred on Beiyu-3 Mining Planet, she was there with her students on an educational field trip.â","The various illnesses of ancient Earthâincluding cancer and AIDSâhad long since been treatable in this era.","The common and troublesome illnesses of this age were various forms of radiation sickness.","Uncle Jiang continued, âWhen the Beiyu-3 mining disaster occurred, there werenât enough seats in the escape pods. She put her students inside and stayed behind. Her entire skeleton has now turned gelatinous. Temporary supports were installed in her brain and chest cavity to keep them functioning.â","Su Yuâs problems were not limited to her bones. Her brain and internal organs had also been irradiated, and she was slowly approaching death.","She was only an ordinary-salaried teacher. Just keeping herself alive had already exhausted all her savings.","Jiang Cheng said bitterly, âWhy is she such a bleeding heart everywhere she goes?â","Then she said, âLet me hear what the two of them are saying.â","Numerous small metal spheres hovered in the air throughout the rest hall. They were surveillance cameras.","No one paid them any attention. This was the rest hall of a pharmaceutical companyâs experimental building, a public space.","One of the metal spheres received the command and flew silently over to the two of them.","From her side, Jiang Cheng could now hear their conversation clearly.","âLi Jiangbingâ: âIâve saved up some money. Letâs replace your skeleton first. Biochemical bone is out of the questionâthe money isnât enough. Weâll start with a metal skeleton.â","âSu Yuâ: âIt wasnât easy for you to save that money. Donât waste it on me. Iâll just live one day at a time.â","Li Jiangbing was a demi-human, and his pay was already lower than that of ordinary people.","He didnât even have a body he could sell to pharmaceutical companies for quick money by participating in research. The only medical studies he could sign up for were psychological ones.","Su Yu said, âItâs all right. I do have some research value. I signed a long-term observation contract with them. They collect data on radiation decay and organ failure from me. My basic living expenses are covered. Is the money you have enough to buy a heart? You should get a cultured heart first. Then youâll be able to reclaim your citizenship.â","Legally speaking, that was possible.","But in reality, Li Jiangbing looked completely mechanical. Even if he regained his citizenship with the help of a biochemical heart and became entitled to equal pay, he would still face discrimination in the real world.","Employers might not be willing to hire a machine-man who had to be paid at least the minimum wage for citizens. There were plenty of cheaper machines.","Li Jiangbing held Su Yuâs soft, mollusk-like hand, carefully, as though he were afraid of crushing her bones.","Tears fell from his eyes.","Jiang Cheng felt a surge of anger.","This was exactly why ultra-high-fidelity virtual worlds had been banned by the government.","Jiang Cheng, a natural-born capitalist, and these peopleâor, more precisely, these poor peopleâcame from two entirely different worlds. They would never have crossed paths in their entire lives.","But after ten months of sharing life and death and working together in the âworldââthe equivalent of 120 hours in realityâshe was now nearly moved to tears by these two poor, unfortunate souls.","How could she not be angry?","Uncle Jiang cast a furtive glance at her.","Jiang Cheng didnât feel like dealing with him.","It had been nothing more than an ordinary treatment session.","Those two lumps of quantum cloud had turned it into this mess just to smuggle in their own agenda. She would settle accounts with them later.","She pulled up Su Yuâs file.","Su Yu had effectively sold her ruined body to a pharmaceutical company as research material in exchange for the basic necessities of survival.","She was currently living on this planet. She went nowhereâand, of course, she couldnât go anywhere.","Her condition required chemotherapy, as well as a bone transplant. Ideally, all her internal organs would be replaced too. Otherwise, even if the chemotherapy succeeded, her lifespan would still be drastically shortened.","The most expensive part was the chemotherapy. The compounds needed to treat the type of radiation damage she had suffered were extremely costly.","Jiang Cheng entered a string of commands.","Uncle Jiang stole another glance at her.","He simply enjoyed imitating the actions of carbon-based humans.","In reality, as the assistant computer to the operations executive, he had no need to âsneak a look.â Every command Jiang Cheng issued had to pass through him.","The only difference was whether she gave him a verbal command directly or entered it through the light-screen interface. In the end, all the data would still pass through Uncle Jiangâs âbrain.â","In the hall, two young men found each other and embraced in delight.","One was a university student, the other a high school student.","The university student was Zhao Yi, and the high school student was Gao Yuxuan.","It wasnât yet the start of the school term in their star sector, and both young men wanted to earn as much tuition money as they could before classes began.","âHoly shit, you know how I died?â Gao Yuxuan gestured animatedly as he told Zhao Yi. âA giant zombie beat me to death, holy shit.â","âWhen I died, I found out what had happened. The system data reassigned me to play a zombie. Hahaha, I understood everything right then, hahaha. But zombies had fixed behavior commands, so we couldnât control ourselves.â","After chatting for a little while, the two confirmed that although they were slightly different in age in reality, they could still become kindred spirits.","After all, they had been drawn to each other in the virtual world because of the foundation provided by their real-life personalities and interests.","Gao Yuxuan had far too many things he wanted to discuss with Zhao Yi.","âThe timeline should have been around the ancient Earthâs turn of the millennium. Iâm especially good at history, so thereâs no way Iâm wrong.â","âActually, move the timeline forward another ten or fifteen years, and âzombiesâ wouldnât have been a problem at all. Theyâd have been taken out instantly. Iâve read A History of Drone Developmentâyou know, drones had already been invented by then.â","âBut did âzombiesâ like that really exist? It doesnât seem to make much sense.â Gao Yuxuan was bursting with curiosity. He would definitely look up the historical records when he got back.","Zhao Yiâs range of knowledge was broader, and he knew a little about the subject. âYouâre younger, so you might not know this, but the original concept may have been based on heavy addicts of âHappy Mood.ââ","âWhat the hell is that?â","âA kind of drug. It was popular for a while when I was a kid. People who took too much of it would completely lose their minds and become extremely aggressive. There was no way to bring them back. Whenever the police encountered one, they shot them on sight instead of making an arrest. The drug was banned later. For a while, public security in the area where I lived deteriorated badly because of it. Thatâs why my foster parent took me and moved away.â [Note]","Gao Yuxuan had far too many things he was dying to discuss with Zhao Yi.","But Zhao Yi had something more urgent to deal with.","âWeâll talk about all that later!â he said. âHelp me find Lesi, quick. Iâm afraid sheâll twist my ear if I donât find her first.â","Gao Yuxuan burst out laughing."]},{"number":200,"title":"Chapter 200: 0200","paragraphs":["âGao Yuxuanâ asked, âThis is my first time taking part in a psychological experiment. They donât erase our memories after it ends?â","He was genuinely confused.","Those memories had a profound effect on people. For example, the delight heâd felt the first time he saw âZhao Yiâ was entirely because the two of them had been inseparable best friends in the virtual world.","In reality, however, they were strangers.","The childâs voice was a little too loud. âZhao Yiâ stiffened, then turned and covered his mouth. âKeep your voice down. Donât shout.â","He lowered his voice and explained to his little brother, âTheyâre supposed to block your memories. Normally, when you wake up, you wonât remember anything that happened during the experiment.â","âGao Yuxuanâ was just as quick-witted as he had been in the virtual world. âSoâ¦â","Zhao Yi said, âSo this is actuallyâ¦ against regulations. I donât know what went wrong on their end. But itâs best not to make a fuss.â","What if the pharmaceutical company discovered this operational or administrative error and came to erase everyoneâs memories? What would happen to him and âZhang Lesiâ then?","Even âGao Yuxuanâ would forget the friendship they had formed.","Gao Yuxuan immediately clamped his mouth shut.","They didnât find âZhang Lesi,â but they did find âLi Jiangbingâ and âSu Yu.â","Li Jiangbingâs figure was impossible to miss. He stood out so much that he could be spotted at a glance in any crowd.","The moment they saw that back, they both had the same premonition. They walked over, and sure enough, it was âLi Jiangbing.â","âLi Jiangbingâ was delighted to see them too. He bumped fists with them and hugged them.","âSu Yuâ smiled as well.","âGao Yuxuanâ looked from âLi Jiangbingâ to âSu Yu.â âYou twoâ¦â","âLi Jiangbingâ gently took Su Yuâs hand. âWeâre planning to get married.â","Su Yu didnât mind that Li Jiangbing was a second-class citizen among the subhumans, and Li Jiangbing didnât mind that Su Yu didnât have much longer to live.","The fact that they had met through a mental-power experiment meant that fate had brought them together.","âZhao Yiâ struggled to hold back his tears.","âGao Yuxuanâ was young and had no hope of controlling his emotions. Tears were already rolling down his cheeks.","He opened his mouth. âIâ¦â","âZhao Yiâ knew him too well. He immediately stepped on his foot to stop him, then said to âLi Jiangbing,â âLetâs exchange contact information.â","They touched their wrists, and the smart computers worn there added one another as friends.","âLi Jiangbingâ said, âAre you looking for Lesi? You should ask at the service desk.â","âZhao Yiâ was afraid that reminding the pharmaceutical company that their memories hadnât been erased would only make things worse, so he hadnât dared to ask.","But Li Jiangbing said, âJingshuo already went.â","âGao Yuxuanâ said, âHuh?â","Li Jiangbing added, âDonât be surprised when you see Jingshuo. He doesnât look much like he did in the virtual world.â","At the service desk stood a young woman named Jiang Cheng.","âIâm sorry, but we canât disclose the private information of other experiment participants.â","âIs that so?â Song Jingshuo said, both hands in his pockets. âA hyper-realistic virtual world with more than ten thousand participants? Thatâs explicitly prohibited by law. And failing to block the participantsâ memories is itself a violation.â","It was a threat.","But the customer-service representative wasnât afraid. The people above had given her instructions long ago.","âIâm sorry for the misunderstanding. Itâs just that this experiment placed a considerable burden on everyoneâs brains, so weâve specifically arranged a period of rest for all participants.â","As she spoke, the representative pressed a button. An announcement rang through the hall:","âParticipants who need memory blocking to erase their virtual memories, please follow the guidance robot along the path marked by the green indicator lights. If you do not require memory blocking, a liability waiver has been sent to your smart terminal. Please confirm it on your personal terminal.â","Quite a few people stood up and followed the guidance robot along the green line of lights that had appeared on the floor to undergo memory blocking.","But many others remained where they were.","A considerable number of people were willing to retain the memories of those ten months.","So memory erasure wasnât mandatory.","âZhao Yiâ let out a huge sigh of relief.","Only âSong Jingshuo,â standing in front of the service desk, frowned.","That back looked much the same as it had in the virtual world. Anyone could tell at a glance that it was Song Jingshuo.","âGao Yuxuanâ raised a hand and waved. âJingshuo!â","His shout drew the attention of quite a few people. In the virtual world, âSong Jingshuoâ had been Jiang Chengâs second-in-command.","âSong Jingshuoâ turned at the sound of his name and smiled when he saw the two young boys.","But âZhao Yiâ and âGao Yuxuanâ both froze.","Li Jiangbing had warned them in advance that they needed to prepare themselves for the possibility that the real person might not resemble their virtual counterpart.","Clearly, âZhao Yiâ and âGao Yuxuanâ hadnât truly been prepared.","âSong Jingshuoââ¦","He was actually a middle-aged man.","âYou know,â Jiang Cheng said, resting her chin on her hand with great interest, âJingshuo is even more attractive like this than he was when he was young.â","The real âSong Jingshuoâ was a fully mature man.","He wasnât as lean as he had been in his youthful appearance, but he was still in excellent shape.","His face hadnât changed all that much, yet it was obvious that he had lived through things. Perhaps it was because the brashness of youth had faded, leaving behind only a restrained bearing.","When he spoke with âZhao Yiâ and âGao Yuxuan,â even his manners and diction were more polished than those of the Song Jingshuo from the âWorld.â","He really did look like the same Song Jingshuo, only fully grown and mature.","âHe looks like he has good genes,â Jiang Cheng remarked.","She pulled up his records, and sure enough, he was not only genetically selected but had also received a remarkably high genetic rating.","How had someone like that ended up here?","A bankrupt business owner.","His rÃ©sumÃ© was exceptionally impressive.","In the âWorld,â he had been a financial elite. In reality, he was almost the exact opposite: a technician by training who had started an industrial business from scratch.","For a time, he had been tremendously successful.","So the guy hadnât been putting on airs. The older man really had once been a high-level business executive.","The greatest mistake of his life had been bringing in outside investors because he wanted to expand.","A practical man had built his company from the ground up, but capital was speculative and bloodthirsty.","The tech-born entrepreneur had nearly been destroyed by financial capital.","In the end, the investors kicked him out of the company he had founded himself and left him saddled with debt.","âSong Jingshuoâ asked, âYou still havenât found Lesi?â","âZhao Yiâ shook his head.","âGao Yuxuanâ said, âI heard not everyone is here. Theyâre leaving in batches. Maybe Lesi isnât in this group.â","Young people really were optimistic.","âSong Jingshuoâ had already thought of another possibility.","But there was no need to say it aloud. When you were young, you had to run into the wall yourself.","âZhao Yiâ asked, âAre you looking for Jiang Cheng?â","âSong Jingshuoâ said, âYes.â","Li Jiangbing hadnât gone looking for Jiang Cheng. It was enough that Su Yu didnât look down on him. He hadnât expected everyone else to feel the same way.","There were no wealthy people among those who came to serve as drug subjects. But even the fallen genetically selected individuals still looked down on people like Li Jiangbing, a subhuman.","But then âSong Jingshuoâ said, âIâm not looking anymore.â","He continued, âIf I canât find her, then I suppose we werenât meant to meet.â","As he spoke, he stared at the enormous corporate emblem on the far wall.","There was the pharmaceutical groupâs logo, but positioned above it was the emblem of a family.","The character was:","âJiang.â","It was written in an archaic script.","âSong Jingshuoâ was highly learned.","He recognized it.","His gaze grew deeper.","âWell, well.â Jiang Chengâs lips curled up. âAs expected of him.â","Uncle Jiang nodded. âIn the virtual world, a âpersonaâ refers only to the identity assigned to someone by the system.â","But in this massive interactive consciousness matrix, what each person revealed through their interactions with others was their own mind and personality.","The intelligent people in the âworldâ could never be fools in reality, and those who were shy and introverted in the âworldâ would not be bold and uninhibited in reality.","That was why Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan had still hit it off at first sight in reality.","That was why Li Jiangbing and Su Yu still liked each other.","Song Jingshuo asked about their studies and encouraged Zhao Yi. âGo on. Look for her properly, and donât let her slip away.â","Zhao Yi was also genetically selected.","Gao Yuxuan was a natural-born human. Natural-born humans were children born when an unpaired man and woman conceived through sexual intercourse, without undergoing genetic matching.","In the Capital Star Cluster, natural-born humans who came from elsewhere were all low-level laborers, doing the most menial work. But in the frontier regions, there were many natural-born humans.","The Jiang Consortiumâs pharmaceutical research center owned the planet they were on. It was located in the frontier regions, which was precisely why they could find so many inexpensive human subjects for drug trials.","The site selection and planning had been clear from the very beginning.","But Gao Yuxuan was obviously one of those natural-born humans who had won the genetic lottery.","His intelligence was plain to see.","Most of the trial subjects were financially strapped, even desperately poor.","Someone like Zhao Yi was probably among the best of themâa university student.","He might be struggling financially at the moment, but he still had prospects for the future. At the very least, he had a brighter future than anyone else here.","Regardless of what Zhang Lesi was like in real life, she probably wouldnât look down on Zhao Yi.","Unlessâ¦","Although Song Jingshuo was warm and easy to talk to, Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan still felt somewhat constrained.","After all, he was a genuine adult, while the other two were still students.","Only after they parted ways did the two of them finally relax.","Gao Yuxuan said, âWeâre doomed. Jiang Cheng might be some old auntie.â","Zhao Yi: âHuh?â","Jiang Cheng: ââ¦â","Gao Yuxuan continued, âLook, Jingshuo is an old man. Jiang Cheng gets along with him so well and they have so much to talk about. She must be an old auntie too. When we see her later, Iâll have to call her Aunt Jiang.â","Gao Yuxuan slapped his fist into his palm. âI knew it. Jiang Cheng can keep me completely under control. Sheâs just like my mother.â","ââ¦â","In the office, Jiang Cheng watched the surveillance screens and ground her teeth. âYou little brat.â","Logically speaking, there was nothing wrong with his reasoning.","The problem was the imbalance of information. Jiang Cheng had received targeted training from birth. She had been raised specifically to become the consortiumâs administrator.","That was why she was so perfectly in sync with a middle-aged entrepreneur.","Jiang Cheng flipped through Song Jingshuoâs biography.","It was obvious that he was an outstanding talent.","Jiang Cheng smiled. âTell me, if I gave him two choices, which one do you think heâd pick?â","Just then, someone ran past Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan.","âRobot, wait! Robot, wait!â","Song Jingshuo saw that person too.","Neither he nor Zhao Yi said anything. Gao Yuxuan was about to call out a greeting, but Zhao Yi stopped him.","The person called out to the robot, âTake me to have my memory blocked.â","Then he followed the robot away.","âWhy did you stop me again?â Gao Yuxuan said. âWasnât that Brother Zhou? Why didnât you say hello?â","Zhao Yi wanted to tell him the truth.","But the so-called âtruthâ was nothing more than a falsehood that had happened inside a virtual world.","Then what about love?","Zhao Yi suddenly felt afraid.","Love had to be real, didnât it?","Look at Jiangbing and Su Yu. Their feelings for each other were real."]}]);
